    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Hsiang-Fu Yu's Home Page\nWelcome to Hsiang-Fu Yu's Home Page\nMy name is\nHsiang-Fu Yu\n. I am a Principal Applied Scientist at Amazon and a Ph.D. graduated from the\nCenter of Big Data Analytics\nof University of Texas at Austin\n\t\t\tsupervised by\nProf. Inderjit Dhillon\n. \n\t\t\tI received my master degree in National Taiwan University with a \n\t\t\tsupervision of\nProf. Chih-Jen Lin\n. \n\t\t\tMy research mainly focus on \n\t\t\tmachine learning and data mining. Please see my\nCurriculum Vitae\nfor further information.\nE-Mail: rofuyu_AT_cs.utexas.edu\nEducation\nPh.D., Department of Computer Science, University of Texas at Austin, 2011 - 2016.\nNational Taiwan University, Taipei, Taiwan\nM.S., Department of Computer Science and Information Engineering, 2008 - 2010\nB.S., Department of Computer Science and Information Engineering, 2004 - 2008\nWork Experience\nAmazon, Palo Alto, U.S. (Oct 2016 - now)\nPrincipal Applied Scientist\nLeading the PECOS project to develop solutions for various projects requiring Predictions for Enormous and Correlated Output Spaces (\ngithub\n)\nWorked on deep learning modeling for personalized recommendation\nWorked on recurrent behavior modeling and context-aware personalization\nWorked on query completion problems in search\nMicrosoft Research,  Redmond, U.S. (Jun 2015 - Aug 2015)\nResearch Intern\nWorked on one-class collabrative filtering problems\nWalmartLabs., San Bruno, U.S. (Jun 2013 - Aug 2013)\nResearch Intern\nAdvised by Manyam Mallela now at\nBlueshift\nEBay Inc., San Jose, U.S. (May 2012 - Aug 2012)\nResearch Intern\nInvestigated large-scale product title classification\nConducted analysis on the feedback given by buyers.\nGoogle Inc., Taipei, Taiwan/Mountain View, U.S. (Jun 2008 - Sep 2008)\nEngineering Intern\nWorked on the projet of universal search.\nInvestigated machine learning approaches for boosting CTR of universal search results.\nInstitute of Plant and Microbial Biology, Academia Sinica, Taiwan (Mar 2008 - May 2008)\nResearch assistent.\nNational Center for Theoretical Sciences, Taiwan (Jul 2005 - Aug 2005, Jul 2006 - Aug 2006)\nSummer Intern\nStudied on graph coloring and related problems\nStudied on Ramsey Theory and related problems\nPublications\nJyun-Yu Jiang, Wei-Cheng Chang, Jiong Zhang, C.-J. Hsieh,\nH.-F. Yu\nRelevance under the Iceberg: Reasonable Prediction for Extreme Multi-label Classification.\nTo Appear at SIGIR, 2022.\nY. Xiong, W.-C. Chang, C.-J. Hsieh,\nH.-F. Yu\n, I. S. Dhillon.\nExtreme Zero-Shot Learning for Extreme Text Classification.\nTo Appear North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies (NAACL), 2022.\nH.-F Yu\n, K. Zhong, J. Zhang, W.-C. Chang, and I. S. Dhillon.\nPECOS: Prediction for Enormous and Correlated Output Spaces.\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (JMLR), 2022.\nP. A. Etter, K. Zhong,\nH.-F Yu\n, L. Ying, and I. S. Dhillon.\nAccelerating Inference for Sparse Extreme Multi-Label Ranking Trees.\nACM International Conference on World Wide Web (WWW), 2022.\nE. Chien, W.-C. Chang, C.-J. Hsieh,\nH.-F Yu\n, J. Zhang, O. Milenkovic, I. S. Dhillon.\nNode Feature Extraction by Self-Supervised Multi-scale Neighborhood Prediction.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2022.\nJ. Zhang, W.-C. Chang,\nH.-F Yu\n, I. S. Dhillon.\nFast Multi-Resolution Transformer Fine-tuning for Extreme Multi-label Text Classification.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 34, 2021.\nX. Liu, W.-C. Chang,\nH.-F Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, and I. S. Dhillon.\nLabel Disentanglement in Partition-based Extreme Multilabel Classification.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 34, 2021.\nP.-H. Chen,\nH.-F Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, and I. S. Dhillon.\nDRONE: Data-aware Low-rank Compression for Large NLP Models.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 34, 2021.\nW.-C. Chang, D. Jiang,\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-H. Teo, J. Zhang, K. Zhong, K. Kolluri, Q. Hu, N. Shandilya, V. Ievgrafov, J. Singh, and I. S. Dhillon.\nExtreme Multi-label Learning for Semantic Matching in Product Search.\nThe conference on Knowledge, Discovery, and Data Mining (KDD), 2021.\nX. Liu,\nH.-F Yu\n, I. S. Dhillon, and C.-J. Hsieh.\nLearning to Encode Positions with Continuous Dynamical Model.\nInternational Conference of Machine Learning (ICML) 37, 2020.\nY. Shen,\nH.-F Yu\n, S. Sanghavi, and I. S. Dhillon.\nExtreme Multi-label Classification from Aggregated Labels.\nInternational Conference of Machine Learning (ICML) 37, 2020.\nW.-C. Chang,\nH.-F. Yu\n, K. Zhong, Y. Yang, and I. S. Dhillon.\nTaming Pretrained Transformers for eXtreme Multi-label Text Classification.\nThe conference on Knowledge, Discovery, and Data Mining (KDD), 2020.\nCode\nL. Wu,\nH.-F. Yu\n, N. Rao, J. Sharpnack, and C.-J. Hsieh.\nGraph DNA: Deep Neighborhood Aware Graph Encoding for Collaborative Filtering.\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2020.\nQ. Hu,\nH.-F Yu\n, V. Narayanan, I. Davchev, R. Bhagat, and I. S. Dhillon.\nQuery Transformation for Multi-Lingual Product Search.\nThe 2020 SIGIR Workshop On eCommerce.\nR. Sen,\nH.-F. Yu\n, and I. S. Dhillon.\nThink Globally, Act Locally: A Deep Neural Network Approach to High-Dimensional Time Series Forecasting.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2019.\nAn earlier version appears in Time Series Workshop at ICML 2019.\nCode\nJ. Zhang,\nH.-F. Yu\n, and I. S. Dhillon.\nAutoAssist: A Framework to Accelerate Training of Deep Neural Networks.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2019.\nCode\n.\nQin Ding,\nH.-F. Yu\n, and C.-J. Hsieh.\nA Fast Sampling Algorithm for Maximum Inner Product Search.\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2019.\nP. Raman, J. Zhang, S. Ji,\nH.-F. Yu\n, S V N Vishwanathan, and I. S. Dhillon.\nExtreme Stochastic Variational Inference: Distributed Inference for Large Scale Mixture Models.\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2019.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, and I. S. Dhillon.\nParallel Asynchronous Stochastic Coordinate Descent with Auxiliary Variables.\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2019.\nW.-C. Chang,\nH.-F. Yu\n, I. S. Dhillon, and Y. Yang.\nSeCSeq: Semantic Coding for Sequence-to-Sequence based Extreme Multi-label Classification.\nNIPS Workshop: Compact Deep Neural Network Representation with Industrial Applications (NIPS CDNNRIA), 2018.\nC. Jiang,\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, and Kai-Wei Chang.\nLearning Word Embeddings for Low-resource Languages by PU Learning.\nNorth American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies (NAACL), 2018.\nCode\n.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, Q. Lei, and I. S. Dhillon.\nA Greedy Approach for Budgeted Maximum Inner Product Search.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NIPS) 30, 2017.\nSupplementary materials are in the end of the paper.\nCode\n.\nH.-F. Yu\n, H.-Y Huang, I. S. Dhillon, and C.-J. Lin.\nA Unified Algorithm for One-class Structured Matrix Factorization with Side Information.\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI) 31, 2017.\nSupplementary materials are in the end of the paper.\nCode\n.\nH.-F. Yu\n, M. Bilenko,  and C.-J. Lin.\nSelection of negative samples for one-class matrix factorization.\nSIAM International Conference on Data Mining (SDM), 2017.\nCode\n.\nY. You, X. Lian, J. Liu,\nH.-F. Yu\n, I. S. Dhillon, J. Demmel, and C.-J. Hsieh.\nAsynchronous Parallel Greedy Coordinate Descent.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NIPS) 29, 2016.\nH.-F. Yu\n, N. Rao, and I. S. Dhillon.\nTemporal Regularized Matrix Factoriztion for High-dimensional Time Series Prediction.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NIPS) 29, 2016.\nA preliminary version appear appears at\nTime Series Workshop at NIPS 2015\n.\nCode\n.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, H. Yun, S V N Vishwanathan, and I. S. Dhillon.\n\tNomadic Computing for Big Data Analytics.\nIEEE Computer. vol. 49:4, pages 52-60, 2016.\nN. Rao,\nH.-F. Yu\n, P. Ravikumar, and I. S. Dhillon.\nCollaborative Filtering with Graph Information: Consistency and Scalable Methods.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NIPS) 28, 2015.\nSpotlight\n.\nCode\n.\nC.-J. Hsieh,\nH.-F. Yu\n, and I. S. Dhillon.\nPASSCoDe:Parallel ASynchronous Stochastic dual Co-ordinate Descent.\nInternational Conference of Machine Learning (ICML) 32, 2015.\nCode\n,\nSlides\n.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, H. Yun, S V N Vishwanathan, and I. S. Dhillon.\nA Scalable Asynchronous Distributed Algorithm for Topic Modeling.\nACM International Conference on World Wide Web (WWW), 2015.\nCode\n.\nH. Yun,\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, S V N Vishwanathan, and I. S. Dhillon.\nNOMAD: Non-locking stOchastic Multi-machine algorithm for Asynchrounous and Descentralized matrix completion.\nVery Large Data Base (VLDB), 2014.\nH.-F. Yu\n, P. Jain, P. Kar, and I. S. Dhillon.\nLarge-scale Multi-label Learning with Missing Values.\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) 31, 2014.\nPre-built Binary Code\n,\nSource Code with Inductive Matrix Factorization Extension\n.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, S. Si, and I. S. Dhillon.\nParallel Matrix Factorization for Recommender Systems.\nKnowledge and Information Systems (KAIS), 41(3), 793--819, 2014.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-H. Ho, Y.-C. Juan, and C.-J. Lin.\nLibShortText: a library for short-text classification and analysis.\nTechnical report 2013.\nLibShortText software\n.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-H. Ho, P. Arunachalam, M. Somaiya, and C.-J. Lin.\nProduct Title Classification versus Text Classification\n.\n\tTechnical report 2012.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, S. Si, and I. S. Dhillon.\nScalable Coordinate Descent Approaches to Parallel Matrix Factorization for Recommender Systems.\nIEEE International Conference on Data Mining(ICDM), December 2012\n,\nbest paper award\n.\nH.-F. Yu\n, C.-J. Hsieh, K.-W. Chang, and C.-J. Lin.\nLarge linear classification when data cannot fit in memory.\nKDD 2010\nbest research paper award\n.\ncode\n. A short version appears in IJCAI 2011. A\njournal version\nappears in \n\tACM Transactions on Knowledge Di...[truncated]"
