    "homepage_text": "Song-Chun Zhu - Homepage\nSong-Chun Zhu\nFounding Director, Â\nBeijing Institute for General Artificial Intelligence (BIGAI)\nDean, Â\nInstitute for Artificial Intelligence & School of Intelligence Science and Technology, Peking University\nChair Professor, Â\nPeking University & Tsinghua University\nResearch Areas\nComputer Vision\nStatistical Modeling & Computing\nCognition\nMachine Learning\nNatural Language and Dialogue\nAI\nRobot Autonomy\nStatistical Modeling & Computing\nComputer Vision\nMachine Learning\nRobot Autonomy\nAI\nCognition\nNatural Language and Dialogue\nTextbooks to build a framework\nThe Tong Test: Evaluating Artificial General Intelligence Through Dynamic Embodied Physical and Social Interactions\nSong-Chun Zhu, Yujia Peng, Yizhou Wang, Zhenliang Zhang, Jiaheng Han\nPosts & Telecommunications Press,2025\nAGI Path based on Chinese Philosophy\nSong-Chun Zhu\nCheers Publishing, 2024\nScientific Models in Chinese Thoughts\nSong-Chun Zhu\nCheers Publishing, 2024\nTalent Cultivation Progarm for General AI\nSong-Chun Zhu, Wenxin Li, Zhouchen Lin, Yuxi Ma\nPeking University Press, 2024\nMonte Carlo Methods\nAdrian Barbu and Song-Chun Zhu\nSpringer, 2020.\nComputer Vision: Statistical Models for Marr's Paradigm\nSong-Chun Zhu and Yingnian Wu\nSpringer, 2021\nComputer Vision: Stochastic Grammars for Parsing Objects, Scenes, and Events\nSong-Chun Zhu and Siyuan Huang\nSpringer, 2021\nCognitive Models for Visual Commonsense Reasoning\nSong-Chun Zhu and Yixin Zhu\nSpringer, 2021\nThe Tong Test: Evaluating Artificial General Intelligence Through Dynamic Embodied Physical and Social Interactions\nSong-Chun Zhu, Yujia Peng, Yizhou Wang, Zhenliang Zhang, Jiaheng Han\nPosts & Telecommunications Press,2025\nAGI Path based on Chinese Philosophy\nSong-Chun Zhu\nCheers Publishing, 2024\nScientific Models in Chinese Thoughts\nSong-Chun Zhu\nCheers Publishing, 2024\nTalent Cultivation Progarm for General AI\nSong-Chun Zhu, Wenxin Li, Zhouchen Lin, Yuxi Ma\nPeking University Press, 2024\nMonte Carlo Methods\nAdrian Barbu and Song-Chun Zhu\nSpringer, 2020.\nComputer Vision: Statistical Models for Marr's Paradigm\nSong-Chun Zhu and Yingnian Wu\nSpringer, 2021\nComputer Vision: Stochastic Grammars for Parsing Objects, Scenes, and Events\nSong-Chun Zhu and Siyuan Huang\nSpringer, 2021\nCognitive Models for Visual Commonsense Reasoning\nSong-Chun Zhu and Yixin Zhu\nSpringer, 2021\nLinks to some Conferences / Workshops / Summer Schools\nIEEE Conf. on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, Long Beach, Los Angeles, CVPR 2019.\nInt'l Workshops on Vision Meet Cognition: Function, Physics, Intent and Causality\n....\nFPIC workshop with cvpr2014\n....\nFPIC workshop with cvpr 2015\n....\nWorkshop with CogSci 2015\n...\nFPIC workshop with cvpr 2017\nInt'l Workshop on\nLanguage and Vision CVPR 2015.\nInt'l Mathematics Forum at Sanya, 2013\nIEEE Conf. on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, Providence, Rhode Island, CVPR 2012\nInt'l Workshop on Stochastic Image Grammar (SIG):\n....\nSIG workshop, with cvpr 2009\n....\nSIG workshop with iccv 2011\n...\nSIG tutorial with cvpr 2012\nSummer Schools on Vision and Learning in China:\n....\nLotus Hill 2005\n.....\nLotus Hill 2006\n....\nLotus Hill 2008\n....\nXi'an 2010\n,...\nBeijing 2012\nSymposium on Vision/Neural/Cognitive Science in Honor of David Mumford\n2007,\nand\n2017\n.\n6th Int'l Conference on EMMCVPR, 2007\nInt'l Workshops on Statistical and Computational Theories of Vision (SCTV):\n....\n1st SCTV, Fort Collins 1999\n, ....\n2nd SCTV, Vancouver 2001\n....\n3rd SCTV, Nice, France, 2003"
