    "homepage_text": "Xiaojin Zhu: Professor in Computer Science at University of Wisconsin-Madison\nXiaojin (Jerry) Zhu\nProfessor\nUniversity of Wisconsin-Madison\npress\nstudents\nteaching\npublications\nresearch\nhome\nJerry Zhu is a Vilas Distinguished Achievement Professor in the\nDepartment of Computer Sciences\nat the\nUniversity of Wisconsin-Madison\n.  Jerry received his Ph.D. from Carnegie Mellon University in 2005. His research interests are in machine learning, particularly optimal teaching, sequential decision making, and learning in game theory.  He currently serves or has served as conference chair for AISTATS and CogSci, position paper track chair for ICML, action editor of the Machine Learning Journal, and a member of the DARPA ISAT advisory group. He is a recipient of an NSF CAREER Award and a winner of multiple best paper awards, including an ICML classic paper prize.\nAwards\nVilas Distinguished Achievement Professor, University of Wisconsin-Madison, 2025\nKellett Mid-Career Award, University of Wisconsin-Madison, 2024\nStephen C. Kleene Professorship, University of Wisconsin-Madison, 2021\nVilas Associate, University of Wisconsin-Madison, 2020\nVilas Faculty Mid-Career Investigator Award, University of Wisconsin-Madison, 2017\nSheldon & Marianne Lubar Professorship, University of Wisconsin-Madison, 2016\nAAAI / Computing Community Consortium\n\"Blue Sky Ideas\" Track Prize\n, 2015\nICML\nClassic Paper Prize, 2013\nBest Paper on Knowledge Discovery, ECML-PKDD 2012\n\"COW\"\nStudent Choice Professor of the Year, 2012\nACM SIGSOFT Distinguished Paper, International Symposium on Software Testing and Analysis, 2011\nNational Science Foundation Faculty Early Career Development (CAREER) award, 2010\nProfessional services\nOrganizer,\nMachine Learning Lunch Meetings (MLLM)\nat UW-Madison\nPosition Paper Track Co-Chair: ICML 2026, ICML 2025\nConference Chair:\nCogSci 2018\nConference Chair:\nAISTATS 2017\nOrganizer:\nNIPS 2017 Workshop on Teaching Machines, Robots, and Humans\n, Dec 9, 2017\nOrganizer:\nDagstuhl Seminar 17351 \"Machine Learning and Formal Methods\"\n, August 2017\nTutorial Co-Chair: ICML 2020\nWorkshop Co-Chair: ICML 2011\nArea Chair / Senior Area Chair / Senior Program Committee:\nNeurIPS 2026\n,\nICML 2026\n,\nAAAI 2026\n,\nNeurIPS 2025\n,\nICML 2025\n,\nICML 2024\n,\nNeurIPS 2023\n,\nAAAI 2023\n,\nNeurIPS 2022\n,\nICML 2022, 2021\n,\nAISTATS 2021\n,\nAAAI 2021\n,\nIJCAI 2021\n,\nNeruIPS 2020\n,\nAAAI 2020\n,\nNeruIPS 2019\n,\nIJCAI 2019\n,\nCogSci 2019\n,\nICML 2019\n,\nAISTATS 2019\n,\nAAAI 2019\n,\nICML 2018\n,\nAAAI 2018\n,\nNIPS 2017\n,\nICML 2016\n,\nAAAI 2016\n,\nNIPS 2015\n,\nICML 2015\n,\nNAACL 2015\n,\nIJCAI 2015\n,\nEMNLP 2014\n,\nNLPCC 2014\n,\nICML 2014\n,\nSDM 2014\n,\nAISTATS 2013\n,\nICML 2013\n,\nSDM 2013\n,\nNIPS 2012\n,\nICML 2012\n,\nNAACL-HLT 2012\n,\nACML 2012\n,\nNIPS 2011\n,\nICML 2011\n,\nACML 2011\nOrganizer, ICML 2014 workshop on\nTopological Methods for Machine Learning\nCurriculum Vitae\nvitae.pdf\nContact\nEmail:\njerryzhu@cs.wisc.edu\nOffice:\nComputer Science 5381\nPhone:\n608.890.0129\nFax:\n608.262.9777\nAddress:\nXiaojin Zhu\nDepartment of Computer Sciences\nUniversity of Wisconsin-Madison\n1210 W. Dayton St.\nMadison, WI, USA 53706"
  },
