    "homepage_text": "Hengshu Zhu's Homepage, ä¸ªäººå­¦æ¯å°ç«\nHengshu Zhu, ç¥æä¹¦, Ph.D.\nDistinguished Member of CCF, Senior Member of ACM, CAAI and IEEE\nProfessor, Computer Network Information Center, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nAdjunct Professor, AI Thrust, The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (GZ)\nAddress: CAS Informatization Plaza No.2 Dong Sheng Nan Lu, Haidian District, Beijing 100083, China\nEmail: hszhu AT cnic.cn\n[\nBiography\n]          \r\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nNews\n]          \r\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPublications\n]          \r\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nHonors & Awards\n]          \r\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nAcademic Services\n]          \r\n\t\t\t\t[\nData Sets\n]\nShort Biography\nDr. Hengshu Zhu is a Full Professor and the Deputy Director (Academic) at the\nComputer Network Information Center (CNIC)\n, Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS), where he leads the\nData Intelligence for Scientific Innovation Lab (DI4Science Lab)\n. Prior to this role, he held several distinguished positions in industry, including serving as Head of the\nTalent Intelligence Center (TIC)\nand as a Principal Architect & Scientist at Baidu, Chinaâs leading search engine and AI company, where he also served as Deputy General Manager of Baidu's HR Intelligent & Information Systems. He additionally held roles as Head of the\nCareer Science Lab (CSL)\nand as a Chief Research Scientist at BOSS Zhipin, China's largest online recruitment platform. He is currently an Adjunct Professor at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (Guangzhou).\nHis research interests lie in data mining and machine learning, with a focus on developing fair, effective, and efficient data analysis techniques for innovative scientific and business applications. He has filed over 100 patents and published more than 200 research papers in top-tier journals (e.g., Nature Cities, Nature Communications, IEEE TKDE, IEEE TMC, ACM TKDD, ACM TOIS) and leading conference proceedings (e.g., KDD, SIGIR, WWW, IJCAI, AAAI). He has received the Best Student Paper Awards at KSEM 2011, WAIM 2013, and CCDM 2014, as well as Best Paper Nominations at ICDM 2014 and WSDM 2022. He was honored with the Distinguished Dissertation Awards from both the Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS) and the Chinese Association for Artificial Intelligence (CAAI) in 2016, and the Special Prize of the Presidentâs Scholarship from CAS in 2014. His research has been widely featured in leading business media outlets such as Harvard Business Review, MIT Technology Review, Nikkei Asian Review, and Fast Company. He also won the Grand Prize of the Ram Charan Management Practice Award from Harvard Business Review in 2018. In recognition of his contributions to data mining research, he has been named among the KDD Top 20 Rising Stars by Microsoft Bing Academic Search (2016), the Most Influential Scholars in Data Mining by Aminer AI 2000 (2022), the Worldâs Top 2% Most Influential Scientists by Stanford University (2022-2024), and the Intelligent Computing Innovators of China by MIT Technology Review & DeepTech (2024).\nHe has served in various leadership roles in academia, including Industry Chair of PRICAI-2022 and Program Co-Chair for the KDD CUP-2019 Regular ML Track, as well as for workshops such as OBTA, TMC, and AICS. He has also been an Area Chair for KDD, AAAI, and IJCAI, and regularly contributes as a (Senior) Program Committee member for numerous top-tier conferences. He is a Distinguished Member of CCF and a Senior Member of ACM, CAAI, and IEEE, as well as a committee member of the CCF Expert Committee on Big Data. He is the Founding and current Chair of the IEEE SA Talent Service and Management Working Group, where he led the development of IEEE Standard 3154-2024.\nOpenings\nä¸­å½ç§å­¦é¢è®¡ç®æºç½ç»ä¿¡æ¯ä¸­å¿ç§å­¦æ°æ®æºè½ä¸åæ°å®éªå®¤é¿ææèå­¦æ¯ç±»/å·¥ç¨ç±»åå£«ãç¡å£«ãåå£«åãå®ä¹ çï¼æ¬¢è¿èç³»ã\n[\nå¯¼å¸ä¿¡æ¯\n]\n[å®éªå®¤ä¸»é¡µ]\nI am currently recruiting MS/PhD students, research interns, and postdoctoral researchers at DI4Science Lab@CNIC to work on research topics related to Data-driven AI for Science (e.g., Earth Science, Life Science, Social Science, Sustainability, etc.), Responsible AI (e.g., Trustworthiness, Fairness, Explainability, Security and Privacy, etc.), and Large Foundation Model-based domain innovations. To apply, please send your resume to hszhu AT cnic.cn.\n[Supervisor Info]\n[Lab Info]\nProjects & Products\nSciHorizon AI4Science Benchmarking Platform (ç§å­¦å°å¹³çº¿AI4Scienceè¯ä»·å¹³å°).\n[\nLink\n] [\nNews\n]\nIEEE Standard 3154-2024 (Recommended Practice for the Application of Knowledge Graph for Talent Services).\r\n                                                [\nLink\n] [\nNews\n]\n2021 Global Top 100 Chinese Rising Stars in Artificial Intelligence (2021 AIåäººæ°æç¾å¼ºæ¦)\r\n \t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nLink\n]\r\n\t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nReport\n]\r\n\t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nNews\n]\n2022 Global Top Chinese Young Scholars in Artificial Intelligence (2022 AIåäººéå¹´å­¦èæ¦å)\r\n \t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nLink\n]\r\n\t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nReport\n]\r\n\t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nNews\n]\n2022 Global Top Chinese Young Female Scholars in Artificial Intelligence (2023 AI åäººå¥³æ§éå¹´å­¦è)\r\n \t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nLink\n]\r\n\t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nReport\n]\r\n\t\t\t\t\t  \t[\nNews\n]\nMedia Coverage & Updates\nWe are organizing\n\"The International Workshop on Talent and Management Computing (TMC)\"\nin conjunction with\nKDD\n. [\nTMC-2025 CFP!\n] [\nTMC-2024\n][\nTMC-2023\n][\nTMC-2021\n][\nTMC-2020\n][\nTMC-2019\n]\nWe organized\n\"The International Workshop on Artificial Intelligence for Career Science (AICS)\"\nin conjunction with\nICDM-2023\n. [\nLink\n]\nWe organized\n\"The KDD Cup 2019 Regular ML Track\"\n,Context-Aware Multi-Modal Transportation Recommendation, [\nLink\n]\nWe organized\n\"The International Workshop on Organizational Behavior and Talent Analytics (OBTA)\"\nin conjunction with\nKDD-2018\n. [\nLink\n]\nApr. 2021,\nåæç½\n,\nâAI+äººæç®¡çâææ°ç ç©¶ææç»ä¸Natureå­å\n,\r\n\t\t\t\t [\nLink\n]\nOct. 2018,\nåä½åä¸è¯è®º\n,\nç¾åº¦äººææºåºï¼å¤§æ°æ®æºè½åäººæç®¡ç\n,\r\n\t\t\t\t[\nLink\n] [\n2018å¹´åº¦æå§â¢æ¥å°ç®¡çå®è·µå¥\n]\nOct. 2018,\nMIT Technology Review\n,\nBaidu is testing neural networks that can match job seekers to jobs\n,\r\n\t\t\t\t[\nLink\n]\nOct. 2018,\nFast Company\n,\nBaidu researchers are testing tech that can match job candidates with postings\n,\r\n\t\t\t\t[\nLink\n]\nNov. 2017,\nNikkei Asian Review\n,\nChinese internet leaders are also HR pioneers\n,\r\n\t\t\t\t[\nLink\n]\nDec. 2016,\nåä½åä¸è¯è®º\n,\nå¤§æ°æ®+äººå·¥æºè½ï¼ç¾åº¦è¿æ ·ç®¡çäººæ\n,\r\n\t\t\t\t[\nLink\n]\nHonors & Awards\n2024, The 2023 Intelligent Computing Innovators of China (2023å¹´ä¸­å½æºè½è®¡ç®åæ°äººç©), MIT Technology Review & DeepTech\n2023, China Management Science Award, Society of Management Science of China ï¼ç¬¬å«å±ä¸­å½ç®¡çç§å­¦å­¦ä¼âç®¡çç§å­¦å¥âï¼\n2022-2023, The World's Top 2% Most Influential Scientists, Stanford University\n2022, Most Influential Scholar in data mining domain, Aminer AI 2000\n2018, æè²é¨èªç¶ç§å­¦ä¸ç­å¥\n2018, Ram Charan Management Practice Award-Grand Prize, Harvard Business Review ï¼2018å¹´åº¦æå§â¢æ¥å°ç®¡çå®è·µå¥-å¨åºå¤§å¥ï¼\n2016, The Seeds of Baidu Top Award\n2016,\nDistinguished Dissertation Award of Chinese\r\n\t\tAcademy of Sciences (CAS)\n(ä¸­å½ç§å­¦é¢ä¼ç§åå£«å­¦ä½è®ºæå¥)\n2016,\nthe Distinguished Dissertation Award of China\r\n\t\tAssociation for Artificial Intelligence (CAAI)\n(ä¸­å½äººå·¥æºè½å­¦ä¼ä¼ç§åå£«å­¦ä½è®ºæå¥)\n2016,\nKDD Top 20 Rising Star by Microsoft Bing Academic Search\n(KDDäºåå¤§å­¦æ¯æ°æ)\n2014, Special Prize of President Scholarship, Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS) (ä¸­å½ç§å­¦é¢é¢é¿ç¹å«å¥)\n2014, IEEE ICDM-2014 Best Paper Nomination\n2014, CCF CCDM-2014 Best Student Paper Award\n2014, The 1st Huayu Scholarship for Graduate Studentsï¼ç¬¬ä¸å±åçå¥å­¦éï¼\n2013, National scholarship for Graduate Students of China ï¼åå£«ç ç©¶çå½å®¶å¥å­¦éï¼\n2013, Springer WAIM-2013 Best Student Paper Award\n2012, Grand Prize of Tencent Innovation Scholarship\n2012, Scholarship Award for Excellent Doctoral Students of China (æè²é¨åå£«å­¦æ¯æ°äººå¥)\n2012, Visting Scholarship granted by China Scholarship Council (å½å®¶å¬æ´¾è®¿é®å­¦è)\n2011, Springer KSEM-2011 Best Student Paper Award\nSelected Publications [\nGoogle Scholar\n] [\nDBLP\n]\nText Book & Standards:\nåºç¦æ¯,  æ±åæ¤¿,\nç¥æä¹¦\n,  çè¾,\nãè¿ç§»å­¦ä¹ ç®æ³ï¼åºç¨ä¸å®è·µã\n,\næºæ¢°å·¥ä¸åºçç¤¾,\näº¬ä¸åå\n, 2023\nIEEE Recommended Practice for the Application of Knowledge Graphs for Talent Services\n,\nIEEE Standards Association,\nIEEE 3154-2024\n, 2023\nTechnical Reports & White Papers:\nWei Zeng,\nHengshu Zhu\n, Chuan Qin, Han Wu, Yihang Cheng, Sirui Zhang, Xiaowei Jin, Yinuo Shen, Zhenxing Wang, Feimin Zhong, Hui Xiong,\nApplication-Driven Value Alignment in Agentic AI Systems: Survey and Perspectives\n,\nTechnical Report,\narXiv:2506.09656\n, 2025\nYang Ji, Ying Sun, Yuting Zhang, Zhigaoyuan Wang, Yuanxin Zhuang, Zheng Gong, Dazhong Shen, Chuan Qin,\nHengshu Zhu\n, Hui Xiong,\nA Comprehensive Survey on Self-Interpretable Neural Networks\n,\nTechnical Report,\narXiv:2501.15638\n, 2025\nChen Zhu, Yihang Cheng, Jingshuai Zhang, Yusheng Qiu, Sitao Xia,\nHengshu Zhu*\n,\nGenerative Organizational Behavior Simulation using Large Language Model based Autonomous Agents: A Holacracy Perspective\n,\nTechnical Report,\narXiv:2408.11826\n, 2024\nJingya Hou, Xiaoyu Chen, Weiqiang Zhang,\nHengshu Zhu\n, Li Liao,\nAge Discrimination, Employment Barriers During the Prime Working Age and Career Behaviours\n,\nTechnical Report,\nSSRN:4992040\n, 2024\nMeng Hua, Yuan Cheng,\nHengshu Zhu*\n,\nThe Career Interests of Large Language Models\n,\nTechnical Report,\narXiv:2407.08564\n, 2024\nYufei Ji, Lan Chen, Lu Wang, Jingya Hou, Xi Chen,\nHengshu Zhu*\n,\nGenerative AIâs labor-replacing impacts on occupations also foster short-run job opportunities for early adopters\n,\nTechnical Report,\nSSRN:4862800\n, 2024\nLan Chen, Yufei Ji, Xichen Yao\nHengshu Zhu*\n,\nOccupation Life Cycle\n,\nTechnical Report,\narXiv:2406.15373\n, 2024\nLan Chen, Xi Chen, Shiyu Wu, Yaqi Yang, Chang Meng,\nHengshu Zhu*\n,\nThe Futur...[truncated]"
