    "homepage_text": "Yuan-Fang Li's Homepage\nYuan-Fang Li’s Homepage\nShangri-La, China, photo credit:\nme\nLatest news\nTwo papers on LLMs accepted at\nICL’24\n: on\nreducing hallucinations\nand\ntime series forecasting\n.\nOne\npaper\non a debiased dataset on social intelligence accepted at\nEMNLP’23\n.\nTwo papers on\ncultural norm discovery\nand\ncross-lingual summarisation\naccepted at\nACL’23\n.\nAbout\nSome information about myself.\nRead More\nPublications\nA list of my publications.\nRead More\nResearch\nMore about my research.\nRead More\nTravel photos\nSome photos, on the road. Coming soon…\nRead More"
  },
  "serper::Chenglong Wang": {
    "homepage": "https://chenglongwang.org/",
    "emails": [
      "chenglong.wang@microsoft.com"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/chenglong-MS",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Chenglong's Homepage\nChenglong Wang\nEmail\nGithub\nHello!\nI'm a principal researcher in Microsoft Research. Our team designs new interative agentic tools to help people better work with data.\nI got my PhD in University of Washington. I was lucky to work with\nRas Bodik\nand\nAlvin Cheung\n, and we built program synthesis-powered tools for data analysis. I studied in Peking University. I was lucky to work with\nZhenjiang Hu\nand\nYingfei Xiong\non program transformation.\nNews\nCheck out\nData Formulator\n, our open-source AI-powered visulaization tool for data exploration.\n[tool]\n[github]\n[video]\nDrop me an email if you'd like to work together.\nPublications\nConference\nPlugMem: A Task-Agnostic Plugin Memory Module for LLM Agents\n(preprint)\nKe Yang*, Zixi Chen*, Xuan He*, Jize Jiang*, Michel Galley, Chenglong Wang, Jianfeng Gao, Jiawei Han, ChengXiang Zhai\n[arxiv]\nReUseIt: Synthesizing Reusable AI Agent Workflows for Web Automation\n(IUI 2026)\nYimeng Liu, Misha Sra, Jeevana Priya Inala, Chenglong Wang\n[arxiv]\nPiCCL: Data-Driven Composition of Bespoke Pictorial Charts\n(VIS 2025)\nHaoyan Shi, Yunhai Wang, Junhao Chen, Chenglong Wang, Bongshin Lee\n[link]\nData Formulator 2: Iterative Creation of Data Visualizations, with AI Transforming Data Along the Way\n(CHI 2025)\nChenglong Wang, Bongshin Lee, Steven Drucker, Dan Marshall, Jianfeng Gao\n[paper]\nDynaVis: Dynamically Synthesized UI Widgets for Visualization Editing\n(CHI 2024, Best Paper Award)\nPriyan Vaithilingam, Elena L. Glassman, Jeevana Priya Inala, Chenglong Wang\n[paper]\nHow Do Analysts Understand and Verify AI-Assisted Data Analyses?\n(CHI 2024)\nKen Gu , Ruoxi Shang, Tim Althoff, Chenglong Wang, and Steven M. Drucker\n[paper]\nPhotoScout: Synthesis-Powered Multi-Modal Image Search\n(CHI 2024)\nCeleste Barnaby, Jocelyn Chen, Chenglong Wang, Isil Dillig\n[paper]\nIs Self-Repair a Silver Bullet for Code Generation?\n(ICLR 2024)\nTheo X. Olausson, Jeevana Priya Inala, Chenglong Wang, Jianfeng Gao, Armando Solar-Lezama\n[paper]\nData Formulator: AI-powered Concept-driven Visualization Authoring\n(VIS 2023, Honorable Mention)\nChenglong Wang, John Thompson, Bongshin Lee\n[paper]\n[overview-video]\n[blog]\nFast and Reliable Program Synthesis via User Interaction\n(ASE 2023)\nYanju Chen, Chenglong Wang, Xinyu Wang, Osbert Bastani, Yu Feng\nOn the Design of AI-powered Code Assistants for Notebooks\n(CHI 2023)\nAndrew McNutt, Chenglong Wang, Rob DeLine, Steven M. Drucker\n[paper]\nLearning Math Reasoning from Self-Sampled Correct and Partially-Correct Solutions\n(ICLR 2023)\nAnsong Ni, Jeevana Priya Inala, Chenglong Wang, Oleksandr Polozov, Christopher Meek, Dragomir Radev, Jianfeng Gao\n[paper]\nFault-Aware Neural Code Rankers\n(NeurIPS 2022)\nJeevana Priya Inala, Chenglong Wang, Mei Yang, Andres Codas, Mark Encarnación, Shuvendu Lahiri, Madan Musuvathi, Jianfeng Gao\n[paper]\nType-Directed Synthesis of Visualizations from Natural Language Queries\n(OOPSLA 2022)\nJocelyn Chen, Shankara Pailoor, Celeste Barnaby, Abby Criswell, Chenglong Wang, Greg Durrett, Isil Dillig\n[paper]\nSynthesizing Analytical SQL Queries from Computation Demonstration\n(PLDI 2022, Distinguished Paper)\nXiangyu Zhou, Rastislav Bodik, Alvin Cheung, Chenglong Wang\n[paper]\n[slides:pdf]\nFalx: Synthesis-powered Visualization Authoring\n(CHI 2021,\nBest Paper Award\n)\nChenglong Wang, Yu Feng, Rastislav Bodik, Isil Dillig, Alvin Cheung, Amy J. Ko\n[paper]\n[preview video]\n[CHI talk video]\n[blog post]\nProgram Synthesis using Deduction-Guided Reinforcement Learning\n(CAV 2020)\nYanju Chen, Chenglong Wang, Osbert Bastani, Isil Dillig, Yu Feng\n[paper]\nScout: Rapid Exploration of Interface Layout Alternatives through High-Level Design Constraints\n(CHI 2020)\nAmanda Swearngin, Chenglong Wang, Alannah Oleson, James Fogarty, Amy J. Ko.\n[paper]\nVisualization by Example\n(POPL 2020)\nChenglong Wang, Yu Feng, Ras Bodik, Alvin Cheung, Isil Dillig.\n[paper]\n[slides:pdf]\nLearning Transferable Graph Exploration\n(NeurIPS 2019)\nHanjun Dai, Yujia Li, Chenglong Wang, Rishabh Singh, Po-Sen Huang, Pushmeet Kohli.\n[paper]\nKnowing When to Stop: Evaluation and Verification of Conformity to Output-size Specs\n(CVPR 2019)\nChenglong Wang, Rudy Bunel, Krishnamurthy Dvijotham, Po-Sen Huang, Edward Grefenstette, Pushmeet Kohli.\n[paper]\n[poster:pdf]\nSpeeding up Symbolic Reasoning for Relational Queries\n(OOPSLA 2018)\nChenglong Wang, Alvin Cheung, Ras Bodik.\n[paper]\n[slides:pdf]\n[project-site]\nFormalizing Visualization Design Knowledge as Constraints: Actionable and Extensible Models in Draco\n(InfoVis 2018,\nBest Paper\n)\nDominik Moritz, Chenglong Wang, Greg L. Nelson, Halden Lin, Adam M. Smith, Bill Howe, Jeffrey Heer.\n[paper]\n[project-site]\nNatural Language to Structured Query Generation via Meta-Learning\n(NAACL 2018) (short paper)\nPo-Sen Huang, Chenglong Wang, Rishabh Singh, Wen-tau Yih, Xiaodong He.\n[paper]\n[source]\nNL2Bash: A Corpus and Semantic Parser for Natural Language Interface to the Linux Operating System.\n(LREC 2018)\nXi Victoria Lin, Chenglong Wang, Luke Zettlemoyer, Michael D. Ernst.\n[paper]\n[source]\nSynthesizing Highly Expressive SQL Queries from Input-Output Examples\n(PLDI 2017)\nChenglong Wang, Alvin Cheung, Rastislav Bodik.\n[paper]\n[slides:pdf]\n[project-site]\nCosette: An Automated SQL Solver\n(CIDR 2017)\nShumo Chu, Chenglong Wang, Konstantin Weitz, Alvin Cheung.\n[paper]\n[project-site]\nTransforming Programs between APIs with Many-to-Many Mappings\n(ECOOP 2016)\nChenglong Wang, Jiajun Jiang, Jun Li, Yingfei Xiong, Xiangyu Luo, Lu Zhang, Zhenjiang Hu.\n[paper]\n[slides:pdf]\nRandom\nTesting query execution engines with mutations\n(DBTest 2020)\nXinyue Chen, Chenglong Wang, Alvin Cheung.\nExecution-Guided Neural Program Decoding\n(NAMPI 2018)\nChenglong Wang, Po-Sen Huang, Alex Polozov, Marc Brockschmidt, Rishabh Singh.\n[paper]\nDemonstration of the Cosette Automated SQL Prover\n(SIGMOD Demo 2017,\nBest Demo\n)\nShumo Chu, Daniel Li, Chenglong Wang, Alvin Cheung, Dan Suciu.\n[demo]\n[paper]\nInteractive Query Synthesis from Input-Output Examples\n(SIGMOD Demo 2017)\nChenglong Wang, Alvin Cheung, Rastislav Bodik.\n[demo]\n[paper]\nComposable and Hygienic Typed Syntax Macros\n(SAC 2015)\nCyrus Omar, Chenglong Wang, Jonathan Aldrich.\n[paper]\n[slides:pdf]\nSWIN: Towards Type-Safe Java Program Adaptation between APIs\n(PEPM 2015)\nJun Li, Chenglong Wang, Yingfei Xiong, Zhenjiang Hu.\n[paper]\n[tech-report]\nFun\n\"So long as you retain your spirit of exploration, surely you shall find your way out. This I believe.\"   --- Map system\nI enjoy playing piano, climbing and skydiving.\n© Chenglong Wang."
