    "homepage_text": "LI Erran LI's Home Page\nLi Erran Li\nAWS AI, Amazon\nIEEE Fellow and ACM Fellow\nAdjunct Professor\nComputer Science Department\nColumbia University\nIf we knew what it   \nwas we were doing, it would not be called research, would it?\n--Albert  \nEinstein\nResearch\n|\nTeaching\n|\nPublications\n|\nPatents\n|\nProfessional    \n      Activities\nResearch\n[Google\n      Scholar Citations\n]\nComputer Vision, Machine Learning Systems and Algorithms\nGraph Parallel Processing\nNetworking and Communication Systems\nMobile Computing\nProjects\nMachine Learning Systems and Algorithms (Michelangelo[\nBlog\n,\nPaper\n], Robot Driver and Voice Assistant)\nGraph Parallel Processing (\nGraphFrames\nand\nGraphTau)\nMachine Learning and Big Data for Cellular Networks (\nLTE Radio\n      Analytics\nand\nCellIQ\nand\nCellScope)\nCellSDN: Software-Defined Cellular Networks\n      (\nOverview\n,\nPRAN\n,\nSoftRAN\n,\nRadioVisor\n,\nSoftCell\n,\nSoftMoW\n)\nMassive MIMO\n Systems:\nScaling cellular Networks using a Large Number of Antennas\nmobile Cloud Computing:\nCloud Computing for Mobile Applications\nTeaching\nCOMS W4121: Computer Systems for Data Science, Spring 2015, Columbia University\nCOMS\n      E6998: Cellular\n      networks and mobile computing\n(Prior Semesters:\nSpring\n      2012\n,\nFall\n      2012\n,\n      and\nSpring 2013\n),\n      Spring 2014, Columbia University\nCOMS E6998: Software\n      Defined Networking\n(Prior\n      Semesters:\nFall 2013\n), Fall 2014, Columbia University\nTutorial and Talks\nTutorial: 3D Deep Learning and Applications in Autonomous Driving, Nov 2, ICCV 2019\nMachine learning for autonomous driving: Recent advances and future challenges\n, Re-Work Deep Learning Summit, London, Sept 17, 2019\nMachine learning for autonomous driving: Recent advances and future challenges\n, Oreilly Artificial Intelligence\nConference, San Jose, Sept 11, 2019\nInvited Talk: 3D Objection Detection: Recent Advances and Future Directions\n, Tokyo Deep Learning Workshop, RIKEN-AIP, Tokyo, March, 2018\nTutorial: Machine Learning for Autonomous Vehicles, Oreilly Artificial Intelligence\nConference, Beijing, April 2018\nKeynote: Machine Learning for Autonomous Vehicles: Recent Advances and Future Challenges\n, Oreilly Artificial Intelligence Conference, Beijing, April 2018\nTutorial: Machine Learning for Autonomous Vehicles\n, ICML, August 2017 \n(co-taught with Jeff Schneider)\nTutorial: Deep Reinforcement Learning: Foundations, Recent Advances and Frontiers,\nDeep Learning Summer School, Bilbao, Spain, July 2017\nInvited Talk: Deep Reinforcement Learning: Recent Advances and Frontiers, REWORK\nDeep Learning Summit, Boston, May 2017\nInvited Talk: Deep Reinforcement Learning: Recent Advances and Frontiers, Oreilly\nArtificial Intelligence Conference, September, San Francisco, September 2017\nScaling Machine Learning as a Service\n, PAPIs, October 2016, Boston\nProfessional Activities\nIEEE Fellow 2013, ACM Distinguished Scientist 2014 and ACM Fellow 2017\nArea Chair, NeurIPS December 2024\nArea Chair, CVPR June 2024\nTechnical Program Committee, Machine learning and Systems, June 2023\nCo-organizer,\nCVPR Workshop on Autonomous Driving, June 2023\nCo-organizer,\nCVPR Workshop on 3D Vision and Robotics, June 2023\nCo-organizer,\nICML Workshop on Safe Learning for Autonomous Driving (SL4AD), July 2022\nCo-organizer,\nCVPR Workshop on Autonomous Driving, June 2022\nCo-organizer,\nICML Workshop on Human in the Loop Learning, July 2021\nCo-organizer,\nCVPR Workshop on 3D Vision and Robotics, June 2021\nCo-organizer,\nCo-organizer,\nNeurIPS 2019 Workshop on Machine Learning for Autonomous Driving,\nDecember 14, 2019, Vancover, Canada\nCo-organizer,\nICCV 2019 Workshop on Autonomous Driving\n- Beyond Single-Frame Perception, Oct 28, 2019, Seoul, Korea\nCo-organizer,\nCVPR 2019 Workshop on Autonomous Driving\n- Beyond Single-Frame Perception, June 16, 2019, Long Beach, CA\nCo-organizer,\nICML Workshop on AI for Autonomous Driving, June 15, 2019, Long Beach, CA\nCo-organizer,\nNIPS Workshop on Machine Learning for Intelligent Transportation Systems (MLITS), Dec 9, 2018, Montreal, Canada\nCo-organizer,\nFederated AI for Robotics Workshop (FAIR) at ICML, July 15, 2018, Stockholm, Sweden\nCo-organizer,\nNIPS Workshop on Machine Learning for Intelligent Transportation Systems (MLITS), Dec 9, 2017, Long Beach, CA\nCo-organizer,\nNIPS Workshop on Machine Learning Systems, Dec 8, 2017, Long Beach, CA\nCo-organizer,\nICML Workshop on Machine Learning for Autonomous Vehicles (MLAV), August 8, 2017, Sydney, Australia\nCo-organizer,\nNIPS Workshop on Machine Learning for Intelligent Transportation Systems (MLITS), Dec 9, 2016, Barcelona, Spain\nCo-organizer,\nNIPS Workshop on Machine Learning Systems, Dec 10, 2016, Barcelona, Spain\nCo-organizer,\nOpen Networking User Group Research Track, March 13 and 14, 2015\nCo-organizer,\nDIMACS Workshop on Systems and Analytics of Big Data, March 17 and 18, 2014\nTPC\n    co-chair,\nNDSS Workshop on Security of\n    Emerging Networking Technologies (SENT) February 23, 2014\nGeneral Chair,\nACM SIGCOMM\n    Workshop of Software Radio Implementation Forum (SRIF), August 18, 2014\nSteering Committee,\nACM SIGCOMM\n    Workshop of Software Radio Implementation Forum (SRIF), August 12, 2013\nTPC co-chair,\nACM MobiSys Workshop On Cellular\n    Networks: Operations, Challenges, and Future Design (CellNet), June 25, 2013\nCo-organizer,\nDIMACS Workshop on Software Defined Networking, Dec 3 and 4, 2012\nTPC co-chair,\nACM SIGCOMM Workshop On Cellular Networks: Operations, Challenges, and Future Design (CellNet), August 2012\nTPC Co-chair,\nIFIP Networking, May 2012\nVice chair,\nFirst Workshop of Software Radio Implementation Forum (SRIF), Jan 2012\nCo-organizer,\nDIMACS Workshop on Systems and Networking Advances in Cloud Computing, Dec 8 and 9, 2011\nTPC Co-chair,\nThe 1st International Workshop on Mobile Cloud Computing & Services: Social Networks and Beyond (MCS), June 2010\nAssociate Editor, IEEE Transaction on Networking (ToN), 2011-2015\nAssociate Editor, IEEE Transaction on Mobile Computing (TMC),  2011-2015\nAssociate Editor, IEEE Journal on Parallel and Distributed Systems, 2009-2012\nAssociate Editor, Wireless Network (WINET) Journal, 2006-2014\nGuest Editor, JSAC special Issue on\n            Non-Cooperative Issues in Networking, 2007\nLast Modified: Jan 31 12:09:00am PDT 2024"
