    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/wu-gang",
    "homepage_text": "Gang Wu / 吴刚\nGang Wu\n@ Adobe Research\nFollow\nSan Jose, California\nEmail\nResearchGate\nLinkedIn\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nMy name is Gang Wu. I am a\nresearch scientist\nat\nAdobe Research\n. My research spans different machine learning fields including statistical modeling, optimization, deep learning, and generative modeling, with data science applications such as digital marketing, user behavior modeling, recommender systems, and computer vision applications such as image compression, video understanding, etc. Prior to joining Adobe, I worked on probabilistic methods for matrix completion during my PhD in\nElectrical & Computer Engineering Department at Iowa State University\n, advised by\nProf. Ratnesh Kumar\n.\nContact\nEmail: gawu[AT]adobe.com\nBusiness Address: 345 Park Ave, San Jose, CA 95110\nHiring Interns!\nI am continuously looking for outstanding and self-motivated PhD student for research internship positions. Please email me with your CV if interested.\nNews\n11/2021, One paper on “decentralized SGD” accepted to\nAAAI-2022\n.\n10/2021, Our ICCV paper on\nPersonal Video Highlights\nis featured in\nan article\nfrom\nSynced/机器之心\n).\n10/2021, Accepted reviewer invitation for\nKnowledge-Based Systems Journal\n(Impact Factor: 8.038).\n09/2021,\nOne patent\non “human outfits synthesis” published.\n08/2021, Accepted the PC member invitation for\nAAAI-2022\n, and reviewer invitation for\nKnowledge-Based Systems Journal\n(Impact Factor: 8.038).\n08/2021, I gave a keynote talk on “digital marketing automation” in\nKDD-2021\nworkshop\nMachine Learning for Consumers and Markets\n.\n08/2021,\nOne paper\non “higher-order ranking and link prediction” accepted to\nCIKM-2021\n.\n07/2021,\nOne paper\non “video summarization” accepted to\nICCV-2021\n.\n07/2021, Accepted the PC member invitations for\nMMAsia-2021\nand\nCVPR-2022\n.\n06/2021, This summer I will mentor/co-mentor four wonderful PhD students: Yang Li (UNC), Uttaran Bhattacharya (UMD), Weixin Jiang and Aravind Talla (Northwestern Univ).\n04/2021, my last summer intern\nUttaran Bhattacharya\nreceived\nAdobe Research Fellowship for 2021\n.\n04/2021, One patent application filed.\n03/2021, One patent application filed.\n03/2021, Accepted the reviewer invitation from\nAlexandria Engineering Journal\n(Impact Factor: 3.732)\n02/2021, Accepted the reviewer invitation for\nICCV-2021\n.\n01/2021, I will serve as an industry mentor in\nIndustry Mentorship Program\nof UMass Amherst during 2021 Spring.\n12/2020,\nOne paper\non “distributed SGD” accepted to\nSDM-2021\n.\n08/2020, Accepted the PC member invitation for\nAAAI-2021\n.\n08/2020, One patent application filed.\n07/2020, One patent application filed.\n07/2020, Accepted the PC member invitations for\nCVPR-2021\n.\n06/2021, This summer I will mentor/co-mentor two wonderful PhD students: Uttaran Bhattacharya (UMD), Gauri Jagatap (NYU).\n05/2020, One patent application filed.\n05/2020,\nOne paper\non “linear quadratic regulator” accepted to\nICML-2020\n."
  },
