    "homepage_text": "Qi Wang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nQi Wang\nQi(琪) Wang (王)\nPostdoc researcher\nEmail:\nqiwangqi@umich.edu\nLinks:\nCV\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nI am a postdoctoral researcher in the Department of Industrial and Operations Engineering at the\nUniversity of Michigan\n, where I have been working with Professor\nUday V. Shanbhag\nsince January 2025. I earned my Ph.D. from the Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering at\nLehigh University\n, where I was fortunate to be advised by Professor\nFrank E. Curtis\n.\nMy research focuses on\ndesigning, analyzing, and implementing algorithms for solving large-scale nonlinear optimization\nproblems that arise in fields such as machine learning.\nI\nreceived\nmy Master of Science degree in Financial Operation Research from the\nUniversity of Edinburgh\nin the UK\ni\nn\n2016\nand my Bachelor of Economics degree from the\nUniversity of International Business and Economics\ni\nn  China in 20\n15\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Yuhao Zhang": {
