    "homepage_text": "Yutian Chen's Homepage\nYutian Chen\nAbout Me\nResearch\nPublications\nAwards\nLast update:\nNov 7, 2024\nYutian Chen (\néå¾¡å¤©\n)\nStaff Research Scientist\nDeepMind\nE-mail:\nShort Bio\nI earned my B.E. of Electronic Engineering from Tsinghua University in China in June 2007.\n        Then I went to the University of California, Irvine in the United States to pursue a doctoral\n        degree. I received M.S. and Ph.D. of Computer Science in machine learning respectively\n        in December 2009 and June 2013 under the supervision of Prof. Max Welling. After graduation\n        I spent two years in the machine learning group in the University of Cambridge, where I worked\n        with Prof. Zoubin Ghahramani as a research associate (Postdoc) on the topic of scalable\n        Bayesian inference methods. In September 2015 I joined DeepMind as a research scientist."
  },
