    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Personal website of Yichong Xu\ntop of page\n本網站是在 Wix 建立。您也來建立網站吧！\n立即開始\nResearch Scientist, Google DeepMind\nYichong Xu\nYichong Xu （徐一翀）\nI'm a Research Scientist at\nGoogle DeepMind\n, working on the\nGemini Models\n. Prior to that, I had a great time doing research at\nCharacter.AI\nworking on multimodal large language models and chatbots, and at\nAI Cognitive Services Research Group\nin Microsoft working on NLP. I'm broadly interested in deep learning, large language models and their applications, especially with multiple modalities. Previously I have done research on knowledge graphs, commonsense reasoning, statistical machine learning, computer vision and game theory. I got my PhD in Machine Learning at CMU in 2020.\nContact: yichongx [at] google.com\nxuyc11[at] gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\ntwitter\nCV\nGitHub\nREAD MORE\nLet me know if you need referral for Google :)\nNews\n02/2022: We organized a successful\ntutorial on Knowledge+NLP at WSDM 2023\n!\n02/2022: Paper on\nAugmenting Commonsense in V+L models\naccepted to CVPR 2023 as a\nhighlight\n!\n02/2022: Paper on\nExtracting Knowledge from LLMs\naccepted to ICLR 2023.\n10/2022: 4 papers accepted to EMNLP 2022, focusing on knowledge-graph QA, multi-task learning, rule-based semi-supervised learning, and unsupervised summarization.\n09/2022: Paper on\nKnowledge+VQA\naccepted to Neurips 2022.\n05/2022: Organizing a\ntutorial on Knowledge-Augmented Methods\nfor NLP at ACL 2022\n04/2022:\nKEAR paper on human parity on CommonsenseQA\naccepted to IJCAI 2022.\n03/2022: Paper on\nVision-Language Pretraining\naccepted to CVPR 2022.\n02/2022: 4 papers accepted to ACL 2022.\n11/2021: We achieved\nhuman parity\non\nCommonsenseQA\n! Check out our\npaper\n,\nblog\nand\nvideo\n.\n11/2021: Paper on\nLong Dialogue Pretraining\naccepted to AAAI 2021.\n09/2021: Paper on\nGPT-3 Labeling\naccepted to EMNLP Findings 2021.\n05/2021: Two papers on commonsense reasoning accepted to ACL Findings 2021.\nList of Publications\nbottom of page"
  },
