    "homepage_text": "Yuandong Tian's webpage\nYuandong Tian\nCo-founder of a stealth startup\nex-Research Scientist Director in\nMeta AI (FAIR)\nEmail:\nyuandong.tian [at] gmail [dot] com\nBrief Bio\nYuandong Tian is an ex-Research Scientist Director in Meta FAIR. His research direction covers multiple aspects of decision making, including reinforcement learning, planning and efficiency, as well as theoretical understanding of LLMs. He is the project lead for\nOpenGo\nproject, an efficient replicate of AlphaZero that beats professional players with a single GPU during inference, serves as the main mentor of\nStreamingLLM\nand\nGaLore\nthat improve the training and inference of LLM,\nCoconut\nthat explores continuous latent reasoning, and is the first-author recipient of 2021 ICML Outstanding Paper Honorable Mentions\nDirectPred\nand 2013 ICCV Marr Prize Honorable Mentions\nHierarchicalDataDrivenDescent\n, and also received the 2022 CGO Distinguished Paper Award\nCompilerGym\n. He co-leads Llama 4 reasoning during his stay in Meta GenAI. Prior to that, he worked in Google Self-driving Car team in 2013-2014 and received a Ph.D in\nRobotics Institute\n, Carnegie Mellon University in 2013. He has been appointed as area chairs for NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, AAAI, CVPR and AIStats.\nGoogle Scholar\nand\nCV\n.\nBlogpost\nResearch Directions:\nDecision-Making, Optimization, Representation Learning, LLMs\n@tydsh\nNews\n[Jan. 27, 2026]\n6 papers (\nspg\ndeep-conf\ncoconut-dynamics\nSTEM\nMobileLLM-R1\nli2\n) are accepted in ICLR2026!\n[Nov. 05, 2025]\nInvited talk in MIT NLP Group about Provable Scaling Laws (\ncogs\n,\nli2\n). Slides\nhere\n.\n[Oct. 20, 2025]\nInvited talk in\nEllison Institute of Technology Oxford\nabout (\nStreamingLLM\n,\ngalore\n,\ncoconut\n,\ncoconut-theory\n,\ncogs\n,\nli2\n). Slides\nhere\n.\n[Sep. 18, 2025]\n2 papers (\ncoconut-theory\ncogs\n) are accepted in NeurIPS2025!\n[Jul. 07, 2025]\n1 papers (\ncoconut\n) is accepted in COLM2025!\n[May. 01, 2025]\n5 papers (\nToken-Assorted\nGSM-Inf\nAgent-as-a-judge\nWeLore\nAdvPrompter\n) are accepted in ICML2025!\n[Apr. 28, 2025]\nInvited talk in ICLR Workshop\nReasoning and planning for LLMs\nand\nFoundation Models in the Wild\n. Slides\nhere\n.\n[Apr. 27, 2025]\nInvited talk in ICLR Workshop\nLLM Sparsity\n. Slides\nhere\n.\n[Mar. 27, 2025]\nKeynote talk in\nCPAL 2025\nin Stanford. Slides\nhere\n.\n[Jan. 22, 2025]\n6 papers (\nPOWER-DL\nDualformer\nParam-Delta\nMagicPIG\nSpinQuant\nR-Sparse\n) are accepted in ICLR2025!\n[Oct. 28, 2024]\nInvited\nguest lecture\nfor LLM Agents Course (\nCS 194/294-196\n) in UC Berkeley. Slides\nhere\n.\n[Sep. 26, 2024]\n2 papers (\nattn-transfer\nreverse-curse\n) are accepted in NeurIPS2024!\n[Sep. 20, 2024]\n1 papers (\nPerSE\n) is accepted in EMNLP2024!\n[Sep. 20, 2024]\n1 papers (\nTTG\n) is accepted in EMNLP Demo2024!\n[Jul. 27, 2024]\nKeynote in\nTheoretical Foundation for Foundation Models\n(T2FM) workshop in ICML 2024 (\njoma\n,\nGaLore\n,\nscan-snap\n).\nSlides\n.\n[Jul. 09, 2024]\n2 papers (\nSearchFormer\nTriForce\n) are accepted in COLM2024!\n[Jul. 08, 2024]\nGuest lecture in UCLA summer school (remote).\n[May. 23, 2024]\nInvited talk in Cybersecurity CRC and CSIRO's Data61 Australia seminar series.\n[May. 11, 2024]\nInvited\ntalk\nin 2nd Workshop on Mathematical and Empirical Understanding of Foundation Models (ME-FoMo) in ICLR 2024 (\nscan-snap\n,\njoma\n,\nGaLore\n,\nMobileLLM\n).\nSlides\n.\n[May. 11, 2024]\nInvited talk in Generative Models for Decision Making\nGen4DM\nin ICLR 2024 (\nAdvPrompter\n,\nSearchFormer\n,\nSurCo\n,\nLANCER\n,\nGenCo\n).\nSlides\n.\n[May. 01, 2024]\n6 papers (\nTravelPlanner\ngalore\nLoCoCo\nMobileLLM\nConPas\nGenCo\n) are accepted in ICML2024!\n[Apr. 18, 2024]\nGuest lecture in Caltech\nCS 148\n(\nDirectCLR\n,\nalpha-CL\n,\nnonlinear-CL\n,\nDirectPred\n,\nscan-snap\n,\njoma\n).\nSlides\n.\n[Apr. 18, 2024]\nGuest lecture in Caltech\nCS 159\n(\nSearchFormer\n,\nSurCo\n,\nLANCER\n,\nGenCo\n).\nVideo\nSlides\n.\n[Apr. 11, 2024]\nSeminar talk\nin LLMs understanding and applications in Stanford NLP seminar (\njoma\n,\nscan-snap\n,\nStreamingLLM\n,\nGaLore\n,\nMobileLLM\n). Slides\nhere\n.\n[Feb. 06, 2024]\nInvited lecture on understanding LLMs and its applications in UC Berkeley\nCS 194\n(\njoma\n,\nscan-snap\n,\nDejaVu\n,\nH2O\n,\npos-interp\n,\nStreamingLLM\n). Slides\nhere\n.\n[Jan. 16, 2024]\n4 papers (\nStreamingLLM\nRLCD\nH-GAP\njoma\n) are accepted in ICLR2024!\n[Dec. 06, 2023]\nInvited\ntalk\nabout Efficient LLM inference in long context (\nDejaVu\n,\nH2O\n,\npos-interp\n,\nStreamingLLM\n). Slides\nhere\n.\n[Oct. 06, 2023]\nInvited talk in RIKEN AIP, Tokyo, Japan (\njoma\n,\nscan-snap\n,\nDejaVu\n,\nH2O\n,\npos-interp\n,\nStreamingLLM\n). Talk\nhere\n, Slides\nhere\n.\n[Sep. 26, 2023]\nInvited talk in HKU Institution of Data Science (HKU IDS) (\njoma\n,\nscan-snap\n,\nDejaVu\n,\nH2O\n,\npos-interp\n). Talk\nhere\n, Slides\nhere\n.\n[Sep. 21, 2023]\n3 papers (\nH2O\nscan-snap\nLANCER\n) are accepted in NeurIPS2023!\n[May. 02, 2023]\n1 papers (\nDOC\n) is accepted in ACL2023!\n[Apr. 24, 2023]\n4 papers (\nDejaVu\nCL-LNS\nSurCo\nCompilerOpt\n) are accepted in ICML2023!\n[Mar. 02, 2023]\nInvited talk in Microsoft on Long-form Story Generation (\nRe3\n,\nDOC\n). Slides\nhere\n.\n[Feb. 28, 2023]\nInvited talk in\nIPAM\nabout AI-guided optimization (\nSurCo\n,\nCZP\n). Slides\nhere\n.\n[Feb. 17, 2023]\n1 papers (\nNeuroShard\n) is accepted in MLSys2023!\n[Jan. 25, 2023]\n1 papers (\nLB-RELAX\n) is accepted in CPAIOR2023!\n[Jan. 20, 2023]\n3 papers (\nTAP\nnonlinear-CL\nMACTA\n) are accepted in ICLR2023!\n[Oct. 17, 2022]\n1 papers (\nAutoCAT\n) is accepted in HPCA2023!\n[Oct. 06, 2022]\n1 papers (\nRe3\n) is accepted in EMNLP2022!\n[Oct. 03, 2022]\nInvited talk in MIT\nPoggio's lab\nabout recent works on contrastive learning (\nalpha-CL\n,\nnonlinear-CL\n). Slides\nhere\n.\n[Sep. 14, 2022]\n2 papers (\nalpha-CL\nDreamShard\n) are accepted in NeurIPS2022!\n[Sep. 13, 2022]\nCo-organize AAAI'23 workshop \"Reinforcement Learning Ready for Production\".\n[Aug. 21, 2022]\nKeynote\ntalk\nin IEEE Conference on Games.\n[Aug. 04, 2022]\nInvited talk in TTIC workshop on representation learning theory.\nLink\n[Jun. 08, 2022]\nInvited talk in VALSE Webinar about SSL.\n[May. 18, 2022]\n1 papers (\nAutoShard\n) is accepted in KDD2022!\n[May. 15, 2022]\n1 papers (\nDenoisedMDP\n) is accepted in ICML2022!\n[Apr. 28, 2022]\nGuest lecture in Tianqi Chen's group in CMU.\n[Apr. 07, 2022]\nInvited talk in UIUC about representation learning.\n[Mar. 05, 2022]\n1 papers (\nAsym-Siam\n) is accepted in CVPR2022!\n[Jan. 24, 2022]\n3 papers (\nDirectCLR\nNASViT\nLaMOO\n) are accepted in ICLR2022!\n[Nov. 29, 2021]\n1 papers (\nLSTMvsTransformer\n) is accepted in AAAI2022!\n[Nov. 05, 2021]\n1 papers (\nCompilerGym\n) is accepted in CGO2022!\n[Sep. 28, 2021]\n4 papers (\nBeBold\nMADE\nLaP3\nLaSynth\n) are accepted in NeurIPS2021!\n[Jul. 19, 2021]\nOur paper\nDirectPred\ngot\nICML Outstanding Paper Award Honorable Mention\n!\n[Jun. 04, 2021]\nInvited talk in University of Washington\nNeuralAI Lab\nabout\nDirectPred\n. Slides\nhere\n. Thanks Eli Shlizerman for inviting!\n[May. 08, 2021]\n3 papers (\nDirectPred\nFewShotNAS\nLearn2Share\n) are accepted in ICML2021!\n[Apr. 29, 2021]\n1 papers (\nNeuroPlan\n) is accepted in SIGCOMM2021!\n[Apr. 21, 2021]\nInvited talk in VALSE Webinar about understanding self-supervised learning. Slides\nhere\n[Apr. 21, 2021]\nInvited Guest Lecture in UPenn (Thanks\nJing Li\n) for the invitation. Slides\nhere\n.\n[Apr. 12, 2021]\nInvited\nTalk\nin UCL DARK Lab. Slides\nhere\n.\n[Feb. 28, 2021]\n2 papers (\nFBNetV3\nFPNAS\n) are accepted in CVPR2021!\n[Jan. 31, 2021]\nIn\nBlack-box optimization challenge\nof NeurIPS'20, two teams extended our\nLaMCTS\nand won 3rd and 8th place! See their reports (\nJetBrains\n,\nKAIST\n).\n[Jan. 22, 2021]\n1 papers (\nRobustTeacherStudent\n) is accepted in AIStats2021!\n[Dec. 12, 2020]\nInvited\ntalk\nin NeurIPS 2020\nworkshop\nof Learning meets Combinatorial Algorithms.\n[Dec. 12, 2020]\nContributed\ntalk\nin NeurIPS 2020\nworkshop\nof Self-supervised Learning, Theory and Practice.\n[Nov. 30, 2020]\nInvited\ntalk\n(\nSlides\n) at\nWorkshop of Reinforcement Learning from Batch Data and Simulation\nin Simons Institute of UC Berkeley.\n[Oct. 20, 2020]\nInvited Guest\nlecture\nin University of Wisconsin Madison (Class\nsyllabus\n).\n[Oct. 14, 2020]\nDistinguished Guest\nlecture\nin IIIS, Tsinghua University.\n[Jun. 06, 2020]\nInvited guest lecture in UCLA.\n[Nov. 07, 2019]\nInvited\ntalk\nin IAS \"Workshop on New Directions in Reinforcement Learning and Control\" in Princeton University.\n[Nov. 06, 2019]\nInvited\ntalk\nin NEC Laboratories Princeton.\n[Oct. 27, 2019]\nInvited\ntalk\nin AI Sys Workshop in SOSP'19\n[Jun. 03, 2019]\nLong oral\ntalk\nabout\nOpenGo\nin ICML 2019.\n[Jan. 03, 2019]\nTalks in\nDeep Learning Summit\n, AAAI 2019 Workshops (\nReproducible AI\nand\nGame and Environments in Artificial Intelligence\n).\n[Jun. 01, 2018]\nMultiple talks in Stanford, AI NextCon, etc.\nlink\n[Dec. 20, 2017]\nKeynote at Future Leaders of AI Retreat (\nFLAIR\n), Shanghai. Slides\nhere\n.\n[Dec. 06, 2017]\nOral talk about\nELF\nplatform, NIPS 2017, Long Beach. Slides\nlink\n.\n[Nov. 05, 2017]\nDRL and Game Tutorial in AI Frontier, Santa Clara. Slides\nlink\n.\n[Oct. 27, 2017]\nDRL and Game Tutorial in Mountain View, ACMMM 2017. Slides\nlink\n.\n[Aug. 10, 2017]\nPresentation in Video Games and Machine Learning\nVGML\nWorkshop, ICML 2017. Slides\nhere\n. The same talk is also presented in University of Sydney on Aug. 11, hosted by Dong Xu.\n[Jul. 03, 2017]\nOn topic \"AI In Games: Achievements and Challenges\", giving 5 talks in China (CASIA, Tsinghua, Shanghai Tech, Brain-AI workshop and CCF-GAIR 2017) located in Beijing, Shanghai and Shenzhen. Slides\nhere\n.\nAll Publications\nAll Major Publications\nAll First-author Publications\nBlog & Novels\nLLM Reasoning\nLLM Agent\nLLM Efficiency\nLLM Story Generation\nReinforcement Learning and Search\nRepresentation Learning\nML-guided Optimization\nML+Sys\nOther Research Topics\nPhD work\n#llm\n#rl\n#optimization\n#search\n#representation\n#theory\n#planning\n#transformer\n#attention\n#combinatorial\n#ssl\n#mcts\n#nonlinear\n#latent-action\n#teacher-student\nSPG: Sandwiched Policy Gradient for Masked Diffusion Language Models\n[\nlink\n]\nChenyu Wang, Paria Rashidinejad, DiJia Su, Song Jiang, Sid Wang, Siyan Zhao, Cai Zhou, Shannon Zejiang Shen, Feiyu Chen, Tommi Jaakkola, Yuandong Tian, Bo Liu\nICLR 2026\nDeep Think with Confidence\n[\nlink\n] [\nwebsite\n]\nYic...[truncated]"
  },
  "serper::Kaisheng Ma": {
    "homepage": "https://group.iiis.tsinghua.edu.cn/~maks/leader.html",
    "emails": [
      "kaisheng@tsinghua.edu.cn",
      "kaishengthu@163.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "ARChip Lab-About our Leader\nWelcome to ARChip Lab\nEmail: kaishengthu@163.com\nARChip Lab\nHome\nAbout our Lab\nAbout our Leader\nPeople\nResearch Directions\nèæºæ¥å£BCI\nPublications\nProjects\nJoin us\nNews\nAbout our leader\nKaisheng Ma - Principal Investigator\nBe Confident !\nWith My Doctoral Superviser Vijay N.\nSupercomputing Center\nBio:\nKaisheng Ma is a tenured associate professor of computer science in Institute for\nInterdisciplinary Information Sciences\n(IIIS),\nTsinghua University\n. He leads the\nAlgorithms, Architecture and Chipset Lab (ARChip)\n. His research interests lie in the interdisciplinary fields of human-machine interface (HMI), brain-spired AI algorithm design, computer vision for self-driving, compact model design, computer architecture and microelectronics. He believes in vertical integration for systems, with a special emphasis on implanted medical and neural devices, and chip level system solutions for self-driving systems. He publishes papers on conferences including NeurIPS, ICCV, AAAI, CVPR, ISCA, ASPLOS, MICRO, HPCA, DAC etc.\nHe received his Ph.D. in Computer Science and Engineering at the Pennsylvania State University, following Professor\nVijaykrishnan Nanrayanan\n@ Penn State,\nYuan Xie\n@ UCSB (Now at Alibaba\nDAMO Computing Lab\n),\nJack Sampson\n@ Penn State. His previous research on Nonvolatile Processor and Energy Harvesting won\n2018 EDAA Best Dissertation Award\n(\nPenn State News\n).\nTalks:\nTitle: Knowledge Self-distillation and Scalable Neural Networks: Towards Accurate, Efficient and Robust Neural Networks\nTitle: Sparse-aware DNN Architecture Design: Insights from Resource Utilization and Memory Bandwidth\nNews:\n[Springer Book Chapter] Kaisheng Ma, Shuangchen Li, Vijaykrishnan Narayanan, and Yuan Xie. \"Nonvolatile Processor Architecture Exploration for Energy-Harvesting Application Scenarios\". In Embedded, Cyber-Physical, and IoT Systems, pp. 175-202. Springer, Cham, 2020. is awarded as\ntop one percent high-impact publications in Springer Nature Research Highlights from China Collection Award 2020.\n(\"Top one percent highly cited papers in their academic fields as of July/August 2020, according to Essential Science Indicators, and highly downloaded, cited and mentioned book chapters, according to SN Insights\".)\nContact information:\nEmail: kaishengthu@163.com | kaisheng@tsinghua.edu.cn\nOffice: Tsinghua University, Beijing, China.\nÂ© Copyright  2020  ARChip Lab  -  All rights reserved"
  },
