    "homepage_text": "Jiuxiang Gu\nSenior Research Scientist\nAdobe Research\nSeattle, WA\nMy name is Jiuxiang Gu (顾久祥). I am a Senior Research Scientist at\nAdobe Research\nin Seattle. I received my Ph.D. from\nNanyang Technological University\n, Singapore (2016.1–2019.5), under the supervision of\nProf. Jianfei Cai\n,\nDr. Gang Wang\n, and\nProf. Tsuhan Chen\n. I currently serve as an\nArea Chair\nfor\nICLR 2025\nand\nWACV 2024/2025\n, a\nSenior Program Committee Member\nfor\nIJCAI 2021–2024\n, and a\nProgram Committee Member\nfor\nAAAI 2021–2023\n,\nNAACL 2021\n, and others. My research journey began in hardware design. From 2010 to 2015, I worked as an ASIC design engineer. In 2015, I made the transition to Artificial Intelligence. My current research interests include:\nMultimodal Foundation Models\n(LLM, MLLM, Diffusion LLM/MLLM, Text-to-Image/Video/3D Generation, Document Intelligence)\nEfficient Architecture & Scaling\n(Pruning, Quantization, KV Cache Optimization, Edge Deployment)\nReasoning & Alignment\n(Chain-of-Thought, Hidden Thinking, Self-supervised Learning, Post-training)\nImpact & Production\n: Contribute to Adobe Firefly and Acrobat AI Assistant\nOpen to\ncollaborations and internships\nin the above areas.\n📧 Feel free to reach out:\njigu@adobe.com\n/\ngu.jiuxiang@gmail.com\nSelected Publications\n2026\nCVPR 2026\nSparse-LaViDa: Sparse Multimodal Discrete Diffusion Language Models\nShufan\n            Li, Jiuxiang\n            Gu, Kangning\n            Liu, and\n4 more authors\nICLR 2026\nLaViDa-O: Elastic Large Masked Diffusion Models for Unified Multimodal Understanding and Generation\nShufan\n            Li, Jiuxiang\n            Gu, Kangning\n            Liu, and\n4 more authors\n2025\nAAAI 2025\nNumerical pruning for efficient autoregressive models\nXuan\n            Shen, Zhao\n            Song, Yufa\n            Zhou, and\n12 more authors\n2024\nICLR 2024\nOral\nLrm: Large reconstruction model for single image to 3d\nYicong\n            Hong, Kai\n            Zhang, Jiuxiang\n            Gu, and\n7 more authors\nICLR 2024\nADoPD: A large-scale document page decomposition dataset\nJiuxiang\n            Gu,\nXiangxi\n              Shi\n, Jason\n            Kuen, and\n5 more authors\n2021\nNeurIPS 2021\nUnidoc: Unified pretraining framework for document understanding\nJiuxiang\n            Gu, Jason\n            Kuen, Vlad I\n            Morariu, and\n5 more authors\n2018\nAAAI 2018\nOral\nStack-Captioning: Coarse-to-Fine Learning for Image Captioning\nJiuxiang\n            Gu,\nJianfei\n              Cai\n,\nGang\n              Wang\n, and\n1 more author\nCVPR 2018\nSpotlight\nLook, Imagine and Match: Improving Textual-Visual Cross-Modal Retrieval with Generative Models\nJiuxiang\n            Gu,\nJianfei\n              Cai\n,\nShafiq\n              Joty\n, and\n2 more authors\nPattern Recognition, 2018\nRecent advances in convolutional neural networks\nJiuxiang\n            Gu, Zhenhua\n            Wang, Jason\n            Kuen, and\n8 more authors\nFeel free to reach out via email or social media.\nPublications by Year\n2026\n(9)\n▼\nICLR 2026\nFastCar: Cache Attentive Replay for Fast Auto-Regres...\nAAAI 2026\nOIDA-QA: A Multimodal Benchmark for Analyzing the Op...\nCVPR 2026\nDiffGraph: An Automated Agent-driven Model Merging F...\nCVPR 2026\nSparse-LaViDa: Sparse Multimodal Discrete Diffusion ...\narXiv preprint arXiv:2602.14147 2026\nLaViDa-R1: Advancing Reasoning for Unified Multimoda...\nText rendering for image generation models\nGenerating 3D models from a single image\narXiv preprint arXiv:2601.04589 2026\nMiLDEdit: Reasoning-Based Multi-Layer Design Documen...\nICLR 2026\nLaViDa-O: Elastic Large Masked Diffusion Models for ...\n2025\n(35)\n▼\nEMNLP 2025\nCommit: Coordinated instruction tuning for multimoda...\nEfficient vision-language retrieval using structural...\nGenerating temporal dependency graphs\nWACV 2025\nARTIST: Improving the Generation of Text-rich Images...\nWACV 2025\nDifferential privacy mechanisms in neural tangent ke...\nSubmitted to ACL 2025\nA multi-llm debiasing framework\nICLR 2025\nImagefolder: Autoregressive image generation with fo...\nICLR 2025\nLoRA-Contextualizing Adaptation of Large Multimodal ...\nTMLR 2025\nPersonalization of large language models: A survey\nAAAI 2025\nNumerical pruning for efficient autoregressive models\nAAAI 2025\nLazyDiT: Lazy Learning for the Acceleration of Diffu...\nCVPR 2025\nMegaSynth: Scaling Up 3D Scene Reconstruction with S...\nICCV 2025\nRefer to Anything with Vision-Language Prompts\nICCV 2025\nDiffIP: Representation Fingerprints for Robust IP Pr...\nICCV 2025\nMultimodal LLMs as Customized Reward Models for Text...\narXiv preprint arXiv:2501.19201 2025\nEfficient Reasoning with Hidden Thinking\nACL 2025\nFrom Selection to Generation: A Survey of LLM-based ...\nSubmitted to NeurIPS 2025\nEfficient Reasoning with Hidden Thinking\nSubmitted to NeurIPS 2025\nADOPT: A Multimodal Framework for Document Understan...\nSubmitted to NeurIPS 2025\nDraftAttention: Fast Video Diffusion via Low-Resolut...\nSubmitted to NeurIPS 2025\nMENTOR: Efficient Multimodal-Conditioned Tuning for ...\nTMLR 2025\nFrom Preferences to Prejudice: The Role of Alignment...\nNeurIPS 2025\nR-KV: Redundancy-aware KV Cache Compression for Reas...\nSubmitted to NeurIPS 2025\nADOPD-Instruct: A Large-Scale Multimodal Dataset for...\nACL 2025\nMetal: A multi-agent framework for chart generation ...\nUtilizing a generative neural network to interactive...\nSubmitted to ICCV 2025\nRobust Latent Matters: Boosting Image Generation wit...\nGenerating 3d models from a single image\nPosition-based text-to-speech model\nCVPR 2025\nQuartDepth: Post-Training Quantization for Real-Time...\nGenerating an improved named entity recognition mode...\nSubmitted to COLM 2025\nTowards Visual Text Grounding of Multimodal Large La...\nUnified pretraining framework for document understan...\narXiv preprint arXiv:2512.14691 2025\nMMGR: Multi-Modal Genera