    "homepage_text": "Jian Peng - Helmholtz-Centre for Environmental Research\nDE\nEN\nToggle navigation\nHome\nUFZ\nResearch\nInfrastructures\nTransfer\nMedia & Press\nEvents\nCareer & Jobs\nImprint\nData Privacy\nDirect Links\nLeipziger KUBUS\nOrganisation structure\nLibrary\nGraduate School HIGRADE\nInternational Office\nFamily Support Office\nsick note notification\nUFZ Teaching Lab\nImprint\nData Privacy\nDirect Links\nLeipziger KUBUS\nOrganisation structure\nLibrary\nGraduate School HIGRADE\nInternational Office\nFamily Support Office\nsick note notification\nUFZ Teaching Lab\nDE\nEN\nResearch\nSmart Models / Monitoring\nRemote Sensing\nTeam\nJian Peng\nProf. Dr. Jian Peng\nHelmholtz Centre for Environmental Research (UFZ)\nHead of Department of Remote Sensing (RS)\nPermoserstr. 15, 04318 Leipzig\nTel.:   ++49 341 6025 482335\nemail:\njian.peng@ufz.de\nUniversity of Leipzig\nFull professor for Hydrology and Remote Sensing\nCareer details\n2020-present\nHead of Remote Sensing Department\nHelmholtz Centre for Environmental Research – UFZ\n2020-present\nW3 Professor for Hydrology and Remote Sensing\nLeipzig University\n2020-present\nEditor-in-Chief\nGeoscience Data Journal\nRoyal Meteorological Society\n2018-2020\nSenior researcher\nUniversity of Oxford\n2018-2020\nPostgraduate Certificate in Teaching and Learning in Higher Education\nUniversity of Oxford\n2015-2017\nResearch scientist\nUniversity of Munich\n2013-2015\nPost-Doc\nMax Planck Institute for Meteorology\n2010-2013\nPhD in Earth science\nMax Planck Institute for Meteorology\nResearch interests\nHydrology and the atmospheric environment\nSatellite remote sensing\nProcess-based modeling and data-driven methods\nClimate extremes and climate variability\nImpact and outreach\n“2019 Remote sensing Young Investigator Award, MDPI”\nhttps://www.mdpi.com/journal/remotesensing/awards.pdf....\n“In the spotlight – promising future leaders in climate science”\nWorld Climate Research Programme (WCRP)\nhttps://www.wcrp-climate.org/future-science-leadership/spotlight-on-early-career-researchers?view=article&id=1074&catid=23\n“Seeing Soil Moisture from the Sky”\nEOS BUZZ news & EOS Editors’ Vox\nhttps://eos.org/editors-vox/seeing-soil-moisture-from-the-sky\n“Research Collaboration Results In Publication Of High-Resolution Dataset For Drought Monitoring”\nNASA Harvest\nhttps://nasaharvest.org/news/research-collaboration-results-publication-high-resolution-dataset-drought-monitoring\n“UFZ Earth Observation Scientist Prof. Dr. Jian Peng in portrait”\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dnn5zLfIwYA\nPublications\nIndex:\n2026 (2)\n2025 (21)\n2024 (28)\n2023 (23)\n2022 (18)\n2021 (11)\nYou could use our\npublication index\nfor further requests.\n2026 (2)\nGarcía-García, A., Stradiotti, P., Di Paolo, F., Filippucci, P., Fischer, M., Orság, M., Brocca, L.,\nPeng, J.\n, Dorigo, W., Gruber, A., Droppers, B., Wanders, N., Haag, A., Weerts, A., Modiri, E., Rakovec, O., Francés, F., Dall’Amico, M., Anderson, M., Hain, C., Samaniego, L. (2026):\nIntercomparison of Earth Observation products for hyper-resolution hydrological modelling over Europe\nRemote Sens. Environ.\n333\n, art. 115131\n10.1016/j.rse.2025.115131\nLi, S., Wang, G., Sun, S., Chen, Z., Mura, M., Lu, J., Liu, Q., Li, J., Hagan, D.F.T., García-García, A.,\nPeng, J.\n(2026):\nObserved declining strength of vegetation-atmosphere coupling\nAgric. For. Meteorol.\n379\n, art. 111051\n10.1016/j.agrformet.2026.111051\nto index\n2025 (21)\nChen, D., Fan, L.,\nPeng, J.\n, De Lannoy, G., Wigneron, J.-P., Frappart, F., Tao, S., Wang, M., Li, X., Liu, X., Wang, H., Yuan, Q., Chen, X., Xiao, Y., Ciais, P. (2025):\nA global long-term (2002–2022) C-band vegetation optical depth record retrieved after merging AMSR-E, AMSR2 and WindSat (Version 1) [Data set]\nZenodo\n10.5281/zenodo.17359730\nChen, D., Fan, L.,\nPeng, J.\n, De Lannoy, G., Wigneron, J.-P., Frappart, F., Tao, S., Wang, M., Li, X., Liu, X., Wang, H., Yuan, Q., Chen, X., Xiao, Y., Ciais, 