    "homepage_text": "Szu-Wei Fu's Web\nHOME\nABOUT ME\nNEWS\nPUBLICATIONs\nCONTACT ME\nSzu-Wei Fu\nMake everything as simple as possible, but not simpler\nMeteora!      This picture was taken in Greece when I attended SLT, 2018.\nAbout Me\nI received my Ph.D. from the CS department at National Taiwan University in 2020, under the advisement of  Prof.\nShou-De Lin.\nand Dr.\nYu Tsao.\nMy research interests include:\nMachine Learning\n,\nDeep learning\n,\nSpeech enhancement\nand\nprocessing\n.\nNews (Last Update:2021/06)\n2021/06:   Join Microsoft as data and applied scientist!\n2021/06:   Two papers are accepted in\nInterspeech 2021\n(\nMetricGAN+\nand\nPhone-Fortified Perceptual Loss\n)\n2020/05:   Join the\nSpeechBrain\nproject at Mila, Canada. Advisor:  Prof.\nYoshua Bengio\nand Dr.\nMirco Ravanelli\n2020/01:   Successfully defense my Ph.D. thesis\n2020/01:   One paper is accepted in\nIEEE/ACM TASLP 2020\n2019/11:   Two papers are accepted in\nIEEE Signal Processing Letters (SPL) 2019\n2019/07:   Start my Research Intern at\nStarkey Hearing Technologies\n, MN, USA. Advisor:  Dr.\nZhang Tao\n2019/07:   Three papers are accepted in\nInterspeech 2019\n2019/05:   One paper is accepted in\nICML 2019 (with Travel Awards)\n2018/09:   One paper is accepted in\nSLT 2018\n2018/06:   One paper is accepted in\nInterspeech 2018 (with Travel Grants)\n2018/03:   One paper is accepted in\nIEEE/ACM TASLP\n2017/10:   One paper is accepted in\nIEEE APSIPA 2017\n2017/08:   One paper is accepted in\nIEEE MLSP\n2016/12:   One paper is accepted in\nIEEE TBME\n2016/10:   Start my Research Intern at\nNICT\n, Kyoto, Japan. Advisor:  Dr.\nXugang Lu\n2016/06:   One paper is accepted in\nInterspeech 2016\n2016/03:   One paper is accepted in\nEntropy\nRecent Publications\nFor a complete  publication list, please see my\nCV\nMetricGAN: Generative Adversarial Networks based Black-box Metric Scores Optimization for Speech Enhancement\nICML\n, 2019 (with Travel Awards)\npaper\ncode\nLearning with Learned Loss Function: Speech Enhancement with Quality-Net to Improve Perceptual Evaluation of Speech Quality\nIEEE Signal Processing Letters (SPL)\n, 2019\npaper\nQuality-Net: An End-to-End Non-intrusive Speech Quality Assessment Model based on BLSTM\nInterspeech\n, 2018 (with Travel Grants)\npaper\ncode\nEnd-to-End Waveform Utterance Enhancement for Direct Evaluation Metrics Optimization by Fully Convolutional Neural Networks\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing\n, 2018\npaper\ncode\nRaw Waveform-based Speech Enhancement by Fully Convolutional Networks\nIEEE APSIPA\n, 2017\npaper\nComplex Spectrogram Enhancement by Convolutional Neural Network with Multi-Metrics Learning\nIEEE International Workshop on Machine Learning for Signal Processing\n, 2017\npaper\nJoint Dictionary Learning-based Non-Negative Matrix Factorization for Voice Conversion to Improve Speech Intelligibility After Oral Surgery\nIEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering\n, 2016\npaper\ncode\nSNR-Aware Convolutional Neural Network Modeling for Speech Enhancement\nInterspeech\n, 2016\npaper\nContact me:\nIf you are interested in my research, please contact me."
