    "homepage_text": "Publications – Bao Lab\nJoin us\nHome\nPublications\nClick here to visit Dr. Gang Bao's Google Scholar Citation Page for our recent publications.\nTITLE\nYEAR\nDetection and quantification of unintended large on-target gene modifications due to CRISPR/Cas9 editing\nSH Park, M Cao, G Bao\nCurrent Opinion in Biomedical Engineering, 100478\n2023\nHigh levels of lipoprotein (a) in transgenic mice exacerbate atherosclerosis and promote vulnerable plaque features in a sex-specific manner\nJM Assini, JR Clark, A Youssef, C Xing, AM Doerfler, SH Park, L Saxena, …\nAtherosclerosis\n2023\nCAGE sequencing reveals CFTR-dependent dysregulation of type I IFN signaling in activated cystic fibrosis macrophages\nJL Gillan, M Chokshi, GR Hardisty, S Clohisey Hendry, …\nScience Advances 9 (21), eadg5128\n2023\nForce-Mediated Endocytosis of Iron Oxide Nanoparticles for Magnetic Targeting of Stem Cells\nL Zhang, S Hajebrahimi, S Tong, X Gao, H Cheng, Q Zhang, DT Hinojosa, …\nACS Applied Materials & Interfaces\n2023\nIn vivo expansion of gene-targeted hepatocytes through transient inhibition of an essential gene\nM De Giorgi, SH Park, A Castoreno, M Cao, A Hurley, L Saxena, …\nbioRxiv, 2023.07. 26.550728\n2023\nTargeted replacement of full-length CFTR in human airway stem cells by CRISPR-Cas9 for pan-mutation correction in the endogenous locus\nS Vaidyanathan, R Baik, L Chen, DT Bravo, CJ Suarez, SM Abazari, …\nMolecular Therapy 30 (1), 223-237\n2022\nComprehensive analysis and accurate quantification of unintended large gene modifications induced by CRISPR-Cas9 gene editing\nSH Park, M Cao, Y Pan, TH Davis, L Saxena, H Deshmukh, Y Fu, …\nScience Advances 8 (42), eabo7676\n2022\nMultiplexed high-throughput localized electroporation workflow with deep learning–based analysis for cell engineering\nCA Patino, N Pathak, P Mukherjee, SH Park, G Bao, HD Espinosa\nScience Advances 8 (29), eabn7637\n2022\nMultichannel power electronics and magnetic nanoparticles for selective thermal magnetogenetics\nB Wang, Z Li, C Sebesta, DT Hinojosa, Q Zhang, JT Robinson, G Bao, …\nJournal of Neural Engineering 19 (2), 026015\n2022\nSubsecond multichannel magnetic control of select neural circuits in freely moving flies\nC Sebesta, D Torres Hinojosa, B Wang, J Asfouri, Z Li, G Duret, K Jiang, …\nNature Materials 21 (8), 951-958\n2022\nSynthesis and application of magnetic nanocrystal clusters\nZ Xiao, L Zhang, VL Colvin, Q Zhang, G Bao\nIndustrial & Engineering Chemistry Research 61 (22), 7613-7625\n2022\nIntegrating micro and nano technologies for cell engineering and analysis: toward the next generation of cell therapy workflows\nP Mukherjee, SH Park, N Pathak, CA Patino, G Bao, HD Espinosa\nACS nano 16 (10), 15653-15680\n2022\nLPA disruption with AAV-CRISPR potently lowers plasma apo (a) in transgenic mouse model: A proof-of-concept study\nAM Doerfler, SH Park, JM Assini, A Youssef, L Saxena, AB Yaseen, …\nMolecular Therapy-Methods & Clinical Development 27, 337-351\n2022\nMultifunctional Magnetic Nanoclusters Can Induce Immunogenic Cell Death and Suppress Tumor Recurrence and Metastasis\nL Zhang, Q Zhang, DT Hinojosa, K Jiang, QK Pham, Z Xiao, VL Colvin, …\nACS nano 16 (11), 18538-18554\n2022\nCharacterization of Hemoglobin Variants Due to in-Frame Deletions in the β-Globin Gene from CRISPR/Cas9 Gene Correction for Sickle Cell Disease\nAA Pendergast, SH Park, LA Binns, CK Kanne, C Karsenty, …\nBlood 140 (Supplement 1), 7793-7794\n2022\nFluorescent Tagging of Endogenous Beta-Globin Gene in S-HUDEP2 Cell Model for Live Cell Monitoring of Beta-Globin Expression and Regulation\nC Karsenty, SHJ Park, G Bao\nBlood 140 (Supplement 1), 12978-12979\n2022\nIntegrated microheater array for efficient and localized heating of magnetic nanoparticles at microwave frequencies\nY Fan, Q Zhang, L Zhang, G Bao, CHI Taiyun\nUS Patent App. 17/650,982\n2022\nIdentification and Validation of CRISPR/Cas9 Off-Target Activity in Hematopoietic Stem and Progenitor Cells\