    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nhomepage\nWelcome to Tianyu Wang's homepage\nContact\nTianyu Wang\nGraduate Teaching Associate\nOffice 222, Math Tower\nDepartment of Mathematics\nOhio State University\nEmail:\nwang.7828@osu.edu\nAbout me\nI am a graduate student in OSU's math department. My advisor is\nDan Thompson\n.\nMy main research interest is thermodynamic formalism of non-uniformly hyperbolic systems. I am also interested in other general dynamics-related probability and dimension theory.\nMy CV can be found\nhere\n.\nI will be graduating in SP 2021.\nPreprints and Publications\n[pdf]\nUnique equilibrium states, Large deviations and Lyapunov spectra for the Katok map, ETDS 2020\n[pdf]\nFluctuations of time averages along closed geodesics in non-positive curvature, with Dan Thompson,\nUndergoing Revision for Communications in Mathematical Physics.\n[pdf]\nMultifractal analysis of geodesic flow on surface with no focal points, with Kiho Park\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Yanqiu Wu": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/nyu.edu/yanqiu-autumn-wu/home",
    "emails": [
      "yanqiu.wu@nyu.edu",
      "yanqiu.wu@mq.edu.au"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "YW\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYW\nYanqiu (Autumn)\nWu\nBiography\nI am Yanqiu (Autumn) Wu, currently employed as a Lecturer in Artificial Intelligence at Macquarie University, School of Computing. From October 2022 to January 2024, I was a CSIRO Early Research Career (CERC) Post-doctoral Fellow in the Distributed Systems Security group, Data61, CSIRO. My current research interests are in the fields of Quantum Machine Learning and Deep Reinforcement Learning. In September 2022, I completed my doctoral degree in Computer Science from New York University (NYU) under the guidance of Professor\nKeith W. Ross\n. During my PhD studies, I worked in the area of deep reinforcement learning. Prior to that, I received my B.S. degree from New York University Shanghai.\nContacts\nyanqiu.wu@mq.edu.au\nyanqiu.wu@nyu.edu\nPublications\nPhD Thesis\nYanqiu Wu.\nImproving Sample Efficiency in Off-policy and Offline Deep Reinforcement Learning\n. NYU\nConferences\nYanqiu Wu\n, Xinyue Chen, Che Wang, Yiming Zhang, Zijian Zhou, Keith Ross.\nAggressive Q-Learning with Ensembles: Achieving Both High Sample Efficiency and High Asymptotic Performance\n.\n36th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems Deep Reinforcement Learning Workshop (NeurIPS) 2022\nChe Wang*,\nYanqiu Wu*\n, Quan Vuong, Keith Ross.\nStriving for Simplicity and Performance in Off-Policy DRL: Output Normalization and Non-Uniform Sampling\n.\nProceedings of the 37th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) 2020\n*Equal Contribution\nXinyue Chen, Zijian Zhou, Zheng Wang, Che Wang,\nYanqiu Wu\n, Qing Deng, and Keith W. Ross.\nBAIL: Best-Action Imitation Learning for Batch Deep Reinforcement Learning\n.\n34th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2020\nMinhui Xue, Cameron Ballard, Kelvin Liu, Carson Nemelka,\nYanqiu Wu\n, Keith W. Ross, Haifeng Qian.\nYou Can Yak But You Can’t Hide: Localizing Anonymous Social Network Users\n.\nProceedings of the 2016 Internet Measurement Conference (2016)\nJournals\nYanqiu Wu\n, Qingyang Li, Zhiwei Qin.\nSpatio-temporal Incentives Optimization for Ride-hailing Services with Offline Deep Reinforcement Learning.\nComputing Research Repository (CoRR) 2022\nYanqiu Wu\n, Tehila Minkus, and Keith W. Ross.\nTakg the Pulse of US College Campuses with LocationBased Anonymous Mobile Apps\n.\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology (2017)\nAcademic Service\nProgram Committee\nThe inaugural AsiaCCS 2023 Workshop on Secure and Trustworthy Deep Learning Systems (SecTL 2023)\nReviewer\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\nThe International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\nThe International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\nThe International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI)\nACM SIGKDD International Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD)\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Quan Vuong": {
