    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nQuang Vuong\nProfessor of Economics, New York University\nQuang Vuong is a Professor of Economics at New York University. His area of expertise is econometrics. He is most well known for his research on model selection with the Vuong test. This test is extensively used in social sciences, sciences and business.  He developed pioneering econometric methods to estimate game theoretic models with complete and incomplete information. He is the recipient of several grants from the National Science Foundation and has published in leading economic journals such as Econometrica, Journal of Political Economy and Review of Economic Studies. He is a Fellow of the Econometric Society.\nCV\nand\nGoogle Scholar page\nEmail:\nqvuong(at)nyu(dot)edu\nAddress:\nDepartment of Economics, New York Unviversity\n19 W 4th St, 6FL New York NY 10012  United States\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Hao Wu": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/haowu/home",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nHao WU\nPostdoc\nCheriton School of Computer Science\nThe University of Waterloo\nBiography\nI am a William T. Tutte Postdoctoral Fellow at the University of Waterloo, hosted by\nFlorian Kerschbaum\n. Prior to this, I was a Postdoctoral Fellow at the University of Copenhagen, supported by the Providentia project and affiliated with Basic Algorithms Research Copenhagen (BARC), hosted by\nRasmus Pagh\n. I completed my PhD at the University of Melbourne, advised by\nAnthony Wirth\nand\nOlga Ohrimenko\n.\nResearch Interests\nMy research focuses on sketching, graph, and differentially private algorithms, with an emphasis on designing practical solutions backed by rigorous mathematical guarantees. Currently, I am integrating differentially private algorithms with cryptographic security mechanisms to develop secure distributed systems.\nSelected\nPublications\n[\nPODS\n]\nOptimal Pure Differentially Private Sparse Histograms in Deterministic Linear Time\nFlorian Kerschbaum, Steven Lee,\nHao WU\n(\nalpha\norder)\nIn ACM Symposium on Principles of Database Systems\n, 202\n6\n[\nICML\n]\nImproved Approximations for Hard Graph Problems using Predictions\nAnders Aamand, Justin Y. Chen, Siddharth Gollapudi, Sandeep Silwal,\nHao WU\n(\nalpha\norder)\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning, 2025\n[\nPODS\n]\nOptimal Bounds for Private Minimum Spanning Trees via Input Perturbation\nRasmus Pagh, Lukas Retschmeier,\nHao WU\n, Hanwen Zhang\n(\nalpha\norder)\nIn ACM Symposium on Principles of Database Systems\n, 202\n5\n[ICLR,\nSpotlight\n]\nLearning-Augmented Frequent Directions\nAnders Aamand, Justin Y. Chen, Siddharth Gollapudi, Sandeep Silwal,\nHao WU\n(\nalpha\norder)\nIn International Conference on Learning Representations, 2025\n[NeurIPS]\nFaster Differentially Private Top-\nk\nSelection: A Joint Exponential Mechanism with Pruning\nHao WU\n, Hanwen Zhang\n(\nalpha\norder)\nIn\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n, 2024\n[ICML]\nProfile Reconstruction from Private Sketches\nHao WU\n, Rasmus Pagh\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning\n, 2024\n[ICML,\nOral\n]\nTight Data Access Bounds for Private Top-k Selection\nHao WU\n, Olga Ohrimenko, Anthony Wirth\nIn\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning\n,\nOral,\n202\n3\n[PODS]\nRandomize the Future: Asymptotically Optimal Locally Private Frequency Estimation Protocol for Longitudinal Data\nOlga Ohrimenko, Anthony Wirth,\nHao WU\n(\nalpha\norder)\nIn\nACM Symposium on Principles of Database Systems\n, 2022\n[AISTATS]\nAsymptotically Optimal Locally Private Heavy Hitters via Parameterized Sketches\nHao WU\n, Anthony Wirth\nIn International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics,\n2022\n[SIGMOD]\nUnifying the Global and Local Approaches: An Eﬀicient Power Iteration with Forward Push\nHao WU\n, Junhao Gan, Zhewei Wei, Rui Zhang\nIn International Conference on Management of Data,\n2021\nMore information about publications can be found on my\nCV\n,\nGoogle Scholar\nand\nDBLP\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
