  "serper::Fengbo Ren": {
    "homepage": "https://search.asu.edu/profile/2436287",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/fengbo-ren-b8062312",
    "homepage_text": "Fengbo Ren | ASU Search\nFengbo Ren\nAdjunct Faculty\n[email protected]\nPhone:\n480-727-5793\n‌\n699 S. Mill Ave # 553 P.O. Box 878809\nTempe, AZ 85281\n‌\n‌\nLong Bio\nFengbo Ren received a bachelor's degree in electrical engineering from Zhejiang University in 2008, and his master's and doctoral degrees in electrical engineering from the University of California, Los Angeles, in 2010 and 2014, respectively.\nHe is an Associate Professor in the School of Computing and Augmented Intelligence at Arizona State University. He is directing the Parallel Systems and Computing Laboratory (PSCLab), and he is affiliated with the NSF Industry/University Cooperative Research Center for Embedded Systems. His current research interests are focused on algorithm, hardware, and system innovations for data analytics and information processing, with emphasis on bringing energy efficiency and data intelligence into a wide spectrum of today’s computing infrastructures, from data center server systems to wearable and Internet-of-things devices. He is a senior member of both IEEE and ACM. He is a member of the Digital Signal Processing Technical Committee and VLSI Systems & Applications Technical Committee of the IEEE Circuits and Systems Society.\nRen received the Broadcom Fellowship in 2012, the prestigious National Science Foundation (NSF) Faculty Early Career Development (CAREER) Award in 2017, the Google Faculty Research Award in 2018. He also received the Top 5 percent Best Teacher Awards from the Fulton Schools of Engineering at ASU in 2017, 2018, and 2019.\nEducation\nPh.D. Electrical Engineering, University of California, Los Angeles 2015\nM.S. Electrical Engineering, University of California, Los Angeles 2010\nB.Eng. Electrical Engineering, Zhejiang University, China 2008\nResearch Website URL\nhttp://ren-fengbo.lab.asu.edu/\nGoogle Scholar URL\nhttps://scholar.google.com/citations?user=f-wp99AAAAAJ&hl=en\nExperts.asu.edu URL\nhttps://asu.pure.elsevier.com/en/persons/fengbo-ren\nResearch Interests\nHardware acceleration, embedded, reconfigurable, and parallel computing solutions for data analytics and information processing, energy-efficient computing, data-driven compressive sensing, hardware-friendly machine learning.\nTeaching Website URL\nhttps://ren-fengbo.lab.asu.edu/content/teaching\nCourses\n2024 Fall\nCourse Number\nCourse Title\nCSE 492\nHonors Directed Study\nCSE 792\nResearch\nCSE 795\nContinuing Registration\nCSE 799\nDissertation\nCEN 799\nDissertation\nCEN 795\nContinuing Registration\n2024 Summer\nCourse Number\nCourse Title\nCSE 795\nContinuing Registration\nCSE 584\nInternship\nCEN 584\nInternship\nCEN 795\nContinuing Registration\n2024 Spring\nCourse Number\nCourse Title\nCSE 792\nResearch\nCSE 795\nContinuing Registration\nCSE 799\nDissertation\nCSE 790\nReading and Conference\nCSE 584\nInternship\nCEN 790\nReading and Conference\nCEN 599\nThesis\nCEN 580\nPracticum\nCSE 580\nPracticum\nCSE 580\nPracticum\nCEN 792\nResearch\nCEN 799\nDissertation\nCEN 590\nReading and Conference\nCEN 795\nContinuing Registration\n2023 Fall\nCourse Number\nCourse Title\nCSE 492\nHonors Directed Study\nCSE 792\nResearch\nCSE 795\nContinuing Registration\nCSE 799\nDissertation\nCSE 580\nPracticum\nCSE 790\nReading and Conference\nCEN 792\nResearch\nCEN 599\nThesis\nCSE 580\nPracticum\nCEN 584\nInternship\nCEN 580\nPracticum\nCEN 790\nReading and Conference\nCEN 799\nDissertation\nCEN 795\nContinuing Registration\n2023 Summer\nCourse Number\nCourse Title\nCSE 795\nContinuing Registration\nCSE 584\nInternship\nCEN 584\nInternship\nCEN 595\nContinuing Registration\nCEN 795\nContinuing Registration\n2023 Spring\nCourse Number\nCourse Title\nCSE 493\nHonors Thesis\nCSE 792\nResearch\nCSE 795\nContinuing Registration\nCSE 799\nDissertation\nCSE 790\nReading and Conference\nCEN 790\nReading and Conference\nCEN 599\nThesis\nCEN 580\nPracticum\nCSE 580\nPracticum\nCSE 580\nPracticum\nCEN 792\nResearch\nCEN 799\nDissertation\