    "homepage_text": "Ruofei ZHANG\n      -  Lingnan Scholars\nLingnan Scholars Home\nHelp & FAQ\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at Lingnan Scholars\nView Scopus Profile\nZHANG Ruofei, Dr.\nLecturer\n,\nCentre for English and Additional Languages\nPhone\n(852) 26167917\nEmail\nrfzhang\nln.edu\nhk\n8 Castle Peak Road, Tuen Mun\nHong Kong\nh-index\nh5-index\n1276\nScopus Citations\n20\nScopus h-Index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n1117\nScopus Citations\n18\nScopus h-Index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2019\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nName in Chinese\n張若斐\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Ruofei ZHANG is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n2\nSimilar Profiles\nLanguage Instruction\nSocial Sciences\n100%\nEnglish as a Foreign Language\nSocial Sciences\n78%\nLearning\nSocial Sciences\n63%\nLanguage Learning\nPsychology\n58%\nLearner\nSocial Sciences\n45%\nWord Learning\nPsychology\n44%\nTechnology\nSocial Sciences\n40%\nVocabularies\nSocial Sciences\n39%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n31\nJournal Article (refereed)\n3\nConference paper (refereed)\n3\nReview article\n1\nBook Chapter\nNon-academic learner socialisation with ChatGPT and its influences on learning English argumentative writing logic\nZHANG, R.\n,\nZOU, D.\n& CHENG, G.,\nJan 2026\n,\nIn:\nEducation and Information Technologies.\n31\n,\n1\n,\np. 99-142\n44 p.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications\n›\nJournal Article (refereed)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nSocialization\n100%\nEnglish\n100%\nChatGPT\n100%\nEnglish as a Foreign Language\n33%\nLearning Experiences\n33%\nChatGPT affordance for logic learning strategies and its usefulness for developing knowledge and quality of logic in English argumentative writing\nZHANG, R.\n, ZOU, D. & CHENG, G.,\n1 Feb 2025\n,\nIn:\nSystem.\n128\n, 103561.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications\n›\nJournal Article (refereed)\n›\npeer-review\nEssay writing\n100%\n18\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nChatGPT-enhanced self-regulated learning in programming education : impacts on motivation, self-efficacy, and learning outcomes\nWANG, Z., ZOU, D.,\nZHANG, R.\n, LEE, L.-K.,\nXIE, H.\n& WANG, F. L.,\n6 Oct 2025\n, (E-pub ahead of print)\nIn:\nInteractive Learning Environments.\n26 p.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications\n›\nJournal Article (refereed)\n›\npeer-review\nSelf-Efficacy\n100%\nSelf-Regulated Learning\n100%\nEducation\n100%\nLearning Experiences\n100%\nChatGPT\n100%\nView all 38 research outputs\nPress/Media\nAI輔助 提升英語學習者寫作能力︱嶺航未來 Commentary on enhancing English writing skills with AI\nXIE, H.\n,\nZOU, D.\n&\nZHANG, R.\n13/12/24\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\n:\nCommentaries"
