    "homepage_text": "Xin's Homepage\nAbout Me\nXin Zhao, Ph.D., Professor.\nSchool of Computer and Communication Engineering, University of Science and Technology Beijing.\nResearch Interests: Computer Vision, Pattern Recognition, Data-centric AI, AI4Science.\nDr. Zhao received his Ph.D. Degree from the University of Science and Technology of China.\nNews\n2026.02:\n1 paper accepted to IJCV.\n2025.10:\nXin servers as the Leading Guest Editor of the Special issue on Evaluate4Science with Pattern Recognition (PR) Journal.\n[Website]\n2025.05:\nXin co-organizes the 4th DataCV Workshop and Challenge with ICCV2025.\n[Website]\n2025.02:\n1 paper accepted to CVPR2025.\n[Project Page]\n2025.02:\nThe book \"Visual Object Tracking: An Evaluation Perspective\" is online.\n[Website]\n2024.05:\nXin servers as the Lead Guest Editor of the Special issue on Visual Datasets with International Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV).\n[Website]\n2024.03:\nXin servers as an Associate Editor (AE) of Pattern Recognition (PR) Journal.\n[Website]\n2024.02:\n1 paper accepted to CVPR2024 and 1 paper accepted to Pattern Recognition (PR).\n2024.02:\nXin co-organizes The 3rd CVPR Workshop on Vision Datasets Understanding.\n[Website]\n2024.02:\n1 paper accepted to AAAI2024 and 1 paper accepted to ICASSP2024.\n2023.10:\n1 paper accepted to IJCV.\n[Project Page]\n2023.09:\n1 paper accepted to IJCV\n[Project Page]\nand 1 paper accepted to NeurIPS 2023 Datasets and Benchmarks track.\n2023.07:\n1 paper accepted to ICCV2023.\n2022.09:\n1 paper accepted to NeurIPS2022.\n2022.06:\n1 paper accepted to Neurocomputing.\n[Project Page]\n2022.03:\n1 paper accepted to CVPR2022.\n[Project Page]\n2022.02:\n1 paper accepted to IEEE TPAMI.\n[Project Page]\n[Arxiv]\n2022.02:\n1 paper accepted to Pattern Recognition (PR).\n2021.12:\n1 paper accepted to AAAI2022.\n2021.06:\n1 paper accepted to IEEE TIP.\n[Arxiv]\n2020.10:\nServe as a Senior Program Committee Member for IJCAI2021.\n2020.03:\n1 paper accepted to IEEE TCSVT.\n2019.11:\n1 paper accepted to IEEE TPAMI.\n[Project Page]\n2019.11:\n3 papers accepted to AAAI2020, 1 ORAL.\nPublication\n2026\n1.\nB\n3\nCT: Three-Branch Learning with Unlabeled Target Signals for Domain-Robust Semantic Segmentation\n.\nChen Liang,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Jian Jia, Junyan Wang, Lijun Cao, Jianguo Zhang, Weihua Chen. (*Corresponding Author).\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n): 2026.\n2.\nGuest Editorial: Special Issue on Visual Datasets\n.\nXin Zhao\n, Liang Zheng, Qiang Qiu, Yin Li, Limin Wang, José Lezama, Qiuhong Ke, Yongchan Kwon, Ruoxi Jia, Jungong Han.\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n): 2026.\n2025\n1.\nVisual Object Tracking: An Evaluation Perspective\n.\nXin Zhao\n, Shiyu Hu, Xu-cheng Yin.\nSpringer Nature: 2025.\n2.\nIDEA-Bench: How Far are Generative Models from Professional Designing?\n.\nChen Liang, Lianghua Huang, Jingwu Fang, Huanzhang Dou, Wei Wang, Zhi-Fan Wu, Yupeng Shi, Junge Zhang,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Yu Liu. (*Corresponding Author).\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n): 2025.\n[Project Page]\n[Arxiv]\n3.\nJoint Feature and Kernel Fusion for Improved Depth-Aware Panoptic Segmentation\n.\nYulong Bai, Shu Tian,\nXin Zhao\n, Xu-cheng Yin.\nIEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (\nICASSP\n): 2025.\n4.\nDistribution Optimization under Gaussian Hypothesis for Domain Adaptive Semantic Segmentation\n.\nChen Liang, Weihua Chen,\nXin Zhao\n, Junyan Wang, Lijun Cao, Junge Zhang.\nIEEE/CVF Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (\nWACV\n): 2025.\n2024\n1.\nGlobal and local multi-modal feature mutual learning for retinal vessel segmentation\n.\nXin Zhao\n, Jing Zhang, Qiaozhe Li, Tengfei Zhao, Yi Li, Zifeng Wu.\nPattern Recognition (\nPR\n): 2024.\n2.\nPeLK: Parameter-efficient Large Kernel ConvNets with Peripheral Convolution\n.\nHonghao Chen, Xiangxiang Chu, Yongjian Ren,\nXin Zhao\n, Kaiqi Huang.\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n): 2024.\n3.\nDDAE: Towards Deep Dynamic Vision BERT Pretraining\n.\nHonghao Chen, Xiangwen Kong, Xiangyu Zhang,\nXin Zhao\n, Kaiqi Huang.\n38th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n): 2024.\n4.\nRobust single-particle cryo-EM image denoising and restoration\n.\nJing Zhang, Tengfei Zhao, ShiYu Hu,\nXin Zhao\n*\n. (*Corresponding Author).\nIEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (\nICASSP\n): 2024.\n[Arxiv]\n2023\n1.\nGlobal Instance Tracking: Locating Target More Like Humans\n.\nShiyu Hu,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Lianghua Huang, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n): 2023.\n[Project Page]\n[Arxiv]\n[BibTex]\n2.\nBioDrone: A Bionic Drone-based Single Object Tracking Benchmark for Robust Vision\n.\nXin Zhao\n, Shiyu Hu, Yipei Wang, Jing Zhang, Yimin Hu, Rongshuai Liu, Haibin Ling, Yin Li, Renshu Li, Kun Liu, Jiadong Li.\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n): 2023.\n[Project Page]\n[Arxiv]\n3.\nSOTVerse: A User-defined Task Space of Single Object Tracking\n.\nShiyu Hu,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n): 2023.\n[Project Page]\n[Arxiv]\n4.\nEfficient-VQGAN: Towards High-Resolution Image Generation with Efficient Vision Transformers\n.\nShiyue Cao, Yueqin Yin, Lianghua Huang, Yu Liu,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Deli Zhao, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (\nICCV\n): 2023.\n5.\nA Multi-modal Global Instance Tracking Benchmark (MGIT): Better Locating Target in Complex Spatio-temporal and Casual Relationship\n.\nShiyu Hu, Dailing Zhang, Meiqi Wu, Xiaokun Feng, Xuchen Li,\nXin Zhao\n, Kaiqi Huang.\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n) Track on Datasets and Benchmarks: 2023.\n[Project Page]\n2022\n1.\nTemporal-adaptive Sparse Feature Aggregation for Video Object Detection\n.\nFei He, Qiaozhe Li,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nPattern Recognition (\nPR\n): 2022.\n[BibTex]\n2.\nRevisiting instance search: A new benchmark using cycle self-training\n.\nYuqi Zhang, Chong Liu, Weihua Chen, Xianzhe Xu, Fan Wang, Hao Li, Shiyu Hu,\nXin Zhao\n*\n. (*Corresponding Author).\nNeurocomputing (\nNeu\n): 2022.\n[Project Page]\n[BibTex]\n3.\nPanopticDepth: A Unified Framework for Depth-aware Panoptic Segmentation\n.\nNaiyu Gao, Fei He, Jian Jia, Yanhu Shan, Haoyang Zhang,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n): 2022.\n[Project Page]\n4.\nInsPro: Propagating Instance Query and Proposal for Online Video Instance Segmentation\n.\nFei He, Haoyang Zhang, Naiyu Gao, Jian Jia, Yanhu Shan,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nThirty-Sixth Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n): 2022.\n5.\nQueryProp: Object Query Propagation for High-Performance Video Object Detection\n.\nFei He, Naiyu Gao, Jian Jia,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\n36th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n): 2022.\n2021\n1.\nGOT-10k: A Large High-Diversity Benchmark for Generic Object Tracking in the Wild\n.\nLianghua Huang\n#\n,\nXin Zhao\n#\n, Kaiqi Huang. (#Equal Contribution).\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n): 2021.\n[Project Page]\n[Arxiv]\n[BibTex]\n[ESI Highly Cited Papers, Hot Papers]\n2.\nLearning Category- and Instance-Aware Pixel Embedding for Fast Panoptic Segmentation\n.\nNaiyu Gao, Yanhu Shan,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (\nTIP\n): 2021.\n[Arxiv]\n[BibTex]\n3.\nSSAP: Single-Shot Instance Segmentation With Affinity Pyramid\n.\nNaiyu Gao, Yanhu Shan, Yupei Wang,\nXin Zhao\n, Kaiqi Huang.\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (\nTCSVT\n): 2021.\n[BibTex]\n2020\n1.\nRecurrent Prediction with Spatio-temporal Attention for Crowd Attribute Recognition\n.\nQiaozhe Li,\nXin Zhao\n, Ran He, Kaiqi Huang.\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (\nTCSVT\n): 2020.\n[BibTex]\n2.\nGlobalTrack: A Simple and Strong Baseline for Long-term Tracking\n.\nLianghua Huang,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\n34rd AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n): 2020.\n[Project Page]\n3.\nTemporal Context Enhanced Feature Aggregation for Video Object Detection\n.\nFei He, Naiyu Gao, Qiaozhe Li, Senyao Du,\nXin Zhao\n, Kaiqi Huang.\n34rd AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n): 2020.\n4.\nTANet: Robust 3D Object Detection from Point Clouds with Triple Attention\n.\nZhe Liu,\nXin Zhao\n, Tengteng Huang, Ruolan Hu, Yu Zhou, Xiang Bai.\n34rd AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n): 2020.\n[Project Page]\n2019\n1.\nFocal Boundary Guided Salient Object Detection\n.\nYupei Wang,\nXin Zhao\n, Xuecai Hu, Yin Li, Kaiqi Huang.\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (\nTIP\n): 2019.\n[BibTex]\n2.\nDeep Crisp Boundaries: From Boundaries to Higher-level Tasks\n.\nYupei Wang,\nXin Zhao\n, Yin Li, Kaiqi Huang.\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (\nTIP\n): 2019.\n[Project Page]\n[Arxiv]\n[BibTex]\n3.\nBridging the Gap Between Detection and Tracking: A Unified Approach\n.\nLianghua Huang,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (\nICCV\n): 2019.\n4.\nSSAP: Single-Shot Instance Segmentation with Affinity Pyramid\n.\nNaiyu Gao, Yanhu Shan, Yupei Wang,\nXin Zhao\n*\n, Yinan Yu, Ming Yang, Kaiqi Huang. (*Corresponding Author).\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (\nICCV\n): 2019.\n5.\nPedestrian Attribute Recognition by Joint Visual-semantic Reasoning and Knowledge Distillation\n.\nQiaozhe Li,\nXin Zhao\n, Ran He, Kaiqi Huang.\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nIJCAI\n): 2019.\n6.\n3D Object Detection Using Scale Invariant and Feature Reweighting Networks\n.\nXin Zhao\n, Zhe Liu, Ruolan Hu, Kaiqi Huang.\n33rd AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n): 2019.\n7.\nVisual-semantic Graph Reasoning for Pedestrian Attribute Recognition\n.\nQiaozhe Li,\nXin Zhao\n, Ran He, Kaiqi Huang.\n33rd AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n): 2019.\n2018\n1.\nIterative Residual Network For Structured Edge Detection\n.\nYupei Wang,\nXin Z...[truncated]"
