    "homepage_text": "Andrew Li\nAndrew Li\n李卓谦\nGraduate Student,\nUniversity of British Columbia\n/\nTherapeutics Inititive\nandrewc.li@ubc.ca\nI'm a graduate student  advised by\nColin Dormuth\nand funded by the\nSSHRC Canada Graduate Scholarship\nand a\nFaculty of Medicine Graduate Student Award\n.\n        My research uses administrative databases to evaluate drug safety and effectiveness.\nPreviously, I studied\npsychology\nat the University of British Columbia and worked as a\nhealth economist/senior health economist\nwith the BC Ministry of Health on the Compensation Initiatives team.\n        Outside of work, I am training for a sub 3:15 marathon and enjoy watching the LA Lakers.\npublications\npharmacoepidemiology\nRelative-age effect on ADHD diagnosis and pharmacologic treatment in children and adolescents\nAndrew Li, Zishan Cui, Wade Thompson, Anshula Ambasta, Greg Carney, Colin Dormuth\nCAPT 2025\nslides\nTrends in school-break effects of ADHD pharmacotherapy: a Canadian population-based study\nZishan Cui, Andrew Li, Anshula Ambasta, Greg Carney, Wade Thompson, Colin Dormuth\nCAPT 2025\nposter\nTwo decades of ADHD diagnosis trends in British Columbia: A population-based study\nZishan Cui, Andrew Li, Ken Bassett, Anshula Ambasta, Greg Carney, Wade Thompson, Colin Dormuth\nCAPT 2025\nposter\nadministrative databases\nData Resource Profile: PharmaNet, the database for prescription drug dispensing in British Columbia, Canada\nAndrew Li, Yinshan Zhao, Scott Emerson, Kim McGrail, Sandra Peterson, Helen Tremlett\nSSRN\npreprint\nneuroscience\nDopamine activity in the nigrostriatal pathway alters cue‐induced risky choice patterns in female rats\nBrett Hathaway, Andrew Li, Hannah Brodie, Mason Silveira, Melanie Tremblay, Yeon Soo Seo, Catharine Winstanley\nEuropean Journal of Neuroscience\npaper\nVentral striatal cholinergic interneurons regulate decision-making or motor impulsivity differentially across learning and biological sex\nTristan Hynes*, Chloe Chernoff*, Kelly Hrelja, Andrew Li, Graeme Betts, Lucas Calderhead, Catharine Winstanley\nJournal of Neuroscience\npaper\npreprint\nDivergent effects of oral cannabis oil extracts marketed as C. indica or C. sativa on exertion of cognitive effort in rats\nHannah Brodie, Brett Hathaway, Andrew Li, Samantha Baglot, Sukhbir Kaur, Matthew Hill, Catharine Winstanley\nBehavioral Neuroscience\npaper\nshinyRGT: An R-Shiny application for extraction and visualization of Rat Gambling Task data\nAndrew Li, Georgios Karamanis, Tristan Hynes, Catharine Winstanley\nPsyArXiv\npreprint\napp\nslides\ncode\nbehavioral economics\nSocioeconomic correlates of the lottery rollover effect in Toronto, Canada\nHin-Ngai Fu, Andrew Li, Ross Otto, Luke Clark\nAddiction Research & Theory\npaper\nposter\nslides\nA meta-analytic cognitive framework of nudge and sludge\nYu Luo, Andrew Li, Dilip Soman, Jiaying Zhao\nRoyal Society Open Science\npaper\nposter\ncode\nshinyjackpot: Visualizing lottery gambling in a large Canadian city\nAndrew Li\nInternational Conference on Human-Computer Interaction\npaper\napp\ncode"
  },
  "serper::Weichen Wang": {
