  "serper::Xiaobo Xia": {
    "homepage": "https://xiaoboxia.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "xiaoboxia@ustc.edu.cn",
      "xiaoboxia.uni@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/xiaoboxia",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xiaobo Xia's Homepage\nXiaobo Xia\n(夏晓波)\nProfessor & Ph.D. Advisor\nSchool of Information Science and Technology, University of Science and Technology of China\nalso affiliate with\nPh.D. Supervisor,\nArtificial General Intelligence Institute\nE-mail: xiaoboxia [AT] ustc.edu.cn / xiaoboxia.uni [AT] gmail.com\nOffice: A424 Room, Building 1, High-Tech Campus.\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nGroup Code Repo on Github\nAbout Me\nDr. Xiaobo Xia currently is a professor at\nSchool of Information Science and Technology, University of Science and Technology of China\n.\nBefore that,\nhe was a postdoctoral research fellow at\nSchool of Computing\nof\nNational University of Singapore\n.\nHe obtained his Ph.D. degree at\nSchool of Computer Science\nof\nThe University of Sydney\nand received his bachelor degree at\nXidian University\n.\nHe is a recipient of Google Fellowship (Google AI), JProcRSNSW Ph.D. Thesis Award, and NeurIPS Top Area Chair Award.\nHe regularly serves as area chairs for ICML/NeurIPS/ICLR/ACM MM.\nHe also serve as an Action Editor for\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research\n.\nGroup\n|\nPublications\n|\nCourse\n|\nExperience\n|\nAwards\n|\nService\nResearch Focus\nOur research is centered on building world models and foundational models that integrate physical laws and spatio-temporal dimensions, leveraging multimodal data and techniques to push the boundaries of AI’s ability to model and reason within complex realistic environments.\nIn our work, we aim to connect fundamental theory and novel algorithms with high-impact applications, particularly in the scientific domain.\nCurrent key words: multimodal AI, world models, foundational models, learning theory.\nRecruitment\nVarious positions (Postdoctoral Researchers/Full-time Ph.D./Master Program/Research Engineers/Assistants) are available. Base: Shanghai or Hefei.\nPlease email me if you are interested in the above topics.\nFor undergraduates, you may read this\nguideline\nto prepare yourself with our group.\nRecent News\n2026.03: Serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 2026.\n2026.03: One paper is accepted to TPAMI.\n2026.03: Serve as an Acition Editor for Transactions on Machine Learning Research.\n2026.02: Three papers are accepted to CVPR 2026.\n2026.02: Serve as an Area Chair for ACM MM 2026.\n2026.01: Two papers are accepted to ICLR 2026.\n2025.11: Two papers are accepted to AAAI 2026 (2 Orals).\n2025.11: Serve as an Area Chair for ICML 2026.\n2025.10: One paper is accepted to Nexus (Cell Press).\n2025.09: Five papers are accepted to NeurIPS 2025.\n2025.08: Serve as an Area Chair for ICLR 2026.\n2025.07: One paper is accepted to ACM MM 2025 as Oral.\n2025.06: One paper is accepted to ICCV 2025 as Highlight.\n2025.05: One paper is accepted to ICML 2025.\n2025.02: Serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 2025."
  },
  "serper::Qiaomin Xie": {
    "homepage": "https://qiaominxie.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "qiaomin.xie@wisc.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/alshedivat",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Qiaomin Xie\nQiaomin Xie\nM1002 Engineering Centers Building\n1513 University Avenue\nMadison, WI 53706\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Industrial and Systems Engineering (ISyE)\nDepartment of Computer Sciences (CS, affiliate)\nUniversity of Wisconsin-Madison\nEmail: qiaomin.xie at wisc dot edu\nI am recruiting PhD students starting 2026. UW-Madison students interested in joining my group: please email me with your CV. Others please apply to the\nUW-Madison ISyE or CS graduate programs\n.\nQiaomin Xie is an assistant professor in the\nDepartment of Industrial and Systems Engineering (ISyE)\nand the\nDepartment of Computer Sciences\n(affiliate) at the\nUniversity of Wisconsin-Madison\n. She was previously a visiting assistant professor at School of Operations Research and Information Engineering (ORIE) at Cornell University. Prior to that, she was a postdoctoral researcher with LIDS at MIT, and a research fellow at the Simons Institute. Qiaomin received her Ph.D. degree in Electrical and Computing Engineering from University of Illinois Urbana Champaign, and her B.E. degree in Electronic Engineering from Tsinghua University.\nHer research interests lie in the fields of reinforcement learning, game theory, applied probability and stochastic networks, with applications to computer and communication networks. She is a recipient of\nNational Science Foundation CAREER Award (2024)\n, JP Morgan Faculty Research Award (2021), Google Systems Research Award (2020), UIUC CSL PhD Thesis Award (2017), and the best paper award from IFIP Performance Conference (2011). She was named a\nNotable Woman in Reinforcement Learning (2024)\n.\nnews\nJul 5, 2025\nI co-organized the NeurIPS 2025 workshop\nML x OR: Mathematical Foundations and Operational Integration of Machine Learning for Uncertainty-Aware Decision-Making\n."
  },
  "serper::Guanghui Lan": {
