    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Rong-Rong Chen's Homepage\nRong-Rong Chen\nPh.D.,\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\n, 2003\nAssociate Professor\nElectrical and\nComputer Engineering\nUniversity of\nUtah\nContact Information\nOffice:\nMEB 3106\nPhone:\n(801)585-7367\nFax:\n(801)581-5281\nEmail:\nrchen at ece dot utah dot edu\nAddress:\n50 S. Central Campus Dr.\nMEB 3280\nSalt Lake City, UT 84112\nResearch\nInterests\nMachine Learning for Communications, Multi-agent Reinforcement Learning, Meta-learning\nCoded Distributed Computing, Wireless Caching Networks\nStatistical signal processing, Markov Chain Monte Carlo Detection\nCoding Theory, Iterative Decoding\nUnderwater Acoustic Communication.\nMachine Learning for Medical Imaging, MRI Image Reconstruction\nNews: 2021 Globecom Best Paper Award (Communication Theory Symposium ): ''A Practical Algorithm Design and Evaluation for Heterogeneous Elastic Computing with Stragglers'', Nicholas Woolsey, Jorg Kliewer, Rong-Rong Chen and Mingyue Ji\nFunded Projects\nNSF funded project (Nov.2026-Oct.2029)\n: Collaborative Research: U.S.-Ireland R&D Partnership: Integrated Sensing and Telecommunications for Intelligent Connection and Transmission (INSTINCT).\nNSF funded project (2022-2026)\n:\nECCS: U.S.-Ireland R&D Partnership: Smart Radio Environments with Reconfigurable Intelligent Surfaces -- Communications Through Blockage in Millimeter-wave Systems (REFLECT-MMWAVE)\nNSF funded project (2022-2026)\n:\nCollaborative Research: SWIFT: Decentralized Intelligent Spectrum Sharing in UAV Networks (DISH-uNET) via Hardware-software Co-design\nNSF funded project (2018-2022)\n:\nCIF: Small: Fundamental Limits of Caching Networks with\nGeneral Topologies\nNSF funded project (2018-2022)\n:\nSpecEES: Dynamic Space Frequency Multiplexing-- A New\nParadigm for Filterbank Multicarrier Spectrum Access\nNSF funded project (2011-2014)\n:\nCollaborative Research: Modulation and statistical detection methods for\nunderwater acoustic communications\nNSF funded project (CAREER, 2006-2012)\n: Efficient\nutilization of multiple antennas for high-rate communications in\nwireless networks.\nNSF funded project (2009-2010)\n:\nStatistical detection methods for underwater acoustic\ncommunications\nCurrent\nCV\nPublications\n(names of my students are\nunderlined)\nPublished Journal Papers\n[J31] Z. Chen, Y. Zhou, R.R. Chen,\nMulti-Agent Off-Policy TDC with Near-Optimal Sample and\nCommunication Complexities\n,\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research,\n, June 2022.\n[J30] M.F. Chen, R.R. Chen,\nTop Eigenpairs of Large Scale Matrices\n,\nCSIAM Transactions on Applied Mathematics (CSIAM-AM),\n, March 2022.\n[J29]\nKazem Hashemizadeh\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Ganesh Adluru,  Edward V. R. DiBella,\nJointly Estimating Parametric Maps of Multiple Diffusion Models from Undersampled Q-Space Data: A Comparison of Three Deep Learning Approaches\n,\nMagnetic Resonance in Medicine\n, Jan 2022.\n[J28]\nNick Woolsey\n, Rong-Rong Chen,  Mingyue Ji,\nCoded Elastic Computing on Machines with Heterogeneous Storage and Computation Speed\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Communications\n, May 2021.\n[J27]\nNick Woolsey\n, Rong-Rong Chen,  Mingyue Ji,\nA New Combinatorial Coded Design for\nHeterogeneous Distributed Computing\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Communications\n, Sep., 2021.\n[J26]\nNick Woolsey\n, Rong-Rong Chen,  Mingyue Ji,\nA Combinatorial Design for Cascaded Coded Distributed Computing on General Networks\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Communications\n, Sep., 2021.\n[J25]\nKazem Hashemizadeh\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Ganesh Adluru, Douglas C. Dean, Andrew L. Alexander, Edward V. R. DiBella,\nSimultaneous multi-slice image reconstruction using regularized image domain split slice-GRAPPA for diffusion MRI\n,\nMedical Image Analysis\n, May 2021.\n[J24]\nNick Woolsey\n, Rong-Rong Chen,  Mingyue Ji,\nTowards Finite File Packetizations in Wireless Device-to-Device Caching Networks\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Communications\n, Sep. 2020.\n[J23]\nNick Woolsey\n, Rong-Rong Chen,  Mingyue Ji,\nUncoded Placement with Linear Sub-Messages for Private Information Retrieval from Storage Constrained Databases\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Communications\n, Oct. 2020.\n[J22]\nNick Woolsey\n, Xingyue Wang, Rong-Rong Chen,  Mingyue Ji,\nFLCD: A Flexible Low Complexity Design of Coded Distributed Computing\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Communications\n, Oct. 2020.\n[J21]\nKazem Hashemizadeh\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Edward V. R. DiBella, Leslie Ying, Ganesh Adluru,\nCoil-Combined Split Slice-GRAPPA for Simultaneous Multi-Slice Diffusion MRI\n,\nMedical Image Analysis\n, May 2019.\n[J20]  Jonathan C Hedstrom, Chung Him (George) Yuen, Rong-Rong Chen, Behrouz Farhang-Boroujeny,\nAchieving Near MAP Performance with an Excited Markov Chain Monte Carlo MIMO Detector\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Wireless Communications\n, vol. 16, no. 12, pp. 7718--7732, Dec. 2017.\n[J19]\nHuajun She\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Dong Liang,  Yuchou\nChang,  Leslie Ying,\nImage Reconstruction from Phased-Array Data Based on Multichannel Blind Deconvolution\n,\nMagnetic Resonance Imaging\n, vol. 33, no. 9, page 1106--1113, Nov., 2015.\n[J18]\nXuehong Mao\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Huajun She, Behrouz Farhang-Boroujeny,\nJoint Markov Chain Monte Carlo Data Detection and Channel Estimation for High-rate MIMO Communicationss\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Signal Processing\n, 2012.\n[J17]\nHuajun She\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Dong\n Liang, Yuchou Chang, Edward DiBella, Leslie Ying,\nSparse BLIP: BLind Iterative\n Parallel Imaging Reconstruction Using Compressive Sensing\n,\nMagnetic Resonance in\n Medicine\n, 2012.\n[J16]\nPooyan Amini\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Behrouz Farhang-Boroujeny,\nFilterbank Multicarrier for Underwater Communications\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Ocean Engineering\n, 2012.\n[J15]\nHong Wan\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Jun W.\nChoi, Andrew Singer, James Preisig, and Behrouz Farhang-Beroujeny,\nMarkov Chain Monte Carlo Detection for Frequency-selective Channels Using List\nChannel Estimates\n,\nIEEE\nJournal on Selected Topics in Signal Processing\n, vol. 5, no. 8, pp. 1537-1547, Dec., 2011.\n[J14] Dong Liang, Edward DiBella, Rong-Rong Chen\nand Leslie Ying,\nk-t ISD: dynamic cardiac MR imaging using compressed sensing with iterative support detection\n,  to appear\nMagnetic Resonance in Medicine\n, 2012.\n[J13] Rong-Rong Chen and Xin Liu,\nDelay\nPerformance of Threshold Policy in Dynamic Spectrum Access\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Wireless\nCommunications,\n, vol. 10, no. 7, pp. 2283-2293, 2011.\n[J12]\nHong Wan\n, Rong-Rong Chen, and\nYingbin Liang,\nOptimality of Beamforming for MIMO Multiple Access\nChannels via Virtual Representation\n,\nIEEE\nTransactions on Signal Processing\n, Nov. 2010.\n[J11] Rong-Rong Chen, Koon Hoo Teo, and Behrouz\nFarhang-Boroujeny,\nRandom Access Protocols for Collaborative\nSpectrum Sensing in Multi-band Cognitive Radio Networks\n,\nIEEE journal on selected topics in signal\nprocessing\n, Feb. 2011.\n[J10]\nRonghui Peng\n, Rong-Rong Chen, and\nBehrouz Farhang-Beroujeny.\nMarkov Chain\nMonte Carlo Detectors for Channels with Intersymbol\nInterference\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Signal\nProcessing\n, vol. 58, no. 4, pp. 2206-2217, April,\n2010.\n[J9] Rong-Rong Chen,\nRonghui Peng\n, A.\nAshikhmin, and Behrouz Farhang-Beroujeny.\nApproaching MIMO Capacity Using Bitwise Markov\nChain Monte Carlo Detection\n,\nIEEE Transactions on\nCommunications\n, vol. 58, no. 2, pp. 423-428, Feb.\n2010.\n[J8] Rong-Rong Chen and\nRonghui Peng\n.\nPerformance of Channel Coded\nNoncoherent Systems: Modulation Choice, Information Rate, and\nMarkov Chain Monte Carlo Detection\n,\nIEEE\nTransactions on Communications\n, vol. 57, no. 10, pp.\n2841-2845, Oct. 2009.\nFull\nVersion\n[J7]\nRonghui Peng\nand Rong-Rong Chen,\nApplication of Nonbinary LDPC Cycle\nCodes to MIMO Channels\n,\nIEEE Transactions on\nWireless Communications\nVol. 7, no. 6, pp. 2020-2026,\nJune., 2008.\n[J6] Haidong Zhu, Behrouz Farhang-Boroujeny,\nRong-Rong Chen\nOn performance of\nsphere decoding and Markov chain Monte Carlo detection\nmethods\n,\nIEEE Signal Processing Letters\n,\nVol. 12, no. 10, pp. 669-672, Oct. 2005.\n[J5] Rong-Rong Chen, Bruce Hajek, Ralf Koetter,Upamanyu Madhow,\nOn fixed input distributions for noncoherent communication over high SNR Rayleigh fading channels\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Information Theory\n, Vol. 50, pp. 3390-3396, Dec. 2004.\n[J4] Rong-Rong Chen, Ralf Koetter,Upamanyu\nMadhow,Dakshi Agrawal,\nJoint\ndemodulation and decodingfor the noncoherent block fading channel:\na practical framework for approachingchannel capacity\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Communications\n, Vol. 51, no.\n10, Oct. 2003.\n[J3] Rong-Rong Chen and Sean Meyn,\nValue Iteration and Optimization of Multiclass\nQueueingNetworks\n,\nQueueing Systems Theory and\nApplications\n, 32(1-3): 65-97, 1999.\n[J2] Rong-Rong Chen,\nAn extended class of time-continuous branching\nprocesses\n,\nJournal of Applied Probability\n,\n34:14-23,1997.\n[J1] Rong-Rong Chen,\nCriticalpoints of three-dimensional bootstrap\npercolation-like cellular automata\n,\nChinese Journal\nof Applied Probability and Statistics\n(English Edition),\n13(4):399-406, Nov 1997.\nSelected Refereed Conference Papers:\n[C69] Ziyi Chen, Yi Zhou, Rong-Rong Chen, Shaofeng Zou, Sample and Communication-Efficient Decentralized Actor-Critic Algorithms with Finite-Time Analysis\n,\nThirty-ninth International Conference on Machine Learning\n(ICML), July 2022.\n[C68] Jiayi Wang, Shiqiang Wang, Rong-Rong Chen,  Mingyue Ji, Demystifying Why Local Aggregation Helps: Convergence Analysis of Hierarchical SGD\n, to appear\nProc. Thirty-Fourth Innovative Applications of Artificial Intelligence Conference\n(AAAI-22), 2022.\n[C67]\nJoohyun Cho, Xiang Huang\n, Rong-Rong Chen, Two Time-Scale Learning for\nBeamforming and Phase Shift Design in RIS-aided Networks\n, to appear\nProc. International Conference on Communications\n(ICC),2022.\n[C66]\nNicholas Woolsey\n, Jorg Kliewer, Rong-Rong Chen and Mingyue Ji, A Practical Algorithm Design and Evaluation for Heterogeneous Elastic Computing with Stragglers\n,\nProc. IEEE Global Communications Conference (GLOBECOM)\n2021 (Best Paper Award, Communication Theory Symposium).\n[C65] Ziyi Chen, Rong-Rong Chen,  Yi Zhou, Multi-Agent Off-Policy TD Learning: Finite-Time Analysis with Near-Optimal Sample Complexity and Communicatio...[truncated]"
