  "serper::Zhuyun Dai": {
    "homepage": "https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~zhuyund/",
    "emails": [
      "zhuyund@cs.cmu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/AdeDZY",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhuyundai/",
    "homepage_text": "Zhuyun Dai, Ph.D. candidate in Carnegie Mellon\nZhuyun Dai\nLanguage Technologies Institute, Carnegie Mellon University\nHome\nPublications\nExperiences\nProjects\nHELLO,\nI am now a Software Engineer at Google. I obtained my Ph.D. in August 2020 from\nLanguage Technologies Institute (LTI)\n, Carnegie Mellon University. During my Ph.D., I worked with Professor\nJamie Callan\n.\nMy research aims to improve language understanding in tody's information retrieval systems, towards building the next-generation information assistant systems that can help people access the world's knowledge in seamless ways. To achieve my goals, I combine advances in deep learning and NLP with insights from information retrieval and large-scale distributed systems.  The methods I developed enable information retrieval systems to understand people better, retrieve more accurate documents, and present results in more natural ways.\nI came to LTI in 2014 fall as a master student in the MLT program, and started the Ph.D. study in 2016 fall. Prior to CMU, I completed my undergraduate study in\nPeking University\n, majoring in Computer Science.\nFor more information, please visit my\nCurriculum Vitae\n, and find my pulications on the\npublications page\nor\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nLast updated: August 18, 2020.\nNEWS\nCONTACT\n2020.6.24\nI defended my PhD thesis: \"Neural Matching and Importance Learning in Information Retrieval\"\n[slides]\n[Dissertation]\n2020.7.20\nOur short paper \"Understanding BERT Rankers Under Distillation\" was accepted at ICTIR 2020\n[paper]\n2020.4.23\nThree papers\nin deep retrieval and conversational search got accepted into SIGIR 2020!\n2020.4.22\nCheck out my talk (\nslides\n) in the Web Conference 2020\n2020.4.10\nOur submission \"DeepCT Retrieval + TF-Ranking BERT Ensemble\" got to the 2nd place on the\nMS MARCO Passage Ranking Leaderboard\n!\n2020.1.10\nOne full paper accepted by the Web Conference 2020 (Oral Presentation).\nEmail:\nzhuyund [at] cs [dot] cmu [dot] edu\nAddress:\n5000 Forbes Avenue\nOffice:\n5513 Gates Hillman Complex\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nEducation\nHonors & Awards\nMS in Language Technologies\nLanguage Technologies Institute, School of Computer Science\nCarnegie Mellon University, Pittsburgh, United States\n2014.08 - 2016.06\nB.S. in Computer Science\nComputer Science Department, School of Electronic Engineering and Computer Science\nPeking University, Beijing, China\n2010.09 - 2014.07\nGPA: 3.77/4.0 (Top 3)\n2019.06\n1st Place in the Forte Woman's Leadership Power Pitch Competition\n2019.03\n2nd Place in the 2019 CMU McGinnis Venture Competition\n2014.07\n2014 Outstanding Graduating Student of Beijing\n2014.06\n2014 Excellent Graduation Thesis, Peking University\n2013.07\nThe Google Anita Borg Memorial Scholarship"
  },
