    "homepage_text": "Rachel Zhang's Portfolio\nWelcome\nI am\nWelcome\nI am\nMy work spans XR experiences, UX/Product Design, and Web Development.\nI am open to selected collaborations and project-based engagements.\nFeel free to reach out for potential opportunities.\nTokyo, Japan\nLinkedIn\nLinkedIn\nRachel Qingzhu Zhang\nRachel Qingzhu Zhang\nï¼å¼µ  æ¸ç«¹ï¼\nï¼å¼µ  æ¸ç«¹ï¼\nFeatured  XR Projects\nSentiSing: An Affect-Driven Immersive Environment for Expressive Vocal Interaction in Virtual Reality\nIndividual Project\nIEEE VR 2026 Demo Paper\nVirtual Reality\nMultimodal\n#Vocal\n#Music\n#Synaesthesia\n#Multi-sensing\nSentiSing: An Affect-Driven Immersive Environment for Expressive Vocal Interaction in Virtual Reality\nIndividual Project\nIEEE VR 2026 Demo Paper\nVirtual Reality\nMultimodal\n#Vocal\n#Music\n#Synaesthesia\n#Multi-sensing\nImmersive AI-powered Gamified Japanese Language Learning in VR\nIndividual/UC Berkeley Thesis Project\nIEEE VR 2025 Demo Paper\nVirtual Reality\nGamification\n#Education\n#AI\n#LanguageLearning\n#AdaptiveLearning\nImmersive AI-powered Gamified Japanese Language Learning in VR\nIndividual/UC Berkeley Thesis Project\nIEEE VR 2025 Demo Paper\nVirtual Reality\nGamification\n#Education\n#AI\n#LanguageLearning\n#AdaptiveLearning\nImmersive Brain Exploration: A VR-Based Gamified System for Neuroanatomy Education with AI-Augmented Learning\nIndividual Project (with assistance of students in Keio University)\nSiggraph Asia 2025 Poster Paper\nVirtual Reality\nGamification\n#Education\n#AI\n#NeuroScience\n#AdaptiveLearning\n#Medicine\nImmersive Brain Exploration: A VR-Based Gamified System for Neuroanatomy Education with AI-Augmented Learning\nIndividual Project (with assistance of students in Keio University)\nSiggraph Asia 2025 Poster Paper\nVirtual Reality\nGamification\n#Education\n#AI\n#NeuroScience\n#AdaptiveLearning\n#Medicine\nSee what I see: Interactive Colorblind Experience in Virtual Reality\nIndividual Project\nVirtual Reality\n#Accessibility\n#Colorblindness\n#Disabilities\n#Empathy\nSee what I see: Interactive Colorblind Experience in Virtual Reality\nIndividual Project\nVirtual Reality\n#Accessibility\n#Colorblindness\n#Disabilities\n#Empathy\nXR Hackathon Projects\nCapsule: VR Experience for enhanced memories\nGroup Project in XR Hackathon, Stanford University\nStanford XR Hack 3rd Meta Prize\nVirtual Reality\n#Empathy\n#Memory\nCapsule: VR Experience for enhanced memories\nGroup Project in XR Hackathon, Stanford University\nStanford XR Hack 3rd Meta Prize\nVirtual Reality\n#Empathy\n#Memory\nPlastic Seas: Virtual Reality Storytelling for Marine Environmental Awareness\nGroup Project in XR Hackathon, MIT University\nMIT Reality Hack Finalist (Top10)\nVirtual Reality\n#Environment\n#Awareness\nPlastic Seas: Virtual Reality Storytelling for Marine Environmental Awareness\nGroup Project in XR Hackathon, MIT University\nMIT Reality Hack Finalist (Top10)\nVirtual Reality\n#Environment\n#Awareness"
