    "homepage_text": "Sen-Ching Cheung\n      -  University of Kentucky\nUniversity of Kentucky Home\nLOGIN & Help\nLink opens in a new tab\nEnglish\nEspañol\nSearch content at University of Kentucky\nContact Expert\nView Scopus Profile\nSen-Ching Cheung, Ph.D.\nProfessor\n,\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nDirector of Undergraduate Certificate, Cybersecurity\n,\nStanley and Karen Pigman College of Engineering\nNeuroscience Research Priority Area\nh-index\n3601\nCitations\n31\nh-index\nCalculated based on the number of publications stored in Pure and citations from PlumX\n1994                 …\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nEducation/Academic qualification\nDoctor of Philosophy, University Of California - Berkeley\n2002\nBachelor of Science, University Of Washington\n1992\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 3\nGood Health and Well-being\nSDG 7\nAffordable and Clean Energy\nSDG 16\nPeace, Justice and Strong Institutions\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Sen-Ching Cheung is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nExperimental Result\nComputer Science\n100%\nBackground Subtraction\nComputer Science\n83%\nVideo Sequences\nComputer Science\n80%\nPrivacy Protection\nComputer Science\n72%\nDeep Learning Method\nComputer Science\n60%\nsecure multiparty computation\nComputer Science\n53%\nPrivacy Information\nComputer Science\n53%\nBiometrics\nComputer Science\n45%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration from the last 5 years on country level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots.\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into 