    "homepage_text": "Baoxiang Wang\nBaoxiang Wang\nBaoxiang Wang\nAssistant Professor, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nI am an assistant professor at School of Data Science, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen. I work on the broad areas of\nreinforcement learning\nand\ngame theory\n. My recent works have a specific focus on interactions of multiple agents in complicated tasks and games.\nI obtained my Ph.D. in Computer Science and Engineering from The Chinese University of Hong Kong in 2020, fortunate to be advised by\nSiu On Chan\nand\nAndrej Bogdanov\n. Before that, I obtained my B.E. in Information Security from Shanghai Jiao Tong University in 2014, under Hai Zhao.\nI am currently visiting Vector Institute at Toronto. I was visiting Vector Institute as a visiting researcher during Jan-Aug 2024, with\nYaoliang Yu\n, and University of Waterloo as a visiting assistant professor during May-Aug 2023, with\nPascal Poupart\n.\nEducation\n2014 - 2020 Ph.D. The Chinese University of Hong Kong\n2010 - 2014 B.E. Shanghai Jiao Tong University\nSome topics I am currently investigating\nReinforcement learning algorithms and specifically the LLM-RL and game-theoretic RL settings.\nUnderstanding and learning the interactions amid multiple intelligent agents in mechanism design problems and large-scale games.\nAd-hoc topics in learning theory and game theory that I find interesting\nProspective students\nI am recruiting PhD students for Fall 2026 enrollment (till April 2026). The degree will be issued by CUHK for PhD in Computer Science or PhD in Data Science, with a mark that the study in completed in the Shenzhen campus. The programs are similar to the ones in Hong Kong. See the\nprogram information\n.\nFor candidates, I care mostly about their math background and their motivation on working on new and explorative problems. Students are required to use AI tools to advance their research.\nContact\nOffice: 503 DY, CUHK Shenzhen.\r\nShenzhen, 518172\nPhone: +86 755 235-17020"
  },
