eng Y\n.\nExtracting post-acute sequelae of SARS-CoV-2 infection symptoms from clinical notes via hybrid natural language processing\n.\nNpj Health Syst\n. 2025 Aug 21;2:10.1038/s44401-025-00033-4. doi: 10.1038/s44401-025-00033-4. Epub ahead of print. PMID: 40958972; PMCID: PMC12435580.\nWang Y, Hilsman J, Li C, Morris M, Heider PM, Fu S, Kwak MJ, Wen A, Applegate JR, Wang L, Bernstam E, Liu H, Chang J, Harris DR, Corbeau A, Henderson D, Osborne J, Kennedy RE, Garduno-Rapp NE, Rousseau JF, Yan C, Chen Y, Patel MB, Murphy TJ, Malin BA, Park CM, Fan JW, Sohn S, Pagali S,\nPeng Y\n, Pathak A, Wu Y, Xia Z, Loguercio S, Reis SE, Visweswaran S.\nDevelopment and validation of natural language processing algorithms in the national ENACT network\n.\nJ Clin Transl Sci\n. 2025 Aug 22;9(1):e199. doi: 10.1017/cts.2025.10116. PMID: 40979101; PMCID: PMC12444719.\nLin M, Holste G, Wang S, Zhou Y, Wei Y, Banerjee I, Chen P, Dai T, Du Y, Dvornek NC, Ge Y, Guo Z, Hanaoka S, Kim D, Messina P, Lu Y, Parra D, Son D, Soto Ã, Urooj A, Vidal R, Yamagishi Y, Yan P, Yang Z, Zhang R, Zhou Y, Celi LA, Summers RM, Lu Z, Chen H, Flanders A, Shih G, Wang Z,\nPeng Y\n.\nCXR-LT 2024: A MICCAI challenge on long-tailed, multi-label, and zero-shot disease classification from chest X-ray\n.\nMed Image Anal\n. 2025 Dec;106:103739. doi: 10.1016/j.media.2025.103739. Epub 2025 Jul 29. PMID: 40795541; PMCID: PMC12396843.\nFang Y, Zhang G, Chen F, Hripcsak G,\nPeng Y\n, Ryan P, Weng C.\nCLEAR: A vision to support clinical evidence lifecycle with continuous learning\n.\nJ Biomed Inform\n. 2025 Sep;169:104884. doi: 10.1016/j.jbi.2025.104884. Epub 2025 Jul 29. PMID: 40744316; PMCID: PMC12339056.\nGautam N, Elhusseiny A, Mansour M, Mehta JL, Andersen OS,\nPeng Y\n, Al'Aref SJ.\nExploring the feasibility of using artificial intelligence to simulate the placebo arm of randomized clinical trials\n.\nPostgrad Med J\n. 2025 Nov 18;101(1202):1239-1241. doi: 10.1093/postmj/qgaf095. Erratum in: Postgrad Med J. 2025 Nov 18;101(1202):1333. doi: 10.1093/postmj/qgaf158. PMID: 40577492; PMCID: PMC12624531.\nSun C, Teichman K, Zhou Y, Critelli B, Nauheim D, Keir G, Wang X, Zhong J, Flanders AE, Shih G,\nPeng Y\n.\nGenerative Large Language Models Trained for Detecting Errors in Radiology Reports\n.\nRadiology\n. 2025 May;315(2):e242575. doi: 10.1148/radiol.242575. PMID: 40392090; PMCID: PMC12130665.\nPress release\nRSNA News\nAuntMinnie\nZhang Y, Wei Y, Wang Y, Xiao Y, Poropatich CRRK, Haas GL, Zhang Y, Weng C, Liu J, Brenner LA, Bjork JM,\nPeng Y\n.\nMachine learning applications related to suicide in military and Veterans: A scoping literature review\n.\nJ Biomed Inform\n. 2025 Jul;167:104848. doi: 10.1016/j.jbi.2025.104848. Epub 2025 May 13. PMID: 40373934.\nZhang G, Xu Z, Jin Q, Chen F, Fang Y, Liu Y, Rousseau JF, Xu Z, Lu Z, Weng C,\nPeng Y\n.\nLeveraging long context in retrieval augmented language models for medical question answering\n.\nNPJ Digit Med\n. 2025 May 2;8(1):239. doi: 10.1038/s41746-025-01651-w. PMID: 40316710; PMCID: PMC12048518.\nFlanders AE, Wang X, Wu CC, Kitamura FC, Shih G, Mongan J,\nPeng Y\n.\nThe Evolution of Radiology Image Annotation in the Era of Large Language Models\n.\nRadiol Artif Intell\n. 2025 Jul;7(4):e240631. doi: 10.1148/ryai.240631. PMID: 40304582; PMCID: PMC12319696.\nPeng Y\n, Chen Q, Shih G.\nDeepSeek is open-access and the next AI disrupter for radiology\n.\nRadiol Adv\n. 2025 Jan;2(1):umaf009. doi: 10.1093/radadv/umaf009. Epub 2025 Feb 18. PMID: 40837590; PMCID: PMC12363671.\nCheng S, Wei Y, Zhou Y, Xu Z, Wright DN, Liu J,\nPeng Y\n.\nDeciphering genomic codes using advanced natural language processing techniques: a scoping review\n.\nJ Am Med Inform Assoc\n. 2025 Apr 1;32(4):761-772. doi: 10.1093/jamia/ocaf029. PMID: 39998912; PMCID: PMC12005631.\nLin M, Wang S, Ding Y, Zhao L, Wang F,\nPeng Y\n.\nAn empirical study of using radiology reports and images to improve intensive care unit mortality prediction\n.\nJAMIA Open\n. 2025 Feb 20;8(1):ooae137. doi: 10.1093/jamiaopen/ooae137. PMID: 39980476; PMCID: PMC11841685.\nPeng Y\n, Malin BA, Rousseau JF, Wang Y, Xu Z, Xu X, Weng C, Bian J.\nFrom GPT to DeepSeek: Significant gaps remains in realizing AI in healthcare\n.\nJ Biomed Inform\n. 2025 Mar;163:104791. doi: 10.1016/j.jbi.2025.104791. Epub 2025 Feb 10...[truncated]"
