    "homepage_text": "Haoran You\nHaoran You\nAbout\nI am currently a Research Scientist at Adobe, developing efficient GenAI models with lower serving cost and optimizing deployment on Nvidia, Intel, AMD, and Apple devices.\n    I obtained my PhD from Georgia Tech, advised by Dr. Yingyan (Celine) Lin. My research is dedicated to creating\nefficient ML systems\nthrough\nalgorithm-hardware co-design\n.\n    This involves addressing the challenge posed by the increasing complexity of advanced AI/ML models, such as large language models (LLMs) and large vision models (LVMs), against the constraints of both edge and cloud computing devices.\nMy research work has received recognition, including winning Gold Medal at the ACM Student Research Competition (SRC) at ICCAD'23, securing the Best Poster Award at the SCS Poster Competition of Georgia Tech, and being selected as an IEEE Micro's Top Pick of 2023. Additionally, I was named one of the Machine Learning and Systems Rising Stars of 2023, received the Outstanding Graduate Research Assistant Award, won first place in the University Best Demonstration at DAC'22, and our ViTCoD project was honored with the Meta Faculty Research Award of 2022.\nSelected News\n[01/2026]\nOur efficient GenAI models for\nGenerative Fill\nand\nRemove\nfeatures are shipped in\nPhotoshop v27.3\nwith one third less serving costs (\nsaved 175 H100 GPUs ≈ $1.2K per hour\n) !\n[10\n/\n2025]\nHaoran was selected as a\nTop Reviewer\nby\nNeurIPS 2025\n!\n[07\n/\n2025]\nOne paper accepted by\nMICRO 2025\n!\n[05\n/\n2025]\nOne paper accepted by\nICML 2025\n!\n[02\n/\n2025]\nTwo papers accepted by\nCVPR 2025\n!\n[09\n/\n2024]\nOur\nShiftAddLLM\nwas accepted by\nNeurIPS 2024\n!\n[05\n/\n2024]\nOur\nLinearized-LLM\nwas accepted by\nICML 2024\n!\n[12\n/\n2023]\nHaoran received the NeurIPS 2023 Scholar Award !\n[11\n/\n2023]\nHaoran won\nFirst Place\nat\nACM Student Research Competition\nat\nICCAD 2023\n!\n[05/2023]\nHaoran was selected as one of the\nML and Systems Rising Stars of 2023\n!\n[04/2023]\nHaoran won the\nBest Poster Award\nat the SCS Poster Competition of GaTech !\n[03/2023]\nHaoran was selected by GaTech to receive the\nOutstanding GRA Award\n!\n[01/2023]\nOur\nEyeCoD\nwas selected as the\nIEEE Micro’s Top Pick of 2023\n!\n[09/2022]\nOur\nViTCoD\nwas selected for\nMeta Faculty Research Award of 2022\n!\n[11\n/\n2022]\nOur\ni-FlatCam\nwon first place in\nUniversity Demonstration at DAC 2022\n!\n[12\n/\n2020]\nOur\nEarly-Bird Tickets\nwas accepted as\nSpotlight at ICLR 2020\n!\nServices\nConference Reviewer or TPC\nICML\n: 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nNeurIPS\n: 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025\nICLR\n: 2022, 2023, 2024, 2026\nCVPR\n: 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026\nICCV\n: 2023\nECCV\n: 2022, 2024\nAAAI\n: 2023, 2024\nDAC\n: 2026\nDATE\n: 2025\nMICRO\n: 2026\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems Part II (TCAS-II)\nIEEE Transactions on Parallel and Distributed Systems (TPDS)\nIEEE Transactions on Very Large Scale Integration Systems (TVLSI)\nJournal of Computer Science and Technology (JSTC)\nVolunteering Service\nStudent helper and website developer for the\nICCAD HALO Workshop\nStudent helper and website developer for the\nEECS Rising Stars Workshop of 2023\nAbout Me\nHaoran You (\n游浩然\n)\nPhD @ Georgia Tech\nContact\nhaoranyou98@gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nTwitter"
  },
