  "serper::Yan Zeng": {
    "homepage": "https://www.yan-zeng.com/",
    "emails": [
      "zeng@chem.fsu.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zeng Research Lab\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZeng Research Lab\nThe Zeng Research\nLab\ndevelops\ninnovative\nmaterials for clean energy technologies and chemical processes for critical energy\nminerals by integrating materials synthesis, characterization,\nlab automation\n,\nartificial intelligence\n, and thermodynamic modeling.\nAutonomous Laboratories\nLearn More >>>\nEnergy Materials\nLearn More >>>\nCritical Minerals\nLearn More >>>\nGroup\nUpdates\nNovember 2025, Dr. Zen\ng received the 2025 Materials Today Rising Star Award in Energy Conversion & Storage.\nCongrats 🎉\nNovember\n2025,\nAjay\npassed\nthe\ncandidacy exam. Congrats 🎉\nNovember 2025, Ashleigh joined the Zeng Lab. Welcome!\nOctober 2025,\nEvelyn defended\nher Master\n's thesis and becomes the first student graduated from the Zeng Lab.\nCongrats 🎉\nOctober 2025, Elena passed the candidacy exam.\nCongrats 🎉\nSeptember 2025, Dr. Zeng gave an invited talk at the 7th Battery and Energy Storage Conference | AIChE meeting and joined the panel discussion on AI for energy storage. - Check the\nlink\nAugust 2025, A co\nllaborative work between the Zeng, Ouyang, and Chen groups on discovering disordered cathode materials \"Origin of Enhanced Disorder in High Entropy Rocksalt Type Li-ion Battery Cathodes\" is published on EES Batteries - Check the\nlink\n📃\nAugust 2025, Elena Scivally was awarded the Dean’s Award for Doctoral Excellence (awarded to rising third-year students) Congrats 🎉\nJuly 2025, A forthcoming book \"Treatise on Process Metallurgy\" is posted, where Dr. Zeng and co-authors contributed to a chapter on \"Hydrometallurgical Processing of Li-ion Battery Materials\" - Check the\nlink\n📖\nJune 2025,\nWelcome\nKaia and Felix\n, high school students from the Young Scholars Program, joining us for summer research. They will be participating in\nsynthesis\nautomation and\nbattery\nprojects.\nJune 2025, A collaborative work between the Zeng and the Ouyang groups, \"Aqueous stability of metallic materials and metal oxides\", is published on Chemistry of Materials - Check the\nlink\n📃\nJune 2025,\nThe Zeng Lab paper \"\nAccelerated development of battery materials leveraging artificial intelligence and automation\n\" is published on\nMRS Communications\n- Check the\nlink\n📃\nMay 2025, Dr. Zeng has been selected as one of 36 recipients of the Oak Ridge Associated Universities (ORAU) Ralph E. Powe Junior Faculty Enhancement Awards - Check the\nlink\n🎊\nMay 2025, The Zeng Lab paper \"News and Views: Self-driving nanoparticle synthesis\" is published on Nature Chemical Engineering - Check the\nlink\n📃\nApril 2025, Dr. Zeng gave an invited talk at the MRS Spring conferences and was awarded the Early Career Distinguished Presenters.\nApril 2025, Dr. Zeng attended the 2nd Scialog\non Automating Chemical Laboratories - Check the\nlink\n💡\nFeb. 2025, The Zeng Lab has been funded as part of the DOE's Low-cost Earth-abundant Na-ion Storage (LENS) Consortium - Check the\nlink\n🔋\nFeb. 2025,\nThe Zeng Lab\npaper\non\nautonomous laboratories\nis published\ni\nn\nNature Computational Science\n- Check the\nlink\n📃\nNov. 2024, Welcome graduate students (Evelyn, Xiaozhao, Seth, Nat, Brandon) and a new postdoc (Dr. Tong Zhao) to the Zeng Lab!\nOct. 2024, The Zeng Lab paper on ionic conductors is published in Advanced Energy Materials - Check the\nlink\n📑\nSept. 2024, The Zeng Group and multiple rotating students set up a robotic liquid handler, named\nCirce\n(name credit: Elena). Circe has started to make materials 🧙🪄\nJune 2024, Welcome Josh, Tommy, and Zoe, high school students from the Young Scholars Program, joining us for summer research. They will be participating in lab automation and materials synthesis projects.\nMay 2024, Welcome Kayla to the Zeng group!\nApril 2024, Dr. Zeng\nwas\nselected as a Scialog Fellow on Automating Chemical Laboratories. She attended the conference in Tucson.\nMarch 2024, Dr. Zeng gave invited talks at th\ne\nACS Spring Meetings, Cornell MSE departmental semina\nr\n, and the ACerS-MRS Virtual Workshop.\nMarch 2024, Elena, Ajay, and Emily synthesized their first samples 🧪\nMarch 2024, Our first robot arm is set to run 🤖\nFeb. 2024, Welcome Emily to the Zeng group!\nJan. 2024, Welcome Elena, Ajay, and Yufang, to the Zeng group!\nJan. 2024, Dr. Zeng started as an Assistant Professor at Florida State University\nOpenings:\nThe Zeng group has Ph.D. and postdoctoral positions available. Interested in joining us?\nSend emails to Dr. Zeng for more information (\nzeng@chem.fsu.edu\n).\nFlorida State University\nDepartment of Chemistry & Biochemistry\nDr. Zeng's Google Scholar\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
