    "homepage_text": "Xiyang Dai · 戴希洋\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nXiyang Dai · 戴希洋\nMicrosoft AI\nPrincipal\nResearcher\nUniversity of Maryland - College Park\nDepartment of Computer Science\nComputer Vision Lab\nxdai<at>cs.umd.edu\nI finish my PhD at University of Maryland - College Park under the advising of Prof. Larry Davis. My research interests started with texture/fine-grained classification and settled down with human action understanding. Recent years, I have done works on action recognition and localization. I am a frequent competitor at ActivityNet challenge. If you have beaten me before during challenge, please let me know :-).\nBefore that, I had my master at NYU and studied shortly in Prof. Yann Lecun's lab doing robots staff.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
