    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Mingzhe Du's URCS Home Page\nMingzhe Du 杜明哲\nEmail: mdu5@cs.rochester.edu\nThe road ahead was steep and long, and I had no firm idea as to how to achieve my goals.\nFirst came the will to do it, then persistence and effort.\nAnd then maybe something else entirely.\n- The Forest of Wool and Steel\nHi, dear friends, welcome to my webpage.\nI am currently a 3rd-year PhD student at URCS, I'm working with\nProf.Michael L.Scott\n.\nI got my master degree at Shenzhen\n                        Institute of Advanced Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences under the guidance of\nProf.Yang Wang\n.\nMy research focuses on\n                        optimizing persistent memory performance for evolving software and hardware.\nPublication\n2021\nWentao Cai, Haosen Wen, Vladimir Maksimovski,\nMingzhe Du\n, Rafaello Sanna, Shreif\n                        Abdallah, Michael L.Scott. Fast nonblocking persistence for concurrent data structures. The 35th Internaltion Symposium on Distributed Computing (DISC'21)\nHaosen Wen, Wentao Cai,\nMingzhe Du\n, Louis Jenkins, Benjamin Valpey, Michael L.Scott. A fast,\n                        general system for buffered persistent data structures. The 50th International Conference on\n                        Parallel Processing (ICPP'21)\n2020\nHaosen Wen, Wentao Cai,\nMingzhe Du\n, Benjamin Valpey, Michael L.Scott. Brief announcement:\n                        Building fast recoverable persistent data structures with montage. The 34th International\n                        Symposium on Distributed Computing (DISC'20)\nMingzhe Du\nYang Wang and Chengzhong Xu, Xi Cheng. Algorithmics of Cost-Driven Computation Offloading in the Edge. ACM Transactions on Computers.\n2019\nMingzhe Du\nand Yang Wang. On Cost-Driven Computation Offloading in the Edge: A New Model Approach. The 19th Annual IEEE/ACM International Symposium in Cluster, Cloud, and Grid Computing.\n2018\nXingsheng Zhao, Jingwen Shi,\nMingzhe Du\n, Fan Ni, Song Jiang, Yang Wang. A Road-aware Spatial Mapping for Moving Objects. The 37th IEEE International Performance Computing and Communications Conference.\nProjects\nBuild Fast Recoverable Persistent Data Structure\nA Fusion Platform Blending Users, Edge Devices and Cloud Centers Based on Cloud Computing\nA Data-driven Technology for Self-adaptive and Self-evolution Applications\nDrought Monitoring and Early Warning System based on Big Data and Cloud Computing\nA very good poem that I'd like to share with you\nNew York is 3 hours ahead of California\nbut it does not make California slow\nSomeone graduated at the age of 22\nbut waited 5 years before securing a good job\nSomeone became a CEO at 25,and died at 50\nWhile another became a CEO at 50,and lived to 90 years\nSomeone is still single,while someone else got married\nObama retires at 55,but Trump starts at 70\nAbsolutely everyone in this world works based on their Time Zone\nPeople around you might seem to go ahead of you\nsome might seem to be behind you\nBut everyone is running their own RACE, in their own TIME\nDon’t envy them or mock them\nThey are in their TIME ZONE, and you are in yours\nLife is about waiting for the right moment to act\nSo, RELAX\nYou’re not LATE\nYou’re not EARLY\nYou are very much ON TIME, and in your, TIME ZONE Destiny set up for you.\nhere\nis my project proposal\nURCS People\nURCS Home Page"
  },
  "serper::Haoran Liu": {
