    "homepage_text": "International Society for Stem Cell Research\n0\nSkip to Content\nEnglish\nJoin the Society\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nEnglish\nJoin the Society\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nExcellence in stem cell science and applications to\nhuman health\n.\nUPCOMING EVENTS\nApr\n21\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\n11:00 – 12:30\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\nBeyond Breakthroughs: How We Preserve Innovation\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\n11:00 – 12:30\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\nAn ISSCR Webinar\n21 April 2026\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\n11:00 – 12:30\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\nMay\n12\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\n11:00 – 12:30\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\nInside Stem Cell Research Oversight: A Live Mock Committee Review\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\n11:00 – 12:30\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\nAn ISSCR Webinar\n12 May 2026\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\n11:00 – 12:30\n11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\nJun\n16\n11:00 AM – 11:45 AM\n11:00 – 11:45\n11:00 AM – 11:45 AM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\nISSCR 2026 Attendee Orientation Webinar\n11:00 AM – 11:45 AM\n11:00 – 11:45\n11:00 AM – 11:45 AM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\n16 June 2026\n11:00 AM – 11:45 AM\n11:00 – 11:45\n11:00 AM – 11:45 AM\nWebinar\n,\ntz-America/New_York\nJul\n8\n8:00 AM\n08:00\n8:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-America/Montreal\nISSCR 2026 Annual Meeting\n8:00 AM\n08:00\n8:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-America/Montreal\nJoin us in Montréal, Canada for the most comprehensive gathering in stem cell research.\n8-11 July 2026\n8:00 AM\n08:00\n8:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-America/Montreal\nSep\n23\n11:00 AM\n11:00\n11:00 AM\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\n,\nInternational Symposia\nThe Stem Cell & Developmental Biology Early Career Symposium\n11:00 AM\n11:00\n11:00 AM\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\n,\nInternational Symposia\nIn Collaboration with the Allen Institute and the Society for Development Biology\nSeattle, USA\n23-25 September 2026\n11:00 AM\n11:00\n11:00 AM\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\n,\nInternational Symposia\nOct\n19\n11:45 PM\n23:45\n11:45 PM\ntz-Asia/Tokyo\n,\nInternational Symposia\niPSC 20th Anniversary Symposium\n11:45 PM\n23:45\n11:45 PM\ntz-Asia/Tokyo\n,\nInternational Symposia\nKyoto, Japan\n20-22 October 2026\n11:45 PM\n23:45\n11:45 PM\ntz-Asia/Tokyo\n,\nInternational Symposia\nDec\n16\n11:00 AM\n11:00\n11:00 AM\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\n,\nInternational Symposia\nDisease Modeling and Drug Discovery Symposium\n11:00 AM\n11:00\n11:00 AM\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\n,\nInternational Symposia\nSan Diego, USA\n16-18 December 2026\n11:00 AM\n11:00\n11:00 AM\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\n,\nInternational Symposia\nJun\n15\n10:00 AM\n10:00\n10:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\nISSCR 2027 Annual Meeting\n10:00 AM\n10:00\n10:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\nJoin us in San Francisco, USA for the most comprehensive gathering in stem cell research.\n15-18 June 2027\n10:00 AM\n10:00\n10:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-America/Los_Angeles\nJun\n27\n3:00 AM\n03:00\n3:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-europe/copenhagen\nISSCR 2028 Annual Meeting\n3:00 AM\n03:00\n3:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-europe/copenhagen\nJoin us in Copenhagen, Denmark for the most comprehensive gathering in stem cell research.\n27-30 June 2028\n3:00 AM\n03:00\n3:00 AM\nAnnual Meeting\n,\ntz-europe/copenhagen\nNEWS\nMar 23, 2026\nISSCR 2025 Guidelines Update Now Available in Korean\nMar 23, 2026\nMar 23, 2026\nMar 13, 2026\nApplications Open for Stem Cell & Developmental Biology Early Career Symposium\nMar 13, 2026\nMar 13, 2026\nMar 12, 2026\nThe ISSCR Launches New Continuing Education Course on Stem Cell Therapies for Parkinson’s Disease\nMar 12, 2026\nMar 12, 2026\nMar 10, 2026\nHuman Biology, Better Medicines: Advancing iPSC-Based Models for Discovery and Development\nMar 10, 2026\nMar 10, 2026\nMar 9, 2026\nStem Cell Reports Seeks Associate Editor to Support Journal’s Growing Global Impact\nMar 9, 2026\nMar 9, 2026\nMar 9, 2026\nNew Podcast Episode. Making Sense of Touch\nMar 9, 2026\nMar 9, 2026\nMar 9, 2026\nMember Spotlight: Maike Sander, MD\nMar 9, 2026\nMar 9, 2026\nMar 5, 2026\nCloaked Stem Cells Evade Immune Rejection in Mice, Pointing to a Potential Universal Donor Cell Line\nMar 5, 2026\nMar 5, 2026\nMar 5, 2026\nmRNA Therapy Restores Fertility in Genetically Infertile Mice\nMar 5, 2026\nMar 5, 2026\nMar 3, 2026\nThe ISSCR Honors Alexander Meissner with the 2026 ISSCR Momentum Award for Exceptional Work in Developmental and Stem Cell Epigenetics\nMar 3, 2026\nMar 3, 2026\nMar 3, 2026\nThe ISSCR Honors Stem Cell COREdinates and CorEUstem with the 2026 ISSCR Public Service Award\nMar 3, 2026\nMar 3, 2026\nMar 3, 2026\nThe ISSCR Honors Dr. Kyle M. Loh with the 2026 Early Career Impact Award for Transformative Advances in Stem Cell Biology\nMar 3, 2026\nMar 3, 2026\nFeb 26, 2026\nThe ISSCR and The Stem Cell Podcast Partner on Special Series Spotlighting Early-Career Scientists\nFeb 26, 2026\nFeb 26, 2026\nFeb 23, 2026\nThe International Society for Stem Cell Research Honors Dr. Allen Eaves and the Late Dr. Connie Eaves with the 2026 ISSCR Lifetime Achievement Award\nFeb 23, 2026\nFeb 23, 2026\nFeb 17, 2026\nThe ISSCR to Open Elections for Officers and Directors 20 February 2026; Must be a Member in Good Standing to Cast a Ballot\nFeb 17, 2026\nFeb 17, 2026\nFeb 13, 2026\nThe ISSCR to Offer Travel Awards to KSSCR Members to Attend ISSCR 2026 in Montreal\nFeb 13, 2026\nFeb 13, 2026\nFeb 12, 2026\nAviv Regev to Deliver Keynote Address at ISSCR 2026 Annual Meeting in Montréal\nFeb 12, 2026\nFeb 12, 2026\nFeb 10, 2026\nWorking Group Members Appointed to the Global Workforce Development in Stem Cell Research and Regenerative Medicine Initiative\nFeb 10, 2026\nFeb 10, 2026\nFeb 10, 2026\nSteadfast Progress in Stem Cell Research: Reflections and Resolve at the Start of 2026\nFeb 10, 2026\nFeb 10, 2026\nFeb 10, 2026\nNew Podcast Episode. Illuminating hPSC-derived Sensory Neurons\nFeb 10, 2026\nFeb 10, 2026\nThe ISSCR’s Open Access Peer-Reviewed Scientific Journal\nStem Cell Reports\nis an open access forum communicating basic discoveries in stem cell research, in addition to translational and clinical studies.\nStem Cell Reports\nfocuses on manuscripts that report original research with conceptual or practical advances that are of broad interest to stem cell biologists and clinicians.\n\"\nStem Cell Reports\nserves as a vital platform for scientists, clinicians, and industry professionals to disseminate their findings on stem cell research, regenerative medicine, and cellular therapies. Its values reflect those of its host society, ISSCR: trustworthy and rigorous science as judged by scientific editors and reviewers who respect the standards laid down by ISSCR.\"  — Janet Rossant, Editor-in-Chief\nExplore the Journal\nNew On-Demand Continuing Education Course on Stem Cell Medicine\nDeveloped by the ISSCR Education Committee and jointly provided with Harvard Medical School, this open access course is designed for clinicians, medical students, and health care professionals. The curriculum is structured into seven expert-led video modules providing an overview of the field, from basic stem cell biology and clinical trials to ethical considerations surrounding unproven stem cell interventions and effective patient communication. Available in six languages and accredited for AMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ and American Nurses Credentialing Center (ANCC) contact hours.\nLearn More\nCurrent Initiatives\nPatient and Public Education\nAdding to ISSCR’s public resources,\nAboutStemCells.org\n, provides patients, families, and the public with trusted information about research and potential therapies...\nlearn more\nStandards Initiative\nInternational standards and best practices that set researchers up for success, ensure rigor in preclinical research, and strengthen the pipeline of therapies for patients…\nlearn more\nSyllabus and Learning Guide\nCurriculum to examine the basics of stem cell biology, key concepts of pluripotency, specification, differentiation, and the latest research technologies…\nlearn more\nPolicy and Regulatory Affairs\nAdvocating for stem cell funding, promoting integrity and ethics in research, preventing the marketing of unproven treatments, and facilitating informed regulatory decision making …\nlearn more\n“It’s unlikely that one person or one lab will solve a problem as big as degenerative diseases... It takes a\ncommunity of people\nin an area to solve a big problem.”\n—\nDoug Melton, PhD\n| ISSCR Founding Member and Vertex Pharmaceuticals Distinguished Fellow"
  },
