    "homepage_text": "Zhouhui Lian's Homepage\nZhouhui\nLian\n(è¿å®è¾)\nTenured Associate Professor (é¿èå¯ææãç ç©¶åãåå¯¼)\nWangxuan Institute of Computer Technology (WICT)\nPeking University\nNo. 128 Zhongguancun North Street, Haidian District\nBeijing\n,\nChina\nPhone: 8\n6\n-\n10-62768782\nEmail:\nlianzhouhui@pku.edu.cn\nOur research group:\nIGCL\nï¼ä¸­æçï¼\nNews\nBio\nResearch\nAchievements\nPublications\nCourses\nOthers\nNews\n:\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2026-02-23]Â\nOur papers \"FISHuman: Fine-grained Single-image 3D Human Reconstruction via Multi-view 4D Remeshing\" and \"Beyond Patches: Global-aware Autoregressive Model for Multimodal Few-Shot Font Generation\" have been accepted by CVPR 2026 (source code and data will be available)\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2026-02-23]Â\nOur paper \"ActMVS: Active Scene Reconstruction with Monocular Multi-View Stereo\" has been accepted by ICRA 2026 (source code and data are available)\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2025-11-24]Â\nOur paper \"IndoorUAV: Benchmarking Vision-Language UAV Navigation in Continuous Indoor Environments\" has been accepted by AAAI 2026 (source code and data are available)\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2025-11-24]Â\nOur paper \"UTDesign: A Unified Framework for Stylized Text Editing and Generation in Graphic Design Images\" has been accepted by SIGGRAPH Asia 2025 (source code and data will be available)\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2025-11-24]Â\nOur paper \"\nMMMG: A Massive, Multidisciplinary, Multi-Tier Generation Benchmark for Text-to-Image Reasoning\n\" has been accepted by NeurIPS 2025 (source code and data are available)\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2025-06-28]Â Our paper \"\nCalliReader: Contextualizing Chinese Calligraphy via an Embedding-Aligned Vision-Language Model\n\" has been accepted by ICCV 2025 (source code and data are available)\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2025-03-06]Â I will serve as a Technical Papers Committee Member for SIGGRAPH Asia 2025.\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2025-03-02]Â Our papers \"\nCreating Your Editable 3D Photorealistic Avatar with Tetrahedron-constrained Gaussian Splatting\n\" (\nhighlight\n), \"\nTexGaussian: Generating High-quality PBR Material via Octree-based 3D Gaussian Splatting\n\" and \"\nART: Anonymous Region Transformer for Variable Multi-Layer Transparent Image Generation\n\" have been accepted by CVPR 2025 (source code and data will be available)\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2025-02-18]Â I will serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 2025.\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2024-12-15]Â I will serve as an Area Chair for ICML 2025.\nÂ Â Â Â\n[2024-12-05]Â I will serve as an Area Chair for ICCV 2025.\nRepresentative Works:\nCanonical Forms for Non-rigid 3D Shape Retrieval\n(\nIJCV 2013\n,\n3DOR 2017\n)\n3D Shape Measures (rectilinearity, convexity)\n(\nIJCV 2010\n,\nCVPR 2012\n)\n3D Shape Retrieval Contest (SHREC)\n(\nIJCV 2016\n,\nPR 2013\n(ESI Highly Cited Paper)\n,\n3DOR 2015\n,\n14\n,\n11\n,\n10\n)\nAesthetic Assessment and Font Recognition for Chinese Characters\n(\nCVPR 2017\n,\nIJCAI 2015\n)\nGeneration of Chinese Fonts\n(\nwww.flexifont.com\n,\nSIGGRAPH (TOG) 19\n,\n20\n,\nSIGGRAPH ASIA (TOG) 19\n)\nTexture Transfer and Text Effects Transfer\n(\nCVPR 18\n,\n19\n,\n20\n)\nBio\n:\nI was graduated from School of Automation Science and Electrical Engineering, Beihang University in Sep. 2011 with Ph.D. From Jan. 2008 to Jan. 2009, supported by the China Scholarship Council (CSC), I visited School of Computer Science, Cardiff University, UK as a visiting scholar. Then, I worked as a Guest Researcher at the Information Technology Lab (ITL), National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST), U.S. from Jul. 2009 to Jul. 2011. After that, I came back to China and worked as a postdoctoral researcher at ICST, Peking University, where I became an Assistant Professor in Jun. 2013. I was promoted to Associate Professor in Aug. 2015 and Tenured Associate Professor in Feb. 2026.\nEducation:\n0\n9/2005~06/2011  Ph.D., School of Automation Science and Electrical Engineering, Beihang University, Beijing, China.\n09/2001~07/2005  B.Eng., College of Automation Engineering, Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics, Nanjing, China.\nWorking Experience:\n02/2026~now, Tenured Associate Professor, Wangxuan Institute of Computer Technology, Peking University, Beijing, China\n08/2015~01/2026, Associate Professor,\nWangxuan Institute of Computer Technology\n, Peking University, Beijing, China\n06/2013~08/2015, Assistant Professor, Institute of Computer Science and Technology, Peking University, Beijing, China\n07/2011~06/2013, Postdoctoral Researcher, Institute of Computer Science and Technology, Peking University, Beijing, China\n07/2009~07/2011, Guest Researcher, Information Technology Laboratory, National Institute of Standards and Technology, USA\n01/2008~01/2009, Academic Visitor, School of Computer Science, Cardiff University, UK\nResearch\n:\nÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â\nBack to top\nMy research interests include\nComputer Graphics,\nComputer Vision, and Artificial Intelligence. More specifically, we have been working on the following topics in the last few years: (1) Font Synthesis; (2) Text Image Analysis and Synthesis; (3) 3D Content Generation.\nStudents:\nPhD Students:\nGuo Pu\nYuxuan Luo\nYixuan Han\nMaster Students:\nXu Liu\nYiming Zhao\nHanxi Liu\nHao Yuan\nLingyun Xie\nAlumni\nBojun Xiong\n(Master 2025)\nHua Li\n(Master 2025)\nYitian Liu\n(PhD 2024)\nShilong Li (Master 2024)\nZeqing Xia\n(PhD 2023)\nJialei Cui (Master 2023)\nShiyao Xu\n(Master 2023)\nZenggui Chen\n(Master 2023)\nYuqing Wang\n(Master 2023)\nYizhi Wang\n(PhD 2022)\nJie Chen\n(Master 2021)\nYue Gao\n(Master 2021)\nShuseng Tang\n(Master 2021)\nTao Sheng\n(Master 2021)\nXiang Zhang\n(Master 2021)\nYifang Men\n(Master 2020)\nXiao Sun\n(Master 2020)\nYichen Gao\n(Master 2020)\nWenguan Wang\n(Master 2020)\nJuncheng Liu\n(PhD 2019)\nYuan Guo\n(Master 2019)\nYue Jiang\n(Master 2019)\nXudong Chen (Master 2017)\nChendong Liu (Master 2017)\nWeikang Song (Master 2016)\nRongju Sun (Master 2016)\nWanqiong Pan (Master 2015)\nHao Sun (Master 2015)\nJun Zhang (Master 2015)\nWenyan Dong (Master 2015)\nTianyang Yi (Master 2014)\nChenxi Wang (Master 2013)\nYang Liu (Master 2012)\nHongmei Li (Master 2012)\nReading List:\nÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â\nAchievements\n:\nÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â\nBack to top\nI have published more than 100 academic papers in\nprestigious journals and conferences (e.g., ToG, TPAMI, IJCV, SIGGRAPH/SIGGRAPH Asia, CVPR, NeurIPS, ICCV, etc)\n.\nI was the principal investigator of several projects funded by the National Natural Science Foundation of China, Beijing Nova Program of Science and Technology, etc., and have led our group to successfully develop practical systems for the generation of Chinese fonts. These systems and techniques related to computer fonts have been adopted by a company called Founder Handwriting since 2016 to create font products that have served millions of users, making significant social and economic benefits.\nÂ Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â\nPublications (selected):\nÂ\nÂ Â Â Â Â Â\nBack to top\nY. Luo, J. Tang, C. Huang, F. Ma,\nZ. Lian*\n, CalliReader: Contextualizing Chinese Calligraphy via an Embedding-Aligned Vision Language Model,\nICCV\n2025\nH. Liu, Y. Men,\nZ. Lian*\n, Creating Your Editable 3D Photorealistic Avatar with Tetrahedron-constrained Gaussian Splatting,\nCVPR\n2025 (\nHighlight\n, Acceptance rate 2.9%)\nB. Xiong, J. Liu, J. Hu, C. Wu, J. Wu, X. Liu, C. Zhao, E. Ding,\nZ. Lian*\n, TexGaussian: Generating High-quality PBR Material via Octree-based 3D Gaussian Splatting,\nCVPR\n2025\nY. Pu, Y. Zhao, Z. Tang, R. Yin, H. Ye, Y. Yuan, D. Chen, J. Bao, S. Zhang, Y. Wang, L. Liang, L. Wang, J. Li, X. Li,\nZ. Lian\n, G. Huang, B. Guo, ART: Anonymous Region Transformer for Variable Multi-Layer Transparent Image Generation,\nCVPR\n2025\nH. Li,\nZ. Lian*\n, HFH-Font: Few-shot Chinese Font Synthesis with Higher Quality, Faster Speed, and Higher Resolution, ACM Transactions on Graphics (\nTOG\n) (presented at\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2024\n)\nG. Pu, Y. Zhao,\nZ. Lian*\n, Pano2Room: Novel View Synthesis from a Single Indoor Panorama.\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n2024\nY. Zhao,\nZ. Lian*\n, UDiffText: A Unified Framework for High-quality Text Synthesis in Arbitrary Images via Character-aware Diffusion Models,\nECCV\n2024 (\ncode\n)\nY. Liu,\nZ. Lian*\n. QT-Font: High-efficiency Font Synthesis via Quadtree-based Diffusion Models,\nSIGGRAPH\n2024 (\nCode\n)\nY. Men, B. Lei, Y. Yao, M. Cui,\nZ. Lian\n, X. Xie. En3D: An Enhanced Generative Model for Sculpting 3D Humans from 2D Synthetic Data,\nCVPR\n2024 (\nCode\n)\nY. Men, H. Liu, Y. Yao, M. Cui, X. Xie,\nZ. Lian*\n, 3DToonify: Creating Your High-Fidelity 3D Stylized Avatar Easily from 2D Portrait Images,\nCVPR\n2024\nJ. Cui, J. Du, W. Liu,\nZ. Lian*\n, TextNeRF: A Novel Scene-Text Image Synthesis Method based on Neural Radiance Fields,\nCVPR\n2024 (\nCode\n)\nY. Liu,\nZ. Lian\n*. DeepCalliFont: Few-shot Chinese Calligraphy Font Synthesis by Integrating Dual-modality Generative Models.\nAAAI\n2024 (\nCode\n)\nY. Luo, Z. Wu,\nZ. Lian*\n, CalliRewrite: Recovering Handwriting Behaviors from Calligraphy Images without Supervision,\nICRA\n2024  (\nCode\n) (Selected as a\nFinalist of\nIEEE ICRA Best Paper Award in Service Robotics\n)\nG. Pu, Y. Men, Y. Mao, Y. Jiang, W. Ma,\nZ. Lian*\n. Controllable Image Synthesis with Attribute-Decomposed GAN.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(\nTPAMI\n). 2023 (\nCode\n)\nG. Pu, P.-S. Wang,\nZ. Lian*\n. SinMPI: Novel View Synthesis from a Single Image with Expanded Multiplane Images.\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n2023\nY. Wang, Y. Wang, L. Yu, Y. Zhu,\nZ. Lian*\n. DeepVecFont-v2: Exploiting Transformers to Synthesize Vector Fonts with Higher Quality.\nCVPR\n2023\nZ. Xia, B. Xiong,\nZ. Lian*\n. VecFontSDF: Learning to Reconstruct and Synthesize High-quality Vector Fonts via Signed Distance Functions.\nCVPR\n2023\nC. Xiao, W. Su, J. Liao, Z. Lian, Y. Song, H. Fu. How Differently Do People Sketch 3D Objects?\nACM Transactions on Graphics (\nTOG\n)\n(presented at\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2022\n)\nY. Men, Y. Yao, M. Cui,\nZ. Lian\n*, X. Xie. DCT-Net: Domain-calibrated Translation for Portrait Stylization.\nACM Transactions on Graphics (\nTOG\n)\n. (Accepted)(to be presented at\nSIGGRAPH 2022\n)  (\nCode\n)\nZ. Chen,\nZ. Lian*\n. Semi-supervised Semantic Segmentation via Prototypical Contrastive Learning.\nACM\nMM\n2022\nY. Wang, G. Pu, W. Luo, Y. Wang, P. Xio...[truncated]"
