  "serper::Yujie Wu": {
    "homepage": "https://yujiewu66.github.io/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yujie’s Personal Homepage | Yujie’s Personal Homepage\nYujie's Personal Homepage\nMy name is Yujie Wu. My contact information is\nhere\n.\nI am a postdoc researcher at the University of Potsdam from fall 2025 to summer 2026, sponsored by the ERC project Comparison and rigidity for scalar curvature “COMSCAL” of\nRudolf Zeidler\n.\nStarting fall 2026, I will be a postdoc researcher at Carnegie Mellon University, mentored by\nRobin Neumayer\n.\nI was a graduate student in the\nmath\ndepartment at Stanford University from Sep 2020 to June 2025. My advisor is\nOtis Chodosh\n.\nMy research area is Differential Geometry, Analysis and PDEs. In particular, I am interested in\nminimal (hyper)surfaces\n; I have recently worked on projects that study how the ambient manifolds’ geometry (in particular their curvature assumptions) influence the topology and geometry of their immersed and embedded stable minimal (hyper)surfaces. I am also thinking about the\nAllen-Cahn\nequation and their relations to minimal surface theory.\nYou can find me on\narxiv\n,\nGoogle Scholar\nand\nORCiD\n.\nPapers\nComparison Theorems and the Intermediate Ricci Curvature Assumption.\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2510.11205\nRigidity of Complete Free Boundary Minimal Hypersurfaces in Convex NNSC Manifolds.\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2504.20585\nCapillary surfaces in manifolds with nonnegative scalar curvature and strictly mean convex boundary.\nInternational Mathematics Research Notices\n, Volume 2025, Issue 9, May 2025\nJournal Link\nFree Boundary Stable Minimal Hypersurfaces in Positively Curved 4-Manifolds.\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2308.08103\nDisssertation\n“Capillary Hypersurfaces and Variational Methods in Positively Curved Manifolds with Boundary.”\nDownload.\nAdvisor:\nOtis Chodosh\nMaster Thesis\n“Construction of Harmonic Maps by MinMax Methods.”\nDownload.\nAdvisor:\nTristan Rivière\n.\nTalks\nApplication of Curvature Comparison Theorems in Minimal Surfaces\nOberseminar Differentialgeometrie,\nUniversity of Augsburg\n, [Jan 2026]\nGNOSC Seminar,\nOnline\n,\nlink to talk\n, [Dec 2025]\nOberseminar Differential Geometry,\nUniversität Münster, Mathematisches Institut\n, [Nov 2025]\nCapillary Hypersurfaces and Variational Methods\nSlides.\nWorkshop on Curvature and Global Shape,\nUniversität Münster, Mathematisches Institut\n, [Aug 2025]\nGeometry Seminar,\nUniversity of Potsdam\n, [Jun 2025]\nFrom $\\mu$-bubble to $\\theta$-bubble: Geometry of Mean Convex Manifolds with NNSC\nGeometry Seminar,\nRice University\n. [Mar 2025]\nDifferential Geometry Seminar,\nUC Berkeley\n. [Mar 2025]\nGeometric Analysis Seminar,\nUniversity of Chicago\n. [Feb 2025]\nGeometry and Topology Seminar,\nUniversity of Wisconsin-Madison\n. [Feb 2025]\nCapillary surfaces in manifolds with nonnegative scalar curvature and strictly mean convex boundary\nConvergence Or Scalar Curvature Seminar (COSC), Online. [Dec 2024]\nYMSC-BJTU Geometry Seminar, Online,\nTsinghua University\n. [Nov 2024]\nGeometric Analysis Seminar, Online,\nBICMR, Peking University\n. [Oct 2024]\nFree boundary stable minimal hypersurfaces in positively curved 4-manifolds:\nGeometry and Analysis Seminar,\nUniversity of California, Santa Cruz\n. [Nov 2023]\nTeaching\nTeaching Assistant\n, Stanford University\nGuide\nto Stanford introductory math courses.\nMath 51: Linear Algebra, Multivariable Calculus, and Modern Applications\n[Winter 2022, Fall 2022, Winter 2023]\nMath 52: Integral Calculus of Several Variables [Winter 2024]\nMath 21: Calculus [Fall 2024]\nCourse Assistant\n, Stanford University\nMath 104: Applied Matrix Theory [Summer 2021, Winter 2025]\nMath 173: Theory of Partial Differential Equations [Spring 2022]\nMath 205A: Real Analysis [Fall 2023]\nCourse Assistant\n, ETH Zurich\nAlgebra I\n: Groups, Rings and Fields [Autumn 2018]\nAlgebra II\n: Galois Theory and Applications [Spring 2019]\nProbability and Statistics\n[Spring 2020]\nOthers\nStanford Geometry Seminar (\nlink\n).\nStanford Student Analysis Seminar (\nlink\n).\nStanford Women in Math Mentoring ( SWIMM 2024 Fall is\nhere\n. Past\nevents\n).\nSWIMM is a mentoring program pairing undergraduates interested in math and computational science with graduate student mentors from math, statistics, and ICME. We also host events, including study halls, dinners, and talks.\nThis site is open source. Made with Github Pages, using Primer, a Jekyll theme."
  },
  "serper::Runmin Cong": {
    "homepage": "https://rmcong.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "rmcong@sdu.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Runmin Cong\nRunmin Cong\nHome\nProfile\nPublications\nAI COURSE\nMVP Group\n中文简介\nContact\nRunmin Cong, a Professor with the School of Control Science and Engineering, Shandong University (SDU), Jinan, China. \n\t  Dr. Cong is the director of\nMultimedia and Vision Processing Group (MVP Group)\n, which is affiliated to the Key Laboratory of Machine Intelligence & System Control，Ministry of Education. \n\t  His current research interests include\nArtificial Intelligence, Pattern Recognition, Machine Learning, Low-altitude Intelligence, and Embodied Perception.\nHe has published more than 120 IEEE/ACM Trans/CCF-A papers, and has received more than 20 awards, including the IEEE SPS Best Paper Award and IEEE Chester W. Sall Award.\n丛润民，山东大学控制科学与工程学院教授、博士生导师、\n国家高层次青年人才计划入选者\n，主要研究方向包括人工智能、模式识别、机器学习、低空智能、具身感知等。在TPAMI、IJCV、CVPR、NeurIPS等CCF-A、IEEE/ACM Trans上发表论文120余篇，\n\t\t获天津市科学技术进步一等奖、中国煤炭工业协会科学技术奖一等奖、中国图象图形学学会自然科学奖二等奖、山东计算机学会自然科学奖一等奖、科睿唯安全球高被引科学家、IEEE SPS Best Paper Award（IEEE TIP期刊最佳论文奖）、IEEE Chester W. Sall Memorial Award（IEEE TCE期刊最佳论文奖）等。\nOpen Positions:\nI am looking for self-motivated candidates who have solid mathematical backgrounds, strong English ability, and strong coding skills, including senior undergraduate and postgraduate.\n\t  If you are interested in doing research on Computer Vision and Machine Learning, please drop me an e-mail (rmcong@sdu.edu.cn) with your detailed CV.\n招收山东大学2026级博士生1-2名（已招满），硕士研究生1-2名（已招满），欢迎电邮咨询 (rmcong@sdu.edu.cn).\n招收博士后1-2名，薪资在26万/年~46万/年，具体详见\n招聘公告\n，欢迎电邮咨询 (rmcong@sdu.edu.cn).\nImportant Notice:\n山东大学\n人工智能课程枢纽\n正式上线，内容包括通识课程资源（本科32学时版、研究生16学时版）和专业课程资源（本科64学时版），欢迎关注！\n欢迎大家关注“MVP Lab成果分享”系列视频\n[点击访问B站视频合集]\nRecent News\n2026/03 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Image Processing\n(CCF A, JCR Q1).\n2026/03 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\n(JCR Q1).\n2026/02 -- Two papers have been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Image Processing\n(CCF A, JCR Q1).\n2026/02 -- Two papers have been accepted by\nCVPR 2026\n(CCF A).\n2026/02 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Multimedia\n(JCR Q1).\n2026/01 -- I was appointed as the\nAssociate Editor\nof the\nPattern Recognition\n(JCR Q1, IF：7.6).\n2026/01 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\n(JCR Q1).\n2025/12 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(JCR Q1, CCF A).\n2025/11 -- I am honored to be recognised as\nHighly Cited Researchers\nby Clarivate.\n2025/11 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(JCR Q1, CCF A).\n2025/11 -- Three papers have been accepted by\nAAAI 2026\nwith two Orals (CCF A).\n2025/10 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Geoscience and Remote Sensing\n(JCR Q1).\n2025/07 -- Four papers have been accepted by\nACM MM 2025\n(CCF A).\n2025/05 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Image Processing\n(CCF A, JCR Q1).\n2025/05 -- One paper has been accepted by\nICML 2025\n(CCF A).\n2025/04 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Multimedia\n(JCR Q1).\n2025/03 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\n(JCR Q1).\n2025/02 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(JCR Q1).\n2025/02 -- One paper has been accepted by\nCVPR 2025\n.\n2025/02 -- I am honored to be recognised as one of the\nTop 0.05% Highly Ranked Scholars\nby ScholarGPS.\n2025/01 -- One paper has been newly selected as\nESI Highly Cited Paper\n(\nTop 1%\nof papers in the academic field).\n2025/01 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Image Processing\n(JCR Q1).\n2025/01 -- One paper has been accepted by\nICLR 2025\n.\n2025/01 -- One paper has been accepted by\nIEEE Trans. Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\n(JCR Q1)."
  },
