    "homepage_text": "Bowen Du – Department of Civil & Mineral Engineering\nSkip to content\nU of T ENGINEERING\nU of T Home\nGive Now\nUrgent Support\nContact\nSearch for:\nSubmit Search\nMain Menu\nDepartment of Civil & Mineral Engineering\nFacebook\nTwitter/X\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nYoutube\nPosted October 16th, 2018\nby\nJeffrey Siegel\nBowen Du\nBackground\nI spent 7 years studying building science, HVAC, and Indoor Air in Tongji University, China before I came to UofT\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests mainly lie in assessing the impacts of indoor environmental quality on occupant health and performance. Currently, I pay major attetion to CO2 and other pollutants and their impacts on cognitive performance\nProjects\nPublications\nDu B, Schwartz-Narbonne H, Tandoc M, Heffernan EM, Mack ML, Siegel JA. 2021. The impact of emissions from an essential oil diffuser on cognitive performance. Early view in\nIndoor Air\n. DOI:\n10.1111/ina.12919\n|\nSummary\n|\nIEQ and Cognitive Function\nSchwartz-Narbonne H, Du B, Siegel JA. 2021. Volatile organic compound and particulate matter emissions from an ultrasonic essential oil diffuser.\nIndoor Air\n,\n31(6)\n, 1982-1992. DOI:\n10.1111/ina.12845\n|\nSummary\n|\nIndoor Chemistry\nGivehchi R, Du B, Razavi M, Tan Z, Siegel JA. 2021. Performance of nanofibrous media in portable air cleaners.\nAerosol Science and Technology\n,\n55(7)\n, 805-816. DOI:\n10.1080/02786826.2021.1901846\n|\nSummary\n|\nFiltration Performance\nMatava C, Collard V, Siegel J, Denning S, Li T, Du B, Fiadjoe J, Fiset P, Engelhardt T. 2020. Use of a high-flow extractor to reduce aerosol exposure in tracheal intubation.\nBritish Journal of Anaesthesia\n,\n125\n, E363-366. DOI:\n10.1016/j.bja.2020.07.014\n|\nSummary\n|\nOperating Room Ventilation\nDu B, Tandoc M, Mack M, Siegel JA. 2020. Indoor CO\n2\nconcentrations and cognitive function: A critical review.\nIndoor Air\n,\n30(6)\n, 1067-1082. DOI:\n10.1111/ina.12706\n|\nSummary\n|\nIEQ and Cognitive Function\nJarvis S, Du B, Siegel JA. 2020. Impact of houseplants on cognitive function. Indoor Air 2020: Proceedings of the 16th International Conference on Indoor Air and Climate, Paper 830.\nDu B, Schwartz-Narbonne H, Tandoc M, Mack M, Siegel JA. 2020. Cognitive Impact of Essential Oil Emissions: Pollutant and Odor Effects. Indoor Air 2020: Proceedings of the 16th International Conference on Indoor Air and Climate, Paper 201\nDu B, Schwartz-Narbonne H, Siegel JA. 2020. Particle Emissions from Essential Oil Diffusers. Indoor Air 2020: Proceedings of the 16th International Conference on Indoor Air and Climate, Paper 210.\nScholarships\nOntario Trillium Scholarship\nPersonal Web Site:\nwww.researchgate.net/profile/Bowen_Du6\nPosted in\nSiegel Students\n© 2026 Faculty of Applied Science and Engineering\nU of T Home\nAccessibility\nPrivacy\nStudent Data Practices\nWebsite Feedback"
