    "homepage_text": "Zijia Lin's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZijia Lin's Homepage\nZijia Lin\n1,2\nPh.D.\n1\nInstitute of Information System & Engineering\n,\nSchool of Software\n2\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nTsinghua University\n, Beijing, 100084, China\nEmail: linzijia07 [AT] tsinghua [DOT] org [DOT] cn\nI achieved my Ph.D. degree in 2016 from Department of Computer Science & Technology, Tsinghua University, and my Bachelor degree in 2011 from School of Software, Tsinghua University. I worked with Professor Guiguang Ding on large-scale image retrieval and multi-label learning.\nRight now I am a Lead Researcher in Microsoft Research Asia. For the full list of my publications, please refer to my\nGoogle Scholar\npage and\nDBLP\npage.\nEducation\n2011 - 2016\n2007 - 2011\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University\nPh.D. in Computer Science and Technology\nGPA: 96.1/100 (Rank: 1/156 in the department, up to 04/2015)\nSchool of Software, Tsinghua University\nB.Eng. in Computer Software\nGPA: 91.1/100 (Rank: 3/63 in the school)\nResearch Interests\n1) Multimedia information retrieval: image auto-annotation / tag-refinement, hashing methods, etc.\n2) Natural language understanding: named entity recognition, dialog policy learning, etc.\nConference Publications\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Mingqing Hu, Jianmin Wang: Semantics-Preserving Hashing for Cross-View Retrieval. CVPR 2015: 3864-3872 [\npdf\n] [\ncodes\n]\n--\nUpdate:\nIn our experiments, for MIRFlickr, instances with only one textual tag were also removed, so as to make the text view of each remaining instance more like a textual document with multiple words.\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Mingqing Hu, Jianmin Wang: Multi-label Classification via Feature-aware Implicit Label Space Encoding. ICML 2014: 325-333 [\npdf\n] [\nslides\n] [\ncodes\n]\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Mingqing Hu: Multi-source Image Auto-annotation. ICIP 2013: 2567-2571 (Oral, Top 10% Paper) [\npdf\n] [\nslides\n]\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Mingqing Hu, Jianmin Wang, Xiaojun Ye: Image Tag Completion via Image-Specific and Tag-Specific Linear Sparse Reconstructions. CVPR 2013: 1618-1625 [\npdf\n] [\ndata\n] [\ncodes\n]\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Mingqing Hu, Jianmin Wang, Jiaguang Sun: Automatic Image Annotation using Tag-Related Random Search over Visual Neighbors. CIKM 2012: 1784-1788 [\npdf\n]\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Jianmin Wang: Image Annotation Based on Recommendation Model. SIGIR 2011: 1097-1098 [\npdf\n]\nJournal Publications\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Jungong Han, Ling Shao: End-to-End Feature-Aware Label Space Encoding for Multilabel Classification With Many Classes. IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems. (Preprint), 2017 [\npdf\n][codes]\n--\nAn extension to substantially improve the efficiency and the effectiveness of our proposed method in ICML 2014 paper.\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Jungong Han, Jianmin Wang: Cross-View Retrieval via Probability-Based Semantics-Preserving Hashing. IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics. (Preprint), 2016 [\npdf\n][\ncodes\n]\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Mingqing Hu: Image Auto-annotation via Tag-dependent Random Search over Range-constrained Visual Neighbours. Multimedia Tools and Applications. Vol. 74, Pages 4091-4116, 2015 [\npdf\n]\nZijia Lin\n,\nGuiguang Ding, Mingqing Hu, Yunzhen Lin, Shuzhi Sam Ge: Image Tag Completion via Dual-view Linear Sparse Reconstructions. Computer Vision and Image Understanding. Vol. 124, Pages 42-60, 2014 [\npdf\n]\nRecent Honors & Awards\nCommunity Service\nReviewer for IEEE Transactions on Image Processing, IEEE Transactions on Multimedia, IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology, Computer Vision and Image Understanding, Multimedia Tools and Applications\nPC Member / Reviewer for AAAI 2018\nOther Stuff\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
