    "homepage_text": "About Me - Lianghao Xia\nLianghao Xia 夏良昊\nFull Professor\nFollow\nShenzhen, China\nHarbin Institute of Technology (Shenzhen)\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nAbout Me\nI am a professor at the School of Computer Science and Technology, Harbin Institute of Technology (Shenzhen). I was a research assistant professor at The University of Hong Kong. I received my Ph.D. (2021) and Bachelor's (2017) from South China University of Technology.\nMy research focuses on LLM agents, AI-Generated Content (AIGC), graph foundation models, retrieval-augmented generation, and recommendation systems.\nJoin Us!\nI am actively recruiting\nPh.D. (2027) and M.S. (2026) students\n. I also regularly accept\nundergraduate and graduate student interns\n, with remote internship opportunities available. Please feel free to\ncontact me at xialh@hit.edu.cn\nalong with your CV.\nHonors and Awards\n📊 Google Scholar citation\n8000+\n, h-index\n44\n, i-10 index\n60\n🏆\nWorld’s Top 2% Scientists\n2024 and 2025 published by Stanford University\n🌟 2025 World AI Conference\n“Rising Star” Candidate Award\n🎖️\nAI 2000 Most Influential Scholars\nby Aminer.\nACM MM 2024\nBest Paper Nomination & Honorable Mention Award\nWWW 2023\nBest Paper Nomination & Spotlight Paper\nWSDM 2022\nBest Paper Nomination & Top-3 Most Cited Paper\nWSDM 2023\nTop-1 Most Cited Paper\nICLR 2023\nSpotlight Paper\n(Top 25%)\n1 × KDD 2024\nMost Influential Papers\n(Rank 6th / 559 Accepted Papers)\n1 × WWW 2024\nMost Influential Papers\n(Rank 1st / 405 Accepted Papers)\n3 × WWW 2023\nMost Influential Papers\n(Rank 3th, 5th, 8th / 323 Accepted Papers)\n1 × SIGIR 2023\nMost Influential Papers\n(Rank 7th / 165 Accepted Papers)\n2 × KDD 2023\nMost Influential Papers\n(Rank 6th, 7th / 497 Accepted Papers)\n2 × SIGIR 2022\nMost Influential Papers\n(Rank 2nd, 3rd / 161 Accepted Papers)\n2 × KDD 2022\nMost Influential Papers\n(Rank 12th, 15th / 450 Accepted Papers)\n1 × SIGIR 2021\nMost Influential Papers\n(Rank 13th / 151 Accepted Papers)\nSelected Publications\n*\nEqual contribution\n†\nCorresponding author\n[Under Review]\n“ViMax: Agentic Video Generation”\n#14 Repo of the Day, GitHub Trending Board, GitHub Stars 1400+\nL. Huang\n*\n, S. He\n*\n, H. Zhou\n*\n, Y. Huang, S. Wu,\nL. Xia\n†\n, C. Huang\n†\n[code & demos]\n[Under Review]\n“VideoAgent: All-in-One Agentic Framework for Video Understanding, Editing, and Remaking”\nReceives over 300 GitHub Stars\nH. Zhou\n*\n, L. Huang\n*\n, S. Wu,\nL. Xia\n†\n, C. Huang\n†\n[code & demos]\n[NeurIPS’25]\n“AI-Researcher: Autonomous Scientific Innovation”\nReceives over 3.8k GitHub Stars\nJ. Tang\n*\n,\nL. Xia\n*\n, Z. Li, C. Huang\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[EMNLP’25]\n“LightRAG: Simple and Fast Retrieval-Augmented Generation”\nReceives over 12k GitHub Stars\nZ. Guo,\nL. Xia\n, Y. Yu, T. Ao, and C. Huang\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[EMNLP’24]\n“OpenGraph: Towards Open Graph Foundation Models”\nReceives over 300 GitHub Stars, Citation 70+\nL. Xia\n, B. Kao, and C. Huang\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[KDD’24]\n“UrbanGPT: Spatio-Temporal Large Language Models”\nMost Influential Papers of KDD’24 (Rank 6 / 559)\nZ. Li,\nL. Xia\n, J. Tang, Y. Xu, L. Xia, D. Yin, and C. Huang\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[MM’24]\n“DiffMM: Multi-Modal Diffusion Model for Recommendation”\nBest Paper Nomination & Honorable Mention Award\nY. Jiang,\nL. Xia\n, W. Wei, D. Luo, K. Lin, and C. Huang\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[WWW’24]\n“RLMRec: Representation Learning with Large Language Models for Recommendation”\nMost Influential Papers of WWW’24 (Rank 1 / 405)\nX. Ren, W. Wei,\nL. Xia\n, L. Su, S. Cheng, J. Wang, D. Yin and C. Huang\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[WWW’23]\n“Automated Self-Supervised Learning for Recommendation”\nSpotlight Paper & Best Paper Nomination (16 / 323), Most Influential Papers of WWW’23 (Rank 8 / 323)\nL. Xia\n, C. Huang, C.Z. Huang, K. Lin, T. Yu and B. Kao\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[WWW’23]\n“Graph-less Collaborative Filtering”\nL. Xia\n, C. Huang, J. Shi and Y. Xu\nCitation 70+\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[ICLR’23]\n“LightGCL: Simple Yet Effective Graph Contrastive Learning for Recommendation”\nSelected as Spotlight Paper (Top 25%), Citation 500+\nX. Cai, C. Huang,\nL. Xia\nand X. Ren\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[SIGIR’22]\n“Hypergraph Contrastive Collaborative Filtering”\nMost Influential Papers of SIGIR’22 (Rank 3 / 161), Citation 500+\nL. Xia\n, C. Huang, Y. Xu, J. Zhao, D. Yin and J. Huang\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[KDD’22]\n“Self-Supervised Hypergraph Transformer for Recommender Systems”\nMost Influential Papers of KDD’22 (Rank 15 / 450), Citation 180+\nL. Xia\n, C. Huang and C. Zhang\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[TKDE’22]\n“Multi-Behavior Sequential Recommendation with Temporal Graph Transformer”\nCitation 100+\nL. Xia\n, C. Huang Y. Xu, and J. Pei\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[WSDM’22]\n“Contrastive Meta Learning with Behavior Multiplicity for Recommendation”\nBest Paper Nomination & Most Cited Papers of WSDM’22 (Rank 3 / 159)\nW. Wei, C. Huang,\nL. Xia\n, Y. Xu, J. Zhao, D. Yin\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[SIGIR’21]\n“Graph Meta Network for Multi-Behavior Recommendation”\nMost Influential Papers of SIGIR’21 (Rank 13 / 151), Citation 270+\nL. Xia\n, Y. Xu, C. Huang, P. Dai and L. Bo\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[AAAI’21]\n“Knowledge-Enhanced Hierarchical Graph Transformer Network for Multi-Behavior Recommendation”\nCitation 280+\nL. Xia\n, C. Huang, Y. Xu, P. Dai, M. Lu and L. Bo\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[IJCAI’21]\n“Spatial-Temporal Sequential Hypergraph Network for Crime Prediction with Dynamic Multiplex Relation Learning”\nCitation 100+\nL. Xia\n, C. Huang, Y. Xu, P. Dai, L. Bo, X. Zhang, T. Chen\n[pdf]\n[code]\n[SIGIR’20]\n“Multiplex Behavioral Relation Learning for Recommendation via Memory Augmented Transformer Network”\nCitation 180+\nL. Xia\n, C. Huang, Y. Xu, P. Dai, B. Zhang and L. Bo\n[pdf]\n[code]\nWork Experience\nHarbin Institute of Technology (Shenzhen)\n11/2025 - Present\nProfessor, School of Computer Science and Technology\nThe University of Hong Kong\n11/2024 - 11/2025\nResearch Assistant Professor, School of Computing and Data Science\nThe University of Hong Kong\n04/2022 - 11/2024\nPostdoctoral Fellow, Department of Computer Science\nEducation Background\nSouth China University of Technology\n09/2017 - 12/2021\nPh.D. in Computer Science and Technology\nSouth China University of Technology\n09/2013 - 06/2017\nBachelor in Computer Science and Technology (English-Taught Class)\nServices\nSenior PC / Area Chair:\nAAAI, ARR\nPC Member / Reviewer:\nSIGIR, KDD, WWW, AAAI, NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, ARR, CIKM, SDM\nJournal Reviewer:\nIEEE TKDE, IEEE TBD, IEEE TNNLS, IEEE TLT, IEEE TNSE, ACM TOIS, ACM TWEB, ACM TKDD, ACM TIST, APIN, DMKD, Neural Networks, Information Science"
