    "homepage_text": "Songlin Yang - Homepage\nSonglin Yang\nMMLab@HKUST\nHong Kong\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nI am a PhD student at\nMMLab\n@HKUST,\nThe Hong Kong University of Science and Technology\n, supervised by\nAnyi Rao\nand\nHongbo Fu\n. I am the recipient of\nIEEE Signal Processing Society (SPS) Scholarship\nand\nBSIG Outstanding Thesis Award\n. I am fortunate to have experiences at\nNLPR@CASIA\n,\nTencent\n,\nMicroSoft Research Lab Asia (MSRA)\n,\nSenseTime Research\n, and\nMMLab@NTU\n.\n🔈\nJOIN US!\nInspired by Richard Feynman’s “What I cannot create, I do not understand,” I aim to understand and enhance human intelligence through generative AI. My research seeks to advance multimodal AIGC to spark human creativity while prioritizing safety and ethics.\nDo not hesitate to drop me an email for any possible collaboration if you are interested in these directions:\nFoundation Model\n: Generation Model, Unified Multimodal Model, and Agentic System\nCreator-Machine Co-Learning\n: Personalization, Interactivity, and Assessment\nTrustworthy AIGC\n: Robustness, Privacy, Watermark, and Detection\n🔥 News\n∙ 2026/02: One paper is accepted by CVPR 2026.\n∙ 2026/01: One paper is accepted by ICLR 2026.\n∙ 2025/12: One paper is accepted by Pattern Recognition.\n∙ 2025/11: One paper is accepted by AAAI 2026.\n∙ 2025/09:\nI am granted by\nIEEE Signal Processing Society (SPS) Scholarship!\n.\n∙ 2025/07: One paper is accepted by IEEE TCSVT.\n∙ 2025/06: One paper is accepted by ICCV 2025.\n∙ 2025/05: One paper is accepted by ICML 2025.\n∙ 2025/02: We are organizing\nthe 6th Workshop on AI for Creative Visual Content Generation Editing and Understanding\nat CVPR 2025.\n∙ 2024/07:\nI am awarded the 2024 Outstanding Thesis Award by\nBSIG!\n.\n∙ 2024/07: One paper is accepted by ACM TOMM.\n∙ 2024/06: I am invited to give a talk about my Master's thesis (\nslides\n).  \n∙ 2024/05: I have successfully defended my Master's thesis.\n∙ 2024/03: One paper is accepted by ICME 2024.\n∙ 2024/01: I am invited by AI TIME to give a\ntalk\n(in Chinese) about\nPlaneDict (AAAI 2024)\n.\n∙ 2023/12: One paper is accepted by AAAI 2024.\n∙ 2023/10: I am granted by National Scholarship (Graduate)!\n∙ 2023/07: One paper is accepted by MM 2023.\n👨‍🎓 Education\nPhD Student in\nMMLab\n@HKUST,\nThe Hong Kong University of Science and Technology\nSupervisors:\nAnyi Rao\nand\nHongbo Fu\nM.S. in\nNew Lab of Pattern Recognition (NLPR)\n,\nCASIA Institute\nSupervisors:\nWei Wang\nand\nJing Dong\nThesis: Dynamic Facial Editing based on Neural Radiance Fields (\nBSIG Outstanding Thesis Award\n)\nB.E. in\nNanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics\nThesis: Face De-Identification based on Generative Adversarial Networks (Jiangsu Outstanding Thesis Award)\n💻 Work Experience\nStudent Researcher, Tencent Video AI Center, PCG,\nTencent\nResearch Associate,\nMMLab@NTU\n,\nNanyang Technological University\nResearch Intern, Content Generation Group,\nSenseTime Research\nResearch Intern, Machine Learning Group,\nMicroSoft Research Lab Asia (MSRA)\nResearch Intern, Identity Verification Group,\nSenseTime Research\n📝 Selected Publications\nUnder Review 2026\nHuman-Centric Content Generation with Diffusion Models: A Survey\nSonglin Yang\n,\nYueming Lyu\n,\nZiyuan Chen\n,\nYang Li\n,\nBeibei Dong\n,\nXiaoxuan Han\n,\nPei Yang\n,\nZiye Wang\n,\nAnyi Rao\n,\nZiwei Liu\n,\nJing Dong\n,\nHongbo Fu\n,\nCaifeng Shan\n,\nXiaoming Liu\n,\nLiang Wang\n,\nChenyang Si\nPaper\nProject\nUnder Review 2026\nDense Semantic Matching with VGGT Prior\nSonglin Yang\n,\nTianyi Wei\n,\nYushi Lan\n,\nZeqi Xiao\n,\nAnyi Rao\n,\nXingang Pan\nPaper\nCode\nCVPR 2026\nSame Attention, Different Truths: Put Logit-Lens over Visual Attention to Detect and Mitigate LVLM Object Hallucination\nZichuan Wang\n,\nSonglin Yang\n,\nBo Peng\n,\nZhenchen Tang\n,\nYang Li\n,\nBeibei Dong\n,\nJing Dong\nThe IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n, 2026\nPaper\nICLR 2026\nAlpha-DPO: Robust Preference Alignment for Diffusion Models via Alpha Divergence\nYang Li\n,\nSonglin Yang\n,\nWei Wang\n,\nXiaoxuan Han\n,\nJing Dong\nThe Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations\n, 2026\nPaper\nAAAI 2026\nRevisiting MLLM Based Image Quality Assessment: Errors and Remedy\nZhenchen Tang\n,\nSonglin Yang\n,\nBo Peng\n,\nZichuan Wang\n,\nJing Dong\nProceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n, 2026\nPaper\nCode\nUnder Review 2026\nInstant Preference Alignment for Text-to-Image Diffusion Models\nYang Li\n,\nSonglin Yang\n,\nXiaoxuan Han\n,\nWei Wang\n,\nJing Dong\n,\nYueming Lyu\n, Ziyu Xue\nPaper\nICCV 2025\nTextured 3D Regenerative Morphing with 3D Diffusion Prior\nSonglin Yang\n,\nYushi Lan\n,\nHonghua Chen\n,\nXingang Pan\nProceedings of the IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n, 2025\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nIEEE TCSVT 2025\nBeyond Inserting: Learning Subject Embedding for Semantic-Fidelity Personalized Diffusion Generation\nYang Li\n*,\nSonglin Yang\n*,\nWei Wang\n,\nJing Dong\n(* Equal Contribution)\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (TCSVT), 2025\nPaper\nProject\nPR 2025\nProbing Unlearned Diffusion Models: A Transferable Adversarial Attack Perspective\nXiaoxuan Han\n,\nSonglin Yang\n,\nWei Wang\n,\nYang Li\n,\nJing Dong\nPattern Recognition, 2025\nPaper\nProject\nSurvey\nCode\nICML 2025\nAdaptive Median Smoothing: Adversarial Defense for Unlearned Text-to-Image Diffusion Models at Inference Time\nXiaoxuan Han\n,\nSonglin Yang\n,\nWei Wang\n,\nYang Li\n,\nJing Dong\nForty-Second International Conference on Machine Learning\n, 2025\nPaper\nAAAI 2024\nLearning Dense Correspondence for NeRF-Based Face Reenactment\nSonglin Yang\n,\nWei Wang\n,\nYushi Lan\n,\nXiangyu Fan\n,\nBo Peng\n,\nLei Yang\n,\nJing Dong\nProceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n, 2024\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nACM MM 2023\nContext-Aware Talking-Head Video Editing\nSonglin Yang\n,\nWei Wang\n,\nJun Ling\n,\nBo Peng\n,\nXu Tan\n,\nJing Dong\nProceedings of the 31st ACM International Conference on Multimedia\n, 2023\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nACM TOMM 2024\nExploiting Backdoors of Face Synthesis Detection with Natural Triggers\nXiaoxuan Han\n,\nSonglin Yang\n,\nWei Wang\n,\nZiwen He\n,\nJing Dong\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing Communications and Applications, 2024\nPaper\nCVPR-W 2023\nExposing Fine-Grained Adversarial Vulnerability of Face Anti-Spoofing Models\nSonglin Yang\n,\nWei Wang\n, Chenye Xu,\nZiwen He\n,\nBo Peng\n,\nJing Dong\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nWorkshop\n, 2023\nLong Oral Presentation\nPaper\n🎖️ Awards\nIEEE Signal Processing Society (SPS) Scholarship\n(2025).\nBSIG Outstanding Thesis Award\n(2024).\nNational Scholarship - Graduate (2023).\nNational Scholarship - Bachelor (2018).\nProvincial Outstanding Graduate (2021).\nProvincial Outstanding Bachelor Thesis Award (2021).\nPresident Scholarship of Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics (2020).\nOutstanding Graduate of Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics (2021).\nOutstanding Student of University of Chinese Academy of Sciences (2022, 2023, 2024).\nScholarship of Aviation Industry Corporation of China (2019, 2020).\nOutstanding Reviewer for\nCVPR Workshop\n(2025).\n🕴️ Professional Services\nOrganizer for\nCVEU Workshop\nat CVPR 2025.\nPublicity Chair for\nIEEE Beijing Biometrics Council Chapter\n(2021-2024).\nIEEE Student Member (2021-Now).\nACM Member (2024-Now).\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia (TMM)\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (TCSVT)\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications, and Applications (TOMM)\nPattern Recognition (PR)\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\nConference Reviewer\nAAAI (2023, 2024, 2025, 2026)\nICCV (2025)\nSIGGRAPH (2025)\nCVPR (2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026)\nICLR (2026)\nMM (2024)\nECCV (2022, 2024)\n3DV (2