    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/wenlinyao",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "About me - Wenlin Yao’s homepage\nwenlinyao\nPrinciple Researcher at Microsoft Research (MSR). wenlin.yao.cs@gmail.com\nFollow\nRedmond, WA\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nHello! I am a Principle Researcher at\nMicrosoft Research (MSR), Redmond\n. Prior to this, I was a Senior Applied Scientist at Amazon Stores Foundational AI, working on\nGenAI for shopping\n. Before that, I was a Senior Researcher at\nTencent AI Lab, Bellevue\n. I earned my Ph.D. from the\nDepartment of Computer Science and Engineering\nat\nTexas A&M University (TAMU)\nin 2020. I got my Bachelor’s degree (with Outstanding Graduate Award) from\nDalian University of Technology (DUT)\nin 2015.\nMy research interests center on improving foundation LLMs through end-to-end Reinforcement Learning and agentic frameworks, with a focus on complex problem-solving, tool usage, and interaction with environments.\nSelected Projects:\nWebVoyager\n,\nOpenWebVoyager\n,\nWebAgent-R1\n,\nDSBench\n,\nInFoBench\n,\nMMC\n.\nRecent News\n2025.8: One paper got accepted to EMNLP 2025!\n2025.5: One paper got accepted to ACL 2025!\n2025.1: Two papers got accepted to ICLR 2025!\n2024.9: One paper got accepted to NeurIPS 2024!\n2024.9: One paper got accepted to EMNLP 2024!\n2024.5: Three papers got accepted to ACL 2024!\n2024.3: Two papers got accepted to NAACL 2024!\n2023.12:\nOur paper got the Outstanding Paper Award of EMNLP 2023!\nRead more:\nBridging Continuous and Discrete Spaces: Interpretable Sentence Representation Learning via Compositional Operations\n2023.10: One paper got accepted to EMNLP 2023!\n2023.9: One paper got accepted to NeurIPS 2023!\n2023.1: One paper got accepted to EACL 2023!\n2023.1: One paper got accepted to ICLR 2023!\n2020.09: I have successfully defended my dissertation!"
  },
  "serper::Lei Zhu": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/lei-zhus-homepage",
    "emails": [
      "lei.zhu@charlotte.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Lei Zhu's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nLei Zhu's Homepage\nLei Zhu, Ph.D.\nDr. Lei Zhu is an Assistant Professor of the\nIndustrial and Systems Engineering\ndepartment at the William States Lee College of Engineering at the\nUniversity of North Carolina at Charlotte\nand an affiliate faculty member\nof the\nSchool of Data Science (SDS)\nat UNC Charlotte.\nResearch lab -\nS\nmart\nI\nnfrastructure and\nM\nobility (SIM), covers Smart Mobility Systems and Spatial Sensing,  Big Data in Transportation, Transportation Energy, and Shared and Automated Mobility System Modeling and Simulation.  Before joining UNC Charlotte, Dr. Zhu was a research scientist at the\nNational Laboratory of the Rockies (NLR)\n(formerly known as the\nNational Renewable Energy Laboratory\n) in Golden, Colorado. Before joining\nNLR\n, he served as a postdoc fellow at the\nUniversity of Nevada, Reno\n, and has worked as a Research Engineer in\nMetropia Inc.\nfor years. Dr. Zhu got his Ph.D. degree in Civil Engineering from the\nUniversity of Arizona\n. He is a Senior Member of IEEE, a member of\nIEEE Smart Cities Technical Committee of Control Systems Society\n, and a member of ASCE.\nMy research interests\n:\nGoogle Scholar website\nEmerging Mobility Systems (Micromobility, Microtransit,\nShared and Automated Mobility\n)\nModeling and Simulation\nWi-Fi log Data Analysis and Human Mobility Modeling\nSpatial Sensing (GPS, LiDAR, Radar, Camera) and Big Data Analysis\nSustainable Transportation Analysis and Transportation Electrification\nLab\nNews:\n02/01/2026 [Publication]: Paper \"\nShared electric scooter energy consumption modeling and influencing factor analysis\n\" has been published on\nTransportation Research Part D: Transport and Environment\n02/01/2026: Welcome new lab members: Mr.\nSabir Ahmed\n(Ph.D. student) and Mr.\nDevarsh Parikh\n(Master's student), join the group! Welcome onboard!\n02/01/2026:\nWelcome new\nundergraduate research assistants,\nMr.\nSujay Jayakumar\nand Mr.\nJason Dai\n,\nto\nthe group to support the WiLD\nash Project\n! Welcome onboard!\n_______________________________________________________________________________________________\nContact information:\nEmail:                   Lei.Zhu@charlotte.edu\nOffice Phone:       704-687-6054\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nGraduate Student Hiring (Ph.D. and/or M.S. Level):\nI am looking for graduate students with expertise in Systems Engineering, Traffic/Transportation Engineering, OR, AI/ML, Computer Vision, Control Theory, etc. Please don't hesitate to contact me if you are interested.\nVisiting Scholars and Collaborations are always welcome!!\nFor M.S. students at the ISE department at UNC Charlotte:\nI am always open to advising M.S. students at the ISE department for Thesis and Capstone projects if you are interested in transportation systems-related topics.\nArchive\n2025\n01/18/2025: [Publications] Paper \"\nA Hierarchical Wi-Fi Log Data Processing Framework for Human Mobility Analysis in Multiple Real-World Communities\n\" has been published on\nTravel Behaviour and Society\n!\n2024\n12/18/2024: [New Hiring]\nOpen\nPh.D. Graduate Research Assistant (GRA) Position\n! Starting in\nFall 2025.\n09/01/2024: Welcome new lab member: Mr. Qingrong Yang, join the group! Welcome onboard!\n05/09/2024: [Media&News] Dr. Zhu's Wi-Fi research is reported by WRAL NEWS SPOTLIGHT-\nWay ahead of its time: small town in Eastern NC creates citywide Wi-Fi system\n!\n03/01/2024: [Media&News] Dr. Zhu's\nresearch effort\nhas been reported by UNC Charlotte College of Engineering!\n01/18/2024: [Hiring]\nOpen\nPh.D. level Graduate Research Assistant (GRA) Position\n! Starting in\nFall 2024.\n2013\n12/31/2023:\nDr. Zhu serves as a guest editor for the Special Issue \"\nSustainable Transportation: Human-Computer Interaction and Intelligent Transportation\n\" at\nSustainability [Deadline for manuscript submissions:\n5 December 2024\n]\n09/18/2023: [Hiring]\nOpen M.S. level\nGraduate Research Assistant (GRA) Position\n! Starting in Spring 2024.\n08/01/2023: Dr. Zhu\nserves as a guest editor for the Special Issue \"\nGeographic Information Science in Transportation and Traffic Safety\n\" at\nSustainability\n[Deadline for manuscript submissions:\n24 May 2024\n]\n03/31/2023:\nMohini is awarded \"\nMaster's and Early Doctoral Student Summer Support\" ($5,000) from UNC Charlotte!! Congratulations!\n02/28/2023: Ms. Mohini Joshi joined us as a research assistant. Welcome!\n2012\n12/29/2022: Dr. Zhu serves as a leading guest editor for the Special Issue \"\nIntelligent Vehicle, Infrastructure Perception and Control Based on Imaging and Sensing\n\" at\nSensors [Deadline for manuscript submissions:\n31 August 2023,\nextended to 31 July 2024\n]\n10/20/2022: Dr. Zhu gave a talk about Wi-Fi research titled \"\nWi-Fi Log Data Processing and Spatial-temporal Analysis for Exploring University Campus Human Mobility Patterns\n\" for the CAGIS Seminar at UNC Charlotte\n06/01/2022: Thomas Orton will join SIM Lab as an undergraduate research assistant! Welcome, Thomas!\n05/13/2022:\n2022 Summer Research Assistant hiring\n!! urgent hiring and start immediately!\n02/13/2022: [Paper] Dr. Zhu's paper \"\nLight-Duty Vehicle Trip Classification using One-Class Novelty Detection and Exhaustive Feature Extraction\n\" will be published in\nIEEE Transactions on Industry Applications\n!\n2011\n11/10/2021: [Paper] Shreya Lohar's paper \"\nSensing Technology Survey for Obstacle Detection in Vegetation\n\" has been published on\nFuture Transportation\n, Congratulations Shreya!!\n10/01/2021: [Paper] Dr. Zhu's paper \"\nReal-Time Highly Resolved Spatial-Temporal Vehicle Energy Consumption Estimation Using Machine Learning and Probe Data\n\" cooperating with researchers from NREL and ORNL, was published at\nTRR\n.\n10/01/2021: Vamshi Yalavarthi, Xavier Gomez, Josh Rodriguez, joined the SIM lab as research assistants. Welcome, all!\n10/01/2021: SIM lab received a donation of\nVelodyne VLP-16\nLiDAR from Renu Robotics.  Thank you very much for the generous support for our research!\n09/27/2021: Shreya Lohar will keep working as an intern at NREL for a project \"Infrastructure Perception and Control.\"\n0\n9\n/\n07\n/2021: Dr. Zhu is serving as a Guest Editor, Special Issue \"\nSustainable and Intelligent Transportation Systems in the Era of the COVID-19 Pandemic\" at Sustainability\n, 2021. [Deadline for manuscript submissions extended to: 30 September 202\n3\n]\n07/01/2021: Dr. Zhu is serving as a member of the Technical Committee of\n2021 International Conference on Transport and Smart Cities (ICoTSC 2021)\n04/30/2021: Shreya Lohar will work as a summer intern (May -July 2021) at National Renewable Energy Lab (NREL) for a mowing machine spatial sensing project. Congratulations, Shreya!\n03/22/2021: Dr. Zhu is serving as a Session Chair,\nTechnical Session 8: CyberPhysical Systems and Security of Intelligent Power Systems\n, IEEE Green Technologies Conference 2021\n03/10/2021: Dr. Zhu is serving as a Guest Editor, Special Issue \"\nSustainable and Intelligent Transportation Systems in the Era of the COVID-19 Pandemic\" at Sustainability\n, 2021.\n02/12/2021: An MOU between UNCC (Lead by Dr. Zhu) and NREL has been signed for Spatial Sensing and Advanced Mobility research!\n01/24/2021: Dr. Zhu is serving as a\nspecial session chair/organizer for IEEE Green Tech 2021 conference\n.\n01/01/2021: Ms. Rachael Yuan will join us as a Ph.D. student in Jan. 2021! Welcome, Rachael!\nOpen Graduate Research Assistant (GRA) Positions!\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
