    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Bao-Liang Lu's Home Page\nBao-Liang Lu\nPh.D., IEEE Fellow, Professor, Directors\nCenter for Brain-like Computing and Machine Intelligence\nDepartment of Computer Science and Engineering\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nKey Laboratory of Shanghai Commission for Intelligent Interaction and Cognitive\n                    Engineering\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nCenter for Brain-Machine Interface and Neuromodulation, RuiJin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine\nRuiJin-MiHoYo Laboratory, RuiJin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine\nbllu AT sjtu DOT edu DOT cn\nPhone.: +86-21-34205422\nOffice: Room 431, Dian Xin Building 3\nAddress: 800 Dong Chuan Road Shanghai 200240, China\nResearch Interest\nBrain-like Computing, Neural Networks, Deep Learning, Emotion AI, Affective Brain-Computer Interface.\nEducation Background\nI received the B.S. degree in instrument and control engineering from Qingdao University\n            of Science and Technology, China, in 1982, the M. S. degree in computer science and\n            engineering from Northwestern Polytechnical University, Xi'an, China, in 1989, and the Dr.\n            Eng. degree in electrical engineering from Kyoto University, Kyoto, Japan, in 1994.\nWork Experience\nFrom 1982 to 1986, I was with the Qingdao University of Science and Technology. From April \n          \t1994 to March 1999, I was a Frontier Researcher at the Bio-Mimetic Control Research Center, \n          \tthe Institute of Physical and Chemical Research (RIKEN), Nagoya, Japan. From April 1999 to \n          \tAugust 2002, I was a Research Scientist at the RIKEN Brain Science Institute, Wako, Japan. \n          \tSince August 2002, I have been a full professor at the Department of Computer Science and \n          \tEngineering, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, China.\nTeaching\nNeural Network Theory and Applications\nParallel Machine Learning with Application to Large-Scale Data Mining\nAwards\n2012 Asia Pacific Neural Network Assembly (APNNA) Excellent Service Award\n2018 IEEE Transactions on Autonomous Mental Development Outstanding Paper Award\n2020 First Prize, Wu Wen Jun AI Science & Technology Award\n2021 Best of IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing Paper Collection\nACM Multimedia 2022 Top Paper Award\n2022 Asia Pacific Neural Network Society (APNNS) Outstanding Achievement Award\nEditorial Board of\nIEEE Transactions on Affective Computing 2022-\nJournal of Neural Engineering 2021-\nChinese Journal of Intelligent Science and Technology 2019-\nPattern Recognition and Artificial Intelligence (in Chinese) 2017-\nIEEE Transactions on Cognitive and Developmental Systems 2016-\nMajor Grants\nInvestigating Age, Gender, and Cultural Differences in Emotion Recognition Using EEG and\n                                Eye Movement Signals\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: NSFC 61976135\nAgency: National Science Foundation of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2020 to Dec. 31, 2023\nA Study on the Discrimination Ability, Representation Characteristics and\n                                Stability of EEG and Eye Movement Signals for Multimodal Emotion Recognition\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: NSFC 61673266\nAgency: National Science Foundation of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2017 to Dec. 31, 2020\nA Study on Visual Cognition Coding and Information Integration Mechanism of the\n                        Brain\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: 2013CB329401\nAgency: National Basic Research Program (973) of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2013 to Dec. 31, 2017\nA Study on Key Techniques for Fatigue Monitoring by Using Forehead EOG\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: NSFC 61272248\nAgency: National Science Foundation of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2013 to Dec. 31, 2016\nA Driving Fatigue Detection System by Combining EOG and EEG Signals\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: 13511500200\nAgency: Science and Technology Commission of Shanghai Municipality\nPeriod: July. 1, 2013 to June 30, 2015\nDry-electrode-based Wireless Wearable EEG-cap and Its Application to Drivers'\n                        Vigilance Monitor System\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: 09511502400\nAgency: Science and Technology Commission of Shanghai Municipality\nPeriod: July. 1, 2009 to June 30, 2011\nThe Basic Mechanism Research of Visual Information Processing\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: 2009CB320901\nAgency: National Basic Research Program (973) of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2009 to Dec. 31, 2013\nEEG Based Vigilance Estimation and Prediction for Drivers\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: NSFC 90820018\nAgency: National Science Foundation of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2009 to Dec. 31, 2011\nIntegrated platform for analysis of metagenomic and metabonomic data and study on\n                        metabolic disease\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: NSFC 2008AA02Z315\nAgency: National High-Tech Research Program (863) of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2008 to Dec. 31, 2010.\nLearning algorithm for Large-scale, multi-label, and imbalanced classification\n                        problems\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: NSFC 60773090\nAgency: National Science Foundation of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2008 to Dec. 31, 2010.\nTask decomposition and module combination for massively parallel pattern classifiers\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: NSFC 60473040\nAgency: National Science Foundation of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2005 to Dec. 31, 2007.\nIncremental learning model\nPrincipal Investigator: Bao-Liang Lu\nGrant Number: NSFC 60375022\nAgency: National Science Foundation of China\nPeriod: Jan. 1, 2004 to Dec. 31, 2006.\nPublication\n2025\nWei-Bang Jiang, Yansen Wang,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Dongsheng Li, NeuroLM: A Universal Multi-task Foundation Model for Bridging the Gap between Language and EEG Signals.In The Thirteenth International Conference on Learning Representations, 2025.\n[pdf]\nHao-Long Yin, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, STAR: A Spatial-Temporal Autoencoder for EEG Restoration in Emotion Recognition, Proc. of ICASSP 2025.\nJian-Ming Zhang, Wei-Bang Jiang, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Multi-Scale Attention-Based Dense Spatial-Temporal Model for Emotion Induction in Response to Olfactory Stimuli, Proc. of ICASSP 2025.\nZiyi Li, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Gram: A Large-Scale General EEG Model for Raw Data Classification and Restoration Tasks, Proc. of ICASSP 2025.\nHaiqing Hu, Hanwen Shi,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Wei-Long Zheng, Multi-Source Multi-Target Domain Similarity Network for Cross-Cultural EEG Emotion Recognition, Proc. of ICASSP 2025.\nDavid Edwin Carlson, Ricardo Chavarriaga, Yiling Liu, Fabien Lotte,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, The NERVE-ML (Neural Engineering Reproducibility and Validity Essentials for Machine Learning) Checklist: Ensuring Machine Learning Advances Neural Engineering, Journal of Neural Engineering.\nHuan Liu, Shusen Yang, Yuzhe Zhang, Mengze Wang, Fanyu Gong, Chengxi Xie, Guanjian Liu, Zejun Liu, Yong-Jin Liu,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Dalin Zhang, Libeer: A comprehensive benchmark and algorithm library for EEG-based emotion recognition, IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing\nYong Peng, Jiangchuan Liu, Honggang Liu, Natasha Padfield, Junhua Li, Wanzeng Kong,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Andrzej Cichocki, Prediction Consistency and Confidence-Based Proxy Domain Construction for Privacy-Preserving in Cross-Subject EEG Classification, IEEE Journal of Biomedical and Health Informatics\nKhin Pa Pa Aung, Hao-Long Yin, Tian-Fang Ma, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, SEED-MYA: A Novel Myanmar Multimodal Dataset for Enhancing Emotion Recognition, IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing\nCunbo Li, Zehong Cao, Yue Pan, Pengcheng Zhu, Peiyang Li, Fali Li, Huafu Chen,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Feng Wan, Dezhong Yao, Peng, Xu, EEG-Based Emotion Monitoring and Regulation System by Learning the Discriminative Brain Network Manifold, IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\nLu Zhang, Hanwen Shi, Ziyi Li, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Multi-View Self-Supervised Domain Adaptation for EEG-Based Emotion Recognition, IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing\nZiyi Li, Le-Yan Tao, Ruo-Xiao Ma, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Investigating the Effects of Sleep Conditions on Emotion Responses with EEG Signals and Eye Movements, IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing\nLinxing Zhu, Shu Jiang, Hai Zhao, Zuchao Li, Jiashuang Huang, Weiping Ding,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Document-Level Neural Machine Translation With Document Embeddings, IEEE Access\nYan-Kai Liu, Jinyu Cai,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Wei-Long Zheng, Multi-to-Single: Reducing Multimodal Dependency in Emotion Recognition Through Contrastive Learning, Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 39 (2), 1438-1446\nXuan-Hao Liu,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Wei-Long Zheng, mixEEG: Enhancing EEG Federated Learning for Cross-subject EEG Classification with Tailored mixup, arXiv preprint arXiv:2504.07987\n2024\nWei-Bang Jiang, Li-Ming Zhao,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Large Brain Model for Learning Generic Representations with Tremendous EEG Data in BCI. In The Twelfth International Conference on Learning Representations, 2024.\n[pdf]\nWei-Bang Jiang*, Ziyi Li*, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Functional Emotion Transformer for EEG-Assisted Cross-Modal Emotion Recognition, Proc. of ICASSP 2024. (*contributed equally as joint first authors)\n[pdf]\nZiyi Li, Li-Ming Zhao, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Temporal-Spatial Prediction: Pre-Training on Diverse Datasets for EEG Classification, Proc. of ICASSP 2024.\n[pdf]\nPengxuan Gao, Tianyu Liu, Jia-Wen Liu,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, Wei-Long Zheng, Multimodal Multi-View Spectral-Spatial-Temporal Masked Autoencoder for Self-Supervised Emotion Recognition, Proc. of ICASSP 2024.\n[pdf]\nYu-Ting Lan, Wei-Bang Jiang, Wei-Long Zheng,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, CEMOAE: A Dynamic Autoencoder with Masked Channel Modeling for Robust EEG-Based Emotion Recognition, Proc. of ICASSP 2024.\n[pdf]\nWei-Bang Jiang*, Yu-Ting Lan*,\nBao-Liang Lu\n, REmoNet: Reducing Emotional Label Noise via ...[truncated]"
