    "homepage_text": "Home\nWeisi\nLin\nBSc, MSc, PhD\nFIEEE, FIET, CEng, Hon. FSIET\nProfessor\nPresident's\nChair in Computer Science\nAssociate Dean (Research)\nCollege of Computing and\nData Science\nNanyang Technological University\n50 Nanyang Avenue, Singapore 639798\nEmail:\nwslin@ntu.edu.sg\nâScience is not only a dsciple of reason but, also, one of romance and passion.â\n-- Stephen Hawking\nPostdoc/RA positions open for visual signal modeling for human/machine intelligence, scent signal  representation, neural network compression, and AI-driven climate/environmental monitoring.\ncontact me at\nwslin@ntu.edu.sg\n.\nA few words about myself...\nI received a Bachelor's degree in Electronics and then a Master's degree in Digital Signal Processing from Sun Yat-Sen University, Guangzhou, China. I obtained my Ph.D. in Computer Vision from Kingâs College, London University, UK.\nI taught and researched in Sun Yat-Sen University, Shantou University (China), Bath University (UK), National University of Singapore, Institute of Microelectronics (Singapore), and Institute for Infocomm Research (Singapore). In February 2007, I joined the faculty of Nanyang Technological University. I am a Fellow of IEEE, a Fellow of IET, a Chartered Engineer, and Honorary Fellow of SIET (Singapore Institute of Engineering Technologists).\nMy research deals with image processing, perception-based modeling, video compression, and multimedia communication. I believe that good theory is practical and effective teamwork can achieve the goal of \"1+1>2\"; I have kept a balance of academic research and industrial deployment in my working life, and also managed over ten successfully-delivered major projects for external customers.\nIt has been my good fortune to have the chances to work with many colleagues and students in various organizations. I always look forward to collaborating with more researchers who think alike, and am eager to meet new students with an interest in image processing, visual understanding and multimedia communication, as well as modeling the relevant physiological, cognitive and psychological findings.\nWe have built a\nCOVID-19 Test Strip Reader\n(video\n) (\nreport\n) with colleagues in School of Chemical and Biomedical Engineering. We have also built a\nRetargeted Image Subjective Quality Database\nand  a database for\nPerceptual Quality Assessment of Screen Content Images\n(SIQAD). Some other past research can be seen\nhere\n.\nAt leisure, I like reading and taking walks. The books I like include: The Seven Habits of Highly Effective People, by Stephen R. Covey; Fishing Lessons-Insights, Fun, and Philosophy from a Passionate Angler, by Paul Quinnett; A Brief History of Time, by Stephen Hawking; Bounce: Mozart, Federer, Picasso, Beckham, and the Science of Success,  by Matthew Syed; The Happy Student: 5 Steps to Academic Fulfillment and Success, by Daniel Wong;\nLETTERS TO HIS SON\n, by the EARL OF CHESTERFIELD; Tan Swie Hian Fables; Teacher Man, by Frank McCourt; Tuesdays with Morrie, by Mitch Albom; The 38 Letters from J.D. Rockefeller to his son: Perspectives, Ideology, and Wisdom. I also like\nProf Randy Pausch's Last Lecture\n, and\nthe transcription of \"You and Your Research'' by Dr. Richard W. Hamming\n.\nMy current research team members:\nMr\nChen Zhuo\nB. Eng\nProject: Deep-learnt visual feature coding\nResearch interests: deep learning and visual feature coding\nPersonal website link\nCongratulations for being selected into Lean LaunchPad Singapore - a governmental innovation\nand commercialisation platform- with technology in  collaborative intelligence, 2020!\nMr\nHou Jingwen\nB.Eng, MSc\nProject: Blind image quality assessment\nResearch interests: deep learning-based perceptual quality assessment\nCongratulations for leading toward Second Runner-up \nfor the 5-Minute Video Clip Contest at IEEE ICIP 2020 !\nMr\nHu Zhi\nB. Eng\nProject: Point-cloud segmentation and applications\nResearch interests: 3D segmentation, Semantic SLAM, Deep Learning\nDr\nZhao Baoquan\nB. Eng, PhD\nProject: 3D Point Cloud Compression\nResearch interests: 3D Point Cloud Processing and Coding, Multimedia Content Analysis\nDr\nZhang Guoqing\nB.Sc, MSc, PhD\nProject: Intelligent visual analysis with pedestrian tracking & person re-identification\nResearch interests: Person re-identification, pattern recognition and machine learning\nDr\nLv Chenlei\nB.Eng, PhD\nProject: Point Cloud Simplification\nResearch interests: Discrete differential geometry, Non-rigid retrieval & registration, Point cloud processing, 3D Face modelling & Recognition\nPersonal website link\nDr\nJin Jian\nB. Eng, M. Eng, PhD\nProject: Perceptual image/video coding\nResearch interests: 2D/3D image/video coding, 3D scene rendering, computer vision, and deep learning\nPersonal website link\nMr\nTeerawat Piriyatharawet\nProject: Lightweight Deep Learning for Image Processing and Understanding\nResearch interests:   image processing, Just-noticeable difference models, deep learning\nMr\nKoh Jun Hao\nProject: Intelligent visual analysis with pedestrian tracking & person re-identification\nResearch interests:  super-resolution reconstruction, machine learning\nIt is my pleasure to have had the chances to\nwork substantially with many researchers since 2007.\nDr\nYang Sheng\nB.Eng, PhD\nProject:  Visual Saliency and Quality Evaluation via Machine Learning\nResearch interests:  Visual Attention, Image Quality Assessment, Machine Learning\nPersonal website link\nDr\nCheng Wentao\nB.Eng, PhD\nProject: Simplification, Filtering and Image-based\nLocalization of 3D Point Clouds\nResearch interests: Tone Mapping, Image-Based Rendering, Real Time Graphics\nCongratulations to Wentao for award of  ICCV 2019 Travel Grant!\nDr\nXinfeng Zhang\nB.Eng, Ph.D\nAssistant Professor, University of Chinese Academic of Sciences, China\nPersonal website link\nDr\nZhang Yabin\nB.Eng, PhD\nSenior Researcher, Tencent, Shenzhen, China\nPersonal website link\nDr\nGu Ke\nB.Sc, PhD\nProfessor, Beijing University of Technology , China\nPersonal website link\nDr\nVinit Jakhetiya\nB.Eng, PhD\nAssistant Professor, Indian Institute of Technology (IIT), Jammu, India\nPersonal website link\nDr\nWang Shiqi\nB.Eng, PhD\nAssistant Professor, City University of Hong Kong\nPersonal website link\nDr\nPrakhya Sai Manoj\nB.Eng, PhD\nSystems Engineer, Aptiv, Wuppertal, Germany\nPersonal website link\nCongratulations to Sai for Best Paper Award in Robotics domain, TENCON 2017!\nCongratulations for Sai's obtaining the Student Travel Grant,  for both  IEEE ICRA2015 and IAPR MVA 2015!\nDr\nJiang Qiuping\nB.Eng, PhD\nAssoc Professor, Ningbo University, China\nDr\nIssac Niwas Swamidoss\nB.Eng., M. Eng., PhD\nResearch Specialist, Tawazun Technology and Innovation (Tawazun Economic Council), Abu Dhabi, UAE\nDr\nXu Long\nB.Eng, M. Eng, Ph.D\nProfessor, National Astronomical Observatories of the Chinese Academy of Sciences (NAOC), China\nCongratulations to Long's being selected into the 100-Talents Plan, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 2014!\nDr\nLi Leida\nB.Sc, Ph.D\nProfessor,\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\n, Xidian University, China\nPersonal website link\nDr\nYuming Fang\nB.Sc., M. Sc., PhD\nProfessorï¼Jiangxi University of Finance and Economics, China\nPersonal website link\nCongratulations to Yuming for the 2012 Dragon Venture â NTU Award!\nDr\nQiaohong Li\nB.Sc., PhD\nResearch Fellow, National University of Singapore (NUS)\nDr\nHuan Yang\nB.Sc., M. Sc., PhD\nAssoc Professor, Qingdao University, China\nPersonal website link\nDr\nJinjian Wu\nB.Eng, PhD\nProfessor, School of Electronic Engineering, Xidian University, China\nPersonal website link\nCongratulations to Jinjian's  IEEE International Symposium on Circuits and Systems  (ISCAS2013) Student Best Paper Award!\nDr\nSharath Chandra Guntuku\nB.E (Hons), PhD\nResearch Assistant Professor,\nSchool of Engineering and Applied Science\n, University of Pennsylvania, USA\nPersonal website link\nCongratulations  for Sharath's obtaining the Student Travel Grants, ACM Multimedia Conference (ACM MM), 2015!\nDr\nYuan Yuan\nB.Eng, PhD\nSenior Algorithm Engineer, Huawei, Singapore\nPersonal website link\nDr\nCong Runmin\nB.Sc, PhD\nAssociate Professor, School of Computer and Information Technology, Beijing Jiaotong University, China\nPersonal website link\nDr\nTsung-Jung Liu\nB. S., M.S., PhD\nAssociate Professor, EE & GICE, National\nChung Hsing University, Taiwan\nPersonal\nwebsite link\nDr\nLu Dong\nB.Sc., PhD\nTeaching & Research Supervisor, Jiangsu EDUBOT Education Technology Group Co. Ltd, China\nMr\nNarasimhan Rajesh\nB.Tech - IT, MSc\nCongratulations to Rajesh for winning the 2nd prize for the ST Electronics Security Apps Challenge (2014, Singapore)!\nDr\nLin Ma\nB.E., M.E., PhD\nPrincipal Researcher, Tencent AI Lab\nPersonal website link\nDr\nXu Qianqian\nB.Eng, M.Eng, PhD\nAssociate Professor, Institute of Computing Technology (ICT), Chinese Academy of Sciences\nPersonal website link\nDr\nManish Narwaria\nB.Tech.,  PhD\nAssistant Professor, Indian Institute of Technology (IIT),  Jodhpur, India\nPersonal website link\nDr\nLining Zhan\ng\nB.Eng, M.Eng, PhD\nSenior Research Scientist,  I2R, A*STAR, Singapore\nDr\nZhouye Gu\nB.Sc., M. Sc., PhD\nResearcher, Apple Inc,  USA\nDr\nAnmin Liu\nB.Sc., PhD\nSenior Researcher, Panasonic, Singapore\nDr\nChenwei Deng\nPh.D\nProfessor, Beijing Institute of Technology, China\nDr\nFeng Shao\nPhD\nProfessor, Ningbo University, China\nDr\nManoranjan Paul\nB.Sc.Eng. (hons.), PhD\nProfessor,  Charles Sturt University, Australia\nPersonal website link\nCongratulations to Ranjan's obtaining of Research Excellence Award 2011 from School of Computing and Mathematics, Charles Sturt University!\nDr\nFan Zhang\nB. Eng, PhD\nResearcher, Lenovo Cooperation Research, Hong Kong\nCongratulations to Fan for winning the ITU-T Study Group 12 competition in June 2012, with the visual quality metrics!\nDr\nGuangtao Zhai\nB.Eng, M.Eng, PhD\nProfessor,  Shanghai Jiao Tong University, China\nCongratulations to Guangtao for the TOP 100 PhD Theses in China 2012!\nDr\nWei Liu\nPh.D\nAssociate Professor, South China Normal University, China\nMr\nKng Poh Leong, Vincent\nB.Eng\nResearch Engineer,  Institute for Inforcomm Research, Singapore\nDr\nNev...[truncated]"
