    "homepage_text": "TC'S HOMEPAGE\n↓\nSkip to main content\nTi-Chung Cheng\ndef decision(human, machine):\nI’m a Ph.D. candidate at\nUIUC\n, working in HCI and CSCW under the guidance of\nProf. Karrie Karahalios\nand\nProf. Hari Sundaram\n. I currently study Quadratic Surveys, a method for eliciting individual preferences for collective action. More broadly, my research investigates tools for collective decision-making and Human-AI interaction. Check out my\nCV\nor learn more\nabout me\n.\nIf you are a master’s or undergraduate student at UIUC interested in research, feel free to send me an email.\nI'm on the job market!\nI am an\nApplied Researcher\nBridging\nAI & Engineering\ninto Practical Applications\nI am a\nSoftware Engineer\nBuilding\nComplex Systems\ninto Scalable Products\nI am a\nUX Researcher\nBlueprinting\nAI Experiences\ninto Decision-Support Tools\nClick to read my resume for\nApplied Researcher\n,\nUX Researcher\nand\nSoftware Engineer\n.\nRecent News\n2025/09/24 —\n“Generative Propaganda” preprint\nis now public. Here’s a slice of the work I did during my MSR Special Projects internship with an amazing team.\n2025/06/09 — My Undergraduate student mentee,\nPranay Midha\n’s poster on the first step to visualizing Quadratic Surveys is accepted as a poster at\nCI 2025\n. Can’t wait to share our preliminary findings with you.\n2025/05/20 — So….why does Quadratic Voting and Quadratic Surveys work? Our latest findings will be presented at\nCI 2025\nin August 2025 and you can take a read\nhere\n. Let’s chat in San Diego if you are there!\n2025/01/17 — The first paper on designing and validating interface for Quadratic Surveys (and also Quadratic Voting) will be presented at\nCHI 2025\n. The full paper can be found\nhere\n.\n2025/12/16 — Check out here! I can finally officially annouce\nHere@Illinois\nas the coolest tool for staffs to manage their courses and events!\n2024/08/27 — My internship project at Microsoft Research with the\nSoftware Analysis and Intelligence in Engineering Systems (SAINTES) Group\nis now readable through this\ntech report\nwhere I outline my iterative prompt priming approach for Generative Expert Metric Generation with Large Language Models.\n2024/05/01 — I am honored to recieve my second\nOutstanding Teaching Assistant Award\nfrom the CS Department in addition to the campus wide\nTA ranked as excellence\nrecognition for\nCS598SPH/SMC Research Methods in HCI\nthat I TAed in Fall 2023!\nRecent\nIdentifying Preferences Is Harder Than You Think\n14 July 2025\n·\n9 mins\nBuilding a Full MySQL React Express Node (MERN) Stack: A Pokemon App\n22 October 2024\n·\n47 mins\nSeattle: My Offbeat & Honest Guide\n23 August 2023\n·\n6 mins\nWhy a redesign?\n18 March 2023\n·\n5 mins\nCasual Picks in Chicago\n1 March 2023\n·\n7 mins\nRead more..."
  },
