    "homepage_text": "Luoyi Fu\nåæ´ä¼       LuoYi Fu\nPersonal Information\nProfessor\nDepartment of Computer Science and Engineering\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\n1-428 SEIEE Building\n800 Dongchuan Road\nShanghai 200240, P. R. China\nEmail\nyiluofu@sjtu.edu.cn\nfu-ly@cs.sjtu.edu.cn\nHomepage\nhttp://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/~fu-ly/index.html\nAcemap\nhttps://www.acemap.info/\nResearch Interest: data-driven IoT, social networking, data mining & engineering, fundamental limits.\nClick\nhere\nto learn more about my recent research projects.\nLearn more about our\nAceKG\nWelcome to try our\nInternet of Papers (IoP)\nWelcome to try our\nDeepReport\nTeaching:\nMobile Internet:\n[Website]\n[Material]\nè¯¾ä»¶ppt:\né¾æ¥\næåç : rbep\nå®éªæå:\né¾æ¥\næåç : ezja\nä½ä¸åå¶ä»èµæº:\né¾æ¥\næåç : mn9a\nBook:\nãIntroduction to Mobile Internetã\nhas been published !\nThird Edition\nFourth Edition\nTMall:\n[BUY]\nJD:\n[BUY]\nDangDang:\n[BUY]\nTalks:\n(You are free to download and use for your own purposes)\nFrom IoT , IoD to IoI: They are All Graph of Things (GoT)\n[slides]\nMeasuring and Analyzing Knowledge in Large Graph based Methodologies-A Case Study in Internet of Papers (IOP)\n[slides]\nQuantifying and Analyzing Knowledge: A Structurized Perspective\n[slides]\nGraph Matching Related Network De-anonymization\n[slides]\nFinding Connections in Uncertain Networks/Graphs\n[slides]\nA Brief Look into The Classic Works of Mobile Internet in Early Years\n[slides]\nMost Widely Used Math Tools in Network Analysis\n[slides]\nNews:\nTop 10 2019\nNÂ²Women  Rising Stars\nin Computer Networking and Communications\nEditor of IEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\nAssociate Editor of ACM Transactions on Sensor Networks\nAssociate Editor of IEEE Transactions on Network Science and Engineering\nTPC of ACM Sigmetrics / Performance 2022, 2023\nGuest Editor of Applied Science (Special Issue: Advances in AI-Driven Data Mining) 2022\nGuest Editor of IEEE Open Journal of the Communications Society\nArea Editor of Computer Networks\nEditor of China Communications (ä¸­å½éä¿¡)\nSelected Articles of Recent Research Focuses:\nGraph Entropy and Its Application\n:\n[TIT]\nL. Fu\n, J. Tang, B. Miao, X. Lin and X. Wang, \"The Effect of Symmetry on the De-anonymizability of Social Networks\", to appear in\nIEEE Transactions on Information Theory\n, 2023\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nL. Fu\n, J. Zhang, S. Qu, H. Kang, X. Wang and G. Chen, \"Measuring Social Network De-anonymizability by Means of Morphism Property\", to appear in\nIEEE Transactions on Networking\n, 2022\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[TIT]\nX. Liu ,\nL. Fu\n, X. Wang, C. Zhou, \"On the Similarity between von Neumann Graph Entropy and Structural Information: Interpretation, Computation, and Applications,\" in\nIEEE Transactions on Information Theory\n, 2022\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[WWW]\nX. Liu,\nL.Fu\n, X. Wang, \"Bridging the Gap between von Neumann Graph Entropy and Structural Information: Theory and Applications\", to appear in\nWWW\n, 2021\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[PLOS]\nL. Fu\n, D. Lu, Q. Li, X. Wang and C. Zhou, \"Can We 'Feel' the Temperature of Knowledge? Modelling Scientific Popularity Dynamics via Thermodynamics\", in\nPLOS ONE\n, 2020\n.\n[PDF]\n[CIKM]\nC. Deng, Y. Jia, H. Xu, C. Zhang, J. Tang,\nL. Fu\n, Weinan Zhang, Haisong Zhang, Xinbing Wang, Chenghu Zhou, \"GAKG: A Multimodal GeoScience Academic Knowledge Graph\" to appear in\nCIKM\n, 2021\n. [\nPDF\n] [\nGithub\n]\n[INFOCOM]\nC. Zhang, Q. Guo,\nL. Fu\n, X. Gan and X. Wang \"ITE: A Structural Entropy Based Approach for Source Detection\", in\nIEEE INFOCOM 2021\n, Vancouver, May, 2021. [\nPDF\n]\n[INFOCOM]\nX. Liu,\nL. Fu\n, X. Wang and J. Hopcroft, \"ProHiCo: A Probabilistic Framework to Hide Communities in Large Networks\", in\nIEEE INFOCOM 2021\n, Vancouver, May, 2021. [\nPDF\n]\nGraph Matching Based Social Network De-anonymizing\n:\n[TON]\nL. Fu\n, J. Zhang, S. Wang, X. Wu, X. Wang and G. Chen, \"De-anonymizing Social Networks with Overlapping Community Structure\", to appear in\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2019\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[INFOCOM]\nJ. Zhang,\nL. Fu\n, X. Wang and G. Chen, \"De-anonymizing Social Networks Under Partial Overlap: An F-score Based Approach\", in\nIEEE INFOCOM 2021\n, Vancouver, May, 2021. [\nPDF\n]\n[MOBIHOC]\nB. Miao, S. Wang,\nL. Fu\nand X. Lin, \"De-anonymizability of Social Network: Through the Lens of Symmetry\", to appear in\nACM MobiHoc\n, 2020\n. [\nPDF\n]\nOther Selected Articles\n:\n[TON]\nL. Fu\n, J. Xu, S. Qu, Z. Xu, X. Wang, G. Chen, Seeking the Truth in a Decentralized Manner,\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2021\n, 29(5): 2296-2312. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nL. Fu\n, Jiapeng Zhang, Shuaiqi Wang, Xinyu Wu, Xinbing Wang, Guihai Chen, De-anonymizing Social Networks with Overlapping Community Structure,\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2020\n, 28(1): 360-375. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nL. Fu\n, S. Ma, L. Kong, S. Shi, X. Wang, \"FINE: A Framework for Distributed Learning on Incomplete Observations for Heterogeneous Crowdsensing Networks\", to appear in\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2018\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nL. Fu\n, X. Fu, Z. Zhang, Z. Xu, X. Wu, X. Wang and S. Lu, \"Joint Optimization of Multicast Energy in Delay-constrained Mobile Wireless Networks\", to appear in\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2018\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nL. Fu\n, X. Fu, Z. Xu, Q. Peng, X. Wang and S. Lu, \"Determining Source-Destination Connectivity in Uncertain Networks: Modeling and Solutions,\" to appear in\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2017\n. [\nPDF\n] [\nCode on ANAP\n]\n[TON]\nL. Fu\n, Xinbing Wang, PR Kumar , Are We Connected? Optimal Determination of Source-Destination Connectivity in Random Networks,\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2017\n, 25(2): 751-764. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nXu Li, Feilong Tang, Yanmin Zhu,\nL. Fu\n, Jiadi Yu, Long Chen, Jiacheng Liu , Processing-while-Transmitting: Cost-Minimized Transmission in SDN-Based STINs,\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2021\n, DOI: 10.1109/TNET.2021.3107413, 2021. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nJiaqi Liu,\nL. Fu\n, Yuhang Yao, Xinzhe Fu, Xinbing Wang, Guihai Chen , Modeling, Analysis and Validation of Evolving Networks With Hybrid Interactions,\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2019\n, 27(1): 126-142. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nX. Wu,\nL. Fu\n,Y. Yao, X. Fu, X. Wang and G. Chen, \"GLP: A Novel Framework for Group-level Location Promotion in Geo-social Networks\", to appear in\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2018\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nJ. Zhang,\nL. Fu\n, Q. Wang, L. Liu, X. Wang, Xinbing Wang,\"Connectivity Analysis in Wireless Networks with Correlated Mobility and Cluster Scalability\" to appear in\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2017\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nXuanyu Cao, Jinbei Zhang,\nL. Fu\n, Weijie Wu, Xinbing Wang , Optimal Secrecy Capacity-delay Tradeoff in Large-scale Mobile ad hoc Networks,\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2016\n, 24(2): 1139-1152. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nJinbei Zhang,\nL. Fu\n, Xinbing Wang , Asymptotic Analysis on Secrecy Capacity in Large-scale Wireless Networks,\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2014\n, 22(1): 66-79. [\nPDF\n]\n[TON]\nXinbing Wang,\nL. Fu\n, Chenhui Hu , Multicast Performance With Hierarchical Cooperation,\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n, 2012\n, 20(3): 917-930. [\nPDF\n]\nSee\nfull publication\nlist for more research highlights!"
