at TAU\nStudent Life Team\nLiving in Tel Aviv\nHousing\nDiversity on Campus\nCommunity Involvement\nSocial Activism\nDean of Students\nCareer Development Center\nNew Olim\nAssistance for New Olim\nSupporting TAU\nConnect with TAU\n2025 Annual Report\nBoard of Governors\nNews and Events\nFriends Associations\nDevelopment & Public Affairs Division\nGalleries\nPrint Publications\nGlobal Campaign\nAbout the Campaign\nMessage from Campaign Chair\nTop Five Projects: The National Center for Traumatic Stress and Resilience\nTop Five Projects: Biomedical Sciences Building\nTop Five Projects: Faculty Recruitment Fund\nTop Five Projects: Student Success Center\nConnections: International Reach\nConvergence: New Paths to Discovery\nClout: Real-World Impact\nCommunity: Stronger Society\n'Bricks and Mortar': Physical Needs\nAttractive School Naming Opportunities\nGive Online Now\nAll Giving Options\nGive through American Friends\nGive through Australian Friends\nGive through Canadian Friends\nGive through Israeli Friends\nGive through UK Friends\nTAU Comprehensive Campaign: Are You Optimistic?\nAlumni\nPartnerships\nAbout\nPartnerships at TAU\nExisting Partnerships\nVisiting Delegations\nPartner With Us\nResearch Partners\nJoint Teaching & Degrees\nMobility Programs\nCustomized & Faculty-Led Programs\nCurrent Joint Funding Opportunities\nYou are here\nHomepage of Tel Aviv University\n> Prof. Ran Gilad-Bachrach\nProf. Ran Gilad-Bachrach\nSchool of Biomedical Engineering\nבית ספר להנדסה ביו-רפואית\nסגל אקדמי בכיר\nQuick navigation:\nMain Research areas\nSelected Publications\nHebrew\nEmail:\nrgb@tauex.tau.ac.il\nMy CRIS profile\nMachine Learning for Health and Well-Being lab\nGoogle Scholar\nX (Twitter) account\nLinkedin profile\nOffice:\nMulti-disciplinary Center, 307\nMain Research areas\n​\nMachine learning and its applications for health and well-being, deep leaning, technology to support behavioral changes, Private-AI\nSelected Publications\nCryptonets: Applying neural networks to encrypted data with high throughput and accuracy\nR Gilad-Bachrach, N Dowlin, K Laine, K Lauter, M Naehrig, J Wernsing\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning, 2016\nMargin based feature selection-theory and algorithms\nR Gilad-Bachrach, A Navot, N Tishby\nProceedings of the twenty-first international conference on Machine learning, 2004\nOptimal distributed online prediction using mini-batches\nO Dekel, R Gilad-Bachrach, O Shamir, L Xiao\nThe Journal of Machine Learning Research , 2012\nFull body gait analysis with Kinect\nM Gabel, R Gilad-Bachrach, E Renshaw, A Schuster\n2012 Annual International Conference of the IEEE Engineering in Medicine and Biology, 2012\nMargin analysis of the LVQ algorithm\nK Crammer, R Gilad-Bachrach, A Navot, N Tishby\nAdvances in neural information processing systems, 2003\nAbout TAU\nAcademic Units\nCampus Map\nTransport & Parking\nEmergency Contacts\nPhone Directory\nDean of Students\nSexual Harassment Prevention\nStudent Union\nComputer Services\nAcademic Calendar\nLibraries\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy and Data Protection\nTAU International\nTAU International website\nAbout\nGraduate Programs\nUndergrad Programs\nLanguage Programs\nSummer Programs\nStudy Abroad\nSupporters\nGlobal TAU Magazine\nFriends Associations\nBoard of Governors\nTAU Alumni\nDevelopment & Public Affairs\nPrint Publications\nAccessibility\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedin\nYoutube\nCoursera\nSpotify\nTel Aviv University makes every effort to respect copyright. If you own copyright to the content contained\nhere and / or the use of such content is in your opinion infringing\nContact us as soon as possible >>\nTel Aviv University, P.O. Box 39040, Tel Aviv 6997801, Israel"
