    "homepage_text": "Florence d’Alché-Buc, Professor, Télécom Paris, Institut Polytechnique de Paris\nune école de\na school from\nPlan d’accès\nActus\nFaire un don\nEnglish\nAccess Map\nNews\nDonate\nFrançais\nRecherche\nThe School\nWhy choose us ? An open school\nOur core mission\nEcosystem\nBrochures\n#TélécommiennesInTech 2022: testimonials\nKey figures\nOur commitment: no to sexual and sexist violence\nPatronage\nTeaching and research departments\nCommunications and electronics\nComputer sciences and networks\nImage, Data, Signal\nEconomics and social sciences\nJob & Internship opportunities\nBenefits\nMaster internships\nCSR commitments\nRankings\nActualités\nNews\nFocus\nNewsroom\nPressroom\nNewsletters\nRSS\nResearch\nLaboratories\nCenter for Research in Economics and Statistics (CREST)\nInterdisciplinary Institute of Innovation (i3)\nInformation Processing and Communications Laboratory (LTCI)\nReview: a year of research at Télécom Paris\nFaculty members\nStrategic Focuses\nDigital innovation, economics and regulation\nDigital Trust\nDesign, Interaction, Perception\nAI and Data Science\nCommunication systems and networks\nMathematical modeling\nPartnership-based research\nResearch chairs\nFinAI-LAB, a joint laboratory between Télécom Paris and BNP Paribas about Financial AI\nTélécom Paris, member of Carnot Télécom & Société Numérique\nResearch & Innovation Webinars by Télécom Paris\nInnovation\nTélécom Paris incubator\nSupport for start-ups\nEntrepreneurship training\nInnovation spaces\nSpin-offs\nIdeas\nThe digital magazine for human kind and its environment\nThe connected migrant at the French Museum of Immigration History\nThe new frontier in quantum computing\nAI applied to medical imaging: the challenges of data\nGenerative AI: environmental footprint\nIT researchers’ carbon footprint\nRegulation of AI against online manipulation during election\nOptical communications in free space: the security challenge\nHybrid, explainable AI for medical imaging\nIntelligent wind turbines for optimised energy production\nAI applied to medical imaging: what research?\nSecuring AI: issues, challenges, solutions\nBiocomputing: computer science applied to the study of viruses\nHuman-machine interaction in the ChatGPT era\nRefurbished batteries, reduced environmental footprint\nWhen AI learns to listen: sound revolution and machine listening\nExploring the risk of biodiversity loss\nArtificial intelligence for 3D mammography\nResearch: the vital balance between targeted innovation and scientific freedom\nCould AI help combat tax evasion?\nRebrAIn: More precise neurosurgery thanks to AI\nSecurity of connected vehicles platoons\nInternational\nStudying at Télécom Paris\nApplication\nOur international programmes\nInternational students: testimonials\nMSc in Engineering\nBefore your arrival at Télécom Paris\nPartners\nSupport for mobility\nWelcome to Télécom Paris – label Campus France***\nATHENS Week at Télécom Paris: Nearly 400 incoming and outgoing exchanges!\nHow to Apply to Our MSc in Engineering\nStudy abroad\nInternational programs\nFinancial aid to study abroad\nInternational outreach\nInternational partnerships\nInternational Key figures\nOur team\nBusiness\nTrain your employees\nRecruiting digital talent\nTransform and innovate with digital technology\nCreate and develop your business\nSupport and funding\nSubmit your internship and job offers\nStudents testimonials\nCampus\nCampus Life\nMaps & Directions\nOur new buildings in Palaiseau\nCatering\nHousing\nSport on campus\nCRDN – Library\nResources\nServices\nResearch and PhD\nEvents\nUseful informations\nClubs and Associations\nMSc in Engineering\nMSc in Engineering: your training\nYour first year: the basics of innovative digital engineering\nYour 2nd year: choose your area of focus\nYour 3rd year: prepare for your career\nHumanities and social sciences\nLanguages and cultures\nSport (en)\nReal-world learning\nA pedagogy centered on you\nProject-based learning to test out ideas\nResponsible training\nMOOCs at the heart of training\nInternational Admissions – MSc in Engineering\nAdmissions for scientific preparatory classes (CPGE) students\nStudents with Bachelor’s and Master’s Degrees\nÉcole polytechnique students through dual degree agreement\nRegistration fees and scholarships\n1st job survey: career opportunities\nMasters\nIP Paris Masters\nData and Economics for Public Policy (Polytechnique-ENSAE Paris-Télécom Paris)\nQuantum, Mathematics, Computer Science (QMI)\nMaster 2 in Quantum, Mathematics & Computer Science (QMI)\nPost Master’s Degree\nAll Post-Master’s Degrees\nPost-Master’s Degree in Smart Mobility\nPost-Master’s Degree in Autonomous AI\nAdmission\nPost-Master’s Degree in AI Data Expert\nFAQ – PMD in Big Data\nPost-Master’s Degree in Cybersecurity and Cyberdefence\nAdmission\nPost-Master’s Degree Expert Cybersecurity Netwoks & Information Systems\nAdmission\nPost Master’s Degree in Digital Project Designer with UX Design Skills\nPost-Master’s Degree in Embedded Systems\nAdmission Embedded Systems\nPost-Master’s Degree in Enterprise Digital Architect\nAdmission\nPost-Master’s Degree in Information Systems Manager\nAdmission\nPost Master’s Degree in Mobile Networks, IoT, and 5G\nPost-Master’s Degree in Network and Cyber Security Architect\nAdmission\nPost-Master’s Degree in Innovation and Entrepreneurship\nContact Post-Master’s degree\nDoctorate (PhD)\nThe PhD at Télécom Paris\nPhD Thesis Topics\nPhD Specializations\nAdmissions and Timeline\nEmployment opportunities and career plan\nPhD defenses\nTélécom Paris PhD Thesis Awards\nExecutive Education\nTélécom Paris Executive Education\nTélécom Evolution\nYou are a…\n• International student\n• Entrepreneur\n• Faculty\n• Company\nEnglish\nFrançais\nHome\nFlorence d’Alché-Buc\nFlorence D'Alché-Buc\nProfessor\nHolder of the Data Science and Artificial Intelligence for Digitalized Industry and Services Chair\nRepères biographiques\nShort Biography\nActivités\nActivities\nPublications\nPublications\nActualités\nNews\nContact\nContact\nRepères biographiques\nShort Biography\nActivités\nActivities\nPublications\nPublications\nActualités\nNews\nContact\nContact\nHome\nFlorence d’Alché-Buc\nContact\nContact\nEnvoyer un e-mail\nSend an e-mail\nTél. 01 75 31 97 06\nSite web personnel\nPersonal Web Site\nÉquipe de recherche :\nResearch Team:\nSignal, Statistique et Apprentissage (S2A)\nSignal, Statistics and Learning (S2A)\nLaboratoire :\nLaboratory:\nLaboratoire Traitement et Communication de l'Information (LTCI)\nInformation Processing and Communication Laboratory (LTCI)\nDépartement :\nDepartment:\nImage, Données, Signal (IDS)\nImage, Data, Signal (IDS)\nRepères biographiques\nShort Biography\nFlorence d’Alché-Buc\nhas been since 2014 a full professor at Télécom Paris, an IMT grande école. Previously, she was a professor at Université d’Evry, an ATIGE (Genopole Thematic Incentive Actions) researcher and joint head of the IBISC lab. She launched and managed the Challenges program as part of the PASCAL European network (2004-08) and since 2017, has become the scientific director of the Digiscome Labex. Her research is on machine learning, network inference, structured prediction and dynamical system modeling.\nSince January 2019, she holds the\nData Science and Artificial Intelligence for Digitalized Industry and Services\nResearch and Teaching Chair.\nFrom September 2021, she is Images, Data, Signal department head.\nShe has authored more than 80 articles in international journals and conference proceedings.\nActivités :\nenseignement,\nrecherche,\nprojets\nActivities :\nTeaching,\nResearch,\nProjects\nResearch interests\nMachine Learning & Artificial Intelligence, bioinformatics & medical applications.\nSubdomains: (Operator-valued) Kernel Methods, Structured Output Prediction, Reliable Machine Learning, Dynamical Systems Modeling.\nTeaching\nAs part of her teaching work, she was for several years co-head of the Data Science Master 2 at Université Paris-Saclay jointly awarded by École Polytechnique, ENSAE Paris and Université Paris Sud.\nShe participated in the conception of the new continuous education programs in artificial intelligence: a Post-Master Degree and a specialist certificate. She is also responsible for the Bearing Point Data Science Education Chair.\n@Télécom Paris\nMachine Learning (2nD Year, level Master 1)\nPACT Project\nPRIM Project\n@Ecole polytechnique\nMaster of Mathematics and applications, Université Paris-Saclay\nAdvanced Machine Learning: from theory to practise\nStructured Data: learning, prediction, dependency, testing\n@Télécom Evolution\nProfessional training:\nSpecialized Certificates Studies (CES) Data Scientist: Introduction to Machine Learning\nMachine Learning and Advanced Machine Learning\nAnd also\nUniversity Professor on secondment,\nUniversité d’Evry/Université Paris-Saclay\n.\nAssociated member and founder of the group AROBAS at\nIBISC\n,\nUniversité d’Evry/Université Paris-Saclay\n.\nOccasional collaborator of\nCMAP\n, Ecole Polytechnique.\nPublications\nPublications\nInterrogation du serveur HAL en cours...\nWaiting for HAL server...\nDernières actualités\nRecent News\nAll news\nEurope : les ressources nécessaires pour une IA de pointe (Le Monde)\nData Science & AI, Faculty Members\n— 03/12/2025\nUne tribune co-signée par Florence d'Alché-Buc parmi une trentaine d’acteurs de l’IA, [...]\nLa lettre Ideas : Hydrogène naturel, Optique libre, IA frugale, Impact des réseaux\n— 04/12/2024\nLe potentiel de l’hydrogène naturel révélé par l’IA. Les réseaux : quel impact environnemental ?\n[Ideas] Comment rendre l'IA frugale ?\nData Science & AI, Faculty Members\n— 27/11/2024\nFlorence d'Alché-Buc : Pourquoi cette notion a-t-elle émergé? Comment élaguer les modèles d’IA?\nLa lettre Ideas : Bioinformatique, Expliquer et sécuriser l'IA\n— 08/10/2024\nEt aussi : Innovation et responsabilité écologique peuvent-elles converger ?\n[Ideas] Explicabilité et confiance en l’IA ?\nDigital Trust, Data Science & AI, Faculty Members\n— 02/10/2024\nFlorence d'Alché-Buc : Ces questions se posent avec acuité depuis l'arrivée des IA génératives, [...]\nEDS 2024: ELLIS Doctoral Symposium on Machine Learning Research\nData Science & AI\n— 03/09/2024\nFocusing on AI & Sustainability, it was held on August 26-30, 2024. It ga...[truncated]"
