    "homepage_text": "Ricardo Martin-Brualla\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\nI am a researcher interested in the intersection of AI and 3D, and excited about creating new products in that space.\nPreviously, I worked at Google for eight years, most recently as a Senior Staff Research Scientist, leading and managing the team working on\ngenerating 3D assets\nfor all products in Google Search, using NeRFs, image diffusion and generative video models. \n                Before that, I worked for five years on 3D telepresence on\nProject Starline\n, from building the first end-to-end demos to leading the ML efforts for real-time novel view synthesis.\nI obtained my PhD in Computer Science and Engineering at the\nUniversity of Washington\nin 2016 with\nSteve Seitz\nas my advisor. Two of my PhD projects went viral online:\ntimelapse mining from Internet photos\n, and a\ntimelapse of Seattle from the Space Needle\n. I hold two bachelor degrees in Math and Informatics from\nBarcelona Tech / UPC\n.\nOutside of work, I love the outdoors and adventures. During COVID-19, my wife and I crossed Alaska from Ketchikan to Kotzebue on foot, packraft and cycling. We wrote about it on our blog called\nnorth2arctic\n, and we were featured in the\nMountaineers magazine\n.\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nTwitter\n/\nGithub\nResearch\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nCAT3D: Create Anything in 3D with Multi-View Diffusion Models\nRuiqi Gao\n,\nAleksander Holynski\n,\nPhilipp Henzler\n, Arthur Brussee,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nPratul P Srinivasan\n,\nJonathan T Barron\n,\nBen Poole\nNeurIPS\n, 2024\nproject page\n/\narXiv\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nIllumiNeRF: 3D Relighting without Inverse Rendering\nXiaoming Zhao\n,\nPratul P Srinivasan\n,\nDor Verbin\n,\nKeunhong Park\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nPhilipp Henzler\nNeurIPS\n, 2024\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\nLFM-3D: Learnable Feature Matching Across Wide Baselines Using 3D Signals\nArjun Karpur, Guilherme Perrotta,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nHoward Zhou\n,\nAndré Araujo\n3DV\n, 2024\nproject page\n/\narXiv\nNAVI: Category-Agnostic Image Collections with High-Quality 3D Shape and Pose Annotations\nVarun Jampani\n,\nKevis-Kokitsi Maninis\n,\nAndreas Engelhardt\n, Arjun Karpur, Karen Truong, Kyle Sargent, Stefan Popov,\nAndré Araujo\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n, Kaushal Patel, Daniel Vlasic,\nVittorio Ferrari\n,\nAmeesh Makadia\n, Ce Liu, Yuanzhen Li,\nHoward Zhou\nNeurIPS\n, 2023\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nCamP: Camera Preconditioningfor Neural Radiance Fields\nKeunhong Park\n,\nPhilipp Henzler\n,\nBen Mildenhall\n,\nJonathan T Barron\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\nSiggraph Asia\n, 2023\nproject page\n/\narXiv\nSCADE: NeRFs from Space Carving with Ambiguity-Aware Depth Estimates\nMikaela Angelina Uy\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nLeonidas Guibas\n,\nKe Li\nCVPR\n, 2023\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\nvideo\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nNovel view synthesis with diffusion models\nDaniel Watson\n,\nWilliam Chan\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nJonathan Ho\n,\nAndrea Tagliasacchi\n,\nMohammad Norouzi\nICLR\n, 2023\nproject page\n/\narXiv\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nNeRF in the Dark: High Dynamic Range View Synthesis from Noisy Raw Images\nBen Mildenhall\n,\nPeter Hedman\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nPratul P Srinivasan\n,\nJonathan T Barron\nCVPR\n, 2022\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\nProject Starline: A high-fidelity telepresence system\nJason Lawrence\n,\nDan B Goldman\n,\nSupreeth Achar\n, Gregory M Blascovich, Joseph G Desloge, Tommy Fortes, Eric M Gomez, Sascha Haberling,\nHugues Hoppe\n, Andy Huibers, Claude Knaus, Brian Kuschak,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n, Harris Nover, Andrew Ian Russell,\nSteven M Seitz\n, Kevin Tong\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n, 2021\npaper\n/\nvideo\nAdvances in Neural Rendering\nAyush Tewari\n,\nJustus Thies\n,\nBen Mildenhall\n,\nPratul P Srinivasan\n,\nEdgar Tretschk\n,\nYifan Wang\n,\nChristoph Lassner\n,\nVincent Sitzmann\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nStephen Lombardi\n,\nTomas Simon\n,\nChristian Theobalt\n,\nMatthias Niessner\n,\nJonathan T. Barron\n,\nGordon Wetzstein\n,\nMichael Zollhöfer\n,\nVladislav Golyanik\nEurographics STAR report\n, 2022\narXiv\nTime-travel rephotography\nXuan Luo\n,\nXuaner Zhang\n, Paul Yoo,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nJason Lawrence\n,\nSteven M Seitz\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\nFeatured in\nTwo Minute Papers\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nHyperNeRF: A Higher-Dimensional Representation for Topologically Varying Neural Radiance Fields\nKeunhong Park\n,\nUtkarsh Sinha\n,\nPeter Hedman\n,\nJonathan T Barron\n,\nSofien Bouaziz\n,\nDan B Goldman\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nSteven M Seitz\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nMip-NeRF: A Multiscale Representation for Anti-Aliasing Neural Radiance Fields\nJonathan T Barron\n,\nBen Mildenhall\n,\nMatthew Tancik\n,\nPeter Hedman\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nPratul P Srinivasan\nICCV\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\nvideo\nBest Paper Honorable Mention\n(top 5 papers)\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nNerfies: Deformable neural radiance fields\nKeunhong Park\n,\nUtkarsh Sinha\n,\nJonathan T Barron\n,\nSofien Bouaziz\n,\nDan B Goldman\n,\nSteven M Seitz\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\nICCV\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\nPress:\nGizmodo\n.\nFeatured in\nTwo Minute Papers\n.\nNeural RGB-D Surface Reconstruction\nDejan Azinović\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nDan B Goldman\n,\nMatthias Nießner\n,\nJustus Thies\nCVPR\n, 2022\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nNerf in the wild: Neural radiance fields for unconstrained photo collections\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nNoha Radwan\n,\nMehdi SM Sajjadi\n,\nJonathan T Barron\n,\nAlexey Dosovitskiy\n,\nDaniel Duckworth\nCVPR\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\nPress:\nPetaPixel\nFeatured in\nTwo Minute Papers\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nIBRNet: Learning multi-view image-based rendering\nQianqian Wang\n, Zhicheng Wang,\nKyle Genova\n,\nPratul P Srinivasan\n,\nHoward Zhou\n,\nJonathan T Barron\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nNoah Snavely\n,\nThomas Funkhouser\nCVPR\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\nNo Shadow Left Behind: Removing Objects and their Shadows using Approximate Lighting and Geometry\nEdward Zhang\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nJanne Kontkanen\n,\nBrian L Curless\nCVPR\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\npaper\nSharf: Shape-conditioned radiance fields from a single view\nKonstantinos Rematas\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nVittorio Ferrari\nICML\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nFiG-NeRF: Figure-Ground Neural Radiance Fields for 3D Object Category Modelling\nChristopher Xie\n,\nKeunhong Park\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nMatthew Brown\n3DV\n, 2021\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\nState of the art on neural rendering\nAyush Tewari\n,\nOhad Fried\n,\nJustus Thies\n,\nVincent Sitzmann\n,\nStephen Lombardi\n,\nKalyan Sunkavalli\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nTomas Simon\n,\nJason Saragih\n,\nMatthias Nießner\n,\nRohit Pandey\n,\nSean Fanello\n,\nGordon Wetzstein\n,\nJun-Yan Zhu\n,\nChristian Theobalt\n,\nManeesh Agrawala\n,\nEli Shechtman\n,\nDan B Goldman\n,\nMichael Zollhöfer\nEurographics STAR report\n, 2020\narXiv\nKeystoneDepth: History in 3D\nXuan Luo\n, Yanmeng Kong,\nJason Lawrence\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nSteven M Seitz\n3DV\n, 2020\nproject page\n/\npaper\n/\nvideo\nGelato: Generative latent textured objects\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nRohit Pandey\n,\nSofien Bouaziz\n,\nMatthew Brown\n,\nDan B Goldman\nECCV\n, 2020\nproject page\n/\narXiv\nMulti-view image fusion\nMarc Comino Trinidad, Ricardo Martin Brualla, Florian Kainz,\nJanne Kontkanen\nICCV\n, 2019\nproject page\n/\npaper\nNeural rerendering in the wild\nMoustafa Meshry\n,\nDan B Goldman\n,\nSameh Khamis\n,\nHugues Hoppe\n,\nRohit Pandey\n,\nNoah Snavely\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\nCVPR\n, 2019\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\nvideo\nBest Paper Award Finalist\n(top 1% of submissions)\nVolumetric capture of humans with a single rgbd camera via semi-parametric learning\nRohit Pandey\n,\nAnastasia Tkach\n, Shuoran Yang,\nPavel Pidlypenskyi\n,\nJonathan Taylor\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nAndrea Tagliasacchi\n,\nGeorge Papandreou\n, Philip Davidson,\nCem Keskin\n,\nShahram Izadi\n,\nSean Fanello\nCVPR\n, 2019\narXiv\n/\nvideo\nLookingood: Enhancing performance capture with real-time neural re-rendering\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nRohit Pandey\n, Shuoran Yang,\nPavel Pidlypenskyi\n,\nJonathan Taylor\n,\nJulien Valentin\n,\nSameh Khamis\n, Philip Davidson,\nAnastasia Tkach\n,\nPeter Lincoln\n,\nAdarsh Kowdle\n,\nChristoph Rhemann\n,\nDan B Goldman\n,\nCem Keskin\n,\nSteven M Seitz\n,\nShahram Izadi\n,\nSean Fanello\n,\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n, 2018\narXiv\n/\nvideo\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\n3D time-lapse reconstruction from internet photos\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nDavid Gallup\n,\nSteven M Seitz\nICCV\n, 2015\nproject page\n/\npaper\n/\nvideo\nPress:\nPetaPixel\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nTime-lapse mining from internet photos\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nDavid Gallup\n,\nSteven M Seitz\nSIGGRAPH\n, 2015\nproject page\n/\npaper\n/\nvideo\nPress:\nWIRED\n,\nBBC\n,\nSeattle Times\n& more.\nThe 3d jigsaw puzzle: Mapping large indoor spaces\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nYanling He\n,\nBryan C Russell\n,\nSteven M Seitz\nECCV\n, 2014\nproject page\n/\npaper\n/\nvideo\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\n3D Wikipedia: Using online text to automatically label and navigate reconstructed geometry\nBryan C Russell\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nDaniel J Butler\n,\nSteven M Seitz\n,\nLuke Zettlemoyer\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n, 2013\nproject page\n/\npaper\n/\nvideo\nPress:\nNew Scientist\n,\nGizmodo\nViewport: A distributed, immersive teleconferencing system with infrared dot pattern\nCha Zhang\n,\nQin Cai\n,\nPhilip A Chou\n,\nZhengyou Zhang\n,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\nIEEE MultiMedia\n, 2013\npaper\nThe role of query sessions in extracting instance attributes from web search queries\nMarius Pasca\n,\nEnrique Alfonseca\n, Enrique Robledo-Arnuncio,\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nKeith Hall\nEuropean Conference on Information Retrieval\n, 2010\npaper\nInstance sense induction from attribute sets\nRicardo Martin-Brualla\n,\nEnrique Alfonseca\n,\nMarius Pasca\n,\nKeith Hall\n, Enrique Robledo-Arnuncio,\nMassimiliano Ciaramita\nColing\n, 2010\npaper"
