  "serper::Binh-Son Hua": {
    "homepage": "https://sonhua.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "binhson.hua@tcd.ie"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/VinAIResearch",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Binh-Son Hua\nBinh-Son Hua\nAssistant Professor, Trinity College Dublin\nbinhson.hua (at) tcd.ie / binhson.hua (at) gmail\nGoogle Scholar\nMy current research interests are in the intersection of computer graphics and computer vision, where I focus on developing deep learning techniques for realistic image and 3D synthesis.\nMar 2025: My group currently have the following open positions to fill: a postdoctoral researcher, a research assistant, and a PhD student.\nPlease submit your application package directly to me via email. Kindly note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.\nBefore joining TCD, I was a Research Scientist at VinAI, the\nfirst AI research lab in Vietnam\nwith a focus on fundamental research in 2020-2023.                            \n\t\t\t\t\tI did my postdoctoral research on physically based rendering with Dr.\nToshiya Hachisuka\nat the University of Tokyo, and on 3D deep learning with Dr.\nSai-Kit Yeung\nat Singapore University of Technology and Design. I received my PhD at National University of Singapore in 2015, working with Dr.\nKok-Lim Low\n.\nNews\nJul 17, 2024: Two papers accepted to ECCV 2024 (diverse text-to-3D generation, and underwater instance visual description)\nFeb 27, 2024: Two papers accepted to CVPR 2024 (object insertion and removal for NeRFs, and underwater image segmentation).\nAug 04, 2023: A co-authored conference paper on Monte Carlo image denoising accepted to SIGGRAPH Asia 2023.\nJuly 14, 2023: Three papers accepted to ICCV 2023 (Stylized neural radiance fields, 360-degree neural scene decoration, and 3D point cloud instance segmentation).\nJune 22, 2023: Two papers accepted to IROS 2023.\nJune 20, 2023: I will serve as Area Chair for CVPR 2024.\nJune 07, 2023: I was recognized as a CVPR 2023 Outstanding Reviewer.\nMar 01, 2023: One paper accepted to CVPR 2023 (3D point cloud instance segmentation)\nOct 11, 2022: Two papers accepted to WACV 2023 (GAN inversion for 3D point clouds, single-image HDR reconstruction) and a paper accepted to ACCV 2022 (self-supervised point cloud learning with multiple-view rendering).\nJuly 04, 2022: Four papers accepted to ECCV 2022 with the following topics: neural scene decoration, 4D point cloud reconstruction, text-to-image synthesis, and few-shot video classification.\nJune 17, 2022: A paper about style transfer for architectural photographs accepted to ICCP 2022.\nMar 26, 2022: Two co-author papers about Monte Carlo rendering accepted to SIGGRAPH North America 2022.\nMar 03, 2022: A paper on GAN inversion accepted to CVPR 2022.\nFeb 14, 2022: An extended version of RIConv++, a simple rotation invariant convolution for point clouds, accepted to IJCV journal 2022.\nOct 20, 2021: A co-author paper on neural sequence transformation was presented at Pacific Graphics 2021 (Computer Graphics Forum).\nSep 29, 2021: A paper on few-shot learning accepted at NeurIPS 2021.\nJuly 23, 2021: Two papers on 3D point cloud learning accepted at ICCV 2021.\nJune 12, 2021: Two papers on medical segmentation are accepted at MICCAI 2021.\nJan 13, 2021: A paper on network pruning (that retraining with proper learning rate schedules matters) is accepted at ICLR 2021!\nResearch\n2023\nISBNet: a 3D Point Cloud Instance Segmentation Network\nwith Instance-aware Sampling and Box-aware Dynamic Convolution\nTuan Duc Ngo\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nKhoi Nguyen\nCVPR 2023\npaper\ncode\nPointInverter: Point Cloud Reconstruction and Editing via a Generative Model with Shape Priors\nJaeyeon Kim,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Duc-Thanh Nguyen, Sai-Kit Yeung\nWACV 2023\nproject\npaper\nSingle-Image HDR Reconstruction by Multi-Exposure Generation\nPhuoc-Hieu Le, Quynh Le, Rang Nguyen,\nBinh-Son Hua\nWACV 2023\nproject\npaper\ncode\n2022\nSelf-Supervised Learning with Multi-View Rendering for 3D Point Cloud Analysis\nBach Tran,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Anh Tuan Tran, Minh Hoai\nACCV 2022\npaper\ncode\nRFNet-4D: Joint Object Reconstruction and Flow Estimation from 4D Point Clouds\nTuan-Anh Vu, Duc-Thanh Nguyen,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Quang-Hieu Pham, Sai-Kit Yeung\nECCV 2022 (\nOral\n)\nproject\npaper\ncode\nNeural Scene Decoration from a Single Photograph\nHong-Wing Pang, Yingshu Chen, Phuoc-Hieu Le,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Duc Thanh Nguyen, Sai-Kit Yeung\nECCV 2022\nproject\npaper\ncode\nTISE: Bag of Metrics for Text-to-Image Synthesis Evaluation\nTan M. Dinh, Rang Nguyen,\nBinh-Son Hua\nECCV 2022\nproject\npaper\ncode\nInductive and Transductive Few-Shot Video Classification via Appearance and Temporal Alignments\nKhoi D. Nguyen, Quoc-Huy Tran, Khoi Nguyen,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Rang Nguyen\nECCV 2022\npaper\ncode\nSelf-Supervised Post-Correction for Monte Carlo Denoising\nJonghee Back,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Toshiya Hachisuka, Bochang Moon\nSIGGRAPH North America Conference Proceedings 2022\nproject\npaper\ncode\nRegression-based Monte Carlo Integration\nCorentin Salaün, Adrien Gruson,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Toshiya Hachisuka, Gurprit Singh\nSIGGRAPH North America 2022\nproject\npaper\nTime-of-Day Neural Style Transfer\n                for Architectural Photographs\nYingshu Chen, Tuan-Anh Vu, Ka-Chun Shum,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Sai-Kit Yeung\nICCP 2022\nproject\npaper\ncode\nHyperInverter: Improving StyleGAN Inversion via Hypernetwork\nTan M Dinh, Anh Tuan Tran, Rang Nguyen,\nBinh-Son Hua\nCVPR 2022\nproject\npaper\ncode\nRIConv++: Effective Rotation Invariant Convolutions for 3D Point Clouds Deep Learning\nZhiyuan Zhang,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Sai-Kit Yeung\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV) 2022\nproject\npaper\ncode\nSS-3DCapsNet: Self-supervised 3D Capsule Networks for Medical Segmentation on Less Labeled Data\nMinh Tran, Loi Ly,\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nNgan Le\nInternational Symposium on Biomedical Imaging (ISBI) 2022\npaper\ncode\n2021\nSingle-Click 3D Object Annotation on LiDAR Point Clouds\nTrung Nguyen\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Duc Thanh Nguyen, Dinh Phung\nNeurIPS Data-Centric AI Workshop 2021\npaper\nPOODLE: Improving Few-shot Learning via Penalizing Out-of-Distribution Samples\nDuong H. Le\n*, Khoi D. Nguyen*, Khoi Nguyen, Quoc-Huy Tran, Rang Nguyen,\nBinh-Son Hua\nNeurIPS 2021\npaper\nreview\ncode\nNeural Sequence Transformation\nSabyasachi Mukherjee\n,\nSayan Mukherjee\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nNobuyuki Umetani\n,\nDaniel Meister\nComputer Graphics Forum (Proceedings of Pacific Graphics) 2021\nproject\npaper\nPoint-set Distances for Learning Representations of 3D Point Clouds\nTrung Nguyen\n, Quang-Hieu Pham, Tam Le, Tung Pham, Nhat Ho,\nBinh-Son Hua\nICCV 2021\nproject\npaper\ncode\nMinimal Adversarial Examples for Deep Learning on 3D Point Clouds\nJaeyeon Kim\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Duc Thanh Nguyen, Sai-Kit Yeung\nICCV 2021\npaper\ncode\n3D-UCaps: 3D Capsules Unet for Volumetric Image Segmentation\nTan Nguyen\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nNgan Le\nMICCAI 2021 (\nOral\n)\npaper\ncode\nPoint-Unet: A Context-aware Point-based Neural Network for Volumetric Segmentation\nNgoc-Vuong Ho\n, \n                Tan Nguyen,\n                Gia-Han Diep,\nNgan Le\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\nMICCAI 2021\npaper\nsupplementary\ncode\nNetwork Pruning That Matters:  A Case Study on Retraining Variants\nDuong H. Le\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\nICLR 2021\npaper\nreview\ncode\n2020\nGlobal Context Aware Convolutions for 3D Point Cloud Understanding\nZhiyuan Zhang,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Wei Chen, Yibin Tian, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\n3DV 2020 (\nOral\n)\npaper\nDeep Combiner for Independent and Correlated Pixel Estimates\nJonghee Back,\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nToshiya Hachisuka\n, and\nBochang Moon\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2020\nproject\npaper\ncode\nLCD: Learned Cross-Domain Descriptors for 2D-3D Matching\nQuang-Hieu Pham\n,\nMikaela Angelina Uy\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Duc Thanh Nguyen, Gemma Roig, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\nAAAI 2020 (\nOral\n)\nproject\n2019\nRevisiting Point Cloud Classification: A New Benchmark Dataset and Classification Model on Real-World Data\nMikaela Angelina Uy\n,\nQuang-Hieu Pham\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Duc Thanh Nguyen, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\nICCV 2019 (\nOral\n)\nproject\nShellNet: Efficient Point Cloud Convolutional Neural Networks using Concentric Shells Statistics\nZhiyuan Zhang,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\nICCV 2019 (\nOral\n)\nproject\nRotation Invariant Convolutions for 3D Point Clouds Deep Learning\nZhiyuan Zhang,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, David W. Rosen, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\n3DV 2019\nproject\nA Survey on Gradient-Domain Rendering\nBinh-Son Hua\n*,\nAdrien Gruson\n*, Victor Petitjean,\nMatthias Zwicker\n, Derek Nowrouzezahrai, Elmar Eisemann, and\nToshiya Hachisuka\nEurographics 2019 State of the Art Reports\npaper\nslides\ncode\nJSIS3D: Joint Semantic-Instance Segmentation of 3D Point Clouds\nwith Multi-Task Pointwise Networks and Multi-Value Conditional Random Fields\nQuang-Hieu Pham, Duc Thanh Nguyen,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Gemma Roig, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\nCVPR 2019 (\nOral\n)\nproject\nReal-time Progressive 3D Semantic Segmentation for Indoor Scene\nQuang-Hieu Pham,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Duc Thanh Nguyen, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\nWACV 2019\nproject\n2018\nLight Transport Simulation in the Gradient Domain\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nAdrien Gruson\n,\nMatthias Zwicker\n, and\nToshiya Hachisuka\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2018 Courses\nslides\nLanguage-Driven Synthesis of 3D Scenes from Scene Databases\nRui Ma\n,\nAkshay Gadi Patil\n,\nMatthew Fisher\n,\nManyi Li\n,\nSören Pirk\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nSai-Kit Yeung\n,\nXin Tong\n,\nLeonidas Guibas\n,\nHao Zhang\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2018\nproject\nCreating and Understanding 3D Annotated Scene Meshes\nZhiyuan Zhang\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nDuc Thanh Nguyen\n,\nLap-Fai Yu\n,\nSai-Kit Yeung\n, and\nDaniela Rus\nInvited Speaker:\nSai-Kit Yeung\nand Quang-Hieu Pham\nIROS 2018 Tutorial\nslides\nGradient-domain Volumetric Photon Density Estimation\nAdrien Gruson\n,\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Nicolas Vibert,\nDerek Nowrouzezahrai\n, and\nToshiya Hachisuka\nSIGGRAPH 2018\npaper\ncode\nslides\nPointwise Convolutional Neural Networks\nBinh-Son Hua\n, Minh-Khoi Tran, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\nCVPR 2018\nproject\npaper\ncode\nCreating Annotated Scene Meshes for Training and Testing Robot Systems\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nDuc Thanh Nguyen\n,\nLap-Fai Yu\n,\nSai-Kit Yeung\n, and\nDaniela Rus\nInvited Speakers:\nDuc Thanh Nguyen\nand Quang-Hieu Pham\nICRA 2018 Tutorial\nslides\nSHREC’18: RGB-D Object-to-CAD Retrieval\nQuang-Hieu Pham,\nBinh-Son Hua\n,\nLap-Fai Yu\n,\nDuc Thanh Nguyen\n, and\nSai-Kit Yeung\nEurographics Workshop on 3D Object Retrieval 2018\nproject\n2017\nA Robust 3D-2D Interactive Tool for Scene Segmenta...[truncated]"
