    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/rui-huang/",
    "homepage_text": "Welcome, adventurers!\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nWelcome, adventurers!\nRui Huang\nSenior Research Engineer at\nGoogle Deepmind\n[\nResume\n] [\nGoogle Scholar\n]\n[\nGithub\n]\n[\nLinkedIn\n]\nEmail:\nA\n@gmail.com (where\nA\n= \"\nruih2c4gcp\")\nRecruiters: please\nno\ncontract, start up, quant trading, tiktok or non-US roles. Thanks for understanding.\nBiography\nI\nwork\non researching and developing new Multimodal Generative AI models.\nMy\nresearch interest\nincludes Deep Learning, Computer Vision, Machine Learning, Multimodal Generative AI, Diffusion Transformer, 3D Deep Learning, Representation Learning, Detection and Segmentation.\nI received my M.S. degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering from\nCarnegie Mellon University\nand B.Eng. degree in Computer Science and Technology from\nChina University of Geosciences\n.\nIn my free time, I play piano and PlayStation console, raise my Shiba Inu\npuppy\n, hiking canyons, and\ncollect artistic keycaps\n!\nWork\n:\nApr. 2025 - I joined Google Deepmind as Senior Research Engineer\nin Mountain View, CA USA.\nNov 2023 - I joined\nGoogle\nas a Senior Machine Learning Algorithm Engineer at Labs in Mountain View, CA USA.\nJan 2021 - I joined Apple as a Computer Vision Algorithm Engineer in Cupertino, CA USA.\nJuly 2019 - I joined\nGoogle AI\nas a\nResident\nin Mountain View CA USA.\nJan, 2019 - I interned at\nNvidia Research\nin Santa Clara CA USA.\nMay, 2018 - I interned at\nMitsubishi Electric Research Laboratories\nin Boston, USA.\nSep. 2017 - I was a graduate assistant at Machine Learning Department CMU, advised by Prof.\nKaterina Fragkiadaki\nand earlier at Cylab Mobility Research Center, CMU Silicon Vally.\nMar, 2017 - I  interned at National Laboratory of Pattern Recognition, Chinese Academy of Sciences, advised by Prof.\nRan He\n.\nPublication:\nSep 2021\n- Our paper \"Coupled Segmentation and Edge Learning via Dynamic Graph Propagation\"  is accepted at\nNeurIPS 2021\n, [\nlink\n][\nslides\n]!\nDec 2020 -\nTensorflow 3D\n,\na codebase for 3d scene understanding is open sourced on Github. [\nGoogle AI blog post\n] [News\n1\n2\n3\n]\nJuly 2020 -\nOur paper\n\"An LSTM Approach to Temporal 3D Object Detection in LiDAR Point Clouds\",\nECCV 2020\n.\n[\narXiv\n][\nwebsite\n][\nshort\n/\nlong\nvideo]\nSep 2019 - One paper on self-supervised GAN is accepted at\nWACV 2020\n![\npaper\n]\n2018  - One paper on online training of detector is accepted at\nAIPR 2018\n. [\npaper\n]\nJuly, 2017 - One paper is accepted at\nICCV 2017\n! \"Beyond Face Rotation: Global and Local Perception GAN for Photorealistic and Identity Preserving Frontal View Synthesis\" TP-GAN is included in high school\ntextbook\nand news\n[1]\n[2]\n[\n3\n]\n. [\npaper\n][\narXiv\n][\ncode\n]\nLe vent se lève, Il faut tenter de vivre\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
