    "homepage_text": "Xingyou (Richard) Song (宋星佑)\nXingyou (Richard) Song\nI am a Research Scientist at\nGoogle DeepMind\n, currently working on Reinforcement Learning for\nGemini Reasoning\n. Previously I worked on a variety of topics in Automated Machine Learning, Transformers, and Robotics.\nI have also worked/interned at\nOpenAI\n,\nCitadel Securities\n, and\nMicrosoft Research Asia\n.\nEmail\n/\nDBLP\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nLinkedin\n/\nGithub\n/\nTwitter\n/\nCV\nGemini Contributions\nAdvanced Version of Gemini with Deep Think Officially Achieves Gold-Medal Standard at the International Mathematical Olympiad\nKey Contributor\nGoogle DeepMind Blog Post 2025\n[Blog]\n[Website]\n[Paper]\nGemini 2.5: Pushing the Frontier with Advanced Reasoning, Multimodality, Long Context, and Next Generation Agentic Capabilities\nThinking/Reasoning Contributor\nGemini Technical Report 2025\n[arXiv]\n[Blog]\nText-to-Text Regression\nRegression Language Models for Code\nYash Akhauri\n*\n, Xingyou Song\n*\n, Arissa Wongpanich, Bryan Lewandowski, Mohamed S. Abdelfattah\nTechnical Report 2025\nPaper:\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\n[Data]\nExternal Media/References:\n[MarkTechPost]\nPerformance Prediction for Large Systems via Text-to-Text Regression\nYash Akhauri, Bryan Lewandowski, Cheng-Hsi Lin, Adrian N. Reyes, Grant C. Forbes, Arissa Wongpanich, Bangding Yang, Mohamed S. Abdelfattah, Sagi Perel, Xingyou Song\nGoogle Technical Report 2025\nPaper:\n[arXiv]\n[Google Research Blog]\n[Code]\nExternal Media/References:\n[MarkTechPost]\n[MG (Video)]\nOmniPred: Language Models as Universal Regressors\nXingyou Song, Oscar Li, Chansoo Lee, Bangding (Jeffrey) Yang, Daiyi Peng, Sagi Perel, Yutian Chen\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR) 2024\nPaper:\n[arXiv]\n[TMLR]\n[Code]\n[US Patent]\n[Poster]\nExternal Media/References:\n[HuggingFace Daily Papers]\n[arXiv Papers (Video)]\n[MarkTechPost]\n[Prompt Engineering Institute]\n[BNN Breaking]\n[MultiPlatform AI]\n[Linnk]\n[Tunadorable Papers]\n[C