  "serper::Chengqi Zhang": {
    "homepage": "https://research.polyu.edu.hk/en/persons/chengqi-zhang/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Chengqi Zhang\n      -  PolyU Scholars Hub\nPolyU Scholars Hub Home\nHelp & FAQ\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at PolyU Scholars Hub\nView Scopus Profile\nChengqi Zhang\nChair Professor\n,\nDepartment of Data Science and Artificial Intelligence\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0001-5715-7154\nPhone\n34003182\nEmail\nchengqi.zhang\npolyu.edu\nhk\nPersonal profile\nResearch interests\nDistributed Artificial Intelligence and Data Mining\nBiography\nProf Chengqi Zhang had joined the Department of Data Science and Artificial Intelligence at The Hong Kong Polytechnic University (PolyU) as a Chair Professor of Artificial Intelligence in September 2024.  He was appointed as the Director of PolyU Shenzhen Research Institute from 1 January 2025.\nHe had been appointed as a Pro Vice-Chancellor (China Enterprise) on 1 December 2017 till 30 November 2025 at the University of Technology Sydney (UTS), a Distinguished Professor on 27 February 2017 till 2027 at UTS, and a Research Professor of Information Technology from 14 December 2001 at UTS.  Before 2001, he was an Associate Professor from January 1999 to December 2001 at Deakin University, an Associate Professor from January 1998 to January 1999 at the University of New England (UNE), a Senior Lecturer from January 1994 to January 1998 at UNE, and a Lecturer from January 1990 to January 1994 at UNE.\nIn addition, he was appointed as an Adjunct Professor from 20 March 2017 to 20 March 2020 at the University of New South Wales (UNSW) and as a Honorary Professor from 1 March 2015 to 31 December 2017 at the University of Queensland (UQ).\nEducation/Academic qualification\nDoctor of Science,\nDeakin University\nBachelor of Science,\nFudan University\nMaster of Science,\nJilin University\nDoctor of Philosophy,\nThe University of Queensland\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Chengqi Zhang is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\nData Mining\nComputer Science\n100%\nArtificial Data\nComputer Science\n100%\nDistributed Artificial Intelligence\nComputer Science\n100%\nDistributed Intelligence\nKeyphrases\n100%\nArtificial Intelligence\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n100%\nView full fingerprint"
  },
