  "serper::Tong Wang": {
    "homepage": "https://www.tongwang-academic.com/",
    "emails": [
      "tong.wang@chicagobooth.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Tong Wang\ntop of page\nTONG WANG\n📣  At the\nINFORMS Annual Meeting 2025\n, my presentation information is as follows:\nMitigating Gender Bias in Higher Ed Instructor Evaluations\nSession Title: ​OM in Education (ME50)\nTime\n: Monday, October 27, 4:15 PM - 4:30 PM (first slot out of five)\nRoom\n: Building B Level 3 B310\nThe Ratings Trap: Prior Ratings, Gender and Instructor Outcomes in Higher Ed\nSession Title: Empirical Research in Socially Responsible Operations (TD52)\nTime\n: Tuesday, October 28, 2:45 PM - 3:03 PM (first slot out of four)\nRoom\n: Building B Level 3 B312\nGenerative AI and Content Homogenization: the Case of Digital Marketing\n​Session Title: Causal Inference and Machine Learning in Operations Management (TD50)\nTime\n: Tuesday, October 28, 3:15 PM - 3:30 PM (third slot out of five)\nRoom\n: Building B Level 3 B310\nWelcome to my website! I have been a Postdoctoral Researcher at\nChicago Booth\nsince\nSummer 2025\n,\nunder the guidance of Professor\nJohn Birge\nand\nProfessor\nAli Hortaçsu\n.\nI did my Ph.D. in the\nManagement Science and Operations Department\nat\nLondon Business School\n, where I am co-advised by Professor\nKamalini Ramdas\nand Professor\nS. Alex Yang\n.​​​\n​\n​My research focuses on\ninnovative operational interventions\nto generate\nsustainable social impact\n. I primarily use empirical methods, including experiments, and analytical methods. I have two research streams:​\n​I examine operational levers to improve equity and inclusion in service evaluations.\nI am interested in enhancing efficiency and sustainability via improved designs in this era of Generative AI.​​\nbottom of page"
  },
  "serper::Zhaoxiang Zhang": {
    "homepage": "https://zhaoxiangzhang.net/",
    "emails": [
      "zhang@ia.ac",
      "zhang@ieee.org"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zhaoxiang Zhang (张兆翔)\nZhaoxiang Zhang (张兆翔)\nHome\nProf.\nZhaoxiang Zhang\nNational Laboratory of Pattern Recognition\n,\nInstitute of Automation\n,\nChinese Academy of Sciences\nUniversity of Chinese Academy of Sciences\nEmail\n: zhaoxiang[dot]zhang[at]ia[dot]ac[dot]cn\nzhaoxiang[dot]zhang[at]ieee[dot]org\nOpening Positions\n:\nStudent\n,\nIntern\n,\nPostDoc\nand\nFaculty\nAbout Me\nZhaoxiang Zhang\nreceived his bachelor’s degree from the\nDepartment of Electronic Science and Technology\nin the\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\n(USTC) in 2004. After that, he was a Ph.D. candidate under the supervision of Professor\nTieniu Tan\nin the\nNational Laboratory of Pattern Recognition\n,\nInstitute of Automation\n,\nChinese Academy of Sciences\n, where he received his Ph.D. degree in 2009. In October 2009, he joined the\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering\n,\nBeihang University\n, as an Assistant Professor (2009-2011) and an Associate Professor (2012-2015). In July 2015, he returned to the\nInstitute of Automation\n,\nChinese Academy of Sciences\n. He is now a full Professor in the\nCenter for Research on Intelligent Perception and Computing\n(CRIPAC) and the\nNational Laboratory of Pattern Recognition\n(NLPR). He is also an Adjunct Professor in\nThe Hong Kong Polytechnic University (PolyU)\nHis research interests include\nComputer Vision\n,\nPattern Recognition\n, and\nMachine Learning\n. Recently, he specifically focuses on\ndeep learning models,\nbiologically-inspired visual computing\nand\nhuman-like learning\n, and their applications on\nhuman analysis\nand\nscene understanding\n.\nHe has published more than 200 papers in international journals and conferences, including reputable international journals such as IEEE T-PAMI, IJCV, JMLR, IEEE TIP, IEEE TNN, IEEE TCSVT, IEEE TIFS and top level international conferences like CVPR, ICCV, NIPS, ICLR, ECCV, AAAI, IJCAI and ACM MM.\nHe is serving or has served as the Associated Editor of\nIEEE T-CSVT\n,\nPatten Recognition\n,\nNeurocomputing\n,  and\nFrontiers of Computer Science\n. He has served as the Area Chairs of top level International conferences like CVPR, NIPS, ICML, AAAI, IJCAI and ACM MM. He is a Senior Member of\nIEEE\n, a Distinguished Member of\nCCF\n, and a Distinguished member of\nCAAI\n.\nHe was elected as an\nIAPR Fellow\nof the International Association for Pattern Recognition (IAPR) in 2024. He has been awarded with “\nThe Chang Jiang Distinguished Professor\n”, “\nThe National Youth Talent Support Program\n” and “\nNew Century Excellent Talents in University\n“. His research has won  the “\nTechnical Inovation Award of the Chinese Association of Aritifical Intelligence\n“.\nGo to Top\nWhat is new\nAug. 2025: 2 papers accepted in\nIEEE TPAMI\nJul. 2025: 3 papers accepted in\nICCV'2025\nMar. 2025: 2 papers accepted in\nCVPR'2025\nJan. 2025: 5 papers accepted in\nICLR'2025\nDec. 2024: 5 papers accepted in\nIEEE TPAMI\nNov. 2024: 2 papers accepted in\nAAAI'2024\nSep. 2024: 1 paper accepted in\nNeurIPS'2024\nJul. 2024: 5 papers accepted in\nECCV'2024\nMar. 2024: 8 papers accepted in\nCVPR'2024\nJan. 2024: 1 paper accepted in\nICLR'2024\nDec. 2023: 5 papers accepted in\nIEEE TPAMI\nSep. 2023: 3 papers accepted in\nNeurIPS'2023\nMar. 2023: 9 papers accepted in\nCVPR'2023\nMar. 2022: 11 papers accepted in\nCVPR'2022\nMar. 2021: 7 papers accepted in\nCVPR'2021\nFeb. 2021: I will serve as the Area Chair of\nACM MM'2021\nFeb. 2021: I will serve as the Associate Editor of the Journal of\nIJAC\nNov. 2020: I will serve as the Area Chair of\nICCV'2021\nNov. 2020: I will serve as the Associate Editor of the journal of\nCJIG\n[中国图象图形学报]\nJul. 2020: I will serve as the Area Chair of\nIJCAI'2021\nJul. 2020: 3 papers accepted in\nECCV'2020\nJul. 2020: Glad to have my position promoted in the\nCEBSIT\n, CAS\nApr. 2020: I am leading a “2035 Innovation Team”of AI fundermental research in CASIA\nMar. 2020: 2 of the 5 papers selected as oral (top 5%) in\nCVPR'2020\nFeb. 2020: 5 papers accepted in\nCVPR'2020\nJan. 2020: I will serve as the Area Chair of\nACM MM'2020\nJan. 2020: I will serve as the Area Chair of\nCVPR'2021\nDec. 2019: I have been an Associate Editor of\nIEEE T-CSVT\nSep. 2019: I have been an Associate Editor of\nPattern Recognition\nMore\nOpening Positions\n依托自动化所、国科大等高水平学术机构招收博士、硕士研究生，欢迎联系\n接纳学术能力突出的科研人员和研发能力突出的工程人员加入团队，欢迎联系\n接纳具有较好研究基础，愿意开展高水平合作研究的博士后研究人员，欢迎联系\n招收本科及研究生学历，动手能力强，有学术追求的实习生，欢迎联系\n搜索：\nZhaoxiang Zhang © 2020"
  },
