  "serper::Liu Leqi": {
    "homepage": "https://leqiliu.github.io/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/alshedivat",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Liu Leqi\nLiu Leqi\nEmail:\nsn.suodc.tuamocce@\nunscramble\nOffice:\nCBA 6.442\nWelcome! I am an AI researcher currently focusing on understanding and developing large language models. My overarching research goal is to build controllable machine intelligence that serves humanity safely. For more information about my research, please check out the\nHUMAIN lab\n.\nCurrent Appointments:\nAssistant Professor (2024 - now) in use-inspired AI at the\nDepartment of Information, Risk, and Operations Management\n, UT Austin\nAffiliated faculty (2025 - now) in\nComputer Science\n, UT Austin\nVisiting Faculty Researcher (20% appointment, 2025 - now), Google\nPast Experience:\nI obtained my Ph.D. from the\nMachine Learning Department\nat\nCarnegie Mellon University\nin 2023, where I was advised by\nZachary Lipton\n. During my Ph.D., I interned at\nGoogle DeepMind\nLondon in Summer 2022, working on deep reinforcement learning for mechanism design, and at\nApple Siri\nin Summer 2019. I was an\nOpen Philanthropy AI Fellow\nfrom 2020 to 2023, and was a postdoctoral researcher at\nPrinceton Language and Intelligence\nfrom 2023 to 2024. My Bachelor’s degrees are in Computer Science from\nBryn Mawr College\nand Mathematics from\nHaverford College\n. During my undergrad, I spent a wonderful semester at\nAIT-Budapest\nin Spring 2016.\nProspective students:\nPlease read our\nlab website\nbefore completing the\nGoogle Form\nto express your interest."
  },
