    "homepage_text": "Mingqing Xiao’s Homepage\nMingqing Xiao\nResearcher at Microsoft Research Asia\nFollow\nShanghai, China\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nABOUT ME\nI am currently a Researcher at Microsoft Research Asia (Shanghai). Previously, I obtained the Ph.D. degree in Intelligence Science and Technology at Peking University in 2025, supervised by Prof.\nZhouchen Lin\n, and obtained the B.S. degree in Computer Science and Technology and B.S. degree in Psychology from Peking University in 2020.\nMy research interests include machine learning, brain-inspired algorithms, neural network optimization, the intersection between deep learning and neuroscience, and deep learning applications.\nIn the summer 2019, I was a visiting student at\nCCVL (Computational Cognition, Vision, and Learning) lab\nin Johns Hopkins University, supervised by Prof.\nAlan Yuille\n. From Sep. 2019 to Jun. 2020, I was a research intern at Microsoft Research Asia Machine Learning Group.\nPublications\nConference Papers\nOnline Pseudo-Zeroth-Order Training of Neuromorphic Spiking Neural Networks\n[openreview]\n[arxiv]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Qingyan Meng, Zongpeng Zhang, Di He, Dongsheng Li, Zhouchen Lin\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2026\nPseuZO: Pseudo-Zeroth-Order Algorithm for Training Deep Neural Networks\n[openreview]\nPengyun Yue, Xuanlin Yang,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Zhouchen Lin\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2025\nLanguage Ranker: A Lightweight Ranking Framework for Language Models\n[openreview]\nChengheng Zhang, Tianqi Du, Jizhe Zhang,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Yifei Wang, Yisen Wang, Zhouchen Lin\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2025\nTemporal Spiking Neural Networks with Synaptic Delay for Graph Reasoning\n[openreview]\n[arxiv]\n[code]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Yixin Zhu, Di He, Zhouchen Lin\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2024\nHebbian Learning based Orthogonal Projection for Continual Learning of Spiking Neural Networks\n[openreview]\n[arxiv]\n[code]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Qingyan Meng, Zongpeng Zhang, Di He, Zhouchen Lin\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2024\nTowards Memory- and Time-Efficient Backpropagation for Training Spiking Neural Networks\n[arxiv]\n[code]\nQingyan Meng,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Shen Yan, Yisen Wang, Zhouchen Lin, Zhi-Quan Luo\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2023\nOnline Training Through Time for Spiking Neural Networks\n[openreview]\n[arxiv]\n[code]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Qingyan Meng, Zongpeng Zhang, Di He, Zhouchen Lin\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2022\n(Spotlight)\nTraining High-Performance Low-Latency Spiking Neural Networks by Differentiation on Spike Representation\n[link]\n[arXiv]\n[code]\nQingyan Meng,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Shen Yan, Yisen Wang, Zhouchen Lin, Zhi-Quan Luo\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2022\nTraining Feedback Spiking Neural Networks by Implicit Differentiation on the Equilibrium State\n[openreview]\n[arxiv]\n[code]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Qingyan Meng, Zongpeng Zhang, Yisen Wang, Zhouchen Lin\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2021\n(Spotlight, Top 3%)\nInvertible Image Rescaling\n[link]\n[arXiv]\n[code]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Shuxin Zheng, Chang Liu, Yaolong Wang, Di He, Jiang Bian, Guolin Ke, Zhouchen Lin, Tie-Yan Liu\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2020\n(Oral, Top 2%)\nTDMPNet: Prototype Network with Recurrent Top-Down Modulation for Robust Object Classification under Partial Occlusion\n[link]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Adam Kortylewski, Ruihai Wu, Siyuan Qiao, Wei Shen, Alan Yuille\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision Workshops (ECCVW), 2020\nJournal Papers\nModel-agnostic linear-memory online learning in spiking neural networks\n[link]\nChaoming Wang, Xingsi Dong, Zilong Ji,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Jiedong Jiang, Xiao Liu, Yuxiang Huan, Si Wu\nNature Communications, 2026\nDeep learning-enabled ultra-broadband terahertz high-dimensional photodetector\n[link]\nZong-kun Zhang, Teng Zhang, Zong-Peng Zhang, Ming-Zhe Chong,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Pu Peng, Peijie Feng, Haonan Sun, Zhipeng Zheng, Xiaofei Zang, Zheyu Fang, Ming-Yao Xia\nNature Communications, 2025\nDesigning Universally-Approximating Deep Neural Networks: A First-Order Optimization Approach\n[link]\nZhoutong Wu,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Cong Fang, Zhouchen Lin\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI), 2024\nSampling Complex Topology Structures for Spiking Neural Networks\n[link]\nShen Yan, Qingyan Meng,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Yisen Wang, Zhouchen Lin\nNeural Networks, 2024\nEfficient and Generalizable Cross-patient Epileptic Seizure Detection through A Spiking Neural Network\n[link]\nZongpeng Zhang,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Taoyun Ji, Yuwu Jiang, Tong Lin, Xiaohua Zhou, Zhouchen Lin\nFrontiers in Neuroscience (section Neuromorphic Engineering), 2024\nCross-patient automatic epileptic seizure detection using patient-adversarial neural networks with spatio-temporal EEG augmentation\n[link]\nZongpeng Zhang, Taoyun Ji,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Wen Wang, Guojing Yu, Tong Lin, Yuwu Jiang, Xiaohua Zhou, Zhouchen Lin\nBiomedical Signal Processing and Control, 2024\nSPIDE: A Purely Spike-based Method for Training Feedback Spiking Neural Networks\n[link]\n[arxiv]\n[code]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Qingyan Meng, Zongpeng Zhang, Yisen Wang, Zhouchen Lin\nNeural Networks, 2023\nInvertible Rescaling Network and Its Extensions\n[link]\n[arxiv]\n[code]\nMingqing Xiao\n, Shuxin Zheng, Chang Liu, Zhouchen Lin, Tie-Yan Liu\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV), 2022\nTraining Much Deeper Spiking Neural Networks with A Small Number of Time-Steps\n[link]\nQingyan Meng, Shen Yan,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Yisen Wang, Zhouchen Lin, Zhi-Quan Luo\nNeural Networks, 2022\nTraining Neural Networks by Lifted Proximal Operator Machines\n[link]\nJia Li,\nMingqing Xiao\n, Cong Fang, Yue Dai, Chao Xu, Zhouchen Lin\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI), 2020\nAcademic Service\nArea Chair: ICML (2026)\nReviewer: NeurIPS (2021-2025), ICML (2022-2025), ICLR (2023-2026), CVPR (2023-2026), ICCV (2023,2025), ECCV (2024), AAAI (2026), IJCV, TNNLS, Neural Networks, TCSVT, Neurocomputing, TMLR"
