    "homepage_text": "Tao Sun\nSearch\nTao Sun\nPhD Student\nStanford University\nGradient Spaces Lab\nI am a PhD student in\nGradient Spaces Lab\n,\nStanford University\n, working with\nIro Armeni\nand\nShuran Song\n. My research focuses on 3D vision and robotics, particularly the understanding and reasoning about 3D shapes for robotic assembly tasks.\nPrior to this, I was at\nByteDance Seed Lab\nwhere I worked on large language models’ (LLMs) post training and reasoning, and at the\nComputer Vison Lab\nat ETH Zurich, focusing on scene understanding and multitask learning. I hold an M.Sc. in Computer Science from\nETH Zurich\nand a B.Sc. in Software Engineering from\nTongji University\n.\nFeel free to reach out to me via email for chats and collaborations!\nInterests\n3D Vision\nVision-Language-Action (VLA) Models\nRobotics\nPublications\nRectified Point Flow: Generic Point Cloud Pose Estimation\nTao Sun\n,\nLiyuan Zhu\n,\nShengyu Huang\n,\nShuran Song\n,\nIro Armeni\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nProject\nNothing Stands Still: A Spatiotemporal Benchmark on 3D Point Cloud Registration Under Large Geometric and Temporal Change\nTao Sun\n,\nYan Hao\n,\nShengyu Huang\n,\nSilvio Savarese\n,\nKonrad Schindler\n,\nMarc Pollefeys\n,\nIro Armeni\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nProject\nNSS Challenge\nSHIFT: A Synthetic Driving Dataset for Continuous Multi-Task Domain Adaptation\nTao Sun\n,\nMattia Segu\n,\nJanis Postels\n,\nYuxuan Wang\n,\nLuc Van Gool\n,\nBernt Schiele\n,\nFederico Tombari\n,\nFisher Yu\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nPoster\nProject\nTalk\nDemo\nOn the Practicality of Deterministic Epistemic Uncertainty\nJanis Postels\n,\nMattia Segu\n,\nTao Sun\n,\nLuca Sieber\n,\nLuc Van Gool\n,\nFisher Yu\n,\nFederico Tombari\nPDF\nCite\nLeveraging Crowdsourced GPS Data for Road Extraction From Aerial Imagery\nTao Sun\n,\nZonglin Di\n,\nPengyu Che\n,\nChun Liu\n,\nYin Wang\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nPoster\nSupp\nCombining Satellite Imagery and GPS Data for Road Extraction\nTao Sun\n,\nZonglin Di\n,\nYin Wang\nPDF\nCite\nSlides\nLink\nStacked U-Nets with Multi-output for Road Extraction\nTao Sun\n,\nZehui Chen\n,\nWenxiang Wen\n,\nYin Wang\nPDF\nCite\nPoster\nLecture Notes\nGuarantees for ML 2021\nMy lecture notes for Guarantees for Machine Learning 2021, ETHz\nAdvanced ML 2020\nMy lecture notes for Advance Machine Learning 2020, ETHz\nContact\nName\nEmail\nMessage\nSend\nStanford, 94305, CA\ntaosun@stanford.edu\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
  "serper::Long Chen": {
    "homepage": "https://longcw.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "longch1024@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/longcw",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/longch/",
    "homepage_text": "Long Chen's Homepage\nLong Chen\nPhD @ Dept. of Computer Science & Technology, Tsinghua University\nEmail:\nlongch1024@gmail.com\nGithub:\nhttps://github.com/longcw\nGoogle Scholar:\nhttps://scholar.google.com/citations?user=FlIzsGQAAAAJ\nLinkedIn:\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/longch\nAbout Me\nI received my PhD in Computer Science from Tsinghua University in June 2021, \n        supervised by\nProf.\n        Haizhou Ai\n, \n        and my BE in Electronic Information Engineering from Huazhong University of Science and Technology in July 2016.\n        I joined\nAiFi\nas the Tech Lead & Engineering Manager since July 2021, \n        before that, I worked there as an intern and Tech Lead in people tracking.\nEducation\nTsinghua University, Beijing, China\nPhD Candidate\n, Dept. of Computer Science and Technology\nResearch Topic:\nMulti­Object Tracking, 3D Human Pose Estimation, Detection and Person\n          Re-identification\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology, Wuhan, China\nBachelor of Electronic and Information Engineering\nRank: 1/175\nResearch Projects\nMulti-Person 3D Pose Estimation and Tracking from Multiple View\nAssociating human keypoints across multiple cameras and frames to reconstruct and track\n          people in 3D space. The method works in real­time and has been deployed to some realworld productions.\nAccepted by CVPR 2020 (\narxiv\n)\nVideo Demo1\n,\nVideo Demo2\nOnline / Near-Online Multi-Object Tracking\nA series of tracking­by­detection approaches that designed for tracking multiple people in a\n          monocular, unconstrained camera.\n          The proposed methods achieved state­-of-­the­-art performance on\nMOTChallenge\nfor both accuracy and speed at that time.\nThe published papers have been cited by over 500 times.\nPaper1\n,\nPaper2\n,\nCode\n,\nVideo Demo\nSingle Camera Relative Depth Estimation with Synthetic Data\nObtianing relative depth from single image, trained using both real-world images from\nNYU Depth\nand\n          synthetic\n          images from the computer game\nGTA-V\n.\nVideo1\n,\nVideo2\n,\nOnline Demo\nObject Detection in Faster R-CNN and YOLO\nLearning PyTorch along with Faster R­CNN and YOLOv2, implemented the first, or one of\n          the firsts, open­source object detector that written in PyTorch.\n          The most interesting part of this project is to read the\n          source code of Torch & PyTorch and implement the RoIPooling using Cuda.\nThe repositories on Github have recieved over 2000 stars in total.\nCodes of\nFaster R-CNN\n,\nYOLOv2\nPublications\nL Chen\n, H Ai, R Chen, Z Zhuang, S Liu “Cross-View Tracking for Multi-Human 3D Pose Estimation at over 100\n        FPS”,\n        CVPR , 2020.\n[pdf]\nL Chen\n, H Ai, R Chen, Z Zhuang, “Aggregate Tracklet Appearance Features for Multi-Object Tracking”,\n        IEEE Signal Processing Letters, 2019.\n[pdf]\nL Chen\n, H Ai, Z Zhuang, C Shang, “Real-time Multiple People Tracking with Deeply Learned\n        Candidate Selection and Person Re-Identification”, IEEE International Conference on Multimedia\n        and Expo, 2018.\n[pdf]\n[code]\nL Chen\n, H Ai, C Shang, Z Zhuang, B Bai, “Online Multi-Object Tracking with Convolutional\n        Neural Networks”, IEEE International Conference on Image Processing, 2017.\n[pdf]\nR Chen, H Ai, C Shang,\nL Chen\n, Z Zhuang, “Learning Lightweight Pedestrian Detector with\n        Hierarchical Knowledge Distillation”, IEEE International Conference on Image Processing, 2019.\n[pdf]\n[code]\nZ Zhuang, H Ai,\nL Chen\n, C Shang, “Cross-Resolution Person Re-identification with Deep Antithetical\n        Learning”, Asian Conference on Computer Vision, 2018.\n[pdf]\nProfessional Skills\nProgramming Language:\nC/C++, Python\nDeep Learning Framework:\nPyTorch, Tensorflow, Caffe"
  },
