    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/kunhao-zheng-x18/",
    "homepage_text": "Kunhao Zheng | Home\nKunhao Zheng\nHi, I’m Kunhao Zheng (pronunced like\ncun-how\n), a passionate learner, as well as a student researcher, in machine/deep learning. I tend to devote myself to projects that are meaningful and do good to the community.\nFeel free to look around. If you want to contact me, drop me a message on\ndyekuu [at] gmail [dot] com\n."
  },
  "serper::Jesse Michael Han": {
    "homepage": "https://jesse-michael-han.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "jessemichaelhan@gmail.com",
      "jmh288@pitt.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/flypitch",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jesse Michael Han\nResearch\nBlog\nMisc.\nJesse Michael Han\nResearch\nBlog\nMisc.\nAbout\nI am a research scientist at\nOpenAI\n. I am also finishing a mathematics PhD under the supervision of\nTom Hales\nat the University of Pittsburgh.\nResearch\nMy\nresearch\nis at the intersection of formal proofs, automated reasoning, and machine learning.\nRecently, I worked on SOTA\nunsupervised machine translation using generative language models only\n.\nBefore that, I applied\nlarge language models to theorem proving\nin Lean, built solvers for\nIMO geometry problems\n, and led the\nFlypitch\nproject.\nContact\nE-mail\n:\njessemichaelhan [at] gmail [dot] com"
  },
