    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Fangyun Wei at Microsoft Research\nSkip to main content\nMicrosoft\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nSearch\nSearch Microsoft Research\nNo results\nCancel\nFangyun Wei\nSenior Research SDE\nAbout\nI got my master degree in Peking University in July, 2017, and joined Microsoft Research Asia (MSRA). My research interests include computer vision, video understanding, self-supervised learning, semi-supervised learning, multi-modality learning, data-efficient learning, sign language translation, object detection and segmentation and human-face related topics. I’m a reviewer of CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, IJCAI, ACM MM, AAAI, IJCV and PAMI.\nI’m hiring long-term research intern(s), please send your resume to fawe@microsoft.com if you are interested in my projects and internship in MSRA.\nOpens in a new tab\nResearch areas\nAlgorithms\nArtificial intelligence\nComputer vision\nFollow us:\nFollow on X\nLike on Facebook\nFollow on LinkedIn\nSubscribe on Youtube\nFollow on Instagram\nSubscribe to our RSS feed\nShare this page:\nShare on X\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nShare on Reddit"
  },
  "serper::Minlie Huang": {
    "homepage": "https://coai.cs.tsinghua.edu.cn/hml",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/thu-coai",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Dr. Minlie Huang's Homepage\nMinlie Huang(黄民烈)\nFull Professor\r\nDepartment of Computer Science,\r\nInstitute for Artificial Intelligence,\r\nTsinghua University\nDBLP\nGoogle Scholar\nEmail\nai{my_last_name}@tsinghua.edu.cn\nPhone\n+86 - 10 - 62777699\nOffice\nRoom 4-504, FIT Building\nAddress\nDept. of Computer Science,\r\nTsinghua University,\r\nBeijing 100084, China\nAbout\nPublications\nHonors & Rewards\nServices\nCourses\nTalks\nRecruitment\nAbout Me\nMy general interests include artificial intelligence, deep learning, and natural language processing. I am particularly interested in the following fields:\nNatural language generation theories, models & evaluation\nFundamental problems in large language models and multi-modal foundation models\nAI alignment, safety and ethics\nSocial intelligence with large language models (emotion, theory-of-mind, mental health applications)\nI am leading a research group named\nConversational AI\n(CoAI,\nGitHub link\n). This group published more than 100 papers on ACL, ICLR, ICML, Neurips conferences, and has won many paper awards including COLING 2010 best paper, ACL 2012 best student paper, IJCAI 2018 distinguished paper, SIGDIAL 2020 best paper, NLPCC 2015/2020 best paper, ACL 2023/2024 area chair award, etc. We have also highly cited works including\nemotional chatting machine\n(AAAI 2018),\nESC\n(ACL 2021),\nPPT\n(ACL 2022),\nMiniLLM\n(ICLR 2024),\nChatGLM\n(2024, with Prof. Jie Tang), etc.\nA full version of group introduction can be seen\nhere\n.\nWe also welcome talented undergraduates and interns to join us for doing interesting and amazing research. I also supervised and led many undergraduates to do research. Here are my thoughts on\nhow undergraduates can make successful research\n.\nResources\nLearning to Ask Questions in Open-domain Conversational Systems with Typed Decoders\n(\ndata link\n, extraction code: yz06)\nAssigning Personality/Profile to a Chatting Machine for Coherent Conversation Generation\n(\ndata link\n, extraction code: 0ls2)\nCommonsense Knowledge Aware Conversation Generation with Graph Attention\n(\ndata link\n)\nGenerating Informative Responses with Controlled Sentence Function\n(\ndata link\n, extraction code: hzo0)\nEmotional Chatting Machine\n(\ndata link\n, including emotion classifier and the emotional STC dataset)\nConvLab-3: A Flexible Dialogue System Toolkit Based on a Unified Data Format\n(\nGithub link\n)\nCritiqueLLM: Towards an Informative Critique Generation Model for Evaluation of Large Language Model Generatio\nn\n(\nGithub link\n)\nShieldLM: Empowering LLMs as Aligned, Customizable and Explainable Safety Detectors\n(\nGithub link\n)\nMiniPLM: Knowledge Distillation for Pre-Training Language Models\n(\nGithub link\n)\nCharacterGLM: Customizing Chinese Conversational AI Characters with Large Language Models\n(\nGithub link\n)\nAISafetyLab: A Comprehensive Framework for AI Safety Evaluation and Improvement\n(\nGithub link\n)\nSelected Publications\nSelect category\nCategory\nAll\n2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n2021\n2020\n2019\n2018\nbefore\nShiyao Cui, Xijia Feng, Yingkang Wang, Junxiao Yang, Zhexin Zhang, Biplab Sikdar, Hongning Wang, Han Qiu, Minlie Huang\nWhen Smiley Turns Hostile: Interpreting How Emojis Trigger LLMs' Toxicity\n.\nAAAI 2026\nZhexin Zhang, Yuhao Sun, Junxiao Yang, Shiyao Cui, yuanchao zhang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nBe Careful When Fine-tuning On Open-Source LLMs: Your Fine-tuning Data Could Be Secretly Stolen\n.\nICLR 2026\nJunxiao Yang, Jinzhe Tu, Haoran Liu, Xiaoce Wang, Chujie Zheng, Zhexin Zhang, Shiyao Cui, Caishun Chen, Tiantian He, Hongning Wang, Yew-Soon Ong, Minlie Huang\nBARREL: Boundary-Aware Reasoning for Factual and Reliable LRMs\n.\nICLR 2026\nMingyu Su, Jian Guan, Yuxian Gu, Minlie Huang, Hongning Wang （with Assoc. Prof. Hongning Wang）\nTrust-Region Adaptive Policy Optimization\n.\nICLR 2026\nJinfeng Zhou, Yongkang Huang, Bosi Wen, Guanqun Bi, Yuxuan Chen, Pei Ke, Zhuang Chen, Xiyao Xiao, Libiao Peng, Kuntian Tang, Rongsheng Zhang, Le Zhang, Tangjie Lv, Zhipeng Hu, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nCharacterBench: Benchmarking Character Customization of Large Language Models\n.\nAAAI 2025\nZhuang Chen*, Yaru Cao*, Guanqun Bi, Jincenzi Wu, Jinfeng Zhou, Xiyao Xiao, Si Chen, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nSocialSim: Towards Socialized Simulation of Emotional Support Conversation\n.\nAAAI 2025\nJiale Cheng, Xiao Liu, Cunxiang Wang, Xiaotao Gu, Yida Lu, Dan Zhang, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nSPaR: Self-Play with Tree-Search Refinement to Improve Instruction-Following in Large Language Models\n.\nICLR 2025\nJiaxin Wen, Ruiqi Zhong, Akbir Khan, Ethan Perez, Jacob Steinhardt, Minlie Huang, Samuel R. Bowman, He He, Shi Feng\nLanguage Models Learn to Mislead Humans via RLHF\n.\nICLR 2025\nJiaxin Wen*, Jian Guan*, Hongning Wang, Wei Wu, Minlie Huang\nUnlocking Reasoning Potential in Large Language Models by Scaling Code-form Planning\n.\nICLR 2025\nYuxian Gu, Li Dong, Hongning Wang, Yaru Hao, Qingxiu Dong, Furu Wei, Minlie Huang\nData Selection via Optional Training for Language Models\n.\nICLR 2025\nYuxian Gu, Hao Zhou, Fandong Meng, Minlie Huang\nMiniPLM: Knowledge Distillation for Pre-Training Language Models\n.\nICLR 2025\nErle Zhu, Yadi Liu, Zhe Zhang, Xujun Li, JinZhou, Xinjie Yu, Minlie Huang, Hongning Wang（with Assoc. Prof. Hongning Wang）\nMAPS: Advancing Multi-Modal Reasoning in Expert-Level Physical Science\n.\nICLR 2025\nZhihua Wen, Zhizhao Liu, Zhiliang Tian, Shilong Pan, Zhen Huang, Dongsheng Li, Minlie Huang（ with Assoc. Prof. Zhiliang Tian）\nScenario-independent Uncertainty Estimation for LLM-based Question Answering via Factor Analysis\n.\nWWW 2025\nMinlie Huang, Yingkang Wang, Shiyao Cui, Pei Ke, Jie Tang\nThe Superalignment of Superhuman Intelligence with Large Language Models\n.\nSCIENCE CHINA  Information Sciences\nChujie Zheng, Ziqi Wang, Heng Ji, Minlie Huang, Nanyun Peng\nModel Extrapolation Expedites Alignment\n.\nACL 2025\nJunxiao Yang, Zhexin Zhang, Shiyao Cui, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nGuiding not Forcing: Enhancing the Transferability of Jailbreaking Attacks on LLMs via Removing Superfluous Constraints\n.\nACL 2025\nYida Lu, Jiale Cheng, Zhexin Zhang, Shiyao Cui, Cunxiang Wang, Xiaotao Gu, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nLongSafety: Evaluating Long-Context Safety of Large Language Models\n.\nACL 2025\nJinfeng Zhou, Yuxuan Chen, Yihan Shi, Xuanming Zhang, Leqi Lei, Yi Feng, Zexuan Xiong, Miao Yan, Xunzhi Wang, Yaru Cao, Jianing Yin, Shuai Wang, Quanyu Dai, Zhenhua Dong, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nSocialEval: Evaluating Social Intelligence of Large Language Models\n.\nACL 2025\nBosi Wen, Pei Ke, Yufei Sun, Cunxiang Wang, Xiaotao Gu, Jinfeng Zhou, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nHPSS: Heuristic Prompting Strategy Search for LLM Evaluator\n.\nFindings of ACL 2025\nTianshu Yu, Chao Xiang, mingchuan yang, Pei Ke, Bosi Wen, Cunxiang Wang, Jiale Cheng, Li Zhang, Xinyu Mu, Chuxiong Sun, Minlie Huang\nTraining Language Model to Critique for Better Refinement\n.\nFindings of ACL 2025\nGuanqun Bi, Zhuang Chen, Zhoufu Liu, Hongkai Wang, Xiyao Xiao, Yuqiang Xie, Wen Zhang, Yongkang Huang, Yuxuan Chen, Libiao Peng, Minlie Huang\nMAGI: Multi-Agent Guided Interview for Psychiatric Assessment\n.\nFindings of ACL 2025\nJiale Cheng, Ruiliang Lyu, Xiaotao Gu, Xiao Liu, Jiazheng Xu, Yida Lu, Jiayan Teng, Zhuoyi Yang, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nVPO: Aligning Text-to-Video Generation Models with Prompt Optimization\n.\nICCV 2025\nRenmiao Chen, Shiyao Cui, Xuancheng Huang, Chengwei Pan, Xijie Huang, Qinglin Zhang, Xuan Ouyang, Zhexin Zhang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nJPS: Jailbreak Multimodal Large Language Models with Collaborative Visual Perturbation and Textual Steering\n.\nACM Multimedia 2025\nShiyao Cui*, Qinglin Zhang*, Xuan Ouyang, Renmiao Chen, Zhexin Zhang, Yida Lu, Hongning Wang, Han Qiu, Minlie Huang\nShieldVLM: Safeguarding the Multimodal lmplicit Toxicity via Deliberative Reasoning with LVLMs\n.\nACM Multimedia 2025\nJinfeng Zhou, Yuxuan Chen, Jianing Yin, Yongkang Huang, Yihan Shi, Xikun Zhang, Libiao Peng, Rongsheng Zhang, Tangjie Lv, Zhipeng Hu, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nCrisp: Cognitive Restructuring of Negative Thoughts through Multi-turn Supportive Dialogues\n.\nEMNLP 2025\nYi Feng, Jiaqi Wang, Wenxuan Zhang, Zhuang Chen, Shen Yutong, Xiyao Xiao, Minlie Huang, Liping Jing, Jian Yu（with Prof. Liping Jing）\nReframe Your Life Story: Interactive Narrative Therapist and Innovative Moment Assessment with Large Language Models\n.\nEMNLP 2025\nChujie Zheng, Hao Zhou, Fandong Meng, Jie Zhou, Minlie Huang\nLarge Language Models Are Not Robust Multiple Choice Selectors\n.\nICLR 2024（Spotlight）\nYuxian Gu, Li Dong, Furu Wei, Minlie Huang\nMiniLLM: Knowledge Distillation of Large Language Models\n.\nICLR 2024\nHaozhe Ji, Pei Ke, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nLanguage Model Decoding as Direct Metrics Optimization\n.\nICLR 2024\nZhibin Gou*, Zhihong Shao*, Yeyun Gong, yelong shen, Yujiu Yang, Minlie Huang, Nan Duan, Weizhu Chen\nToRA: A Tool-Integrated Reasoning Agent for Mathematical Problem Solving\n.\nICLR 2024\nJian Guan, Jesse Dodge, David Wadden, Minlie Huang, Hao Peng\nLanguage Models Hallucinate, but May Excel at Fact Verification\n.\nNAACL 2024\nZhuang Chen, Jiawen Deng, Jinfeng Zhou, Jincenzi Wu, Tieyun Qian, Minlie Huang\nDepression Detection in Clinical Interviews with LLM-Empowered Structural Element Graph\n.\nNAACL 2024\nHaozhe Ji, Cheng Lu, Yilin Niu, Pei Ke, Hongning Wang, Jun Zhu, Jie Tang, Minlie Huang\nTowards Efficient Exact Optimization of Language Model Alignment\n.\nICML 2024\nChujie Zheng, Fan Yin, Hao Zhou, Fandong Meng, Jie Zhou, Kai-Wei Chang, Minlie Huang, Nanyun Peng\nOn Prompt-Driven Safeguarding for Large Language Models\n.\nICML 2024\nJiale Cheng, Xiao Liu, Kehan Zheng, Pei Ke, Hongning Wang, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang, Minlie Huang\nBlack-Box Prompt Optimization: Aligning Large Language Models without Model Training\n.\nACL 2024\nPei Ke, Bosi Wen, Zhuoer Feng, Xiao Liu, Xuanyu Lei, Jiale Cheng, Shengyuan Wang, Aohan Zeng, Yuxiao Dong, Hongning Wang, Jie Tang, Minlie Huang\nCritiqueLLM: Towards an Informative Critique Generation Model f...[truncated]"
  },
  "serper::Zhengxiong Luo": {
    "homepage": "https://fouzhe.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "fouzhe15@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/fouzhe",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhengxiong-luo-801306313/",
    "homepage_text": "Zhengxiong Luo\nZhengxiong Luo\nAbout\nI'm a research fellow at National University of Singapore (NUS), hosted by\nProf Abhik Roychoudhury\n. Before that, I\treceived my doctoral degree from Tsinghua University, advised by\nProf Yu Jiang\n, and BS degree from Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications (BUPT).\nResearch\nMy research focuses on ensuring the security and privacy of real-world systems (e.g., network protocols, IoT platforms) through program analysis, software testing, and reverse engineering techniques. Currently, I am exploring how LLMs can revolutionize these methods with superior reasoning capabilities and cross-domain scalability.\nSelected Publications\n[Full List]\n[S&P'26]\nAgentic Concolic Execution.\n[paper]\n[code]\nZhengxiong Luo\n, Huan Zhao, Dylan Wolff, Cristian Cadar, Abhik Roychoudhury.\nAccepted in\nIEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy (S&P) 2026.\n[TSE'25]\nEnhancing Protocol Fuzzing via Diverse Seed Corpus Generation.\n[paper]\nZhengxiong Luo\n, Qingpeng Du, Yujue Wang, Abhik Roychoudhury, Yu Jiang.\nAccepted in\nIEEE Transactions on Software Engineering (TSE) 2025.\n[NDSS'24]\nDynPRE: Protocol Reverse Engineering via Dynamic Inference.\n[paper]\n[slides]\nZhengxiong Luo\n, Kai Liang, Yanyang Zhao, Feifan Wu, Junze Yu, Heyuan Shi, and Yu Jiang.\nAccepted in\nNetwork and Distributed System Security (NDSS) 2024.\n[EMSOFT/TCAD'24]\nParallel Fuzzing of IoT Messaging Protocols through Collaborative Packet Generation.\n[paper]\nZhengxiong Luo\n, Junze Yu, Qingpeng Du, Yanyang Zhao, Feifan Wu, Heyuan Shi, Wanli Chang, Yu Jiang.\nAccepted in\nInternational Conference on Embedded Software (EMSOFT) 2024\n, and published in\nIEEE Trans. Comput. Aided Des. Integr. Circuits Syst (TCAD).\n[SEC'23]\nBleem: Packet Sequence Oriented Fuzzing for Protocol Implementations.\n[paper]\n[slides]\nZhengxiong Luo\n, Junze Yu, Feilong Zuo, Jianzhong Liu, Yu Jiang, Ting Chen, Abhik Roychoudhury, and Jiaguang Sun.\nAccepted in\nUSENIX Security Symposium 2023.\n[DAC'20]\nICS Protocol Fuzzing: Coverage Guided Packet Crack and Generation.\n[paper]\n[slides]\nZhengxiong Luo\n, Feilong Zuo, Yuheng Shen, Xun Jiao, Wanli Chang, and Yu Jiang.\nAccepted in\nDesign Automation Conference (DAC) 2020.\n[EMSOFT/TECS'19]\nPolar: Function Code Aware Fuzz Testing of ICS Protocol.\n[paper]\n[slides]\n[code]\nZhengxiong Luo\n, Feilong Zuo, Yu Jiang, Jian Gao, Xun Jiao, and Jiaguang Sun.\nAccepted in\nInternational Conference on Embedded Software (EMSOFT) 2019\n(\nBest Paper Nominee\n), and published in\nACM Trans. Embed. Comput. Syst. (TECS).\nSelected Awards\nACM SIGBED-SIGSOFT Frank Anger Memorial Award, 2024\nACM China Doctoral Dissertation Award Nomination, 2024 (Top 5 in China)\nACM SIGBED China Doctoral Dissertation Award, 2024\nCCF Embedded System Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award, 2024\nEMSOFT Best Paper Nominee, 2022 (3 out of 171 submissions)\nBest Paper Nominee in EMSOFT 2019 (3 out of 105 submissions)\nTsinghua Software Scholarship, 2021\nNational Scholarship, 2020\nSilver Medal, The ACM-ICPC Asia Regional Contest Nanning Site, 2017\nAcademic Services\nProgram Committee Member for ISSTA'26, ICST'26\nExecutive Committee Member for CCF Embedded Systems (CCF TCEBS)\nProgram Committee Member for FUZZING'25, ISSTA'25 Tool, Eurosys'25 Shadow\nReviewer for ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology (TOSEM), 2024-2026\nReviewer for IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security (TIFS), 2025\nReviewer for ACM Computing Surveys, 2023-2024\nReviewer for IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (TDSC), 2023\nProfile\nZhengxiong Luo (罗正雄)\nResearch Fellow @ NUS\nNews\n[12/2025]\nInvited to serve as the PC member for\nICST'26\n. Please consider submitting your work.\n[11/2025]\nTransRE got accepted by FSE'26.\n[09/2025]\nInvited to serve as the PC member for\nISSTA'26\n. Please consider submitting your work.\n[09/2025]\nConcoLLMic got accepted by SP'26.\n[08/2025]\nPSG got accepted by TSE'25.\n[12/2024]\nHonored with ACM  China Doctoral Dissertation Award Nomination (Top 5 in China).\n[08/2024]\nHonored with CCF Embedded System Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award.\n[08/2024]\nHonored with ACM SIGBED China Doctoral Dissertation Award.\n[07/2024]\nMPFuzz got accepted by EMSOFT'24.\n[07/2024]\nLogos got accepted by ISSTA'24.\n[05/2024]\nHonored with ACM SIGBED-SIGSOFT Frank Anger Memorial Award.\n[02/2024]\nSPFuzz got accepted by DAC'24.\nContact\nfouzhe15 at gmail dot com\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nTwitter"
