    "homepage_text": "Songzhu's Academic Site\nSearch\nSongzhu Zheng\nPhD Student of Statistics\nStony Brook University\nBiography\nI’m a statistics PhD student at Stony Brook University. My research focus on robust machine learning methods against label noise or data posioning attack. I’m also interested\nin the application of machine leanring method to solve financial problem.\nDownload my\nresumé\n.\nInterests\nArtificial Intelligence\nMachine Learning\nStatistical Inference\nEducation\nPhD in Statistics, 2022 (expected)\nStony Brook University\nMA in Statistics, 2017\nRice University\nBS in Statistics, 2015\nCommunication University of China\nPublications\nQuickly discover relevant content by\nfiltering publications\n.\nSongzhu Zheng\n,\nYikai Zhang\n,\nHubert Wagner\n,\nMayank Goswami\n,\nChao Chen\n(2021).\nTopological Detection of Trojaned Neural Networks\n.\nNeurIPS.\nPDF\nYikai Zhang+\n,\nSongzhu Zheng+\n,\nPengxiang Wu+\n,\nMayank Goswami\n,\nChao Chen\n(2021).\n(Spotlight, +equalcontribution) Learning with Feature Dependent Label Noise: a Progressive Approach\n.\nICLR.\nPDF\nCode\nPengxiang Wu+\n,\nSongzhu Zheng+\n,\nMayank Goswami\n,\nDimitris Metaxas\n,\nChao Chen\n(2020).\n(+equal contribution) A Topological Filter for Learning with Label Noise\n.\nNeurIPS.\nPDF\nCode\nSongzhu Zheng\n,\nPengxiang Wu\n,\nAman Goswami\n,\nMayank Goswami\n,\nDimitris Metaxas\n,\nChao Chen\n(2020).\nError-Bounded Correction of Noisy Labels\n.\nICML.\nPDF\nCode\nSlides\nExperiences\nAI Researcher Intern\nMorgan Stanley\nJun 2021 –\nAug 2021\nNYC\nResponsibilities include:\nDesign DNN that identifies learnable data out of majority noisy dataset\nConstruct optimal MBS products with maximized market value with RL\nProjects\n*\nAll\nMachine Learning\nOther\nExploring the Relationship Between Cancer and Unhealthy Habits\nInvestigate the top risk factors that correlate with cancer cases using demographic data\nSongzhu Zheng\nSlides\nForecasting the Volatility of Stock Market with Bayes Stochastic Volatility Model\nGarch model in Bayes frame work - an application of PyMc package\nSongzhu Zheng\nPDF\nGrammatical Facial Expression Recognition\nRecognize the grammical facial expression using machine learning\nSongzhu Zheng\nCode\nSlides\nRecent Posts\nBuild a R Package with Rcpp in 30 minutes\nRcpp is package with which you could write c++ code within R. You could simply write a inline C++ code in R like this: library(Rcpp) # Define a Rcpp function add_vec <- Rcpp::cppFunction( 'Rcpp::NumericVector add_vec( Rcpp::NumericVector a, Rcpp::NumericVector b){ return a+b; }' ) # See the result t(add_vec(c(1,2,3), c(2,3,4))) Or you could save your .\nSongzhu Zheng\nLast updated on\nJan 15, 2021\n4 min read\nTool\nContact\nName\nEmail\nMessage\nDo not fill this field unless you are a bot:\nSend\nimzszhahahaha@gmail.com\nDM Me\nMessage Me\nEmail Me\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
