    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yi-wu-a15951193",
    "homepage_text": "Yi Wu's Homepage\nYi Wu | 武艺\nAssistant Professor @University of Oklahoma\nPh.D. @University of Tennessee, Knoxville\nGreetings! Welcome to my homepage. I am an Assistant Professor in the\nComputer Science\ndepartment at University of Oklahoma.\n      Previously, I was a Postdoctoral Researcher in the\nCenter of Data Science\nat Emory University, working with\nDr. Xiao Hu\n. \n      I completed my Ph.D. at\nMin H. Kao Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science\nat University of Tennessee, Knoxville, under supervison of\nDr. Jian Liu\n.\nMy research interests encompass the areas of\nmobile sensing & computing\n,\nhuman-computer interaction\n, and\ncybersecurity & privacy\n. Particularly, I utilize machine learning and signal processing techniques to create next-generation applications for human-computer interaction, smart health monitoring, and identifying potential security/privacy issues on IoT devices.\n      My research work has been published at top-tier mobile-computing/security/HCI venues, including S&P/Oakland, ACM CCS, ACM MobiCom, ACM UbiComp, and ACSAC.\nI will not be recruiting new Ph.D. students for Fall 2026. Thank you for your understanding.\nRecent News\n[Sep. 2025] One paper accepted to\nTS4H NeurIPS 2025 (Workshop)\n.\n[July 2025] One article published at\nSIAM News\n.\n[July 2025] One paper accepted to\nRaid 2025\n.\n[June 2025] One paper accepted to\nUbiComp / ISWC 2025\n.\n[May 2025] Invited to deliever a talk on security & privacy issues in VR and wireless charging at University of Oklahoma (\nCybersecurity Essential Training Workshop\n).\n[Apr. 2025] Invited to serve as a panelist for an NSF review panel.\n[Mar. 2025] Invited to serve on the TPC for\nACSAC 2025\n.\n[Mar. 2025] Invited to serve on the TPC for\nIEEE COMPSAC 2025\n.\n[Oct. 2024] Invited to deliever a talk on sensing opportunities and security issues in VR/AR at University of North Texas (\nData Science Talk Series\n).\n[Oct. 2024] One paper accepted to\nIEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing (TMC).\n[July 2024] Successfully defended my Ph.D. dissertation!\n[July 2023] I will join\nTruveta\nthis fall as a research intern, working on LLM pre-training, LLM fine-tuning, and medical image de-identification.\n[July 2023] One paper accepted to\nUbiComp / ISWC 2023.\n[May 2023] One paper accepted to\nACM DRONET 2023.\n[Mar. 2023] One paper accepted to\nIEEE S&P 2023.\n[Feb. 2023] I will join\nSnap Research\nthis summer as a research intern, working with the\nComputational Imaging\nteam.\n[Apr. 2022]\nBioFace-3D\nhas been selected as the\nSigMobile Research Highlights 2022\n.\n[Aug. 2021] One paper accepted to\nACSAC 2021.\n[Aug. 2021] Two papers accepted to\nACM MobiCom 2021.\nPublications\nConference Papers\n[ACM UbiComp'23]\nSmarCyPad: A Smart Seat Pad for Cycling Fitness Tracking Leveraging Low-cost Conductive Fabric Sensors\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Luis Gonzalez, Zhenning Yang, Gregory Croisdale, Cagadas Karatas, Jian Liu\n[IEEE S&P'23]\nPrivacy Leakage via Unrestricted Motion-Position Sensors in the Age of Virtual Reality: A Study of Snooping Typed Input on Virtual Keyboards\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Cong Shi, Tianfang Zhang, Payton Walker, Jian Liu, Nitesh Saxena, Yingying Chen\n[ACM DRONET'23]\nDroneChase: A Mobile and Automated Cross-Modality System for Continuous Drone Tracking\n[PDF]\nNeel R Vora,\nYi Wu\n, Jian Liu, Phuc Nguyen\n[ACSAC'21]\nTime to Rethink the Design of Qi Standard? Security and Privacy Vulnerability Analysis of Qi Wireless Charging\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Zhuohang Li, Nicholas Van Nostrand, Jian Liu\n[ACM MobiCom'21]\nBioFace-3D: Continuous 3D Facial Reconstruction Through Lightweight Single-ear Biosensors\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Vimal Kakaraparthi, Zhuohang Li, Tien Pham, Jian Liu, Phuc Nguyen\n[Project Website]\n[SIGMOBILE Research Highlight]\n[ACM MobiCom'21]\nFace-Mic: Inferring Live Speech and Speaker Identity via Subtle Facial Dynamics Captured by AR/VR Motion Sensors\n[PDF]\nCong Shi, Xiangyu Xu, Tianfang Zhang, Payton R. Walker,\nYi Wu\n, Jian Liu, Nitesh Saxena, Yingying Chen, Jiadi Yu\n[AsiaCCS'21]\nHVAC: Evading Classifier-based Defenses in Hidden Voice Attacks\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Xiangyu Xu, Payton R. Walker, Jian Liu, Nitesh Saxena, Yingying Chen, Jiadi Yu\n[ACM CCS'20]\nAdvPulse: Universal, Synchronization-free, and Targeted Audio Adversarial Attacks via Subsecond Perturbations\n[PDF]\nZhuohang Li,\nYi Wu\n, Jian Liu, Yingying Chen, Bo Yuan\n[IEEE DySPAN'19]\nSemi-black-box Attacks Against Speech Recognition Systems Using Adversarial Samples\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Jian Liu, Yingying Chen, Jerry Cheng\nJournal Papers & Magazine Articles\n[IEEE TMC'24]\n3D Facial Tracking and User Authentication through Lightweight Single-ear Biosensors\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Xiande Zhang, Tianhao Wu,Bing Zhou, Phuc Nguyen, Jian Liu\n[ACM GetMobile'22]\nBioFace-3D: 3D Facial Tracking and Animation via Single-ear Wearable Biosensors\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Vimal Kakaraparthi, Zhuohang Li, Tien Pham, Jian Liu, Phuc Nguyen\nPosters\n[ACM SenSys'20]\nPoster Abstract: Security and Privacy in the Age of Cordless Power World\n[PDF]\nYi Wu\n, Zhuohang Li, Nicholas Van Nostrand, Jian Liu\nTeaching\nTeaching Assistant, The University of Tennessee, Knoxville\nCOSC 356 Computer Architecture (Fall 2019, Spring 2020)\nCOSC 361 Operating Systems (Fall 2020, Fall 2021, Fall 2022, Spring 2023)\nECE 315 Signals and Systems I (Spring 2022)\nECE 469/569 Mobile/Embedded System Security (Spring 2021, Fall 2021)\nGrader, Rutgers University\nECE 501 System Analysis (Spring 2019)\nAwards\nOutstanding Graduate Research Assistant of UTK,\n2023\nS&P Student Travel Award,\n2023\nACM SigMobile Research Highlight,\n2022\nACSAC Student Conference Grant,\n2021\nCCS Student Conference Grant,\n2021\nDySPAN Student Travel Award,\n2019\nMerit Scholarship of UESTC,\n2015\nServices\nTechnical Program Committee\nIEEE COMPSAC 2023\nReviewer\nThe Proceedings of the ACM on Interactive, Mobile, Wearable and\n      Ubiquitous Technologies (IMWUT)\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\nIEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Systems & Rehabilitation Engineering\nVirtual Reality\nRECENT ADVANCES IN ELECTRICAL & ELECTRONIC ENGINEERING\nMisc.\nI enjoy watching movies & reading detective fictions in my leisure time.\n\"The Pursuit of Happyness\"\n,\n\"Batman: The Dark Knight\"\nand\n\"Tokyo Godfathers\"\nare my favourites.\nI also enjoy swimming & watching NBA games."
  },
