    "homepage_text": "Qiuxia Lai | Communication University of China\nQiuxia Lai\nAssociate Professor\nCommunication University of China\nashleylqx (at) gmail.com\nAbout Me\nI am an associate professor at Communication University of China. I received my Ph.D. degree from the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, the Chinese University of Hong Kong in 2021. Before that, I received the M.S. and B.E. degrees from the School of Automation, Huazhong University of Science and Technology, in 2016 and 2013, respectively. I was an intern at Inception Institute of Artificial Intelligence, UAE from Jun. 2019 to Dec. 2019.\nResearch Interests\nComputer Vision:\nimage recognition, attention mechanism\nMachine Learning:\nrepresentation learning, continual learning\nNews\n[Jul. 2025]\nOur papers about image generation and compositional zero-shot learning are accepted to ICCV 2025.\n[Sep. 2024]\nOur paper about continual learning is accepted to NeurIPS 2024.\n[Sep. 2024]\nOur paper about representation learning is accepted to CVIU.\n[Feb. 2024]\nOur paper about remote sensing detection is accepted to CVPR 2024.\nSelected Publications\nICCV\nCycle-Consistent Learning for Joint Layout-to-Image Generation and Object Detection\nXinhao Cai*,\nQiuxia Lai*\n, Gengsheng Pei, Xiangbo Shu, Yazhou Yao, Wenguan Wang (* Equal contribution)\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision\n(ICCV)\n, 2025.\nPDF\nICCV\nA Conditional Probability Framework for Compositional Zero-shot Learning\nPeng Wu*,\nQiuxia Lai*\n, Hao Fang, Guo-Sen Xie, Yilong Yin, Xiankai Lu, Wenguan Wang (* Equal contribution)\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision\n(ICCV)\n, 2025.\nPDF\nCode\nNeurIPS\nVector Quantization Prompting for Rehearsal-Free Continual Learning\nLi Jiao,\nQiuxia Lai\n, Yu Li, Qiang Xu (\nCorresponding author)\nNeural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n, 2024.\nPDF\nCode\nCVIU\nSpatial Attention for Human-Centric Visual Understanding: An Information Bottleneck Method\nQiuxia Lai\n, Yongwei Nie, Yu Li, Hanqiu Sun, Qiang Xu\nComputer Vision and Image Understanding\n(CVIU)\n, 2024.\nPDF\nCode\nCVPR\nPoly Kernel Inception Network for Remote Sensing Detection\nXinhao Cai*,\nQiuxia Lai*\n, Yuwei Wang*, Wenguan Wang, Zeren Sun, Yazhou Yao (* Equal contribution)\nIEEE / CVF Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference\n(CVPR)\n, 2024.\nPDF\nCode\nTCSVT\nSelf-supervised Video Representation Learning via Capturing Semantic Changes Indicated by Saccades\nQiuxia Lai\n, Ailing Zeng, Ye Wang, Lihong Cao, Yu Li, Qiang Xu\nIEEE Trans. on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\n(IEEE TCSVT)\n, 2023.\nPDF\nCode\nTIP\nWeakly Supervised Visual Saliency Prediction\nQiuxia Lai\n, Tianfei Zhou, Salman Khan, Hanqiu Sun, Jianbing Shen, Ling Shao\nIEEE Trans. on Image Processing\n(IEEE TIP)\n, 2022.\nPDF\nCode\nIJCAI\nInformation Bottleneck Approach to Spatial Attention Learning\nQiuxia Lai\n, Yu Li, Ailing Zeng, Minhao Liu, Hanqiu Sun, Qiang Xu\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(IJCAI)\n, 2021.\nPDF\nCode\nTPAMI\nSalient object detection in the deep learning era: An in-depth survey\nWenguan Wang,\nQiuxia Lai\n, Huazhu Fu, Jianbing Shen, Haibin Ling, Ruigang Yang\nIEEE Trans. on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(IEEE TPAMI)\n, 2021.\nPDF\nCode\nTMM\nUnderstanding more about human and machine attention in deep neural networks\nQiuxia Lai\n, Salman Khan, Yongwei Nie, Hanqiu Sun, Jianbing Shen, Ling Shao\nIEEE Trans. on Multimedia\n(IEEE TMM)\n, 2020.\nPDF\nPR\nVideo super-resolution via pre-frame constrained and deep-feature enhanced sparse reconstruction\nQiuxia Lai\n, Yongwei Nie, Hanqiu Sun, Qiang Xu, Zhensong Zhang, Mingyu Xiao\nPattern Recognition\n(PR)\n, 2020.\nPDF\nTIP\nVideo saliency prediction using spatiotemporal residual attentive networks\nQiuxia Lai\n, Wenguan Wang, Hanqiu Sun, Jianbing Shen\nIEEE Trans. on Image Processing\n(IEEE TIP)\n, 2019.\nPDF\nCode\nCGI\nTemporal coherent video super-resolution via pre-frame-constrained sparse reconstruction\nQiuxia Lai\n, Yongwei Nie, Zhensong Zhang, Hanqiu Sun\nComputer Graphics International\n(CGI)\n, 2018.\nPDF\nServices\nConference Reviewers\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2023-2025\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) 2024-2025\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) 2024-2025\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) 2024-2025\nAssociation for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI) 2025\nACM International Conference on Multimedia (ACM MM) 2025\nJournal Reviewers\nIEEE Trans. on Image Processing (TIP)\nIEEE Trans. on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)\nIEEE Trans. on Multimedia (TMM)\nIEEE Trans. on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (TCSVT)\nPattern Recognition (PR)\nNeurocomputing"
  },
