    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jianhao(Elliott) Yan - Homepage\nJianhao(Elliott) Yan\nWestlake University\nPhD Student @ Westlake NLP\nHangZhou\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nI am a first-year PhD student at WestlakeNLP, where I am supervised by Professor Yue Zhang. Prior to this, I was a researcher at WeChatAI, Tencent, where I worked with Dr. Fandong Meng.\nI obtained my master’s degree in Computer Science from Tsinghua University, where I was supervised by Professor Jian Li and Professor Ying Liu.\nI obtained my bachelor’s degree from Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications.\nMy research interest includes natural language generations, especially language models and machine translation.\n📝 Publications\nArxiv\nDC-MBR: Distributional Cooling for Minimum Bayesian Risk Decoding\nJianhao Yan\n, Jin Xu, Fandong Meng, Jie Zhou, Yue Zhang\nPaper\nEMNLP 2022\nDigging Errors in NMT: Evaluating and Understanding Model Errors from Partial Hypothesis Space\nJianhao Yan*\n, Chenming Wu*, Fandong Meng, Jie Zhou\nPaper\nCode\nNIPS 2022\nLearning to Break the Loop: Analyzing and Mitigating Repetitions for Neural Text Generation\nJin Xu, Xiaojiang Liu,\nJianhao Yan\n, Deng Cai, Huayang Li, Jian Li\nPaper\nCode\nACL 2021\nSelective Knowledge Distillation for Neural Machine Translation\nFusheng Wang*,\nJianhao Yan*\n, Fandong Meng, Jie Zhou\nPaper\nCode\nEMNLP 2020\nMulti-Unit Transformers for Neural Machine Translation\nJianhao Yan\n, Fandong Meng, Jie Zhou\nPaper\nCode\nWMT 2020 Winner in Zh-En\nWeChat Neural Machine Translation Systems for WMT20\nFandong Meng,\nJianhao Yan\n, Yijin Liu, Yuan Gao, Xianfeng Zeng, Qinsong Zeng, Peng Li, Ming Chen, Jie Zhou, Sifan Liu, Hao Zhou\nPaper\nEMNLP 2020 Findings\nA Sentiment-Controllable Topic-to-Essay Generator with Topic Knowledge Graph\nLin Qiao,\nJianhao Yan\n, Fandong Meng, Zhendong Yang, Jie Zhou\nPaper\nNAACL 2019\nRelation Extraction with Temporal Reasoning based on Memory Augmented Distant Supervision\nJianhao Yan\n, Lin He, Ruqin Huang, Jian Li, Ying Liu\nPaper\nCode\n📖 Educations\n2022.08 - 2026.08 (now)\n, PhD, Westlake University(西湖大学), Hangzhou, China\n2016.09 - 2019.06\n, Master, Tsinghua University(清华大学), Beijing, China\n2011.09 - 2015.06\n, Undergraduate, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications(北京邮电大学), Beijing, China\n💻 Work Experience\n2019.07 - 2022.08\n, Researcher, Wechat AI, China."
  },
  "serper::D. Jiang": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/site/danlingjiang",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/SBU-BBL",
    "linkedin": "http://www.linkedin.com/in/danling-jiang",
    "homepage_text": "Danling Jiang's Homepagege\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nDanling Jiang's Homepagege\nHome\nDr. Danling Jiang: Professor of Finance\nDanling Jiang is a Professor of Finance and the Associate Dean for Programs at the College of Business, Stony Brook University, where she previously served as the Associate Dean of Research and Faculty Development. She co-directs the Center of Entrepreneurial Finance and the Blockchain Business Lab in the College. Her research involves studying investments and asset pricing, blockchain and cryptos, corporate and household finance from behavioral and social finance approaches, and her work has been published in leading journals like\nJournal of Financial Economics\n,\nReview of Financial Studies\n,\nManagement Science\n,\nOrganizational Behavior and Human Decision Processes\n,\nJournal of Financial and Quantitative Analysis\n,\nReview of Finance, Review of Asset Pricing Studies\n,\nReview of Accounting Studies,\namong others.\nShe has served as a reviewer for more than 60 journals, publishers, and funding agencies and in different roles for many conferences and associations. She received a Ph.D. in finance and an M.A. in Economics from the Ohio State University.\nCollege of Business\n,\nStony Brook University\n| Profile\nat\nSBU\nHomepage at\nLinkedin\n|\nHomepages at\nSSRN\n|\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nOrcid ID\n: 0000-0001-5104-6023 |\nResearcherID\n: K-4424-2013 |\nWeb of Science\n(\nClarivate\n)  |\nScopus Author ID\n: 23094381000 |\nElsevier Pure\n(SBU)\nResearchGate/Publon\n|\nMendeley\n|\nKudos\n|\nAcademia\n|\nRePEC\nYouTube Channel\n|\n🙂\nAbout me\n🎓\nProfessor\nof Finance and Associate Dean for Programs\n📊\nResearcher\nof financial markets and market participants by integrating\npsychology, sociology, political science, and more\n🖊️\nWriter\nof academic papers on stock and blockchain investments & managerial, analyst, and household financial decision making\n🔗\nMentor\nof\nstudents across all disciplines in the Blockchain Business Lab and Center of Entrepreneurial Finance to inspire the next generations of investment\ngurus\nand blockchain natives\n🙋‍♀️\nSupporter\nof women academics via founding the Friends of Women in Finance in Greater New York Network\n(FWFS-GNY)\nwith like-minded\n🗽\nAdvocat\ne\nof\nfinancial and blockchain literacy\nto help achieve financial resilience and independence through lifelong learning: f\nree newsletter and research resources at\nStonyFinLab\n🥪\nMember\nof Board and Investment Committee to enhance student campus life experiences via\nASA\n🌳\nCFO\nand Board member to help build a\nstronger Asian-American entrepreneur network\nvia\nAAEA\nResearch\nPrograms:\nBlockchain Business Lab\n:\nR\nesearch blockchain and AI business applications\nas well as\nstock\nand\ncrypto investing\nVertically Integrated Projects Program\n- \"\nBlockchain, Crypto, and Web3 in Business and Finance\n\"\nBBL:\nLinked\nI\nn\n,\nGitbook\n,\nGithub\n,\nDiscord\nDatabases:\nCoinMarketCap\n(\nAPI\n),\nGlassnode\n,\nHugging Face\nCenter of Entrepreneurial Finance\n:\nResearch and practice platform for entrepreneurship and entrepreneurial financing.\nClick here to donate to the Center of Entrepreneurial Finance\nStony Finance Lab\n:  Community-based network to promote financial intelligence and financial freedom through lifelong learning\nStony Finance Lab YouTube Channel\n|\nStony Finance Lab Free Newsletter\n|\nInvestment Briefcase Podcast\nE-mail: Danling.Jiang @ stonybrook.edu | Google Phone: (631) 403-2268\nHomepage:\nhttps://tinyurl.com/drjiang  (\nhttps://sites.google.com/site/danlingjiang/\n)\nAddress:\nCollege of Business\nStony Brook University\n30\n1\nHarriman Hall\nStony Brook, NY 11794-3775\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::H. Feng": {
    "homepage": "https://i.astro.tsinghua.edu.cn/~hfeng/",
    "emails": [
      "hfeng@tsinghua.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Hua Feng's Home Page\nHua Feng\nProfessor of Astrophysics\nTsinghua University\n[Chinese]\nHome\nResume\nTeaching\nResearch\nContact\nHua Feng\nProfessor of Astrophysics\nTsinghua University\n[Chinese]\nHome\nResume\nTeaching\nResearch\nContact\nGreat things are accomplished only by the perfection of minor details\nHua Feng conducts research in high energy astrophysics, focusing on observational X-ray astronomy and instrumentation for future space astronomy. He leads a group at Tsinghua University devoted to the study of high-sensitivity X-ray polarimetry, a new and promising window in X-ray astronomy. In October 2018, he led the launch of PolarLight, which is a novel X-ray polarimeter based on the electron tracking technique onboard a CubeSat. PolarLight is expected to re-detect the polarization from the Crab nebula and pulsar, and re-open the field that has been closed for more than 40 years. He is also interested in X-ray and optical observations of accreting compact objects, trying to reveal observational signatures associated with supercritical accretion. In recent years, he has been trying to understand the outflow driven by supercritical accretion.\nEducation and Employment\nSince Apr 2019, Professor, Department of Astronomy, Tsinghua University (adjunct professor in Engineering Physics)\nDec 2012 - Apr 2019, Professor, Department of Engineering Physics & Center for Astrophysics, Tsinghua University\nNov 2008 - Dec 2012, Associate Professor, Department of Engineering Physics & Center for Astrophysics, Tsinghua University\nFeb 2008 - Oct 2008, Assistant Research Scientist, Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of Iowa\nJan 2005 - Jan 2008, Postdoctoral Research Scholar, Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of Iowa\nSep 2001 - Dec 2004, Ph.D., Department of Engineering Physics & Center for Astrophysics, Tsinghua University\nSep 1997 - Jul 2001, B.E., Department of Engineering Physics, Tsinghua University\nTeaching\nSpring 2023, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2022, Introduction to Astrophysics (undergraduate)\nSpring 2022, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2021, Introduction to Astrophysics (undergraduate)\nSpring 2021, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2020, Introduction to Astrophysics (undergraduate)\nSpring 2020, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2019, Introduction to Astrophysics (undergraduate)\nSpring 2019, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2018, Introduction to Astrophysics (undergraduate)\nSpring 2018, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2017, Introduction to Astrophysics (undergraduate)\nFall 2016, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2016, Introduction to Astrophysics (undergraduate)\nFall 2015, Introduction to Astrophysics (undergraduate)\nSpring 2015, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2013, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2012, General Physics: Mechanics and Heat (undergraduate)\nFall 2012, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2011, General Physics: Mechanics and Heat (undergraduate)\nFall 2011, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2010, General Physics: Mechanics and Heat (undergraduate)\nFall 2010, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nFall 2009, High Energy Astrophysics (graduate)\nResearch\nProjects\nMASS: a future Compton telescope for nuclear astrophysics based on CZT detectors\nPolarLight: an X-ray polarimeter on a CubeSat\neXTP: a future X-ray observatory for timing and polarimetry [\nrefs\n]\nGRID: A student project to monitor the gamma-ray sky for multi-messenger astronomy [\nref\n]\nSupercritical accretion and outflows\nChandra Archival Survey of Nearby Galaxies\nPress\nPolarLight reopens the window of soft X-ray polarimetry:\nTsinghua news\n,\nCGTN\nTwo mid-sized black holes in M82:\nChandra press release\n,\nChandra Photo Album\n,\nHEASARC picture of the week\n,\nEurekAlert\nX-ray triple rings around the M87 jets:\nChandra photo album\n,\nNASA press release\n,\nHEASARC picture of the week\nPublications\nLink\nto Feng's publications on NASA/ADS\nContact\nOffice:\nS-619\nMongManWei Building for Science and Technology\n, Tsinghua University\nPhone:\n(8610) 62792153\nEmail:\nhfeng [at] tsinghua.edu.cn\nLast update on 2021.05.27"
  },
