  "serper::Susung Hong": {
    "homepage": "https://susunghong.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "susung@cs.washington.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/SusungHong",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/susung-hong-1600bb253",
    "homepage_text": "Susung Hong\nSusung\nHong\nWelcome to my website! I am a Ph.D. student in\nGRAIL\nat the\nUniversity of Washington\n, co-advised by\nSteve Seitz\n,\nBrian Curless\n, and\nIra Kemelmacher-Shlizerman\n. My research interests lie in the foundations of generative AI, and its applications to producing immersive video/3D content.\nI love cats, coffee (especially lattes), video games, cooking, and playing baseball. I enjoy learning new things beyond my research area.\nIf you are interested in collaboration or would like to learn more about my research, please connect:\nnews\nFeb 27, 2026\nI will be joining\nGoogle\nas a PhD Student Researcher starting in March.\nFeb 20, 2026\nMusicInfuser\nhas been accepted to\nCVPR 2026\n.\nFeb 26, 2025\nOur two papers,\nPerturb-and-Revise\nand\nSpatiotemporal Skip Guidance (STG)\nhave been accepted to\nCVPR 2025\n.\nSep 25, 2024\nOur two papers,\nSmoothed Energy Guidance (SEG)\nand\nEffective Rank Regularizaiton for 3DGS\nhave been accepted to\nNeurIPS 2024\n.\nselected publications\nPreprint\nCOMIC: Agentic Sketch Comedy Generation\nSusung Hong\n, Brian Curless, Ira Kemelmacher-Shlizerman, and Steve Seitz\nPreprint\n, 2026\narXiv\nWebsite\nCVPR\nMusicInfuser: Making Video Diffusion Listen and Dance\nSusung Hong\n, Ira Kemelmacher-Shlizerman, Brian Curless, and Steven M Seitz\nCVPR\n, 2026\narXiv\nWebsite\nCVPR\nPerturb-and-Revise: Flexible 3D Editing with Generative Trajectories\nSusung Hong\n, Johanna Karras, Ricardo Martin-Brualla, and Ira Kemelmacher-Shlizerman\nCVPR\n, 2025\narXiv\nWebsite\nCVPR\nSpatiotemporal Skip Guidance for Enhanced Video Diffusion Sampling\nJunha Hyung\n*\n, Kinam Kim\n*\n,\nSusung Hong\n, Min-Jung Kim, and Jaegul Choo\nCVPR\n, 2025\narXiv\nWebsite\nNeurIPS\nSmoothed Energy Guidance: Guiding Diffusion Models with Reduced Energy Curvature of Attention\nSusung Hong\nNeurIPS\n, 2024\narXiv\nWebsite\nICCV\nImproving Sample Quality of Diffusion Models Using Self-Attention Guidance\nSusung Hong\n, Gyuseong Lee, Wooseok Jang, and Seungryong Kim\nICCV\n, 2023\narXiv\nWebsite"
  },
  "serper::Xipeng Qiu": {
    "homepage": "https://xpqiu.github.io/en.html",
    "emails": [
      "xpqiu@fudan.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/xpqiu",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "﻿\nXipeng Qiu\nXipeng Qiu\nProfessor, School of Computer Science, Fudan University\nHome\n|\nStudents\n|\nSelected Publications\n|\n中文\nLink\nEmail\nGithub\nWeibo\nZhihu\nContact\nBuilding 2X, No. 2005 Songhu Road,Shanghai, China\nAbout Me\nXipeng Qiu is a professor at the School of Computer Science, Fudan University. He received his B.S. and Ph.D. degrees from Fudan University. His research interests include natural language processing and deep learning. He has published more than 60 top journal/conference papers (e.g., TACL, TKDE, T-ALS, ACL, EMNLP, IJCAI, AAAI, ICCV). \n\t\t\t\t\t\tHe also leads the development of [\nGitHub\n] \t[\nGoogle Code\n] and\nFastNLP\n[\nGitHub\n].\nAwards\nYoung Talent Program of China Association for Science and Technology, 2015\nAdversarial Multi-Criteria Learning for Chinese Word Segmentation\n, ACL 2017 Outstanding Paper Award\nHow to Fine-Tune BERT for Text Classification?\n, CCL 2019 Best Paper Award\nAminer \"Most Influential Scholar Award Honorable Mention\", 2020\nProfessional Activity\nPC/SPC\nACL (2014, 2015,2016,2017,2018,2019), EMNLP (2012, 2013, 2014,2015,2017,2020)\nAAAI (2019,2020), IJCAI (2015,2016,2018,2019,2020)\nArea Chair\nACL (2020), EMNLP (2019), AACL (2020)\nCCL (2018,2019), CCKS (2016,2017), NLPCC-ICCPOL (2016)\nPC Chair\nIALP (2019)\nCourses\nCompilers\n, for UG students\nNeural Networks and Deep Learning\n, for PG students\nText Management and Analysis\n, for UG students"
  },
