    "homepage_text": "Connor Lin\nSearch\nConnor Lin\nResearch Scientist\nLuma Labs\nI am a research scientist at\nLuma Labs\n. Previously, I was the co-founder and CTO of\nApparate Labs\n. My research explores generative AI, human avatars, and 3D neural representations for reconstruction, generation, and editing.\nI received my PhD in computer science from Stanford University, co-advised by\nLeonidas Guibas\nand\nGordon Wetzstein\n. During my PhD, I interned at\nGoogle Research\n,\nNVIDIA Research\n, and\nAdobe Research\n.\nPreviously, I worked at Google as a software engineer on Portrait Mode. I was also a Computer Science undergraduate and graduate student at Carnegie Mellon University, advised by\nKeenan Crane\n.\nOutside of work, I enjoy\ncooking\n, badminton, swimming, boardgames, and\nmusic\n(long-time swiftie). Also a fan of traveling and sports – go Ravens!\nInterests\nComputer Vision\nComputer Graphics\nGenerative AI\nGeometry Processing\nEducation\nPhD in Computer Science, 2020-2024\nStanford University\nMSc in Computer Science, 2018-2019\nCarnegie Mellon University\nBSc in Computer Science, 2015-2018\nCarnegie Mellon University\nPublications\nGazeFusion: Saliency-guided Image Generation\n.\nACM SAP 2024 (Best Paper Award) |\nPaper Link\nYunxiang Zhang, Nan Wu,\nConnor Z. Lin\n, Gordon Wetzstein, Qi Sun\nSingle-Shot Implicit Morphable Faces with Consistent Texture Parameterization\n.\nSIGGRAPH 2023 |\nPaper Link\nConnor Z. Lin\n, Koki Nagano, Jan Kautz, Eric R. Chan, Umar Iqbal, Leonidas Guibas, Gordon Wetzstein, Sameh Khamis\nNeuForm: Adaptive Overfitting for Neural Shape Editing\n.\nNeurIPS 2022 (Oral) |\nPaper Link\nConnor Z. Lin\n, Niloy J. Mitra, Gordon Wetzstein, Leonidas Guibas, Paul Guerrero\n3D GAN Inversion for Controllable Portrait Image Animation\n.\nECCV 2022 (\nLearn3DG Workshop\n) |\nPaper Link\nConnor Z. Lin\n*, David B. Lindell*, Eric R. Chan, Gordon Wetzstein\nEG3D: Efficient Geometry-aware 3D Generative Adversarial Networks\n.\nCVPR 2022 (Oral) |\nPaper Link\nEric R. Chan*,\nConnor Z. Lin\n*, Matthew A. Chan*, Koki Nagano*, Boxiao Pan, Shalini De Mello, Orazio Gallo, Leonidas Guibas, Jonathan Tremblay, Sameh Khamis, Tero Karras, Gordon Wetzstein\nACORN: Adaptive Coordinate Networks for Neural Scene Representation\n.\nSIGGRAPH 2021 |\nPaper Link\nJulien N. P. Martel*, David B. Lindell*,\nConnor Z. Lin\n, Eric R. Chan, Marco Monteiro, Gordon Wetzstein\nExperience\nResearch Scientist\nLuma Labs\nSep 2024 –\n              \n                Present\nPalo Alto, CA\nCo-founder and CTO\nApparate Labs\nJan 2024 –\n              \n                Sep 2024\nPalo Alto, CA\nReal-time visual embodiment with generative humans\nPhD Candidate\nStanford University\nSep 2020 –\n              \n                Jan 2024\nPalo Alto, CA\nResearch Internships\nSummer 2023 – Google Research (Perception)\nSummer 2022 – NVIDIA Research (Toronto Lab)\nSummer 2021 – Adobe Research (London Lab)\nTeaching Assistant\nCS248B (Computer Graphics)\nCS221 (Artificial Intelligence)\nSoftware Engineer\nGoogle\nSep 2019 –\n              \n                Sep 2020\nMountain View, CA\nPortrait mode development on the Android Camera Algorithms Team\nSoftware Engineer Intern\nGoogle\nMay 2018 –\n              \n                Aug 2018\nNew York, NY\nHandwriting in AR/VR on the Google Daydream team\nSoftware Engineer Intern\nYahoo!\nMay 2017 –\n              \n                Aug 2017\nSunnyvale, CA\nTeaching Assistant\nCarnegie Mellon University\nJan 2017 –\n              \n                May 2019\nPittsburgh, PA\nComputer Graphics\nSpring 2019\nFall 2018\nFall 2017\nPrinciples of Imperative Computation\nSpring 2017\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
