    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/mingzhang-yin",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Mingzhang Yin\nmingzhang.yin@warrington.ufl.edu\nHome\nI am an assistant professor in the\nMarketing Department\nof the Warrington College of Business, the University of Florida.  I’m also an affiliate assistant professor in the\nDepartment of Statistics\n,  and an affiliated member in the UF\nArtificial Intelligence Academic Initiative\n.\nPreviously, I was a postdoctoral scholar at the Data Science Institute, Columbia University, working with\nProf. David M. Blei\nand\nProf. Simon Tavaré\n. I received my Ph.D. in Statistics from the University of Texas at Austin, supervised by\nProf. Mingyuan Zhou\n.  Before coming to UT, I spent four years as an undergraduate at the math department of  Fudan University, Shanghai.\nMy research focuses on the intersection of Bayesian statistics, machine learning, causal inference, and quantitative marketing. The topics I am interested in include\nProbabilistic machine learning\n: deep generative model, meta-learning, conformal prediction, factor model\nBayesian inference and modeling\n: variational inference, uncertainty estimation, discrete latent variable models\nCausal inference\n: heterogeneous treatment effects, sensitivity analysis, quasi-experiments, fairness\nQuantitative marketing\n: targeting, online advertising, unstructured data analysis"
  },
