    "homepage_text": "Di Chen's Personal Website\nHome\nDi Chen\nI'm a Ph.D. in Computer Science with a focus on AI and Machine Learning. Currently, I hold the position of Director of Research and Engineering at Deep Reasoning AI Inc.\nHere is my\nCV\n.\nRead More\nAbout Me\nI earned my Ph.D. in Computer Science from Cornell University under the mentorship of Professor\nCarla P. Gomes\n. My research expertise lies in the realms of artificial intelligence and machine learning, with a particular emphasis on integrating prior knowledge-based logical and constraint reasoning with advanced deep learning techniques. My work encompasses solving complex problems in structured prediction, multi-entity modeling, covariate shift, and task-based learning.\nPost-graduation, I joined Deep Reasoning AI Inc., where I served as the Director of Research and Engineering and led Deep Reasoning AI’s research and development of AI for Rapid Personalized\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t3D Anatomical Modeling.\nApart from my professional pursuits, I am a big fan in competitive programming, and our team was the champion in\nACM-ICPC\nGreat New York Regional and proceeded to compete in the 42nd ACM-ICPC World Finals. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tMy foundational education in this field was at the Zhiyuan College of Shanghai Jiaotong University, China, where I graduated with a B.Sc. in 2017 from the\nACM honored Class\n.\nRead More\nHonors and Awards\nVerSe20 Large Scale Vertebrae Segmentation Challenge hosted by MICCAI 2020\n●\nBest\nmean-performance and overall\nrank 2\nout of 26 teams, 2020\nACM International Collegiate Programming Contest\n● 56th out of 140 teams in the 42nd ACM-ICPC World Finals in Beijing, China, 2018\n● Champion in New York, GNYR Regional, 2017\n● Gold Medal in Taiwan, Asia Regional, 2014\n● Silver Medal in Xi'an, Asia Regional ,2014\nZhiyuan Outstanding Student Scholarship, 2017\nKoGuan Scholarship, 2014\nAcademic Excellence Scholarship, 2014\nNational Olympiad in Informatics, China\n● Silver Medal (National), 2012\n● Gold Medal (Province), 2011 & 2012\nRead More\nPublications & Patents\nTask-oriented machine learning and a configurable tool thereof on a computing environment\nYada Zhu,\nDi Chen\n, Xiaodong Cui, Upendra Chitnis, Kumar Bhaskaran, Wei Zhang. Patent number 11586919. 2023\nDeep learning with citizen science data enables estimation of species diversity and composition at continental extents\nCourtney L. Davis, Yiwei Bai,\nDi Chen\n, Orin Robinson, Viviana Ruiz-Gutierrez, Carla P. Gomes, Daniel Fink. Ecology. 2023\nCost-Efficient Reinforcement Learning for Optimal Trade Execution on Dynamic Market Environment\nDi Chen\n, Yada Zhu, Miao Liu, Jianbo Li. ICAIF. 2022\nMaterials structure-property factorization for identification of synergistic phase interactions in complex solar fuels photoanodes\nDan Guevarra, Lan Zhou, Matthias H. Richter, Aniketa Shinde,\nDi Chen\n, Carla P. Gomes, John M. Gregoire. npj. Computational Materials. 2022.\nMonitoring Vegetation from Space at Extremely Fine Resolutions via Coarsely-Supervised Smooth U-Net\nJoshua Fan,\nDi Chen\n, Jiaming Wen, Ying Sun, Carla Gomes. IJCAI. 2022.\nSuper Fine-Resolution SIF via Coarsely-Supervised UNet Regression\nJoshua Fan,\nDi Chen\n, Jiaming Wen, Ying Sun, Carla Gomes. Tackling Climate Change with Machine Learning workshop at NeurIPS. 2021.\nVerSe: A Vertebrae labelling and segmentation benchmark for multi-detector CT images\nAnjany Sekuboyina, ...,\nDi Chen\n, Yiwei Bai, Brandon H Rapazzo, et al. Medical Image Analysis 2021.\nCLR-DRNets: curriculum learning with restarts to1solve visual combinatorial games\nYiwei Bai,\nDi Chen\n, Carla P. Gomes. CP 2021.\nAutomating Crystal-Structure Phase Mapping by Combining Deep Learning with Constraint Reasoning\nDi Chen\n, Yiwei Bai, Sebastian Ament, Wenting Zhao, Dan Guevarra, Lan Zhou, Bart Selman, R.Bruce van Dover, John M. Gregoire, Carla P. Gomes. Nature Machine Intelligence 2021.\nTask-Based Learning via Task-Oriented Prediction Network with Applications in Finance\nDi Chen\n, Yada Zhu, Xiaodong Cui, Carla Gomes. IJCAI2020.\nDeep Hurdle Networks for Zero-Inflated Multi-Target Regression: Application to Multiple Species Abundance Estimation\nShufeng Kong, Junwen Bai, Jae Hee Lee,\nDi Chen\n, Andrew Allyn, Michelle Stuart, Malin Pinsky, Katherine Mills, Carla Gomes. IJCAI2020.\nDeep Reasoning Networks for Unsupervised Pattern De-mixing with Constraint Reasoning\nDi Chen\n, Yiwei Bai, Wenting Zhao, Sebastian Ament, John M. Gregoire, Carla Gomes. ICML2020.\nBias Reduction via End-to-End Shift Learning: Application to Citizen Science\nDi Chen\n, Carla Gomes. AAAI\n(Oral)\n2019.\nAutomatic Detection and Compression for Passive Acoustic Monitoring of the\r\n                        African Elephant\nJohan Bjrck, Brendan Rappazzo,\nDi Chen\n, Richard Bernstein, Peter Wrege, Carla Gomes. AAAI 2019.\nConvolutional Neural Network-Based Intention Forecasting and Lane Change Path Predicting of the human driver\nKaiming Yang, Zhanhong Yan,\nDi Chen\n, Xuewu Ji, Kimihiko Nakano. ASME 2019.\nEnd-to-End Learning for the Deep Multivariate Probit Model\nDi Chen\n, Yexiang Xue, Carla Gomes. ICML\n(Oral)\n, 2018.\nMulti-Entity Dependence Learning with Rich Context via Conditional Variational\r\n                        Auto-encoder\nLuming Tang, Yexiang Xue,\nDi Chen\n, Carla Gomes. AAAI, 2018.\nPiecewise Affine-Based Shared Steering Torque Control Scheme for Cooperative Path-Tracking: A Game-Theoretic Approach\nKaiming Yang, Xiangkun He, Yulong Liu, Xuewu Ji,\nDi Chen\n. SAE Technical Paper, 2018.\nDeep Multi-Species Embedding\nDi Chen\n, Yexiang Xue, Daniel Fink, Shuo Chen, Carla Gomes. IJCAI\n(Oral)\n, 2017.\nRead More\nContact\ndi [AT] deepreasoningai [DOT] com    chendi9412 [AT] gmail [DOT] com\nSeattle, WA 98109 USA"
