    "homepage_text": "Lingda Leonard Wang\nLingda Wang\nECE Ph.D. at UIUC\nFollow\nUrbana, IL, USA\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nNice to e-meet you! I am Lingda (Leonard) Wang (王凌达), an ECE Ph.D. at\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\n, advised by\nProf. Zhizhen Jane Zhao\n. I also closely work with my friends\nBingcong Li\nand\nHuozhi Zhou\n.\nMy current research focuses on:\nMachine/Deep Learning\n: Large scale time series forecasting for demand prediction and inventory planning; Spatio-temporal sequence forecasting for climate and precipitation prediction; Multi-armed (contextual) bandits with its applications for recommendation systems and social networks; Graph neural nets\nOptimization\n: Acceleration for convex optimization; Stochastic optimization for large-scale optimization problems\nSignal Processing/Data Analysis\n: Community detection; Phase synchronization; Spectral methods; Computational imaging\nNews\nDec 2023\nDefensed!\nMay 2023\nStart a summer intern at Amazon SCOT forecasting as an Applied Scientist.\nMar 2023\nOne paper about joint community detection and phase synchronization is accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Signal and Information Processing over Networks\n.\nMay-Aug 2022\nInternship at Amazon as an Applied Scientist.\nJan 2022\nOne paper is accepted by\nICASSP’22\n, which was the probabilistic time serires forecasting project during my internship at Amazon.\nJan 2022\nPass my preliminary exam!"
  },
