    "homepage_text": "Tianjian Meng - The University of Texas at Austin\nTianjian Meng\n(Tien-Chien Meng 孟天健)\n2317 Speedway, Austin, TX 78712\n(412) 888-9277\nmengtianjian@utexas.edu\nI'm currently a PhD student at UT Austin, advised by\nProf. Philipp Krähenbühl\n. I was a Software Engineer at Google Cloud, working closely with\nDr. Mingxing Tan\n,\nDr. Yin Cui\n,\nDr. Quoc Le\nand\nProf. Ming-Hsuan Yang\n. I received my Bachelor of Science in Computer Science from\nUniversity of Pittsburgh\nsumma cum laude. I'm lucky to have worked with\nProf. Zhangyang (Atlas) Wang\nat UT Austin and\nProf. Xiaolong Wang\nat\nCarnegie Mellon University\n.\nGitHub\n/\nLinkedIn\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nCV\nPublications\nDeepFusion: Lidar-Camera Deep Fusion for Multi-Modal 3D Object Detection\nYingwei Li*, Adams Wei Yu*,\nTianjian Meng\n, Ben Caine, Jiquan Ngiam, Daiyi Peng, Junyang Shen, Bo Wu, Yifeng Lu, Denny Zhou, Quoc V. Le, Alan Yuille, Mingxing tan\nIn\nThe IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(CVPR).\nTowards the Co-design of Neural Networks and Accelerators\nYanqi Zhou, Xuanyi Dong,\nTianjian Meng\n, Mingxing Tan, Berkin Akin, Daiyi Peng, Amir Yazdanbakhsh, Da Huang, Ravi Narayanaswami, James Laudon\nIn\nFifth Conference on Machine Learning and Systems\n(MLSys).\nSpatiotemporal Contrastive Video Representation Learning\nRui Qian*,\nTianjian Meng*\n, Boqing Gong, Ming-Hsuan Yang, Huisheng Wang, Serge Belongie, Yin Cui\nIn\nThe IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(CVPR), June 2021.\nA Design Space Study for LISTA and Beyond\nTianjian Meng*\n, Xiaohan Chen*, Yifan Jiang, Zhangyang Wang\nIn\nThe 9th International Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR), May 2021.\nGo Wide, Then Narrow: Efficient Training of Deep Thin Networks\nDenny Zhou, Mao Ye, Chen Chen*,\nTianjian Meng*\n, Mingxing Tan*, Xiaodan Song, Quoc Le, Qiang Liu, Dale Schuurmans\nIn\nThe 37th International Conference on Machine Learning\n(ICML), July 2020.\nSSN: Learning Sparse Switchable Normalization via SparsestMax\nWenqi Shao*,\nTianjian Meng*\n, Jingyu Li, Ruimao Zhang, Yudian Li, Xiaogang Wang, Ping Luo\nIn\nThe IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(CVPR), June 2019.\nResearch Experiences\nThe University of Texas at Austin\nAug 2021 - Present\nPhD Student\nAdvisor:\nProf. Philipp Krähenbühl\nGoogle Research\nSep 2019 - Aug 2021\nSoftware Engineer\nBrain Team\nHost:\nDr. Mingxing Tan\n,\nDr. Golnaz Ghiasi\nand\nDr. Quoc Le\nCarnegie Mellon University\nJan 2019 - Jul 2019\nResearch Assistant\nThe Robotics Institute\nCooperator:\nProf. Xiaolong Wang\nEducation\nThe University of Texas at Austin\nAug 2021 - Present\nAustin, TX\nDoctor of Philosophy in Computer Science\nUniversity of Pittsburgh\nAug 2016 - Aug 2019\nPittsburgh, PA\nBachelor of Science in Computer Science (summa cum laude)\nCarnegie Mellon University\nMay 2017 - May 2018\nPittsburgh, PA\nVisiting/Non-Degree Student\nBeijing Jiaotong University\nSep 2014 - Jun 2016\nBeijing, China\nBachelor of Engineering, Discontinued (Transferred out)"
