    "homepage_text": "Yining Wang's homepage\nEducation\nExperiences\nPublications\nYining Wang\nAssociate professor\nOperations Management Area\n,\nNaveen Jindal School of Management\n,\nUniversity of Texas at Dallas\nRichardson, TX, USA\nEmail: ynwang dot yining at gmail dot com or\nyining dot wang at utdallas dot edu\nOffice: JSOM Building Room 4.810\nI am an associate professor of operations management at the\nNaveen Jindal School of Management\nof\nUnversity of Texas at Dallas\n.\nBefore joining UTD, I am an assistant professor of information systems and operations management at the\nWarrington College of Business\nof\nUniversity of Florida\n.\nI obtained my PhD in\nMachine Learning\nat\nCarnegie Mellon University\n,\nadvised by\nAarti Singh\n.\nBefore coming to CMU, I was an undergraduate student at the\nYao Class\nin\nTsinghua University\n.\nI am generally interested in machine learning and its applications in revenue management and information systems research.\nMy main research focus is on the development and analysis of sequential decision making methods under uncertainty,\nwith emphasis to revenue management applications such as assortment optimization and dynamic pricing.\nMy research is also connected with bandit online learning and reinforcement learning in machine learning research.\nDownload CV\nEmployments\nUniversity of Texas at Dallas\nNaveen Jindal School of Management\nAssociate Professor (with tenure) of Operations Management\nAssociate Professor of Operations Management\n, until 2024\nSince 2022\nUniversity of Florida\nWarrington College of Business\nAssistant Professor of Information Systems and Operations Management\n2019 - 2022\nEducation\nCarnegie Mellon University\nPhD in Machine Learning, School of Computer Science\nAdvisor:\nAarti Singh\n2014 - 2019\nTsinghua University\nB. Eng. in Computer Science\nUndergraduate thesis: Spectral Methods in Supervised Topic Modeling\nThesis advisor:\nJun Zhu\n2010 - 2014\nPapers\nFull list of publications available\nhere\n."
  },
  "serper::Hao Lu": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/site/poppinace/",
    "emails": [
      "hlu@hust.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/poppinace",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Hao Lu's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nHao Lu's Homepage\nHao Lu  陆 昊\nPh.D., Associate Professor\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence and Automation\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nWuhan 430074, China\nE-mail:     hlu@hust.edu.cn\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nAbout Me\nI am currently Associate Professor with\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology.\nI was Senior Research Associate with School of Computer Science, The University of Adelaide, under the supervision of Prof.\nChunhua Shen\n. I received my Ph.D. degree from the School of Artificial Intelligence and Automation, Huazhong University of Science and Technology, China, supervised by Prof.\nZhiguo Cao\n.\nMy research interests include computer vision and machine learning. I am currently working on visual dense prediction problems, a broad range of tasks that deal with per-pixel labeling such as image matting, object counting, semantic segmentation, object detection, and depth estimation. I am particularly interested in developing simple yet effective solutions to problems in reality from deep, novel insights.\nNews\n21 Feb 2026: One paper accepted to CVPR26!\n10 Dec 2024: One paper accepted to AAAI25!\n15 Jul 2024: One paper accepted to IJCV!\n1 Jul 2024: One paper accepted to ECCV 2024!\n27 Feb 2024: Two papers on image matting accepted to\nCVPR 2024\n!\n14 Jul 2023: Four papers accepted to\nICCV 2023\n!\n13 Jun 2023: I have accepted the invitation being Associate Editor of\nPlant Phenomics\n!\n5 Jun 2023: One paper on how to manage uncertainty for barycentric coorespondence\ncoordinates accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n!\n17 May 2023: One paper on geometric-invarriant coordinate representations for feature correspondence accepted to\nIJCV\n!\n13 Mar 2023: One paper on object counting accepted to\nIJCV\n!\n19 Nov 2022: Three papers on deep matting, correspondence pruning, and aesthesic image cropping accepted to\nAAAI 2023\n!\n15 Sep 2022: One paper on general-purpose feature upsampling accepted to\nNeurIPS 2022\n!\n3 Jul 2022: Four papers accepted to\nECCV 2022\n!\n30 Jun 2022: Two papers accepted to\nMM 2022\n!\n2 Mar 2022: Two papers accepted to\nCVPR 2022\n!\n23 Jul 2021: One paper accepted to\nICCV2021\n!\n2 Mar 2021: Two papers accepted to\nCVPR 2021\n!\n9 Feb 2021: One paper on plant counting accepted to\nIEEE TGRS\n!\n23 Jan 2021: One paper on simultaneous crowd counting and localization accepted to\nIEEE TIP\n!\n5 Nov 2020: I am joining in Huazhong University of Science and Technology as an Associate Professor!\n3 Jul 2020: One paper on object counting with reinforcement learning accepted to\nECCV 2020\n! Code is released!\n8 Jun 2020: One paper on generic upsampling operators accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n!\n23 Jul 2019: Two papers accepted to\nICCV 2019\n! One is about image matting, and the other is about object counting.\n17 Jul 2018: Our paper ‘In-field automatic observation of wheat heading stage using computer vision’ won the EurAgEng Outstanding Paper Award 2018!\n17 May 2018: I passed my PhD thesis defense!\n19 Mar 2018: One paper on visual domain adaptation accepted to\nIEEE TIP\n!\n28 Feb 2018: One paper on monocular depth estimation accepted to\nCVPR 2018\n!\n17 Jul 2017: One paper on tensor domain adaptation accepted to\nICCV 2017\n!\nEducation\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology, China                                          Sep. 2013 - Jun. 2018\nPh.D. in Control Science and Engineering\nRecipient of the Graduate National Scholarship\nThe University of Adelaide, Australia Centre for Visual Technologies                      Aug. 2016 - Sep. 2017\nVisiting Student, Co-supervised by Prof.\nChunhua Shen\nChina University of Geosciences (Wuhan), China                                                      Sep. 2009 - Jun. 2013\nB.S., Technique and Instrumentation of Measurements\nRecipient of the National Scholarship\nSelected Publications\nMy full publication list can be found\nhere\n. + equal contribution; * corresponding author.\nIndex Networks\nHao Lu\n, Yutong Dai, Chunhua Shen, Songcen Xu\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence, 2022\nPDF\nCode\nFrom Open Set to Closed Set: Supervised Spatial Divide-and-Conquer for Object Counting\nHaipeng Xiong\n+\n,\nHao Lu\n+,\nChengxin Liu\n, Liang Liu, Chunhua Shen,\nZhiguo Cao\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision\n, 202\n3\nPDF\nCode\nSAPA: Similarity-Aware Point Affiliation for Feature Upsampling\nHao Lu\n,\nWenze Liu, Zixuan Ye, Hongtao Fu, Yuliang Liu, Zhiguo Cao\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2022\nPDF\nCode\nFADE: Fusing the Assets of Decoder and Encoder for Task-Agnostic Upsampling\nHao Lu\n, Wenze Liu,\nHongtao Fu\n, Zhiguo Cao\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV)\n, 2022\nPDF\nCode\nLearning Affinity-Aware Upsampling for Deep Image Matting\nYutong Dai+,\nHao Lu\n+\n, Chunhua Shen\nIEEE\n/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 202\n1\nPDF\nCode\nIndices Matter: Learning to Index for Deep Image Matting\nHao Lu\n, Yutong Dai, Chunhua Shen, Songcen Xu\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2019\nPDF\nCode\nCounting Crowd by Weighing Counts：A Sequential Decision-Making Perspective\nHao Lu\n, Liang Liu, Hu Wang,\nZhiguo Cao\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems, 2022\nPDF\nCode\nWeighing Counts: Sequential Crowd Counting by Reinforcement Learning\nLiang Liu+,\nHao Lu\n+\n,\nHongwei Zou, Haipeng Xiong, Zhiguo Cao\n, Chunhua Shen\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2020\nPDF\nCode\nDecoupled Two-Stage Crowd Counting and Beyond\nJian Cheng\n, Haipeng Xiong,\nZhiguo Cao\n,\nHao Lu\n*\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing, 2021\nPDF\nCode\nTasselNetV3: Explainable Plant Counting With Guided Upsampling and Background Suppression\nHao Lu\n, Liang Liu, Ya-Nan Li, Xiao-Ming Zhao, Xi-Qing Wang, Zhi-Guo Cao\nIEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing, 2022\nPDF\nDataset\nNSSNet: Scale-Aware Object Counting With\nNon-Scale Suppression\nLiang Liu,\nZhiguo Cao\n,\nHao Lu\n*\n, Haipeng Xiong,\nChunhua Shen\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems, 2020\nPDF\nCode\nFrom Open Set to Closed Set: Counting Objects by Spatial Divide-and-Conquer\nHaipeng Xiong+,\nHao Lu\n+\n, Chengxin Liu, Liang Liu, Zhiguo Cao, Chunhua Shen\n+ Equal contribution\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2019\nPDF\nCode\nAn Embarrassingly Simple Approach to Visual Domain Adaptation\nHao Lu\n, Chunhua Shen, Zhiguo Cao, Yang Xiao, Anton van den Hengel\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing, 2018\nPDF\nCode\nMonocular Relative Depth Perception with Web Stereo Data Supervision\nKe Xian, Chunhua Shen, Zhiguo Cao,\nHao Lu\n, Yang Xiao, Ruibo Li, Zhenbo Luo\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2018\nPDF\nProject Page\nToward Good Practices for Fine-Grained Maize Cultivar Identification With Filter-Specific Convolutional Activations\nHao Lu\n, Zhiguo Cao, Yang Xiao, Zhiwen Fang, Yanjun Zhu\nIEEE Transactions on Automation Science and Engineering, 2018\nPDF\nProject Page\nWhen Unsupervised Domain Adaptation Meets Tensor Representations\nHao Lu\n+\n,\nLei Zhang+, Zhiguo Cao, Wei Wei, Ke Xian, Chunhua Shen, Anton van den Hengel\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2017\nPDF\nCode\nTwo-dimensional subspace alignment for convolutional activations adaptation\nHao Lu\n, Zhiguo Cao, Yang Xiao, Yanjun Zhu\nPattern Recognition, 2017\nPDF\nProject Page\nTasselNet: counting maize tassels in the wild via local counts regression networks\nHao Lu\n, Zhiguo Cao, Yang Xiao, Bohan Zhuang, Chunhua Shen\nPlant Methods, 2017\nPDF\nDataset\nIn-field automatic observation of wheat heading stage  using computer vision\nYanjun Zhu, Zhiguo Cao,\nHao Lu\n, Yanan Li, Yang Xiao\nBiosystems Engineering, 2016\nEurAgEng Outstanding Paper Award\nPDF\nAcademic Service\nJournal\nEditor\nAssociate Editor of Plant Phenomics Journal\nGuest Editor of Frontiers in Plant Science Journal\nConference\nCommittee\nSenior Program Committee of AAAI 2026\nExecutive Area Chair of VALSE\nArea Chair of PRCV 2023\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\nPattern Recognition\nComputer Vision and Image Understanding\nPlant Phenomics\nComputers and Electronics in Agriculture\nBiosystems Engineering\nGeoscience and Remote Sensing Letters\nEngineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence\n...\nConference Reviewer\nICML 2024\nICLR 2024\nNeurIPS 2023\nICCV 2023\nCVPR 2024, CVPR2023, CVPR2022, CVPR2021, CVPR2020\nECCV 2022, ECCV 2024\nACM MM 2023\nAAAI 2023\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2020\nWACV2021\nACCV2020\nICIP2020, ICIP2019\nICPR2018\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
