    "homepage_text": "Homepage of Shitong Luo\nShitong Luo\nPh.D. Student\nMIT EECS\nluost26(at)gmail.com\nluost(at)mit.edu\nShitong Luo\nI am a second-year Ph.D. student at\nMIT\nEECS\n.\nPreviously, I received my B.S. degree from Peking University in 2021 and worked at a biotech startup from 2021 to 2024.\nluost26(at)gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nAbout Me\nI am a second-year Ph.D. student at\nMIT\nEECS\n.\nPreviously, I received my B.S. degree from Peking University in 2021 and worked at a biotech startup from 2021 to 2024.\nFavorite Publications\n(view all\n)\nEfficient and Programmable Exploration of Synthesizable Chemical Space\nShitong Luo\n,\nConnor W. Coley\nTechnical Report\n2025\nPrexSyn is based on a decoder-only transformer trained on a billion-scale datastream of synthesizable pathways paired with molecular properties, enabled by a real-time, high-throughput C++-based data generation engine. It sets a new state of the art in synthesizable chemical space coverage, molecular sampling efficiency, and inference speed.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Code: Data Engine]\n[Documentation]\nEfficient and Programmable Exploration of Synthesizable Chemical Space\nShitong Luo\n,\nConnor W. Coley\nTechnical Report\n2025\nPrexSyn is based on a decoder-only transformer trained on a billion-scale datastream of synthesizable pathways paired with molecular properties, enabled by a real-time, high-throughput C++-based data generation engine. It sets a new state of the art in synthesizable chemical space coverage, molecular sampling efficiency, and inference speed.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Code: Data Engine]\n[Documentation]\nProjecting Molecules into Synthesizable Chemical Spaces\nShitong Luo\n,\nWenhao Gao\n,\nZuofan Wu\n,\nJian Peng\n,\nConnor W. Coley\n,\nJianzhu Ma\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n2024\nChemProjector \"projects\" any molecular graph into a new molecular representation called\npostfix notation of synthesis\nthat guarantees synthesizability.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\nProjecting Molecules into Synthesizable Chemical Spaces\nShitong Luo\n,\nWenhao Gao\n,\nZuofan Wu\n,\nJian Peng\n,\nConnor W. Coley\n,\nJianzhu Ma\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n2024\nChemProjector \"projects\" any molecular graph into a new molecular representation called\npostfix notation of synthesis\nthat guarantees synthesizability.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\nRotamer Density Estimator is an Unsupervised Learner of the Effect of Mutations on Protein-Protein Interaction\nShitong Luo\n,\nYufeng Su\n,\nZuofan Wu\n,\nChenpeng Su,\nJian Peng\n,\nJianzhu Ma\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2023\nRDE estimates the distribution of amino acid side-chain conformations (rotamers), from which we can predict the effect of mutations on protein-protein interactions by comparing the entropy of the distributions.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[OpenReview]\nRotamer Density Estimator is an Unsupervised Learner of the Effect of Mutations on Protein-Protein Interaction\nShitong Luo\n,\nYufeng Su\n,\nZuofan Wu\n,\nChenpeng Su,\nJian Peng\n,\nJianzhu Ma\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2023\nRDE estimates the distribution of amino acid side-chain conformations (rotamers), from which we can predict the effect of mutations on protein-protein interactions by comparing the entropy of the distributions.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[OpenReview]\nAntigen-Specific Antibody Design and Optimization with Diffusion-Based Generative Models for Protein Structures\nShitong Luo\n,\nYufeng Su\n,\nXingang Peng\n,\nSheng Wang\n,\nJian Peng\n,\nJianzhu Ma\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n2022\nDiffAb is a diffusion model that can design new antibodies and optimize existing ones for antigen binding.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Demo]\nAntigen-Specific Antibody Design and Optimization with Diffusion-Based Generative Models for Protein Structures\nShitong Luo\n,\nYufeng Su\n,\nXingang Peng\n,\nSheng Wang\n,\nJian Peng\n,\nJianzhu Ma\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n2022\nDiffAb is a diffusion model that can design new antibodies and optimize existing ones for antigen binding.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Demo]\nDeep Learning-Guided Optimization of Human Antibody Against SARS-CoV-2 Variants with Broad Neutralization\nSisi Shan*\n,\nShitong Luo*\n,\nZiqing Yang*,\nJunxian Hong*,\nYufeng Su\n,\nFan Ding,\nLili Fu,\nChenyu Li,\nPeng Chen,\nJianzhu Ma\n,\nXuanling Shi,\nQi Zhang,\nBonnie Berger\n,\nLinqi Zhang\n,\nJian Peng\n(*\nequal contribution\n)\nProceedings of the National Academy of Sciences (PNAS)\n2022\nOptimizing antibodies against SARS-CoV-2 variants with geometric deep learning, experimentally validated.\n[Paper]\nDeep Learning-Guided Optimization of Human Antibody Against SARS-CoV-2 Variants with Broad Neutralization\nSisi Shan*\n,\nShitong Luo*\n,\nZiqing Yang*,\nJunxian Hong*,\nYufeng Su\n,\nFan Ding,\nLili Fu,\nChenyu Li,\nPeng Chen,\nJianzhu Ma\n,\nXuanling Shi,\nQi Zhang,\nBonnie Berger\n,\nLinqi Zhang\n,\nJian Peng\n(*\nequal contribution\n)\nProceedings of the National Academy of Sciences (PNAS)\n2022\nOptimizing antibodies against SARS-CoV-2 variants with geometric deep learning, experimentally validated.\n[Paper]\nA 3D Generative Model for Structure-Based Drug Design\nShitong Luo\n,\nJiaqi Guan\n,\nJianzhu Ma\n,\nJian Peng\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n2021\nLearning the distribution of atom occurence in protein binding pockets to generate 3D molecules.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Slides]\n[Publication]\nA 3D Generative Model for Structure-Based Drug Design\nShitong Luo\n,\nJiaqi Guan\n,\nJianzhu Ma\n,\nJian Peng\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n2021\nLearning the distribution of atom occurence in protein binding pockets to generate 3D molecules.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Slides]\n[Publication]\nDiffusion Probabilistic Models for 3D Point Cloud Generation\nShitong Luo\n,\nWei Hu\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n2021\nSimply a diffusion model for 3D point cloud generation.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Suppl.(Corrected)]\n[Demo Created by S.H.]\n[Publication]\nDiffusion Probabilistic Models for 3D Point Cloud Generation\nShitong Luo\n,\nWei Hu\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n2021\nSimply a diffusion model for 3D point cloud generation.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Suppl.(Corrected)]\n[Demo Created by S.H.]\n[Publication]\nAll publications"
