    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yunyang Xiong's Homepage\nYunyang Xiong\nMeta Reality Labs\n1 Hacker Way, Menlo Park, CA 94025\nEmail:\nyunyang [at] fb.com\n[GitHub]\n[Google Scholar]\nI am a senior research scientist at\nFacebook Reality Lab\n. Prior to that, I completed my Ph.D. in the department of\nComputer Sciences\nat University of Wisconsin-Madison under\nVikas Singh\n. \n    Before joining Facebook, I was a research intern at\nGoogle Mobile Vision\nworking on neural architecture search (MobileDets). I also did research internship at\nFacebook AI\nand\nAmazon Lab 126\n.\nMy research interests include natural language modeling, efficient Transformers, and neural architecture search. I am paritcularly interested in efficient AI.\nPublications\nMixture-of-Supernets: Improving Weight-Sharing Supernet Training with Architecture-Routed Mixture-of-Experts\nGanesh Jawahar, Haichuan Yang, Yunyang Xiong, Zechun Liu, Dilin Wang, Fei Sun, Meng Li, Aasish Pappu, Barlas Oguz, Muhammad Abdul-Mageed, Laks VS Lakshmanan, Raghuraman Krishnamoorthi, Vikas Chandra\n[arxiv]\nCastling-ViT: Compressing Self-Attention via Switching Towards Linear-Angular Attention at Vision Transformer Inference\nHaoran You, Yunyang Xiong, Xiaoliang Dai, Bichen Wu, Peizhao Zhang, Haoqi Fan, Peter Vajda, Yingyan Celine Lin\nCVPR 2023.\n[pdf]\nSelf-positioning Point-based Transformer for Point Cloud Understanding\nJinyoung Park, Sanghyeok Lee, Sihyeon Kim, Yunyang Xiong, Hyunwoo J Kim\nCVPR 2023.\n[pdf]\nFast Point Cloud Generation with Straight Flows\nLemeng Wu, Dilin Wang, Chengyue Gong, Xingchao Liu, Yunyang Xiong, Rakesh Ranjan, Raghuraman Krishnamoorthi, Vikas Chandra, Qiang Liu\nCVPR 2023.\n[pdf]\nSagemix: Saliency-guided mixup for point clouds\nSanghyeok Lee, Minkyu Jeon, Injae Kim, Yunyang Xiong, Hyunwoo J Kim\nNeurIPS 2022.\n[pdf]\nYou only sample (almost) once: Linear cost self-attention via bernoulli sampling\nZeng, Zhanpeng, Yunyang Xiong, Sathya Ravi, Shailesh Acharya, Glenn M. Fung, Vikas Singh\nICML 2021.\n[pdf]\nMobileDets: Searching for Object Detection Architectures for Mobile Accelerators\nYunyang Xiong, Hanxiao Liu, Suyog Gupta, Berkin Akin, Gabriel Bender, Yongzhe Wang, Pieter-Jan Kindermans, Mingxing Tan, Vikas Singh, Bo Chen\nCVPR 2021.\n[arxiv]\nNystrÃ¶mformer: A NystrÃ¶mformer-based Algorithm for Approximating Self-Attention\nYunyang Xiong, Zhanpeng Zeng, Rudrasis Chakraborty, Mingxing Tan, Glenn Fung, Yin Li, Vikas Singh\nAAAI 2021.\n[pdf]\nMobileDets: Searching for Object Detection Architectures for Mobile Accelerators\nYunyang Xiong, Hanxiao Liu, Suyog Gupta, Berkin Akin, Gabriel Bender, Yongzhe Wang, Pieter-Jan Kindermans, Mingxing Tan, Vikas Singh, Bo Chen\nNeurIPS 2020, Workshop on MetaLearning.\n[arxiv]\nPerforming Group Difference Testing on Graph Structured Data from GANs: Analysis and Applications in Neuroimaging?\nTuan Quang Dinh, Yunyang Xiong, Zhichun Huang, Tien Vo, Akshay Mishra, Won Hwa Kim, Sathya Ravi, Vikas Singh\nTPAMI 2020.\n[pdf]\nResource Constrained Neural Network Architecture Search: Will a Submodularity Assumption Help?\nYunyang Xiong, Ronak Mehta, Vikas Singh\nICCV 2019.\n[arxiv]\nScaling Recurrent Models via Orthogonal Approximations in Tensor Trains\nRonak Mehta, Rudrasis, Chakraborty, Yunyang Xiong, Vikas Singh\nICCV 2019.\n[pdf]\nMixed Effects Neural Networks (MeNets) with Applications to Gaze Estimation\nYunyang Xiong, Hyunwoo J. Kim, Vikas Singh\nCVPR 2019.\n[pdf]\nANTNets: Mobile Convolutional Neural Networks for Resource Efficient Image Classification\nYunyang Xiong, Hyunwoo J. Kim, Varsha Hedau\nCVPR 2019, ECV Workshop (Oral).\n[arxiv]\nOn Training Deep 3D CNN Models with Dependent Samples in Neuroimaging\nYunyang Xiong, Hyunwoo J. Kim, Bhargav Tangirala, Ronak Mehta, Sterling C. Johnson, Vikas Singh\nIPMI 2019 (Oral).\n[pdf]\nBuilding Bayesian Neural Networks with Blocks: On Structure, Interpretability and Uncertainty\nHao Henry Zhou, Yunyang Xiong, Vikas Singh\n[arxiv]\nFilter Flow made Practical: Massively Parallel and Lock-Free\nSathya N. Ravi, Yunyang Xiong, Lopamudra Mukherjee, Vikas Singh\nCVPR 2017.\n[pdf]"
  },
