    "homepage_text": "Alan J.X. Guo\nAlan J.X.\nGuo\nCenter for Applied Mathematics, Tianjin University\nNo. 92 Weijin Road, Tianjin, 300072.\njiaxiang.guo@tju.edu.cn\nI am an Associate Professor with Center for Applied Mathematics, Tianjin University. \n          At this time, my research fields mainly focus on machine learning and combinatorics.\nExperience\nCenter for Applied Mathematics, Tianjin University\nAssociate Professor\nJuly 2021 - Present\nCenter for Applied Mathematics, Tianjin University\nLecturer\nJuly 2016 - June 2021\nCenter for Combinatorics, Nankai University\nPh.D in applied mathematics\nSeptember 2011 - June 2016\nSchool of mathematics, Jilin University\nB.S. in mathematics and applied mathematics\nSeptember 2007 - June 2011\nPublications\nMachine Learning\nGuo A J X\n, Wei M, Dai Y, Wei Y, Zhang P. Disturbance-based Discretization, Differentiable IDS Channel, and an IDS-Correcting Code for DNA-based Storage, The 40th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI 2026\n).\nCode\n.\nBibTeX\n.\nGuo A J X\n, Sun S, Wei X, Wei M, Chen X. DoDo-Code: an Efficient Levenshtein Distance Embedding-based Code for 4-ary IDS Channel, The Thirty-Ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS 2025\n).\nCode\n.\nBibTeX\n.\nWei X#,\nGuo A J X#*\n, Sun S H, Wei M Y, Yu W. Levenshtein Distance Embedding with Poisson Regression for DNA Storage, The 38th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI 2024\n).\nBibTeX\n.\nGuo A J X\n, Liang C, Hou Q-H. Deep Squared Euclidean Approximation to the Levenshtein Distance for DNA Storage, International Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML 2022\n), PMLR, 2022: 8095-8108.\nPMLR\n.\nCode\n,\nBibTeX\n.\nZhang G, Xu S, Li J,\nGuo A J X*\n. Group-based network pruning via nonlinear relationship between convolution filters, Applied Intelligence, 2022.\ndoi\n.\nGuo A J X\n, Qi H. Using Artificial Neural Networks to Model Errors in Biochemical Manipulation of DNA Molecules, IEEE/ACM Transactions on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics, 2021.\ndoi\n,\nCode\n,\nBibTeX\n.\nGuo A J X\n, Zhu F. Improving Deep Hyperspectral Image Classification Performance with Spectral Unmixing, Signal Processing, 183 (2021): 107949.\narXiv:2004.00583\n,\nCode\n,\nBibTeX\n.\nZhao X, Liang Y,\nGuo A J X*\n, Zhu F. Classification of small-scale hyperspectral images with multi-source deep transfer learning, Remote Sensing Letters, vol. 11, no. 4, pp. 303-312, 2020.\nBibTeX\n.\nLiang Y, Zhao X,\nGuo A J X*\n, Zhu F. Hyperspectral Image Classification with Deep Metric Learning and Conditional Random Field. IEEE Geoscience and Remote Sensing Letters, vol. 17, no. 6, pp. 1042-1046, Jun. 2020.\narXiv:1903.06258\n,\nBibTeX\n.\nGuo A J X\n, Zhu F. A CNN-based Spatial Feature Fusion Algorithm for Hyperspectral Imagery Classification. IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing, vol. 57, no. 9, pp. 7170-7181, Sep. 2019.\narXiv:1801.10355\n,\nCode\n,\nBibTeX\n.\nGuo A J X\n, Zhu F. Spectral-spatial feature extraction and classification by ANN supervised with center loss in hyperspectral imagery[J]. IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing, vol. 57, no. 3, pp. 1755-1767, Mar. 2019.\narXiv:1711.07141\n,\nCode\n,\nBibTeX\n.\nLi M, Zhu F,\nGuo A J X\n, Chen J. A Graph Regularized Multilinear Mixing Model for Nonlinear Hyperspectral Unmixing, Remote Sensing, 11(19),2188, 2019.\nCombinatorics\nFan N J Y,\nGuo A J X\n. On 1234-nesting Kazhdan-Lusztig R-polynomials for the symmetric group.[J]. Communications in Algebra 46.2 (2018): 644-652.\nChen W Y C,\nGuo A J X\n, Guo P L, et al. s-inversion Sequences and P-Partitions of type B[J]. SIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics 30.3 (2016): 1632-1643.\nChen W Y C, Fan N J Y,\nGuo A J X\n, et al. Combinatorial proof of the inversion formula on the Kazhdan-Lusztig R-polynomials[J]. Mathematische Zeitschrift, 2014, 277(3-4): 1017-1025.\nCodes\nIn most cases, the codes will be pushed to Github after the corresponding paper is accepted. \n          Until now, we have the following codes on Github:\nDisturbance-based Discretization, Differentiable IDS Channel, and an IDS-Correcting Code for DNA-based Storage.\nTHEA-Code\n.\nDoDo-Code: an Efficient Levenshtein Distance Embedding-based Code for 4-ary IDS Channel.\nDoDo-Code\n.\nDeep Squared Euclidean Approximation to the Levenshtein Distance for DNA Storage.\nGithub\n.\nUsing Artificial Neural Networks to Model Errors in Biochemical Manipulation of DNA Molecules.\nGithub\n.\nSpectral-spatial feature extraction and classification by ANN supervised with center loss in hyperspectral imagery.\nGithub\n.\nA CNN-based Spatial Feature Fusion Algorithm for Hyperspectral Imagery Classification.\nGithub\n.\nImproving Deep Hyperspectral Image Classification Performance with Spectral Unmixing.\nGithub\n."
  },
