    "homepage_text": "Shuang Liu\n=\nShuang Liu's (刘爽) Homepage\nContact Information\nAddress:\nDepartment of Mathematics\nUniversity of North Texas\n1155 Union Circle #311430\nDenton, TX 76203-5017\nOffice:\nGAB 440H\nE-mail:\nshuang.liu@unt.edu\nCV:\nShuang Liu's CV (updated Janurary 2024)\nI am an assitant profesor in the\nDepartment of Mathematics\nat\nUniversity of North Texas\n. \n  During Janurary 2021 and June 2023, I was a\nSEW Assistant Professor\nin the\nDepartment of Mathematics\nat\nUniversity of California, San Diego\n, working with Prof.\nLi-Tien Cheng\nand Prof.\nBo Li\n. Before that, I was a Postdoc Research Associate in applied mathematics and plasma physics group\nat TDS center\nat\nLos Alamos National Laboratory\nunder the supervison of\nDr. Xianzhu Tang.\nI received my PhD in 2019 from\nDepartment of Mathematics\nfrom University of South Carolina  under Prof.\nXinfeng\nLiu\n.\nEmployment\n08/2023-Now  Assistant Professor, University of North Texas, Denton, TX, USA\n01/2021–06/2023 S.E.W. Visiting Assistant Professor, University of California at San Diego, La Jolla, CA USA.\n01/2020–01/2021 Postdoc Research Associate, Los Alamos National Laboratory, Los Alamos, NM USA.\nEducation\nAug.2015-Dec.2019, Ph.D., University of South Carolina, Columbia, SC USA. (Advisor: Dr.\nXinfeng\nLiu\n).\nSep.2012-July.2015, M.S., Henan Normal University, Xinxiang, Henan, China. (Advisor: Dr. \n                Zongming\nGuo).\nSep.2008-July.2012, B.S., Henan Normal University, Xinxiang, Henan, China.\nSupervison\nMr. Zunding Huang at University of California, San Diego, 2021-2023\nResearch and Publications\nMy research interests are in the area of numerical methods for free boundary problems and mathematics of scientific computing,  with applications in ecology specially in the field of population dynamics, phasma physics, computational biology, and biological physics. \n            Please see\nResearch\nand\nPublications\nfor more details. My research was supported by research fund at UCSD and\nthe AMS-Simons Travel Grants\n.\nHonors and Awards\n07/2021-06/2023 AMS Simons Travel Grant, AMS, USA, $5,000.\nResearch fund of department of mathematics, UCSD, $4,000.\n2019 National Science Foundation(NSF)-Mathematical Sciences Graduate Internship at Los Alamos National Laboratory. 06/10/2019-08/16/2019.\nThe 2019 George W. Johnson Graduate Fellowship.  $3,000.\nVisiting student scholarship (University of New England, Australia).  07/2018\nSAMSI 2017 IMSM Workshop (North Carolina State University).   07/2017\nThe Outstanding First Year Graduate ACM Student Award. (UofSC)  04/2016\nTravel Award by Graduate School of University of South Carolina.  $1,000\nTravel Award by AMS and SIAM.   around $1,500\nSelected Conference and Talks\nJIM Research Team Building Section in JIM MCNATT Institute for Logistics Research at University of North Texas, Denton, TX   November 2023\nMillican Colloquium in Department of Mathematics at University of North Texas, Denton, TX  November 2023\n2023 Fall Southeastern Sectional Meeting at University of South Alabama, Mobile, AL    October 2023\nMathematics in Action (MiA2023): Modeling and Analysis in Biology and Material Sciences    June 2023\nAMS Western Sectional special session on Mathematical Modeling of Biological\n                        and Social Systems   October 2022\nSouthern California Applied Mathematics Symposium (SOCAMS)   May 2022\nPostdoc Seminar at UCSD          April 2022\nApplied Mathematics Seminar at University of Georgia   September 2021\nCenter For Computational Mathematics Seminar at UCSD  May 2021\nApplied and Computational Mathematics Seminar at U of South Carolina March 2021\nPostdoc Seminar at University of California, San Diego           April 2021\nTalk at Daniel Appelö research group at Michigan State University   March 2021\nSeminars on Mathematics for Complex Biological Systems at UCSD   December 2020\nPrincipal Talk at SIAM  Northern State Section Student Chapters Conference at Utah State  University  October 2020\nTalk in  TDS SciDAC Webinar in  Applied Mathematics and Plasma Physics Group at Los Alamos National Laboratory (LANL). August 2019\nJob Talking Presentation at Worcester Polytechnic Institute  October 2019\nTalk in Earth and Environmental Science Group at LANL  August 2019\nNonlinear Evolution Equations & Wave Phenomena at U of Georgia   April 2019\nApplied and Computational Mathematics Seminar (ACM) at U of South Carolina  February 2019\n1st Annual Symposium on Multi-scale Cell Fate at UC, Irvine  October 2018\n42nd SIAM  Conference on Applied Mathematics at UNC at Chapel Hill  March 2018\n9th Annual Graduate Student Mini-conference in Computational Mathematics at U of South Carolina  February 2018"
  },
