    "homepage_text": "Ling Zhou\nLing Zhou\nHome\nResearch\nTalks\nTeaching\nAbout Me\nI am a\nPhillip Griffiths Assistant Research Professor\nat Duke University, mentored by Prof.\nEzra Miller\n.\nI obtained my Ph.D. in the\nDepartment of Mathematics\nat Ohio State University in 2023, under the supervision of Prof.\nFacundo Mémoli\n. In Fall 2023, I was a\nSemester Postdoc\nat the\nInstitute for Computational and Experimental Research in Mathematics\n(ICERM), located at Brown University. My postdoc mentor was Prof.\nVladimir Itskov\n.\nResearch Interests\nAlgebraic topology, metric geometry, and discrete homotopy theory\nApplied topology, topological data analysis, and computational geometry\nApplications in neuroscience, network science, and machine learning\nContact Information\nOffice:\nRoom 208, Physics Building, 120 Science Dr, Durham, NC 27710\nEmail:\nling.zhou@duke.edu\nLinks:\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nCurriculum Vitae\n|\nORCID\nUpcoming Events\n2026/6/2-5:\nCG Week 2026 (SoCG and Workshops)\n, Rutgers University, New Brunswick, NJ\n2026/5/18-21:\nFoundations of Computational Geometry and Topology\n, ICERM\n2026/4/8:\nApplied Topology Seminar (online participation)\n, AATRN\n2026/3/28-29:\nAMS Sectional Meeting\n, Special Session on\nTopological Data Analysis, Theory and Applications\n, Georgia Southern University (Armstrong Campus), Savannah, GA\nPast Events (Selected)\n2026\n2026/3/2-5:\nBuilding-up differential homotopy theory 2026 (online participation)\n, Shinshu University, Japan\n2025\n2025/11/21-24:\nConference on Topological Data Analysis: Recent Developments and Applications\nat University of Missouri\n2025/8/10-15:\nBIRS Workshop\n, Banff (Online participants)\n2025/8/4-8/8:\nBridging Algebraic Combinatorics, Topology and Applications\nat Rutgers\n2025/7/28-8/1:\nCollaborate@ICERM\n, ICERM\n2025/7/21-25:\nMCA 2025\n, Miami\n2025/5/11-16:\nDagstuhl Seminar 25201\nat Schloss Dagstuhl, Germany\n2025/3/6-8:\nSTDC 2025\nat CNU\n2024\n2024/10/19-20:\nAMS Eastern Sectional Meeting\nat UAlbany\n2024/10/11-13:\nAISC conference\nat UNCG\n2024/03/23-24:\nAMS Spring Sectional Meeting\nat Florida State University\n2024/03/11-15:\nTopology Seminar at UCSB\n, Santa Barbara\n2024/02/25-03/01:\nDagstuhl Seminar 24092\nat Schloss Dagstuhl, Germany\n2024/01:\nJMM\n, San Francisco (\nTalk 1\n,\nTalk 2\n)\n2023\n2023/Fall:\nSemester Program\nat ICERM\n2023/07:\nWinCompTop 3, Bernoulli Center\n2023/06:\nAIM workshop\n, San Jose\n2023/06:\nSoCG 2023\n, Dallas\n2023/06:\nGTDAML\n, Boston\n2023/03:\nAMS special session\n, Georgia Tech\n2023/03:\nAIM workshop, San Jose\n2023/01:\nJMM\n, Boston\n2022\n2022/06:\nATMCS\n, Oxford\n2022/06:\nAWM, UMN\n2022/06:\nSoCG 2022\n, Berlin\n2022/05:\nMRC\n, Buffalo"
