    "homepage_text": "Duan, Tiehang -\n\t\t\t\tGVSU College of Computing -\n\t\tGrand Valley State University\nSkip to main content\nGVSU College of Computing\nTiehang Duan, Ph.D.\nAssistant Professor, Department of Computer Science\nEmail:\n[email protected]\nPhone: 616-331-7033\nOffice: DCIH 530F\nEducation\nPh.D. in Computer Science & Engineering, University of Buffalo, 2021\nSemester Schedule\nOther office hours by appointment only.\nDay\nSession Title\nTime\nLocation\nMonday\nTuesday\nWednesday\nOffice Hours\n1:00 p.m. - 3:00 p.m.\nDCIH 530F\nThursday\nFriday\nAdditional Courses\nAsynchronous Courses: AI 201-2\nBiography\nDr. Tiehang Duan is an expert in machine learning, brain-computer interfaces, and medical informatics. His research focuses on decoding brain signals to develop assistive technologies, such as brain-controlled wheelchairs and exoskeletons. He previously worked as a research scientist at Meta AI and held visiting scholar roles at West Virginia University and the Mayo Clinic. His work has been widely published in top-tier journals and conferences, and he is passionate about advancing AI-driven solutions that improve lives and inspire the next generation of innovators.\nOutside of academia, Duan enjoys a variety of sports, including basketball, table tennis, billiards and bowling, and is looking forward to immersing himself into the Greater Grand Rapids tech and research community.\nRecent Publications\nOnline continual decoding of streaming EEG signal with a balanced and informative memory buffer. Tiehang Duan, Zhenyi Wang, Fang Li, Gianfranco Doretto, Donald Adjeroh, Yiyi Yin, Cui Tao. Neural Networks, vol. 176, 2024.\nRetain and Adapt: Online Sequential EEG Classification with Subject Shift. Tiehang Duan, Zhenyi Wang, Li Shen, Gianfranco Doretto, Donald Adjeroh, Fang Li, Cui Tao. IEEE Transactions on Artificial Intelligence, vol. 5, no. 6, 2024.\nTraining A Secure Model against Data-Free Model Extractio. Zhenyi Wang, Li Shen, junfeng guo, Tiehang Duan, Siyu Luan, Tongliang Liu, Mingchen Gao. European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2024.\nRefAI: a GPT-powered retrieval-augmented generative tool for biomedical literature recommendation. Yiming Li et al. Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association, Vol. 31, 2024.\nReplay with Stochastic Neural Transformation for Online Continual EEG Classification\nTiehang Duan, Zhenyi Wang, Gianfranco Doretto, Fang Li, Cui Tao, Donald Adjeroh.\nIEEE International Conference on Bioinformatics and Biomedicine (BIBM), 2023.\nDistributionally Robust Memory Evolution with Generalized Divergence for Continual Learning. Zhenyi Wang, Li Shen, Tiehang Duan, Qiuling Suo, Le Fang, Wei Liu, Mingchen Gao\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence, vol. 45 no. 12, 2023.\nPage last modified January 12, 2026\nReport a problem with this page"
  },
