    "homepage_text": "Yupeng Zhang\nYupeng Zhang\nHome\nPublications\nStudents\nTeaching\nActivities\nYupeng Zhang\nAssistant Professor\nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\nEmail: zhangyp at illinois dot edu\nGoogle Scholar\nCV\nI am an assistant professor at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign, in\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nand\nComputer Science\n(affiliate).\nMy research is in the area of cybersecurity and applied cryptography. Recently, I am working on zero-knowledge proofs, secure multiparty computations and their applications in blockchain and machine learning to enhance privacy, fairness and scalability.\nMy research has been generously supported by the\nNSF CAREER award\n,\nAir Force Research Lab\n,\nDARPA\n,\nFacebook Research Award\nand Google Research Award.\nBefore joining UIUC, I spent 4 great years at the Computer Science and Engineering department of Texas A&M University. I was a postdoctoral researcher at UC Berkeley hosted by\nDawn Song\n. I obtained my PhD from\r\nUniversity of Maryland and my advisors are\nCharalampos Papamanthou\nand\nJonathan Katz\n.\nI co-taught a Massive Open Online Course (MOOC) on Zero-Knowledge Proofs in Spring 2023. Please check\nzk-learning.org\nif you are interested!\nI'm always looking for motivated students, please send me an email with your CV.\nPage generated 2026-01-21 20:02:47 CST, by\njemdoc+MathJax\n."
  },
