    "homepage_text": "Linwei Wang | Computational Biomedicine Laboratory | RIT\nRIT Logo with Text\nComputational Biomedicine Laboratory\nRIT logo and full name\nComputational Biomedicine Laboratory\nLinwei Wang\nLinwei Wang\nBruce B Bates Endowed Professor\nPhD Program of Computing and Information Sciences\nRochester Institute of Technology\nRm 74-1075\nPhone: (585) 475-4238\nEmail:\nlinwei.wang@rit.edu\nThe full curriculum vitae is available\nhere\n.\nEducation\n2007 - 2009\nPhD, Computing and Information Science\nRochester Institute of Technology, Rochester, NY, USA\nDissertation: Personalized Noninvasive Imaging of Volumetric Cardiac Electrophysiology\n2005 - 2007\nMPhil, Electronic and Computer Engineering (GPA: A+ (11.80/12.0))\nHong Kong University of Science and Technology\nThesis: Noninvasive Imaging of 3D Cardiac Electrophysiology\n2001 - 2005\nBE, Optic-Electronic Information Engineering\nZhejiang University, Hangzhou, China\nMajor GPA: 3.90/4.0 (Top 1/158 of 2005 class)\nAdvanced Class of Engineering Education GPA: 3.89/4.0\nTeaching\n2010 - present\nCISC-820: Quantitative Foundations (PhD Core; previously 4040-820)\n2009 - present\nCISC-862: Computational Modeling and Simulation (PhD Elective; previously 4040-849)\n2013-2014\nCSCI-530: Introduction to Computer Graphics (Computer Science Undergraduate)\n2012-2013\n4003-570/4005-761: Computer Graphics I (Computer Science Undergraduate/Graduate)\n2010-2012\n4005-759-01: Topics in Artificial Intelligence (Computer Science Elective)\nOn the Map\nLaboratory for Applied Computing,\nLAC/074\nRm 74 - 1075\nSearch RIT\nClose\nX\nThis website uses cookies to provide better user experience and functionality. You can control and configure cookies in your web browser.\nCookie Statement\n|\nHow to Disable Cookies\nOK"
