    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/soochan-lee-a23b2aa3/",
    "homepage_text": "Soochan Lee\nHi, I'm Soochan.\nI'm a Ph.D. candidate in the Dept. of Computer Science and Engineering, Seoul National University.\nFind Out More\nAbout Me\nI'm a Ph.D. candidate in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering at Seoul National University.\n                    As a member of\nVision & Learning Lab\n, I study machine learning under the supervision of\nProf. Gunhee Kim\n.\nIn the pursuit of artificial general intelligence, I believe that one of the next major challenges is\ncontinual learning\n.\n                    Especially, my recent focus has been on meta-continual learning, also known as learning to continually learn.\n                    In addition, I hold a profound interest in\nlanguage models\nand overcoming their limitations through innovative solutions.\nEducation\nMar. 2013 – Aug. 2017\nSeoul National University\nComputer Science and Engineering\nBachelor of Science\nSep. 2017 – Aug. 2019\nSeoul National University\nComputer Science and Engineering\nVision and Learning Lab\nMaster of Science\nSep. 2019 –\nSeoul National University\nComputer Science and Engineering\nVision and Learning Lab\nPh.D. Candidate\nPublications\nLearning to Continually Learn with the Bayesian Principle\nSoochan Lee\n, Hyeonseong Jeon, Jaehyeon Son, and Gunhee Kim\nICML 2024\nCode\nPaper\nWhen Meta-Learning Meets Online and Continual Learning: A Survey\nJaehyeon Son*,\nSoochan Lee*\n, and Gunhee Kim\narXiv preprint 2023\nPaper\nRecasting Continual Learning as Sequence Modeling\nSoochan Lee\n, Jaehyeon Son, and Gunhee Kim\nNeurIPS 2023\nCode\nPaper\nRecursion of Thought: A Divide and Conquer Approach to Multi-Context Reasoning with Language Models\nSoochan Lee\nand Gunhee Kim\nFindings of ACL 2023\nPoster\nCode\nPaper\nA Neural Dirichlet Process Mixture Model for Task-Free Continual Learning\nSoochan Lee\n, Junsoo Ha, Dongsu Zhang, and Gunhee Kim\nICLR 2020\nCode\nPaper\nHarmonizing Maximum Likelihoods with GANs for Multimodal Conditional Generation\nSoochan Lee\n, Junsoo Ha, and Gunhee Kim\nICLR 2019\nProject\nCode\nPaper\nImproving Occlusion and Hard Negative Handling for Single-Stage Pedestrian Detectors\nJunhyug Noh,\nSoochan Lee\n, Beomsu Kim, and Gunhee Kim\nCVPR 2018\nProject\nPaper\nHonors & Awards\nQualcomm Innovation Fellowship Korea\n2023\nICLR 2021 Outstanding Reviewer\n2021\nQualcomm Innovation Fellowship Korea\n2020\nNeurIPS 2020 Top 10% Reviewer\n2020\nNaver Ph.D. Fellowship\n2019\nSilver Award, 25th Samsung Humantech Paper Award\n2019\nCurriculum Vitae\nDownload\nContact\nHave a question or feedback about my work? That's great!\nSend me an email and I will get back to\n                    you as soon as possible.\nsoochan.lee@vision.snu.ac.kr\nsoochan-lee\nSoochan Lee\n@SoochanL33"
  },
