  "serper::Zhisheng Xiao": {
    "homepage": "https://xavierxiao.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "zxiao@uchicago.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/XavierXiao",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhisheng-xiao-2b9356130",
    "homepage_text": "Zhisheng Xiao\nZhisheng Xiao\nFollow\nBellevue, WA\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nI currently work at Google Deepmind, mainly focusing on improving the efficiency of diffusion models, such as\nImagen 4\n,\nVeo 3\nand\nGemini’s native image generation\n.\nPreviously I was an Applied Scientist at AWS AI. At AWS, I worked on training large diffusion-based generative models, which finally turned into\nTitan Image Generator\n.\nI graduated from University of Chicago with a Ph.D. degree in\nComputational and Applied Mathematics\nin 2022. I did my Ph.D. studies under Prof.\nYali Amit\n. During two wonderful summer internships at\nNVIDIA\n, I worked with\nArash Vahdat\nand\nKarsten Kreis\n. My research mainly focuses on deep probablistic generative models and optimization. Here is a\ncopy\nof my Ph.D. thesis.\nI obtained my bachelor’s degrees in Applied Mathematics and Statistics from UC Berkeley in 2017."
  },
