  "serper::Chi-Guhn Lee": {
    "homepage": "https://cglee.mie.utoronto.ca/",
    "emails": [
      "cglee@mie.utoronto.ca"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Professor Chi-Guhn Lee | Department of Mechanical and Industrial EngineeringProfessor Chi-Guhn Lee\nProfessor Chi-Guhn Lee\nUofT\nEngineering\nMIE\nSearch\nMenu\nSkip to content\nChi-Guhn Lee (이치근), Ph.D.\nProfessor\nChi-Guhn Lee\nis a professor in the Department of Mechanical and Industrial Engineering at the University of Toronto. He received his Ph.D. from the University of Michigan, Ann Arbor and joined the University of Toronto faculty in 2001.\nHis research interests include both the theory and the application of the Markov decision processes. In particular, he is tackling Markov decision processes involving high dimensional state space, multiple agents making decisions, reinforcement learning and deep reinforcement learning. Applications of his interest have been diverse from finance to supply chain management and to revenue management.\nResume\nCV of Chi-Guhn Lee\nContact Information\nEmail:\ncglee@mie.utoronto.ca\nHomepage:\nhttps://cglee.mie.utoronto.ca/\nCampus Phone: (416) 946-7867 (temporarily unavailable)\nFax: (416) 978-7753\nOffice Location: MC322 (Mechanical Building)\nAddress: 5 King’s College Road, Toronto, Ontario  M5S 3G8"
  },
