    "homepage_text": "Hyunwoo Lee\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nHyunwoo Lee\nHyunwoo Lee\n이현우\nhyunwoo(dot)lee(at)kaist(dot)ac(dot)kr\n(Photo by Sang-il Oum)\nHello! I'm a fourth-year (also my final year) graduate student at KAIST, Department of Mathematical Sciences, and a student researcher at IBS ECOPRO.\nMy research interests lie in Extremal Combinatorics.\nMy advisor is Prof.\nJaehoon Kim\n.\nEmail: hyunwoo(dot)lee(at)kaist(dot)ac(dot)kr\nHere is my\nCV\n(Last update:  2026 / February / 07)\nEducation\nIntegrated master’s/doctoral program, Department of Mathematical Sciences, KAIST, 2023-Current\nB.S. in Department of Mathematical Sciences, KAIST, 2019-2023\nSelected Publications\nOn a Ramsey--Turán variant of Roth's theorem\n, 16 pages,\nwith\nMatija Buc\nić\n,\nMicha Christoph\n,\nJaehoon Kim\n,\nand\nVarun Sivashankar\n.\n(\nBLMS\n, accepted\n)\nHamilton cycles in pseudorandom graphs: resilience and approximate decompositions\n, 34 pages,\nwith\nNemanja Dragan\nić\n,\nJaehoon Kim\n,\nDavid Munhá Correia\n,\nMatías Pavez-Signé\n, and\nBenny Sudakov\n.\nRandom matchings in linear hypergraphs\n, 15 pages.\n(\nForum of Mathematics, Sigma\n, accepted\n)\nOn rainbow Turan densities of trees\n,\nwith\nSeonghyuk Im\n,\nJaehoon Kim\n, and\nHaesong Seo\n.\n(\nRSA\n)\nTowards a high-dimensional Dirac's theorem\n.\n(\nS\nIDMA\n)\nHamilton transversals in tournaments\n,\nwith\nDebsoumya Chakraborti\n,\nJaehoon Kim\n, and\nJaehyeon Seo\n.\n(\nCombinatorica\n)\nOn perfect subdivision tilings\n.\n(\nCPC\n)\nMilitary Service\nTechnical Research Personnel\n, KAIST, South Korea, 202\n5 March - 2028 Feb (Expected)\nRestrictions during my military duty:\n(1) Only 90 days are allowed to stay outside of Korea.\n(Current remaining days:\n53\ndays)\n(2) I should work as a PostDoc in Korea for 1 year after I get my phD.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
