    "homepage_text": "Xuanchi's Homepage\nSearch\nXuanchi Ren\nStudent\nUniversity of Toronto\nBiography\nI am a PhD student at University of Toronto. I am also a research scientist at\nNVIDIA\n. My supervisor is Prof.\nSanja Fidler\n. During my undergraduate years at HKUST, I was supervised by Prof.\nQifeng Chen\nand I was fortunate to work with Dr.\nLi Erran Li\n, Prof.\nAlexandre Alahi\n@EPFL, Dr.\nYuwang Wang\n@MSRA and Prof.\nXiaolong Wang\n@UCSD.\nMy research interests are in computer vision, particularly generative modeling and 3D vision.\nInterests\nComputer Vision\nDeep Learning\nEducation\nPhD student in Computer Science, 2022-Now\nUniversity of Toronto\nExchange student, 2020 Spring\nEPFL\nBSc in Compter Science and Math, 2017-2022\nHKUST\nFeatured Publications\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nYifan Lu*\n,\nTianshi Cao*\n,\nRuiyuan Gao*\n,\nShengyu Huang\n,\nAmirmojtaba Sabour\n,\nTianchang Shen\n,\nTobias Pfaff\n,\nJay Zhangjie Wu\n,\nRunjian Chen\n,\nSeung Wook Kim\n,\nJun Gao\n,\nLaura Leal-Taixe\n,\nMike Chen\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nHuan Ling\nJune 2025\nWhite Paper\nCosmos-Drive-Dreams: Scalable Synthetic Driving Data Generation with World Foundation Models\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nTianchang Shen*\n,\nJiahui Huang\n,\nHuan Ling\n,\nYifan Lu\n,\nMerlin Nimier-David\n,\nThomas Müller\n,\nAlexander Keller\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nJun Gao\nMarch 2025\nCVPR 2025 Highlight (3% acceptance rate)\nGEN3C: 3D-Informed World-Consistent Video Generation with Precise Camera Control\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nNVIDIA\nMarch 2025\nWhite Paper (Core Contributor; Featured in Jensen Huang's GTC 2025 keynote)\nCosmos-Transfer1: Conditional World Generation with Adaptive Multimodal Control\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nJiahui Huang\n,\nXiaohui Zeng\n,\nKen Museth\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nFrancis Williams\nNovember 2023\nCVPR 2024 Highlight (2.8% acceptance rate)\nXCube: Large-Scale 3D Generative Modeling using Sparse Voxel Hierarchies\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nXiaolong Wang\nMarch 2022\nCVPR 2022\nLook Outside the Room: Synthesizing A Consistent Long-Term 3D Scene Video from A Single Image\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nPublications\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nYifan Lu*\n,\nTianshi Cao*\n,\nRuiyuan Gao*\n,\nShengyu Huang\n,\nAmirmojtaba Sabour\n,\nTianchang Shen\n,\nTobias Pfaff\n,\nJay Zhangjie Wu\n,\nRunjian Chen\n,\nSeung Wook Kim\n,\nJun Gao\n,\nLaura Leal-Taixe\n,\nMike Chen\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nHuan Ling\n(2025).\nCosmos-Drive-Dreams: Scalable Synthetic Driving Data Generation with World Foundation Models\n.\nWhite Paper.\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nTianchang Shen*\n,\nJiahui Huang\n,\nHuan Ling\n,\nYifan Lu\n,\nMerlin Nimier-David\n,\nThomas Müller\n,\nAlexander Keller\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nJun Gao\n(2025).\nGEN3C: 3D-Informed World-Consistent Video Generation with Precise Camera Control\n.\nCVPR 2025 Highlight (3% acceptance rate).\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nNVIDIA\n(2025).\nCosmos-Transfer1: Conditional World Generation with Adaptive Multimodal Control\n.\nWhite Paper (Core Contributor; Featured in Jensen Huang's GTC 2025 keynote).\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nJay Zhangjie Wu*\n,\nYuxuan Zhang*\n,\nHaithem Turki\n,\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nJun Gao\n,\nMike Zheng Shou\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nZan Gojcic†\n,\nHuan Ling†\n(2025).\nDifix3D+: Improving 3D Reconstructions with Single-Step Diffusion Models\n.\nCVPR 2025 Best Paper Award Candidate (Top 14).\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nYifan Lu*\n,\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nJiawei Yang\n,\nTianchang Shen\n,\nZhangjie Wu\n,\nJun Gao\n,\nYue Wang\n,\nSiheng Chen\n,\nMike Chen\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nJiahui Huang\n(2025).\nInfiniCube: Unbounded and Controllable Dynamic 3D Driving Scene Generation with World-Guided Video Models\n.\nICCV 2025.\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nYifan Lu*\n,\nHanxue Liang\n,\nJay Zhangjie Wu\n,\nHuan Ling\n,\nMike Chen\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nFrancis Williams\n,\nJiahui Huang\n(2024).\nSCube: Instant Large-Scale Scene Reconstruction using VoxSplats\n.\nNeurIPS 2024.\nCite\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nJiahui Huang\n,\nXiaohui Zeng\n,\nKen Museth\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nFrancis Williams\n(2023).\nXCube: Large-Scale 3D Generative Modeling using Sparse Voxel Hierarchies\n.\nCVPR 2024 Highlight (2.8% acceptance rate).\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nChenyang Lei*\n,\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nZhaoxiang Zhang\n,\nQifeng Chen\n(2023).\nBlind Deflickering by Neural Filtering with a Flawed Atlas\n.\nCVPR 2023.\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nXiaolong Wang\n(2022).\nLook Outside the Room: Synthesizing A Consistent Long-Term 3D Scene Video from A Single Image\n.\nCVPR 2022.\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nTao Yang*\n,\nYuwang Wang\n,\nWenjun Zeng\n(2021).\nLearning Disentangled Representation by Exploiting Pretrained Generative Models: A Contrastive Learning View\n.\nICLR 2022.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nDacheng Yin*\n,\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nChong Luo\n,\nYuwang Wang\n,\nZhiwei Xiong\n,\nWenjun Zeng\n(2021).\nRetriever: Learning Content-Style Representation as a Token-Level Bipartite Graph\n.\nICLR 2022.\nPDF\nCite\nWebsite\nTao Yang\n,\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nYuwang Wang\n,\nWenjun Zeng\n(2021).\nTowards Building A Group-based Unsupervised Representation Disentanglement Framework\n.\nICLR 2022.\nPDF\nCode\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nTao Yang\n,\nYuwang Wang\n,\nWenjun Zeng\n(2021).\nRethinking Content and Style: Exploring Bias for Unsupervised Disentanglement\n.\nICCV Workshop 2021.\nPDF\nCode\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nTao Yang*\n,\nLi Erran Li\n,\nAlexandre Alahi\n,\nQifeng Chen\n(2021).\nSafety-aware Motion Prediction with Unseen Vehicles for Autonomous Driving\n.\nICCV 2021.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nXuanchi Ren*\n,\nZian Qian*\n,\nQifeng Chen\n(2020).\nVideo Deblurring by Fitting to Test Data\n.\nPreprint\n.\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nHaoran Li\n,\nZijian Huang\n,\nQifeng Chen\n(2019).\nSelf-supervised Dance Video Synthesis Conditioned on Music\n.\nACM MM 2020. Full Oral Presentation (9% acceptance rate).\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nProjects\nInnovate the Retail Industry with Automatic Checkout System\nXuanchi Ren\n,\nZian Qian\n,\nZhiwei Wang\nPDF\nOn the Performance Benefits of Zeroth Order Methods in the Context of Adversarial Training\nXAlice Biryukov\n,\nNicolas Dutly\n,\nXuanchi Ren\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
