    "homepage_text": "Faculty Biography | Faculty & Staff | Mathematics & Statistics  | TTU\nTexas Tech University\nDepartment\nof\nMathematics\n&\nStatistics\nMenu\nSearch\nTexas Tech\nMathematics & Statistics\nFaculty & Staff\nFaculty Biography\nJob Title:\nAssistant Professor\nEmail:\nsenwei.liang@ttu.edu\nPhone:\n806 834-1120\nOffice:\nMA 232\nDegree:\nPh.D. 2022 Purdue University\nOffice Hours:\nW 3:00-4:00\nF 3:00-4:00\nTR 2:30-3:30\nWebsite:\nPersonal Website\nDr. Senwei Liang\nResearch Interests\nMachine Learning, Scientific Computing\nBiography\nDr. Senwei Liang joined Texas Tech University as an Assistant Professor in Fall 2025. He earned his Ph.D. in Applied Mathematics from Purdue University in 2022 and was a postdoctoral researcher at Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory under the U.S. Department of Energy from 2022 to 2025. His research focuses on integrating advanced AI techniques with numerical algorithms to create scalable mathematical solvers for high-dimensional problems.\n« Back to Faculty List\nContact Contact TTU\nContact Contact TTU\nContact TTU\nNews for News\nNews for News\nNews\nEvents\nEvents\nEvents\nDepartment\nof\nMathematics\n&\nStatistics\nAddress\nTexas Tech University, 1108 Memorial Circle, Lubbock, TX 79409-1042\nPhone\n806.742.2566\nEmail\nmath.dept@ttu.edu\n© 2026            \t\t\t\t\t Texas Tech University\nSep 22, 2025\n2:04 PM"
  },
