rs in Variables\n  Models with Binary Response\nXu, K., Ma, Y. and Wang, L.\n2015,\nScandinavian Journal of Statistics,\n42, 104-117.\nEstimating Disease Onset Distribution Functions in\n    Mutation Carriers with  Censored Mixture Data.\nMa, Y. and Wang, Y.\n2014,\nJournal of the Royal Statistical\n    Society, Serie C\n, 63, 1-23.\nCombining Isotonic Regression and EM\nAlgorithm to Predict Genetic Risk under\nMonotonicity Constraint\nQin, J., Garcia, T., Ma, Y., Tang, M., Marder, K. and Wang, Y.\n2014,\nAnnals of Applied Statistics,\n8, 1182-1208.\nSemiparametric Efficient and Robust Estimation \n    of an Unknown Symmetric Population under Arbitrary Sample\n    Selection Bias.\nMa, Y., Kim, M. and Genton, M. G.\n2013,\nJournal of the American Statistical\n    Association\n, 108, 1090-1104.\nQuick and easy kernel based one-step estimation of parameters\n  in differential equations\nHall, P. and Ma, Y.\n2014,\nJournal of the Royal Statistical\n    Society, Serie B\n, 76, 735-748.\nSemiparametric analysis of linear transformation models with covariate \nmeasurement errors\nSinha, S. and Ma, Y.\n2014,\nBiometrics\n, 70, 21-32.\nEffective use of multiple error-prone covariate measurements\nin capture-recapture models\nXu, K. and Ma, Y.\n2014,\nStatistica Sinica\n, 24, 1529-1546.\nEfficient Estimation in Sufficient\n  Dimension Reduction.\nMa, Y. and Zhu, L.\n2013,\nAnnals of Statistics\n, 41, 250-268.\nEfficiency Loss Caused by Linearity Condition in\nDimension Reduction.\nMa, Y. and Zhu, L.\n2013,\nBiometrika\n, 100, 371-383.\nDoubly Robust and Efficient Estimators for\nHeteroscedastic Partially \nLinear Single-index Model Allowing High Dimensional Covariates.\nMa, Y. and Zhu, L.\n2013,\nJournal of the Royal Statistical Society, Serie B\n,  75, 305-322.\nTesting Overall and Subpopulation Treatment\nEffects with Measurement Errors.\nMa, Y. and Yin, G.\n2013,\nStatistica Sinica\n, 23, 1019-1042.\nA Review on Dimension Reduction.\nMa, Y. and Zhu, L.\n2013,\nInternationa