  "serper::K. Sun": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/kesun",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/datake",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ke-sun-17bb881b9/",
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Ke Sun's Homepage.\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nWelcome to Ke Sun's Homepage.\nI am a Machine Learning researcher.\nMy name is Ke Sun (孙科). I am currently a postdoctoral researcher at University of Pennsylvania, working with\nProf. Qi Long\nand\nProf. Weijie Su\n.\nPreviously, I was a postdoctoral f\nellow working with\nProf. Susan A. Murphy\nat Harvard University in 2025.\nI received my Ph.D. degree in\nStatistical Machine Learning\nfrom\nUniversity of Alberta in 2024, advised by\nProf. Linglong Kong\n, and was affiliated at\nAlberta Machine Intelligence Institute (\nAmii\n)\n. During my Ph.D., I was fortunate to visit\nProf. Chengchun Shi\nat the London School of Economics and Political Science\n(LSE) in 2023.\nI obtained my\nMPhil in Data Science at Peking University (PKU)\nin 2020 under the supervision of\nProf. Zhouchen Lin\nand\nProf. Zhanxing Zhu\n. I earned my Bachelor's degree in statistics from SouthWestern University of Finance and Economics (SWUFE) in 2017.\nContact\n:\nkesun6[AT] upenn\n.edu\nLinks\n:\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nCV\n/\nGithub\n/\nLinkedIn\nResearch Interests\nMy research interest is\nreinforcement learning.\nI analyze and develop sequential\ndecision-making algorithms\ngrounded in\nmathematical and statistical principles\nto build intelligent agents that can reason, explore, and adapt in complex and unknown environments to achieve\ndecision intelligence\n, with broad applications in games, robotics, control, health, economics, and language.\n[1] Algorithmic and Theoretical Foundations in Pure RL:\nUncertainty & Exploration\n:\nDistributional Learning and Risk Control, Entropy Regularization, Predictive Uncertainty\nRobustness & Adaptation\n:\nEnvironmental Nonstationarity\n, Safe and Robust RL, Transfer/Multi-task/Meta/\nContinual RL\nOffline &\nCausality\n: Imitation\nLearning,\nOffline and Hy\nbrid\nRL, Causality for RL, Adaptive Experiment Design\n[2] From Pure RL to General Intelligence:\nLanguage Intelligence\n: LLM Alignment and Reasoning\nPhysical /\nEmbodied\nIntelligence\n:\nRepresentation,\nModel-based/\nWorld Model, Generative/Unsupervised RL, Multi-agent RL\nSelected\nPreprints\n/ Publications [\nFull Publications\n]\n[7] Ke Sun,\nLinglong Kong, Hongtu Zhu, Chengchun Shi.\nARMA-Design: Optimal Treatment Allocation Strategies for A/B Testing in Partially Observable Experiments\n.\n(\nMinor\nRevision in Journal of American Statistical Association, 2025\n)\n[6]\nKe Sun\n*\n,\nHongming Zh\nang*\n,\nJun Jin, Chao Gao, Xi Chen, Wulong Liu, Linglong Kong.\nPrincipled Fast and Meta Knowledge Learners for Continual Reinforcement Learning\n.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 202\n6\n.  [\nCode\n]\n[\n5\n]\nKe Sun\n, Yingnan Zhao, Enze Shi, Yafei Wang, Xiaodong Yan, Bei Jiang, Linglong Kong.\nIntrinsic Benefits of Being Categorical Distributional: Uncertainty-aware Regularized Exploration in Reinforcement Learning\n.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2025\n[\n4\n]\nKe Sun\n, Yingnan Zhao, Wulong Liu, Bei Jiang, Linglong Kong.\nDistributional Reinforcement Learning with Regularized Wasserstein Loss\n[code]\n.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2024\n[3]\nKe Sun\n*, Yafei Wang*, Yi Liu, Yingnan Zhao, Bo Pan, Shangling Jui, Bei Jiang, Linglong Kong. (\n*\nequal contribution in alphabetical order).\nDamped Anderson Mixing for Deep Reinforcement Learning: Acceleration, Convergence, and Stabilization\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2021.\n[\nC\node\n]\n.\n[2]\nKe Sun\n, Zhanxing Zhu, Zhouchen Lin.\nAdaGCN: AdaBoosting Graph Convolutional Networks into Deep Models\n.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2021\n.\n[\nC\node\n]\n[1] Ke Sun\n, Zhouchen Lin, Zhanxing Zhu.\nMulti-Stage Self-Supervised Learning for Graph Convolutional Networks on Graphs with Few Labels\n.\nAssociation for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI)\n, 2020.\n[\nC\node\n]\n* denotes equal contribution\nFavorite Quotes\nPractice without theory is blind, but\nequally,\ntheory without practice is mere intellectual play.  ——Immanuel Kant\nThe statistical community has been committed to the almost exclusive use of data models. This commitment has led to irrelevant theory, questionable conclusions, and has kept statisticians from working on a large range of interesting current problems.\n…… The danger is that if we define the boundaries of our field in terms of familiar tools and familiar problems, we will fail to grasp the new opportunities.\n—— Leo Breiman\nTalk is cheap, show me the code.\n—— Linus Torvalds\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
