    "homepage_text": "Biography | Qianying Liu\nQianying Liu\n刘 倩莹\nView My GitHub Profile\nBiography\nI am now a researcher at\nNII Research and Development Center for Large Language Models (国立情報学研究所大規模言語モデル研究開発センター)\n.\nI obtained my PhD at Kyoto University, majoring in Intelligence Science and Technology, working under the supervision of\nSadao Kurohashi\nat\nKurohashi-Chu-Murawaki’s lab\n. I received my bachelor’s degree at the School of Mathematical Science, Peking University, majoring in Information and Computing Science. I received a double major bachelor’s degree in Computer Science from the School of Electronics Engineering and Computer Science, PKU. I previously worked under the supervision of\nSujian Li\nat\nthe Institute of Computational Linguistics\n. During my master’s period, my supervisor was\nDaisuke Kawahara\n. I have done research internships at\nATR RIKEN\nand\nNICT\n.\nEmail:\nying at nii dot ac dot jp\n[Publication]\n[About]\nResearch Interest:\nNatural Language Processing, focusing on numerical reasoning and information extraction.\nMachine Learning, focusing on applying transfer learning and semi-supervised learning methods to specific NLP tasks.\nDigital Humanities and Quantitative History, focusing on implying social network analysis methods to historical research\nPlease contact me if you have any ideas in the field of digital humanities and you are seeking for a programmer :)"
