    "homepage_text": "Qiangqiang WU\n      -  CityUHK Scholars\nCityUHK Scholars Home\nResearcher Login\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at CityUHK Scholars\nDr. Qiangqiang WU, 吴強強\nh-index\n433\nScopus Citations\n9\nScopus h-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2021\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nAuthor IDs\nORCID iD:\n0000-0002-3847-7838\nGoogle Scholar Profile:\nhNO_FXIAAAAJ\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 3\nGood Health and Well-being\nSDG 11\nSustainable Cities and Communities\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Qiangqiang WU is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nTracking Object\nComputer Science\n100%\nOptical Tracking\nComputer Science\n46%\nExperimental Result\nComputer Science\n40%\nAnnotation\nComputer Science\n32%\nZero-Shot Learning\nComputer Science\n32%\nAttention (Machine Learning)\nComputer Science\n28%\nFeature Extraction\nComputer Science\n24%\nVertebral Column\nComputer Science\n24%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration based on locations. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a place from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a place to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a place from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n13\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n8\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\nBoosting 3D Single Object Tracking with 2D Matching Distillation and 3D Pre-training\nWu, Q.\n, Xia, Y., Wan, J. &\nChan, A. B.\n,\n2025\n,\nComputer Vision – ECCV 2024: 18th European Conference, Milan, Italy, September 29–October 4, 2024, Proceedings, Part XII.\nLeonardis, A., Ricci, E., Roth, S., Russakovsky, O., Sattler, T. & Varol, G. (eds.). Cham:\nSpringer\n,\np. 270-288\n(Lecture Notes in Computer Science; vol. 15070).\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nTracking Object\n100%\nPoint Cloud\n40%\nRobotics\n20%\nSparsity\n20%\nArt Performance\n20%\n8\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nCGATracker: Correlation-Aware Graph Alignment for Referring Multi-Object Tracking\nZhuang, S., Li, G.,\nWu, Q.\n, Lu, Y., Hu, H.-M. & Wang, H.,\nNov 2025\n,\nIn:\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology.\n35\n,\n11\n,\np. 11337-11349\n13 p.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nMulti Object Tracking\n100%\nRelationship Modeling\n33%\nMultimodal Learning\n33%\nDistinctAD: Distinctive Audio Description Generation in Contexts\nFang, B.\n, Wu, W.,\nWu, Q.\n, Song, Y. &\nChan, A. B.\n,\n13 Aug 2025\n,\n2025 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR).\nIEEE\n,\np. 13571-13581\n(Proceedings (IEEE Computer Society Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition. Online)).\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nNarrative\n100%\nAudio description\n100%\nTV\n50%\nLanguage Modeling\n50%\nMaximization\n50%\nMGCA-Net: Multi-Graph Contextual Attention Network for Two-View Correspondence Learning\nLin, S., Lo, M., Chen, H., Liang, Y. &\nWu, Q.\n,\nAug 2025\n,\nProceedings of the Thirty-Fourth International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI-25).\nKwok, J. (ed.).\nInternational Joint Conferences on Artificial Intelligence\n,\np. 1539-1547\n9 p.\n(IJCAI International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence).\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nAttention (Machine Learning)\n100%\nPose Estimation\n40%\nExperimental Result\n20%\n3d Reconstruction\n20%\nFeature Information\n20%\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitation\n(Scopus)\nProgressive Semantic-Visual Alignment and Refinement for Vision-Language Tracking\nLiang, Y.,\nWu, Q.\n, Cheng, L., Xia, C. & Li, J.,\nMay 2025\n,\nIn:\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology.\n35\n,\n5\n,\np. 4271-4286\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nVisual Feature\n100%\nSemantic Feature\n100%\nSemantic Representation\n33%\nVisual Representation\n33%\nTracking Method\n33%\n3\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 21 research outputs\nThesis\nMatching-based Representation Learning for Object Tracking and Segmentation with Limited Annotations\nWU, Q.\n(Author),\nChan, A. B.\n(Supervisor),\n3 May 2024\nStudent thesis\n:\nDoctoral Thesis"
