    "homepage_text": "Homepage of Furong Xu's group\nNews\nPeople\nProfessor\nStudents\nResearch\nPublications\nPhotos\nLinks\nChinese\nProfessor Furong Xu (è®¸ç«è£)\nProfessor, School of Physics\nManaging Director,\nChina-U.S. Theory Institute for Physics with Exotic Nuclei (CUSTIPEN)\nDirector, PKU-IMPCAS (Lanzhou) Joint Center for Nuclear Physics\nDeputy Director, State Key Laboratory of Nuclear Physics and Technology\nVisiting Professor, University of Surrey, UK\nEducation/Academic Career:\nDegrees at Peking University: B.Sc. (1984), M.Sc. (1987), PhD (1993)\nResearch fellows: Royal Institute of Technology (KTH), Stockholm, Sweden (1995-1997),\nDepartment of Physics, University of Surrey, UK (1997-2000)\nProfessorship at Peking University: Assistant professor (1987-1990), Associate professor (1990-1995), professor (2000-2016), Peking University Boya Distinguished Professor of Physics(2016- )\nHead of Department of Technical  Physics, Peking University: 2001-2015\nResearch interests:\nTheoretical Nuclear Structure: nuclear forces, chiral effective field theory (N3LO),\nab-initio\nmethods, shell model, many-body perturbation theory (MBPT), Green's Function, Bruckner-Hartree-Fock, \n\trandom phase approximation (RPA), configuration-constrained cranking Skyrme Hartree-Fock-Pairing; exotic nuclei, \n\tnuclear collective and non-collective excitations, nuclear clustering and decays...\nAwards/Honors:\nZhong Sheng Biao Research Award (2019)\nPeking University Excellent Teaching Prize (2017)\nPKU Yang Fuqing Wang Yangyuan Prize (2013)\nPKU excellent supervisor awards (2012; 2011)\nWu Youxun Prize of Chinese Physical Society (2009)\nFirst Prize for Science and Technology, China Ministry of Education (2007; 2001)\nNSFC Distinguished Young Scholar (2005)\nBest Achievement Prize for Chinese Key Basic Research Program (Project 973), Ministry of Science and Technology of China\nHu Jimin Prize of Chinese Nuclear Physical Society (2000)\nCommittees/Services:\n2018â : Editorial Board member, Journal of Physics G: Nuclear and Particle Physics\n2017â : Panel Member, Special Programs for China Theoretical Physics, National Natural Science Foundation of China.\n2017â : Editorial Board member, Communications in Theoretical Physics.\n2014- : Board member, Asian Nuclear Physics Association (ANPhA)\n2014- : Associate editor-in-chief, Chinese Science Bulletin (Chinese Edition)\n2013- : Member of the standing council, Chinese Nuclear Physical Society.\n2013- : Review Specialist for National Prizes of Science of China.\n2013- : Member, Scientific Committee of Engineering Research Center for Nuclear Technical Applications (Ministry of Education of China).\n2013- : Editorial Board member, Nuclear Physics Review.\n2013- : Member, Committee for Physical Nominal Explanation China.\n2012- : Member, the Scientific Committee of the Lanzhou National Laboratory for Heavy Ion Physics\n2012- : Member, the Physics-II Grants Panel of National Natural Science Foundation of China.\n2012- : Member, Consulting Committee of Chinese Physics Society.\n2012- : Member, Committee for Physical Nominal Explanation, Chinese Physics Society.\n2009â2014: Editorial Board Member, Science Bulletin\n2005- : Deputy director, Steering Committee for High Education in Nuclear Engineering and Technology, \n\tMinistry of Education, China\nReferee:\nNature, Nature physics, Nature communications, Rev. Mod. Phys., Phys. Rev. Lett., Phys. Rev. C, \n\tEuro. Phys. J. A, J. of Phys. G, Physica Scripta, Canadian J. Physics, Chinese Science Bulletin, \n\tScience China, Chinese Physics Letters, Chinese Physics C â¦\nContact Info:\nAddress:\nRm 418, Accelerator Building, School of Physics, Peking University, Beijing, China, 100871\nTel:\n+86-010-62758994\nEmail:\nfrxu_at_pku.edu.cn\nResearcherID:\nhttp://www.researcherid.com/rid/K-4178-2013\nHomepage of Junchen Pei's group:\nhttp://www.phy.pku.edu.cn/~jcpei/index.html\nHomepage of Students:\nhttp://www.phy.pku.edu.cn/~frxu/people.html\nUpdated at July. 18, 2019\nCopyright Â© 2019 Peking University\nBackground picture supported by Simin Wang"
  },
