    "homepage_text": "CURELab Research Group\nSearch\nCURELab\nAt the\nCU\nHK\nRE\nliable Computing laboratory (CURE Lab.), our core research methodology is rooted in creating innovative solutions that directly tackle the limitations of state-of-the-art computing technologies. Currently, we are passionately committed to the exploration and advancement of artificial intelligence across a variety of cutting-edge directions:\n✨ AI-Native EDA\n✨ Time Series\n✨ Generative AI\nWe are continue to work on the safety and security aspects of AI, developing robust AI models that can withstand adversarial attacks and operate reliably even under uncertain or volatile conditions.\nLatest News\nOct 23, 2023\n2 min read\nAre transformers effective for time series forecasting? is Selected as Most Influential AAAI Papers of 2023\nCongratulations to Ailing Zeng and Muxi Chen for winning the most influential AAAI papers of 2023 for their paper “Are transformers effective for time series forecasting?”\nPeople\nProfessor\nQiang Xu 徐强\nProfessor, Director pf CURE Lab\nPh.D. Student\nJiaying Zhu 朱佳颖\nPh.D. - 2024 fall\nKezhi Li 李柯志\nPh.D. - 2024 fall\nYuxuan Bian 卞宇轩\nPh.D. - 2024 fall\nZeju Li 李泽钜\nPh.D. - 2024 fall\nChenchen Zhao 赵晨辰\nPh.D. - 2023 fall\nJianyuan Zhong 钟坚元\nPh.D. - 2023 fall\nZiyang Zheng 郑紫阳\nPh.D. - 2023 fall\nXiangyu Wen 温翔宇\nPh.D. - 2022 fall\nXuan Ju 鞠璇\nPh.D. - 2022 fall\nYi Liu 刘奕\nPh.D - 2022 fall\nZhengyuan Shi 石正源\nPh.D. - 2021 fall\nZhijian Xu 许智健\nPh.D. - 2021 fall\nRuiyuan Gao 高瑞元\nPh.D. - 2020 fall\nSadaf Khan\nPh.D. - 2020 fall\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
