    "homepage_text": "Jie Qin's Homepage (秦杰)\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJie Qin (秦杰)\nShort Bio\nI am currently a\nProfessor\nand Director of the\nMultimedia and Visual Perception Laboratory\n(\nMVP Lab\n)\nat the College of Artificial Intelligence, Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics (\nNUAA\n), Nanjing, China. Before that, I was a\nResearch Scientist with the Inception Institute of Artificial Intelligence (\nIIAI\n), Abu Dhabi, UAE, a\nnd a Postdoctoral Researcher working with\nProf. Luc Van Gool\nat the Computer Vision Laboratory (\nCVL\n),\nETH Zurich\n, Zurich, Switzerland. I obtained my Ph.D. degree from Beihang University (\nBUAA\n), Beijing, China, under the supervision of\nProf. Yunhong Wang\n. During my Ph.D., I visited\nThe University of Sheffield\n, Sheffield, UK, as a Visiting Researcher, working with\nProf. Ling Shao\n.\nEmail\n: qinjiebuaa[AT]gmail[DOT]com or jie\n[DOT]qin[AT]\nnuaa\n[DOT]\nedu\n[DOT]cn\nNews\n2\n1\n/02/202\n6\nTwo papers are accepted to\nCVPR 2026\n.\n31\n/\n12\n/2025    One paper is accepted to\nIEEE T\nCSVT\n.\n08/11/2025    Three papers are accepted to\nAAAI 2026\n.\n1\n6\n/\n10\n/2025\nOur paper has won the\nBest Paper\nHo\nnorable Mention Award\nof\nCyberworlds\n2025\n.\n1\n8\n/0\n9\n/2025    T\nwo\npapers are accepted to\nNeurIPS 2025\n.\n11\n/0\n7\n/2025\nThree\npapers\nare\naccepted to\nECAI 2025\n.\n26\n/0\n6\n/202\n5\nOne paper is accepted to\nICCV 2025\n.\n05\n/0\n4\n/202\n5\nOne paper is accepted to\nSIGIR 2025\n.\n25\n/\n03\n/202\n5\nOne paper is accepted to\nIEEE TIP\n.\n06/\n01\n/202\n5\nOne paper is accepted to\nIEEE TCSVT\n.\n10\n/12/202\n4\nOne paper is accepted to\nAAAI 2025\n.\n1\n6/07/202\n4\nOne\npaper\nis\naccepted to\nACM MM 2024\n.\n1\n1\n/07/2024\nOur\nICME\n20\n24\npaper is selected as\nBest Paper Candidate\n!\n03\n/0\n7\n/202\n4\nOne paper is accepted to\nIEEE TMM\n.\n01\n/0\n7\n/2024\nOne paper is\naccepted to\nECCV\n2024\n.\n17/04/2024    Two papers are accepted to\nIJCAI 2024\n.\n26\n/0\n3\n/202\n4\nOne paper is accepted to\nSIGIR\n2024\n.\n2\n7\n/02/202\n4\nTwo papers\nare\naccepted to\nCVPR 2024\n.\n0\n9/1\n2\n/202\n3\nOne\npaper is accepted to\nAAAI 2024\n.\n01/11/2023    Our paper has won the\nHonorable Mention Award (Top 1‰)\nof\nACM MM 2023\n!\n26\n/07/202\n3\nT\nhree\npapers are accepted to\nACM MM 2023\n(1 Oral &\n2\nPosters).\n14\n/07/202\n3\nOne paper is accepted to\nICCV 2023\n.\n26/03/2023    One paper is accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\n24/03/2023    One paper is accepted to\nIEEE TMM\n.\n20/03/2023    One paper is accepted to\nIEEE TMI\n.\n28\n/0\n2\n/202\n3\nOne paper is accepted to\nCVPR 2023\n.\n16\n/0\n2\n/20\n23\nOne paper is accepted to\nIJCV\n. Two papers are accepted to\nICASSP 2023\n.\n14\n/0\n2\n/202\n3\nOne paper is accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\n19\n/\n11\n/2022    Two papers are accepted to\nAAAI 2023\n.\n12/0\n7\n/2022\nOur\nSHREC 2022\ntrack paper has been accepted to\nComputers & Graphics\n.\n0\n4\n/07/202\n2\nTwo\npapers are accepted to\nECCV 2022\n.\n15\n/0\n6\n/2022    Call For Papers:\nSensors\n(IF: 3.576)\nSpecial Issue on\nPerson Re-identification Based on Computer Vision\n. (DDL: 15\nFeb\n. 202\n3\n)\n31\n/05/20\n22\nCall For Papers:\nSensors\n(IF: 3.576)\nSpecial Issue on Advances in Sensor-Based Biometric Recognition\n. (DDL: 1\n5\nDec. 2022)\n21/04/2022    One paper is accepted to\nIJCAI 2022\n.\n16/\n01\n/202\n2\nOne\npaper\nis\naccepted to\nIEEE TMM\n.\n01/01/2022    We are organizing the\nSHREC 2022\nTrack:\nSketch-Based 3D Shape Retrieval in the Wild\n. Looking forward to your participation!\n01/12/2021    Two\npapers\nare\naccepted to\nAAAI 2022\n.\n2\n9\n/0\n9\n/2021    One paper is accepted to\nNeurIPS 2021\n.\n23/07/2021    One paper is accepted to\nICCV 2021\n.\n07/07/2021    Two papers\n(1 Oral\n& 1\nPoster)\nare accepted to\nACM MM 2021\n.\n26/03/2021    One paper is accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\n01/03/2021    Two papers are accepted to\nCVPR 2021\n.\n30/01/2021    One paper is accepted to\nICASSP 2021\n.\n13/12/2020    One paper is accepted to\nIEEE TIP\n.\n02/12/2020    One paper is accepted to\nAAAI 2021\n.\n15/10/2020    One paper is accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\n06/08/2020    Two papers are accepted to\nACM MM 2020\n.\n14/07/2020    Our\nIJCV Special Issue\nis now online. Congratulations to all the accepted papers!\n03/07/2020    Four papers\n(1 Oral, 1 Spotlight & 2 Posters)\nare accepted to\nECCV 2020\n.\n24/02/2020    Three papers are accepted to\nCVPR 2020\n.\n18/12/2019    One paper is accepted to\nIEEE TIP\n.\n10/03/2019    One paper is accepted to\nICME 2019\nas an oral presentation.\n03/03/2019    Three papers are accepted to\nCVPR 2019\n. Two papers are accepted to\nIEEE TCSVT\n.\n05/07/2018    Three papers (1 Oral & 2 Posters) are accepted to\nECCV 2018\n. See you in Munich!\n19/05/2018    Call For Papers: International Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n)\nSpecial Issue on Efficient Visual Recognition\n.\n30/03/2018    We are organizing the 2nd International Workshop on Compact and Efficient Feature Representation and Learning in Computer Vision (\nCEFRL 2018\n) in conjunction with\nECCV 2018\n.\n30/01/2018    One paper is accepted to\nICASSP 2018\nas an oral presentation.\nEducation\n09/2011 - 03/2017    Ph.D., School of Computer Science and Engineering, Beihang University, China (\nThesis: Research on Video-Based Human Action Recognition)\n09/2014 - 09/2015    Visiting Researcher, Department of Electronic and Electrical Engineering, The University of Sheffield, UK\n09/2007 - 07/2011    B.Eng., School of Computer Science and Engineering, Beihang University, China\nResearch Interests\nComputer Vision, Machine Learning, Pattern Recognition, Image/Video Processing\nIn particular: Human Activity Analysis, Person Re-Identification, Content-Based Image/Video Retrieval, Few/Zero-Shot Learning, 3D Vision\nSelected Publications [\nFull List\n,\nGoogle Scholar\n]\n(\n*\n=corresponding author; *=equal contribution)\nJournal Articles:\nY. Yuan, P. Gao, Q. Dai,\nJ. Qin*\nand W. Xiang, \"\nUncertainty-Guided Refinement for Fine-Grained Salient Object Detection\n\", IEEE Transactions on Image Processing (\nTIP\n), vol. 34, pp. 2301-2314, Apr. 2025.\nY. Yan, J. Li,\nJ. Qin*\n, P. Zheng, S. Liao and X. Yang, \"\nEfﬁcient Person Search: An Anchor-Free Approach\n\",\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n),\nvol. 131, pp. 1642-1661, Mar.\n2023.\nY. Yan*,\nJ. Qin*\n, B. Ni, J. Chen, L. Liu, F. Zhu, W.-S. Zheng, X. Yang and L. Shao, \"\nLearning Multi-Attention Context Graph for Group-Based Re-Identification\n\",\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n),\nvol. 45, no. 6, pp. 7001-7018, Jun. 2023. [\nA New Large-Scale Dataset for Group Re-ID\n]\nL. Huang,\nJ. Qin\n, Y. Zhou, F. Zhu, L. Liu and L. Shao, \"\nNormalization Techniques in Training DNNs: Methodology, Analysis and Application\n\",\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n),\n2023.\nP. Zheng, H. Fu, D.-P. Fan, Q. Fan,\nJ. Qin\n, Y.-W. Tai, C.-K. Tang and L. V. Gool, \"\nGCoNet+: A Stronger Group Collaborative Co-Salient Object Detector\n\",\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n),\n2023.\nJ. Li, G. Wang, Y. Yan, F. Yu, Q. Jia,\nJ. Qin\n, S. Ding and X. Yang, \"\nGPS: Generalizable Person Search on Large-scale User-Generated Video Content\n\", IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (\nTCSVT\n), Jan. 2025.\nY. Yan, J. Li, S. Liao and\nJ. Qin\n, \"TAL: Two-stream Adaptive Learning for Generalizable Person Re-identification\", Machine Intelligence Research\n(\nMIR\n), vol. 22, no. 2, Apr. 2025.\nY. Jia, R. Quan, H. Chen, J. Liu, Y. Yan, S. Bai and\nJ. Qin*\n, \"\nDisaggregation Distillation for Person Search\n\", IEEE Transactions on Multimedia (\nTMM\n), 2024.\nW. Zhou, L. Kong, Y. Han,\nJ. Qin*\nand Z. Sun, \"\nContextualized Relation Predictive Model for Self-Supervised Group Activity Representation Learning\n\",\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia (\nTMM\n), vol. 2\n6\n, pp.\n353\n-\n366, Apr\n. 202\n3\n.\nG. Chen,\nJ. Qin*\n, B. B. Amor, W. Zhou, H. Dai, T. Zhou, H. Huang and L. Shao, \"\nAutomatic Detection of Tooth-Gingiva Trim Lines on Dental Surfaces\n\", IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (\nTMI\n), 2023.\nH. Xiong\n, M. Yu, L. Liu, F. Zhu,\nJ. Qin\n, F. Shen and L. Shao, \"\nA Generalized Method for Binary Optimization: Convergence Analysis and Applications\n\",\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n), vol. 44, no. 9, pp. 4524-4543,\nSept\n. 2\n022.\nJ. Qin\n, et al., \"\nSHREC’22 Track: Sketch-Based 3D Shape Retrieval in the Wild\n\", Computers & Graphics (\nC&G\n), vol. 107, pp. 104-115, Oct. 2022.\nR. Gao, X. Hou,\nJ. Qin*\n, Y. Shen, Y. Long, L. Liu, Z. Zhang and L. Shao, \"\nVisual-Semantic Aligned Bidirectional Network for Zero-Shot Learning\n\",\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia (\nTMM\n), vol. 25, pp. 1649-1\n664,\nJan. 2022.\nM. Qi,\nJ. Qin\n, Y. Yang, Y. Wang and J. Luo, \"\nSemantics-Aware Spatial-Temporal Binaries for Cross-Modal Video Retrieval\n\", IEEE Transactions on Image Processing (\nTIP\n), vol. 30, pp. 2989-3004, Feb. 2021.\nY. Huang, X. Hou\n*\n, Y. Dun\n*\n,\nJ. Qin*\n, L. Liu, X. Qian and L. Shao, \"Learning Deformable and Attentive Network for Image Restoration\", Knowledge-Based Systems (\nKBS\n), vol. 231, Nov. 2021.\nL. Liu, M. Pietikäinen,\nJ. Qin\n, W. Ouyang and L. Van Gool, \"\nEfficient Visual Recognition\n\", International Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n), vol. 128, pp. 1997-2001, Sept. 2020.\nR. Gao, X. Hou*,\nJ. Qin*\n, J. Chen, L. Liu, F. Zhu, Z. Zhang and L. Shao, \"\nZero-VAE-GAN: Generating Unseen Features for Generalized and Transductive Zero-Shot Learning\n\", IEEE Transactions on Image Processing (\nTIP\n),\nvol. 29, pp. 3665-3680, Jan. 2020\n.\nM. Qi, Y. Wang,\nJ. Qin\n, A. Li, J. Luo and L. Van Gool, \"\nstagNet: An Attentive Semantic RNN for Group Activity and 