    "homepage_text": "ï»¿\nYong-Shun Zhang @ LAMDA, NJU-AI\nYong-Shun Zhang (å¼ æ°¸é¡º)\nYong-Shun Zhang\nMaster. candidate,\nLAMDA Group\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\nNanjing University\n, Nanjing, China\nSupervisor:\nProf. Jianxin Wu\nEmail: zhangys@lamda.nju.edu.cn\nAbout Me\nCurrently I am a second year graduate student of\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\nin\nNanjing University\nand a member of\nLAMDA\nGroup, led by professor\nZhi-Hua\n    Zhou\n.\nI got my B.Sc. degree in June 2019 from\nHarbin Institute of Technology (HIT)\n. In the same year, I was admitted to pursue for a M.Sc. degree in\nNanjing University\nwithout entrance examination.\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests include Computer Vision and Machine Learning.\nPublications\nYongshun Zhang\n, Xiu-Shen Wei, Boyan Zhou, and Jianxin Wu. Bag of Tricks for Long-Tailed Visual Recognition with Deep Convolutional Neural Networks. In: Proc. the 35th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2021. [\npaper\n][\ncode\n]\nXin Jin, Yanping Xie, Xiu-Shen Wei, Bo-Rui Zhao,\nYongshun Zhang\n, Xiaoyang Tan, and Yang Yu. A Lightweight Encoder-Decoder Path for Deep Residual Networks.\n                IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS), 2020. [\npaper\n][\ncode\n]\nContests & Awards\nThe\nfirst place\nof the\niWildCam\ntrack in FGVC 7 (in association with\nCVPR 2020\n), 2020.\nThe\nfirst place\nfor Similar Image Retrieval in\nChina Artificial Intelligence Competition\n, 2019.\næå®æ¯ä»äºç­å¥å­¦é, Nanjing University, 2020.\nç ç©¶çè±æä¸ç­å¥å­¦é, Nanjing University, 2019.\nServices\nConference Paper Reviewer:\nECCV2020\n,\nICPR2020\n.\nCorrespondence\nEmail:\nzhangys@lamda.nju.edu.cn\nOffice:\nRoom 113, Computer Science Building, Xianlin Campus of Nanjing University\nPage updated on 2019.09.04,via\njemdoc\n."
