    "homepage_text": "Jun Zhang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJun Zhang\nHome\nAbout me:\nI am currently a\nTenure-track Assistant Professor at the Institute of Geometry and Physics at the University of Science and Technology of China (\nUSTC-IGP\n).\nMy mathematical interests are the following subjects:\nsymplectic geometry\ncontact geometry\npersistent homology\nmicrolocal sheaf theory\n.\nI received my Ph.D. in 2016 at the University of Georgia in USA under the supervision of Professor Michael Usher.\nFrom October 2016 t\no\nSeptember 2019, I was a postdoctoral researcher at Tel Aviv University in Is\nrael\n, working with Professor Leonid Polterovich. From\nSeptember 2019 to August 2021, I was a CRM-ISM Postdoctoral Fellow at CRM - University of Montreal in Canada, working with Professor Egor Shelukhin and Professor Octav Cornea.\nContact information:\nAddress: No. 96 Jinzhai Road, Hefei, Anhui, China 230026.\nEmail: jzhang4518 at\nustc\ndot\nedu dot cn\nCurriculum Vitae\nHere\nis my Google Scholar.\nMy papers on\narXiv\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
