    "homepage_text": "Lin Pan @ TJU\nSearch\nLin Pan\nAssistant Professor\nSchool of Marine Science and Technology\nTianjin University\nBiography\nLin Pan is an assistant professor with the School of Marine Science and Technology, Tianjin University.\nHe joined the department in Jan 2016.\nHis research interests include\nnetwork science\n,\nsocial computing\nand\ncomputational social science\n, data mining, and artificial intelligence.\nInterests\nNetwork Science\nSocial Copmuting and Computational Social Science\nData Mining\nArtificial Intelligence\nEducation\nPhD in School of Computer Science and Technology, 2009.09-2016.01\nTianjin University\nBSc in School of Software Engineering, 2005.09-2009.07\nTianjin University\nFeatured Publications\nPengfei Jiao\n,\nXuan Guo\n,\nTing Pan\n,\nWang Zhang\n,\nYulong Pei\n,\nLin Pan\nNovember, 2021\nIEEE Transactions on Big Data\nA Survey on Role-Oriented Network Embedding\nRecent Publications\nQuickly discover relevant content by\nfiltering publications\n.\nYinghui Wang\n,\nQiyao Peng\n,\nWenjun Wang\n,\nXuan Guo\n,\nMinglai Shao\n,\nHongtao Liu\n,\nWei Liang\n,\nLin Pan\n(2022).\nNetwork Alignment Enhanced via Modeling Heterogeneity of Anchor Nodes\n.\nKnowledge-Based Systems\n.\nPDF\nCite\nDOI\nTianpeng Li\n,\nWenjun Wang\n,\nPengfei Jiao\n,\nYinghui Wang\n,\nRuomeng Ding\n,\nHuaming Wu\n,\nLin Pan\n,\nDi Jin\n(2022).\nExploring Temporal Community Structure via Network Embedding\n.\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\n.\nPDF\nCite\nDOI\nWang Zhang\n,\nYang Yu\n,\nTing Pan\n,\nLin Pan\n,\nPengfei Jiao\n,\nWenjun Wang\n(2021).\nGenerating Structural Node Representations via Higher-order Features and Adversarial Learning\n.\n2021 IEEE International Conference on Data Mining (ICDM)\n.\nPDF\nCite\nDOI\nSee all publications\nContact\nlinpan@tju.edu.cn\nNo.92 Weijin Road, Nankai District, Tianjin 300072\nRoom 114, Building No.8, Tianjin University (\nMap\n)\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
