    "homepage_text": "Liunian Harold Li\nLiunian Harold Li\nHi, welcome to my homepage! I completed my Ph.D. at the\nDepartment of Computer Science, UCLA\n. I was fortunated to work with\nProf. Kai-Wei Chang\nfocusing on problems in\nNatural Language Processing\nand\nComputer Vision\n.\nPublications (Selected)\n[Google Scholar]\n[Semantic Scholar]\nOn the Paradox of Learning to Reason from Data\nHonghua Zhang,\nLiunian Harold Li\n, Tao Meng, Kai-Wei Chang, Guy Van den Broeck.\nIJCAI. 2023\n.\nGrounded Language-Image Pre-training\nLiunian Harold Li*\n, Pengchuan Zhang*, Haotian Zhang*, Jianwei Yang, Chunyuan Li, Yiwu Zhong, Lijuan Wang, Lu Yuan, Lei Zhang, Jenq-Neng Hwang, Kai-Wei Chang, Jianfeng Gao.\nCVPR 2022\n.\nBest Paper Finalist.\nVisualBERT: A Simple and Performant Baseline for Vision and Language\nLiunian Harold Li\n, Mark Yatskar, Da Yin, Cho-Jui Hsieh, Kai-Wei Chang.\nArxiv\n. Short Version Published as\nWhat Does BERT with Vision Look At?\nat\nACL 2020\n.\nEfficient Contextual Representation Learning With Continuous Outputs\nLiunian Harold Li\n, Patrick H. Chen, Cho-Jui Hsieh, Kai-Wei Chang.\nTACL 2019\n.\nAwards\nGoogle Ph.D. Fellowship 2023\nCVPR 2022 Best Paper Finalist\nAmazon-UCLA Fellowship 2022\nService\nReviewing for EMNLP, NAACL, NeurIPS, CVPR, ICCV, ICLR\nHonored to serve as a student co-chair for NAACL Student Research Workshop 2022\nHonored to serve as a workflow co-chair for AAAI 2023"
  },
