    "homepage_text": "Haoran Xie's Homepage\nHomepage Menu\nHome\nEducation\nPublications\nFunding\nAwards\nServices\nNews\nDownloads\nProf. Haoran Xie's Homepage\nProf.  Haoran Xie\nPhD (CityU HK), EdD (Bristol), SrMACM, SrMIEEE\nProfessor & Person-in-Charge, Division of Artificial Intelligence\nInterim Person-in-Charge, Division of Industrial Data Science\nDirector, LEO Dr David P. Chan Institute of Data Science\nAssociate Dean, School of Data Science\nProgramme Director, Bachelor of Science in Data Science\nLingnan University, Hong Kong\nEmail: hrxie AT ln.edu.hk\nOffice: \r\n\r\n\r\n Unit A, 1/F, Lingnan Hub\nLingnan University, Tuen Mun, Hong Kong\nOffice Phone: +852-26168129 Office Fax: +852-28922442\nBiography\nProf. XIE Haoran is the Professor and Person-in-Charge at the\nDivision of Artificial Intelligence\n, Interim Person-in-Charge at the\nDivision of Industrial Data Science\n, the Associate Dean of the\nSchool of Data Science\n, the Director of the\nLEO Dr David P. Chan Institute of Data Science\nand the Prgramme Director of the\nBachelor of Science in Data Science\nat\nLingnan University\n, Hong Kong. \r\n  He is the Co-Editor-in-Chief of\nKnowledge Management & E-Learning\n(The University of Hong Kong),\r\n  Editor-in-Chief of\nNatural Language Processing Journal\n(Elsevier),\nComputers & Education: X Reality\n(Elsevier),\nComputers & Education: Artificial Intelligence\n(Elsevier), and\nArtificial Intelligence in Language Education\n(Castledown),\r\n  the Associate Editors of\nInternational Journal of Machine Learning and Cybernetics\n(Springer),\nArray\n(Elseiver),\nInternational Journal of Mobile Learning and Organisation\n(InderScience), and\nAustralasian Journal of Educational Technology\n(till 2022). \r\n    He has totally published 484 research publications including 299 journal articles (90 papers as first or corresponding author), 7 edited books, 70 book chapters, 102 conference proceedings and 6 patents. Among all 299 journal articles, there are 239 SCI/SSCI indexed, \r\n    including IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence, IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering, IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing, IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics, Computers & Education, British Journal of Educational Technology, Education Technology & Society, Education and Information Technologies and so on. Among all book chapters and conference proceedings, there are many papers from top-tier conferences like AAAI, ACM MM, CVPR, ICCV, ACL, EMNLP, IJCAI, CIKM, and so on. He has served as 18 guest editors in special issues of journals, editors of 7 books, organization committee chairs/members of more than 59 conferences, and reviewers of 40 international journals.\r\nTill March 2026, his totally Google Scholar citation counts is 31827, h-index is 69, and i-10 index is 257 at Google Scholar. One of his work about Least squares generative adversarial networks (LSGAN) which has received more than 6828 citations ins Google Scholar, published in ICCV 2017 and TPAMI 2019, included by computer science courses of Stanford University and National Taiwan University, and implemented by Google TensorFlow.\nEditorship\nEditor-in-Chief,\nArtificial Intelligence in Language Education\n(Castledown)\nEditor-in-Chief,\nNatural Language Processing Journal\n(Elsevier)\nEditor-in-Chief,\nComputers & Education: X Reality\n(Elsevier)\nEditor-in-Chief,\nComputers & Education: Artificial Intelligence\n(Elsevier)\nCo-Editor-in-Chief,\nKnowledge Management & E-Learning\n(The University of Hong Kong)\nAssociate Editor,\nPLOS One\n(PLOS)\nAssociate Editor,\nInternational Journal of Machine Learning and Cybernetics\n(Springer)\nAssociate Editor,\nArray\n(Elseiver)\nAssociate Editor,\nInternational Journal of Mobile Learning and Organisation\n(InderScience)\nAssociate Editor,\nAustralasian Journal of Educational Technology\n(till 2022)\nEditorial Board Member,\nEducational Technology & Society\n(International Forum of Educational Technology and Society)\nEditorial Board Member,\nEducational Technology & Society\n(Taiwan Normal University)\nEditorial Board Member,\nJournal of Computers in Education\n(Springer)\nEditorial Board Member,\nAdvances in Computational Intelligence\n(Springer)\nEditorial Board Member,\nHuman-Centric Intelligent Systems\n(Springer)\nEditorial Board Member,\nInternational Journal of Distance Education Technologies\n(IGI Global)\nGoogle Scholar Rank\nArtificial Intelligence in Education\n- World Rank #4 (Google Scholar)\nLanguage Learning\n- World Rank #5 (Google Scholar)\nLarge Language Model\n- World Rank #10 (Google Scholar)\nResearch Interests\nHis research interests include Artificial Intelligence in Education, Technology-Enhanced Learning, Language Learning, Technology-Enhanced Language Learning, Natural Language Processing, Large Language Model, Educational Data Mining.\nRA, MPhi, PhD, PostDoc and Visiting Scholar Opportunties\n[24. Oct, 2025] We are currently recruiting\n1 Postdoctoral Researcher (Remaining Quota: 1)\nat Lingnan University. Please email your full CV, including your research interests and publications, to\nhrxie@ln.edu.hk\n.\n[24. Oct, 2025] We are currently recruiting\n4 full-time PhD students (Remaining Quota: 4)\nat Lingnan University. Please submit your full CV (with GPA & your publications) and indicate your study mode (self-financed/studentship/fellowship) for your application to my email\nhrxie@ln.edu.hk\n. For the round of 2026/27, the application deadline is\n30 November 2025\nand please contact me as early as possible.\n[24. Oct, 2025] There are\n2 vacancies of full-time research assistants (Remaining Quota: 2)\nin my research teams in both Lingnan University, and Hong Kong Metropolitan University (collaborative affiliation). Students/Researchers who are interested in AI in Education, Large Language Model, Natural Language Processing, Educational Technology are welcome to send your inquiries to my email\nhrxie@ln.edu.hk\n. Please submit your full CV and indicate your preferred posts, available periods, and expected salary for your application by\n30 November 2025\n.\nNews\n[01. Jan, 2024] I have been appointed as the Editorial Board Member of\nEducational Technology & Society\n[A journal of Taiwan Normal University]. You are welcome to submit your papers to this journal!\n[01. Jul, 2023] I have been appointed as the Co-Editor-in-Chief of\nKnowledge Management & E-Learning\n[A journal of The University of Hong Kong]. You are welcome to submit your papers to this journal!\n[01. Jul, 2022] I have been appointed as the Editor-in-Chief of\nNatural Language Processing Journal\n[A new journal of Elsevier]. You are welcome to submit your papers to this journal!\n[01. Jul, 2022] I have been appointed as the Editor-in-Chief of\nComputers & Education: X Reality\n[A new journal of Elsevier]. You are welcome to submit your papers to this journal!\n[13. Jul, 2020] I have been appointed as the Editor-in-Chief of\nComputers & Education: Artificial Intelligence\n[A new journal of Elsevier]. You are welcome to submit your papers to this journal!\n[25. Jun, 2020] I have been appointed as the Associate Editor of\nArray\n[A new journal of Elsevier]. You are welcome to submit your papers to this journal!\n[05. May, 2020] I have been appointed as the Associate Editor of\nInternational Journal of Mobile Learning and Organisation\n[Index by Scopus, Q1]. You are welcome to submit your papers to this journal!\n[02. Mar, 2020] I have been a guest editor of\nFrom Conventional AI to Modern AI in education- Re-examining AI and Analytics Techniques for Teaching and Learning\n,\nJournal of Educational Technology & Society\n[Indexed by SSCI, Impact Factor = 4.000]. You are welcome to submit your papers to this special issue!\nMore...\nAwards\n2025 - World’s Top 2% Scientists, Stanford University\n2024 - #2,773 Highly Ranked Scholar - Prior Five Years, ScholarGPS\n2024 - Best Computer Science Scientists, Research.com\n2024 - World's Top 2% Scientists, Stanford University\n2024 - Silver Award, 49th International Exhibition of Inventions of Geneva\n2024 - Teaching Excellence Awards Scheme (TEAS) 2023/2024, Certificate of Merit, Lingnan University\n2023 - World's Top 2% Scientists, Stanford University\n2023 - Healthy Longevity Catalyst Awards, Research Grant Council\n2022 - World's Top 2% Scientists in (1) Artificial Intelligence and (2) Education, Stanford University\n2022 - Most Cited Article in Computer-Assisted Language Learning, Taylor & Francis\n2022 - Gold Medal, International Invention Innovation Competition in Canada (iCAN)\n2022 - Special Award, International Invention Innovation Competition in Canada (iCAN)\n2022 - Research Output Excellence Award, Lingnan University\n2022 - Teaching Excellence Awards Scheme (TEAS) 2021/2022, Certificate of Merit, Lingnan University\n2021 - World's Top 2% Scientists in (1) Artificial Intelligence and (2) Education, Stanford University\n2021 - Most Cited Article in Computers & Education, Elsevier\n2020 - WI-AIT 2020 Best Research Paper Award\n2020 - Literia Award 2020 (Outstanding Paper), Emerald Publisher\n2020 - Silver Award, International Innovation and Invention Competition Taiwan\n2020 - ICBL 2020 Excellent Research Paper Award\n2019 - Gold Medal, International Invention Innovation Competition in Canada (iCAN)\n2019 - Special Award - British Innovation Award, International Invention Innovation Competition in Canada (iCAN)\n2019 - Outstanding Research Achievement Award, Asia Pacific Society for Computing and Information Technology\n2019 - Silver Award, Multimedia Grand Challenges, ACM Multimedia 2019\n2019 - Silver Award, 47th International Exhibition of Inventions of Geneva\n2019 - President's Award for Outstanding Performance in Research, The Education University of Hong Kong\n2019 - Research Output Prize (Faculty), The Education University of Hong Kong\n2017 - DASFAA 2017 Best Paper Award (Runner Up)\n2016 - ICBL 2016 Excellent Research Paper Award\n2015 - SECOP 2015 Best Paper Award\nJournal Articles\n[J299] Xieling Chen, Di Zou,\nHaoran Xie\n,\nTechnologies in content and language integrated learning: types, purposes, and outcomes\n, International Journal of Mobile Lea...[truncated]"
