    "github": "https://github.com/wpqmanu",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/panqu",
    "homepage_text": "Panqu Wang’s Homepage - Panqu Wang’s Homepage\nPanqu Wang 王泮渠\nMaking Scalable L4 Autonomous Driving Possible.\nFollow\nShanghai, China\nZERON 零一汽车\nWebsite\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nGithub\nLinkedIn\nZhihu\nPanqu Wang’s Homepage\nHello! My name is Panqu Wang (王泮渠). I am currently the Partner, Autonomous Driving at\nZERON 零一汽车\n, leading the team to invent high-performance, strong-generalization, and cost-efficient L4 autonomous driving product. Prior to ZERON, I was the Director of Deep Perception at\nTuSimple\n, creating efficient and effective perception system for L4 autonomous driving trucks.\nI obtained my Ph.D. degree in March, 2017 from the\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nat\nUC San Diego\n. My advisor is\nProfessor Garrison W. Cottrell\n. My research areas are on perception and cognitive modeling. I build brain-inspired neurocomputational models that explain how face and objects are processed and recognized in human visual pathway. For the full publication list, please check my\nGoogle Scholar Page\n.\nI come from\nTianjin\n, China, and my lovely hometown is in\nJilin\nprovince. Heading south, I spent 4 years in\nFudan University\n, Shanghai, to get my bachelor degree in Electrical Engineering. During my senior year, I visited UCSD and joined\nProfessor Nuno Vasconcelos\n’s lab doing projects on building a speed limit sign detector an Android phone.\nWe are Hiring!\nWe are hiring highly motivated interns to perform research and development in End-to-end autonomous driving. The positions are located in Shanghai, opening all-year-round. If you are interested, please contact me directly or apply through the following link:\n高级算法工程师-端到端自动驾驶/多模态大模型\n自动驾驶算法实习生-端到端大模型\n自动驾驶研发实习生-3DGS/AIGC\nExperience\n2023 - Now,\nZERON 零一汽车\n, Partner, Autonmous Driving\n2017 - 2023,\nTuSimple, Inc.\n, Director of Deep Perception\n2011 - 2017,\nUC San Diego\n, Ph.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering\n2007 - 2011,\nFudan University\n, B.S. in Electrical Engineering"
  },
