    "homepage_text": "menu\nHome\nPublication\nAwards\nActivities\nTeaching\nJie Zhou (周 杰)\nAssociate Professor\nThe School of Computer Science and Technology\nEast China Normal University\nContact\n: Shanghai, China, 200062\nRoom B702, Science Building, No. 3663, North Zhongshan Road\nEmail\n:\njzhou\n[@] cs [DOT] ecnu [DOT] edu [DOT] cn\n[\nCV\n] [\nGithub\n] \n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]\nAbout me\nDr. Zhou is an associate professor (Zijiang Youth Scholar) and Ph.D. supervisor at School of Computer Science and Technology at East China Normal University. He obtained his Ph.D. in 2021 from the School of Computer Science at East China Normal University and completed his postdoctoral research from 2021 to 2023 at Fudan NLP, the director is\nProf. Xuanjing Huang\n. He has published over 70 papers in prestigious international conferences and journals, such as AAAI, ACL, and ACM Computing Surveys, with more than 1,400 citations on Google Scholar. Dr. Zhou received the Outstanding Paper Award at COLING 2022 (as the first author), a cover paper in FITEE, and the Shanghai Science and Technology Progress Award (Second Prize, third contributor). He has also been recognized by the Sponsored by Shanghai Sailing Program and the Shanghai Super Postdoctoral Fellowship.\nResearch\nMy research interests include\nNatural Language Processing\nLarge Language Models\nContinual Learning\nSelected Publications\nRecent Advances of Foundation Language Models-based Continual Learning: A Survey\nYutao Yang,\nJie Zhou*\n, Xuanwen Ding, Tianyu Huai, Shunyu Liu, Qin Chen, Liang He, Yuan Xie\nACM Computing Survey 2024,\nIF 23.8\n. [\npdf\n] [\nGithub\n]\nEnhancing Uncertainty Modeling with Semantic Graph for Hallucination Detection\nKediChen, Qin Chen,\nJie Zhou\n, XinqiTao, dingbowen, Jingwen Xie, Mingchen Xie, Peilong Li, Zheng Feng\nAAAI 2025.\nBoosting Large Language Models with Continual Learning for Aspect-based Sentiment Analysis\nXuanwen Ding,\nJie Zhou*\n, Liang Dou, Qin Chen, Yuanbin Wu, Chengcai Chen, Liang He\nEMNLP 2024.\nFrom Individual to Society: A Survey on Social Simulation Driven by Large Language Model-based Agents\nXinyi Mou, Xuanwen Ding, Qi He, Liang Wang, Jingcong Liang, Xinnong Zhang, Libo Sun, Jiayu Lin,\nJie Zhou\n, Xuanjing Huang, Zhongyu Wei\nArxiv 2024. [\npdf\n]\nPI-Fed: Continual Federated Learning With Parameter-Level Importance Aggregation\nLang Yu, Lina Ge, Guanghui Wang, Jianghao Yin, Qin Chen,\nJie Zhou\n, Liang He\nIEEE Internet of Things Joural 2024.\nRecent Advances in Robot Navigation via Large Language Models: A Review\nHaotian Pan, Shibo Huang, Jian Yang, Jinpeng Mi, Ke Li, Xiong You, Xuan Tang, Peidong Liang, Jinbo Yang, Yingjie Liu, Jianfeng Zhang, Muyu Wang, Jie Yang, Xinyu Zhang, Lijun Zhao, Mingsong Chen,\nJie Zhou*\n, Xian Wei*\nArxiv 2024.\nMathematical language models: A survey\nWentao Liu, Hanglei Hu,\nJie Zhou*\n, Yuyang Ding, Junsong Li, Jiayi Zeng, Mengliang He, Qin Chen, Bo Jiang, Aimin Zhou*, Liang He\nArxiv 2023.\nCMM-Math: A Chinese Multimodal Math Dataset To Evaluate and Enhance the Mathematics Reasoning of Large Multimodal Models\nWentao Liu, Qianjun Pan, Yi Zhang, Zhuo Liu, Ji Wu,\nJie Zhou*\n, Aimin Zhou*, Qin Chen, Bo Jiang, Liang He\nArxiv 2024. [\npdf\n] [\nGithub\n]\nBoosting Large Language Models with Socratic Method for Conversational Mathematics Teaching\nYuyang Ding, Hanglei Hu,\nJie Zhou*\n, Qin Chen, Bo Jiang, Liang He\nCIKM 2024.\nBoosting conversational question answering with fine-grained retrieval-augmentation and self-check\nLinhao Ye, Zhikai Lei, Jianghao Yin, Qin Chen,\nJie Zhou\n, Liang He\nSIGIR 2024.\nMelo: Enhancing model editing with neuron-indexed dynamic lora\nLang Yu, Qin Chen,\nJie Zhou\n, Liang He\nAAAI 2024.\nDiaHalu: A Dialogue-level Hallucination Evaluation Benchmark for Large Language Models\nKedi Chen, Qin Chen,\nJie Zhou\n, Yishen He, Liang He\nEMNLP 2024. [\npdf\n] [\nGithub\n]\nA Multi-Format Transfer Learning Model for Event Argument Extraction via Variational Information Bottleneck\nJie Zhou\n, Qi Zhang, Qin Chen, Zhang Qi, Liang He, Xuanjing Huang\nCOLING 2022,\nOutstanding Paper\nChatGPT: potential, prospects, and limitations\nJie Zhou\n, Pei Ke, Xipeng Qiu, Minlie Huang, Junping Zhang\nFrontiers of Information Technology and Electronic Engineering\n 2023,\n封面论文\n. [\npdf\n]\nCausalABSC: Causal Inference for Aspect Debiasing in Aspect-Based Sentiment Classification\nJie Zhou\n, Yuanbiao Lin, Qin Chen, Qi Zhang, Xuanjing Huang, Liang He\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing\n 2023. [\npdf\n]\nMulti-modal multi-hop interaction network for dialogue response generation\nJie Zhou\n, Junfeng Tian, Rui Wang, Yuanbin Wu, Ming Yan, Liang He, Xuanjing Huang\nExpert Systems with Applications 2023. [\npdf\n]\nA Regularization-based Transfer Learning Method for Information Extraction via Instructed Graph Decoder\nKedi Chen,\nJie Zhou\n, Qin Chen, Shunyu Liu, Liang He\nCOLING 2024.\nLearning Intrinsic Dimension via Information Bottleneck for Explainable Aspect-based Sentiment Analysis\nZhenxiao Cheng,\nJie Zhou*\n, Wen Wu, Qin Chen, Liang He\nCOLING 2024.\nDomain Generalization via Causal Adjustment for Cross-Domain Sentiment Analysis\nSiyin Wang,\nJie Zhou*\n, Qin Chen, Qi Zhang, Tao Gui, Xuanjing Huang\nCOLING 2024.\nLet's Rectify Step by Step: Improving Aspect-based Sentiment Analysis with Diffusion Models\nShunyu Liu,\nJie Zhou*\n, Qunxi Zhu, Qin Chen, Qingchun Bai, Jun Xiao, Liang He\nCOLING 2024.\nEduchat: A large-scale language model-based chatbot system for intelligent education\nYuhao Dan, Zhikai Lei, Yiyang Gu, Yong Li, Jianghao Yin, Jiaju Lin, Linhao Ye, Zhiyan Tie, Yougen Zhou, Yilei Wang, Aimin Zhou, Ze Zhou, Qin Chen*,\nJie Zhou*\n, Liang He, Xipeng Qiu\nCCKS 2024.\nEnhancing event-level sentiment analysis with structured arguments\nQi Zhang,\nJie Zhou*\n, Qin Chen, Qingchun Bai, Liang He\nSIGIR 2022\nAn Information Minimization Based Contrastive Learning Model for Unsupervised Sentence Embeddings Learning\nShaobin Chen,\nJie Zhou\n, Yuling Sun, Liang He\nCOLING 2022\nCausal Intervention Improves Implicit Sentiment Analysis\nSiyin Wang,\nJie Zhou*\n, Changzhi Sun, Junjie Ye, Tao Gui, Qi Zhang, Xuanjing Huang\nCOLING 2022\nFarewell to Aimless Large-scale Pretraining: Influential Subset Selection for Language Model\nXiao Wang, Weikang Zhou, Qi Zhang,\nJie Zhou\n, Songyang Gao, Junzhe Wang, Menghan Zhang, Xiang Gao, Yunwen Chen, Tao Gui\nACL 2023\nA Confidence-based Partial Label Learning Model for Crowd-Annotated Named Entity Recognition\nLimao Xiong,\nJie Zhou*\n, Qunxi Zhu, Xiao Wang, Yuanbin Wu, Qi Zhang, Tao Gui, Xuanjing Huang, Jin Ma, Ying Shan\nACL 2023\nRethinkingTMSC: An Empirical Study for Target-Oriented Multimodal Sentiment Classification\nJunjie Ye,\nJie Zhou*\n, Junfeng Tian, Rui Wang, Qi Zhang, Tao Gui, Xuanjing Huang\nEMNLP 2023\nCross-modal fine-grained alignment and fusion network for multimodal aspect-based sentiment analysis\nLuwei Xiao, Xingjiao Wu, Shuwen Yang, Junjie Xu,\nJie Zhou\n, Liang He\nIPM 2023.\nSentiment-aware multimodal pre-training for multimodal sentiment analysis\nJunjie Ye,\nJie Zhou*\n, Junfeng Tian, Rui Wang, Jingyi Zhou, Tao Gui, Qi Zhang, Xuanjing Huang\nKnowledge-Based Systems 2022.\nDualGCN: An aspect-aware dual graph convolutional network for review-based recommender\nLiye Shi, Wen Wu, Wenxin Hu,\nJie Zhou\n, Jiayi Chen, Wei Zheng, Liang He\nKnowledge-Based Systems 2022.\nSk-gcn: Modeling syntax and knowledge via graph convolutional network for aspect-level sentiment classification\nJie Zhou\n, Jimmy Xiangji Huang, Qinmin Vivian Hu, Liang He\nKnowledge-Based Systems 2020.\nPosition-aware hierarchical transfer model for aspect-level sentiment classification\nJie Zhou\n, Qin Chen, Jimmy Xiangji Huang, Qinmin Vivian Hu, Liang He\nInformation Sciences 2020.\nAttending via both Fine-tuning and Compressing\nJie Zhou\n, Yuanbin Wu, Qin Chen, Xuanjing Huang, Liang He\nACL 2021\nIs “hot pizza” positive or negative? mining target-aware sentiment lexicons\nJie Zhou\n, Yuanbin Wu, Changzhi Sun, Liang He\nEACL 2021\nSentix: A sentiment-aware pre-trained model for cross-domain sentiment analysis\nJie Zhou\n, Junfeng Tian, Rui Wang, Yuanbin Wu, Wenming Xiao, Liang He\nCOLING 2021\nSNNN: promoting word sentiment and negation in neural sentiment classification\nQinmin Hu,\nJie Zhou\n, Qin Chen, Liang He\nAAAI 2018\nVisitors"
