    "github": "https://github.com/chihkuanyeh",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/chih-kuan-jason-yeh-8859378b/",
    "homepage_text": "Chih-Kuan Yeh\nSearch\nChih-Kuan Yeh\nResearch Scientist at Google Brain\nBiography\nI am a research scientist in Google Brain. During my PhD in CMU, my research interests focus on understanding and interpreting machine learning models by more objective explanations (which may be functional evaluations or theoretical properties). More recently, I am interested in building better large-scale models with less (but more efficient) data, and improving models through our understanding obtained by model explanations. Feel free to contact me if you are interested in working with me.\nInterests\nArtificial Intelligence\nMachine Learning\nExplainable AI\nAlgorithmic Game Theory\nEducation\nPhD Student in Machine Learning, 2017- 2022 (expected)\nCarnegie Mellon University\nBSc in Electrical Engineering, 2016\nNational Taiwan University\nExperience\nPhD Student\nCarnegie Mellon University Machine Learning department\nSep 2017 –\nPresent\nPennsylvania\nFocused on understanding and explaining machine learning methods working with professor Pradeep Ravikumar.\nResearch Intern\nGoogle\nJun 2019 –\nOct 2019\nCalifornia\nWorked on formalizing the ‘‘completeness’’ concept for Concept-Based explanations with Been Kim, Sercan Arik, Chun-Liang Li, and Thomas Pfister. Paper published in NeurIPS 2020.\nResearch Intern\nGoogle\nJun 2021 –\nNov 2021\nCalifornia\nWorked on Scalable Data Influence methods for NLP models with Ankur Taly, Frederick Liu, and Mukund Sundararajan. Paper submitted.\nFeatured Publications\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nAnkur Taly\n,\nMukund Sundararajan\n,\nFrederick Liu\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\nSeptember 2022\nTo appear In NeurIPS 2022\nFirst is Better than Last for Language Data Influence\nA new scalable data influence method that significantly improves upon existing methods.\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nKuan-Yun Lee\n,\nFrederick Liu\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\nApril 2022\nIn AISTATS 2022\nThreading the needle for off-manifold and on-manifold value functions for Shapley Value Explanations\nA new value function that addresses issues of on-manifold and off-manifold value functions to be used with Shapley value.\nChe-Ping Tsai\n,\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\nJanuary 2022\nIn Submission\nFaith-Shap: The faithful Shapley Interaction Index\nAn Shapley interaction index that unquely satisfies well-known axioms and the faithful criteria for explanations.\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nBeen Kim\n,\nSercan O. Arik\n,\nChun-Liang Li\n,\nTomas Pfister\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\nDecember 2020\nIn NeurIPS 2020\nOn Completeness-Aware Concept-Based Explanations in Deep Neural Networks\nDefine ``completeness'' of concepts and direct application of concepts.\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nCheng-Yu Hsieh\n,\nArun Suggala\n,\nDavid Inouye\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\nDecember 2019\nIn NeurIPS 2019\nOn the (In)fidelity and Sensitivity of Explanations\nProvides metrics for saliency methods with a unified viewpoint. Implemented in Captum (a Pytorch XAI framework).\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nJoon Sik Kim\n,\nIan En-Hsu Yen\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\nDecember 2018\nIn NeurIPS 2018\nRepresenter Point Selection for Explaining Deep Neural Networks\nDecompose test point predictions by training data with representer theorem.\nRecent Publications\nQuickly discover relevant content by\nfiltering publications\n.\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nAnkur Taly\n,\nMukund Sundararajan\n,\nFrederick Liu\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n(2022).\nFirst is Better than Last for Language Data Influence\n.\nTo appear In NeurIPS 2022.\nPDF\nCite\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nKuan-Yun Lee\n,\nFrederick Liu\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n(2022).\nThreading the needle for off-manifold and on-manifold value functions for Shapley Value Explanations\n.\nIn AISTATS 2022.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nChe-Ping Tsai\n,\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n(2022).\nFaith-Shap: The faithful Shapley Interaction Index\n.\nIn Submission.\nPDF\nCite\nCheng-Yu Hsieh\n,\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nXuanqing Liu\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n,\nSeungyeon Kim\n,\nSanjiv Kumar\n,\nCho-Jui Hsieh\n(2021).\nEvaluations and Methods for Explanation through Robustness Analysis\n.\nIn ICLR 2021.\nPDF\nCite\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nBeen Kim\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n(2021).\nHuman-Centered Concept Explanations for Neural Networks\n.\nBook Chapter In Neuro-Symbolic Artificial Intelligence– The State of the Art.\nPDF\nCite\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n(2021).\nObjective criteria for explanations of machine learning models\n.\nIn Applied AI letters 2021.\nPDF\nCite\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nBeen Kim\n,\nSercan O. Arik\n,\nChun-Liang Li\n,\nTomas Pfister\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n(2020).\nOn Completeness-Aware Concept-Based Explanations in Deep Neural Networks\n.\nIn NeurIPS 2020.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nCheng-Yu Hsieh\n,\nArun Suggala\n,\nDavid Inouye\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n(2019).\nOn the (In)fidelity and Sensitivity of Explanations\n.\nIn NeurIPS 2019.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nExternal packages\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nJianshu Chen\n,\nChengzhu Yu\n,\nDong Yu\n(2019).\nUnsupervised Speech Recognition via Segmental Empirical Output Distribution Matching\n.\nICLR 2019.\nPDF\nCite\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nJoon Sik Kim\n,\nIan En-Hsu Yen\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n(2018).\nRepresenter Point Selection for Explaining Deep Neural Networks\n.\nIn NeurIPS 2018.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nBlog\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nCheng-Yu Hsieh\n,\nHsuan-Tien Lin\n(2018).\nAutomatic Bridge Bidding Using Deep Reinforcement Learning\n.\nIn IEEE Trasaction of Games 2018 (shorter version in ECAI 2016).\nPDF\nCite\nChung-Wei Lee\n,\nWei Fang\n,\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nYu-Chiang Frank Wang\n(2018).\nMulti-Label Zero-Shot Learning With Structured Knowledge Graphs\n.\nIn CVPR 2018.\nPDF\nCite\nChih-Kuan Yeh\n,\nWei-Chieh Wu\n,\nWei-Jen Ko\n,\nYu-Chiang Frank Wang\n(2017).\nLearning Deep Latent Space for Multi-Label Classification\n.\nIn AAAI 2017.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nContact\nName\nEmail\nMessage\nDo not fill this field unless you are a bot:\nSend\njason6582(at)gmail.com\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
