    "homepage_text": "James Whittington\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJames Whittington\nPrincipal Investigator, Department of Experimental Psychology, University of Oxford\nGoogle scholar profile\nCV\nPhD Thesis\nemail: jcrwhittington at gmail dot com\ntwitter: @jcrwhittington\nNote to potential PhD applicants\nIf you are interested in pursuing a PhD (\"DPhil\") at my lab, please apply to the\nDPhil in Neuroscience\n,\nDPhil in Physiology, Anatomy and Genetics\n(focus on neuroAI),\nDPhil in Experimental Psychology\n,\nDPhil in Computer Science\n,\nInterdisciplinary Life Science (ILESLA) program\n,\nFundamentals of AI CDT\n,\nHealthcare Data Science\n(EPSRC CDT)\n,\nor a scholarship from Oxford (e.g.\nClarendon\n) or a funding body. Deadlines are early December!\nNote to\ncurrent\nmasters\nstudents / visitors who want to do a project with me\nPlease email me the following information:  1) CV; 2) Which MSc (or other) Program you are on; 3) Start and end date, incl. availability for ramp-up; 4) Research interest / Project proposals.\nProspective masters students\nIf you are interested in pursuing a\nMasters and want to work with me, please apply to the\nMSc in Neuroscience\n(with strong computational elements),\nMSc by Research in Experimental Psychology\n,\nMSc in Advanced Computer Science\n,\nMSc by Research in Engineering Science\n, or\nMSc in Clinical and Therapeutic Neuroscience\n.\nResearch Interests\nComputational/ Theoretical neuroscience, Foundations of AI, Mechanistic Interpretability / Explainability.\nNews\nI started as a Principal Investigator at the Department of Experimental Psychology at the University of Oxford.\nPublications, Preprints\n(see\ngoogle scholar\nfor updated list)\n202\n6\n\"How much neuroscience does a neuroscientist need to know?\" [\npaper\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, W Dorrell\narXiv, 2026\n202\n5\n\"Constructing future behaviour in the hippocampal formation through composition and replay\" [\npaper\n]\nJJW Bakermans, J Warren,\nJCR Whittington*\n, TEJ Behrens*\nNature Neuroscience\n, 202\n5\n\"\nRange, not Independence, Drives Modularity in Biologically Inspired Representations\n\" [\npaper\n]\nW Dorrell, K Hsu, L Hollingsworth, JH Lee, J Wu, C Finn, PE Latham, TEJ Behrens,\nJCR Whittington\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 202\n5\n\"Inferential planning in the frontal cortex\" [\npaper\n]\nF Donnarumma, T Parr, K Friston,\nJCR Whittington,\nG Pezzulo\nbioRxiv, 2025\n2024\n\"A tale of two algorithms: Structured slots explain prefrontal sequence memory and are unified with hippocampal cognitive mapsA Cellular Basis for Mapping Behavioural Structure\" [\npaper\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, W Dorrell, TEJ Behrens, S Ganguli, M El-Gaby\nN\neuron\n, 2024\n\"A Cellular Basis for Mapping Behavioural Structure\" [\npaper\n]\nM El-Gaby, AL Harris,\nJCR Whittington,\nW Dorrell, A Bhomick, MW Walton, T Akam, TEJ Behrens\nNature\n, 202\n4\n\"\nThe Zamba2 Suite: Technical Report\n\" [\npaper\n]\nP Glorioso, Q Anthony, Y Tokpanov, A Golubeva, V Shyam,\nJCR Whittington\n, J Pilault, B Millidge\narxiv\n, 2024\n\"Don't Cut Corners: Exact Conditions for Modularity in Biologically Inspired Representations\"\n[\npaper\n]\nW Dorrell, K Hsu, L Hollingsworth, JH Lee, J Wu, C Finn, PE Latham, TEJ Behrens,\nJCR Whittington\narXiv, 2024\n\"Zyda: A 1.3 T Dataset for Open Language Modeling\"\nY Tokpanov, B Millidge, P Glorioso, J Pilault, A Ibrahim,\nJCR Whittington\n, Q Anthony\narXiv, 202\n4\n\"Zamba: A Compact 7B SSM Hybrid Model\"\nP Glorioso, Q Anthony, Y Tokpanov,\nJCR Whittington\n, J Pilault, A Ibrahim, B Millidge\narXiv, 2024\n202\n3\n\"Disentanglement with Biological Constraints: A Theory of Functional Cell Types\"\n[\npaper\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, W Dorrell, S Ganguli, TEJ Behrens\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 202\n3. (Oral & Outstanding Paper Award honourable mention)\n\"Actionable Neural Representations: Grid Cells from Minimal Constraints\"\n[\npaper\n]\nW Dorrell, PE Latham, TEJ Behrens,\nJCR Whittington\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2023\n\"\nDisentanglement via latent quantization\n\" [\npaper\n]\nK Hsu, W Dorrell,\nJCR Whittington\n, J Wu, C Finn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 20\n23\n2022\n\"\nHow to build a cognitive map\n\" [\npaper\n] [\npreprint\n] [\ncode\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, D McCaffa\nr\ny, JJW Bakermans, TEJ Behrens\nNature Neurosciene\n, 202\n2\n\"Relating transformers to models and neural representations of the hippocampal formation\" [\npaper\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, J Warren, TEJ Behrens\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n, 202\n2\n\"\nReinforcement learning: Dopamine ramps with fuzzy value estimates\n\" [\npaper\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, TEJ Behrens\nCurrent Biology\n, 202\n2\n202\n1\n\"\nConstellation: Learning relational abstractions over objects for compositional imagination\n\" [\npaper\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, R Kabra, L Matthey,\nCP\nBurgess, A\nLerchner\narXiv\n, 202\n1\n2020\n\"The Tolman-Eichenbaum Machine: Unifying space and relational memory through generalisation in the hippocampal formation\" [\npaper\n]\n[\npreprint\n]\n[\ncode\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, TH Muller, S Mark, G Chen, C Barry, N Burgess, TEJ Behrens\nCell, 2020\n2019\n\"\nTheories of error back-propagation in the brain\" [\npaper\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, R Bogacz\nTrends in cognitive sciences, 2019\n2018\n\"What is a cognitive map? Organising knowledge for flexible behaviour\" [\npaper\n]\nTEJ Behrens, TH Muller,\nJCR Whittington\n, S Mark, AB Baram, KL Stachenfeld, Z Kurth-Nelson\nNeuron, 2018\n\"Generalisation of structural knowledge in the hippocampal-entorhinal system\" [\npaper\n] [\ncode\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, TH Muller, S Mark, C Barry, TEJ Behrens\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2018. (Oral)\n\"Intuitive planning: global navigation through cognitive maps based on grid-like codes\" [\npaper\n]\nAB Baram, TH Muller,\nJCR Whittington\n, TEJ Behrens\nbioRxiv, 2018\n2017\n\"An approximation of the error backpropagation algorithm in a predictive coding network with local hebbian synaptic plasticity\" [\npaper\n,\ncode\n]\nJCR Whittington\n, R Bogacz\nNeural computation, 2017\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
