    "homepage_text": "Ji Hoon Kim\n      -  Johns Hopkins University\nJohns Hopkins University Home\nSearch content at Johns Hopkins University\nView Scopus Profile\nJi Hoon Kim\nResearch Associate\nSchool of Medicine\n1997                 …\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Ji Hoon Kim is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n3\nSimilar Profiles\nActin\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n100%\nSynapse\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n61%\nDrosophilidae\nKeyphrases\n59%\nDynamics\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n58%\nCell Migration\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n39%\nCell Membrane\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n37%\nTranscription Factors\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n36%\nCell Fusion\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n32%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n13\nArticle\n3\nReview article\n1\nChapter\nThe Drosophila larval salivary gland, a simple and elegant model system to understand secretory organ development and function\nKim, J. H.\n, Shoemaker, A. M., Hutchings, K. A., Shinde, S. &\nAndrew, D. J.\n,\nFeb 2026\n,\nIn:\nCurrent Opinion in Insect Science.\n73\n, 101435.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nReview article\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nTranscription Factors\n100%\nSecretion (Process)\n100%\nOrganogenesis\n100%\nSalivary Gland\n100%\nMorphology\n50%\nArc controls organ architecture through modulation of Crb and MyoII\nKim, J. H.\n, Maruyama, R., Kim, K., Vertrees, D. A., Paul, P., Britson, K., Laughner, N. R. &\nAndrew, D. J.\n,\nSep 1 2025\n,\nIn:\nThe Journal of cell biology.\n224\n,\n9\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nMyosin\n100%\nArc Control\n100%\nCell Membrane\n33%\nSalivary Gland\n33%\nPrecursor\n16%\nHedgehog and Drosophila germ cell migration\nDeshpande, G.,\nKim, J. H.\n, Hanlon, C. D., Schedl, P. &\nAndrew, D. J.\n,\nDec 2025\n,\nIn:\nDevelopment (Cambridge).\n152\n,\n24\n, dev205291.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nReview article\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nDrosophilidae\n100%\nGerm Cells\n100%\nHedgehog\n100%\nGerm Cell Proliferation\n100%\nGerm Cell\n100%\nRibbon boosts ribosomal protein gene expression to coordinate organ form and function\nLoganathan, R., Levings, D. C.,\nKim, J.\n, Wells, M. B., Chiu, H., Wu, Y., Slattery, M. &\nAndrew, D. J.\n,\nApr 4 2022\n,\nIn:\nJournal of Cell Biology.\n221\n,\n4\n, e202110073.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nGene Expression\n100%\nCell Growth\n100%\nRibbon\n100%\nRibosomal Protein Genes\n100%\nRibosome Protein\n100%\nHedgehog signaling and Tre1 regulate actin dynamics through PI(4,5)P\n2\nto direct migration of Drosophila embryonic germ cells\nKim, J. H.\n, Hanlon, C. D., Vohra, S.,\nDevreotes, P. N.\n&\nAndrew, D. J.\n,\nMar 2 2021\n,\nIn:\nCell Reports.\n34\n,\n9\n, 108799.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nDynamics\n100%\nHedgehog Signaling Pathway\n100%\nActin\n100%\nTre1\n100%\nG Protein Coupled Receptor\n33%\nView all 17 Research outputs"
