    "homepage_text": "Jean-Baptiste Cordonnier\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\nLearning Life's Language @\nInceptive\nGeneva, Switzerland\njbcdnr@gmail.com\nCV\n•\nGithub\n•\nSemantic\n•\nTwitter\nI obtained my PhD in 2023 from\nEPFL\nunder the supervision of\nProf. Martin Jaggi\nin the laboratory of Machine\n        Learning and Optimization.\n        My research focuses on understanding attention-based models and applying transformers to different data\n        modalities.\n        I also had the chance to collaborate closely with\nAndreas Loukas\non\n        graph related topics.\n        I received my Bachelor and Master degrees in Communication Systems from EPFL and previously interned with Amazon\n        Berlin and Google Brain Berlin.\nPublications\nAttention is Not\nAll\nYou Need: Pure Attention Loses Rank Doubly Exponentially with Depth\nYihe Dong,\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\n, Andreas Loukas\nICML 2021 (long oral)\n          •\nPaper\n•\nCode\n•\nBibTex\n@article{DBLP:journals/corr/abs-2103-03404,\n  author    = {Yihe Dong and\n               Jean{-}Baptiste Cordonnier and\n               Andreas Loukas},\n  title     = {Attention is Not All You Need: Pure Attention Loses Rank Doubly Exponentially\n               with Depth},\n  journal   = {CoRR},\n  volume    = {abs/2103.03404},\n  year      = {2021},\n  url       = {https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.03404},\n  archivePrefix = {arXiv},\n}\nDifferentiable Patch Selection for Image Recognition\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\n*, Aravindh Mahendran*, Alexey Dosovitskiy, Dirk Weissenborn, Jakob Uszkoreit,\n          Thomas Unterthiner\nCVPR 2021\n          •\nPaper\n•\nCode\n•\nSlides\n•\nBibTex\n@misc{cordonnier2021differentiable,\n      title={Differentiable Patch Selection for Image Recognition},\n      author={Jean-Baptiste Cordonnier and Aravindh Mahendran and Alexey Dosovitskiy and Dirk Weissenborn and Jakob Uszkoreit and Thomas Unterthiner},\n      year={2021},\n      eprint={2104.03059},\n      archivePrefix={arXiv},\n      primaryClass={cs.CV}\n}\nGroup Equivariant Stand-Alone Self-Attention For Vision\nDavid W. Romero*,\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\n*\nICLR 2021\n          •\nPaper\n•\nCode\n•\nBibTex\n@inproceedings{\n  romero2021group,\n  title={Group Equivariant Stand-Alone Self-Attention For Vision},\n  author={David W. Romero and Jean-Baptiste Cordonnier},\n  booktitle={International Conference on Learning Representations},\n  year={2021},\n  url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=JkfYjnOEo6M}\n}\nOn the Relationship between Self-Attention and Convolutional Layers\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\n, Andreas Loukas and Martin Jaggi\nICLR 2020\n          •\nPaper\n•\nCode\n•\nBlog\n•\nExplore\n•\nSlides\n•\nBibTex\n@inproceedings{\n  cordonnier2020on,\n  title={On the Relationship between Self-Attention and Convolutional Layers},\n  author={Jean-Baptiste Cordonnier and Andreas Loukas and Martin Jaggi},\n  booktitle={International Conference on Learning Representations},\n  year={2020},\n  url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=HJlnC1rKPB}\n}\nExtrapolating Paths with Graph Neural Networks\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\nand Andreas Loukas\nIJCAI 2019\n          •\nPaper\n•\nCode\n•\nBibTex\n@inproceedings{DBLP:conf/ijcai/CordonnierL19,\n  author    = {Jean{-}Baptiste Cordonnier and\n               Andreas Loukas},\n  title     = {Extrapolating Paths with Graph Neural Networks},\n  booktitle = {Proceedings of the Twenty-Eighth International Joint Conference on\n               Artificial Intelligence, {IJCAI} 2019, Macao, China, August 10-16,\n               2019},\n  pages     = {2187--2194},\n  year      = {2019}\n}\nSparsified SGD with Memory\nSebastian U. Stich,\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\nand Martin Jaggi\nNeurIPS 2018\n          •\nPaper\n•\nPoster\n•\nCode\n•\nBibTex\n@inproceedings{DBLP:conf/nips/StichCJ18,\n    author    = {Sebastian U. Stich and\n                 Jean{-}Baptiste Cordonnier and\n                 Martin Jaggi},\n    title     = {Sparsified {SGD} with Memory},\n    booktitle = {NeurIPS},\n    pages     = {4452--4463},\n    year      = {2018}\n}\nConvex Optimization using Sparsified SGD with Memory\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\nMaster thesis EPFL\n          •\nPaper\n•\nBibTex\n@article{Cordonnier:262760,\n    title = {Convex Optimization using Sparsified Stochastic Gradient  Descent with Memory},\n    author = {Cordonnier, Jean-Baptiste},\n    pages = {49 pages},\n    year = {2018},\n    url = {http://infoscience.epfl.ch/record/262760},\n}\nProjects\nAvalanche Accidents Visualization\nJean-Baptiste Cordonnier\n, Brune Bastide and Arnaud Lesimple\nAMLD 2018\n          •\nWebsite\nBest project award in Applied Data Analysis course"
