    "homepage_text": "Vo Nguyen Le Duy\nVo Nguyen Le Duy\nHome\nResearch Group\nTeaching\nPresentations\nVo Nguyen Le Duy (Ph.D.)\n[\nGitHub\n|\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nLinkedIn\n]\nLecturer\n(a.k.a. Assistant Professor)\nUniversity of Information Technology\n,\nVietnam National University - HCM\nVisiting Scientist\nRIKEN\nCenter for Advanced Intelligence Project\nUniversity Ambassador\n/\nCertified Instructor\n(\nAI for Anomaly Detection\n)\nNVIDIA\nEmail: vo.nl.duy[\nat\n]gmail.com   or   duyvnl[\nat\n]uit.edu.vn\nResearch interests: statistical machine learning, hypothesis testing, data mining.\nI'm looking for motivated students interested in conducting research on CV and LLMs.\nIf you're interested, please reach out via\nemail\n(with CV and transcript)\n.\nNews\nOctober 2025: My students, Khoa (B4) and Nam (B3), have had their paper on\nFW-GAN: Frequency-Driven Handwriting Synthesis with Wave-Modulated MLP Generator\naccepted for publication in\nExpert Systems with Applications\n.\nSeptember 2025: My Master's students, Tung and Phuc, have had their paper on\nTowards Explainable Trajectory Classification: A Segment-Based Perturbation Approach\naccepted for publication in\nNeurocomputing\n.\nSeptember 2025: My students (B4), Tam and My, have had their paper on\nPost-Transfer Learning Statistical Inference in High-Dimensional Regression\naccepted for publication in\nStatistics and Computing\n.\nJuly 2025: My students (B2), Phu and Loc, have had their paper on\nStatistical Inference for Clustering-based Anomaly Detection\naccepted to\nStat\njournal.\nJune 2025: My students (B2), Phong and Luat, have had their paper on\nControllable RANSAC-based Anomaly Detection via Hypothesis Testing\naccepted to\nStat\njournal.\nJanuary 2025: My students (B2), Loi and Loc, have had their paper on\nStatistical Inference for Feature Selection after Optimal Transport-based Domain Adaptation\naccepted to\nAISTATS 2025\n.\nPublications\nJournal Publications\nFW-GAN: Frequency-Driven Handwriting Synthesis with Wave-Modulated MLP Generator\nPaper\nCode\nH.T.D. Khoa, D.H. Nam,\nV.N.L. Duy\nExpert Systems with Applications\n(IF in 2024 = 7.5), 2025.\nTowards Explainable Trajectory Classification: A Segment-Based Perturbation Approach\nPaper\nCode\nL.X. Tung, B.D. Phuc,\nV.N.L. Duy\nNeurocomputing\n(IF in 2024 = 6.5), 2025.\nPost-Transfer Learning Statistical Inference in High-Dimensional Regression\nPaper\nCode\nN.V.K. Tam, C.H. My,\nV.N.L. Duy\nStatistics and Computing\n(IF in 2024 = 1.6), 2025.\nStatistical Inference for the Dynamic Time Warping Distance, with Application to Abnormal Time-Series Detection\nV.N.L. Duy\n, I. Takeuchi\nAnnals of the Institute of Statistical Mathematics\n, 2025.\nPaper\nCode\nStatistical Inference for Clustering-based Anomaly Detection\nPaper\nCode\nN.T.M. Phu, D.T. Loc,\nV.N.L. Duy\nStat\n, 2025.\nControllable RANSAC-based Anomaly Detection via Hypothesis Testing\nPaper\nCode\nL.H. Phong, H.N. Luat,\nV.N.L. Duy\nStat\n, 2025.\nSelective Inference for Changepoint Detection by Recurrent Neural Network\nPaper\nCode\nT. Shiraishi, D. Miwa,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, I. Takeuchi\nNeural Computation\n, 2024.\nMulti-agent Statistical Discriminative Sub-trajectory Mining and an Application to NBA Basketball\nPaper\nCode\nR. Bunker,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, Y. Tabei, I. Takeuchi, K. Fujii\nJournal of Quantitative Analysis in Sports\n, 2024.\nBounded P-values in Parametric Programming-based Selective Inference\nPaper\nCode\nT. Shiraishi, D. Miwa,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, I. Takeuchi\nJapanese Journal of Statistics and Data Science\n, 2024.\nMore Powerful Conditional Selective Inference for Generalized Lasso by Parametric Programming\nPaper\nCode\nV.N.L. Duy\n, I. Takeuchi\nJournal of Machine Learning Research\n(\nJMLR\n), 2022.\nExact Statistical Inference for the Wasserstein Distance by Selective Inference\nPaper\nCode\nV.N.L. Duy\n, I. Takeuchi\nAnnals of the Institute of Statistical Mathematics\n(\nAISM\n), 2022.\nConditional Selective Inference for Robust Regression and Outlier Detection using Piecewise-Linear Homotopy Continuation\nPaper\nT. Tsukurimichi, Y. Inatsu,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, I. Takeuchi\nAnnals of the Institute of Statistical Mathematics\n(\nAISM\n), 2022.\nStat-DSM: Statistically Discriminative Sub-trajectory Mining with Multiple Testing Correction\nPaper\nCode\nV.N.L. Duy\n, T. Sakuma, T. Ishiyama, H. Toda, K. Arai, M. Karasuyama, Y. Okubo, M. Sunaga, H. Hanada, Y. Tabei, I. Takeuchi\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering\n(\nIEEE TKDE\n).\nConference Publications\nStatistical Inference for Feature Selection after Optimal Transport-based Domain Adaptation\nPaper\nCode\nN.T. Loi, D.T. Loc,\nV.N.L. Duy\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (\nAISTATS 2025\n).\nCAD-DA: Controllable Anomaly Detection after Domain Adaptation by Statistical Inference\nPaper\nV.N.L. Duy\n, H.-T. Lin, I. Takeuchi\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (\nAISTATS 2024\n).\nStatistical Test for Attention Map in Vision Transformer\nPaper\nCode\nT. Shiraishi, D. Miwa, T. Katsuoka,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, K. Taji, I. Takeuchi\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML 2024\n).\nValid P-Value for Deep Learning-Driven Salient Region\nPaper\nCode\nD. Miwa,\nV.N.L. Duy (co-first)\n, I. Takeuchi\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR 2023\n).\nQuantifying Statistical Significance of Neural Network-based Image\n  Segmentation by Selective Inference\nPaper\nCode\nV.N.L. Duy\n, S. Iwazaki, I. Takeuchi\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS 2022\n).\nFast and More Powerful Selective Inference for Sparse High-order Interaction Model\nPaper\nD. Das,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, H. Hanada, K. Tsuda, I. Takeuchi\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI 2022\n). Selected for\nOral\npresentation.\nMore Powerful and General Selective Inference for Stepwise Feature Selection using Homotopy Method\nPaper\nCode\nK. Sugiyama,\nV.N.L. Duy (co-first)\n, I. Takeuchi\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML 2021\n).\nParametric Programming Approach for More Powerful and General Lasso Selective Inference\nPaper\nCode\nV.N.L. Duy\n, I. Takeuchi\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (\nAISTATS 2021\n).\nComputing Valid\np\n-value for Optimal Changepoint by Selective Inference using Dynamic Programming\nV.N.L. Duy\n, H. Toda (co-first), R. Sugiyama, I. Takeuchi\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS 2020\n). Accepted as\nSpotlight, top 4.0%\n= (105+280)/9454.\nPaper\nCode\nSpotlight Talk\nPoster\nStatistically Discriminative Sub-trajectory Mining with Multiple Testing Correction\nPaper\nCode\nV.N.L. Duy\n, T. Sakuma, T. Ishiyama, H. Toda, K. Arai, M. Karasuyama, Y. Okubo, M. Sunaga, H. Hanada, Y. Tabei, I. Takeuchi\nInternational Conference on Advances in Geographic Information Systems (\nACM SIGSPATIAL 2019)\n.\nPreprints\nHTR-ConvText: Leveraging Convolution and Textual Information for Handwritten Text Recognition\nPaper\nCode\nP.T.T. Truc, D.H. Nam, H.T.D. Khoa,\nV.N.L. Duy\nArXiv, 2025\nStatistical Inference for Autoencoder-based Anomaly Detection after Representation Learning-based Domain Adaptation\nT.T. Kiet, N.T. Loi,\nV.N.L. Duy\nArXiv, 2025\nPaper\nCode\nWriteViT: Handwritten Text Generation with Vision Transformer\nPaper\nCode\nD.H. Nam, H.T.D. Khoa,\nV.N.L. Duy\nArXiv, 2025\nMulti-level Supervised Contrastive Learning\nPaper\nN. Ghanooni, B. Pajoum, H. Rawal, S. Fellenz,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, M. Kloft\nArXiv, 2025\nStatistical Inference for Sequential Feature Selection after Domain Adaptation\nPaper\nCode\nD.T. Loc, N.T. Loi,\nV.N.L. Duy\nArXiv, 2025\nAdaptive Two-Phase Finetuning LLMs for Japanese Legal Text Retrieval\nPaper\nQ.H. Trung, N.V.H. Phuc, L.T. Hoang, Q.H. Hieu,\nV.N.L. Duy\nArXiv, 2024\nStatistical Test for Generated Hypotheses by Diffusion Model\nPaper\nCode\nT. Katsuoka, T. Shiraishi, D. Miwa,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, I. Takeuchi\nArXiv, 2024\nStatistical Test for Anomaly Detections by Variational Auto-Encoders\nPaper\nCode\nD. Miwa, T. Shiraishi,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, T. Katsuoka, I. Takeuchi\nArXiv, 2024\nValid and Exact Statistical Inference for Multi-dimensional Multiple Change-Points by Selective Inference\nPaper\nR. Sugiyama, H. Toda,\nV.N.L. Duy\n, Y. Inatsu, I. Takeuchi\nArXiv, 2021\nBiography\nEducation\nApr 2020 - Dec 2022, Doctor of Engineering,\nNagoya Institute of Technology, Japan.\nSupervisors:\nAssoc. Prof. Masayuki Karasuyama\nand\nProf. Ichiro Takeuchi\nApr 2018 - Mar 2020, Master of Engineering,\nNagoya Institute of Technology, Japan.\nSupervisor:\nProf. Ichiro Takeuchi\nOct 2017 - Mar 2018, Research Student,\nNagoya Institute of Technology, Japan.\nSep 2012 - Aug 2017, Bachelor of Engineering,\nDanang University of Science and Technology, Vietnam.\nJob Experience\nSep 2023 - present, Lecturer,\nUniversity of Information Technology\n,\nVietnam National University - HCMC\n, Vietnam.\nJan 2024 - present, Visiting Scientist,\nRIKEN\n, Japan.\nSep 2024, Visiting Scholar,\nMachine Learning Group\n,\nUniversity of Kaiserslautern-Landau (RPTU)\n, Germany.\nJan 2023 - Dec 2023, Postdoctoral Researcher,\nRIKEN\n, Japan.\nApr 2023 - Dec 2023, Visiting Researcher,\nNagoya University\n, Japan.\nJune 2023, Exchange Faculty,\nComputational Learning Lab\n,\nNational Taiwan University\n, Taiwan.\nApr 2020 - Dec 2022, Junior Research Associate,\nRIKEN\n, Japan.\nOthers\nResearch Grants\nOct 2024 - Sep 2025, VinIF Domestic Postdoctoral Fellowship Program (PI)\nAug 2023 - Mar 2025, RIKEN Incentive Research Projects (2,910,000 JPY, PI)\nJun 2023 - Mar 2024, JST AIP Challenge (1,000,000 JPY, PI)\nProfessional Activities\nReviewer, Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n2023, 2024, 2025)\nReviewer, International Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n2024, 2025)\nReviewer, International Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n2025, 2026)\nReviewer, International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (\nAISTATS\n2024, 2026)\nReviewer, AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n2026)\nReviewer, Asian Conference on Machine Learning (ACML 2024, 2025)\nReviewer, Transactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR 2024, 2025)\nReviewer, Statistics and Computing (2023, 2025)\nReviewer, Journal of Statistical Computation and Simulation (JSCS 2023)\nReviewer, Stat (2023)"
