    "homepage_text": "Chang-Su Kim\n      -  Korea University Pure\nKorea University Pure Home\nSearch content at Korea University Pure\nView Scopus Profile\nChang-Su Kim\nProfessor\nSchool of Electrical Engineering\nCenter for Artificial Intelligence Research\n* World 2% Researchers\nRobotics & Autonomous Driving\nVision & Perception\nLearning & Reasoning\nManufacturing & AI\nHealthcare & AI\nEmail\nchangsukim\nkorea.ac\nkr\nh-index\n8575\nCitations\n44\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n1995                 …\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Chang-Su Kim is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nExperimental Result\nComputer Science\n100%\nSimulation Result\nEngineering\n61%\nVideo Sequences\nComputer Science\n58%\nConventional Algorithm\nComputer Science\n44%\nEncoder\nKeyphrases\n31%\nDecoder\nKeyphrases\n26%\nContrast Enhancement\nKeyphrases\n24%\nVideo Transmission\nComputer Science\n24%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n171\nConference contribution\n112\nArticle\n34\nConference article\n14\nPaper\n3\nMore\n1\nChapter\n1\nEditorial\n1\nReview article\nLUTFormer: Lookup table transformer for image enhancement\nKo, J., Ko, K., Kim, H. &\nKim, C. S.\n,\n2026 Jan 7\n,\nIn:\nNeurocomputing.\n660\n, 131863.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nLookup Table\n100%\nImage Enhancement\n100%\n3D Lookup Table\n50%\nStructured Query\n50%\nMultilevel Image\n50%\nContour-based object forecasting for autonomous driving\nJang, J., Kim, D., Jin, D. &\nKim, C. S.\n,\n2025 Feb\n,\nIn:\nJournal of Visual Communication and Image Representation.\n106\n, 104343.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nAutonomous Driving\n100%\nFuture Frame\n100%\n3D Rendering\n66%\nExperimental Result\n50%\nDepth Estimation\n50%\n4\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nError-Mask-Adaptive Dynamic Filtering for Image Inpainting\nKo, K., Woo, S. &\nKim, C. S.\n,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nIEEE Access.\n13\n,\np. 18403-18417\n15 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nDynamic Filter\n100%\nAdaptive Dynamics\n100%\nImage Inpainting\n100%\nVarying Filter\n100%\nFilter Layer\n33%\nFlow-Guided Consistent Video Depth Estimation for Cross-Dataset Generalization\nJang, J. &\nKim, C. S.\n,\n2025\n,\n2025 Asia Pacific Signal and Information Processing Association Annual Summit and Conference, APSIPA ASC 2025.\nInstitute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.\n,\np. 2270-2275\n6 p.\n(2025 Asia Pacific Signal and Information Processing Association Annual Summit and Conference, APSIPA ASC 2025).\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nConference contribution\nForbes: Face Obfuscation Rendering via Backpropagation Refinement Scheme\nKim, J., Yang, S., Jeong, S. G. &\nKim, C. S.\n,\n2025\n,\nComputer Vision – ECCV 2024 - 18th European Conference, Proceedings.\nLeonardis, A., Ricci, E., Roth, S., Russakovsky, O., Sattler, T. & Varol, G. (eds.).\nSpringer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH\n,\np. 54-70\n17 p.\n(Lecture Notes in Computer Science (including subseries Lecture Notes in Artificial Intelligence and Lecture Notes in Bioinformatics); vol. 15127 LNCS).\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nConference contribution\nObfuscation\n100%\nFace Obfuscation\n100%\nExperimental Result\n50%\nIdentity Information\n50%\nFacial Appearance\n50%\nView all 334 research outputs\nPress/Media\nStudy Results from Kyonggi University Update Understanding of Engineering (Vit-core Plus : Lightweight Anomaly Detection Using Cut-paste and Transformer-based Feature Extractor)\nKim, C.-S.\n&\nKim, C.-H.\n26/3/4\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\n:\nPress / Media\nKyonggi University Researchers Describe Research in Engineering (ViT-Core+: Lightweight Anomaly Detection Using Cut-Paste and Transformer-Based Feature Extractor)\nKim, C.-S.\n&\nKim, C.-H.\n25/10/30\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\n:\nPress / Media\nMajor Korean law firms shift hiring from prosecutors to antitrust and labor experts\nKim, C.-S.\n&\nLee, I.\n25/10/10\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\n:\nPress / Media\nResearchers at Catholic University of Korea Have Published New Study Findings on Engineering (Error-Mask-Adaptive Dynamic Filtering for Image Inpainting)\nKim, C.-S.\n25/2/17\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\n:\nPress / Media\nResearchers at Pai Chai University Zero in on Engineering (A FSTCN-Based Leak Detection Method for Large-Scale Pipeline Transportation Systems)\nKim, C.-S.\n25/1/16\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\n:\nPress / Media\nView all 37 press/media"
