    "homepage_text": "Yonglong Tian\nYonglong Tian\nemail\n/\nscholar\n/\ntwitter\n/\ngithub\nBased in Cambridge, I am an Artificial Intelligence researcher at Google DeepMind. My main research interests lie in the intersection of machine perception, generation and reasoning, mainly from the perspective of vision.\nPrior to that, I obtained my Ph.D. from MIT EECS in 2022, advised by\nPhillip Isola\n. Before that, I completed my M.Phil degree at CUHK, advised by\nXiaoou Tang\nand\nXiaogang Wang\n, and attended Tsinghua University for undergrad.\nRecent 5 Papers\nAutoregressive Image Generation without Vector Quantization\nTianhong Li,\nYonglong Tian\n, He Li, Mingyang Deng, Kaiming He\narXiv 2024\nSelf-Correcting Self-Consuming Loops for Generative Model Training\nNate Gillman, Michael Freeman, Daksh Aggarwal, Chia-Hong Hsu, Calvin Luo,\nYonglong Tian\n, Chen Sun\nICML 2024\nDenoising Vision Transformers\nJiawei Yang, Katie Z Luo, Jiefeng Li, Kilian Q Weinberger,\nYonglong Tian\n, Yue Wang\narXiv 2024\nLearning Vision from Models Rivals Learning Vision from Data\nYonglong Tian\n*, Lijie Fan*, Kaifeng Chen, Dina Katabi, Dilip Krishnan, Phillip Isola\nCVPR 2024\nScaling Laws of Synthetic Images for Model Training ... for Now\nLijie Fan*, Kaifeng Chen, Dilip Krishnan, Dina Katabi, Phillip Isola,\nYonglong Tian\n*,\nCVPR 2024\nGem stolen from\nhere"
  },
