    "homepage_text": "Yisen Wang @ Peking University\nYisen Wang\nSchool of Intelligence Science and Technology\nPeking University\nEmail: yisen.wang AT pku DOT edu.cn\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]\n[\nGithub\n]\n[\nPKU Homepage\n]\n[\nStudents\n]\n[\nRecruitment Instructions\n]\nResearch Topics\nTheory of Learning Paradigm\nAI Safety\nReasoning in LLMs\nGraph Learning\nI am now a Tenure-track Assistant Professor (Ph.D. Advisor) at\nPeking University\n.\n              I am also a faculty member of\nZERO Lab\nled by\nProf. Zhouchen Lin\n.\n              I got my Ph.D. degree from\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\n,\nTsinghua University\n.\n              I have visited\nGeorgia Tech\n, USA, hosted by\nProf. Le Song\nand\nProf. Hongyuan Zha\n, and\nThe University of Melbourne\n, Australia, hosted by\nProf. James Bailey\n.\nMy research centers on\nRepresentation Learning\n, with a focus on deriving meaningful and robust representations from diverse data types--including unlabeled, noisy, and adversarial data--grounded in principled and theoretically driven methodologies.\n              Specifically, we recently focus on\nTheoretical and Algorithmic Foundations of LLMs\n(e.g., Self-Supervised/Weakly-Supervised Learning, In-context Learning, Reinforcement Learning, and Reasoning) and\nAI Safety\n(ensuring Trustworthy and Reliable AI Systems).\nWe have received the\nBest Paper Award\nof ECML-PKDD 2021\n,\nBest Paper Award\nof NeurIPS 2025 Workshop\n,\nBest Paper Award\nof ICML 2024 Workshop\n,\nSilver Best Paper Award\nof ICML 2021 Workshop\n,\nBest Paper Runner-Up Award\nof ICLR 2025 Workshop\n,\n1st Place\nin the CVPR 2021 Adversarial Competitions\n, and\nChampion\nin the 2020 GeekPwn CAAD Competitions\n.\nOpenings\nWe are always actively recruiting highly motivated Postdocs, Ph.D. students and Interns! For Prospective applicants, please read this\nInstructions\nfor recruiting information, and\nCSRankings\nfor ranking information!\nNews\n2025.8, We will give a tutorial on the\nPrinciples of Self-supervised Learning in the Foundation Model Era\nat IJCAI 2025.\n2024.12, My PhD student won the CAA Outstanding Ph.D. Dissertation Award!\n2024.6, We released\nInterpretable Self-Supervised Learning Library\nto cover all interpretable-related algorithms of our group!\n2024.5, We released\nTrustworthy Machine Learning Library\nto cover all trustworthy-related algorithms of our group!\n2024.4, Our jailbreaking work (\nIn-context Attack\n) has been featured and scaled up by\nAnthropic\n(Claude 3 Group)!\n2024.3, My PhD student won the CAAI Outstanding Ph.D. Dissertation Runner-Up Award!\nPublications \n                (\nRecent\n/\nSelected\n/\nAll by date\n/\nAll by topic\n)\n(* Equal  Contribution and # Corresponding  Author)\nAn Augmentation Overlap Theory of Contrastive Learning\nQi Zhang, Yifei Wang,\nYisen Wang#\nJMLR 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nArxiv\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@article{zhangjmlr2025,\n                          author  = {Qi Zhang and Yifei Wang and Yisen Wang},\n                          title   = {An Augmentation Overlap Theory of Contrastive Learning},\n                          journal = {Journal of Machine Learning Research},\n                          year    = {2025},\n                          volume  = {26},\n                          number  = {228},\n                          pages   = {1--42}\n                        }\nJailbreak and Guard Aligned Language Models with Only Few In-Context Demonstrations\nZeming Wei, Yifei Wang, Ang Li, Yichuan Mo,\nYisen Wang#\nTPAMI 2026\n(Featured and Scaled up by Anthropic)\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nAnthropic Blog\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@article{wei2023jailbreak,\n                        title={Jailbreak and Guard Aligned Language Models with Only Few In-Context Demonstrations},\n                        author={Wei, Zeming and Wang, Yifei and Wang, Yisen},\n                        journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2310.06387},\n                        year={2023}\n                      }\nOn the Adversarial Transferability of Generalized \"Skip Connections\"\nYisen Wang\n, Yichuan Mo, Dongxian Wu, Mingjie Li, Xingjun Ma, Zhouchen Lin\nTPAMI 2026\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nDifficult Examples Hurt Unsupervised Contrastive Learning: A Theoretical Perspective\nYige Zhang, Jingyi Cui, Qiran Li,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2026\n(Oral, Top 1.2%)\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nWhen More is Less: Understanding Chain-of-Thought Length in LLMs\nYuyang Wu, Yifei Wang, Tianqi Du, Stefanie Jegelka,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2026\n(ICLR 2025 Workshop Best Paper Runner-up)\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nAutoregressive Models Rival Diffusion Models at ANY-ORDER Generation\nTianqi Du, Lizhe Fang, Weijie Yang, Chenheng Zhang, Zeming Wei, Yifei Wang,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2026\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nOn the Limits of Sparse Autoencoders: A Theoretical Framework and Reweighted Remedy\nJingyi Cui, Qi Zhang, Yifei Wang,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2026\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nG1: Teaching LLMs to Reason on Graphs with Reinforcement Learning\nXiaojun Guo, Ang Li, Yifei Wang, Stefanie Jegelka,\nYisen Wang#\nNeurIPS 2025\n(Best Paper Award at NeurIPS 2025 Workshop)\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@inproceedings{guo2025g1,\n                            title={G1: Teaching llms to reason on graphs with reinforcement learning},\n                            author={Guo, Xiaojun and Li, Ang and Wang, Yifei and Jegelka, Stefanie and Wang, Yisen},\n                            booktitle={NeurIPS},\n                            year={2025}\n                          }\nLanguage Ranker: A Lightweight Ranking framework for LLM Decoding\nChenheng Zhang, Tianqi Du, Jizhe Zhang, Mingqing Xiao, Yifei Wang,\nYisen Wang#\n, Zhouchen Lin#\nNeurIPS 2025\n(Beyond Reward Models: Efficient LLM Decoding with Lightweight Reranking)\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nFinding and Reactivating Post-Trained LLMs' Hidden Safety Mechanisms\nMingjie Li, Wai Man Si, Michael Backes, Yang Zhang,\nYisen Wang#\nNeurIPS 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nAre Smarter LLMs Safer? Exploring Safety-Reasoning Trade-offs in Prompting and Fine-Tuning\nAng Li, Yichuan Mo, Mingjie Li, Yifei Wang,\nYisen Wang#\nPreprint\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@article{li2025smarter,\n                            title={Are Smarter LLMs Safer? Exploring Safety-Reasoning Trade-offs in Prompting and Fine-Tuning},\n                            author={Li, Ang and Mo, Yichuan and Li, Mingjie and Wang, Yifei and Wang, Yisen},\n                            journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2502.09673},\n                            year={2025}\n                          }\nLong-Short Alignment for Effective Long-Context Modeling in LLMs\nTianqi Du, Haotian Huang, Yifei Wang,\nYisen Wang#\nICML 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nAn Augmentation-Aware Theory for Self-Supervised Contrastive Learning\nJingyi Cui, Hongwei Wen,\nYisen Wang#\nICML 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nIdentifying and Understanding Cross-Class Features in Adversarial Training\nZeming Wei, Yiwen Guo,\nYisen Wang#\nICML 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nIncorporating Arbitrary Matrix Group Equivariance into KANs\nLexiang Hu,\nYisen Wang\n, Zhouchen Lin#\nICML 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\nWhat is Wrong with Perplexity for Long-context Language Modeling?\nLizhe Fang, Yifei Wang, Zhaoyang Liu, Chenheng Zhang, Stefanie Jegelka, Jinyang Gao, Bolin Ding,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2025\n(New Reliable Metric for Long-context LLMs)\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nArxiv\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@inproceedings{fang2025what,\n                            title={What is Wrong with Perplexity for Long-context Language Modeling?},\n                            author={Lizhe Fang and Yifei Wang and Zhaoyang Liu and Chenheng Zhang and Stefanie Jegelka and Jinyang Gao and Bolin Ding and Yisen Wang},\n                            booktitle={ICLR},\n                            year={2025}\n                            }\nRethinking Invariance in In-context Learning\nLizhe Fang, Yifei Wang, Khashayar Gatmiry, Lei Fang,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@inproceedings{fang2025rethinking,\n                          title={Rethinking Invariance in In-context Learning},\n                          author={Lizhe Fang and Yifei Wang and Khashayar Gatmiry and Lei Fang and Yisen Wang},\n                          booktitle={ICLR},\n                          year={2025}\n                          }\nCan In-context Learning Really Generalize to Out-of-distribution Tasks?\nQixun Wang, Yifei Wang, Xianghua Ying#,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@inproceedings{wang2025can,\n                          title={Can In-context Learning Really Generalize to Out-of-distribution Tasks?},\n                          author={Qixun Wang and Yifei Wang and Xianghua Ying and Yisen Wang},\n                          booktitle={ICLR},\n                          year={2025}\n                          }\nProjection Head is Secretly an Information Bottleneck\nZhuo Ouyang, Kaiwen Hu, Qi Zhang, Yifei Wang,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@inproceedings{ouyang2025projection,\n                            title={Projection Head is Secretly an Information Bottleneck},\n                            author={Zhuo Ouyang and Kaiwen Hu and Qi Zhang and Yifei Wang and Yisen Wang},\n                            booktitle={ICLR},\n                            year={2025}\n                            }\nSaLoRA: Safety-Alignment Preserved Low-Rank Adaptation\nMingjie Li, Wai Man Si, Michael Backes, Yang Zhang,\nYisen Wang#\nICLR 2025\n[\nPDF\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nBib\n]\n@inproceedings{li2025salora,\n                            title={SaLo{RA}: Safety-Alignment Preserved Low-Ra...[truncated]"
