  "serper::Lei Feng": {
    "homepage": "https://lfeng1995.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "lfengqaq@gmail.com",
      "fenglei@seu.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Lei Feng\nLei Feng\nHome\nPublications\nProfessional Services\nCode & Data\nNews\nHome\nLei Feng (冯磊)\nProfessor\n@\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering, Southeast University, China\n[Google Scholar Profile]\n[官方主页]\nE-mail: fenglei@seu.edu.cn, lfengqaq@gmail.com (for review invitation)\nOpenings: I am also looking for highly motivated postdoctoral research fellows.\nPlease drop me an email if you are interested.\nBrief Biography\nI am a Full Professor at\nPALM Lab\n,\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering, Southeast University, China\n. I am also affiliated with RIKEN Center for Advanced Intelligence Project, as a Visiting Scientist (part-time). I earned my PhD degree from Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. My main research interests lie in machine learning, data mining, and statistics, with a particular emphasis on addressing various security/reliability/robustness/privacy issues faced by multimodal large language models and AI agents.\nTop News\n[Dec 2025] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for IJCAI'26.\n[Nov 2025] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for ICML'26.\n[Aug 2025] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for ICLR'26.\n[Jun 2025] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for AAAI'26.\n[Feb 2025] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS'25.\n[Dec 2024] Invited to serve as an Action Editor for Neural Networks.\n[Dec 2024] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for ICML'25.\n[Dec 2024] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for IJCAI'25.\n[Nov 2024] Invited to serve as an Action Editor for TMLR.\n[Aug 2024] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for ICLR'24.\n[Jun 2024] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS'24 Datasets and Benchmarks Track.\n[Mar 2024] Invited to serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS'24.\nSee more news\nhere\n.\nEducation\nPh.D.\nin Computer Science. Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (Aug 2017 - Dec 2020)\nSubmitted thesis in Aug 2020, left NTU in Dec 2020, defended thesis in Jan 2021, received degree in Feb 2021.\nNTU SCSE Outstanding PhD Thesis Award Runner-Up (in the situation of early graduation). Supervised by\nProf. Bo An\n.\nB.E.\nin Computer Science. Southwest University, Chongqing, China (Sep 2013 - Jul 2017)\nOutstanding Graduate of Southwest University.\nHonors & Awards\n[2024] WAIC 2024 Youth Outstanding Paper Nomination Award.\n[2024] Asia-Pacific Leaders Under 30 in 2024.\n[2022] Forbes 30 Under 30 Asia.\n[2022] Champion in the Learning and Mining with Noisy Labels Challenge at IJCAI-ECAI 2022.\n[2022] Chongqing Youth Pioneer in Science and Technology Innovation.\n[2022] ICLR 2022 Outstanding Paper Award Honorable Mention.\n[2021] Forbes 30 Under 30 China.\n[2021] NTU SCSE Outstanding PhD Thesis Award Runner-up (in the situation of early graduation)."
  },
