  "serper::Qianqian Xu": {
    "homepage": "https://qianqianxu010.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "xuqianqian@ict.ac.cn"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/qianqianxu010",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Qianqian Xu's Homepage – Professor at ICT, CAS\nQianqian Xu's Homepage\nProfessor at ICT, CAS\nWelcome\nWelcome\nHi! Welcome to my homepage. I’m\nQianqian Xu (许倩倩)\n, a Professor with the Institute of Computing Technology (ICT), Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS). I received the Ph.D degree from the University of Chinese Academy of Sciences (UCAS) under the supervision of Prof.\nQingming Huang\n(Professor at UCAS, IEEE Fellow) in 2013. After that, I was a Postdoctoral Fellow in BICMR, Peking University, under the supervision of Prof.\nYuan Yao\n(Professor at HKUST). During 2011, I have studied in the School of Computer Science and Engineering, Nanyang Technological University, under the supervision of Prof.\nWeisi Lin\n(Professor at NTU, IEEE Fellow). I am also lucky to have opportunities to collaborate with\nShuqiang Jiang\n(Professor at CAS),\nZhipeng Wu\n(Research Fellow at APPLE, Japan),\nTingting Jiang\n(Professor at PKU),\nJiechao Xiong\n(Research Fellow at Tencent Lab AI Lab),\nXiaochun Cao\n(Professor at CAS),\nMing Yan\n(Professor at MSU),\nXi Chen\n(Professor at NYU), and\nBraxton Osting\n(Professor at UTAH),\netc\n.\nMy research interests include statistical machine learning, with applications in multimedia and computer vision. It has been my good fortune to have the chances to work with many colleagues and students in various organizations.\nInternship and Graduate Students Opening\n: I am looking for self-motivated candidates who have solid mathematical backgrounds, strong English ability, and strong coding skills. If you are interested in doing research on Multimedia, Computer Vision and Machine Learning, please send detailed CV to me.\nRecent News\nNEW\n2026.2\n: Six papers are accepted by CVPR’26\nNEW\n2026.1\n: One paper is accepted by IEEE TPAMI\nNEW\n2025.12\n: Two papers are accepted by IEEE TPAMI\n2025.11\n: One paper is accepted by IEEE TPAMI\n2025.11\n: Three papers are accepted by AAAI’26\n2025.09\n: Two papers are accepted by NeurIPS’25\n2025.09\n: Three papers are accepted by IEEE TPAMI\nEducation\nSep. 2009 – Jun. 2013, Ph.D. in Computer Application, University of Chinese Academy of Sciences\nSep. 2007 – Aug. 2009, M. Eng. in Computer Application, University of Chinese Academy of Sciences\nSep. 2003 – Jul. 2007, B. Eng. in Electronic Information Science and Technology, China University of Mining and Technology\nProfessional Experience\nOct. 2022 – Present, Professor in Institute of Computing Technology, CAS\nMar. 2018 – Oct. 2022, Associate Professor in Institute of Computing Technology, CAS\nOct. 2015 – Mar. 2018, Associate Professor in Institute of Information Engineering, CAS\nJul. 2015 – Oct. 2015, Assistant Professor in Institute of Information Engineering, CAS\nJul. 2013 – Jul. 2015, Postdoctor in Beijing International Center for Mathematical Research, Peking University\nQianqian Xu\nProfessor,\nInstitute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nGitHub\nE-Mail\nGoogleScholar\nDBLP"
  },
