    "github": "https://github.com/claw-eval",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Tong Yang | Homepage\nWelcome to Tong Yang's Homepage\nHomepage\nTalks\nNews!\nPhotos!\nTong Yang\nTong Yang (杨仝) (\nGoogle Scholar\n) received his PHD degree in Computer Science from Tsinghua University in 2013. He visited Institute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS) China from 2013.7 to 2014.7. Now he is an associate professor in School of Computer Science, Peking University.\nResearch Area\n: LLM, New Data Structures in Network Measurement, Databases, Data Mining, Machine Learning, and etc.\n实验室长期招收本校及外校优秀本科生进行科研实习。同时常年招聘博士后研究人员。每年均有硕士与博士研究生名额，尤其硕士名额较多，欢迎联系申请！\nEmail:\nyangtongemail@gmail.com\nNews:\n03/2026\n: 研究团队开源\nClawEval\n—— 首个面向\nOpenClaw\n场景、\n真实可复现\n的智能体测评框架。该框架在\n15 个模拟企业服务\n及真实 Web/终端环境中构建端到端评测，支持\n错误注入\n、\nDocker 沙箱复现\n与\nJSONL Trace 全链路回放\n，覆盖\n104 个任务\n、\n7 大类别\n，并同步开源代码、榜单及\n100+ 中英测试用例\n，为真实世界 Agent 能力评估提供透明基准。\n[GitHub链接]\n[榜单链接]\n[新闻链接]\n02/2026\n: 研究团队发布\nAgentRob\n—— 首个基于\nMCP\n打通\n在线论坛—LLM 智能体—真实机器人\n的框架：用户论坛\n@\n即可触发指令理解、规划执行与回帖汇报的\n全自动闭环\n，支持\n多形态机器人协作\n并具备权限与安全机制。\n[论文链接]\n[GitHub链接]\n[新闻链接]\n12/2025\n: 研究团队提出通用极低比特量化框架\nFairy2i\n—— 在\n无需重新预训练\n的前提下，将实数大模型无损转换为复数形式，并结合\n相位感知量化\n与\n递归残差量化\n，实现\n2-bit 性能逼近 FP16\n、显著优于现有 2-bit/3-bit 方法，使通用大模型在手机等边缘设备上也能\n流畅运行\n。\n[GitHub链接]\n[模型链接]\n[论文链接]\n09/2025\n: 联合360研究团队发布\nTinyR1-32B\n模型——以仅\n20k\n数据实现\n安全性能里程碑式突破\n：超同尺寸 Qwen3-32B\n25分\n、超 DeepSeek-R1-0528\n17分\n，推理性能达后者的\n93%\n；提出\nControl Token\n动态安全控制，打破安全与可用二选一困境，同步推出轻量安全模型\nTinyR1-Safety-8B\n。\n[模型链接-32B]\n[模型链接-8B]\n[新闻链接]\n08/2025\n: 研究团队发布\niFairy\n——首个将全部参数约束在 {±1, ±i} 的\n2-bit 复数量化大模型\n，实现\n无乘法、仅加法\n的高效推理与约\n1/8\n存储压缩，并在语言建模与下游任务上\n超越同尺寸全精度 LLaMA\n；相关论文及代码全面开源，进一步\n为低功耗与边缘部署提供新路径\n。\n[GitHub链接]\n[模型链接]\n[论文链接]\n[新闻链接]\n[报告视频]\n08/2025\n: 研究团队发布\nProof2Hybrid\n，为\n首个全自动数学基准合成架构\n。该架构以\n多大语言模型流水线\n为核心，实现数学评测集的自动、高效构建；并据此推出\n首个专注于代数几何领域\n的基准\nAlgGeoTest\n。\n[论文链接]\n[数据集链接]\n07/2025\n: 受邀担任\nCCF Computility 2025 “智算集群创新与实践” 论坛主席\n，论坛将于2025年7月在甘肃兰州举行，聚焦大模型训练推理中的智算基础设施发展与挑战。\n[链接]\n06/2025\n: 研究团队发布\nScholarSearch\n数据集，为\n首个专注于评估大语言模型在学术研究中复杂信息检索能力的基准\n。结果显示，即便是最强搜索增强模型 GPT-4o-search-preview 的准确率也仅为 18.83%。\n[论文链接]\n[数据集链接]\n05/2025\n: 研究团队发布\nFairyR1-32B\n模型，采用“分合蒸馏”思路，实现在\n仅 5% 参数量下，数学与代码能力超越 DeepSeek-R1 满血版\n，充分探索在有限资源下实现高性能模型的可行性。\n[模型链接]\nResearch:\nPreprint Papers\nWenrui Liu, Yaxuan Wang, Xun Zhang, Yanshu Wang, Jiashen Wei, Yifan Xiang, Yuhang Wang, Mingshen Ye, Elsie Dai, Zhiqi Liu, Yingjie Xu, Xinyang Chen, Hengzhe Sun, Jiyu Shen, Jingjing He,\nTong Yang\n. AgentRob: From Virtual Forum Agents to Hijacked Physical Robots.\narxiv preprint 2026.\nLink\nJunting Zhou, Jin Chen, Linfeng Hao, Denghui Cao, Zheyu Wang, Qiguang Chen, Chaoyou Fu, Jiaze Chen, Yuchen Wu, Ge Zhang, Mingxuan Wang, Wenhao Huang,\nTong Yang\n. BABE: Biology Arena BEnchmark.\narxiv preprint 2026.\nLink\nWenrui Liu, Zixiang Liu, Elsie Dai, Wenhan Yu, Lei Yu,\nTong Yang\n, Jinjun Han, Hong Gao. MCPAgentBench: A Real-world Task Benchmark for Evaluating LLM Agent MCP Tool Use.\narxiv preprint 2026.\nLink\nZehua Zhao, Zhixian Huang, Junren Li, Siyu Lin, Junting Zhou, Fengqi Cao, Kun Zhou, Rui Ge, Tingting Long, Yuexiang Zhu, Yan Liu, Jie Zheng, Junnian Wei, Rong Zhu, Peng Zou, Wenyu Li, Zekai Cheng, Tian Ding, Yaxuan Wang, Yizhao Yan, Tingru Wei, Haowei Ming, Weijie Mao, Chen Sun, Yiming Liu, Zichen Wang, Zuo Zhang,\nTong Yang\n, Hao Ma, Zhen Gao, Jian Pei. SUPERChem: A Multimodal Reasoning Benchmark in Chemistry.\narxiv preprint 2025.\nLink\nFeiyu Wang, Xinyu Tan, Bokai Huang, Yihao Zhang, Guoan Wang, Peizhuang Cong,\nTong Yang\n. Fairy2i: Training Complex LLMs from Real LLMs with All Parameters in {±1,±i}.\narxiv preprint 2025.\nLink\nYuemeng Xu, Haoran Chen, Jiarui Guo, Mingwei Cui, Qiuheng Yin, Cheng Dong, Daxiang Kang, Xian Wu, Chenmin Sun, Peng He, Yang Gao, Lirong Lai, Kai Wang, Hongyu Wu,\nTong Yang\n, Xiyun Xu. Zephyrus: Scaling Gateways Beyond the Petabit-Era with DPU-Augmented Hierarchical Co-Offloading.\narxiv preprint 2025.\nLink\nLiya Zhu, Peizhuang Cong, Aowei Ji, Wenya Wu, Jiani Hou, Chunjie Wu, Xiang Gao, Jingkai Liu, Zhou Huan, Xuelei Sun, Yang Yang, Jianpeng Jiao, Liang Hu, Xinjie Chen, Jiashuo Liu, Jingzhe Ding,\nTong Yang\n, Zaiyuan Wang, Ge Zhang, Wenhao Huang. LPFQA: A Long-Tail Professional Forum-based Benchmark for LLM Evaluation.\narxiv preprint 2025.\nLink\nTongxuan Liu, Tao Peng, Peijun Yang, Xiaoyang Zhao, ... , Zirui Liu, Yanshu Wang,\nTong Yang\n, et al. xLLM Technical Report.\narxiv preprint 2025.\nLink\n|\nPDF Download\nFeiyu Wang, Guoan Wang, Yihao Zhang, Shengfan Wang, Weitao Li, Bokai Huang, Shimao Chen, Zihan Jiang, Rui Xu,\nTong Yang\n. iFairy: the First 2-bit Complex LLM with All Parameters in {±1, ±i}.\narxiv preprint 2025.\nLink\n|\nVideo(中文讲解)\nLin Sun, Guangxiang Zhao, Xiaoqi Jian, Yuhan Wu, Weihong Lin, Yongfu Zhu, Change Jia, Linglin Zhang, Jinzhu Wu, Junfeng Ran, Sai-er Hu, Zihan Jiang, Junting Zhou, Wenrui Liu, Bin Cui,\nTong Yang\n, Xiangzheng Zhang. TinyR1-32B-Preview: Boosting Accuracy with Branch-Merge Distillation.\narxiv preprint 2025.\nLink\n|\nPDF Download\nGuoqi Yu, Yaoming Li, Xiaoyu Guo, Dayu Wang, Zirui Liu, Shujun Wang,\nTong Yang\n. LiNo: Advancing Recursive Residual Decomposition of Linear and Nonlinear Patterns for Robust Time Series Forecasting.\narxiv preprint 2024.\nLink\nShimao Chen, Zirui Liu, Zhiying Wu, Ce Zheng, Peizhuang Cong, Zihan Jiang, Yuhan Wu, Lei Su,\nTong Yang\n. INT-FlashAttention: Enabling Flash Attention for INT8 Quantization.\narxiv preprint 2024.\nLink\nYanshu Wang, Wenyang He,\nTong Yang\n. Athena: Efficient Block-Wise Post-Training Quantization for Large Language Models Using Second-Order Matrix Derivative Information.\narxiv preprint 2024.\nLink\nYanshu Wang, Wang Li, Zhaoqian Yao,\nTong Yang\n. QET: Enhancing Quantized LLM Parameters and KV cache Compression through Element Substitution and Residual Clustering.\narxiv preprint 2024.\nLink\nYanshu Wang,\nTong Yang\n, Xiyan Liang, Guoren Wang, Hanning Lu, Zhe Xu, Yaoming Li, Weitao Li. Art and Science of Quantizing Large-Scale Models: A Comprehensive Overview.\narxiv preprint 2024.\nLink\nPeizhuang Cong, Aomufei Yuan, Shimao Chen, Yuxuan Tian, Bowen Ye,\nTong Yang\n. Prediction Is All MoE Needs: Expert Load Distribution Goes from Fluctuating to Stabilizing.\narxiv preprint 2024.\nPDF Download\nPapers in 2026\nCe Zheng, Hanyue Zheng, Jingwei Shi, Xinye Xu, Wei Zhou,\nTong Yang\n, Zhenyu Guan, Yong Cui. AlignSketch: A Framework for Aligning Theoretical and Practical Estimation Errors.\nIEEE ICDE 2026.\nPDF Download\n丛培壮, 王飞宇, 王国安, 王砚舒, 郑策,\n杨仝\n. 大语言模型低比特量化的历史、现状和未来：以复域量化为例[J].\n计算机研究与发展, 2026,63(2): 276−293.\nLink\nYaxuan Wang, Yifan Xiang, Ke Li, Xun Zhang, BoWen Ye, Zhuochen Fan, Fei Wei,\nTong Yang\n. Can a Robot Walk the Robotic Dog: Triple-Zero Collaborative Navigation for Heterogeneous Multi-Agent Systems.\nICRA 2026.\nZhongxian Liang, Qilong Shi, Xiyan Liang, Zihan Li, Wenjun Li,\nTong Yang\n, Yangyang Wang, Mingwei Xu, Weizhe Zhang. JitterSketch: Finding Jittery Flows in Network Streams.\nACM WWW 2026.\nPDF Download\nZihang Li, Yangdong Ruan, Wenjun Liu, Zhengyang Wang,\nTong Yang\n. CFT-RAG: An Entity Tree Based Retrieval Augmented Generation Algorithm With Cuckoo Filter.\nICLR 2026.\nLink\nHaozhe Wang, Haoran Que, Qixin Xu, Minghao Liu, Wangchunshu Zhou, Jiazhan Feng, Wanjun Zhong, Wei Ye,\nTong Yang\n, Wenhao Huang, Ge Zhang, Fangzhen Lin. Reverse-Engineered Reasoning for Open-Ended Generation.\nICLR 2026.\nLink\nQinyan Zhang, Xinping Lei, Ruijie Miao, Yu Fu, Haojie Fan, Le Chang, Jiafan Hou, Dingling Zhang, Zhongfei Hou, Ziqiang Yang, Changxin Pu, Fei Hu, Jingkai Liu, Jiaheng Liu,\nTong Yang\n, Zaiyuan Wang, Ge Zhang, Xinjie Chen, Jianpeng Jiao, Wenhao Huang. Inverse IFEval: Can LLMs Unlearn Stubborn Training Conventions to Follow Real Instructions?\nICLR 2026.\nLink\nFeiyu Wang, Qiuheng Yin, Yixin Zhang,\nTong Yang\n. Foresight Indexing: Accelerating B+tree Index with Programmable Switches on the Network Path.\nIEEE INFOCOM 2026.\nPDF Download\nZhicheng Li, Pinghui Wang, Qiheng Song, Rundong Li,\nTong Yang\n, Qun Huang. ZRing: A Dynamic Sketch for Weighted Cardinality Estimation in Data Streams.\nSIGKDD 2026.\nZhuochen Fan, Zhongxian Liang, Zirui Liu, Dayu Wang, Dong Wen, Wenjun Li,\nTong Yang\n, Yuzhou Liu, Weizhe Zhang. PBSketch: Finding Periodic Burst Items in Data Streams.\nSIGKDD 2026.\nMengbo Wang, Zhuochen Fan, Dayu Wang, Guorui Xie, Qing Li, Zeyu Luan, Yong Jiang,\nTong Yang\n, Mingwei Xu. RatioSketch: Towards More Accurate Frequency Estimation in Data Streams via a Lightweight Neural Network.\nAAAI 2026.\nYuxuan Tian, Zihan Wang, Yebo Peng, Aomufei Yuan, Zhiming Wang, Bairen Yi, Xin Liu, Yong Cui,\nTong Yang\n. KeepKV: Achieving Periodic Lossless KV Cache Compression for Efficient LLM Inference.\nAAAI 2026.\nPDF Download\nPapers in 2025\nYuanpeng Li, Xian Niu, Yikai Zhao,\nTong Yang\n, Yannan Hu, Yuchao Zhang, Xiangwei Deng, Qiuheng Yin, Ziyun Zhang, Ruwen Zhang, Yisen Hong, Kaicheng Yang, Ruijie Miao, Kun Meng, Dahui Wang, Yong Cui. TitanLog: Hierarchical and Elastic Logging for High-speed Network Data Stream.\nIEEE Transactions on Networking (ToN) 2025.\nPDF Download\nCe Zheng, Zhouran Shi, Ruijie Miao, Wenpu Liu,\nTong Yang\n, Bin Cui, Steve Uhlig. Answering Subset Query over Multi-Attribute Data Streams using Hyper-USS.\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE) 2025.\nPDF Download\nYuhan Wu, Fenghao Dong, Qizhi Chen, Aomufei Yuan, Kaicheng Yang, Hanglong Lv,\nTong Yang\n, Wenrui Liu, Gaogang Xie. PipHeap: Approximate Heap in the Pipeline Empowering Network Measurement.\nIMC 2025.\nPDF Download\nYuhan Wu, Hanbo Wu, Xilai Liu, Yuxuan Tian, Yikai Zhao,\nTong Yang\n, Rui Qiu, Kaicheng Yang, Sha Wang, Tao Li, Lihua Miao, Gaogang Xie. Approaching 100% Confidence in Stream Summary through ReliableSketch.\nIMC 2025.\nPDF Download\nZhuochen Fan#, Ruixin Wang#, Zihan Jiang# (# co-first authors), Ruwen Zhang,\nTong Yang\n, Sha Wang, Yuhan Wu, Ruijie Miao, Kaicheng Yang, Bui Cui. SandwichSketch: A More Accurate Sketch for Frequent Object Mining in Data Streams.\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE) 2025.\nPDF Download\nPeizhuang Cong, Yuchao Zhang, Jun Wang, Wendong Wang,\nTong Yang\n, Dan Li, and Ke Xu. I2BGP: A Privacy-Preserving Intra-AS State-Assisted Inter-AS Routing Scheme.\nIEEE Transactions on Networking (ToN) 2025.\n...[truncated]"
