  "serper::Lingjie Liu": {
    "homepage": "https://lingjie0206.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "lingjie.liu@seas.upenn.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/panxkun",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/huynhquynhanh/",
    "homepage_text": "Lingjie Liu\nLingjie Liu\nAravind K. Joshi Assistant Professor\nDepartment of Computer and Information Science\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\nEmail: lingjie.liu@seas.upenn.edu | Address: Office 570, Levine Hall, 3330 Walnut Street, Philadelphia, PA 19104-6389\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nTwitter\nAbout Me.\nI am the Aravind K. Joshi Assistant Professor in the Department of Computer and Information Science at the\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\n, where I lead the Penn Computer Graphics Lab and I am also a member of the\nGeneral Robotics, Automation, Sensing & Perception (GRASP) Lab\n.\nPreviously, I was a Lise Meitner Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Max Planck Institute for Informatics. I received my Ph.D. degree at the University of Hong Kong in 2019.\nMy research interests are at the interface of Computer Graphics, Computer Vision, and AI, with a  focus on\nNeural Scene Representations, Neural Rendering, Human Performance Modeling and Capture\n, and\n3D Reconstruction\n. I am especially excited about exploring a new genre of 3D reconstruction and rendering algorithms for human characters and general scenes, which combine classical computer graphics pipelines with deep learning techniques.\nMy long-term vision is to develop AI technologies that can perceive, understand and interact with 3D objects, people, and environments. Specifically, my research will pursue three goals:\n(1) High-quality 3D reconstruction of real-world scenes from sparse inputs;\n(2) Efficient and photo-realistic image synthesis of real-world scenes with 3D control;\n(3) Large-scale 3D scene generation.\nProspective Students.\nThere are multiple open research positions in my Lab.\nTopics of interest include:\nNeural Representations and Rendering for 3D/4D Reconstruction\nPhysics-Grounded 3D/4D Reconstruction\n3D/Video World Simulator\nPhysics-based Human Motion Generation\nHumanoid Robots and Dexterous Hands\nOther topics in Graphics, Vision and Robotics\nIf you are interested in visiting or applying for a research position (e.g., intern, PhD, visiting PhD, or postdoc) in the lab, please fill in the\napplication form\n. We review the form submissions on a biweekly basis. You will be contacted if a fit can be found. Due to the high volume of emails regarding applications, please refrain from emailing me directly. Thank you!\n[For 2026 Intern Applicants]\nWe are currently looking for multiple 2026 interns for both\nin-person\nand\nremote\nroles. If you’re interested, please feel free to fill out the application form above.\nGroup Members.\nPhD Students:\nChen Wang (\nMeshy AI Fellowship 2025 Outstanding Prize Recipient\n)\nYiming Huang\nQiao Feng (\nMeshy AI Fellowship 2025 Finalist\n)\nChuhao Chen\nVisiting PhD Students:\nXiaokun Pan\nLei Yao\nMaster, Undergraduate, and Intern Students:\nDaniel Mika (Undergrad)\nMutian Tong (co-advise with Jiatao Gu)\nBoao Shi\nSiyu Li (Master)\nYifan Li (Master)\nTuen Yue Tsui (Master)\nXuhai Chen\nAbhimanyu Suthar\nJacob Mollot (Master)\nSteven Su (Undergrad)\nQifei Cui (Master)\nShufan Sun\nRuichi Zhang (Master)\nLucky Qi (Master)\nAlumni:\n▼\n(expand for details)\nYusu Fang (Intern of 2025)\nZhiyao Sun (Visiting Student of 2025, from Tsinghua University)\nZhuoman Liu (Visiting Student of 2025, from Hong Kong Polytechnic University)\nQilin Huang (Intern of 2025)\nQuynh Anh Huynh (Master of 2025)\nChuhao Chen (Intern of 2025)\n-> now PhD at UPenn\nQingxuan Wu (Master of 2025)\n-> now Machine Learning Engineer at Bytedance\nJiahang (Jay) Mao (Master of 2025)\n-> now Co-founder of Rita.ai\nXuyi Meng (Master of 2025)\n-> now PhD at Cornell\nHeguang Lin (Master of 2025)\n-> now PhD at Scripps Research\nXiangyu Han (Master of 2025)\n-> now PhD at SJTU\nYunzhou Song (Master of 2025)\n-> now PhD at UPenn\nLinzhan Mou (Intern of 2025)\n-> now PhD at Princeton\nZhiyang Dou (Visiting Student of 2025, from HKU)\n-> now PhD at MIT\nAnjun Chen (Visiting Student of 2025, from Zhejiang University)\n-> now Assistant Professor at Xiamen University\nTingyang Zhang (Intern of 2024)\n-> now Researcher at Mihoyo\nLibo Zhang (Intern of 2024)\n-> now PhD at Tsinghua Univesity\nYiming Huang (Master of 2024)\n-> now PhD at UPenn\nProfessional Activities.\nServices:\nAssociate Editorship:\nACM TOG (2026 - present)\nIEEE TVCG (2023 - present)\nProgram Co-Chair:\nPacific Graphics'26\n, Program Co-Chair\n3DV'26\n, Program Co-Chair\nICCV'25\n, Broadening Participation Co-Chair\nACM SCA'25\n, Program Co-Chair\nEurographics'25\n, Doctoral Consortium Co-Chair\nEurographics'24\n, Posters Co-Chair\nProgram Committee Member:\nACM SIGGRAPH 2022, 2023, 2025\nACM SIGGRAPH Asia 2023, 2026\nPacific Graphics 2022, 2023\nArea Chair:\nCVPR 2024, 2025\nICCV 2025\n3DV 2024\nWorkshops, Tutorials, and Invited Talks:\n▼\n(expand for details)\nOrganizers:\nTutorial on Human Motion Generation\n, ICCV'25\nWorkshop on Wild3D: 3D Modeling, Reconstruction, and Generation in the Wild\n, ICCV'25\nWorkshop on Scalable 3D Scene Generation and Geometric Scene Understanding\n, ICCV'25\nWorkshop on 3D Digital Twin: Progress, Challenges, and Future Directions\n, CVPR'25\nWorkshop on Ind3D: Enforcing Inductive Bias in 3D Generation\n, CVPR'25\nWorkshop on Neural Fields Beyond Conventional Cameras\n, CVPR'25\nWorkshop on  AI for Content Creation workshop\n, CVPR'25\nWorkshop on Neural Fields Beyond Conventional Cameras\n, ECCV'24\nWorkshop on Wild 3D: 3D Modeling, Reconstruction, and Generation in the Wild\n, ECCV'24\nWorkshop on Generative Models for Computer Vision\n, CVPR'24\nWorkshop on AI for Content Creation Workshop\n, CVPR'24\nWorkshop on Generative Models for Computer Vision\n, CVPR'23\nWorkshop on AI for Content Creation Workshop\n, CVPR'23\nWorkshop on 3D Generative Models\n, Banff International Research Station for Mathematical Innovation and Discovery (BIRS)'23\nCourses:\nNeural Actor: Neural Free-view Synthesis of Human Actors with Pose Control,\nTutorial in 3DV 2021 Course on Advances in Neural Rendering\n.\nFast Rendering of Neural Radiance Fields,\nTutorial in SIGGRAPH 2021 Course on Advances in Neural Rendering\n.\nSelected Invited Talks:\nTowards Next-Gen 3D Reconstruction and Generation: From Visual Fidelity to Multimodal and Physical Understanding,\nCVPR'25 Workshop on Real-to-Sim: Bridging the Gap between Neural Rendering and Robot Learning\n.\nTowards Next-Gen 3D Reconstruction and Generation: From Visual Fidelity to Multimodal and Physical Understanding,\nETH Robotics, Vision, and Controls Talk Series\n.\nHigh-Fidelity Human Pose Tracking and Realistic Motion Synthesis in Real-World Scenes,\nKeynote at ACM MIG'24\n.\nHuman Pose Tracking and Controllable Motion Generation,\nECCV'24 workshop on Scalable 3D Scene Generation and Geometric Scene Understanding\n.\nEfficient Creation of Photo-realistic Controllable Human Characters,\nCVPR'24 workshop on The 1st Workshop on Neural Volumetric Video\n.\nTracking and Segmentation for Non-Static Scene Reconstruction,\nCVPR'24 Workshop on ScanNet++\n.\nGeneralized 3D Reconstruction,\nCVPR'24 Workshop on XRNeRF: Second Workshop on Advances in Radiance Fields for the Metaverse\n.\nGeneralized 3D Reconstruction,\nKeynote at 3DV 2024\n[Recording]\n.\nReconstruction of 3D Real-world Scenes,\nICCV'23 Workshop on NeRF4ADR: Neural Fields for Autonomous Driving and Robotics\n.\nNeural Representations of 3D Real-world Scenes,\nIROS'23 Workshop on Robotic Perception and Mapping\n.\nNeural Representation and Neural Rendering of 3D Real-world Scenes, Toronto Geometry Colloquium\n[Recording]\n.\nNew Methods for Reconstruction and Rendering of 3D Real-world Scenes, GAMES Webinar\n[Recording (Chinese)]\n.\nAwards.\nMeta Distinguished Faculty Award, 2025\nBest Paper Honorable Mention Award of ACM SIGGRAPH, 2024\nBest Paper Honorable Mention Award of ACM Symposium on Computer Animation (SCA), 2023\nAravind K. Joshi Assistant Professorship, 2023\nBest Paper Award of ACM International Conference on Intelligent Virtual Agents (IVA), 2021\nPublications.\n(* and † indicate equal contribution)\nRecent Preprints:\nPixie: Physics from Pixels\nLong Le, Ryan Lucas, Chen Wang, Chuhao Chen, Dinesh Jayaraman, Eric Eaton,\nLingjie Liu\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nOmniGuide: Universal Guidance Fields for Enhancing Generalist Robot Policies\nYunzhou Song*, Long Le*, Yong-Hyun Park, Jie Wang, Junyao Shi,\nLingjie Liu\n, Jiatao Gu, Eric Eaton, Dinesh Jayaraman, Kostas Daniilidis\n[Project Page]\n2026\ntttLRM: Test-Time Training for Long Context and Autoregressive 3D Reconstruction\nChen Wang, Hao Tan, Wang Yifan, Zhiqin Chen, Yuheng Liu, Kalyan Sunkavalli, Sai Bi,\nLingjie Liu†\n, Yiwei Hu†\nCVPR 2026\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nUniPixie: Unified and Probabilistic 3D Physics Learning via Flow Matching\nQilin Huang*, Quynh Anh Huynh*, Long Le*, Chen Wang, Chuhao Chen, Ryan Lucas, Eric Eaton,\nLingjie Liu\nCVPR 2026\nNext-Scale Autoregressive Models for Text-to-Motion Generation\nZhiwei Zheng, Shibo Jin,\nLingjie Liu\n, Mingmin Zhao\nCVPR 2026\nText2Interact: High-Fidelity and Diverse Text-to-Two-Person Interaction Generation\nQingxuan Wu, Zhiyang Dou, Chuan Guo, Yiming Huang, Qiao Feng, Bing Zhou, Jian Wang,\nLingjie Liu\nICLR 2026\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n2025\nGECO: Generative Image-to-3D within a SECOnd\nChen Wang, Jiatao Gu, Xiaoxiao Long, Yuan Liu,\nLingjie Liu\nTVCG 2025\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\nPhysCtrl: Generative Physics for Controllable and Physics-Grounded Video Generation\nChen Wang*, Chuhao Chen*, Yiming Huang, Zhiyang Dou, Yuan Liu, Jiatao Gu,\nLingjie Liu\nNeurIPS 2025\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\nPhysHMR: Learning Humanoid Control Policies from Vision for Physically Plausible Human Motion Reconstruction\nQiao Feng, Yiming Huang, Yufu Wang, Jiatao Gu,\nLingjie Liu\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2025\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\nZero-1-to-G: Taming Pretrained 2D Diffusion Model for Direct 3D Generation\nXuyi Meng*, Chen Wang*, Jiahui Lei, Kostas Daniilidis, Jiatao Gu,\nLingjie Liu\nTMLR 2025\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\nCFC: Simulating Character-Fluid Coupling using a Hierarchical World Model\nZhiyang Dou*, Chen Peng*, Xinyu Lu, Xiaohan Ye, Lixing Fang, Yuan Liu, Wenping Wang, Chuang Gan,\nLingjie Liu\n, Taku Komura\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2025 (ACM Transactions on Graphics,\nJournal track\n, Conditionally Accepted)\nModSkill: Physical...[truncated]"
