    "homepage_text": "Jiawei Han\nJiawei Han\nMichael\r\n  Aiken Chair Professor\nSiebel\r\n  School\nof Computing and Data Science\nUniv. of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\nRm\r\n  2132, Siebel Center for Computer Science\n201 N. Goodwin Avenue\nUrbana, IL 61801, USA\nE-mail:\nhanj\n[at]illinois.edu\nPh.D. (1985), Computer Science, Univ. Wisconsin-Madison\nData Mining, Text Mining,\r\n  Intelligent Systems\nData Mining Research Group\n(DMG\r\n  Misc Info)\nData and Information Systems Research\r\n  Laboratory (DAIS)\nUIUC Calendar\n,\nmy.CS\n,\nmyzoom\nOffice:   (217) 333-6903\nFax:       (217) 265-6494\nWeb:\nhanj.cs.illinois.edu\nCalendar\r\n  Schedule\nSelected\r\n  Research Publications\nCurrent Research (\nSelected\r\nPublications\n)\n§\nNSF AI Institute for Molecular Discovery,\r\nSynthetic Strategy, and Manufacturing: Molecule Maker Lab Institute\n§\nNSF I-Guide:\nInstitute for Geospatial Understanding\r\nthrough an Integrative Discovery Environment\n§\nNSF EAGER: Multi-Hop\r\nReasoning with LLMs: A Structure-Guided Reasoning Approach\nTeaching\n·\nUIUC\r\nCS412: An Introduction to Data Warehousing and Data Mining (The course is\r\ntaught by Ruby Tahboub, Arindam Benerjee,\nHanghang\nTong)\n·\nUIUC\r\nCS512: Data Mining: Principles and Algorithms (The course is taught by\r\nProfessor\nHanghang\nTong)\n·\nUIUC\r\nCS598JH: Text Mining with Large Language Models\n: 12:30-1:45pm\r\nWednesday/Friday 1035 CIF (Fall 2025)\n·\nData\r\nMining Research Group Meeting,\nMondays\n@\nSiebel Center (for DMG group member\r\nonly)\nBooks\n·\nJiawei Han,\r\nJian Pei, and\nHanghang\nTong,\nData Mining: Concepts and Techniques, 4\nth\nedution\n,\nMorgan\r\nKaufmann\n, 2023.\n(1st ed., 2000)\n(\n2\nnd\ned., 2006\n) (\n3\nrd\ned., 2012\n)\n·\nJiaming Shen and Jiawei Han,\nAutomated Taxonomy Discovery and Exploration\n,\nSpringer\n, 2022 (Series:\r\nSynthesis Lectures on Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery)\n·\nChao Zhang and Jiawei Han,\nMultidimensional Mining of Massive Text Data