    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/ming1993li",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Ming Li\nMing\nPh.D. graduated from NUS, interested in AIGC and MLLMs\nFollow\nShenzhen, China\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nI am a Senior Research Scientist (Genius Nova Program) in Guangming Lab, Shenzhen. I am conducting research on Large Language Models (LLMs), Vision Language Models, LLM Agent, and Reinforcement Learning. I have published\n43 papers\n, including 22 first or corresponding-author papers (1 IJCV, 1 ICML, 2 ICLR, 1 NeurIPS, 3 CVPR, 5 ICCV, 1 IEEE TIP, 2 AAAI, 1 IJCAI, 1 ACM MM, 3 IEEE TMM (One ESI Highly Cited Paper), 1 IJAS) and 21 other-author papers (2 ICML, 4 CVPR, 1 ICCV, 1 AAAI, 1 ACM MM, 1 PR, 3 ICME, 1 ICASSP, 1 IEEE TCSVT, 1 JBHI, 1 Neurocomputing, 2 JMSE, and 2 ICPR). I worked as a research scientist intern at Sea AI Lab.\nAcademic Services: Associate Editor of IEEE Transactions on Industrial Informatics and Pattern Recognition; Area Chair of WACV 2026; Regular Reviewer of TPAMI, IJCV, ICML, ICLR, NeurIPS, CVPR, ICCV.\nI completed my Ph.D. study (President PhD Fellowship Holder), supervised by\nProf. Shuicheng Yan\n(Fellow of AAAI, ACM, IEEE) and\nProf. Mike Shou\n, at\nInstitute of Data Science\nof\nNational University of Singapore\n. I also work closely with\nProf. Fei Richard Yu\n(Member of the Academia Europaea, Fellow of Canadian Academy of Engineering, IEEE),\nProf. Xiangyu Xu\n(Stanford’s Top 2% Most Highly Cited Scientist),\nProf. Huazhu Fu\n, and\nProf. Jun Liu\n.\nMany of my research outcomes have been recognized by leading experts, public media, prestigious universities, investment partners, highly cited indicators, and top-tier conference oral presentations:\nThe Grouped MoE technique proposed in our UniF2ace (ICLR 2026) to handle the fundamental pattern conflicts in unified models is adopted in Bagel developed by a\nworld-class AI team\nBytedance (TikTok) Seed!\nIn Mar. 2025,\nmuch earlier than Qwen3-VL\n(Nov. 2025), we propose deepstack-based multi-granularity visual feature injection in our FaVChat paper to boost the VLMs’ capability of answering fine-grained questions.\nOur CVPR 2025 paper, EventGPT, has attracted significant attention from the academic community. Notably, we received collaboration inquiries from many famous research groups. The work was also featured by the\nprominent AI platform\nPrompt Layer.\nOur multiple research studies received\npositive recognitions from leading experts\n, such as the Member of the U.S. National Academy of Engineering and the Member of Academia Europaea.\nOur AAAI 2026 paper on Agentic AI, StyleTailor, is accepted as an\nOral Presentation (top 4%)\n.\nOur IJCV paper, Instant3D, attracts many\ncooperation invitations from famous institutes\n, like the University of Michigan, Huawei, and miHoYo, which presents a novel fast text-to-3D generation paradigm.\nThe leading investment partner Gaorong Ventures also discusses its\ncommercialization and real-world potential\n.\nOur IEEE TMM paper for vehicle re-Identification has been repeatedly selected as an\nESI Highly Cited Paper\n.\nMy results on Track3 of AI City Challenge, organized by NVIDIA on CVPR 2020,\nrank 1st\non the official leaderboard, which surpasses the second ones by very large margins!\nI was a full-time Research Assistant in\nVISLab\nsupervised by\nProf. Ziming Zhang\nat\nWorcester Polytechnic Institute\nfrom Nov. 2019 to Apr. 2021. Before that, I worked as an RA supervised by\nProf. Dinggang Shen\n(Fellow of IEEE, AIMBE, IAPR, MICCAI) at\nUNC Chapel Hill\nfrom Aug. 2018 to Oct. 2019. I graduated with a Master’s degree from\nSchool of EECS\nat\nPeking University\nin Jul. 2018. And I received my Bachelor’s degree from the School of EE of\nXidian University\nin Jul. 2015.\nRecent news\n[Feb. 2026]\nFive papers are accepted by CVPR 2026. Congratulations to Keyang, Zhiyu, and others!\n[Jan. 2026]\nTwo papers are accepted by ICLR 2026. Congratulations to Junzhe and Shaoyu!\n[Dec. 2025]\nI am very pleased to give an invited talk about \"Fine-grained Multi-modal Learning and Reasoning\" at the School of Computer Science, Zhejiang University, Hangzhou.\n[Nov. 2025]\nThree papers are accepted by AAAI 2026, specially including an\nOral Presentation\npaper! Congratulations to Hongbo, Hongbin, and Zichen!\n[Jul. 2025]\nOne paper is accepted by NeurIPS 2025. Congratulations to Zihan!\n[Jul. 2025]\nOne paper is accepted by ACM MM 2025. Congratulations to Zhicong!\n[Jun. 2025]\nThree papers are accepted by ICCV 2025. Congratulations to Cui Miao, Meihan, and Yufei!\n[Jun. 2025]\nI was invited as a Guest Speaker at the Global Artificial Intelligence Technology Conference 2025, held on June 7–8 in Hangzhou, Zhejiang, China!\n[Apr. 2025]\nThree papers are accepted by ICML 2025. Congratulations to Songbai, Xiang Zhang, and Run He!\n[Apr. 2025]\nOne paper is accepted by IJCAI 2025. Congratulations to Gan Chen!\n[Apr. 2025]\nOur CVPR 2025 paper, EventGPT, has attracted significant attention from the academic community. Notably, we received collaboration inquiries from famous researchers. The work was also featured by the prominent U.S. AI platform PromptLayer in a special article titled “EventGPT: Giving AI the Power of Superhuman Vision”!\n[Feb. 2025]\nTwo papers are accepted by CVPR 2025, one of the top-tier AI/CV conferences. Congratulations to Shaoyu and Weilong!\n[Feb. 2025]\nOne paper is accepted by IEEE TMM. Congratulations!\n[Dec. 2024]\nOur team advances to the finals of the 2024 Shenzhen Intelligent Robot Dexterous Hand Competition and is awarded the Excellence Prize.\n[Nov. 2024]\nI am invited to give a talk titled \"From Visual Recognition to Multimodal Learning\" at the School of Software Engineering, Sun Yat-Sen University!\n[Jul. 2024]\nI start my career journey as a Full Professor and PI at Guangming Lab, Shenzhen.\n[May. 2024]\nI successfully passed my Ph.D. defense and received my certificate!\n[Apr. 2024]\nMy paper \"Instant3D: Instant Text-to-3D Generation\" is accepted by International Journal of Computer Vision.\n[Feb. 2024]\nI received many cooperation invitations from famous industrial institutes, like Gaorong Capital and Huawei, after we proposed a novel fast text-to-3D generation paradigm in our manuscript \"Instant3D: Instant Text-to-3D Generation\".\n[Jan. 2024]\nI am very pleased to give an invited talk, hosted by Prof. Hehe Fan, about 3D AIGC at School of Computer Science, Zhejiang University, Hangzhou.\n[Nov. 2023]\nMy paper \"EDR-FER: Discriminative and Robust Representation Learning for Facial Expression Recognition\" is accepted by IEEE Transactions on Multimedia.\n[Oct. 2023]\nMy paper \"Exploiting Multi-view Part-wise Correlation via an Efficient Transformer for Vehicle Re-Identification\" published on IEEE Transactions on Multimedia has been selected as\nESI Highly Cited Papers\nseveral times.\n[Apr. 2023]\nOur paper \"FakePoI: A Large-scale Fake Person of Interest Video Detection Benchmark and a Strong Baseline\" is accepted by IEEE Transactions on CSVT.\n[Jun. 2022]\nI am very pleased to give an invited online talk about Facial Expression Recognition at School of Science, Harbin Institute of Technology, Shenzhen.\n[Dec. 2021]\nMy paper \"Exploiting Multi-view Part-wise Correlation via an Efficient Transformer for Vehicle Re-Identification\" is accepted by IEEE Transactions on Multimedia.\n[Jul. 2021]\nMy paper \"Self-supervised Geometric Features Discovery with Interpretable Attention for Vehicle Re-Identification and Beyond\" is accepted by ICCV 2021 as a poster paper!\n[Apr. 2021]\nI complete my RA work at WPI!\n[Mar. 2021]\nI am awarded a four-year's PhD fellowship from National University of Singapore!\n[Oct. 2020]\nTwo papers are accepted by ICPR 2020!\n[Aug. 2020]\nThe video demo of my MTMC results on\nAI City Challenge 2020\nis\nhere\n!\n[Jul. 2020]\nOur paper on \"3D LiDAR Odometry Estimation\" has been accepted for presentation at the ACM Multimedia 2020 conference!\n[Jun. 2020]\nMy results on\nAI City Challenge 2020\nTrack3: City-Scale Multi-Camera Vehicle Tracking rank 1st on the official leaderboard, which surpasses the second ones by very large margins! Please check\nthe screenshot of the ranking results\n!\n[Nov. 2019]\nI start my research work on person/vehicle re-identification at Worcester Polytechnic Institute in MA, US.\n[Aug. 2018]\nI start my RA work on medical image processing at UNC-Chapel Hill in NC, US.\n[Jul. 2018]\nI complete my Master study in Peking University successfully!\n</ul>\n© Ming Li | Last updated: 30 Jun 2024"
  },
  "serper::Z. Guo": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/zguo/home",
    "emails": [
      "zihua.guo@monash.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZihua Guo\nProfessor\nARC Future Fellow\nMonash  University\nE\n-mail:  zihua.guo(at)monash.edu\nI'm a\np\nrofessor at\nSchool of Mathematics\n,\nMonash University\nin\nMelbourne\n, Australia.\nMy research interest lies in harmonic analysis and nonlinear evolution equations.\nMy Monash profile\nis\nhere\n.\nMy Google scholar page is\nhere\n.\nMy recent\npaper is on\narxiv\n.\nEducation/Employment\nEducation\n2004, Sun Yat-sen University, B.S.\n2007-2008, University of Chicago, visiting PhD\n2009, Peking University, PhD\nEmployment\n2009-2012, Peking University, Assistant Professor\n2012-2015, Peking University, Associate Professor\n2010-2011, Institute for Advanced Study, Postdoc Member\n2014.2-6, The Australian National University, Research fellow\n2015-\n2024.6\n, Monash University, Associate Professor\n2024.\n7-current\n, Monash University, Professor\n2024.11-2025.2, RIMS, Kyoto University, Invited visiting professor\nResearch interest\nI am interested in the interplay between harmonic analysis and partial differential equations, as well as their interactions with other fields.\nHarmonic analysis\nto study the boundedness in various function spaces\nof\nmany\nlinear/multilinear operators related to the Fourier\nrestriction problems\nand PDE, space-time estimates for dispersive equations\n, adaptive\nfunction spaces\nand\na\nnalysis tools associated to operators and PDE\nNonlinear partial differential equation\nto study the nonlinear evolution PDE arising in mathematical physics such as nonlinear dispersive equations (\nSchrodinger equation, KdV equation,\nwave equations, etc)\n, Euler equation, Navier-Stokes equation.  Main concerns are the low-regularity local/global well-posedness theory, long-time/blow-up behaviour of the solution, stability of the equation, playing tools from many other areas including harmonic analysis, functional analysis, ODE and probability, etc.\nSee here for more descriptions.\nRe\ncent\nIn S2 2025,\nJustin Forlano\nand I will teach the unit:\nMTH4123/5123: Partial differential equations\nI am one of the organisers for the following workshops:\nFeb\n1\n-\n7\n, 202\n6\n,\nAsia-Pacific International Conference on Dispersive Equations\n(APICDE II)\n,\nSydney\n, Australia\nDec 9-12, 2025, Special session \"Harmonic Analysis and Hamiltonian PDE\", at the 69th\nAnnual Meeting of the Australian Mathematical Society,\nMelbourne\n, Australia\nDec 16-20, 2024, Harmonic and Microlocal Analysis in PDE, MATRIX, Melbourne, Australia\nDec 9-13, 2024, Special session \"Harmonic Analysis and Hamiltonian Partial Differential Equations\", at Joint meeting of the NZMS, AustMS and AMS, Auckland, New Zealand\nOct 28-Nov 1, 2024,\nAsia-Pacific International Conference on Dispersive Equations\n(APICDE I)\n, Xiamen, China\nDec 10-15, 2023, Nonlinear dispersive and wave equations: Recent developments and future directions, M\nelbourne\n, Australia\nDec 5-8, 2023, Special session \"Harmonic analysis \" at the 67th Annual Meeting of the Australian Mathematical Society, Queensland, Australia\n2020-2023, Webinar on Analysis and PDE (to promote communications and collaborations for Chinese researchers during COVID period)\nI am a chief investigator for the following projects:\nIntrinsic structures in partial differential equations\n1/01/26-31/21/28, CI, ARC Discovery project, DP260100485\nPartial differential equation: Schrodinger operator and long-time dynamics\n30/06/24 → 29/06/28, ARC Future fellowship,\nFT230100588\nNonlinear harmonic analysis and dispersive partial differential equations\n8/04/20 → 31/12/23, CI, ARC Discovery project,  DP\n200101065\nHarmonic analysis and dispersive partial differential equations\n1/01/17 → 1/11/20,  Lead CI,  ARC Discovery project,  DP\n170101060\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
