    "homepage_text": "Niao He\nHome\nProf. Niao He\nPeople\nPublications\nTeaching\nOpenings\nStudent Projects\nContact\nNiao He\nI am currently an Associate Professor in the Department of\nComputer Science\nat\nETH Zurich\n, and leading the\nOptimization & Decision Intelligence (ODI) Group\n.\nInstitute of Machine Learning\nETH AI Center\nETH Foundations of Data Science\nMax Planck ETH Center for Learning Systems\nMy work lies in the interface of optimization and machine learning, with a primary focus on the algorithmic and theoretical foundations for principled, scalable, and trustworthy decision intelligence.\nI am also interested in developing machine learning models and algorithms for interdisciplinary applications in operations management, mechanism design, control and robotics.\nThanks to Swiss National Science Foundations, ETH Foundations, and NCCR Automation for generously funding our current research.\nAcademic Positions\nPresent\n2025.01\nAssociate Professor\nComputer Science\nETH Zurich\n2024.12\n2020.12\nAssistant Professor\nComputer Science\nETH Zurich\n2020.12\n2016.01\nAssistant Professor\nIndustrial and Systems Engineering\nCoordinated Science Laboratory\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\nEducation\nPh.D.\n2015\nPh.D. in Operations Research\nGeorgia Institute of Technology\nSchool of Industrial & Systems Engineering\nAdvisor: Arkadi Nemirovski\nM.S.\n2015\nM.S. in Computational Science & Engineering\nGeorgia Institute of Technology\nCollege of Engineering\nB.S.\n2010\nB.S. in Mathematics\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nSpecial Class of Gifted Young\nHonors, Awards and Grants\n2025\nBest Paper Finalist, L4DC 2025\n2023\nSNSF Starting Grant\n2023\nSNSF Sinergia Grant\n2021\nELLIS Scholar\n2020\nCAS Beckman Fellow\n2019\nNSF HDR TRIPODS Grant\n2018\nNCSA Faculty Fellow\n2018\nList of Teachers Ranked as Excellent (UIUC)\n2018\nNSF CISE CRII Award\n2017\nList of Teachers Ranked as Excellent (UIUC)\n2017\nSIAM Early Career Travel Award\n2016\nList of Teachers Ranked as Outstanding (UIUC)\n2016\nAISTATS Best Paper Award\n2016\nCollins Scholar (UIUC)\nConferences Program Committee\nAssociate Editor: SIAM Journal on Optimization, Mathematics of Operations Research, Journal of Optimization Theory and Applications\nSenior Area Chair: ICML 2026, NeurIPS 2024\nArea Chair: NeurIPS 2020, ICLR 2021, UAI 2021, ICML 2021, COLT 2022, ICML 2022, NeurIPS 2023\nSenior Program Committee: AAAI 2019\nProgram Committee: ICML 2015-2019, NeurIPS 2016-2018, AAAI 2017, AISTATS 2016"
  },
