    "homepage_text": "Personal Information - Yikai Zhang\nYikai Zhang\nPh.D. student at Fudan University. Research Intern at Bytedance AI Lab.\nFollow\nShanghai, China\nFudan University\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nGithub\nX (formerly Twitter)\nPersonal Information\nProfile\nYikai Zhang (张益恺)\nis a second-year Ph.D. student at Fudan University in the School of Computer Science, Shanghai, China. His research topics are mostly around multimodal learning and autonomous agents, including (but not limited to):\nMultimodal Representation Learning\n: Cross-modal alignment and training of multi-modal models.\nReasoning and Planning\n: Endowing language models with human-like reasoning and planning capabilities.\nSimulated Environments\n: Building dynamic and interactive environments for the evaluation of agents.\nExperience\nFudan University\n2022 - Present\nRole: Ph.D. Student\nTopics: Multimodal Learning and Autonomous Agents\nByteDance\n2024 - Present\nRole: Research Intern\nTopics: Multi-agent Learning\nI am very willing to collaborate with researchers in the fields of LLM, LMM, and autonomous agents! 🥳 If you are interested, please contact me via\nemail\n.🤩"
  },
  "serper::Qihan Ren": {
