    "homepage_text": "Academic\nSearch\nYingxue Zhang\nAssistant Professor\nComputer Science\nBinghamton University\nEmail: yzhang42@binghamton.edu\nBiography\nYingxue Zhang is an Assistant Professor in\nComputer Science Department\nat\nBinghamton University\n. She got her Ph.D. degree in Data Science from Worcester Polytechnic Institute in 2022. Her broad research interests include: (1) designing novel deep learning and AI techniques to solve spatial-temporal big data analytics problems related to smart cities, and (2) human behavior analysis and decision making modeling\nOpenings:\nI am looking for self-motivated PhD students to work on deep learning topics. I’m particularly interested in candidates with background in CS/AI/Data Mining/Machine Learning/Stat/Math and strong programming skills. Please send me a short email with your CV and transcript.\nInterests\nArtificial Intelligence\nReinforcement Learning\nImitation Learning\nSpatial-Temporal Data Mining\nLLMs\nGenerative AI\nRepresentation Leaning\nEducation\nPhD in Data Science, 2022\nWorcester Polytechnic Institute\nMS in Financial Engineering, 2018\nStevens Institute of Technology\nBS in Computer Science, 2016\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nRecent News\n[Paper]\n11/2025: One paper was accepted by\nKDD 2026\n. Congratulations to Yuhang!﻿\n[Paper]\n08/2025: One paper was accepted by\nICDM 2025\n. Congratulations to Yuhang!\n[Award]\n08/2025: I have received the Educator of the Year Award from the School of Computing at Binghamton University (2024-25).\n[TPC]\n06/2025: PC for CIKM 2025.\n[Paper]\n05/2025: One paper was accepted by\nKDD 2025\n. Congratulations to Yuhang!\n[TPC]\n03/2025: PC for NeurIPS 2025.\n[Paper]\n11/2024: One paper was accepted by TKDD.\n[TPC]\n11/2024: PC for IJCAI 2025.\n[Paper]\n09/2024:One paper was accepted by ﻿\nNeurIPS 2024\n!\n[Paper]\n09/2024: One paper was accepted by ﻿\nICDM 2024\n. Congratulations to Yuhang!\n[TPC]\n06/2024: PC for KDD 2025, AAAI 2025 and ICLR 2025.\n[Paper]\n05/2024: One paper was accepted by\nKDD 2024\n. Congratulations to Xinbo!\n[TPC]\n02/2024: PC for IJCAI 2024.\n[TPC]\n01/2024: PC for KDD 2024.\n[TPC]\n09/2023: PC for SDM 2024.\n[TPC]\n09/2023: PC for ICLR 2024.\n[Student]\n08/2023: Two Ph.D. students join the lab. Welcome, Xinbo and Yuhang!\n[TPC]\n08/2023: PC for AAAI 2024.\n[TPC]\n03/2023: PC for NeurIPS 2023.\n[TPC]\n01/2023: PC for KDD 2023 and IJCAI 2023.\n[Paper]\n12/2022: One paper was accepted by\nSDM 2023\n!﻿\n[Paper]\n09/2022: Two papers were accepted by\nICDM 2022\n!\n[Position]\n08/2022: Joined the Computer Science Department at Binghamton University as an Assistant Professor!\n[TPC]\n03/2022: PC for KDD 2022\nPublications\nQuickly discover relevant content by\nfiltering publications\n.\nYuhang Liu\n,\nYingxue Zhang\n,\nXin Zhang\n,\nYanhua Li\n,\nJun Luo\n(2025).\nUniLLM: A Unified Large Language Model for Multi -Modal Urban Dynamics Prediction\n.\nIn Proceedings of the 32st ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD ’26), August 9–13, 2026, Jeju, Korea..\nYuhang Liu\n,\nYingxue Zhang\n,\nXin Zhang\n,\nYu Yang\n,\nYanhua Li\n,\nJun Luo\n(2025).\nMARCEL: Multifaceted Spatial-Temporal Contrastive Learning for Generic Spatial-Temporal Representations\n.\nIEEE International Conference on Data Mining (ICDM), 2025. (Full paper acceptance rate = 13.5%).\nYuhang Liu\n,\nYingxue Zhang\n,\nXin Zhang\n,\nYanhua Li\n,\nand Jun Luo\n(2025).\nUrbanMind: Urban Dynamics Prediction with Multifaceted Spatial-Temporal Large Language Models\n.\nIn Proceedings of the 31st ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD ’25), August 3–7, 2025, Toronto, ON, Canada..\nYingxue Zhang\n,\nYanhua Li\n,\nXun Zhou\n,\nZhenming Liu and Jun Luo\n(2024).\nC3-GAN+: Complex-Condition-Controlled Generative Adversarial Networks with Enhanced Embedding\n.\nACM Transactions on Knowledge Discovery from Data (TKDD).\nRuohan Li\n,\nYiqun Xie\n,\nXiaowei Jia\n,\nDongdong Wang\n,\nYanhua Li\n,\nYingxue Zhang\n,\nZhihao Wang and Zhili Li\n(2024).\nSolarCube: An Integrative Benchmark Dataset Harnessing Satellite and In-situ Observations for Large-scale Solar Energy Forecasting\n.\nNeurIPS 2024 (Datasets and Benchmarks Track), Vancouver, Canada (acceptance rate: ~25%).\nSee all publications\nStudents\nCurrent PhD Students\nX﻿inbo Zhao\nPhD Student, Computer Science, Binghamton University\nM.S., Computer Science, Waseda University, 2023\nB.S., Computer Science, SiChuan Univeristy, 2021\nY﻿uhang Liu\nPhD Student, Computer Science, Binghamton University\nM.S., Computer Engineering, University of California, Riverside, 2022\nB.S., Software Engineering, Wuhan University of Science and Technology, 2020\nMaster Students\nJ﻿unjie Xu (MS student in CS at Binghamton University), Summer 2023-Fall 2023\nTeaching\nINFO 501 Information Systems I-Python and Data Mining\nINFO 535 Applied Data Mining\nINFO 536 Applied Machine Learning\nContact\nyzhang42@binghamton.edu\n4400 Vestal Pkwy E, Binghamton, NY 13902\nN04, Engineering Building\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
  "serper::Zuoyu Yan": {
