    "github": "https://github.com/MarcusYF",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/fan-yao-028540241/",
    "homepage_text": "Fan Yao\nESC\nAll Results\nSearching...\nNo results found\nClear search\n↑↓\nNavigate\n↵\nSelect\nPowered by Hugo Blox\n✈️\nFan Yao\nAssistant Professor\nUniversity of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\nAbout Me\nI am an assistant professor in the Department of Statistics and Operations Research (\nSTOR\n) at UNC Chapel Hill.\nI received my PhD in Computer Science from the University of Virginia, advised by\nHaifeng Xu\nand\nHongning Wang\n. Prior to obtaining my PhD, I spent two years at the University of Chicago and received both my BS and MS in Computational Mathematics from Peking University. My\nCV\nis available here.\nMy research interests include social and ethical aspects of AI, human-centered machine learning, strategic and multi-agent systems, recommender systems and digital platform economy. If you share similar interests, feel free to contact me via email. Prospective students are encouraged to review\nthis\nbefore contacting me.\n👈🏻 Find my email and working address by clicking the icons on the left.\nCurrent status: ✈️ in Chicago (☕️regular ✈️traveling 🏖vacation ⏳deadline mode)\nResearch\nI study algorithmic interplays between human behaviors and ML/AI systems through theoretical frameworks, drawing insights from algorithmic game theory, online/reinforcement learning, dynamical systems and learning theory. Full list of publications can be found in my\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nSelected Publications\nYurong Chen\n,\nYu He\n,\nMichael I. Jordan\n,\nFan Yao\n(2026).\nHow Sampling Shapes LLM Alignment: From One-Shot Optima to Iterative Dynamics\n.\nSource Document\nPreprint\nFan Yao\n,\nYuwei Cheng\n,\nErmin Wei\n,\nHaifeng Xu\n(2025).\nSingle-Agent Poisoning Attacks Suffice to Ruin Multi-Agent Learning\n.\nICLR\n, 2025.\nPDF\nHaruka Kiyohara\n,\nFan Yao\n,\nSarah Dean\n(2025).\nPolicy Design for Two-sided Platforms with Participation Dynamics\n.\nICML\n, 2025.\nCode\nSlides\nLink\nPreprint\nFan Yao\n,\nChuanhao Li\n,\nDenis Nekipelov\n,\nHongning Wang\n,\nHaifeng Xu\n(2024).\nHuman vs Generative AI in Content Creation Competition: Symbiosis or Conflict?\n.\nICML\n, 2024.\nOral presentation at Econometric Society Interdisciplinary Frontiers (ESIF) conference on Economics and AI+ML.\nPDF\nVideo\nPreprint\nFan Yao\n,\nYiming Liao\n,\nMingzhe Wu\n,\nChuanhao Li\n,\nYan Zhu\n,\nJames Yang\n,\nJingzhou Liu\n,\nQifan Wang\n,\nHaifeng Xu\n,\nHongning Wang\n(2024).\nUser Welfare Optimization in Recommender Systems with Competing Content Creators\n.\nKDD\n, 2024.\nLong-term experiment on Instagram Reels.\nPDF\nPreprint\nSee all\nTeaching\nView all my courses and syllabi\nRecent News\nMar. 2026\nGiving a talk about our work on\nLLM alignment dynamics\nat\nLLMs and Strategic Agents for Machine Learning workshop\nhosted in Northwestern University – find me to chat!\nFeb. 2026\nGiving a talk about our work on\nLLM alignment dynamics\nat\nFTEC Seminar\nonline in HKUST(Guangzhou).\nOct. 2025\nCo-hosting a session\nPreference Learning in Large Language Models\nwith Chong Liu and giving a talk “Rethinking the role of GenAI in content creation ecosystem” at INFORMS, Atlanta.\nSep. 2025\nAttending\nAligning AI with Society workshop\nat UNC as an invited panelist.\nAug. 2025\nI’m joining\nSTOR\nat UNC Chapel Hill as a tenure-track assistant professor.\nMisc\nMore personal details about me can be found\nhere\n…"
  },
