    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Yuan Gao's Homepage\nYuan Gao\nAssociate Professor\nWuhan University\nBiography\nI am an Associate Professor of the Computational and Photogrammetric Vision Team (\nCaptain\n), School of Artificial Intelligence, Wuhan University. Prior to that, I was a senior research scientist at\nTencent AI Lab\n. I received Ph.D. degree in Electronic Engineering Department of\nCity University of Hong Kong\n, during which I visited\nCenter for Cognition, Vision, and Learning (CCVL)\nof UCLA. Before that, I obtained B.S. and M.S. degrees both from\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\n.\nI developed several Machine Learning algorithms and have applied them to Computer Vision with\nProf. Alan Yuille\n, to Complex Network with\nProf. Guanrong Chen\n, to Bioinformatics with\nDr. Rosa Chan\nand\nDr. Panpan Hou\n, with products delivered at\nTencent\nand\nPinduoduo\n.\nMy current research interests include Multi-Modality & Multi-Task AI, with its efficiency in training & inference, and its applications mainly to Computer Vision.\nInterests\nMachine Learning: Multi-Task/Modality Learning, Neural Architecture Search, Efficient Deep Learning\nComputer Vision: 3D Reconstruction, Pose Estimation, Point Cloud Analysis\nEducation\nPhD in Electronic Engineering, 2016\nCity University of Hong Kong\nMEng in Pattern Recognition and Machine Intelligence, 2012\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nBSc in Biomedical Engineering, 2009\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nNews\nMore Posts\nThu, Sep 18, 2025\n1 paper (Coreset Selection) was accepted to\nNeurIPS\n.\nWed, Sep 10, 2025\n1 paper (Whole-Scene Image Holistic Semantic Segmentation) was accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\nTue, Aug 5, 2025\n1 paper (Generalizble Training-Free 3D Pose Estimation) was accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\nTue, Jul 1, 2025\n1\nACL\n(Efficient Optimization-based LLM Pruning) and 1\nICCV\n(Heterogeneous Knowledge Distillation) papers were accepted.\nThu, May 2, 2024\n2 papers (Multi-Task Grouping, Efficient Diffusion Models) were accepted to\nICML\n.\nSelected Publications\nFull List\nTowards Human-Level 3D Relative Pose Estimation: Generalizable, Training-Free, with Single Reference.\nYuan Gao\n*^\n, Yajing Luo\n*\n, Junhong Wang, Kui Jia, and Gui-Song Xia\n^\n. (\n*\nindicates equal contributions,\n^\nindicates corresponding authors)\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\n, 2025.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\nVideo\nSupp. Materials\narXiv\nFuse Before Transfer: Knowledge Fusion for Heterogeneous Distillation.\nGuopeng Li, Qiang Wang, Ke Yan, Shouhong Ding,\nYuan Gao\n^\n, and Gui-Song Xia\n^\n. (\n^\nindicates corresponding authors)\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)\n, 2025.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\narXiv\nBypass Back-propagation: Optimization-based Structural Pruning for Large Language Models via Policy Gradient.\nYuan Gao\n*\n, Zujing Liu\n*\n, Weizhong Zhang\n*\n, Bo Du, and Gui-Song Xia. (\n*\nindicates equal contributions)\nThe Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL)\n, 2025.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\narXiv\nPoster\nDMTG: One-Shot Differentiable Multi-Task Grouping.\nYuan Gao\n, Shuguo Jiang, Moran Li, Jin-Gang Yu, and Gui-Song Xia.\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n, 2024.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\narXiv\nPoster\nAnchor-based Robust Finetuning of Vision-Language Models.\nJinwei Han, Zhiwen Lin, Zhongyisun Sun, Yingguo Gao, Ke Yan, Shouhong Ding,\nYuan Gao\n^\n, and Gui-Song Xia\n^\n. (\n^\nindicates corresponding authors)\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2024.\nPDF\nBibTex\narXiv\nAux-NAS: Exploiting Auxiliary Labels with Negligibly Extra Inference Cost.\nYuan Gao\n, Weizhong Zhang, Wenhan Luo, Lin Ma, Jin-Gang Yu, Gui-Song Xia, and Jiayi Ma.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n, 2024.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\narXiv\nPoster\nLocality Preserving Refinement for Shape Matching with Functional Maps.\nYifan Xia, Yifan Lu,\nYuan Gao\n^\n, Jiayi Ma\n^\n. (\n^\nindicates corresponding authors)\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\n, 2024.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\nExploiting Learnable Joint Groups for Hand Pose Estimation.\nMoran Li\n*\n,\nYuan Gao\n*\n, and Nong Sang. (\n*\nindicates equal contributions)\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\n, 2021.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\narXiv\nMTL-NAS: Task-Agnostic Neural Architecture Search towards General-Purpose Multi-Task Learning.\nYuan Gao\n*\n, Haoping Bai\n*\n, Zequn Jie, Jiayi Ma, Kui Jia, and Wei Liu. (\n*\nindicates equal contributions)\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2020.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\nSupp. Materials\narXiv\nPoster\nEstimation of 3D Category-Specific Object Structure: Symmetry, Manhattan and/or Multiple Images.\nYuan Gao\n^\n, and Alan L. Yuille. (\n^\nindicates corresponding author)\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\n, 2019.\nPDF\nBibTex\nSupp. Materials\nNDDR-CNN: Layerwise Feature Fusing in Multi-Task CNNs by Neural Discriminative Dimensionality Reduction.\nYuan Gao\n, Jiayi Ma, Mingbo Zhao, Wei Liu, and Alan L. Yuille.\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2019.\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\nSupp. Materials\narXiv\nPoster\nFeature-guided Gaussian Mixture Model for Image Matching.\nJiayi Ma, Xingyu Jiang, Junjun Jiang, and\nYuan Gao\n^\n. (\n^\nindicates corresponding author)\nPattern Recognition\n, vol.92, pp.231-245, 2019.\nPDF\nBibTex\nInactivation of KCNQ1 potassium channels reveals dynamic coupling between voltage sensing and pore opening.\nPanpan Hou, Jodene Eldstrom, Jingyi Shi, Ling Zhong, Kelli McFarland,\nYuan Gao\n, David Fedida, and Jianmin Cui.\nNature Communications\n, vol.8, article no.1730, 2017.\nPDF\nBibTex\nExploiting Symmetry and/or Manhattan Properties for 3D Object Structure Estimation from Single and Multiple Images.\nYuan Gao\n, and Alan L. Yuille.\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2017.\nPDF\nBibTex\nSupp. Materials\narXiv\nSemi-Supervised Sparse Representation Based Classification for Face Recognition with Insufficient Labeled Samples.\nYuan Gao\n, Jiayi Ma, and Alan L. Yuille.\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\n, vol.26, no.5, pp.1-16, 2017.\n(ESI Highly Cited Paper)\nPDF\nBibTex\nCode\narXiv\nSymmetric Non-Rigid Structure from Motion for Category-Specific Object Structure Estimation.\nYuan Gao\n, and Alan L. Yuille.\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV)\n, 408-424, 2016.\nPDF\nBibTex\nSupp. Materials\narXiv\nComputational classification of different wild-type zebrafish strains based on their variation in light-induced locomotor response.\nYuan Gao\n, Gaonan Zhang, Beth Jelfs, Yuk Fai Leung, Rosa H.M. Chan,\net al\n.\nComputers in Biology and Medicine\n, vol.69, pp.1–9, 2016.\nPDF\nBibTex\nNaming Game on Networks: Let Everyone be Both Speaker and Hearer.\nYuan Gao\n, Guanrong Chen, and Rosa H. M. Chan.\nScientific Reports\n, vol.4, no.6149, 2014.\nPDF\nBibTex\nSupp. Materials\narXiv\nA high-throughput zebrafish screening method for visual mutants by light-induced locomotor response.\nYuan Gao\n, Rosa H. M. Chan, Tommy W. S. Chow, Liyun Zhang, Sylvia Bonilla, Yuk Fai Leung,\net al\n.\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics (TCBB)\n, vol.11, no.4, pp.693-701, 2014.\nPDF\nBibTex\nSupp. Materials"
