  "serper::Zhiru Zhang": {
    "homepage": "https://www.csl.cornell.edu/~zhiruz/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/cornell-zhang",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/matthew-hofmann-a54920190",
    "homepage_text": "Zhiru Zhang\nComputer Systems Laboratory\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nSoftware Releases\nGroup Website\nZhiru Zhang\nProfessor\nComputer Systems Laboratory\nSchool of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nCollege of Engineering\nCornell University\noffice:\n320 Rhodes Hall, Ithaca, NY 14853\nphone:\n(607) 255-5954\nemail:\nzhiruz -at- cornell.edu\nDr. Zhiru Zhang is a Professor in the School of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Cornell University and a member of the Computer Systems Laboratory. His current research investigates new algorithms, methodologies, and design automation tools for heterogeneous computing systems. Recent publications from his group focus on the topics of high-level synthesis (HLS), hardware specialization for machine learning, and programming models for software-defined FPGAs.\nHe is an IEEE Fellow and has been honored with the Intel Outstanding Researcher Award, AWS AI Amazon Research Award, Facebook Research Award, Google Faculty Research Award, DAC Under-40 Innovators Award, Rising Professional Achievement Award from the UCLA Henry Samueli School of Engineering and Applied Science, DARPA Young Faculty Award, IEEE CEDA Ernest S. Kuh Early Career Award, NSF CAREER Award, and Ross Freeman Award for Technical Innovation from Xilinx. He has won multiple Best Paper Awards from top conferences and journals, including ASPLOS (2025), ISPD (2025), FPGA (2024, 2022, 2021, 2019), AutoML (2024), FCCM (2018), ACM TODAES (2012), and Top Picks in Hardware and Embedded Security (2020). His papers on HLS scheduling and application-specific instruction-set processor (ASIP) compilation have been inducted into the ACM/SIGDA TCFPGA Hall of Fame for the classes of 2022 and 2023, respectively. On the teaching side, he received the Ruth and Joel Spira Award for Excellence in Teaching (2018) and twice the Michael Tien'72 Excellence in Teaching Award (2016, 2022), the highest recognition for teaching in the College of Engineering.\nHe holds a B.S. in Computer Science from Peking University and an M.S. and Ph.D. in Computer Science from UCLA. He co-founded AutoESL based on his dissertation research on HLS; the company was later acquired by Xilinx (now AMD), and its HLS technology evolved into Vivado HLS (now Vitis HLS), widely used for FPGA-based accelerator design. He also co-founded RapidStream, which developed agile FPGA acceleration tools and was acquired by a major global proprietary trading firm.\nTeaching\nECE 5775 (now 6775)\n[site]\n: High-Level Digital Design Automation (FA'25, '24, '23, '22, '18, '17, '16, '15, '14)\nENGRD/ECE 2300\n[site]\n: Digital Logic and Computer Organization (SP'25, '24, '22, '21, '18, '17, '16, '15, '14)\nECE 6980: Special Topics on Hardware Acceleration of Deep Learning (SP'23)\nENGRG 1050: Freshman Engineering Seminar (FA'22, '17, '13)\nECE 5950: Special Topics on High-Level Digital Design Automation (SA'13)\nRecent News\nHeuriGym\nand\nFlashDLM\naccepted to ICLR'26 (1/25/2026)\nMercer Distinguished Lecture at RPI on\naccelerator design and programming\n(11/19/2025)\nNiansong awarded\nLAD fellowship\n(11/15/2025)\nTawa\naccepted to CGO'26 (11/3/2025)\nAPU characterization\naccepted to MICRO'25 (7/14)\nASPEN\naccepted to MLCAD'25 (7/4/2025)\nEqMap\nand\ne-boost\naccepted to ICCAD'25 (6/30/2025)\nInvited talk on AI-driven hardware design at ISCA'25 Workshop (6/21/2025)\nCirSTAG\nnominated for\nDAC'25\nbest paper (5/13/2025)\nJUMP 2.0 SRC e-workshop talk on differentiable compiler optimization (4/29/2025)\nSmoothE\nwon\nASPLOS'25\nBest Paper Award (4/1/2025)\nCypress\nwon\nISPD'25\nBest Paper Award (3/19/25)\nPrepropagation GNN\naccepted to MLSys'25 (2/10/2025)\nHanchen\nsuccessfully defended his dissertation (2/3/2025)\nNikita\nsuccessfully defended his dissertation (1/22/2025)\nShaojie\nsuccessfully defended his dissertation (1/10/2025)\nARIES\naccepted to FPGA'25 (11/29/2024)\nInvited talk on differentiable e-graph extraction at NVIDIA (11/8/2024)\nInvited talk on accelerator programming at Stanford (11/7/2024)\nSmoothE\naccepted to ASPLOS'25 (10/31/2024)\nFLIQS\nwon\nAutoML'24\nBest Paper Award (9/12/2024)\nInvited talk on data specialization for ML at MLCAD (9/9)\nHongzheng\nwon 3rd place in the\nPLDI'24 Student Research Competition\n(6/27/2024)\nInvited talk on accelerator programming \"at\" IBM (6/14/2024)\nGPU pangenome layout\naccepted to SC'24 (6/14/2024)\nHongzheng\nselected as\n2024 MLCommons Rising Stars\n(5/16/2024)\nInvited AI-day tech talk on binarized deep learning \"at\" RTX (5/8/2024)\nGrateful to receive\nAWS AI Amazon Research Award\n(4/29/2024)\nGrateful to receive\nIntel Outstanding Researcher Award\n(4/11/2024)\nSabre\naccepted to OSDI'24 (3/21/2024)\nLLM FPGA\naccepted to FCCM'24 journal track (3/19/2024)\nHLS formal verification\nwon FPGA'24 Best Paper Award (3/5/2024)\nInvited talk on scalable graph learning\nat\nFPGA'24 SpatialML Workshop\n(3/3/2024)\nAllo\naccepted to PLDI'24 (2/26/2024)\nChenhui\nsuccessfully defended his dissertation (2/23/2024)\nHOGA\naccepted to DAC'24 (2/13/2024)\nPolynormer\naccepted to ICLR'24 (1/16/2024)\nUniSparse\naccepted to OOPSLA'24 (12/22/2023)\nSlapo\naccepted to ASPLOS'24 (11/7/2023)\nYichi\nsuccessfully defended his dissertation (9/29/2023)\nBMT\naccepted to NeurIPS'23 (9/21/2023)\nInvited talk on ML for HLS\n\"at\"\nESWeek\n(9/19/2023)\nInvited panel on\nHLS adoption\nat DAC (7/13/2023)\nInvited talk on\ndatapath synthesis\nat DAC (7/11/2023)\nYixiao\nreceived Cornell ECE\nOutstanding PhD TA Award\n! (4/20/2023)\nInvited panel on\nEDA for domain specific computing\nat ISPD (3/29/2023)\nASIP synthesis paper\ninducted into ACM/SIGDA\nTCFPGA Hall of Fame\n(2/13/2023)\nMore news\nResearch Group\n[site]\n[github]\n[youtube]\n[linkedin]\nJordan Dotzel\n(MS/PhD, started FA'19, with Prof. Mohamed Abdelfattah)\nJie Liu\n(MS/PhD, started FA'19)\nZichao Yue (MS/PhD, started SU'20)\nYixiao Du\n(MS/PhD, started SU'20)\nYaohui Cai\n(MS/PhD, started SP'21, with Prof. Chris De Sa)\nAndrew Butt\n(MS/PhD, started FA'21)\nHongzheng Chen\n(MS/PhD, started FA'21)\nJiajie Li\n(MS/PhD, started FA'21)\nNiansong Zhang\n(MS/PhD, started FA'21)\nMatthew Hofmann\n(MS/PhD, started FA'22)\nZhanqiu (Summer) Hu\n(MS/PhD, started FA'23, with Prof. Udit Gupta)\nVesal Bakhtazad\n(MS/PhD, started SP'24)\nDr. Grace Dinh\n(PostDoc, 2024-)\nDr. Yizhao Gao (PostDoc, 2025-)\nAlumni\nDr. Hanchen Jin\n(MS/PhD, 2018-2025), now with MangoBoost, Bellevue, WA\nDr. Nikita Lazarev\n(MS/PhD, 2019-2025), now co-founder of a stealth startup (AI infra)\nDr. Shaojie Xiang\n(MS/PhD, 2018-2025), now with AWS AI, Santa Clara, CA\nDr. Chenhui Deng\n(PhD, 2018-2024,\ndissertation\n) now with\nNVIDIA Research, Santa Clara, CA\nDr. Yichi Zhang\n(PhD, 2018-2023,\ndissertation\n) now with Google DeepMind, Mountain View, CA\nDr. Zhongyuan Zhao\n(PostDoc, 2020-2023) now with Qualcomm, San Diego, CA\nProf. Qi Sun\n(PostDoc, 2022-2023) now with\nZhejiang University\nDr. Ecenur Ustun\n(PhD, 2016-2022,\ndissertation\n) now with Meta Reality Labs, Redmond, WA\nProf. Debjit Pal\n(PostDoc, 2019-2022) now with\nUniversity of Illinois Chicago, Chicago, IL\nDr. Yi-Hsiang (Sean) Lai\n(PhD, 2016-2021,\ndissertation\n) now with AWS AI, Santa Clara, CA\nDr. Yuan Zhou\n(PhD, 2015-2021,\ndissertation\n) now with AWS AI, Santa Clara, CA\nDr. Nitish Srivastava\n(PhD, 2014-2020,\ndissertation\n) now with\nMeta, New York City, NY\nDr. Ritchie Zhao\n(PhD, 2014-2019,\ndissertation\n) now with\nNVIDIA, Redmond, WA\nProf. Cunxi Yu\n(PostDoc, 2018-2019) now with\nUniversity of Maryland, College Park, MD\nDr. Zhenghong (John) Jiang\n(PostDoc, 2016-2019) now with\nCadence, San Jose, CA\nDr. Steve Dai\n(PhD, 2013-2018,\ndissertation\n) now with\nNVIDIA Research, Santa Clara, CA\nDr. Gai Liu\n(PhD, 2013-2018,\ndissertation\n) now with Google, Mountain View, CA\nDr. Mingxing Tan\n(PostDoc, 2013-2015)\nnow with Waymo Research,\nMountain View, CA"
  },
  "serper::Zhou Lu": {
    "homepage": "https://leozoroaster.github.io/",
