    "homepage_text": "Xuchen You | Joint Center for Quantum Information and Computer Science (QuICS)\nSkip to main content\nSearch\nShow Main Menu\nSearch\nPeople\nXuchen You\nGraduate Student (2020-2023)\nGraduate Student\n,\nAlumni\nContact Information\nxyou@cs.umd.edu\nOffice:\n3257 Atlantic Building\nBio\nXuchen You was a QuICS graduate student from 2020 to 2023.  He received his PhD in Computer Science from the University of Maryland in 2023.  He is interested in quantum algorithms and machine learning. His advisor at QuICS was Xiaodi Wu.\nRecent Publications\nAnalyzing Convergence in Quantum Neural Networks: Deviations from Neural Tangent Kernels\n,\n,\narXiv\n,\n(\n2023\n)\nA Convergence Theory for Over-parameterized Variational Quantum Eigensolvers\n,\n,\narXiv\n,\n(\n2022\n)\nExponentially Many Local Minima in Quantum Neural Networks\n,\n,\nProceedings of the 38th International Conference on Machine Learning, PMLR\n,\n139\n,\n12144–12155\n,\n(\n2021\n)\nLoad More Publications\nRelated Events\nApril 6, 2023 4:00 pm\nDissertation Defense\nOptimization Problems in Quantum Machine Learning: when are variational algorithms trainable\nXuchen You\n(QuICS)\nView All QuICS Events\nAffiliated Research Centers\nRQS\nLearn More"
  },
  "serper::Dana Yang": {
