    "homepage_text": "Mingrui Zhang\nMingrui Zhang\nPh.D. Candidate, Imperial College London\nApplied Modelling & Computation Group\nEmail: mingrui.zhang18 (at) imperial.ac.uk\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\nBiography\nMingrui Zhang\n(\n张铭睿\n)\nis a final year Ph.D. student at\nImperial College London\nadvised by\nProf. Matthew Piggott\n.\n          He obtained my Master's degree from Imperial College London and Bachelor's degree from\nZhejiang University\n. Previously,\n          he worked with\nDr. Tiantian Liu\nand\nDr. Yuanming Hu\nat\nTaichi Graphics\n.\n\n          His research interests includes physics-based simulation, machine learning and their applications in scientific computing, computer graphics, generative AI.\nNews\nGenesis\nis released. Welcome contribution from everyone!\nResearch\n(* indicates equal contribution)\nBAG: Body-Aligned 3D Wearable Asset Generation\nZhongjin Luo\n,\nYang Li\n,\nMingrui Zhang\n,\nSenbo Wang\n,\nHan Yan\n,\nXibin Song\n,\nTaizhang Shang\n,\nWei Mao\n,\nHongdong Li\n,\nXiaoguang Han\n, \n              and\nPan Ji\narXiv  2025\n/\nHomepage\n/\nPaper\n/\nbibtex\n@article{luo2025bag,\n          title={BAG: Body-Aligned 3D Wearable Asset Generation},\n          author={Zhongjin Luo and Yang Li and Mingrui Zhang and Senbo Wang and Han Yan and Xibin Song and Taizhang Shang and Wei Mao and Hongdong Li and Xiaoguang Han and Pan Ji},\n          year={2025},\n          eprint={2501.16177},\n          archivePrefix={arXiv},\n          primaryClass={cs.CV},\n          url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.16177}, \n        }\nFrom PIV to LSPIV: Harnessing deep learning for environmental flow velocimetry\nJames Tlhomole\n,\nGraham O Hughes\n,\nMingrui Zhang\n,\n                    and\nMatthew D Piggott\nJournal of Hydrology  2025\n/\nPaper\n/\nbibtex\n@article{Tlhomole2025piv,\n        title={From PIV to LSPIV: Harnessing deep learning for environmental flow velocimetry},\n        author={James B Tlhomole and Graham O Hughes and Mingrui Zhang and Matthew D Piggott},\n        journal={Journal of Hydrology},\n        volume={649},\n        year={2025}\n      }\nPhyCAGE: Physically Plausible Compositional 3D Asset Generation from a Single Image\nHan Yan\n,\nMingrui Zhang\n,\nYang Li\n,\nChao Ma\n,\n                    and\nPan Ji\narXiv 2024\n/\nProject Page\n/\nPaper\n/\nVideo\n/\nbibtex\n@misc{yan2024phycage,\n        title={PhyCAGE: Physically Plausible Compositional 3D Asset Generation from a Single Image}, \n        author={Han Yan and Mingrui Zhang and Yang Li and Chao Ma and Pan Ji},\n        year={2024},\n        eprint={2411.18548},\n        archivePrefix={arXiv},\n        primaryClass={cs.CV},\n        url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.18548}, \n    }\nTowards Universal Mesh Movement Networks\nMingrui Zhang\n,\nChunyang Wang\n,\nStephan Kramer\n,\nJoseph G. Wallwork\n,\nSiyi Li\n,\nJiancheng Liu\n,\nXiang Chen\nand\nMatthew D Piggott\nNeurIPS 2024\n/\nProject Page\n/\nPaper\n/\nCode\n/\nbibtex\nSpotlight Presentation\n@article{zhang2024um2n,\n  author={Mingrui Zhang and Chunyang Wang and Stephan Kramer and Joseph G. Wallwork and Siyi Li and Jiancheng Liu and Xiang Chen and Matthew D Piggott},\n  title={Towards Universal Mesh Movement Networks},\n  journal={Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems},\n  volume={37},\n  year={2024}\n}\nEnd-to-end wind turbine wake modelling with deep graph representation learning\nSiyi Li\n,\nMingrui Zhang\n,\n              and\nMatthew D Piggott\nApplied Energy 2023\n/\nPaper\n/\nbibtex\n@article{li2023graph,\n  title={End-to-end wind turbine wake modelling with deep graph representation learning},\n  author={Mingrui Zhang, Siyi Li and Matthew Piggott},\n  journal={Applied Energy},\n  volume={339},\n  year={2023}\n}\nLearning to Estimate and Refine Fluid Motion with Physical Dynamics\nMingrui Zhang\n,\nJianhong Wang\n,\nJames Tlhomole\nand\nMatthew D Piggott\nICML 2022\n/\nPaper\n/\nCode\n/\nbibtex\n@InProceedings{zhang22learning,\n  title = {Learning to Estimate and Refine Fluid Motion with Physical Dynamics},\n  author = {Zhang, Mingrui and Wang, Jianhong and Tlhomole, James B and Piggott, Matthew},\n  booktitle = {Proceedings of the 39th International Conference on Machine Learning},\n  year = {2022}\n}\nM2N: mesh movement networks for pde solvers\nWenbing Song\n*\n,\nMingrui Zhang\n*\n,\nJoseph G. Wallwork\n,\nJunpeng Gao\n,\nZheng Tian\nFanglei Sun\nMatthew D Piggott\nJunqing Chen\nZuoqiang Shi\nXiang Chen\nand\nJun Wang\nNeurIPS 2022\n/\nPaper\n/\nbibtex\n@article{song2022m2n,\n  author={Wenbin song and Mingrui Zhang and Joseph G. Wallwork and Junpeng Gao and Zheng Tian and Fangfei Sun and Matthew D Piggott and Junqing Chen and Zuoqiang Shi and Xiang Chen and Jun Wang},\n  title={M2N: mesh movement networks for pde solvers},\n  journal={Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems},\n  volume={35},\n  year={2022}\n}\nNeural network control of fully-differentiable fluid-rigid structure interaction problem\nJianhui Yang\n,\nMingrui Zhang\n,\nAndrew G Buchan\n,\n                    and\nLiang Yang\n,\nCIMNE 2023\n/\nPaper\n/\nbibtex\n@article{yang23dffsi,\n      title = {Neural network control of fully-differentiable fluid-rigid structure interaction problem},\n      author = {Jianhui Yang and Mingrui Zhang and Andrew G Buchan and Liang Yang},\n      journal = {CIMNE 2023},\n      year = {2023}\n      }\nComplex locomotion skill learning via differentiable physics\nYu Fang\n*\n,\nJiancheng Liu\n*\n,\nMingrui Zhang\n*\n,,\nJiasheng Zhang\n,\nYidong Ma\n,\nMinchen Li\n,\nYuanming Hu\n,\nChenfanfu Jiang\n,\n              and\nTiantian Liu\n,\narXiv 2022\n/\nPaper\n/\nCode\n/\nbibtex\n@article{fang22complex,\ntitle = {Complex locomotion skill learning via differentiable physics},\nauthor = {Yu Fang and Jiancheng Liu and Mingrui Zhang and Jiasheng Zhang and Yidong Ma and Minchen Li and Yuanming Hu and Chenfanfu Jiang and Tiantian Liu},\njournal = {arXiv preprint arXiv:2206.02341},\nyear = {2022}\n}\nE2N: error estimation networks for goal-oriented mesh adaptation\nJoseph G. Wallwork\n,\nJingyi Lu\n,\nMingrui Zhang\n,\n              and\nMatthew D Piggott\narXiv 2022\n/\nPaper\n/\nbibtex\n@article{joe2022e2n,\ntitle = {E2N: error estimation networks for goal-oriented mesh adaptation},\nauthor = {Joseph G. Wallwork and Jingyi Lu and Mingrui Zhang and Matthew D Piggott},\njournal = {https://arxiv.org/pdf/2207.11233.pdf},\nyear = {2022}\n}\nUnsupervised Learning of Particle Image Velocimetry\nMingrui Zhang\n,\n                    and\nMatthew D Piggott\nISC 2020\n/\nPaper\n/\nCode\n/\nbibtex\n@InProceedings{zhang20unsupervised,\n  title = {Unsupervised Learning of Particle Image Velocimetry},\n  author = {Mingrui Zhang and Matthew D Piggott},\n  booktitle = {International Conference on High Performance Computing (ISC)},\n  year = {2020}\n}\nMiscellaneous\nDoriflow\n:\n              A CPU/GPU fluid simulation engine integrated with Blender, supporting fluid-rigid coupling, white-water, non-newtonian fluids, surface reconstruction etc."
