    "homepage_text": "Home | Hangfeng He\nHangfeng He\nI am an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Computer Science\nand the\nGoergen Institute for Data Science and Artificial Intelligence\nat the University of Rochester. I obtained my Ph.D. from the University of Pennsylvania, where I worked with\nDan Roth\nand\nWeijie Su\n. I received my bachelor’s degree from Peking University.\nMy research interests include natural language processing and machine learning, with a focus on interpreting deep learning models, leveraging indirect signals, and advancing reasoning in large language models.\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n] [\nCV\n]\nContact\nOffice: 3009 Wegmans Hall, 250 Hutchison Rd, Rochester, NY 14620\nEmail: hangfeng.he@rochester.edu"
  },
  "serper::Yuan Deng": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/uchicago.edu/yudeng/research",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yu Deng's Homepage - Research\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYu Deng's Homepage\nResearch\nI am interested in anything that is related to PDEs.\nTopics that I have been looking at recently include: probabilistic theory of PDEs, wave turbulence and kinetic theory, statistical physics\nand quantum field theory\n, inviscid and Landau damping.\nTopics that I may be looking at in the future include: random geometry, formation and non-formation of singularity, infinite dimensional KAM theory.\nSelected\nP\napers (full\npublication list\n):\nKinetic theory / Wave turbulence:\nY. Deng, Z. Hani and X. Ma.\nLong time derivation of Boltzmann equation from hard sphere dynamics\n.\nAnn. of Math.,\nto appear.\nY. Deng and Z. Hani.\nLong time justification of wave turbulence theory\n. arXiv:2311.10082.\nY. Deng and Z. Hani.\nFull derivation of the wave kinetic equation\n.\nInvent. Math.\n233 (2023), no. 2, 543\n–\n724.\nNotes on the long-time derivation of Boltzmann:\nExpository notes:\nOverview of the proof\n(surveys the main ingredients of the proof),\nToy model algorithms\n(explains the cutting algorithm with full details in a simplified setting)\nPKU lecture series:\nLecture 1\n,\nLectures 2-3\n,\nLecture 4\n,\nLecture 5\n(\np\nlease note there might be minor notational differences between the notes and the actual lectures)\nProbabilistic PDEs:\nB. Bringmann, Y. Deng, A. Nahmod and H. Yue.\nInvariant Gibbs measures for the three dimensional cubic nonlinear wave equation\n.\nInvent. Math.\n236 (2024), no. 3, 1133\n–1\n41\n1.\nY. Deng, A. Nahmod and H. Yue.\nRandom tensors, propagation of randomness, and nonlinear dispersive equations\n.\nInvent. Math.\n228 (2022), no. 2, 539\n–\n686.\nY. Deng, A. Nahmod and H. Yue.\nInvariant Gibbs measures and global strong solutions for nonlinear Schrödinger equations in dimension two\n.\nAnn. of Math. (2)\n200 (2024), no. 2, 399\n–486.\nMiscellaneous:\nY. Deng and N. Masmoudi.\nLong time instability of the Couette flow in low Gevrey spaces\n.\nComm. Pure Appl. Math.\n76 (2023), no. 10, 2804\n–\n2887.\nY. Deng.\nOn growth of Sobolev norms for energy critical NLS on irrational tori: Small energy case\n.\nComm. Pure Appl. Math.\n72 (2019), no. 4, 801–834.\nY. Deng, A. Ionescu, B. Pausader and F. Pusateri.\nGlobal solutions of the gravity-capillary water wave system in three dimensions\n.\nActa Math.\n219 (2017), no. 2, 213–402.\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Haonan Duan": {
    "homepage": "https://haonan-duan.github.io/",
    "emails": [
