    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJiaming Xu\n（许嘉铭）\nI'm currently a visiting assistant professor at Ohio State University. Before coming to Columbus, I spent a year as a postdoc at\nKTH\nand\nInstitut\nMittag-Leffler\n, mentored by\nGaultier Lambert\n.\nI did my PhD in math department of University of Wisconsin-Madison. My advisors were\nVadim Gorin\nand\nBenedek Valko\n.\nMy\nCV\n.\nI'm broadly interested in probability theory, and its connections to combinatorics and representation theory. My current focus lies in integrable probability and random matrices.\nRemark: Jiaming is a quite popular name in China...There is another\nprobabilist\nwith the same (spelling of) name as me.\nContact\nDepartment of Mathematics, Ohio State University\nColumbus, United States\nOffice:\nMath Tower 542\nEmail:\njxu0800@gmail.com\nPublications/Preprints\n(With\nCesar Cuenca\n)\nLaw of Large Numbers for continuous $N$-particle ensembles at fixed temperature. [\narxiv\n].\n2.\n(With\nVadim Gorin\nand\nLingfu Zhang\n) Airy_beta line ensemble and its Laplace transform. [\narxiv\n], submitted.\n3.\n(With\nDavid Keating\n)\nAiry limit for &\\beta&\n-additions through Dunkl operators\n. [\narxiv\n]\n, submitted.\n4.Rectangular matrix additions in low and high temperatures.\n[arxiv]\n, submitted.\n5.\n(With\nVadim Gorin\n) Random sorting networks: edge limit.\n[arxiv]\n.\nAnnales de l'Institut Henri Poincare: Probability and Statistics\n.\nTalks and conferences\nSeminar talks:\nJuly 2025. Chinese Academy of Sciences, probability seminar.\nMay 2025. Leipzig University, integrable probability seminar.\nApril 2025. KTH, probability seminar.\nNovember 2024. Institut Mittag-Leffler,\nRandom Matrices and Scaling Limits\n.\nMarch 2024. MIT integrable probability seminar.\nMarch 2024.\nRandomness and Lie-theoretic\nStructures (participant talks).\nOctober 2023. Ohio States combinatorics and probability seminar.\nApril 2023. UW-Madison probability seminar.\nFebruary 2023. UC Berkeley probability seminar.\nOctober 2022. Virginia probability seminar.\nSeptember 2022.\nGraduate student probability conference.\nRecent or upcoming conferences:\nJune 23-27, 2025,\nWorkshop on stochastic interacting particle systems and random matrices\nAugust 28-December 13, 2024,\nRandom Matrices and Scaling Limits\nMarch 11-June 14 , 2024.\nGeometry, Statistical Mechanics, and Integrability.\nMarch 4-5, 2024,\nRandomness and Lie-theoretic Structures\n.\nAugust 14-August 25, 2023.\nDimers: Combinatorics, Representation Theory and Physics\n.\nJune 26-June 30, 2023.\nRandom Matrix Theory and Applications.\nMay 14- May 18, 2023.\nThe 24th Midrasha Mathematicae: Random Schrödinger Operators and   Random Matrices\n.\nTeaching\nI'm lecturing Math2173 (Calculus 2) at OSU, 2025 fall.\nI have been teaching assistant of several courses at UW-Madison. Details below.\nMath 221, Calculus and Analytic Geometry I: Fall 2022, Fall 2023.\nMath 22\n2\n, Calculus and Analytic Geometry II:\nFall\n20\n19\n, Fall 20\n20, Fall 2021, Spring 2023\n.\nMath 2\n34\n, Calculus and Analytic Geometry III:\nSpring 2020.\nMath 320, Linear Algebra and Differential Equations: Spring 2022.\nMath 217, Calculus with Algebra and Trigonometry II: Spring 2021.\nOutreach\nI was a co-organizer for the\nGraduate Student Probability Conference\n, September 10-11, 2022.\nI was an organizer and problem writer for the\nmega math meet\nin May 2023.\nOthers\nI love choral music. Below is my annual piece of 2023:\nSunrise Mass -\nOla Gjeilo\nPresented by Echo Chamber Choir from Shanghai, during a time period when the city was recovering from the pandemic.\nAnd an astoundingly beautiful piece I heard in 2024:\nSalve Regina - Franco Prinsloo -\nStellenbosch University Choir\nA lovely Swedish traditional song for my 2025:\nI denna ljuva sommartid\" (In this sweet summertime)\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  },
