    "homepage_text": "Kaizhao Liang - AI Researcher\nKaizhao Liang\nKaizhao Liang\nAI Researcher | Austin, Texas, United States\nAbout\nI am a Ph.D. student advised by\nProf. Qiang Liu\nfrom UT Austin.\nIn the past, I was a senior tech lead at\nSambaNova Systems\nworking on software and hardware codesign.\nBefore that, I obtained my B.S. in CS from UIUC advised by\nProf. Bo Li\n.\nRecently, I joined Microsoft as a Senior Researcher working on AI-agents self-improvement.\nI am also actively contributing to opensourced frameworks, such as\nGradio\nand\nTransformers\n.\nInterests\nEfficient training and efficient neural architecture, for more details please refer to my\nresearch statement\nOpensource Contribution: 🤗Huggingface timm adopts Cautious Optimizers\nOne of the last minute papers I added support for that delayed this release was 'Cautious Optimizers'... Consider me impressed, this boost appears more consistent than some of the new optimizers.\n— Ross Wightman (@wightmanr)\nDecember 3, 2024\nBlogposts\nYour Linear Layers are Secretly Fast Weights\nDesign Memory Mechanism from Optimizers\nSelected Publications\nCautious Weight Decay [ICLR 2026]\nLizhang Chen, Jonathan Li,\nKaizhao Liang\n, Baiyu Su, Cong Xie, Nuo Wang Pierse, Chen Liang, Ni Lao, Qiang Liu\nCautious Optimizers: Improving Training with One Line of Code [ICLR 2026]\nKaizhao Liang\n, Lizhang Chen, Bo Liu, Qiang Liu\nMemory-Efficient LLM Training with Online Subspace Descent [NeurIPS 2024]\nKaizhao Liang\n, Bo Liu, Lizhang Chen, Qiang Liu\nPixelated Butterfly: Simple and Efficient Sparse training for Neural Network Models [ICLR 2022]\nBeidi Chen, Tri Dao,\nKaizhao Liang\n, Jiaming Yang, Zhao Song, Atri Rudra, Christopher Re\nUncovering the Connections Between Adversarial Transferability and Knowledge Transferability [ICML 2020]\nKaizhao Liang*\n, Jacky. Y. Zhang*, Boxin Wang, Zhuolin Yang, Sanmi Koyejo, Bo Li\nPast Media Coverage\nSambaNova and Hugging Face make AI chatbot deployment easier with one-click integration – VentureBeat\nCoverage on advances in accessible AI deployment involving Hugging Face.\nSambaNova challenges OpenAI’s O1 model with LLaMA 3.1-powered demo on Hugging Face – VentureBeat\nHighlights collaboration and emerging competition in the generative AI space.\nReview Service\nCVPR[2021-2023], ICCV[2021, 2025], ICLR[2022-2024], AISTATS2022, NEURIPS[2023-2025]\nContact\nkaizhaol@utexas.edu"
  },
