ce on Artificial Intelligence, 2019\nBN-invariant Sharpness Regularizes the Training Model to Better Generalization\nMingyang Yi, Huishuai Zhang, Wei Chen, Zhiming Ma, Tie-Yan Liu\nIJCAI, 2019\nOn the local Hessian in back-propagation\nHuishuai Zhang, Wei Chen, Tie-Yan Liu\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), December 2018\nReshaped Wirtinger flow for solving quadratic system of equations\nHuishuai Zhang, Yingbin Liang\nNeural Information Processing System (NeurIPS), Barcelona, Spain, December 2016\nAccelerated method for solving quadratic system of equations\nYi Zhou, Huishuai Zhang, Yingbin Liang\nAllerton Conference, Champaign, Illinois, September 2016\nOn orthogonal compressive sensing\nYi Zhou, Huishuai Zhang, Yingbin Liang\nAllerton Conference on Communication, Control and Computing, Champaign, Illinois, September 2016\nProvable non-convex phase retrieval with outliers: Median truncated Wirtinger flow\nHuishuai Zhang, Yuejie Chi, Yingbin Liang\nICML, New York City, USA, June 2016\nAnalysis of robust PCA via local incoherence\nHuishuai Zhang, Yi Zhou, Yingbin Liang\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NIPS), Montreal, Canada, December 2015\nSecret key capacity: Talk or keep silent?\nHuishuai Zhang, Yingbin Liang, Lifeng Lai\nProc. IEEE International Symposium on Information Theory (ISIT), Hong Kong, China, June 2015\nTwo-key generation for a cellular model with a helper\nHuishuai Zhang, Yingbin Liang, Lifeng Lai, Shlomo Shamai\nProc. IEEE International Symposium on Information Theory (ISIT), Hong Kong, China, June 2015\nKey capacity region for a cellular source model\nHuishuai Zhang, Yingbin Liang, Lifeng Lai\nProc. IEEE Information Theory Workshop (ITW), Hobart, Tasmania, Australia, November 2014\nHelper-assisted asymmetric two key generation\nHuishuai Zhang, Yingbin Liang, Lifeng Lai\nProc. Asilomar Conference on Signals, Systems and Computers, Pacific Grove, CA, USA, November 2014\nThe secret key-private key generation over three terminals: Capacity region\nHuishuai Zhang, Lifeng Lai, Yingbin Liang, Hua Wang\nProc. IEEE International Symposium on Information Theory (ISIT), Honolulu, HI, USA, June 2014\nJournals\n©Plug-in Authorizatio...[truncated]"
