    "homepage_text": "Ruize Gao\n      -  Luxembourg Institute of Health\nLuxembourg Institute of Health Home\nSearch content at Luxembourg Institute of Health\nContact expert\nView Scopus Profile\nRuize Gao\nDoctor, PhD\nPostdoctoral Fellow\n,\nTumor  Immunotherapy and Microenvironment\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-3582-4726\nrue Nicolas-Ernest Barblé\n,\n6\n1210\nLuxembourg\nLuxembourg\n1278\nCitations\n2015\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Ruize Gao is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nSorafenib\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n100%\nAutophagy\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n93%\nTumor Microenvironment\nMedicine and Dentistry\n62%\nHippo Signaling Pathway\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n61%\nNeoplasm\nMedicine and Dentistry\n54%\nSmall Hairpin RNA\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n46%\nFUNDC1\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n46%\nZyxin\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n46%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nProjects\n2\nFinished\nC2I:\nCHECKPOINT INHIBITORS IMPROVEMENT FOR THE TREATMENT OF CANCER\nJanji, B.\n(PI),\nGao, R.\n(Partner) &\nVan Moer, K.\n(Partner)\nFNR - Fonds National de la Recherche\n1/04/22\n→\n15/07/24\nProject\n:\nResearch\nMalignant Neoplasm\n100%\nImmunotherapy\n100%\nImmune Checkpoint Blockade\n50%\nCheckpoint Inhibitors\n50%\nCancer Treatment\n50%\nINCITE:\nInvestigating  the role of CMTM proteins in the regulation of PD-L1 expression\nJanji, B.\n(PI),\nRamos, T.\n(Partner) &\nGao, R.\n(Partner)\nFNRS - Fonds National de la Recherche Scientifique\n1/04/22\n→\n14/03/25\nProject\n:\nResearch\nMesenchymal-Epithelial Transition\n100%\nProgrammed Death 1 Ligand 1\n100%\nEpithelial Mesenchymal Transition\n60%\nProgrammed Death-ligand 1 Expression\n50%\nProgrammed Death-ligand 1 (PD-L1)\n50%\nResearch output\n10\nArticle\n1\nEditorial\nTargeting the atypical chemokine receptor 2 (Ackr2) improves the benefit of anti-PD-1 immunotherapy in melanoma mouse model\nNoman, M. Z.,\nSzpakowska, M.\n, Xiao, M.,\nGao, R.\n,\nVan Moer, K.\n, Kumar, A.,\nOllert, M.\n,\nBerchem, G.\n,\nChevigné, A.\n&\nJanji, B.\n,\n18 Apr 2025\n,\nIn:\nOncoImmunology.\n14\n,\n1\n,\n9 p.\n, 2494426.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nChemokine Receptor\n100%\nImmunotherapy\n100%\nMelanoma\n100%\nMouse Model\n100%\nMelanoma Mouse Model\n100%\n1\nCitation\n(Scopus)\nProtocol to screen for Sorafenib resistance regulators using pooled lentiviral shRNA library and a Sorafenib-resistant hepatocellular carcinoma cell model\nGao, R.\n, Tang, F. & Christofori, G.,\n16 Jun 2023\n,\nIn:\nSTAR Protocols.\n4\n,\n2\n, 102273.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nSmall Hairpin RNA\n100%\nSorafenib\n100%\nLentiviral shRNA\n100%\nSorafenib-resistant\n25%\nHepatocellular Carcinoma Model\n25%\n7\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nHypoxia features as potential indicators in prognosis, immunotherapy and drug screening in hepatocellular carcinoma patients\nGao, R.\n,\nNov 2022\n,\nIn:\nTranslational Cancer Research.\n11\n,\n11\n,\np. 3932-3934\n3 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nEditorial\nOpen Access\n1\nCitation\n(Scopus)\nUSP29-mediated HIF1α stabilization is associated with Sorafenib resistance of hepatocellular carcinoma cells by upregulating glycolysis\nGao, R.\n, Buechel, D., Kalathur, R. K. R., Morini, M. F., Coto-Llerena, M., Ercan, C., Piscuoglio, S., Chen, Q., Blumer, T., Wang, X., Dazert, E., Heim, M. H., Hall, M. N., Tang, F. & Christofori, G.,\nJul 2021\n,\nIn:\nOncogenesis.\n10\n,\n7\n, 52.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nHypoxia Inducible Factor 1\n100%\nSorafenib\n100%\nCarcinoma Cell\n100%\nUSP29\n100%\nSorafenib Resistance\n100%\n50\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nLATS1 but not LATS2 represses autophagy by a kinase-independent scaffold function\nTang, F.,\nGao, R.\n, Jeevan-Raj, B., Wyss, C. B., Kalathur, R. K. R., Piscuoglio, S., Ng, C. K. Y., Hindupur, S. K., Nuciforo, S., Dazert, E., Bock, T., Song, S., Buechel, D., Morini, M. F., Hergovich, A., Matthias, P., Lim, D. S., Terracciano, L. M., Heim, M. H. & Hall, M. N.\n& 1 others\n,\nChristofori, G.\n,\n1 Dec 2019\n,\nIn:\nNature Communications.\n10\n,\n1\n, 5755.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nAutophagy\n100%\nProtein Kinase A\n100%\nScaffolding Function\n100%\nKinase-independent\n100%\nUbiquitination\n28%\n51\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 11 research outputs\nYour message has successfully been sent.\nYour message was not sent due to an error.\nx\nContact Ruize Gao\nSubject:\n*\nMessage:\n*\nYour name:\n*\nYour email:\n*\nSend me a copy of this message\n*required field\nSee privacy policy in the footer of the page\nCancel\nSend"
