    "homepage_text": "Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJie Shen\nAssistant Professor (Tenure-Track)\nDepartment of Computer Science\nStevens Institute of Technology\nEmail: jieshen.sjtu [AT] gmail [DOT] com\nOffice: Gateway Academic Center South 351\nShort bio:\nI obtained my B.S. in Mathematics & Applied Mathematics in 2011 and M.S. in Computer Science in 2014, both from Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\nI obtained my\nPh.D.\nin Computer Science in 2018 from Rutgers University-New Brunswick.\nI was a visiting scholar at National University of Singapore (2013 - 2014) and at Duke University (Summer 2018).\nNews\nFeb. 2024: Grace arrived!!!\nFeb. 2023: Received\nNSF CAREER award.\nJan. 2021: Chloe arrived!!!\nResearch (\npublications\n,\ngoogle scholar\n,\ndblp\n)\nMy research interests lie in both the theoretical aspects and applications of machine learning. I am particularly interested in the following problems and their interplay:\nlearning in the presence of noise, e.g. label noise, malicious data;\nlearning with unsupervised learning, e.g. contrastive learning, pre-training;\ndata-efficient learning, e.g. high-dimensional statistics, meta/transfer learning\n;\nlabel-efficient learning, e.g. active learning, learning with enriched queries.\nGrants\nNSF-AF-2239376 (CAREER)\n,\nNSF-RI-1948133 (CRII)\nAcademic\nServices\nArea Chair:\nICML\n,\nNeurIPS\n,\nICLR (2024\n- present\n)\n, AISTATS (2025 - present),\nACML\n(\n2022\n- present\n)\nAction Editor/Associate Editor: TMLR, Visual Intelligence (2024 - present)\nReviewer: FOCS, COLT, ICML, NeurIPS/NIPS, AISTATS, ICLR, JMLR, ML, TIT, TSP, SP\nNSF Panel: 2023 - present\n(Chloe's 100th day)\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
