    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Huikang Liu\nHome\nResearch\nCode\nHuikang Liu\nHuikang Liu\nAssistant Professor\nSchool of Information Management and Engineering\nShanghai University of Finance and Economics\nRm 914, Research and Experiment Center Building,\nShanghai University of Finance and Economics\nNo. 777, Guoding Rd, Yangpu Block, Shanghai, China\nEmail: hkliu2014\nat\ngmail\ndot\ncom\nResearch Interests\nMy research area is mainly in continuous optimization and its application to machine learning, statistics and signal processing. I am particularly interested in various analytic issues of optimization problems and algorithms arising from these applications.\nResearch Experience & Education\nI received my BSE degree in Mathematics from\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nin 2014. Then, I received my PhD degree in Department of Systems Engineering and Engineering Management from\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong\n, under the supervision of\nProf. Anthony Man-Cho So\n. Then, I joint the Department of Electronic Engineering at the Chinese University of Hong Kong as a research associate, working with\nDr. Wing-Kin (Ken) Ma\n. After that, I worked as a research associate in the Business School at\nImperial College London\n, under the supervison of\nProf. Wolfram Wiesemann\n. Now, I am an assistant professor in Shanghai University of Finance and Economics."
  },
