    "homepage_text": "Zhanhong Tan's Homepage\nSearch\nZhanhong Tan\nPh.D. Candidate\nTsinghua University\nBiography\nZhanhong Tan is currently a Ph.D. student of\nAlgorithm, Architecture, and Chip Lab (Archip)\nat\nInstitute for Interdisciplinary Information Sciences (IIIS), Tsinghua University\n, following\nProf. Kaisheng Ma\n. His research interests lie in the fields of computer architecture and hardware-inspired algorithms for the deep learning domain. From 2019 to 2021, he was also in charge of the landing projects at the\nResearch Center for Advanced Architecture and Intelligent Chip\nin\nInstitute for Interdisciplinary Information Core Technology (IIISCT)\n, which is an affiliated research institute of IIIS, Tsinghua. He received a bachelor’s degree in microelectronics from\nSun Yat-sen University\n, where he was advised by\nProf. Zhiyi Yu\n.\nInterests\nComputer Architecture for Deep Learning\nHigh Power-Efficient Chip Design\nHardware-Inspired Algorithm Development\nEducation\nPh.D. Candidate in Computer Science, Now\nTsinghua University\nBachelor in Microelectronics, 2019\nSun Yat-sen University\nRecent News\nOne paper is accepted by ICML 2022!\nI was invited to ChinaSys 2021 (Hangzhou, Zhejiang) for our ISCA 2021 work.\nI was invited to the 2021 Formal Meeting of AI Industry Development Alliance (Xi'an, Shannxi).\nOur NN-Baton paper about chipet-based accelerator has been accepted in ISCA 2021!\nPublications\nCocco: Hardware-Mapping Co-Exploration towards Memory Capacity-Communication Optimization\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nZijian Zhu\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of ACM International Conference on Architectural Support for Programming Languages and Operating Systems (ASPLOS)\n, 2024\nCite\nA Scalable Multi‑Chiplet Deep Learning Accelerator with Hub‑Side 2.5D Heterogeneous Integration\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nYifu Wu\n,\nYannian Zhang\n,\nHaobing Shi\n,\nWuke Zhang\n,\nJingwei Cai\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of IEEE Hot Chips 35 Symposium (HCS)\n, 2023\nPDF\nCite\nPHEP: Paillier Homomorphic Encryption Processors for Privacy Preserving Applications in Cloud Computing\nGuiming Shi\n,\nYi Li\n,\nXueqiang Wang\n,\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nDapeng Cao\n,\nJingwei Cai\n,\nYuchen Wei\n,\nZehua Li\n,\nYifu Wu\n,\nWuke Zhang\n,\nWei Xu\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of IEEE Hot Chips 35 Symposium (HCS)\n, 2023\nPDF\nCite\nA 28nm 68MOPS 0.18μJ/Op Paillier Homomorphic Encryption Processor with Bit-Serial Sparse Ciphertext Computing\nGuiming Shi\n,\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nDapeng Cao\n,\nJingwei Cai\n,\nWuke Zhang\n,\nYifu Wu\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of IEEE International Solid-State Circuits Conference (ISSCC)\n, 2023\nPDF\nCite\nDOI\nYOLoC: Deploy Large-Scale Neural Networks by ROM-based Computing-in-Memory using Residual Branch on a Chip\nYiming Chen\n,\nGuodong Yin\n,\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nMingyen Lee\n,\nHongyang Chen\n,\nZekun Yang\n,\nYongpan Liu\n,\nHuazhong Yang\n,\nKaisheng Ma\n,\nXueqing Li\nIn\nProceedings of 59th Design Automation Conference (DAC)\n, 2022\nPDF\nCite\nFinding the Task-Optimal Low-Bit Sub-Distribution in Deep Neural Networks\nRunpei Dong\n,\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nMengdi Wu\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of 39th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n, 2022\nPDF\nCite\nNN-Baton: DNN Workload Orchestration and Chiplet Granularity Exploration for Multichip Accelerators\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nHongyu Cai\n,\nRunpei Dong\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of Annual International Symposium on Computer Architecture (ISCA)\n, 2021\nPDF\nCite\nDOI\nA 400MHz NPU with 7.8 TOPS²/W High-Performance-Guaranteed Efficiency in 55nm for Multi-Mode Pruning and Diverse Quantization Using Pattern-Kernel Encoding and Reconfigurable MAC Units\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nSia-Huat Tan\n,\nJan-Henrik Lambrechts\n,\nYannian Zhang\n,\nYifu Wu\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of IEEE Custom Integrated Circuits Conference (CICC)\n, 2021\nPDF\nCite\nSlides\nDOI\nPCNN: Pattern-based Fine-Grained Regular Pruning Towards Optimizing CNN Accelerators\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nJiebo Song\n,\nXiaolong Ma\n,\nSia-Huat Tan\n,\nHongyang Chen\n,\nYuanqing Miao\n,\nYifu Wu\n,\nShaokai Ye\n,\nYanzhi Wang\n,\nDehui Li\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of 57th Design Automation Conference (DAC)\n, 2020\nPDF\nCite\nSlides\nDOI\nSCAN: A Scalable Neural Networks Framework Towards Compact and Efficient Models\nLinfeng Zhang\n,\nZhanhong Tan\n,\nJiebo Song\n,\nJingwei Chen\n,\nChenglong Bao\n,\nKaisheng Ma\nIn\nProceedings of 32nd Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n, 2019\nPDF\nCite\nSource Document\nProjects\nQIMING 920 AI Chip (MUSEv2 Architecture)\nA unified architecture supporting diverse pruning and quantization modes\nQIMING 910 AI Chip (MUSEv1 Architecture)\nA sparsity-aware architecture for ternary networks (my first tape-out project!)\nContact\nFIT Building Floor 6, Tsinghua University, Haidian District, Beijing, 100084\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
