  "serper::Yichao Zhou": {
    "homepage": "https://yichaozhou.com/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/zhou13",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yichao-zhou-1bba8232/",
    "homepage_text": "Yichao Zhou\nSearch\nYichao Zhou\nPh.D. in Computer Science\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\nBiography\nI am a research scientist in\nVladlen Koltun\n‘s org at Apple, working on video world model and 3D perception. Previously, I worked at Apple SLAM team for ARKit. I earned my Ph.D. degree in\nComputer Science\nat UC Berkeley.\nPrior to Berkeley, I received my Bachelor’s degree from\nYao Class\nat Tsinghua University.\nIn high school, I represented my country at\nInternational Olympiad in Informatics (IOI 2011)\nand won a silver medal.\nMy expertise lies in video/image synthesis, 3D perception, and neural rendering, with a broader interest in AI and CV.\nMy PhD research focused on geometric deep learning from images with dissertation on\n“Learning to Detect Geometric Structures from Images for 3D Parsing”\n.\nInterests\nWorld Model\nArtificial Intelligence\nComputer vision\nEducation\nPh.D. in Computer Science, 2020\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\nB.Eng in Computer Science and Technology, 2015\nTsinghua University\nPublications\n”*” indicates equal contribution\nAleksei Bochkovskii\n,\nAmael Delaunoy\n,\nHugo Germain\n,\nMarcel Santos\n,\nYichao Zhou\n,\nStephan R. Richter\n,\nVladlen Koltun\n(2025).\nDepth Pro: Sharp Monocular Metric Depth in Less Than a Second\n.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) 2025.\nPreprint\nStergios Roumeliotis\n,\nYichao Zhou\n,\nAbdelhamid Dine\n,\nOleg Naroditsky\n(2024).\nPose Predictor for Moving Platform\n.\nPatent US20250110567A1, 2024.\nShichen Liu\n,\nYunxuan Cai\n,\nHaiwei Chen\n,\nYichao Zhou\n,\nYajie Zhao\n(2022).\nRapid Face Asset Acquisition with Recurrent Feature Alignment\n.\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2022.\nPDF\nShichen Liu\n,\nYichao Zhou\n,\nYajie Zhao\n(2021).\nVaPiD: A Rapid Vanishing Point Detector via Learned Optimizers\n.\nCVPR 2021.\nPDF\nYichao Zhou\n,\nShichen Liu\n,\nYi Ma\n(2021).\nNeRD: Neural 3D Reflection Symmetry Detector\n.\nCVPR 2021.\nPreprint\nCode\nYichao Zhou\n(2020).\nLearning to Detect Geometric Structures from Images for 3D Parsing\n.\nDoctoral Dissertation.\nPDF\nVideo\nYichao Zhou\n,\nJingwei Huang\n,\nXili Dai\n,\nLinjie Luo\n,\nZhili Chen\n,\nYi Ma\n(2020).\nHoliCity: A City-Scale Data Platform for Learning Holistic 3D Structures\n.\nTechnical Report. arXiv:2008.03286 [cs.CV].\nPreprint\nCode\nProject\nYichao Zhou\n,\nShichen Liu\n,\nYi Ma\n(2020).\nLearning to Detect 3D Reflection Symmetry for Single-View Reconstruction\n.\nTechnical Report. arXiv:2006.10042 [cs.CV].\nPreprint\nCode\nJingwei Huang\n,\nYichao Zhou\n,\nLeonidas Guibas\n(2020).\nManifoldPlus: A Robust and Scalable Watertight Manifold Surface Generation Method for Triangle Soups\n.\nTechnical Report. arXiv:2005.11621 [cs.GR].\nPreprint\nCode\nYichao Zhou\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\nJingwei Huang\n,\nYi Ma\n(2019).\nNeurVPS: Neural Vanishing Point Scanning via Conic Convolution\n.\nNeurIPS 2019.\nPreprint\nCode\nPoster\nSlides\nYichao Zhou\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\nYi Ma\n(2019).\nEnd-to-End Wireframe Parsing\n.\nICCV 2019.\nPreprint\nCode\nPoster\nJingwei Huang\n,\nYichao Zhou\n,\nThomas Funkhouser\n,\nLeonidas Guibas\n(2019).\nFrameNet: Learning Local Canonical Frames of 3D Surfaces from a Single RGB Image\n.\nICCV 2019.\nPreprint\nCode\nYichao Zhou\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\nSimon Zhai\n,\nQi Sun\n,\nZhili Chen\n,\nLi-Yi Wei\n,\nYi Ma\n(2018).\nLearning to Reconstruct 3D Manhattan Wireframes from a Single Image\n.\nICCV 2019\n(Oral Presentation)\n.\nPreprint\nCode\nDataset\nPoster\nVideo\nJingwei Huang*\n,\nYichao Zhou*\n,\nMatthias Nießner\n,\nJonathan Shewchuk\n,\nLeonidas Guibas\n(2018).\nQuadriFlow: A Scalable and Robust Method for Quadrangulation\n.\nSGP 2018\n(Best Paper)\n, Computer Graphics Forum.\nPDF\nCode\nDataset\nDemo\nOnline Tool\nYichao Zhou\n,\nWei Chu\n,\nSam Young\n,\nXin Chen\n(2017).\nBandNet: A Neural Network-Based, Multi-Instrument Beatles-Style MIDI Music Composition Machine\n.\nISMIR 2019.\nPreprint\nPoster\nSlides\nAudio\nYichao Zhou\n,\nBruce R. Donald\n,\nJianyang Zeng\n(2016).\nParallel Computational Protein Design\n.\nMethods in Molecular Biology.\nPDF\nCode\nYichao Zhou\n,\nYuexin Wu\n,\nJianyang Zeng\n(2015).\nComputational Protein Design Using AND/OR Branch-and-Bound Search\n.\nRECOMB 2015.\nPreprint\nCode\nDataset\nSlides\nYichao Zhou\n,\nJianyang Zeng\n(2015).\nMassively Parallel A* Search on a GPU\n.\nAAAI 2015\n(Oral Presentation)\n.\nPDF\nCode\nSlides\nAppendix\nYichao Zhou\n,\nWei Xu\n,\nBruce R. Donald\n,\nJianyang Zeng\n(2014).\nAn Efficient Parallel Algorithm for Accelerating Computational Protein Design\n.\nISMB 2014, Bioinformatics.\nPDF\nCode\nDataset\nPoster\nSlides\nAwards\nSilver medal\nin\nInternational Olympiad in Informatics (\nIOI\n2011)\nGolden medal\nin\nChinese National Olympiad in Informatics (\nNOI\n2010)\nSilver medal\nin 2011 ACM-ICPC Asia Beijing Regional Contest (Teammate:\nFangrui Song\nand\nShunhao Fan\n)\nPress Coverage\nSongwriter AI emulates the Beatles with a little help from its friends\nNew Scientist Magazine, Issue 3214\nArchive.org\nBlog Posts\nHow to Downgrade the MacOS System (2025 Version)\nA guide to downgrading from macOS beta to a stable version on Apple Silicon Macs, including backup tips and Migration Assistant workarounds.\nMay 28, 2025\n3 min read\nIT\nUniform Sampling on Disks, Shells, Balls, and Triangles.\nI will discuss the generalized approach to sample points on an arbitrary geometry.\nMar 10, 2024\n3 min read\nmath\nOrientation Estimation from IMUs with Error-State Kalman Filters\nI will discuss the math and intuition behind the 3D altitude filter, linear Kalman filter, extended Kalman filter, error-state Kalman filter, and Lie group calculus for deriving the math for orientation estimation.\nOct 23, 2022\n17 min read\nmath\nThe Risk of GLD and Gold ETFs\nI will summarize my superficial understand of the risk in paper gold.\nMar 26, 2022\n4 min read\ninvestment\nVanishing Points and “Gaussian Sphere Representation”\nI will summarize what vanishing points (and their “Gaussian sphere representation”) are, how to represent them, what information they encode, how to find them, and why they are useful.\nApr 2, 2019\n7 min read\nmath\nExperience\nFebruary 2021 –\nPresent\nCalifornia, USA\nResearch Scientist\nApple Inc.\nI am a research scientist in\nVladlen Koltun\n‘s Photorealism team at Apple, working on video world model. Previously, I worked at the Apple SLAM team for ARKit on Vision Pro.\nMay 2019 –\nAugust 2019\n3000 El Camino Real, Palo Alto, CA 94306\nResearch Intern\nBytedance Inc.\nI created a real-world data platform of urban environments by aligning the city CAD model to the street-view panorama images. I was advised by\nYi Ma\nand\nLinjie Luo\n.\nMay 2018 –\nAugust 2018\n345 Park Ave, San Jose, CA 95110\nResearch Intern\nAdobe Research\nI did the research on how to reconstruct a 3D scene for urban environments by utilizing their global regularities and symmetries. I enjoyed my time with my advisors\nQi Sun\n,\nZhili Chen\n,\nLi-Yi Wei\n, and\nKalyan Sunkavalli\n.\nMay 2017 –\nAugust 2017\n523 Ocean Front Walk, Venice, CA 90291\nResearch Intern\nSnapchat Inc.\nI worked on a project about algorithm-based Beatles-style music composition with the help from an outstanding composer and percussionist\nSam Young\nat UCLA. I was advised by Wei Chu and Xin Chen.\nMay 2016 –\nAugust 2016\n1901 S Bascom Ave #1300, Campbell, CA 95008\nResearch Intern\nBellus 3D Inc.\nDuring the internship, I implemented a software to\ndeform\na face mesh to fit the point cloud of a scanned face along with the\nMorphable Face Model\n. I was advised by\nJames Davis\nand\nJing Liu\n.\nSeptember 2015 –\nDecember 2020\nUniversity of California, Berkeley, CA 94720\nResearch Assistant\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\nI received my Ph.D. degree here. My advisor is\nProf. Yi Ma\n. My dissertation is on “Learning to Detect Geometric Structures from Images for 3D Parsing”.\nDecember 2013 –\nJune 2015\n30 Shuangqing Rd, Haidian District, Beijing 100084\nResearch Assistant\nTsinghua University\nAdvised by\nJianyang Zeng\n, I did research related to the proteins’ 3D structures in the\nMachine Learning and Computational Biology Group\nat IIIS when I was an undergraduate. I designed fast and massively parallel combinotorial search\nalgorithms\nand tested them on the\nprotein design\nproblems. I also implemented a CUDA version of\nRELION\nto accelerate the 3D reconstruction of protein structures from cryo-microscopy images, which later turned into my undergraduate thesis.\nAugust 2013 –\nNovember 2013\n5 Danling St, Haidian District, Beijing 100080\nResearch Intern\nMicrosoft Research Asia\nI was a research intern in the Natural Language Processing Group at MSRA, advised by\nJianwen Zhang\n. I studied method of applying\nMarkov Logic Network\nfor the knowledge database completion problem to fill in the missing entires in\nFreebase\n.\nService\nI was a teaching assistant of the following courses at UC Berkeley:\nCS 189 / 289A:\nIntroduction to Machine Learning\nPhysics 8A: Introductory Physics\nSkills\nPython\nDeep Learning\nC++\nCUDA\nBlender 3D\nOpenGL/GLSL\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
