    "homepage_text": "Shenlong Wang\nShenlong Wang Â\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nTwitter\n/\nCV\nI am an Assistant Professor at the\nUIUC Department of Computer Science\n, affiliated with\nComputer Vision @ UIUC\n,\nIllinois Robotics Group\nand\nCenter for Immersive Computing @ UIUC\n.\nI finished my PhD at\nDepartment of Computer Science\n,\nUniversity of Toronto\nand worked as a research scientist at Uber, advised by\nRaquel Urtasun\n.\nI work at the intersection of\n3D vision\nand\nrobotics\n. My group builds (a)\nspatial intelligence\nâalgorithms that perceive, reconstruct, and reason about the 3D physical world; and (b)\ndigital twins\nâphysics-informed models that faithfully replicate the real world, simulate its dynamics, and even predict how it will evolve. We use these world models to power real-world decision-making in robotics, autonomous systems, immersive computing, and agricultural and ecological applications.\nPositions\nWe are always looking for motivated students to join us.\nProspective PhD students:\nThank you for your interest! Please apply to the PhD programs in UIUC CS or ECE and list me as a potential advisor. Iâm sorry that I canât respond to individual admissions emails, but I warmly encourage you to apply through the official portal.\nCurrent UIUC grad and undergrad students:\nPlease send me an email with your CV and transcript if you are interested.\nVisiting students:\nPlease send me your CV and transcript through email.\nGroup Members\nTianhang Cheng\nCS PhD\n(w/\nKaiyu Guan\n)\nHanxiao Jiang\nCS PhD\n(w/\nYunzhu Li\n)\nChih-Hao Lin\nCS PhD\nShaowei Liu\nCS PhD\n(w/\nSaurabh Gupta\n)\nJing Wen\nCS PhD\n(w/\nAlex Schwing\n)\nHongchi Xia\nCS PhD\nAlbert J. Zhai\nCS PhD\nVlas Zyrianov\nCS PhD\nHenry Che\nCS MS\nJason Mei\nECE MS\nGloria Wang\nCS BS\nSydney Yu\nCS BS\nPast members:\nSee this link\nNews\nShow Recent\nShow All\n[2025.11] Talk at\nAIFARMS\non agricultural digital twins.\n[2025.10] Best Paper Award at\nISMAR 2025\n. Congratulations to Yihan and the team!\n[2025.10] Keynote at\nIROS RobotGen Workshop\n(with Best Keynote Speaker Award).\n[2025.10] Co-organizing the\n3D in the Wild Workshop\nat ICCV 2025.\n[2025.09] Three papers accepted to NeurIPS 2025.\n[2025.08] We are grateful to\nNSF Formal Methods in the Field (FMitF)\nfor supporting certifiable visual computing.\n[2025.07] Talks at Stanford and XPeng.\n[2025.07] Four papers accepted to ICCV 2025 (one spotlight). Congratulations to the team!\n[2025.06] Invited talk at\nInd3D: Enforcing Inductive Bias in 3D Generation\nworkshop at CVPR 2025.\n[2025.06] Co-host the\nVision Meets Physics: Synergizing Physical Simulation and Computer Vision\nand\nFoundation Models Meet Embodied Agents\nworkshops at CVPR 2025.\n[2025.05] Invited talk at IMMERSE Symposium.\n[2025.05] Thank you Airbrush for your research gift!\n[2025.04] We are grateful to receive the\nDean's Award for Excellence in Research\n.\n[2025.04] One paper has been accepted by RSS 2025. Congratulations to the team!\n[2025.03] Five papers have been accepted by CVPR 2025. Congratulations to the team!\n[2025.03] Invited talk at UPenn, 3DV AC Workshop and NUS.\n[2025.01] One paper has been accepted by ICLR 2025. Congratulations to the team!\n[2025.01] One paper has been accepted by ICRA 2025. Congratulations to the team!\n[2024.11] Four papers have been accepted by 3DV 2025. Congratulations to the team!\n[2024.10] Co-host the\n3D Modeling, Reconstruction, and Generation in the Wild Workshop\nat ECCV 2024.\n[2024.10] Invited talk at\nCV4Metaverse Workshop\nat ECCV 2024.\n[2024.08] Two papers have been accepted by ECCV 2024. Congratulations to the team!\n[2024.08] One paper has been accepted by TRO. Congratulations to the team!\n[2024.08] Invited talk at AVIATE Seminar.\n[2024.06] We are grateful to the\nMeta\nfor sponsoring our research on generative models for immersive computing.\n[2024.06] We are grateful to the\nNSF Foundational Research in Robotics (FRR)\nfor sponsoring our research on introspection and counterfactual reasoning for autonomy.\n[2024.06] One paper has been accepted by RA-L. Congratulations to the team!\n[2024.06] Chih-Hao and Albert has been selected as\n2024 Qualcomm Innovation Fellowship Finalist.\nCongrats!\n[2024.06] Invited talk at Peking U, Tsinghua U, NJU, HKU, CUHK.\n[2024.05] Invited talk at Nvidia and Waabi.\n[2024.05] We are grateful to the\nNSF Cyber-Physical Systems (CPS)\nfor sponsoring our research on radar-based perception.\n[2024.03] Invited talk at\nAICE Spring Research Symposium\n[2024.03] Three papers have been accepted by CVPR 2024. Congratulations to the team!\n[2024.01] One paper has been accepted by ICRA. Congratulations to the team!\n[2024.01] We are grateful to the\nNSF Robust Intelligence Program\nfor suppporting our research on digital twins with a CAREER award.\n[2024.01] Invited talk at\nIMMERSE Annual Symposium\n[2024.01] Thank you\nMeta\nfor the research gift support!\n[2023.11] One paper has been accepted by RA-L. Congratulations to the team!\n[2023.09] One paper has been accepted by NeurIPS 2023. Congratulations to Tianhang!\n[2023.09] Invited talk at\nC3.ai Generative AI Workshop\n[2023.09] We are grateful to the\nNSF Safe Learning-Enabled Systems Program\nfor sponsoring our research on safe autonmous .\n[2023.09] We are grateful to the\nNSF Robust Intelligence Program\nfor sponsoring our research on neural scene models.\n[2023.09] Thank you\nAmazon-Illinois AICE center\nfor the research grant support!\n[2023.07] Four papers have been accepted by ICCV 2023. Congratulations to Albert, Yuan, Chih-Hao, Xiyue and Shaowei!\n[2023.07] Thank you\nIntel\nfor the research gift support!\n[2023.06] Talks at CVPR 2023:\nScene Understanding Workshop\n,\nSecure and Safe Autonomous Driving Workshop\n.\n[2023.06] Co-host the\nEnd-to-End Autonomous Driving Workshop\nat CVPR 2023.\n[2023.05] Thank you\nIBM\nfor the research grant support!\n[2023.05] Vlas won\nNew Frontier Fellowship\n. Congratulations to Vlas!\n[2023.03] Thank you\nJump-Arches\nand\nNCSA\nfor the research grant support!\n[2023.03] One paper has been accepted by CVPR 2023. Congratulations to Shaowei!\n[2023.01] One paper has been accepted by L4DC 2023 as spotlight. Congratulations to Sheng!\n[2022.09] Two papers have been accepted by NeurIPS 2022. Congratulations to Yuan, Yuefan and Zeyuan!\n[2022.08] Thank you\nInsper-Illinois fund\nfor the research grant support!\n[2022.08] Our group is honored to receive the\nAmazon Research Award\n.\n[2022.09] One paper has been accepted by ECCV 2022. Congratulations to Vlas!\n[2022.03] Two papers have been accepted by CVPR 2022. Congratulations to Wei-Chiu and Chih-Hao!\n[2022.03] Vlas won NSF GRFP honorable mention. Congratulations to Vlas!\n[2022.01] Thank you Nvidia for the hardware research grant support!\n[2021.06] Talks at CVPR 2021:\nAutonomous Driving Workshop\n,\nData Compression Tutorial\nand\nSelf-Driving Tutorial\n.\n[2021.03] Three papers have been accepted by CVPR 2021 (one oral).\n[2021.01] One paper has been accepted by ICRA 2021.\n[2020.09] One paper has been accepted by NeurIPS 2020.\n[2020.09] One paper has been accepted by IROS 2020 (Best Application Paper Finalist).\n[2020.08] Three papers have been accepted by ECCV 2020 (one spotlight).\n[2020.03] Two papers have been accepted by CVPR 2020 as oral presentations.\nPublications\nShow Selected\nShow by Date\nAll Topics\nDigital Twins\nSpatial Understanding\nEmbodied AI\nSelf-Driving\nAI for Crop & Climate\nContent Creation\nLow-level Vision\nCropCraft: Complete Structural Characterization of Crop Plants from Images\nAlbert J. Zhai\n,\nXinlei Wang\n,\nKaiyuan Li\n,\nZhao Jiang\n,\nJunxiong Zhou\n,\nSheng Wang\n,\nZhenong Jin\n,\nKaiyu Guan\n,\nShenlong Wang\n3DV\n, 2026 (\nOral\n)\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nAda: A Distributed, Power-Aware, Real-Time Scene Provider for XR\nYihanÂ Pang\n,\nSushantÂ Kondguli\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\n,\nSaritaÂ Adve\nISMAR\n, 2025 (\nBest Paper Award\n)\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nHoloScene: Simulation-Ready Interactive 3D Worlds from a Single Video\nHongchiÂ Xia\n,\nChih-HaoÂ Lin\n,\nHao-YuÂ Hsu\n,\nQuentinÂ Leboutet\n,\nKatelynÂ Gao\n,\nMichaelÂ Paulitsch\n,\nBenjaminÂ Ummenhofer\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\nNeurIPS\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nNoPo-Avatar: Generalizable and Animatable Avatars from Sparse Inputs without Human Poses\nJingÂ Wen\n,\nAlexÂ Schwing\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\nNeurIPS\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nVisual Sync: Multi-Camera Synchronization via Cross-View Object Motion\nShaoweiÂ Liu*\n,\nDavidÂ YifanÂ Yao*\n,\nSaurabhÂ Gupta\n+\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\n+\nNeurIPS\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nDemeter: A Parametric Model of Crop Plant Morphology from the Real World\nTianhangÂ Cheng\n,\nAlbertÂ J.Â Zhai\n,\nEvanÂ Z.Â Chen\n,\nRuiÂ Zhou\n,\nYawenÂ Deng\n,\nZitongÂ Li\n,\nKejieÂ Zhao\n,\nJaniceÂ Shiu\n,\nQianyuÂ Zhao\n,\nYideÂ Xu\n,\nXinleiÂ Wang\n,\nYuanÂ Shen\n,\nShengÂ Wang\n,\nLisaÂ Ainsworth\n,\nKaiyuÂ Guan\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\nICCV\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nControllable Weather Simulation and Removal with Video Diffusion Models\nChih-HaoÂ Lin\n,\nZianÂ Wang\n,\nRuofanÂ Liang\n,\nYuxuanÂ Zhang\n,\nSanjaÂ Fidler\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\n,\nZanÂ Gojcic\nICCV\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Data]\nInvRGB+L: Inverse Rendering of Complex Scenes with Unified Color and LiDAR Reflectance Modeling\nXiaoxueÂ Chen\n,\nBhargavÂ Chandaka\n,\nChih-HaoÂ Lin\n,\nYa-QinÂ Zhang\n,\nDavidÂ Forsyth\n,\nHaoÂ Zhao\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\nICCV\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nAD-GS: Object-Aware B-Spline Gaussian Splatting for Self-Supervised Autonomous Driving\nJiaweiÂ Xu\n,\nKaiÂ Deng\n,\nZexinÂ Fan\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\n,\nJinÂ Xie\n,\nJianÂ Yang\nICCV\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nPhysTwin: Physics-Informed Reconstruction and Simulation of Deformable Objects from Videos\nHanxiaoÂ Jiang\n,\nHao-YuÂ Hsu\n,\nKaifengÂ Zhang\n,\nHsin-NiÂ Yu\n,\nShenlongÂ Wang\n,\nYunzhuÂ Li\nICCV\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code