    "homepage_text": "Shuxiao Chen\nPh.D. Student\nDepartment of Statistics and Data Science, the Wharton School\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\nEmail: shuxiaoc [@] wharton [DOT] upenn [DOT] edu\n[Google Scholar]\nAbout me\nI obtained my Ph.D. degree in statistics in 2022 from the Wharton School, where I was advised by Prof.\nZongming Ma\n.\nI received my bachelor’s degree from Cornell University, where I worked with Prof.\nJacob Bien\n.\nResearch interest\nMy doctoral research focused on:\nCausal inference;\nMachine learning on graphs;\nMulti-task learning;\nApplications of above techniques in single-cell biology.\nRecent work\nIntegration of spatial and single-cell data across modalities with weak linkage\nShuxiao Chen, Bokai Zhu, Sijia Huang, John W. Hickey, Kevin Z. Lin, Michael Snyder, William J. Greenleaf, Garry P. Nolan, Nancy R. Zhang, and Zongming Ma. 2023\nRobust Single-cell Matching and Multi-modal Analysis Using Shared and Distinct Features\nBokai Zhu, Shuxiao Chen, Yunhao Bai, Han Chen, Nilanjan Mukherjee, Gustavo Vazquez, David R. McIlwain, Alexandar Tzankov, Ivan T. Lee, Matthias S. Matter, Yury Goltsev, Zongming Ma, Garry P. Nolan, and Sizun Jiang.\nNature Methods\n, 2023.\nOne-Way Matching of Datasets with Low Rank Signals\nShuxiao Chen, Sizun Jiang, Zongming Ma, Garry P. Nolan, and Bokai Zhu. 2022."
