    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Homepage of Hongyuan Zhu\nHongyuan Zhu\nhongyuanzhu.cn (AT) gmail (DOT) com\n[DBLP]\n[Google Scholar]\nHomepage\nBrief Bio:\nHi! My name is Hongyuan Zhu (Chinese: 朱宏远).  I am currently leading the Advanced Perception Reasoning (APR) lab in the Institute of Infocomm Research (I2R), at the Agency for Science, Technology, and Research (A*STAR), Singapore. We do interesting and exiciting research to eveloping intelligent agent that can assist human with multi-modal scene and event knowledge learning and reasoning capabilities under limited and unbalanced resources.\nWorking Experience:\nInstitut of Infocomm Research (I2R), Agency for Science, Technology and Research (A*STAR), Singapore.\n- Unit Head/Group Manager, Principal Investigator, Satellite Sensing/Geospatial/Weather Climate Solution Group (2025.08-Now)\n- Senior Scientist, Principal Investigator, Lab Head for Advanced Perceptual Reasoning Lab (2023.06-Now)\n- Scientist III, Principal Investigator, Lab Head for Advanced Perceptual Reasoning Lab (2021.04-2023.06)\n- Scientist II, Principal Investigator, Lab Head for Advanced Perceptual Reasoning Lab (2014.04-2021.04)\n- Scientist I, Principal Investigator (2014.08-2019.04)\nResearch Interests:\nComputational Photography\n- The research on\n\"Differentiable Physical based Image Enhancement\"\ncan be found\n>> HERE\nMulti-modal Learning and Reasoning\n- The research on\n\"Semantic Parsing with Various Supervision\"\ncan be found\n>> HERE\n- The research on\n\"Rapid Human Action Detection\"\ncan be found\n>> HERE\n- The research on\n\"Multi-modal Video Question Answering\"\ncan be found\n>> HERE\nOther Topics @ APR Lab\n- Feel free to approach me if you would like to collaborate/explore on the topics you are interested. APR offers a series of exiting moonshoot projects.  There is no limit to our research topics ;-)\nRecent News:\n2024-02: One paper accepted by CVPR2024, Congrats to our APR's student: Sijin! See you all in Seattle :)\n2023-12: One paper accepted by AAAI2024, Congrat to our APR's student Siyuan for first tiered-1 AI paper as a bachelor student in NTU SCSE\n2023-12: One paper accepted by AAAI2024, Congrat to our co-supervised student Zijing for his first tier-1 conference paper!\n2023-12: One paper accepted by TCSVT, Congrat to our APR's student Haoyang's efforts\n2023-10: Our APR team together with Fudan Team won the 1st place of Scene2Cap Challenge!\n2023-10: Welcome to join our Human Centric Multimedia Analysis in ACM MM2023\n2023-08: One paper accepted by ACM MM2023, Congrat to Hu Peng!\n2023-07: Welcome Huaiyuan, Muli, Liu Chang and James to join APR's staff!\n2023-06: Congrats to Yuwei's paper accepted by ICCV 2023!\n2023-02: One paper accepted by BMVC 2023, Congrat to our SINGA student Burak!\n2023-02: Three papers accepted by CVPR2023, Congrats to our APR's students: Sijin, Yuanbiao and Yanglin! See you all in Vancouver :)\n2022-11: Congrats to Zihan's solid work on object centric pre-training is accepted by Pattern Recognition\n2022-11: Congrats to Chuangguan's solid works 3D few-shot learning benchmark accepted by IJCV\n2022-09: Congrats to my ARAP PhD student Xu Ke's first work of WIFI self-supervised learning was accepted by JHBI\n2022-06: Our team achieve the third place in EPIC KITCHEN Multi-Instance Action Retrieval Challenge, Congrats to Burak!\n2022-05: Our team's work on \"Unsupervised Contrastive Cross-modal Hashing\" is accepted by TPAMI!\n2022-04: Congrats to my intern student Mr.Duan Jiafei received A*STAR NSS scholarhip to start research in UW,Seattle!\n2022-04: Congrats to my intern student Ms.Huang Ziqi received NTU research scholarhip to start research in NTU S-Lab!\n2022-03: Our team is awarded a new 2Mil EDB OSTIN Grant for Satellite Image Analytics. Thanks for the support from EDB!\n2022-02: Congrats to Eng Yen's paper on efficient point cloud recogntion accepted by RAL, ICRA2022 track!\n2022-01: Congrats to Xiuchao's first CVPR2022 paper on optical flow estimation!\n2022-01: Our developed 1st few-shot point cloud recognition paper is accpeted by WACV22, Congrats to my Mphil Chuanguan!\n2021-11: Our developed weakly supervised point cloud instance segmentation using 1000x less labeled date is accepted by PAMI, Congrats to my Mphil YongBin!\n2021-10: I receved the A*STAR Career Development Fund and Robot HTPO seed fund ($600K) to develop embodied capabilities, Thanks A*STAR!\n2021-09: I'll serve as the Area Chair of ACM MM Asia 2021 at Gold Coast, Australia.\n>\n2021-02: Our A*STAR CHRIS Team is the only team from Asia won the KUKA Innovation Award Finalist! (top5)\n(Link)\n2020-11: Congrats to Hu Peng's paper accepted by AAAI 2021!\n2020-09: Appoint as the Associate Editor of Visual Computer, Elsevier\n2019-04: One papers\n\"COMIC: Multi-view Clustering Without Parameter Selection\"\nhas been accepted by\nICML\n.\n2019-04: Our ICCV17 extended journal paper\n\"YoTube: Searching Action Proposal via Recurrent and Static Regression Networks\"\nhas been selected as ESI Highly Indexed Paper.\n>\n2019-04: I have been invited as a PC member for  CVPR, ICCV, ACM MM, AAAI in 2019.\n2019-03: One paper\n\"Spatial Fusion GAN for Image Synthesis\"\nhas been accepted by\nCVPR 2019\n.\n2019-03: One paper for\n\"Anomaly Detection in Video Surveillance\"\nhas been accepted by\nIEEE TIFS\n.\n2019-01: One paper for\nhave been accepted by\nAAAI 2019\nas Oral Paper!\n2018-11: Our ICCV17 work on action detection has been adversertised as A*STAR Research Highlighted Research among 25 Research Institutes!.\nI'm selected as IET Image Processing Special Issue Guest Editor, Call For Paper:\nAdversarial Learning in Image Processing\n>\nAcademic Activities:\nProfessional Activities\n-\n- Associate Editor: Visual Computer, Elsevier, 09/2020 - Now\n- Guest Editor: IET Image Processing, 2018. Guest Editor\n- Area Chair: ACM MM Asia, 2022\n- Senior Program Committee, IJCAI 2021\n- Session Chair: IJCAI 2018, PCM 2014\n- Journal Reviewer: IEEE TPAMI, TIP, TCSVT, TNNLS, TMM, ACCESS, Elsevier JVCI, CVIU\n- Conference Reviewer: CVPR, ICCV, NIPS, ACM MM, AAAI, ACCV, ICME, ICIP, VCIP\nAwards:\n- 2017 International Consortium of Chinese Mathmaticians 2017, Distinguished Paper\n- 2014 ICIP14 SPS Travel Grant \\& ICIP14 Top-10\\% paper award \n- 2014 WACV14 Student Travel Grant \n- 2010 ~ 2014 NTU Graduate Research Scholarship  \n- 2010 Ocean-Tech Award for Best Student Final Year Project. \n- 2010 First Prize of IEEE Perl Riverl Delta FYP Competition. \n- 2009 BNU Affinity Card Scholarship(Awarded to top 3 students). \n- 2008 Henry Fork Foundation Scholarship(Awarded to top 3 students).\n- 2006 - 2010 Dean's Honor List (Awarded to top $10\\%$ students)"
  },
