  "serper::Wei Ao": {
    "homepage": "https://wei-ao.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "autofhe@fhe.org",
      "aowei@msu.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/Wei-Ao",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Wei Ao’s Homepage - Wei Ao’s Homepage\nWei Ao\nCS PhD Student at MSU\nFollow\nEast Lansing, MI, US\nEmail\nTwitter\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nWelcome to Wei Ao’s Homepage\nI am a Ph.D. student in CSE at MSU under the supervision of\nProf. Vishnu Boddeti\nin\nHAL Lab\n. My research focuses on\nPrivate AI\n. I am working on an end-to-end secure inference system to protect\ndata privacy\nunder fully homomorphic encryption (\nFHE\n). Before joining MSU, I obtained my Master’s degree from Fudan University in 2019 where I worked on image processing and target detection. I published papers in USENIX Security Symposium, NeurIPS, GECCO, IEEE TIP.\nNews!\n[03/2026]\nReviewer at ECCV 2026 and BMVC 2026.\n[09/2025] I’m starting a new position as an Applied Scientist Intern at Amazon AWS AI in Seattle.\n[02/2025] I have TWO papers and ONE tutorial accepted by\nCVPR 2025\n!\n[02/2025] I am invited to be a reviewer of\nICCV 2025\n.\n[12/2024] I am invited to be a PC member of\nAutoML 2025\n.\n[12/2024] I serve as a reviewer at\nCVPR 2025\n.\n[08/2024] I present our solution to AI safety\nAutoFHE\nat\nUSENIX Security Symposium 2024\nin Philadelphia, PA.\n[06/2024] I am invited to be a PC member for the workshop track of AutoML 2024.\n[03/2024] I present our USENIX Security’ 24 paper\nAutoFHE\nat\nFHE.org Conference 2024\n.\n[Slides]\n[Video]\n[03/2024] I serve as a reviewer at\nAutoML 2024\n.\n[09/2023]\nAutoFHE\nis accepted by\nUSENIX Security Symposium 2024\n."
  },
