    "homepage_text": "Zheng Ma – Department of Government\nSkip to content\nHARVARD.EDU\nZheng Ma\nZheng\nMa\nPh.D. Student in Government\nZheng Ma is a PhD student in the Department of Government at Harvard University. His research interests include political economy, social policy, and computational social science. Prior to coming to Harvard, he obtained an M.A. in Social Sciences from the University of Chicago and a B.A. in Economics and Political Science from the University of Wisconsin-Madison.\nContact\nzma@g.harvard.edu\n1737 Cambridge Street,\nCGIS Knafel Building\nSubfields\nComparative Politics | Methods and Formal Theory\nAcademic Interests\nBureaucracy | Data Science & Political Methodology |Education Policy | Environmental Policy | Institutions | Political Economy & Development | Political Psychology | Public Opinion | Public Policy | Social Policy & the Welfare State | State-Society Relations | State & Local Politics | Technology & Governance\nResearch Methods\nExperiments | Formal Theory | Quantitative Methods | Surveys\nGeographic Regions of Study\nChina | Asia | United States\nclose menu\nclose search\nSearch\nSearch Site"
