    "homepage_text": "L&E Research | We bring companies and people together to talk. We’re the experts in qualitative recruitment.\nParticipate\nClient login\nBid request\nWe bring companies and people together to talk.\nThat's the magic behind smarter decisions.\nWe offer specialized recruitment and research solutions across industries.\nOur expert teams and advanced strategies support healthcare,\nconsumer, and legal sectors.\nL&E\nHealth\nPrecise, efficient healthcare\nrecruitment with a specialized team, advanced technology, and a vast participant database.\nLEARN MORE\nL&E\nConsumer\nDecades of expertise, innovative recruitment strategies, and exceptional\nclient satisfaction for superior results.\nLEARN MORE\nL&E\nLegal\nThe trusted partner for legal professionals seeking reliable recruitment and seamless mock legal research execution.\nLEARN MORE\nWe’re the experts in qualitative research recruitment\nConnecting companies with people since 1984, L&E Research helps brands uncover trusted insights through top-rated facilities & nationwide recruiting.\n99%\nof clients recommend us\nMeet us to find out why L&E\nTrusted by the world's largest brands to connect them with their customers.\nPerfect recruit and seamless execution at facility!\nInnovation Research Coordinator,  Sterling-Rice Group\nRecruit was seamless. Team was professional. Participants were articulate and engaged.\nResearch Manager,  Smarty Pants LLC\nIncredible response time and partnership from Jaimee on the research from day 0 to conclusion!\nOral-B Analytics & Insights Director Innovation,  Procter & Gamble\nToni was an amazing PM.  She was extremely responsive, very organized, detailed and super fun!\nOperations Manager, Field Services, Ignite 360\nDanielle and team went above and beyond to ensure a successful study. Top notch service as usual!\nSr. Human Factors Specialist, Priority Designs\nJaimee is always the best at being flexible and finding solutions to any recruitment roadblocks.\nAccount Director, Olson Zaltman\nJaimee was tenacious in her pursuit of tricky segments, and always wonderfully pleasant to work with.\nSr. Insight Manager, Olson Zaltman\nThis was a very challenging recruit,  but Kristie and her team were able to pull it together on time, with 100% attendance.\nIndependent Contractor, Real Insight, Inc\nL&E manages to take on our toughest recruits and complete them. The PM gives updates daily which we love and is always available.\nProject Manager, Human Factors\nAs always, Jaimee is the best to work with! Always a treat when she's put on our project because we know all of the details are taken care of.\nAccount Director\nJaimee continues to be one of the best pms we’ve ever had. Flexible and she always finds who we need.  Sincerely appreciate her efforts every time.\nAccount Director\nDenise was fantastic. Very communicative, focused on finding great solutions and great participants for my research. Can't wait to work with her again.\nQualitative Research Manager\nThe front desk staff was top notch - we felt really supported the entire time we were at the facility and all of our needs and requests were met promptly!\nSr. Human Factors Specialist\nDenise did a great job proactively communicating and replacing respondents when needed. Most participants were early and highly articulate. Thanks for a smooth project!\nResearch Manager\nKristie was great to work with throughout the entire project. We had many challenges, delays, and pauses from our client throughout the project that Kristie was able to manage for us. Great job!\nSenior Project Manager, Project and Proposal Operations\nTracy and her team made a huge effort to find excellent participants. And Fara and her team have just been so lovely and caring during the fieldwork. Hope to be back soon!\nManaging Partner\nFantastic experience from start to finish, we were impressed, our client was and Traci helped me with everything via white-glove approach. We will always turn to L&E! Thank you!!\nSenior Vice President of Integrated Services\nThe consumers were great.  Very articulate, thoughtful, and prompt.  We also had stellar participation rates. Denise was, as always, very on top of everything and just fantastic! 🙂 Very happy customer!\nVice President of Operations\nTrenny and Lindsay did a fantastic job!  Straight from my client, \"The research went really well, we loved the facility and staff, the co-creation research room was awesome, and the recruits were spot on.\"  Thanks!!!\nVP Qualitative Field Management\nThe project was recruited really well even with some segmentation that made it a little challenging and a client request to change some respondents around in the groups which Denise and team handled professionally and in a timely manner.\nProject Manager\nDanielle was an absolute pleasure to work with. Not only did she finish the recruit in a short amount of time, the participants that she identified were stellar and provided excellent insight to our research. We'd love to work with Danielle again in the future.\nSenior Research Analyst\nWe had never been to L&E NYC so to be honest, we were slightly nervous.  However, the entire team exceeded expectations from the recruit all the way to the in-person experience at the facility.  Our team loved working with your NYC crew and we'll definitely be back! 🙂\nVice President of Operations, Wonderlust Collective\nHelped my first big study go by in a breeze! Everyone was always super responsive and nice. 🙂\nProducts Researcher, Procter & Gamble\nVery smooth projecting, very quick recruiting, high quality recruits and transparent communication.\nThank you Danielle and team for a great job! I appreciate the speedy responsiveness and dedication to my project.\nCEO\nJaimee went over and above to help make the recruitment as solid as possible.  The Raleigh facility went over and above to accommodate me and the clients.\nPrincipal, The Thought Bubble\nJaimee and the team went above and beyond to satisfy the recruit, including going the extra mile to ensure we had the best mix possible. Always a pleasure!\nInsight Manager, Olson Zaltman\nAs an L&E client for more than a decade, I appreciate what L&E brings to every engagement: excellent client service, rapid responses, a high degree of listening, options and solutions, always-competitive pricing, and high-quality recruiting.  As a result, they are a clear and easy ‘go to’ for anything qualitative.\nVP, Qualitative Services, Deft Research\nA seamless recruit with a 100% show rate.  Excellent!\nL&E has never let me down. I would work with them again and refer them to my friends and colleagues.\nKelly, Fara and your NY team have continued to be absolutely outstanding!\nPresident\nSuch great hospitality from your team in Cincinnati. Please don't ever get rid of the fresh baked cookies!\nSr Insights Manager\nDenise was amazing. Very organized, attentive, and flexible. Will be requesting her support in the future!\nSenior Scientist, Beauty Care\nDanielle is easy to work with, very responsive, and collaborative. I feel like we are a really effective team!\nSenior Study Recruitment Specialist\nThe Cincinnati L&E team was top-notch as always!  Excellent service and adaptability to our funky project needs!\nProducts Researcher\nGabrielle was so helpful throughout the whole study. She was very responsive and always helping the study run smoothly.\nR&D Senior Scientist\nRecruitment was GREAT, client and team really liked all the interviews. And Trenny and Jane from L&E have been VERY accommodating.\nProject Manager\nTara was very responsive to our recruitments needs and did a great job of following up with participants and keeping them on track.\nProject Manager\nThe L&E team was extremely helpful throughout the qualitative research and collecting the diary after the fact.  Everyone was a pleasure to work with.\nR&D Scientist\nOrganization: timely and organized responses from Sarah and team. Screener support: fantastic support on screener development. Recruits: quality of recruits surpassed expectations.\nSenior Strategy Director\nTeam was very intentional about their communication and quickly adjusted client's requests on recruiting a mix of different demographics. The facility needs were taken care of quickly for a seamless experience.\nQualitative Research Specialist\nThank you so much for all your help - our research was very successful and we have you to thank for a seamless execution. It can be stressful having to go into a brand new territory and facility but you were so welcoming and so organized. We really appreciate it!\nProject Manager\nJaimee was the BEST. You have a true gem. Fantastic communication throughout - KOC, setup, initial recruiting updates, recruiting changes, updates during fielding. Got us wonderful participants and client was very happy. You are lucky to have such a wonderful project manager like Jaimee.\nQualitative Research Manager\nDespite multiple changes, delays, and updates on our end, the L&E team was very adaptable.  Ultimately, our team had to delay the planned testing, in no part due to the services provided by L&E.\nProducts Researcher\nWhat an amazing team, their ability to find the most hard to reach consumers is phenominal!\nDavid J\nHead of research at the Ford Motor company\nThank you Danielle and team for a great job! I appreciate the speedy responsiveness and dedication to my project.\nMary J\nJaimee went over and above to help make the recruitment as solid as possible.  The Raleigh facility went over and above to accommodate me and the clients.\nPrincipal\nThe Thought Bubble\nJaimee and the team went above and beyond to satisfy the recruit, including going the extra mile to ensure we had the best mix possible. Always a pleasure!\nRandall R\nInsight Manager, Olson Zaltman\nOur latest insights\nBLOG\nPanel Size Is a Vanity Metric. Quality Is a Different Story.\nA research team needed 30 consumers for a two-day product evaluation. The specs were specific but not unusual: primary grocery...\nSEE THE RESULTS\nBLOG\nWhy Your Product Tests Are Only Telling Half the Story\nSurvey data told the product ...[truncated]"
  },
  "serper::Luofeng Liao": {
    "homepage": "https://luofengliao.github.io/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/alshedivat",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/luofeng-liao-7a1027181",
    "homepage_text": "Luofeng  Liao\nLuofeng\nLiao\nPh.D. in Operations Research\n2025, Guangdong, China\nHi! My name is Luofeng Liao (廖烙锋 in Chinese). I am currently a Research Scientist in Meta working on ranking/recommendation algorithms. I completed my PhD in Operations Research at Columbia University, which I attended from 2021/09 to 2025/03.\nA bit on pronouncing my name: “Luo” (adding a ‘w’ sound in “law”), “Feng” (like “fung” in fung shui), “Liao” (rhymes with “meow”).\nMy research interests are machine learning methods for causal inference and econometrics, learning and inference in market design, and adversarial optimization.\nPreviously, I worked with my advisor Prof.\nChristian Kroer\non statistical inference theory for equilibrium in auction markets, a theory that is useful for internet advertising business.\nPrior to Columbia, I received my bachelor’s degree in computer science in Fudan University in China and a master’s degree in statistics in University of Chicago. In UChicago, I used to work with Prof.\nMladen Kolar\nand Prof.\nZhaoran Wang\n. In Fudan I was advised by Prof.\nKe Wei\n.\nPapers\nConference\nThe Bias-Variance Tradeoff in Data-Driven Optimization: A Local Misspecification Perspective\nHaixiang Lan, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Luofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Adam N. Elmachtoub, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Christian Kroer, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Henry Lam, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Haofeng Zhang\nNeurIPS (Neural Information Processing Systems)\n2025\nHTML\nUnder Review\nOnline Fair Allocation with Best-of-Many-Worlds Guarantees\nZongjun Yang, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Luofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Yuan Gao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Christian Kroer\nUnder Review in Management Science\n2024\nHTML\nJournal\nStatistical Inference and A/B Testing in Fisher Markets and Paced Auctions\nLuofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Christian Kroer\nAccepted, Management Science\n2024\nHTML\nConference\nInterference Among First-Price Pacing Equilibria: A Bias and Variance Analysis\nLuofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Christian Kroer, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Sergei Leonenkov, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Okke Schrijvers, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Liang Shi, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Nicolas Stier-Moses, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Congshan Zhang\nICLR (International Conference on Learning Representations)\n2024\nHTML\nConference\nBootstrapping Fisher Market Equilibrium and First-Price Pacing Equilibrium\nLuofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Christian Kroer\nICML (International Conference on Machine Learning)\n2024\nAbs\nHTML\nBootstrap inference in ad auction platforms.\nConference\nGreedy-Based Online Fair Allocation with Adversarial Input: Enabling Best-of-Many-Worlds Guarantees\nZongjun Yang, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Luofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Christian Kroer\nAAAI (Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence Conference)\n2024\nAbs\nHTML\nPresent worst-case guarantees for the PACE algorithm (proposed in previous papers) for online resource allocation.\nConference\nStatistical Inference and A/B Testing for First-Price Pacing Equilibria\nLuofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Christian Kroer\nICML (International Conference on Machine Learning)\n2023\nAbs\nHTML\nPropose a statistical inference framework for revenues A/B testing in auction markets.\nConference\nStatistical Inference for Fisher Market Equilibrium\nLuofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Yuan Gao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Christian Kroer\nICLR (International Conference on Learning Representations)\n2022\nAbs\nHTML\nPropose a statistical inference framework for revenues and social welfare in market equilibrium where agents behave in a strategic manner.\nConference\nNonstationary Dual Averaging and Online Fair Allocation\nLuofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Yuan Gao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Christian Kroer\nNeurIPS (Neural Information Processing Systems)\n2022\nAbs\nHTML\nWe consider the problem of fairly allocating items to a set of individuals, when the items are arriving online with fairness and efficiency guarantees.\nJournal\nLocal AdaGrad-Type Algorithm for Stochastic Convex-Concave Minimax Problems\nLuofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Li Shen, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Jia Duan, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Mladen Kolar, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Dacheng Tao\nMachine Learning - Springer\n2022\nAbs\nHTML\nWe propose a commmunication-efficient and distributed adversarial learning algorithm with theoretical guarantees.\nJournal\nInstrumental Variable Value Iteration for Causal Offline Reinforcement Learning\nLuofeng Liao, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Zuyue Fu, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Zhuoran Yang, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Yixin Wang, \n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Mladen Kolar, \n                \n              \n    ...[truncated]"
