    "homepage_text": "Yujun Lin | NVIDIA\nYujun Lin\nResearch Scientist\nNVIDIA\nAbout Me\nI am currently a research scientist at\nNVIDIA\n. I finished my PhD at\nMIT HAN Lab\nof\nMIT EECS\n, advised by\nProf. Song Han\n. I received my B.Eng. in Electronic Engineering from Tsinghua University.\nMy research area is efficient deep learning, with a special focus on the co-design of algorithm, system and hardware for foundation models (diffusion models, LLMs, etc).\nNews\n[05/2025]\n“\nSANA 1.5: Efficient Scaling of Training-Time and Inference-Time Compute in Linear Diffusion Transformer\n” is accepted to ICML’25.\n[05/2025]\n“\nSparse Video-Gen: Accelerating Video Diffusion Transformers with Spatial-Temporal Sparsity\n” is accepted to ICML’25.\n[02/2025]\n“\nQServe: W4A8KV4 Quantization and System Co-design for Efficient LLM Serving\n” is accepted to MLSys’25.\n[02/2025]\n“\nLServe: Efficient Long-Sequence LLM Serving with Unified Sparse Attention\n” is accepted to MLSys’25.\n[01/2025]\n“\nSVDQuant: Absorbing Outliers by Low-Rank Components for 4-Bit Diffusion Models\n” is accepted to ICLR’25 (Spotlight).\n[01/2025]\n“\nSANA: Efficient High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Linear Diffusion Transformers\n” is accepted to ICLR’25 (Oral).\n[10/2024]\n“\nLEGO: Spatial Accelerator Generation and Optimization for Tensor Applications\n” is accepted to HPCA’25.\n[05/2023]\n“\nVideoTime³: A 40-uJ/frame 38 FPS Video Understanding Accelerator With Real-Time DiffFrame Temporal Redundancy Reduction and Temporal Modeling\n” is accepted to IEEE Solid-State Circuits Letters.\n[08/2022]\n“\nTorchSparse: Efficient Point Cloud Inference Engine\n” is accepted to MLSys’22.\n[04/2022]\n“\nQuantumNAS: Noise-Adaptive Search for Robust Quantum Circuits\n” is accepted to HPCA’22.\n[10/2021]\nSeleted as DAC Young Fellow 2021.\n[07/2021]\n“\nPointAcc: Efficient Point Cloud Accelerator\n” is accepted to MICRO’21.\n[06/2021]\nGot into\nthe 2021 Qualcomm Innovation Fellowship\nwinners list\n[02/2021]\n“\nNAAS: Neural Accelerator Architecture Search\n” is accepted to DAC’21.\nSelected Publications\nICML\nSparse Video-Gen: Accelerating Video Diffusion Transformers with Spatial-Temporal Sparsity\nHaocheng Xi, Shuo Yang, Yilong Zhao, Chenfeng Xu, Muyang Li, Xiuyu Li,\nYujun Lin\n, Han Cai, Jintao Zhang, Dacheng Li, Jianfei Chen, Ion Stoica, Kurt Keutzer, Song Han\nICML\n, 2025.\nPaper\nCode\nICML\nSANA 1.5: Efficient Scaling of Training-Time and Inference-Time Compute in Linear Diffusion Transformer\nEnze Xie, Junsong Chen, Yuyang Zhao, Jincheng Yu, Ligeng Zhu, Chengyue Wu,\nYujun Lin\n, Zhekai Zhang, Muyang Li, Junyu Chen, Han Cai, Bingchen Liu, Daquan Zhou, Song Han\nICML\n, 2025.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nICLR\nSVDQuant: Absorbing Outliers by Low-Rank Components for 4-Bit Diffusion Models\nMuyang Li*,\nYujun Lin*\n, Zhekai Zhang*, Tianle Cai, Xiuyu Li, Junxian Guo, Enze Xie, Chenlin Meng, Jun-Yan Zhu, Song Han.\nICLR\n, 2025.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nSpotlight Presentation\nHPCA\nLEGO: Spatial Accelerator Generation and Optimization for Tensor Applications\nYujun Lin*\n, Zhekai Zhang*, Song Han.\nHPCA\n, 2025.\nProject Page\nICLR\nSANA: Efficient High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Linear Diffusion Transformers\nEnze Xie, Junsong Chen, Junyu Chen, Han Cai,\nYujun Lin\n, Zhekai Zhang, Muyang Li, Yao Lu, Song Han\nICLR\n, 2025.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nOral Presentation\nMLSys\nQServe: W4A8KV4 Quantization and System Co-design for Efficient LLM Serving\nYujun Lin*\n, Haotian Tang*, Shang Yang*, Zhekai Zhang, Guangxuan Xiao, Chuang Gan, Song Han.\nMLSys\n, 2025.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nMLSys\nLServe: Efficient Long-Sequence LLM Serving with Unified Sparse Attention\nShang Yang*, Junxian Guo*, Haotian Tang, Qinghao Hu, Guangxuan Xiao, Jiaming Tang,\nYujun Lin*\n, Zhijian Liu, Yao Lu, Song Han\nMLSys\n, 2025.\nProject Page\nSSCL\nVideoTime³: A 40-uJ/frame 38 FPS Video Understanding Accelerator With Real-Time DiffFrame Temporal Redundancy Reduction and Temporal Modeling\nMiaorong Wang,\nYujun Lin\n, Zhekai Zhang, Ji Lin, Song Han, Anantha P Chandrakasan.\nIEEE Solid-State Circuits Letters\n, 2023.\nPaper\nProject Page\nMLSys\nTorchSparse: Efficient Point Cloud Inference Engine\nHaotian Tang*, Zhijian Liu*, Xiuyu Li*,\nYujun Lin\n, Song Han.\nMLSys\n, 2022.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nHPCA\nQuantumNAS: Noise-Adaptive Search for Robust Quantum Circuits\nHanrui Wang, Yongshan Ding, Jiaqi Gu, Zirui Li,\nYujun Lin\n, David Z. Pan, Frederic T. Chong, Song Han.\nHPCA\n, 2022.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nOral Presentation\nMICRO\nPointAcc: Efficient Point Cloud Accelerator\nYujun Lin\n, Zhekai Zhang, Haotian Tang, Hanrui Wang, Song Han\nMICRO\n, 2021.\nPaper\nProject Page\nOral Presentation\nDAC\nNAAS: Neural Accelerator Architecture Search\nYujun Lin*\n, Mengtian Yang*, Song Han\nDAC\n, 2021.\nPaper\nProject Page\nOral Presentation\nECCV\nSearching Efficient 3D Architectures with Sparse Point-Voxel Convolution\nHaotian Tang*, Zhijian Liu*, Shengyu Zhao,\nYujun Lin\n, Ji Lin, Hanrui Wang, Song Han\nECCV\n, 2020.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nNeurIPS\nMCUNet: Tiny Deep Learning on IoT Devices\nJi Lin, Wei-Ming Chen,\nYujun Lin\n, John Cohn, Chuang Gan, Song Han\nNeurIPS\n, 2020.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nSpotlight Presentation\nICLR\nLite Transformer with Long-Short Range Attention\nZhanghao Wu*, Zhijian Liu*, Ji Lin,\nYujun Lin\n, Song Han\nICLR\n, 2020.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nNeurIPS\nPoint-Voxel CNN for Efficient 3D Deep Learning\nZhijian Liu*, Haotian Tang*,\nYujun Lin\n, Song Han\nNeurIPS\n, 2019.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nSpotlight Presentation\nCVPR\nHAQ: Hardware-Aware Automated Quantization with Mixed Precision\nKuan Wang*, Zhijian Liu*,\nYujun Lin*\n, Ji Lin, Song Han\nCVPR\n, 2019.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nOral Presentation\nDAC\nLong live TIME: improving lifetime for training-in-memory engines by structured gradient sparsification\nYi Cai*,\nYujun Lin*\n, Lixue Xia, Xiaoming Chen, Song Han, Yu Wang, Huazhong Yang\nDAC\n, 2018.\nPaper\nICLR\nDeep Gradient Compression: Reducing the communication bandwidth for distributed training\nYujun Lin\n, Song Han, Huizi Mao, Yu Wang, William J. Dally\nICLR\n, 2018.\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nServices\nConference Reviewer: ICLR, ICML, NeurIPS\nJournal Reviewer: TPAMI, TACD, TACO, TAI, TCSVT, TETC, TECS, TKDE, TNNLS, VISI, etc.\nPowered by Jekyll and\nMinimal Light\ntheme."
