    "homepage_text": "Yuliang Xu (徐玉良)\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYuliang Xu (徐玉良)\nEmail:\nyuliangx@umich.edu\n(permanent)\nyuliangx@uchicago.edu\n(current)\nNews: From July 1st, 2026, I will start\na new\nposition as an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Applied Mathematics and Statistics\nat Johns Hopkins University, with a secondary appointment in the\nDepartment of Biostatistics\n.\nMy recent research interest is i\nn the distributional evaluation of generative models for scientific data generation, especially in microbiome synthetic data generation and evaluation.\nPreviously, I've been a postdoc\nadvised by Prof.\nLi Ma\n,\nin the\nDepartment of Statistics\nand\nData Science Institute\nat the University of Chicago (July 2025 - June 2026), and in the\nDepartment of Statistical Science\n, Duke University (July 2024 - June 2025).\nI obtained my Ph.D.\nin\nBiostatistics\n, at the University of Michigan\n, advised by\nProf.\nJian Kang\n.\nDuring my time at Michigan, I also collaborated with Prof.\nFlorian Gunsilius\n. I obtained my B.S. degree in M\nathematics\nfrom\nSouth China University of Technology\nin 201\n7\nand M.S. degree in Statistics from\nUniversity of\nWaterloo\nin 201\n9\n.\nEducation\nPh.D Biostatistics,\nUniversity of Michigan\n(Ann Arbor, MI, US)\n. 2024.\nM.S. Statistics\n,\nUniversity of\nWaterloo\n(Waterloo, ON, Canada).\n201\n9\n.\nB.S. in M\nathematics and Applied\nMathematics\n,\nSouth China University of Technology\n(Guangzhou, Guangdong, China) 2017.\nEmployment\nPostdoc,\nDepartment of Statistics\n&\nData Science Institute\n,\nUniversity of Chicago,\n(July 2025 - June 2026)\nPostdoc,\nD\nepartment of\nStatistical S\ncience\n, Duke University\n(July 202\n4\n- June 202\n5\n)\nResearch Interests (Theory and Methods)\nGenerative Models\nNonparametric Bayesian Statistics\nOptimal transport\nCausal inference\nResearch Interests (\nApplication and Data\n)\nBrain Imaging Applications (volumetric fMRI)\nMicrobiome Data (Count data and relative abundance data)\nDNA-sequencing Data\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Tommy Xiang": {
