    "homepage_text": "Ji-Hwan Lee\n      -  Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology\nKorea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology Home\nSearch content at Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology\nView Scopus Profile\nJi-Hwan Lee\nAssociate Professor\nSchool of Management Engineering\nEmail\njihwanlee\nkaist.ac\nkr\nh-index\n622\nCitations\n13\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2005\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nEducation\n▶ Ph.D., London Business School\n▶ MBA, Seoul National University\n▶ BBA, Seoul National University\nProfessional Experience\n▶ Vice President, Korean Society of Strategic Management\n▶ Vice President, Korean Academy of International Business\n▶ Formerly, Editor-in-Chief, Journal of Strategic Management\n▶ Formerly, Assistant Professor, Ewha Womans University\nResearch interests\nCorporate Strategy (Diversification, M&A), Corporate Governance (BOD, TMT), Global Business Strategy, Social Entrepreneurship\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 8\nDecent Work and Economic Growth\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Ji-Hwan Lee is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n1\nSimilar Profiles\nCorporate Governance\nSocial Sciences\n100%\nIndustry\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n100%\nOrganizational Change\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n100%\nOrganizational Learning\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n75%\nCorporate Strategy\nSocial Sciences\n50%\nBusiness Strategy\nSocial Sciences\n50%\nDiversification Strategy\nSocial Sciences\n50%\nSocial Economy\nSocial Sciences\n50%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n19\nArticle\n1\nChapter\n1\nConference article\n1\nReview article\nExploring the Cloud Storage Service Adoption Through the Dual Perspectives: Protection Motivation Theory (PMT) and the Extended Unified Theory of Technology Acceptance Model (UTAUT2)\nSong, C. H.,\nLee, J. H.\n& Roh, T.,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nInternational Journal of Human-Computer Interaction.\n41\n,\n4\n,\np. 2745-2762\n18 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nCloud Storage Service\n100%\nPerceived Vulnerability\n11%\nPerformance Attribute\n11%\nHedonic Motivation\n11%\nPerceived Severity\n11%\n4\nScopus \n citations\nDoes government support make small and medium-sized enterprises reluctant to grow? Evidence from South Korea\nChoi, J. U.,\nLee, C. Y.\n&\nLee, J. H.\n,\n2024\n,\nIn:\nJournal of the Asia Pacific Economy.\n29\n,\n2\n,\np. 668-692\n25 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpportunity Cost\n100%\n2\nScopus \n citations\nThe pitfalls of corporate social irresponsibility: Hypocrisy of family firms in South Korea\nChoi, J., Roh, T. &\nLee, J. H.\n,\n5 Jan 2024\n,\nIn:\nJournal of Cleaner Production.\n435\n, 140557.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nFamily Business\n100%\nCorporate Hypocrisy\n33%\nDigitalization\n33%\nEnvironmental Dynamism\n33%\nFinancial Analysis\n33%\n18\nScopus \n citations\nHow and when female directors effectively cut down acquisition premiums\nLim, M. H. &\nLee, J. H.\n,\nJan 2023\n,\nIn:\nManagerial and Decision Economics.\n44\n,\n1\n,\np. 84-101\n18 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nGroup Dynamic\n100%\nGroup Dynamics\n100%\n2\nScopus \n citations\nThe effects of CEO narcissism on corporate social responsibility and irresponsibility\nHong, J. K.,\nLee, J. H.\n& Roh, T.,\nSep 2022\n,\nIn:\nManagerial and Decision Economics.\n43\n,\n6\n,\np. 1926-1940\n15 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nSocial Responsibility\n100%\nFirm Behavior\n66%\n23\nScopus \n citations\nView all 22 Research outputs\nPress/Media\nDifferent neuroprognostication thresholds of neuron-specific enolase in shockable and non-shockable out-of-hospital cardiac arrest: a prospective multicenter observational study in Korea (the KORHN-PRO registry)\nLee, J.-S.\n,\nLee, J.-H.\n,\nKim, Y.-G.\n,\nKim, J. W.\n&\nLee, J.\n9/08/23\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media"
