    "homepage_text": "Kyogu Lee's Homepage\nKyogu\nLee\nhttp://ccrma.stanford.edu/~kglee\nkglee (at) ccrma (dot) stanford (dot) edu\nFore more up-to-date information, please\nvisit my new homepage at\nhttp://marg.snu.ac.kr\n!\nPh.D.\nComputer-based Music\nTheory and\nAcoustics\nCenter for Computer Research in\nMusic and Acoustics\n(CCRMA)\nDepartment of Music\n,\nStanford University\nAdvisor: Prof.\nJulius O. Smith\nCo-Advisor:\nProf. Jonathan Berger,\nDr. Malcolm Slaney\nDissertation: A System for Acoustic Chord\nTranscription and Key Extraction from Audio Using Hidden Markov Models\nTrained on Synthesized Audio\nResearch Interests\nMusic Information Retrieval\nMachine Learning Methods for Music Applications\nComputational Model of Music Perception/Cognition\nComputational Auditory Scene Analysis\nDigital Audio Signal Processing\nPublications\n(in\nreverse chronological order)\n2009\nChing-Wei Chen\n,\nMarkus\nCremer\n, Kyogu Lee\n, Peter\nDiMaria, Ho-Hsiang Wu, “Improving Perceived Tempo Estimation by\nStatistical Modeling of Higher-Level Musical Descriptors”,\nAudio Engineering Society Convention\nPaper, to be presented at the 126th Convention, Munich, Germany\nKyogu Lee\n, Markus\nCremer, “Automatic Labelinig of Training Data for Singing Voice\nDetection in Musical Audio”,\nin\nProceedings of International Conference on Signal Processing, Pattern\nRecognition and Applications\n2008\nKyogu Lee\n, Markus\nCremer, “Segmentation-based Lyrics-Audio Alignment Using Dynamic\nProgramming”,\nin\nProceedings of International Conference on Music Information\nRetrieval, 2008, to appear\nKyogu Lee\n, “A System\nfor Acoustic Chord Transcription and Key Extraction from Audio\nUsing Hidden Markov Models Trained on Synthesized Audio”,\nPh.D. thesis, Stanford University\nKyogu Lee\n, Malcolm\nSlaney, “Acoustic Chord Transcription and Key Extraction from Audio\nUsing Key-Dependent\nHMMs Trained on Synthesized Audio”,\nin The IEEE\nTransactions on Audio, Speech and Language Processing, 16 (2), pp.\n291-301\n2007\nKyogu Lee\n, Malcolm\nSlaney, “A Unified System for Chord Transcription and Key Extraction\nUsing Hidden Markov Models”,\nin\nProceedings of International Conference on Music Information\nRetrieval,\n2007\nKyogu Lee\n, “A System\nfor\nAutomatic Chord Transcription Using Genre-Specific Hidden Markov\nModels”,\nin Proceedings of\nInternational\nWorkshop on Adaptive Multimedia Retrieval, 2007\n2006\nKyogu Lee\n, “Identifying\nCover Songs from Audio Using Harmonic Representation”,\nextended abstract submitted to MIREX\n(Music Information Retrieval Evaluation eXchange) task on Audio Cover\nSong Identification, 2006\nKyogu Lee\n, Malcolm\nSlaney, “Automatic Chord Recognition from Audio Using a Supervised HMM\nTrained with Audio-from-Symbolic Data”,\nin Proceedings of Audio and Music\nComputing for\nMultimedia Workshop in conjunction with ACM Multimedia, 2006\nKyogu Lee\n, Malcolm\nSlaney, “Automatic Chord Recognition Using an HMM with Supervised\nLearning”,\nin Proceedings of\nInternational Conference on Music Information Retrieval, 2006\nKyogu Lee\n, “Automatic\nChord Recognition Using Enhanced Pitch Class Profile”,\nin Proceedings of International Computer\nMusic\nConference, 2006\n2005\nKyogu Lee\n, Minjong Kim,\n“Estimating the Amplitude of the Cubic Difference Tone Using a\nThird-Order Adaptive Volterra\nFilter”,\nin Proceedings of\nInternational Conference on Digital Audio Effects, 2005\nKyogu Lee\n, Greg\nSell, Jonathan Berger, “Sonification Using Digital Waveguide\nAnd 2- and 3-Dimensional Digital Waveguide Mesh”,\nin\nProceedings of International\nConference on Auditory Display, 2005\nKyogu Lee\n, “Automatic\nChord Recognition Using a Summary Autocorrelation Function”,\nStanford EE391 Special Report, 2005\nAaron Master,\nKyogu Lee\n,\n“Explicit Onset Modeling Using Time Reassignment”,\nin IEEE Proceedings of International\nConference\non\nAcoustics, Speech, and Signal\nProcessing, 2005\n2004\nKyogu Lee\n,“Pitch\nPerception: Place Theory, Temporal Theory, and Beyond”,\nStanford EE391 Special Report, 2004\nKyogu Lee\n, Julius\nSmith,\n“Implementation of a Highly Diffusing 2-D Digital Waveguide Mesh with a\nQuadratic Residue\nDiffuser”,\nin Proceedings of\nInternational Computer Music Conference, 2004\nRyan Cassidy, Jonathan Berger,\nKyogu\nLee\n, “\nAnalysis of\nhyperspectral colon tissue images using vocal synthesis models\n”,\nin\nIEEE Asilomar Conference On\nSignals, Systems, and Computers, 2004\nRyan Cassidy, Jonathan Berger,\nKyogu\nLee\n, “Auditory Display of Hyperspectral Colon Tissue Images\nUsing Vocal Synthesis Models”,\nin\nProceedings of International\nConference on Auditory Display, 2004\nCurriculum Vitae"
