    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "ï»¿\nWelcome to Yang Yang Lab\nHome\nMembers\nPrincipal Investigator\nResearch Staff\nPostdocs\nPh.D Students\nPh.D Alumni\nOther Alumni\nResearch\nOrganic Photovoltaics\nPerovskite Photovoltaics\nCZTS Photovoltaics\nThin-film Transistors\nPublications\nPress & Awards\nPress\nAwards\nIssued Patents\nOur Articles and Videos\nFacilities\nContact\nMore:\nWelcome to Prof. Yang Yang's Laboratory.\nWe are working on solution processable thin film electronic devices.\r\n\r\nThe devices we study include photovoltaic cells, digital memory units, light emitting diodes and thin film transistors. We are using various kinds of materials, including conjugate polymers, carbon based nanomaterials, as well as solution processable inorganic semiconductors, to pursue the highest performance based on a thin film made at extremely low cost.\nWe are recruiting Post-Doctoral reseachers with background in chemistry and device physics.\nHard-working undergrads, master and PhD students are also welcomed to apply for our group!\nAnnouncement\nWe are seeking hard working MS students to join our group.\nNews\nUCLA Materials Scientists Lead Global Team in Finding Solutions to Biggest Hurdle for Solar Cell Technology\n3/2022\nALS Science Highlights: A Properly Tailored Tail Boosts Solar-Cell Efficiency\n4/2021\nProf. Yang Yang was invited to join the Advanced Materials Hall of Fame.\n4/2021\næ¨é³è¯¾é¢ç»è¿ç¯Scienceï¼åç°ééç¿ä¸­åå­çâåéäººæ ¼âï¼\n2/2021\nè¥¿æ¹å¤§å­¦åé¢é¿ï¼è¢«å¼11ä¸æ¬¡ï¼Hææ°157ï¼æ¡ææ»¡å¤©ä¸ï¼\n2/2021\nUCLA Material Scientists Discover New Ways to Power Up Nanomaterials for Electronic Applications\n2/2021\nå«æ¬¡æç ´ä¸ççºªå½ï¼å¹å»ååä½ä½éå¹´ææï¼UCLAæ¨é³:ä¼¯ä¹å¦ä½æé åéé©¬\n1/2021\nPerovskite Photovoltaics: The Road Ahead\n11/2020\nAs November 1st, 2020, Prof. Yang Yang has returned to UCLA full time ï¼æ¨é³èå¸å·²äº2020å¹´11æ1æ¥å¨èåå°UCLAï¼.\nEffective from July 1st, 2019, Prof. Yang Yang took a Leave of Absence to join the Westlake University in Hangzhou, China. He can still be reached via email.\nProf. Yang named 2019 Sustainable Energy Award Winner by Royal Society of Chemistry\n4/2019\nç§å­¦å®¶çèæ´ï¼ç¨åå¡æ¹é å¤ªé³è½çµæ± åï¼è½ææé«äº20%\n4/2019\nCaffeine Peps Up Solar Energy: our latest research shows the human energizer also improves the efficiency and stability of perovskite solar cells\n4/2019\nCongratulations to Professor Huanping Zhou to be named 35 Innovators Under 35 by MIT Technology Review!\n7/2018\nCongratulations to our graduated PhD student Letian Dou to become an assistant professor in Purdue Univeristy!\n7/2018\nCongratulations to Professor Yang and Dr. Gang Li to be named Highly Cited Researchers 2015 by Thomson Reuters\n1/2016\nCongratulations to our paper in 2005 \"High-efficiency solution processable polymer photovoltaic cells by self-organization of polymer blends\" to be the second most cited research in the last decade\n12/2015\nOur paper \"Printable Ultrathin Metal Oxide Semiconductor-Based Conformal Biosensors\" is highlighted on the cover of latest issue of ACS Nano. Congratulations! (12/2015)\nWelcome our new postdoc, Dr.\nLijian Zuo\nfrom Zhejiang University! (10/2015)\nWelcome young students to join YYLab:\nMichael Zhou, Onur Sahin, Kaiyue Wang and Aneeket Palankar\n! (10/2015)\nProf.\nYang\nbecame Fellow of the American Physical Society (APS). Congratulations!  (10/2015)\nCongratulations to\nJingbi\n, his paper on long lifetime perovskite solar cells has published online in the Nature Nanotechnology. (10/2015)\nCongratulations to\nLetian\n(PhD 2014), his paper on 2D perovskite material has published in the Science Magazine.  (09/2015)\nNew members joining YYLab: Dr.\nEn-Ping Yao\n(Postdoc) and\nZhanlue Yang\n. Welcome! (09/2015)\nCongratulations to\nPeter\n, he passed his PhD Oral Qualifying Exam. (09/2015)\nDr.\nJeehwan Kim\nbecomes assistant professor at Department of Mechanical Engineer, MIT.  Jeehwan, remember to get some sleep.\nRoger\npassed his PhD Oral Qualifying Exam. Congratulations. (08/2015)\nSuper good news,\nHuanping\nreceived the Young Thousand Talent award from China, and becomes an Assistant Professor (Materials Science) of Peking University. (07/2015)\nSuper good news,\nJingbi\nreceived the Young Thousand Talent award from China,  and becomes Professor of the Institute of Semiconductors, Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS). (07/2015)\nMore"
  },
