    "homepage_text": "Ge Zhang\nGe Zhang 张鸽\nLecturer\nSchool of Computer Science and Technology\nDonghua University\nShanghai, China\n[Google Scholar]\nEmail: gezhang [at] dhu.edu.cn\nBIOGRAPHY\nGe Zhang, Ph.D., is a lecturer at the College of Information and Intelligent Science, Donghua University, and a recipient of the Shanghai Pujiang Talent Program. She earned her Ph.D. in Computer Science from Macquarie University, Australia, in 2024, and was awarded the Microsoft Research PhD Fellowship Award in 2022 (the only recipient in the Australia & New Zealand region that year). Her research interests include Anomaly Detection and Large Language Models. Prospective graduate or undergraduate students with an interest in the above research topics are welcome to join her team.\n张鸽，博士，东华大学信息与智能科学学院讲师，上海市浦江人才。 2024年于澳大利亚麦考瑞大学获得计算机科学博士学位，2022年获Microsoft Research Phd Fellowship Award (微软学者奖，2022年澳大利亚&新西兰地区唯一获奖者)。研究兴趣为异常检测、大语言模型等领域。目前已在相关领域中国计算机协会(CCF)推荐A类会议及SCI 1区期刊上发表多篇论文。欢迎对以上研究感兴趣的准研究生或本科生加入团队。\nPROJECTS\n1. 上海市白玉兰人才计划浦江项目（A类），主持，在研\n2. 中央高校自由探索项目，主持，在研\nPUBLICATIONS\nLearning Subgraph-based Normality for Interpretable Graph-level Anomaly Detection\nGe Zhang\n, Zhenyu Yang, Jia Wu, Pengfei Jiao, Jian Yang, Hao Peng, Xixun Lin\nIEEE Transactions on Information Forensics & Security (TIFS), 2026\nCCF A类，中科院一区Top\nGeneralizable Graph-level Anomaly Detection via Prompted Anomaly Expansion and Normality Extraction\nGe Zhang\n, Jiapei Chen, Guohao Sun, Xiu Fang, Zhenyu Yang, Xixun Lin, Liang Yang\nInternational World Wide Web Conference (WWW), 2026\nCCF A类\nEnhancing Graph Neural Networks for Out-of-distribution Graph Detection\nGe Zhang\n, Zhenyu Yang, Jia Wu, Pengfei Jiao, Jian Yang\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Network and Learning Systems (TNNLS), 2025\n中科院一区Top\nCINA: Curvature-based Integrated Network Alignment with Hypergraph\nPengfei Jiao, Yuanqi Liu, Yinghui Wang,\nGe Zhang* (corresponding author)\nIEEE International Conference on Data Engineering (ICDE)\n,  2024\nCCF A类\nGraph Neural Networks for Imbalanced Graph-level Anomaly Detection\nGe Zhang\n, Zhenyu Yang, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Shan Xue, Hao Peng, Jianlin Su, Chuan Zhou, Quan Z. Sheng, Leman Akoglu, Charu Aggarwal\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n,   2022\nCCF A类\n[PDF]\neFraudCom: An E-commerce Fraud Detection System via Competitive Graph Neural Networks\nGe Zhang\n, Zhao Li, Jiaming Huang, Jia Wu, Chuan Zhou and Jian Yang\nACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS), 40(3), pp.1-29\n,   2022\nCCF A类\n[PDF]\nFRAUDRE: Fraud Detection Dual-Resistant to Graph Inconsistency and Imbalance\nGe Zhang\n, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Amin Beheshti, Chuan Zhou, Quan Z. Sheng\nIEEE International Conference on Data Minging (ICDM)\n,   2021\nCCF B类\nAcceptance Rate: 9.9%,\nBest Student Paper Award 最佳学生论文奖\n[PDF]\nFinding Communities with Hierarchical Semantics by Distinguishing General and Specialized Topic\nGe Zhang\n, Di Jin, Jian Gao, Pengfei Jiao, Francoise Fogelman Soulie and Xin Huang\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial and Intelligence (IJCAI)\n,   2018\nCCF A类\n[PDF]\nRevisiting Graph-Level Anomaly Detection: From Partially to Fully Unsupervised Learning\nZhenyu Yang,\nGe Zhang\n, Shan Xue, Xiaoxiao Ma, Jian Yang, Hao Peng, Amin Beheshti, Jia Wu\nInternational World Wide Web Conference (WWW), 2026\nCCF A类\nLearning from Graph-Graph Relationship: A New Perspective on Graph-level Anomaly Detection\nZhenyu Yang,\nGe Zhang\n, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Hao Peng\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE), 2025\nCCF A类\nGlobal Interpretable Graph-level Anomaly Detection Via Prototype\nZhenyu Yang,\nGe Zhang\n, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Shan Xue, Amin Beheshti, Hao Peng, Quan Z. Sheng\nSIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD), 2025\nCCF A类\nConformal Graph-level Out-of-distribution Detection with Adaptive Data Augmentation\nXixun Lin, Yanan Cao, Nan Sun, Lixin Zou, Chuan Zhou, Peng Zhang, Shuai Zhang,\nGe Zhang\n, Jia Wu\nInternational World Wide Web Conference (WWW), 2025\nCCF A类\nState of the Art and Potentialities of Graph-level Learning\nZhenyu Yang,\nGe Zhang\n, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Quan Z Sheng, Shan Xue, Chuan Zhou, Charu Aggarwal, Hao Peng, Wenbin Hu, Edwin Hancock, Pietro Liò\nACM Computing Surveys (CSUR), 2024\n中科院一区Top\n[PDF]\nMinimum Entropy Principle Guided Graph Neural Networks\nZhenyu Yang,\nGe Zhang\n, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Quan Z Sheng, Hao Peng, Angsheng Li, Shan Xue, Jianlin Su\nACM Conference on Web Search and Data Mining (WSDM)\n,   2023\nCCF B类\n[PDF]\nDetecting Communities with Multiplex Semantics by Distinguishing Background, General and Specialized Topics\nDi Jin, Kunzeng Wang,\nGe Zhang\n, Pengfei Jiao, Dongxiao He, Francoise Fogelman Soulie and Xin Huang\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE), 32(11), pp. 2144-2158\n,   2019\nCCF A类\n[PDF]\nGraph-level Neural Networks: Current Progress and Future Directions\nGe Zhang\n, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Chuan Zhou, Hao Peng, Quan Z. Sheng, and Charu Aggarwal\narXiv:2205.15555\n,   2022\n[PDF]\nAWARDS\n上海市浦江人才（科研开发类）\n上海市人才工作局\n, 2025\nVice-Chancellor’s Commendation for Academic Excellence (校长奖）\nMacquarie University\n, 2024\nFaculty Excellence Award (Excellence in HDR Student Award Highly Commended)\nFaculty of Science and Engineering, Macquarie University\n, 2022\nMicrosoft Research PhD Fellowship Award (2022年澳大利亚新西兰地区唯一获奖者）\nMicrosoft Research\n,   2022.\n[Link 链接]\nNeurIPS Scholar Award\nNeurIPS\n,   2022.\nHigher Degree Research Rising Star Award\nSchool of Computing, Faculty of Science and Engineering, Macquarie University\n,   2022.\nBest Student Paper Award\nIEEE ICDM\n, 2021.\n[Link 链接]"
