    "github": "https://github.com/ZhenyuYangMQ",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zhenyu Yang's homepage\nZhenyu Yang\nPhD Candidate with the School of Computing at Macquarie University\nSydney, NSW, AU\nEmail\nGitHub\nGoogle Scholar\nBIOGRAPHY\nZhenyu Yang is currently a Ph.D. student with the\nSchool of Computing at Macquarie University\n, supervised by\nProf. Jia Wu\nand\nProf. Jian Yang\n. His research interest is to build trustworthy and robust graph anomaly algorithms upon weakly supervised or unsupervised real-world scenarios. Previously, he received his Master's degree in the School of Computing at Macquarie University.\nNEWS\n2026/01: Our paper on\nGeneralizable Graph-level Anomaly Detection via Prompted Anomaly Expansion and Normality Extraction\nhas been accepted by WWW.\n2026/01: Our paper on\nSemi-Supervised Fake News Detection with Mixture of Experts\nhas been accepted by WWW.\n2026/01: Our paper on\nRevisiting Graph-Level Anomaly Detection From Partially to Fully Unsupervised Learning\nhas been accepted by WWW.\n2025/12: Our paper on\nLearning Subgraph-Based Normality for Interpretable Graph-Level Anomaly Detection\nhas been accepted by TIFS.\n2025/10: Our paper on\nLearning from Graph-Graph Relationship A New Perspective On Graph-level Anomaly Detection\nhas been accepted by TKDE.\n2025/08: Awarded the\nKDD 2025 Travel Grant\nby SIGKDD.\n2025/06: Our paper on\nEnhancing Graph Neural Networks for Out-of-distribution Graph Detection\nhas been accepted by TNNLS.\n2025/05: Our paper on\nGlobal Interpretable Graph-level Anomaly Detection via Prototype\nhas been accepted by SIGKDD.\n2024/09: Our paper on\nState of the Art and Potentialities of Graph-level Learning\nhas been accepted by CSUR.\n2024/05: Awarded the\nDigital Finance Cooperative Research Centre (DFCRC) PhD Top-Up Scholarship\nby DFCRC.\n2023/11: Awarded the\nHigher Degree Research Rising Star\nby School of Computing, Macquarie University.\n2023/02: Our paper on\nMinimum Entropy Principle Guided Graph Neural Networks\nhas been accepted by WSDM.\n2022/11: Our paper on\nDual-discriminative Graph Neural Network for Imbalanced Graph-level Anomaly Detection\nhas been accepted by NeurIPS.\n2022/01: Our paper on\nLow-rank and Sparse Representation Based Learning for Cancer Survivability Prediction\nhas been accepted by Information Science.\n2021/08: Awarded the\nInternational Research Training Program (iRTP) Scholarship\nby Macquarie Univerisity.\n2021/07: Awarded the\nExcellence Graduates\nby School of Computer Science and Engineering, University of New South Wales.\nPUBLICATIONS\n2026\nGeneralizable Graph-level Anomaly Detection via Prompted Anomaly Expansion and Normality Extraction\nGe Zhang, Jiapei Chen, Guohao Sun, Xiu Fang, Zhenyu Yang, Xixun Lin, Liang Yang\nWWW (CCF-A)\nSemi-Supervised Fake News Detection with Mixture of Experts\nZhenyu Yang, Chaoyu Yang, Wenfeng Xu, Xiuxiu Hao, Huan Wang, Ge Zhang, Xiaoxiao Ma, Jun Shen\nWWW (CCF-A)\nRevisiting Graph-Level Anomaly Detection From Partially to Fully Unsupervised Learning\nZhenyu Yang, Ge Zhang, Shan Xue, Xiaoxiao Ma, JiaWu, Jian Yang, Hao Peng, Amin Beheshti\nWWW (CCF-A)\n2025\nLearning Subgraph-Based Normality for Interpretable Graph-Level Anomaly Detection\nGe Zhang, Zhenyu Yang, Jia Wu, Pengfei Jiao, Jian Yang, Hao Peng, Xixun Lin\nTIFS (CCF-A)\nLearning from Graph-Graph Relationship A New Perspective On Graph-level Anomaly Detection\nZhenyu Yang, Ge Zhang, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Hao Peng, Pietro Liò\nTKDE (IF 10.4, CCF-A)\nEnhancing Graph Neural Networks for Out-of-distribution Graph Detection\nGe Zhang, Zhenyu Yang, Jia Wu, Pengfei Jiao, Jian Yang\nTNNLS (IF 8.9, CCF-B)\nGlobal Interpretable Graph-level Anomaly Detection via Prototype\nZhenyu Yang, Ge Zhang, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Shan Xue, Amin Beheshti, Hao Peng, Quan Z. Sheng\nSIGKDD (CCF-A)\n2024\nState of the Art and Potentialities of Graph-level Learning\nZhenyu Yang, Ge Zhang, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Quan Z. Sheng, Shan Xue, Chuan Zhou, Charu Aggarwal, Hao Peng, Wenbin Hu, Edwin Hancock, Pietro Li`o\nCSUR (IF 28)\n2023\nMinimum Entropy Principle Guided Graph Neural Networks\nZhenyu Yang, Ge Zhang, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Quan Z. Sheng, Hao Peng, Angsheng Li, Shan Xue, Jianlin Su\nWSDM (CCF-B)\n2022\nDual-discriminative Graph Neural Network for Imbalanced Graph-level Anomaly Detection\nGe Zhang, Zhenyu Yang, Jia Wu, Jian Yang, Shan Xue, Hao Peng, Jianlin Su, Chuan Zhou, Quan Z. Sheng, Leman Akoglu, Charu C. Aggarwal\nNeurIPS (CCF-A)\nLow-rank and Sparse Representation Based Learning for Cancer Survivability Prediction\nJie Yang, Jun Ma, Khin Than Win, Junbin Gao, Zhenyu Yang\nInformation Science (CCF-B)\nAWARDS\n•\nKDD 2025 Travel Grant\n.\n–– SIGKDD, 2025\n•\nDigital Finance Cooperative Research Centre (DFCRC) PhD Top-Up Scholarship\n.\n–– DFCRC, 2024\n•\nHigher Degree Research Rising Star\n.\n–– School of Computing, Macquarie University, 2023\n•\nInternational Research Training Program (iRTP) Scholarship\n.\n–– Macquarie Univerisity, 2021\n•\nExcellence Graduates\n.\n–– School of Computer Science and Engineering, University of New South Wales, 2021"
  },
  "serper::Jian Yang": {
    "homepage": "https://jianyang.org/",
    "emails": [
      "jianyang_phi@outlook.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "HOME - JIAN YANG\nSkip to content\nJIAN YANG\nMenu\nClose\nI’m a Senior Research Fellow at the Institute of Advanced Study in Law, Technology, and Humanities at Northwest University of Political Science and Law. Previously, I was an Associate Professor at the Law School of Nanjing Normal University. I have held visiting positions at Soochow University in Taiwan, Indiana University in the United States, and Cornell University.\nFrom 2010 to 2020, my research primarily focused on the normative analysis of legal concepts within the Chinese political context, addressing issues such as legal culture (fa zhi wen hua), the rule of law society (fa zhi she hui), grassroots social governance, and China’s artificial intelligence policies. In recent years, I have also been exploring the general nature and grounding issues of legal theory within analytical jurisprudence.\nYou can contact me at\njianyang_phi@outlook.com\n, and download my\nCV\nhere."
  },
