    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xinchao Wang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nXinchao Wang\nXinchao Wang\nAssociate Professor\nxML Lab\n@\nNUS\n,\nCDE\n,\nECE\nxinchao-AT-nus.edu.sg\nWe are always looking for\nPhD Students\n/\nPostdocs\nVisiting Students / Scholars\nResearch Assistants\non Machine Learning, and Artificial Intelligence\n.\nSimplicity is the final achievement. --- Frederic Chopin\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n] [\nDBLP\n]\nNews\nO\nur lab members becoming faculty members since 2025\nWeihao Yu\n(\nPhD Student), Assistant Professor,\nPeking\nUniver\nsi\nty\n(2026)\nJie Hu\n(Postdoc)\n,\nAssociate\nProfessor,\nXiamen\nUniversity (202\n6\n)\nJingwen Ye\n(\nPostdoc), Assistant Professor,\nMonash University\n(202\n5\n)\nSonghua Liu\n(\nPhD Student), Assistant Professor,\nShanghai Jiaotong\nUniversity\n(2025)\nXingyi Yang\n(\nPhD Student),  Assistant Professor\n+ Presidential Young Scholar\n,\nThe Hong Kong Polytechnic University\n(2025)\nOct 2025.\nSingapore Young Scientist Award\n.\nFeb 2025.\nAI's 10 to Watch\n, IEEE.\nDec\n2024. Our PhD student,\nFang Gongfan\n,\nawarded\nByteDance Scholarship.\nNov 2024. Our PhD student,\nMa Xinyin\n, awarded\nGoogle Fellowship\n.\nAug 2024.\nYoung Research Award\n, NUS.\nApr 2024. Our PhD students,\nLiu Songhua\nand\nYang Xingyi\nawarded\nChinese Government Award for Outstanding Self-financed Students Abroad\n.\nApr 2024.\nYoung Research Award\n, NUS CDE.\nJun 2023. Serving as an Associate Editor for\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\n.\nApr 202\n3\n. Our PhD student,\nYu Weihao\nawarded\nChinese Government Award for Outstanding Self-financed Students Abroad\n.\nFeb 2023.\nOutstanding Early Career Award\n, NUS CDE.\nFeb 2023.\nCollege Teaching Excellence Award\n, NUS CDE.\nDec 2022.\nBest Paper Award\n,\nIEEE VCIP 2022.\nNov 2022.\nPaper Award Nomination\n, NeurIPS 2022.\nBiography\nXinchao is currently an associate professor (with tenure) in the\nDepartment of ECE,\nNational University of Singapore (NUS)\n, where he previously held the position of Presidential Young Professor (Assistant Professor). Prior to joining NUS, he was an assistant professor\nin the\nDepartment of CS\n,\nStevens Institute of Technology\n. He\ndid a Postdoc at the\nImage Formation and Professing (IFP)\ngroup with late Prof\nThomas Huang\nat\nBeckman Institute\n,\nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (UIUC)\n. Xinchao received Ph.D. from the\nComputer Vision Lab\n,\nÉcole polytechnique fédérale de Lausanne (EPFL)\nin 2015 under the supervision of Prof\nPascal Fua\n,\nand the first-class honorable B.Sc. in\nDept. of Computing\n,\nthe Hong Kong Polytechnic University (HKPU)\nin 2010 (GPA 4.0/4.0, most outstanding thesis award).\nTeaching\nEE2211\nIntroduction to Machine Learning\n, National University of Singapore\nEE4704 Image Processing and Analysis, National University of Singapore\nEE5907 Pattern Recognition, National University of Singapore\nEE59\n34 Deep\nLearning\n, National University of Singapore\nEE6733 Advanced Topics on Vision and Machine Learning, National University of Singapore\nEE4808/EE4300 Machine Learning: Models and Applications\n, National University of Singapore R\nesearch Institute (SuZhou and Chongqing)\nOutstanding Teaching Recognition\n(Stevens Institute of Technology), Fall 2020.\nOutstanding Teaching Recognition\n(Stevens Institute of Technology), Fall 2019.\nCS 559, Machine Learning Fundamentals and Applications (Spring/Fall 2018, 2019, 2020), Stevens Institute of Technology\nCS 558, Computer Vision  (Spring 2019, 2020), Stevens Institute of Technology\nAlumni\nOur list of alumni can be found\nhere\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Mufan Bill Li": {
    "homepage": "https://mufan-li.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "mufan.li@uwaterloo.ca"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/academicpages",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/mufan-li-35749833/",
    "homepage_text": "Mufan Li\nFollow\nEmail\nTwitter\nBluesky\nLinkedIn\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout\nI am an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Statistics and Actuarial Science\nat the University of Waterloo, and a Faculty Affiliate at the\nVector Institute\n.\nPreviously I was a DataX Postdoctoral Research Associate at Princeton University, where I worked with\nBoris Hanin\n.\nI received my PhD from the Department of Statistical Sciences at the University of Toronto, where my advisors were\nDaniel Roy\nand\nMurat Erdogdu\n.\nYou can find my CV\nhere\n.\nResearch\nI am broadly interested in\ndeep learning theory\n.\nMost recently, I have been thinking a lot about\nscaling limits\nof large neural networks and their training dynamics.\nYou can find a list of my research work\nhere\n.\nBlog\nI attempt to maintain a blog of interesting mathematics I encounter, but does not necessarily fit into my research program. You can find the current list of my blog posts\nhere\n."
  },
