    "homepage_text": "Chengxuan Zhu's Homepage\nChengxuan\nZhu\nEmai1: peterzhu [at] pku [dot] edu [dot] cn\nI am a second-year Ph.D. student at National Key Lab of General AI, School of Intelligence Science and Technology,\nPeking University\n. Currently I’m working in\nCameraLab\n, supervised by Prof.\nBoxin Shi\nand Prof.\nChao Xu\n. I received my B.Sc. degree from\nschool of electronic engineering and computer science\nin\nPeking University\n.\nMy research interest lies in computer vision and computational photography. I’m open to new ideas and cross-field collaboration. Feel free to contact me for further discussion.\nDuring free time, I am also a passionate professional photographer, working with Visual China Group and Peking University. You may find my works published at the official account of PKU on such platforms as Weibo, Wechat, Instagram, etc.\nPublications\n(*: Equal Contribution)\nBokehDiff: Neural Lens Blur with One-Step Diffusion\nChengxuan Zhu\n,\nQingnan Fan\n,\nQi Zhang\n, Jinwei Chen, Huaqi Zhang, Chao Xu,\nBoxin Shi\nIn\nProceedings of International Conference on Computer Vision\n, 2025.\npdf\ncode\nPlaNet: Learning to Mitigate Atmospheric Turbulence in Planetary Images\nYifei Xia\n,\nChu Zhou\n,\nChengxuan Zhu\n, Chao Xu,\nBoxin Shi\nIn\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n, 2025.\npdf\nNB-GTR: Narrow-Band Guided Turbulence Removal\nYifei Xia\n,\nChu Zhou\n,\nChengxuan Zhu\n,\nMinggui Teng\n, Chao Xu,\nBoxin Shi\nIn\nProceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n, 2024.\npdf\nNeural Underwater Scene Representation\nYunkai Tang*,\nChengxuan Zhu\n*,\nRenjie Wan\n, Chao Xu,\nBoxin Shi\nIn\nProceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n, 2024.\npdf\nColorizing Monochromatic Radiance Fields\nYean Cheng\n,\nRenjie Wan\n,\nShuchen Weng\n,\nChengxuan Zhu\n, Yakun Chang,\nBoxin Shi\nOral\n, In\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n, 2024.\npdf\ncode\nOcclusion-Free Scene Recovery via Neural Radiance Fields\nChengxuan Zhu\n,\nRenjie Wan\n, Yunkai Tang,\nBoxin Shi\nIn\nProceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n, 2023.\npdf\ncode\nWhen Visible Light (Backscatter) Communication Meets Neuromorphic Cameras in V2X\nKenuo Xu\n*, Kexing Zhou*,\nChengxuan Zhu\n*,\nShanghang Zhang\n,\nBoxin Shi\n, Xiaoqiang Li,\nTiejun Huang\n,\nChenren Xu\nIn\nProceedings of the 24th International Workshop on Mobile Computing Systems and Applications\n, 2023.\npdf\nNeural Transmitted Radiance Fields\nChengxuan Zhu\n*,\nRenjie Wan\n*,\nBoxin Shi\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n, 2022.\npdf\ncode\nExperiences\nIntern Algorithm Engineer, Vivo, 2024\nGuest Lecturer\non Photojournalism\n, YASP PKU, Spring 2024\nTeaching Assistant, Scientific Writing, Spring 2023-2024\nTeaching Assistant, Learning Data Science with Python, Spring 2022-2023\nTeaching Assistant, Introduction to Computer Systems, Fall 2022-2023\nTeaching Assistant, Algorithm Design and Analysis, Spring 2021-2022\nTeaching Assistant, Introduction to Computer Systems, Fall 2021-2022\nChief Photographer, Student News Agency of Peking University, 2023/10-Present\nVice Editor in Chief, Student News Agency of Peking University, 2022/3-2024/9\nChief Editor in photography, Student News Agency of Peking University, 2021/3-2022/3\nVice Editor in photography, Student News Agency of Peking University, 2020/9-2021/3"
  },
  "serper::Xiangming Gu": {
    "homepage": "https://guxm2021.github.io/",
    "emails": [
