    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/BingCS",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/bing-wang-303926263",
    "homepage_text": "WANG Bing\nWANG\nBing\nAssistant Professor @\nFaculty of Engineering\n,\nThe Hong Kong Polytechnic University\nI am an Assistant Professor in\nRobotics and Autonomous Systems\nat the Faculty of Engineering, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University (PolyU). Before joining PolyU, I was recognized as a TopMinds (天才少年) by Huawei, where I led a research team in the Optical Product Line and developed advanced solutions for Autonomous Driving and AR-HUD.\nI completed my DPhil in Computer Science at the University of Oxford, under the supervision of\nProf. Niki Trigoni\nand\nProf. Andrew Markham\n. Prior to this, I was supervised by\nProf. Qingquan Li\nin Spatial Information.\nMy research focuses on\nSpatial Intelligence\n, a dynamic field where I aim to advance human-level spatial perception and world understanding on mobile robotics platforms such as drones, ground robots and underwater vehicles. My work addresses the critical need for robust and efficient spatial perception solutions that substantially improve the\nreliability, intelligence, and security\nof intelligent machines in real-world settings. At the core of my research are four pivotal dimensions: Multi-modal Learning, 3D Reconstruction, Scene Understanding, and Pose Estimation. Discover more about my research on my\nProjects\npage.\nNews\nJan 10, 2026\nVery honored to join\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\nas an\nAssociate Editor\n!\nDec 24, 2025\nOur team has received multiple prestigious recognitions, including\nWorkshop Best Paper Award @ ACM MobiCom 2025 HotSense\n,\nJohn Davison Second Prize @ PE&RS 2025\nand\nSmart City Technology Innovation Bronze Award @ ICUI 2025\n!\nDec 20, 2025\nOur papers\nMini-Splatting2\nand\nGrowSP++\nare accepted by\nTPAMI\n!\nOct 16, 2025\nOur papers\nMMOne\n,\nNormalCrafter\n,\nMambaML\nare accepted by\nICCV 2025\n!\nAug 31, 2025\nInvited as a\nTechnical Papers Committee Member (Area Chair)\n, and also serving as\nSession Chair @ 4D & Dynamic Scene Generation and Reconstruction\nin December 2025 for\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2025\n!\nAug 06, 2025\nWe will organize a Thematic Session,\nSpatial Intelligence in the Wild\nat the International Society for Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing\nISPRS Congress 2026\n. See you in Toronto!\nJun 10, 2025\nTwo papers,\nCMFM\nand\nPF-USIE\n, have been accepted to\nISPRS J\nand\nInformation Fusion\n, respectively!\nSelected Publications\nTPAMI\nEfficient Scene Modeling via Structure-Aware and Region-Prioritized 3D Gaussians\nGuangchi Fang, and\nBing Wang\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n, 2025\nISPRS J\nCross-Modal 2D-3D Feature Matching: Simultaneous Local Feature Description and Detection across Images and Point Clouds\nWei Ma, Yucheng Huang, Shengjun Tang, Xianwei Zheng, and\n5 more authors\nISPRS Journal of Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing\n, 2025\nICCV\nMMOne: Representing Multiple Modalities in One Scene\nZhifeng Gu, and\nBing Wang\nIn Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n, 2025\nECCV\nMini-Splatting: Representing Scenes with a Constrained Number of Gaussians\nGuangchi Fang, and\nBing Wang\nIn The European Conference on Computer Vision\n, 2024\narXiv\nCode\nECCV\nEqui-GSPR: Equivariant SE(3) Graph Network Model for Sparse Point Cloud Registration\nXueyang Kang, Zhaoliang Luan, Kourosh Khoshelham, and\nBing Wang\nIn The European Conference on Computer Vision\n, 2024\nECCV’24 Oral\nCode\nISPRS J\nLook at the Whole Scene: General Point Cloud Place Recognition by Classification Proxy\nYue Xie,\nBing Wang\n, Haiping Wang, Fuxun Liang, and\n3 more authors\nISPRS Journal of Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing\n, 2024\nHTML\nCode\nTNNLS\nDeep Learning for Visual Localization and Mapping: A Survey\nChanghao Chen,\nBing Wang\n, Chris Xiaoxuan Lu, Niki Trigoni, and\n1 more author\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\n, 2023\nHTML\nCode\nICLR\nDM-NeRF: 3D Scene Geometry Decomposition and Manipulation from 2D Images\nBing Wang\n, Lu Chen, and Bo Yang\nIn The International Conference on Learning Representations\n, 2023\narXiv\nCode\nICCV\nP2-Net: Joint Description and Detection of Local Features for Pixel and Point Matching\nBing Wang\n, Changhao Chen, Zhaopeng Cui, Jie Qin, and\n7 more authors\nIn The IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n, 2021\nHTML\nCode\nAAAI\nAtLoc: Attention Guided Camera Localization\nBing Wang\n, Changhao Chen, Chris Xiaoxuan Lu, Peijun Zhao, and\n2 more authors\nIn The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n, 2020\nAAAI’20 Oral\narXiv\nHTML\nCode"
