    "homepage_text": "Minhao Yan\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nMinhao Yan\nMinhao Yan\nWelcome to my website!\nI’m a Research Data Scientist at Google with a Ph.D. in Applied Economics from Cornell University.\nHere is my\nCV\n.\nFields of interest:\nDevelopment Economics, Food and Agricultural Economics, Behavioral Research\nMethodologies:\nDynamic Optimization, Machine Learning, Statistical Modeling\nMy current research focuses on examining social welfare policies, such as food pantries and SNAP, to address food security challenges, while also investigating supply chain management strategies to ensure food safety. With a strong foundation in operations research and statistics from my bachelor’s and master’s degrees, I apply machine learning and advanced statistical modeling to tackle real-world issues in applied economics. Additionally, I analyze public policy through the lens of behavioral economics, striving to provide insights that can inform more effective and equitable policy solutions.\nContact:\nmy497@cornell.edu\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Linyuan Gong": {
    "homepage": "https://gonglinyuan.com/",
