    "homepage_text": "Chenjie Gu\n      -  Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University\nXi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University Home\nSearch content at Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University\n©\ncopyrightStatement\nView Scopus Profile\nChenjie Gu\nAssistant Professor\nThink Tank\nPhone\n+86 (0)512 81884963\nEmail\nChenjie.Gu\nxjtlu.edu\ncn\nh-index\n126\nCitations\n2\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2021\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nPersonal profile\nDr. Chenjie Gu is an Assistant Professor at the XIPU Institution, XJTLU. He got PhD in Management Science and Engineering from Tongji University. His doctoral thesis focuses on the simulation and optimization of ecosystem services and land use pattern at a city scale. The research fields include: ecological plan, land use simulation, urban analytic, spatial analysis, and smart city.\nResearch interests\nurban analytic and spatial analysis\nland use simulation\necological plan\nExperience\nAssistant Professor, XIPUI, XJTLU, 2023-present\nEducation/Academic qualification\nPhD Management Science and Engineering, Tongji University, 2023\nMS Smart Cities and Urban Analytic, University College London, 2018\nBA Urban Planning, XJTLU, 2017\nPerson Types\nStaff\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 8\nDecent Work and Economic Growth\nSDG 9\nIndustry, Innovation, and Infrastructure\nSDG 11\nSustainable Cities and Communities\nSDG 15\nLife on Land\nSDG 17\nPartnerships for the Goals\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Chenjie Gu is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nSpatial Mismatch\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n100%\nEcosystem Service\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n100%\nSocioeconomic Status\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n100%\nScenario Analysis\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n100%\nMegacity\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n100%\nChina\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n100%\nRatio\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n44%\nUrban Vegetation\nSocial Sciences\n25%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nProjects\n4\nFinished\n4\nActive\nThe Yangtze River Delta Research Base for S&amp;T Innovation and Sustainable Development\nSong, Y.\n(PI),\nZhu, X.\n(Team member),\nBai, X.\n(Team member),\nLin, Q.\n(Team member),\nGu, C.\n(Team member), Hu, C. (Team member), Ge, Y. (Team member),\nXu, Y.\n(Team member), Yao, X. (Team member), Lin, L. (Team member), Li, H. (Team member),\nRuan, Z.\n(Team member),\nXu, S.\n(Team member),\nMa, F.\n(Team member),\nKuang, X.\n(Team member),\nHao, J.\n(Team member),\nMeng, M.\n(Team member),\nLiu, X.\n(Team member),\nHan, J.\n(Team member),\nWang, X.\n(Team member),\nCao, X.\n(Team member),\nChen, Y.\n(Team member),\nZong, L.\n(Team member),\nZhang, X.\n(Team member),\nXie, L.\n(Team member),\nSun, J.\n(Team member),\nChen, B.\n(Team member),\nLu, X.\n(Team member),\nJiang, J.\n(Team member), Lu, N. (Team member), Fang, W. (Team member), Li, Z. (Team member), Xu, Z. (Team member) & Shen, W. (Team member)\n1/01/26\n→\n31/12/29\nProject\n:\nGovernmental Research Project\nEconomic and Social Development\n100%\nThe impact of the digital infrastructure on urban ESG development\nGu, C.\n(PI)\n20/07/25\n→\n19/07/27\nProject\n:\nGovernmental Research Project\nEnvironmental, Social and Corporate Governance\n100%\nESG\n100%\n数字基础设施对城市ESG发展的影响\nGu, C.\n(PI) & Chen, X. (Team member)\n20/07/25\n→ …\nProject\n:\nCollaborative Research Project\nEvolution Mechanism and Optimization of Ecosystem Services Supply-Demand Equilibrium in Mega-cities in China\nGu, C.\n(PI)\n1/01/25\n→\n31/12/26\nProject\n:\nInternal Research Project\nEcosystem Services\n100%\nMegacity\n100%\nSpatial optimization and simulation of land use from the perspective of carbon neutrality in mega cities in China\nGu, C.\n(PI)\n1/07/24\n→\n31/08/24\nProject\n:\nInternal Research Project\nView all 8 projects\nResearch output\n4\nArticle\n4\nLetter\n1\nCommissioned report\n1\nConference Proceeding\nFragmented but greener? Bad geography promotes higher green space accessibility: evidence from 356 Chinese cities\nWang, L.,\nGu, C.\n, Zhang, Z. & Song, W.,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nEcological Indicators.\n180\n,\n114339\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\n1\nCitation\n(Scopus)\n苏州低空经济高质量发展的三重协同路径\nGu, C.\n&\nSong, Y.\n,\n29 Jul 2025\n,\nIn:\n苏州日报.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nLetter\n长三角地区迈向碳中和的土地利用多情景模拟\nGu, C.\n& Chen, J.,\n2025\n,\n2025中国城市规划年会论文集.\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book or Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nConference Proceeding\n›\npeer-review\nEvaluating the driving factors of the environmental injustice caused by the spatial mismatch of ecosystem services in mega cities in China\nGu, C.\n, Shi, Q. & Chao, X.,\nAug 2024\n,\nIn:\nUrban Ecosystems.\n27\n,\n4\n,\np. 1349-1365\n17 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nChina\n100%\nEcosystem Service\n100%\nMegacity\n100%\nSpatial Mismatch\n100%\nRatio\n44%\n1\nCitation\n(Scopus)\n强链补链完善低空经济产业发展布局\nGu, C.\n,\n26 Nov 2024\n,\nIn:\n苏州日报.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nLetter\nView all 10 research outputs\nActivities\n1\nPublication Peer-review\n1\nMembership of committee\nThe Commerce Economy Association of China (External organisation)\nGu, C.\n(Member)\n19 Jul 2025\n→\n18 Jul