    "homepage_text": "Yuwei Hu's Homepage 胡雨韦\n胡雨韦\nYuwei Hu\nI am currently a 2nd-year Ph.D. student at\nGaoling School of Artificial Intelligence\n,\nRenmin University of China\n. I am honored to be advised by Prof.\nZhewei Wei\n.\nEmail\n/\nGithub\nResearch Interests\nMy past research experience is mainly in the fileds of graph neural networks, including graph transformer, graph lottery tickets.\nPublications\nIntruding with Words: Towards Understanding Graph Injection Attacks at the Text Level\nRunlin Lei, Yuwei Hu, Yuchen Ren, and Zhewei Wei.\nTo appear in NeurIPS 2024, arXiv preprint arXiv:2405.16405, 2024.\nWe are the first to unveil the dynamics of text-level graph adversarial attacks on TAGs, especially for GIAs.\nWe propose three effective text-level GIAs and demonstrate the trade-off between attack performance and text interpretability.\nWe reflect on the challenges of graph adversarial attacks at the text level.\nScalable and Accurate Graph Reasoning with LLM-based Multi-agents\nYuwei Hu, Runlin Lei, Xinyi Huang, Zhewei Wei, and Yongchao Liu.\narXiv preprint arXiv:2410.05130, 2024.\nWe propose the first LLM-based multi-agents fine-tuning-free framework for graph reasoning.\nWe expand the scale of graph reasoning tasks handled by LLMs from 100 nodes to 1,000 nodes.\nOur framework demonstrates the ability to tackle real-world applications like webpage importance analysis.\nSelected Honors and Awards\nNone\n, none, 2023"
  },
