    "homepage_text": "Zeyu Jia\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nPublications\nZeyu Jia\nZeyu Jia (è´¾æ³½å®)\nDepartment of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science\nMassachusetts Institute of Technology\nEmail: zyjia at mit dot edu\n[Google Scholar]\n[LinkedIn]\n[CV]\nI am on 2025-26 job market!\nI am currently seeking faculty positions, postdoctoral opportunities, and roles in industry. If you believe there's a potential fit, feel free to reach out.\nAbout Me\nI am a PhD candidate at\nDepartment of EECS\nat MIT. I am extremely fortunate to be advised by\nYury Polyanskiy\nand\nAlexander Rakhlin\n. I am also a member of\nLaboratory for Information and Decision System (LIDS)\nat MIT. Prior to that, I did my undergraduate at\nPeking University\n,\nSchool of Mathematical Science\n, advised by\nZaiwen Wen\n.\nMy research interests include machine learning theory especially reinforcement learning theory, optimization and information theory.\nNews\n(2025.09)    Two papers accepted by\nNeurIPS 2025\n(2025.05)    Our paper\nOn the Minimax Regret of Sequential Probability Assignment via Square-Root Entropy\nis accepted by\nCOLT 2025\n(2025.05)    Our paper\nDo We Need to Verify Step by Step? Rethinking Process Supervision from a Theoretical Perspective\nis accepted by\nICML 2025\n(2025.02)    Our paper\nRate of convergence of the smoothed empirical Wasserstein distance\nis accepted by\nAnnales de l'Institut Henri PoincarÃ©\n(2024.09)    Our paper\nHow Does Variance Shape the Regret in Contextual Bandits?\nis accepted by\nNeurIPS 2024\nPage generated 2025-10-25 11:19:22 EDT, by\njemdoc\n."
  },
