  "serper::Kezhen Chen": {
    "homepage": "https://www.kezhenchen.net/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Kezhen Chen | Kezhen Chen's Homepage\ntop of page\nKezhen Chen's Homepage\nResearch Scientist\n(Google) X, the moonshot factory\n​\n​\nI am currently the Staff Research Scientist at Together AI. Befor joining Together AI, I worked as a research scientist at the\n(Google) X, the moonshot factory\n. I am interested in LLM pretraining, finetuning, inference, multimodal understanding, AI for Science, Neuro-Symbolic Learning, Analogical Learning, Cognitive Modeling and Knowledge Representation & Reasoning. I earned my Computer Science Ph.D. at Northwestern University. When I was a Ph.D. student, I worked in the\nQualitative Reasoning Group\nadvised by Prof.\nKen Forbus\n. I received my bachelor's degree in Computer Science from the University of Rochester in 2016. I was a research assistant at UofR and worked with Prof. Jiebo Luo, Prof. Ehsan Hoque, and Prof. Henry Kautz.\n​\nMy CV can be downloaded\nhere\n.\nbottom of page"
  },
  "serper::Qiuyuan Huang": {
    "homepage": "https://huangqiukk.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "huangqiuyuan123@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/alshedivat",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Qiuyuan HUANG\nQiuyuan HUANG\nPostdoctoral researcher. University of Tokyo. huangqiuyuan123@gmail.com\n+81 03-5841-5266\nRoom 404, No.5 Building, 1-1-1 Yayoi\nBunkyo-ku,Tokyo 113-8657, Japan\nGreetings, my name is HUANG Qiuyuan and I am a postdoctoral researcher at the Department of Biomaterial Sciences, Graduate School of Agricultural and Life Sciences, The University of Tokyo. I am passionate about the development of sustainable materials and dedicated to contributing to the fields of eco-friendly polymers, eco-materials, biodegradable plastics, polymer structure and polymer synthesis.\nI received my Ph.D. from the Graduate School of Agricultural and Life Sciences, The University of Tokyo, where my research focused on biodegradable polymers. Since then, I have continued my research journey and my current work focuses on the development of innovative biodegradable polymers that are both environmentally friendly and sustainable.\nI am honoured to have the opportunity to work with a team of brilliant researchers at the University of Tokyo and to contribute to the development of sustainable materials that will shape the future of our planet.\nselected publications\nEnzymatic self-biodegradation of poly (l-lactic acid) films by embedded heat-treated and immobilized proteinase K\nQiuYuan Huang, Masatoshi Hiyama, Taizo Kabe, and\n2 more authors\nBiomacromolecules\n, 2020\nBib\n@article\n{\nhuang2020enzymatic\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Enzymatic self-biodegradation of poly (l-lactic acid) films by embedded heat-treated and immobilized proteinase K}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Huang, QiuYuan and Hiyama, Masatoshi and Kabe, Taizo and Kimura, Satoshi and Iwata, Tadahisa}\n,\njournal\n=\n{Biomacromolecules}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{21}\n,\nnumber\n=\n{8}\n,\npages\n=\n{3301--3307}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2020}\n,\npublisher\n=\n{American Chemical Society}\n,\n}\nDevelopment of self-degradable aliphatic polyesters by embedding lipases via melt extrusion\nQiuYuan Huang, Satoshi Kimura, and Tadahisa Iwata\nPolymer Degradation and Stability\n, 2021\nBib\n@article\n{\nhuang2021development\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Development of self-degradable aliphatic polyesters by embedding lipases via melt extrusion}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Huang, QiuYuan and Kimura, Satoshi and Iwata, Tadahisa}\n,\njournal\n=\n{Polymer Degradation and Stability}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{190}\n,\npages\n=\n{109647}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2021}\n,\npublisher\n=\n{Elsevier}\n}\nPlease contact me trough Email."
  },
