  "serper::Yang Lin": {
    "homepage": "https://yangjlin.com/",
    "emails": [
      "yang.lin@epfl.ch"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/Yang-J-LIN",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yanglinphd2025/",
    "homepage_text": "Yang's Homepage | Yang Lin's Homepage\n☕️\nYang Lin\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nEPFL\nAbout Me\nI am currently a postdoctoral researcher at\nAQUA Lab\n, EPFL. I am working on marrying single-photon avalanche diodes (SPADs) with artificial and spiking neural networks for biological and medical imaging.\nInterests\nMachine Learning\nIntelligent Image Sensors\nComputer Vision\nBiomedical Imaging (e.g. FLIM)\nMicroscopy/Macroscopy\nSingle-photon avalanche diode\nEducation\nPh.D. in Computational and Quantitative Biology (2025)\nÉcole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne\nB.Eng. in Automation (2020)\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\n📚 My Research\nI’m a postdoctoral researcher in the AQUA lab at EPFL. I am working on integrating neural networks near and within the SPAD sensors, especially recurrent neural networks and spiking neural networks.\nI design the ASIC SPAD image sensors, FPGA-based neural processing units, software for control and visualization, and optical setup for biomedical imaging applications, esp. fluorescence lifetime imaging.\nI am currently open to work opportunities as a researcher or engineer in Switzerland, with a starting date around Oct, 2026.\n😃\nProjects\nImage Sensor\nTransporter\nTransporter, designed for active time-resolved imaging, is world’s first SPAD image sensor with an on-chip encoder for SNN processing.\nJun 2, 2025\nFLIM\nReal-time FLIM\nWe built a histogram-free, real-time fluorescence lifetime imaging (FLIM) system with an in-house micrscope, SPAD image sensor, and FPGA with RNN.\nOct 26, 2023\nBioinformatics\nLncLocator 2\nLncLocator 2 is a subcellular localization predictor for long non-coding RNA, with integrated gradients for explanation.\nJun 30, 2020\nRecent Publications\nYang Lin\n(2025).\nSPAD Image Sensors with Embedded Intelligence\n.\nEPFL Thesis.\nCite\nDOI\nURL\nAudrey Eshun\n,\nDominique Davenport\n,\nBrandon Demory\n,\nShervin Kiannejad\n,\nPaul Mos\n,\nYang Lin\n,\nTiziana Bond\n,\nMichael C Rushford\n,\nErin E Nuccio\n,\nTy J Samo\n,\nOthers\n(2025).\n3D quantum ghost imaging microscope\n.\nOptica\n.\nCite\nDOI\nYang Lin\n,\nClaudio Bruschini\n,\nEdoardo Charbon\n(2025).\nTransporter: A 128$\\times$4 SPAD Imager with On-chip Encoder for Spiking Neural Network-based Processing\n.\nInternational Image Sensor Workshop (IISW)\n.\nPDF\nCite\nDOI\nDuncan P Ryan\n,\nPaul Moş\n,\nYang Lin\n,\nClaudio Bruschini\n,\nEdoardo Charbon\n,\nJames H Werner\n(2025).\nTime-resolved detectors for quantum ghost imaging\n.\nThe European Physical Journal Plus\n.\nCite\nDOI\nDominique Davenport\n,\nAudrey Eshun\n,\nBrandon Demory\n,\nShervin Kiannejad\n,\nPaul Mos\n,\nYang Lin\n,\nEdoardo Charbon\n,\nTiziana Bond\n,\nMike Rushford\n,\nClaudio Bruschini\n,\nOthers\n(2025).\n3D quantum ghost imaging microscope\n.\nQuantum Sensing, Imaging, and Precision Metrology III\n.\nCite\nSee all publications\nRecent & Upcoming Talks\nThesis Defense\nSPAD Image Sensors with Embedded Intelligence\nThesis Directors: Prof. E. Charbon, Dr C. Bruschini\nComputational and Quantitative Biology doctoral program\nThesis Nr. 11448\nTo take part in the public defense, please contact directly the speaker\nNov 11, 2025\nPoster\nTransporter: A 128×4 SPAD Imager with On-chip Encoder for Spiking Neural Network-based Processing\nI will present in the flash presentation and poster session. Feel free to discuss with me during the poster session!\nJun 2, 2025\nPoster\nSpiking Neural Networks for Active Time-Resolved SPAD Imaging\nJan 6, 2024\nPresentation\nReal-time Recurrent Neural Network-based Fluorescence Lifetime Imaging with SPAD Sensors\nApr 4, 2023\nPresentation\nReal-time neural network-based fluorescence lifetime imaging with SPAD sensors\nI am honored to receive the Award for the Best Talk of a Young Researcher at BMPN 2022.\nDec 6, 2022\nContact\nyang.lin@epfl.ch\n+41 21 693 47 82\nEPFL STI IMT AQUA\nRue de la Maladière 71b\nNeuchâtel 2000\nSwitzerland\npremium bootstrap themes"
  },
