  "serper::Yuting Wei": {
    "homepage": "https://yutingwei.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "ytwei@wharton.upenn"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yuting-wei-32830a7b",
    "homepage_text": "Home\nBio\nResearch\nResearch by topic\nTeaching\nTalks\nGroup\nYuting Wei\nAssociate Professor\nWharton Statistics Department\nytwei (at) wharton (dot) upenn (dot) edu\nStatistics & Data Science,\n307 Academic Research Building,\nUniversity of Pennsylvania,\nPhiladelphia, PA 19104\nAbout Me\nDr. Yuting Wei is an Associate Professor in the\nDepartment of Statistics and Data Science\nat the Wharton School,\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\n.\nPrior to that, Dr. Wei spent two years at\nCarnegie Mellon University\nas an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Statistics and Data Science\n, and one year as a Stein's Fellow at\nStanford Statistics Department\n.\nShe received her Ph.D. in Statistics at\nBerkeley Statistics Department\nadvised by two amazing supervisors\nMartin Wainwright\nand\nAditya Guntuboyina\n; She was also associated with the Berkeley Artificial Intelligence Research group (\nBAIR\n).\nDr. Wei's research interests lie broadly in the span of statistics, mathematical optimization, information theory and machine learning.  \nMore specifically, she has been developing theoretical and algorithmic tools for learning from high dimensional and structured data, and understanding the sample efficiency in reinforcement learning and diffusion models.  \nShe is also interested in statistical problems arising from genetics and genomics.\nCV\nOpenings\nDr. Wei is currently looking for\nstudents and postdocs\ninterested in high dimensional statistics and machine learning. Please email a CV to apply.\nNews\nI am deeply honored to recieve the\nPeter Gavin Hall IMS Early Career Prize\nfrom\nIMS\n.\nI presented a tutorial on “Mathematical Foundations of Reinforcement Learning” in\nAustralian Information Theory School\n.\nI am truly grateful to receive the\n2025 Gottfried E. Noether Early Career Scholar Award\nfrom\nASA\n.\nEducation\nStanford University, Stein's Fellow / Lecturer, 2018 - 2019\nUniversity of California, Berkeley: Ph.D. in Statistics, 2013 - 2018\nPeking University: Bachelor of Science (B.S.) Statistics, 2009 - 2013\nPeking University: Bachelor of Arts (B.A.) Economics, 2010 - 2013\nContact\nGoogle Scholar Profile\nLinkedIn Profile\nPage generated 2026-03-20 22:54:28 EDT, by\njemdoc\n."
  },
  "serper::Qi Feng": {
