sium on Foundations of Computer Science\n(\nFOCS\n), 2020 [\nvideo\n]\nMultinomial Logit Bandit with Low Switching Cost\nKefan Dong, Yingkai Li, Qin Zhang, Yuan Zhou\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning\n(\nICML\n), 2020\nFair Resource Sharing and Dorm Assignments\nBo Li, Yingkai Li\nInternational Conference on Autonomous Agents and Multiagent Systems\n(\nAAMAS\n), 2020\nApproximately Maximizing the Broker’s Profit in a Two-sided Market\nJing Chen, Bo Li, Yingkai Li\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(\nIJCAI\n), 2019\nOptimal Auctions vs. Anonymous Pricing: Beyond Linear Utility\nYiding Feng, Jason Hartline, Yingkai Li\nACM Conference on Economics and Computation\n(\nEC\n), 2019 [\nvideo\n]\nNearly Minimax-Optimal Regret for Linearly Parameterized Bandits\nYingkai Li, Yining Wang, Yuan Zhou\nConference on Learning Theory\n(\nCOLT\n), 2019\nRevenue Maximization with Imprecise Distribution\nYingkai Li, Pinyan Lu, Haoran Ye\nInternational Conference on Autonomous Agents and Multiagent Systems\n(\nAAMAS\n), 2019\nInformation Elicitation for Bayesian Auctions\nJing Chen, Bo Li, Yingkai Li\nInternational Symposium on Algorithmic Game Theory\n(\nSAGT\n), 2018\nDynamic Fair Division Problem with General Valuations\nBo Li, Wenyang Li, Yingkai Li\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(\nIJCAI\n), 2018\nBayesian Auctions with Efficient Queries\nJing Chen, Bo Li, Yingkai Li, Pinyan Lu\nInternational Colloquium on Automata, Languages and Programming\n(\nICALP\n), 2018\nEfficient Approximations for the Online Dispersion Problem\nJing Chen, Bo Li, Yingkai Li\nInternational Colloquium on Automata, Languages and Programming\n(\nICALP\n), 2017"
