    "homepage_text": "Yihong Wu\nInfo\nHome\nCV\nResearch\nPublications\nSoftware\nBooks and lecture notes\nTeaching\nECE563\nECE598YW\nSTAT364\nS&DS241\nS&DS684\nS&DS677\nYihong Wu\nJames A. Attwood Professor of Statistics and Data Science\nChair,\nDepartment of Statistics and Data Science\n(Administrative assistant:\nCheri Cercone\n)\nYale University\n📧     yihong.wu@yale.edu\n✉\nKline Tower\n, Room 1017\n219 Prospect St\nNew Haven, CT 06511\nResearch interests\nI am broadly interested in the theoretical and algorithmic aspects of high-dimensional statistics, information theory, and optimization.\nRecent papers\nYanjun Han, Jonathan Niles-Weed, Yandi Shen, and Yihong Wu, \"\nBesting Good–Turing: Optimality of Non-Parametric Maximum Likelihood for Distribution Estimation\n\", Sep 2025.\nSimiao Jiao, Yihong Wu, and Jiaming Xu, \"\nThe broken sample problem revisited: Proof of a conjecture by Bai-Hsing and high-dimensional extensions\n\", Mar 2025.\nZhou Fan, Leying Guan, Yandi Shen, and Yihong Wu, \"\nGradient flows for empirical Bayes in high-dimensional linear models\n\", Dec 2023.\nYutong Nie and Yihong Wu, \"\nLarge-scale multiple testing: Fundamental limits of false discovery rate control and compound oracle?\n\", The Annals of Statistics, 2026.\nYandi Shen and Yihong Wu, \"\nPoisson Empirical Bayes estimation: When does\n-modeling beat\n-modeling in theory (and in practice)?\n\", The Annals of Statistics, 2026.\nPage generated 2026-01-21 11:26:51 Eastern Standard Time, by\njemdoc\n."
  },
