  "serper::Yu-Shen Liu": {
    "homepage": "https://yushen-liu.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "liuyushen00@gmail.com",
      "liuyushen@tsinghua.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/weiqi-zhang",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yu-Shen Liu - Tsinghua University\nBio\nParticipated Projects\nTeaching\nAwards\nAcademic Activities\nPublications\nAI Conference Deadlines\n中文版本\nYu-Shen Liu （刘玉身）\nAssociate Professor\nSchool of Software, Tsinghua University,\nBeijing, P. R. China\nContacts:\nE-mail:\nliuyushen@tsinghua.edu.cn\nE-mail:\nliuyushen00@gmail.com\nTel:\n+86-10-62795455\nHomePages:\nTsinghua homepage\n,\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nDBLP\n,\nCSRanking\nDr. Yu-Shen Liu is an Associate Professor in School of Software at Tsinghua University, China. He spent three years as a post-doctoral researcher in Purdue University from 2006 to 2009. He earned his PhD in the Department of Computer Science and Technology at Tsinghua University, China, in 2006. He received his BS in mathematics from Jilin University, China, in 2000. His current research interests include 3D computer vision, 3D reconstruction and generation, 3D foundation models, AI for industry, and building information modeling (BIM). He has served as Area Chair, senior PC and PC members for some top conferences, such as IJCAI, AAAI, ACM Multimedia, ICLR. He has published 60+ papers in top journals and conferences like TPAMI/TIP/CVPR/ICCV/ECCV/NeurIPS/ICML/AAAI/IJCAI/ACM MM, with a total of more than 5,600 citations on Google Scholar. He has undertaken 5 National Natural Science Foundation projects as PI, and 2 National Key R&D Program projects, and participated in the compilation of three national standards (ranked 3rd). His group has received the 2022 Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award of the Chinese Society of Graphics (CSG), the 2021 \"Outstanding Graphics Open Source Dataset\" Award of the Computer-Aided Design and Graphics Professional Committee of the Chinese Computer Society (CCF CAD&CG), the Highly Cited Research Award by Advanced Engineering Informatics (the Elsevier journal), the Best Student Presentation Award of ICCCBE 2016, and the Best Student Paper Award of CAD/Graphics 2005. One TPAMI paper was selected as an ESI highly cited paper, and he was listed in 2024 World's Top 2% Scientists released by Stanford University and Elsevier. His teaching achievements have won the Tsinghua University Excellent Courses, Tsinghua University Annual Teaching Excellence Award, Tsinghua University Outstanding Class Teacher First Prize (2 times), etc., and the graduate students guided by him have won the Beijing Outstanding Graduates, Tsinghua University Outstanding Graduates, and Tsinghua University Outstanding Dissertations for several times.\nEducation\n2000-2006:\nTsinghua University\n, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPh.D. in Computer Science and Technology.\n1996-2000:\nJilin University\n, B.Sc. in Mathematics\nExperience\n2009- present:\nSchool of Software at\nTsinghua University\n, Beijing, China.\n2006-2009:\nPurdue University\n, West Lafayette, IN, USA. Postdoctoral researcher in School of Mechanical Engineering\nResearch Interests\n3D Computer Vision, 3D Deep Learning\n3D Representation and Recognition, 3D Geometry Processing and Semantic Understanding, 3D Reconstruction\nBuilding Information Modeling (BIM)\nCurrently, I am looking for\nPhD students\nand\nResearch Assistants\nto work on the top publications. Please feel free to contact me.\nResearch Funds\n1.\nNSF of China: Learning Deep Implicit Functions of 3D Point Clouds for Reconstruction (62272263), 2023.01-2026.12, PI.\n2.\nNSF of China: Research on Semantic-Instance Segmentation and Shape Completion for 3D Point Clouds based on Feature Representation Learning (62072268), 2021.01-2024.12, PI.\n3.\nNational Key R&D Program of China (2022YFC3800601), 2022.11-2025.12, PI.\n4.\nDeep Earth Probe and Mineral Resources Exploration-National Science and Technology Major Project (2024ZD1003405), 2024.11-2028.10, PI of sub-project.\n5.\nNational Key R&D Program of China (2020YFF0304100), 2020.10-2022.12, PI of sub-project.\n6.\nNational Key R&D Program of China (2018YFB0505403), 2018.05-2022.04, PI.\n7.\nNSF of China: Studies on semantic retrieval for building information modeling (BIM) resources based on IFC (61472202), 2015.01-2018.12, PI.\n8.\nNSF of China: Studies on shape matching for 3D articulated models based on metric geometry (61272229), 2013.01-2016.12, PI.\n9.\nNSF of China: Study of non-rigid 3D shape retrieval (61003095), 2011.01-2013.12, PI.\n10.\nNational Technological Support Program for the 12th-Five-Year Plan of China (2012BAJ03B07), 2012.01-2015.09, main researcher.\n11.\nNSF of China: China building information technology strategic research (U0970155), finished, main researcher.\nTeaching\nInstructor: \"Fundamental of Programming\", the undergraduate course, 2017-present\nTsinghua University Excellent Course Award\n(2021-2024), 2021 - (Top 25%)\nInstructor: “Digital Geometry Processing”, the graduate course, 2016 - present\nTsinghua University Annual Teaching Excellence Award\n2018 - (Top 5%)\nInstructor: “Software Engineering (1)”, the undergraduate course, 2013 - 2016\nCo-Instructor: “Business Process and Asset Management”, the graduate course, 2015 - present\nCo-Instructor: “Digital Media (2)”, the graduate course, 2019\nTsinghua University Excellent Class Advisor\n(First Prize), 2017\nAwards\nBest Open Graphics Benchmark Award\nin the field of the CAD/Graphics area in 2021, which is selected by Technical Committee on Computer Aided Design and Computer Graphics (TCCADCG) affiliated with the China Computer Federation (CCF).\nIn 2021, he led his team to win the ranked 3rd place in MVP Point Cloud Completion Challenge 2021 at ICCV 2021 - The 3rd Workshop on Sensing, Understanding and Synthesizing Humans.\nHighly Cited Research Award\nThe paper, “The IFC-based path planning for 3D indoor spaces”, published in Advanced Engineering Informatics (the Elsevier journal) is awarded Highly Cited Research on December, 2016. This paper was published in 2013, which is one of the most highly cited papers during 2014, 2015 and up until June 2016 according to data from Scopus. Dr. Yu-Shen Liu is the corresponding author of this paper.\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\n[Bib]\nBest Student Presentation Award\n, at the 16th International Conference on Computing in Civil and Building Engineering (ICCCBE2016), held on July 6-8, at 2016, Osaka, Japan. Dr. Yu-Shen Liu is the corresponding author of this paper, and Mr. Ge Gao is the first author.\n[Paper]\nBest Student Paper Award\n, at the Proceedings of the Ninth International Conference on Computer Aided Design and Computer Graphics (CAD-CG'05), 306–312, September, 2005, Hong Kong, China.\nAcademic Service\nAssociate Editor (AE)\nIEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics (TVCG) 2025\nArea Chair (AC)\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2026\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) 2026\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI) 2025\nSenior Program Committee (SPC)\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI) 2021, 2023, 2024, 2025\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI) 2022, 2026\nOthers\nOutstanding Program Committee Award (AAAI 2026)\nOutstanding reviewer for Automation in Construction (2018)\nOutstanding reviewer for Journal of Computational and Applied Mathematics (2018)\nSelected Publications\n(*: corresponding author, #: co-first author)\n2026\nJunsheng Zhou#, Weiqi Zhang#, Baorui Ma, Kanle Shi,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n, Zhizhong Han. UDFStudio: A Unified Framework of Datasets, Benchmarks and Generative Models for Unsigned Distance Functions.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n)\n, 2026, PrePrints pp. 1-18. Early Access. DOI: 10.1109/TPAMI.2026.3668763.\n[Project Page]\n[Github]\nWenyuan Zhang, Chunsheng Wang, Kanle Shi,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n, Zhizhong Han. VRP-UDF: Towards Unbiased Learning of Unsigned Distance Functions from Multi-view Images with Volume Rendering Priors.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n)\n, 2026, PrePrints pp. 1-18. Early Access. DOI: 10.1109/TPAMI.2026.3653901.\n[Project Page]\n[ArXiv]\nQing Li, Huifang Feng*, Kanle Shi, Yue Gao, Yi Fang,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n, Zhizhong Han. PFF-Net: Patch Feature Fitting for Point Cloud Normal Estimation.\nIEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics (\nTVCG\n)\n, 2026, 32(2): 1713-1728.\n[Project Page]\n[ArXiv]\n[PDF]\nJunsheng Zhou#, Zhifan Yang#, Liang Han, Wenyuan Zhang, Kanle Shi, Shenkun Xu,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n. 4C4D: 4 Camera 4D Gaussian Splatting.\nProceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n)\n, 2026.\nWeiqi Zhang#, Junsheng Zhou#, Haotian Geng, Kanle Shi, Shenkun Xu, Yi Fang,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n. GaussianGrow: Geometry-aware Gaussian Growing from 3D Point Clouds with Text Guidance.\nProceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n)\n, 2026.\nTakeshi Noda,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n, Zhizhong Han. 3D Gaussian Splatting with Self-Constrained Priors for High Fidelity Surface Reconstruction.\nProceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n)\n, 2026.\nJuntong Fang#, Zequn Chen#, Weiqi Zhang#, Donglin Di, Xuancheng Zhang, Chengmin Yang,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n. MoRe: Motion-aware Feed-forward 4D Reconstruction Transformer.\nProceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n)\n, 2026.\n[ArXiv]\n[Github]\nPeng Xiang, Liang Han, Hui Zhang*,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n, Zhizhong Han. VGGS: VGGT-guided Gaussian Splatting for Efficient and Faithful Sparse-View Surface Reconstruction.\nThe 40th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n)\n, 2026.\nShengtao Li, Yudong Liu, Ge Gao*, Ming Gu,\nYu-Shen Liu\n. I-Filtering: Implicit Filtering for Learning Neural Distance Functions from 3D Point Clouds.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n)\n, 2026, 48(1): 109-126.\n[Project Page]\n[PDF]\n[Github]\n2025\nWenyuan Zhang#, Jimin Tang#, Weiqi Zhang, Yi Fang,\nYu-Shen Liu*\n, Zhizhong Han. MaterialRefGS: Reflective Gaussian Splatting with Multi-view Consistent Material Inference.\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2025.\n[Project Page]\n[ArXiv]\n[PDF]\nJunsheng Zhou#, Xingyu Shi#, Haichuan...[truncated]"
  },
  "serper::Han Li": {
