    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nDr. Han Li\nhan_li@alumni.brown.edu\nI am currently a Senior Test Developer at the Law School Admission Council.  I have also taught at Lincoln University, Rutgers-New Brunswick, Rutgers-Camden, Rowan University, and was Visiting Assistant Professor at Kansas State University.  I have served as the primary instructor for classes in epistemology, ethics, logic, decision theory, the philosophy of probability, political philosophy, and introduction to philosophy.\nMy research is\nmainly in epistemology, but also have research interests in ethics, philosophy of science (especially philosophy of probability) and decision theory.  I received my PhD from Brown University with a dissertation supervised by David Christensen.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
