    "homepage_text": "Di Huang - The Su Lab - Bioinformatics and Genomics\nSkip to main content\nVisit the University of North Carolina at Charlotte homepage\nExplore\nVisit the University of North Carolina at Charlotte homepage\nClose\nWhat can we help you find?\nSubmit search query to search.charlotte.edu\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nCampus Life\nResearch\nAthletics\nAbout\nApply\nVisit\nGive\nNews & Events\nDirectory\nMy UNC Charlotte\nQuick Links\nMajors & Minors\nGraduate Programs\nCalendar\nCampus Maps\nClass Registration\nFinancial Aid\nHousing\nLibrary\nReport an Incident\nResources\nProspective Students\nAlumni & Friends\nFaculty & Staff\nCurrent Students\nParents & Family\nColleges\nArts + Architecture\nBusiness\nComputing and Informatics\nEducation\nEngineering\nGraduate School\nHealth and Human Services\nHonors College\nHumanities & Earth and Social Sciences\nScience\nCollege of Computing and Informatics\nThe Su Lab - Bioinformatics and Genomics\nGo to Search Page\nSearch this site\nSearch\nDi Huang\nDi Huang\nAlumni\n713-441-5664\nDHuang@tmhs.org\nResearch Interests:\nStatistical modeling and informatics tools for identifying the important biomarkers and copy number estimation for SNP array.\nDi Huang received her Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering from City University of Hong Kong. She is currently a postdoc research fellow in Bioinformatics, The Methodist Hospital Research Institute. Her research interests include statistical modeling and informatics tools to identify the important biomarkers for complex disease, such as metabolic diseases and cancers, and infer pathways further for understanding them.\nFaculty Page\nZhengChang Su\n, PhD, Professor\nBioinformatics Research Center\nDepartment of Bioinformatics and Genomics\nBioinformatics 351\n704‑687‑7996\nBioinformatics and Genomics\nBioinformatics Research Center\nGlobal Ensemble Clusters of Binding Sites\nTFBS PFM Database Search\nMotifClick"
