    "homepage_text": "Boyuan Pan\nAbout\nPublications\nExperiences\nCV\nAbout\nPublications\nExperiences\nState Key Lab of CAD&CG\n,\nZhejiang University\nContact\n: panby AT zju.edu.cn\nCurriculum Vitae\nGoogle Scholar\nGithub\nBoyuan Pan (潘博远)\nI received my Ph.D. degree from\nZhejiang University\nin China. My advisors are Prof.\nXiaofei He\nand Prof.\nDeng Cai\n. During my Ph.D. career, I was a visiting scholar at UIUC (working with Prof.\nBo Li\n) and OSU (working with Prof.\nHuan Sun\n).\nMy research interests fall in the general areas and applications of machine learning and natural language processing (NLP), especially the recent developments in transfer learning, reinforcement learning and adversarial learning to work towards the goal of the combination of language understanding and generation.\nNews\nMay 2021\n• Our paper \"TopNet: Learning from Neural Topic Model to Generate Long Stories\" got accepted in\nKDD 2021\n.\nJan 2021\n• Our paper \"Self-Supervised Attention Flow for Dialogue State Tracking\" got accepted in\nNeurocomputing\n.\nSeptember 2020\n• Our paper \"T3: Tree-Autoencoder Regularized Adversarial Text Generation for Targeted Attack\" got accepted in\nEMNLP 2020\n.\nMore News\nJune 2020\n• Our paper \"Adversarial Mutual Information for Text Generation\" got accepted in\nICML 2020\n, Vienna, Austria.\nJan 2020\n• Our paper \"Bi-Decoder Augmented Network for Neural Machine Translation\" got accepted in\nNeurocomputing\n.\nOctober 2019\n• I am excited to visit the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign and work with Prof.\nBo Li\n!\nJune 2019\n• I'm excited to join the\nAlibaba DAMO Academy\nas a research intern!\nMay 2019\n• Our paper \"Reinforced Dynamic Reasoning for Conversational Question Generation\" got accepted in\nACL 2019\n, Florence, Italy.\nNovember 2018\n• I am excited to visit the Ohio State University and work with Prof.\nHuan Sun\n!\n• Our work in NeurIPS 2018 was invited to have a talk on the\n16th China Symposium on Machine Learning Applications (MLA 2018)\n, Nanjing, China.\nSeptember 2018\n• Our paper \"MacNet: Transferring Knowledge from Machine Comprehension to Sequence-to-Sequence Models\" got accepted in\nNeurIPS 2018\n, Montreal, Canada.\nMay 2018\n• Our work in ACL 2018 was invited to present on\nThe Third SFU-ZJU Joint Symposium on Big Data and Visual Computing\n, Hangzhou, China.\nApril 2018\n• Our paper \"Discourse Marker Augmented Network with Reinforcement Learning for Natural Language Inference\" got accepted in\nACL 2018\n(oral)\n, Melbourne, Australia.\nMay 2017\n• Our Model \"MEMEN\" achieved the second place on the SQuAD leaderboard!\nApril 2017\n• Our paper \"Robust Asymmetric Bayesian Adaptive Matrix Factorization\" got accepted in\nIJCAI 2017\n, Melbourne, Australia.\nPublications\n2021\nTopNet: Learning from Neural Topic Model to Generate Long Stories\nYazheng Yang*,\nBoyuan Pan\n*, Deng Cai, Huan Sun\nThe 2021 ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining\n(KDD 2021) (Research Track)\n[paper]\n[code]\nSelf-Supervised Attention Flow for Dialogue State Tracking\nBoyuan Pan\n*, Yazheng Yang*, Bo Li, Deng Cai\nNeurocomputing\n[paper]\n2020\nT3: Tree-Autoencoder Regularized Adversarial Text Generation for Targeted Attack\nBoxin Wang, Hengzhi Pei,\nBoyuan Pan\n, Qian Chen, Shuohang Wang, Bo Li\nThe 2020 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing\n(EMNLP 2020)\n[paper]\n[code]\nAdversarial Mutual Information for Text Generation\nBoyuan Pan\n*, Yazheng Yang*, Kaizhao Liang, Bhavya Kailkhura, Zhongming Jin, Xian-sheng Hua, Deng Cai, Bo Li\nThirty-seventh International Conference on Machine Learning\n(ICML 2020)\n[paper]\n[code]\nTowards Evaluating the Robustness of Chinese BERT Classifiers\nBoxin Wang,\nBoyuan Pan\n, Xin Li, Bo Li\narXiv preprint arXiv:2004.03742\n[paper]\nBi-Decoder Augmented Network for Neural Machine Translation\nBoyuan Pan\n, Yazheng Yang, Zhou Zhao, Yueting zhuang, Deng Cai\nNeurocomputing\n[paper]\n2019\nDiscriminate and Reconstruct: Learning from Language Model to Answer Keyword Questions\nBoyuan Pan\n, Yazheng Yang, Yueting Zhuang, Deng Cai\nThe second China Symposium on Cognitive Computing and Hybrid Intelligence\n(CCHI 2019) (oral)\n[paper]\nReinforced Dynamic Reasoning for Conversational Question Generation\nBoyuan Pan\n, Hao Li, Ziyu Yao, Deng Cai, Huan Sun\nProceedings of the 57th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics\n(ACL 2019)\n[paper]\n[code]\n2018\nMacNet: Transferring Knowledge from Machine Comprehension to Sequence-to-Sequence Models\nBoyuan Pan\n, Yazheng Yang, Hao Li, Zhou Zhao, Yueting Zhuang, Deng Cai, Xiaofei He\nThirty-second Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS 2018)\n[paper]\n[poster]\nDiscourse Marker Augmented Network with Reinforcement Learning for Natural Language Inference\nBoyuan Pan\n, Yazheng Yang, Zhou Zhao, Yueting Zhuang, Deng Cai, Xiaofei He\nProceedings of the 56th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics\n(ACL 2018) (oral)\n[paper]\n[code]\n[slides]\n2017\nKeyword-based Query Comprehending via Multiple Optimized-Demand Augmentation\nBoyuan Pan\n, Hao Li, Zhou Zhao, Deng Cai, Xiaofei He\narXiv preprint arXiv:1711.00179\n[paper]\nMEMEN: Multi-layer Embedding with Memory Networks for Machine Comprehension\nBoyuan Pan\n, Hao Li, Zhou Zhao, Bin Cao, Deng Cai, Xiaofei He\narXiv preprint arXiv:1707.09098\n[paper]\nRobust Asymmetric Bayesian Adaptive Matrix Factorization\nXin Guo,\nBoyuan Pan\n, Deng Cai, Xiaofei He\nProceedings of the 26th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(IJCAI 2017)\n[paper]\nEducation\n2016/09 - 2021/06\n• Ph.D. in Computer Science and Technology, Zhejiang University.\n2012/09 - 2016/06\n• B.S. in Mathematical Science, Zhejiang University.\n2014/08 - 2014/09\n• Summer School, University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA).\nExperiences\n2020/12 - 2021/06\n• Research Intern at\nAlibaba Group\n, Hangzhou, China.\n2019/09 - 2020/08\n• Visiting Scholar at\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (UIUC)\n, Urbana, USA.\n2019/06 - 2019/09\n• Research Intern at\nAlibaba DAMO Academy\n, Hangzhou, China.\n2018/11 - 2019/05\n• Visiting Scholar at\nOhio State University (OSU)\n, Columbus, USA.\n2016/11 - 2017/09\n• Research Intern at\nEigen Technologies\n, Hangzhou, China.\nProfessional Services\nProgram Committee Member:\nAAAI (2018), NeurIPS (2019), ACL (2018, 2019, 2020), EMNLP (2020), NAACL (2021).\nJournal Reviewer:\nIEEE TNNLS."
  },
  "serper::Handong Zhao": {
    "homepage": "https://hdzhao.github.io/",
    "emails": [
