    "homepage_text": "Wenxian Shi\nWenxian Shi (施文娴)\nI am a researcher at ByteDance AI-Lab\nMLNLC group\n, adivsed by Dr.\nHao Zhou\nand Dr.\nLei Li\n. Before that, I received my master's degree\nfrom\nPeking University (PKU)\n, advised by Prof. Junfeng Hu.\nEmail: wxsh1213 [at] gmail.com / shiwenxian [at] bytedance.com\nGithub\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nCV\nResearch Topics\nMy research interests lie in the general area of machine learning, particularly in\nrepresentation learning\nand\ngenerative modeling\n. Currently, I focus on applications on discrete and structured data settings such as\nnatural language processing\n(\ne.g.\n, text generation and representation) and\ncomputational biology\n(\ne.g.\n, molecular generation for drug discovery).\nPublication\n(* equal contribution)\nFollow Your Path: a Progressive Method for Knowledge Distillation\nWenxian Shi*\n, \n                                        Yuxuan Song*, \n                                        Hao Zhou, \n                                        Bohan Li, \n                                        Lei Li\nthe European Conference on Machine Learning and Principles and Practice of Knowledge Discovery in Databases (ECML-PKDD)\n, 2021\nDispersed Exponential Family Mixture VAEs for Interpretable Text Generation\nWenxian Shi\n, \n                                        Hao Zhou, \n                                        Ning Miao, \n                                        Lei Li\nProceedings of the 37th International Conference on Machine learning (ICML)\n, 2020\nVariational Template Machine for Data-to-Text Generation\nRong Ye,\nWenxian Shi\n, \n                                        Hao Zhou, \n                                        Zhongyu Wei, \n                                        Lei Li\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n, 2020\nKernelized Bayesian Softmax for Text Generation\nNing Miao, \n                                        Hao Zhou, \n                                        Chengqi Zhao,\nWenxian Shi\n, \n                                        Lei Li\nthe 33rd Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n, 2019\nEducation\nSep. 2016 - July 2019: Peking University\nM.S. in Computer Science\nAdvisors: Junfeng Hu.\nSep. 2012 - July 2016: Peking University\nB.S. in Physics (Yuanpei Program)\nUpdated at Nov. 2020\nThanks\nJon Barron\nfor this amazing work"
  },
  "serper::Lei Li": {
