    "homepage_text": "Neil Xu\nNeil Xu\nHi - I’m Neil. I’m a PhD student in\nStatistics and Data Science\nat CMU.\nI’m fortunate enough to be advised by\nAaditya Ramdas\n. I also collaborate with\nRuodu Wang\n.\nI’ve recently been working on\nmultiple hypothesis testing\nand\npost-selection inference\n, and I’m interested in the intersection of statistical and game theory.\nI am grateful to\nJustin Khim\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\n, and\nDavid P. Woodruff\nfor showing me the ropes of how to do theory research.\nIn my undergrad, I had a stint of working on natural language processing applications, and had the fortune of working with\nZhou Yu\non dialog agents and\nGraham Neubig\non machine translation.\nEmail: ecks zee why at cmu dot edu\n*I publish under my legal name, which is abbreviated ZX.\nPreprints\nBringing Closure to False Discovery Rate Control: A General Principle for Multiple Testing\nZX\n,\nAldo Solari\n,\nLasse Fischer\n,\nRianne de Heide\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\n,\nJelle Goeman\n2025\n[arXiv 2509.02517]\n[talk]\n[slides]\nActive multiple testing with proxy p-values and e-values\nZX\n,\nCatherine Wang\n,\nLarry Wasserman\n,\nKathryn Roeder\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\n2025\n[arXiv 2502.05715]\n[slides]\nAn online generalization of the (e-)Benjamini-Hochberg procedure\nLasse Fischer\n,\nZX\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\n2024\n[arXiv 2407.20683]\nMore powerful multiple testing under dependence via randomization\nZX\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\n2023\n[arXiv 2305.11126]\n[code]\nPublications\nActive, anytime-valid risk controlling prediction sets\nZX\n,\nNikos Karampatziakis\n,\nPaul Mineiro\nNeurIPS 2024\n[arXiv 2406.10490]\n[code]\nPost-selection inference for e-value based confidence intervals\nZX\n,\nRuodu Wang\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\nElectronic Journal of Statistics 2024\n[arXiv 2203.12572]\n[journal]\n[poster]\n[talk]\n[slides]\nRunner-up Poster Prize @ MCP 2022\nFoundations of Testing for Finite-Sample Causal Discovery\nTom Yan\n,\nZX\n,\nZachary C. Lipton\nICML 2024\n[proceedings]\nOnline multiple testing with e-values\nZX\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\nAISTATS 2024\n[arXiv 2311.06412]\n[proceedings]\n[poster]\n[slides]\n[code]\nRisk-limiting Financial Audits via Weighted Sampling without Replacement\nShubhanshu Shekhar\n,\nZX\n,\nZachary C. Lipton\n,\nPierre J. Liang\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\nUAI 2023\n[arXiv 2305.06884]\n[proceedings]\n[code]\nMemory Bounds for the Experts Problem\nVaidehi Srinivas\n,\nDavid P. Woodruff\n,\nZX\n,\nSamson Zhou\nSTOC 2022\n[arXiv 2204.09837]\n[proceedings]\n[Samson's talk]\nA unified framework for bandit multiple testing\nZX\n,\nRuodu Wang\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\nNeurIPS 2021\n[arXiv 2107.07322]\n[proceedings]\n[poster]\n[talk]\n[slides]\n[code]\nDynamic Algorithms for Online Multiple Testing\nZX\n,\nAaditya Ramdas\nMath. and Sci. ML 2021\n[arXiv 2010.13953]\n[proceedings]\n[talk]\n[slides]\n[code]\nClass-Weighted Classification: Trade-offs and Robust Approaches\nZX\n,\nChen Dan\n,\nJustin Khim\n,\nPradeep Ravikumar\nICML 2020\n[arXiv 2005.12914]\n[proceedings]\n[talk]\n[code]\nStrategy and Policy Learning for Non-Task-Oriented Conversational Systems\nZhou Yu\n,\nZX\n,\nAlan W Black\n,\nAlexander Rudnicky\nSIGDIAL 2016\n[proceedings]\nChatbot Evaluation and Database Expansion via Crowdsourcing\nZhou Yu\n,\nZX\n,\nAlan W Black\n,\nAlexander Rudnicky\nRE-WOCHAT workshop of LREC 2016\n[proceedings]"
