  "serper::Hui Ye": {
    "homepage": "https://huiye19.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "huiyehy@hkbu.edu.hk"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/hui-ye-ba53b39a/",
    "homepage_text": "Hui Ye@HKBU\nHui Ye 叶卉\nAssistant Professor • Hong Kong Bapist University\nHKBU Profile\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nORCiD\nEmail\nI am a tenure-track Assistant Professor at the\nDepartment of Interactive Media\n,\nSchool of Communication\n,\nHong Kong Baptist University\n. Previously I worked as an\nRGC Postdoctoral Fellow\nat the Division of Arts and Machine Creativity, the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) and School of Creative Media, City University of Hong Kong (CityUHK). I obtained my PhD degree from CityUHK, under the supervision of\nProf. Hongbo Fu\n. I received a BA in communication and a minor in computer science and technology from the University of Science and Technology of China (USTC), with\nGuo Moruo Scholarship\nhonored.\nResearch\nMy research interests lie at the intersection of technical and empirical Human-Computer Interaction (HCI), Computer Graphics (CG), and Communication & Media Studies, with a focus on content creation and interaction design with emerging technologies such as Generative AI and AR/VR. My work spans various practical and creative applications including 3D sketching, animation creation, game design and development, cultural heritage preservation, creativity support, and artistic expression. My recent research explores:\nNovel interactive techniques, tools, and systems with GenAI and AR/VR\nHow people utilize GenAI and LLMs in domain-specific creative applications\nTechnology-assisted artistic practice and creative works\nI am actively looking for self-motivated PhD/Mphil students, research assistants, student helpers, and visiting students to join my group. Please refer to\nGroup\npage for more details.\nNews\n2025-12\n: Our paper on GenAI-assisted creative drawing\nGenFoDrawing\nis accepted by IEEE TVCG.\n2025-12\n: I organize an interactive showcase of course GAME4007 AI for Game Design.\n2025-12\n: I attend SIGGRAPH Asia 2025 in Hong Kong.\n2025-10\n: I am invited to give a guest lecture at HKUST(GZ) and HKUST.\n2025-09\n: I am invited to give a talk on Art-Tech: Technology-assisted Artistic Creation at the Federation of Hong Kong Jiangsu Youth.\n2025-09\n: I am invited to give a guest lecture at HKUST.\n2025-08\n: I have joined the Hong Kong Baptist University (HKBU) as a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor. Start a new journey!\n2025-05\n: I will serve as a Program Committee member for the SIGGRAPH Asia 2025 Emerging Technologies.\n2025-04\n: I am invited to give a talk and share my experience about\nInterdisciplinary Research on HCI, CG, and Communication\nat Striving for Excellence PhD Workshop, Chinese Society of Graphic Science.\n2025-03\n: We are organizing the\nFirst HKUST AI Film Festival\nwith\nCVM 2025\non April 19. This event has garnered significant attention, receiving coverage from over 200 media outlets worldwide.\n2025-03\n: I will serve as a member of the technical program committee (TPC) for ISWC Notes and Briefs of UbiComp/ISWC 2025.\n2025-02\n: I will serve as a member of the International Program Committee (IPC) of the CAD/Graphics 2025.\n2024-12\n: I serve as the Web Chair for the Computer Graphics International 2025 (CGI 2025).\n2024-12\n: I will serve as an International Program Committee (IPC) member for the 9th ACM/EG Expressive Symposium (Expressive 2025).\n2024-12\n: I attend SIGGRAPH Asia 2024 in Tokyo.\n2024-11\n: I serve as the MC for the opening of the exhibition \"\nAltering Nature: Exploring Life in Computational Art\n\" at HKUST.\n2024-10\n: I am invited to give a talk at the\nTechnical Colloquium: Academic Rising Stars Forum\nat Chinagraph 2024.\n2024-06\n: Our paper\nSketch2Human\nis accepted by IEEE TVCG.\n2024-05\n: I serve as the organization co-chair for the 13th international conference on Computational Visual Media (CVM 2025), held in Hong Kong.\n2024-05\n: I attend CHI'24 in person at Honolulu, Hawaii. Our paper\nProInterAR\nis presented and we show a hot-desk demo. I also chair the session \"Immersive Experiences: Creating and Communicating\".\n2024-04\n: I will serve as a Program Committee member for the Pacific Graphics (PG) 2024.\n2024-03\n: I will serve as a Technical Program Committee (TPC) member for the ISWC Notes and Briefs of UbiComp/ISWC 2024.\n2024-03\n: I will serve as a Program Committee member for the SIGGRAPH Asia 2024 Emerging Technologies.\n2024-01\n: Our paper\nProInterAR\nhas been accepted by CHI 2024.\n2024-01\n: I will serve as an Associate Chair (AC) for the CHI 2024 Late-Breaking Work (LBW) Program Committee!\n2023-10\n: I was awarded the Third Prize in the Science and Technology Progress Award of Anhui (安徽省科学技术进步三等奖).\n2023-07\n: I will serve as an Associate Chair (AC) for the CSCW 2024 Program Committee.\n2023-04\n: The interactive digital book\n\"Press Time to Sit Flight: Exploring the Secrets of Nature Science Tour\"\n（坐着时间去飞行）, which I participated in planning and producing, is included in the Key Publication Planning Project during the 13th Five-Year Plan and was selected as a\n2022 National Outstanding Popular Science Works\n.\n2023-01\n: I will serve as an Associate Chair (AC) for the CSCW 2023 Program Committee!\n2023-01\n: Our paper\nProObjAR\nhas been accepted by CHI 2023.\n2022-12\n: I will serve as an Associate Chair (AC) for the CHI 2023 Late-Breaking Work (LBW) Program Committee!\n2022-11\n: I have attended the RGC Award Ceremony.\n2022-09\n: Started my postdoc at CityUHK!\n2022-08\n: I attended CAD&CG 2021+2022 in Dalian, China, and gave an invited talk.\n2022-06\n: I successfully defended my Ph.D. thesis:\n3D Content and Interaction Prototyping with Mobile Augmented Reality\n.\n2022-05\n: Our paper\nDrawingInStyles\nwas accepted by IEEE TVCG.\n2022-05\n: Our paper\nPredict-and-Drive\nwas accepted by ISMAR 2022 and will be published in a special issue of IEEE TVCG.\n2022-05\n: I was awarded the\nRGC Postdoctoral Fellowship\nand will conduct postdoctoral research with Prof. Hongbo Fu. I am honored to be one of the 50 awardees globally!\n2022-04\n: I was invited to give a talk on\n\"Mobile AR Prototyping for Proxemic and Gestural Interactions\"\nat TAFA EAA Youth Academic Forum in Tianjin Fine Arts Institute.\n2022-02\n: Our paper\nProGesAR\nwas accepted by CHI 2022. I will present it on CHI 2022 online in May.\n2022-01\n: My Ph.D. thesis was selected for the\nSIGGRAPH PhD Thesis Fast Forward 2021\nprogram.\n2021-09\n: I was invited to give a\ntalk\nat Graphics and Mixed Environment Symposium (GAMES) about ARAnimator. The talk video can be found\nhere\n.\n2021-09\n: I was awarded\n\"Shidi CAD & CG Excellent Student Award 2021\"\nand \"Outstanding Academic Performance Award\" from CityU.\n2021-09\n: I was featured in\nSCM Newsletters (Issue 8 (2021))\n.\n2021-03\n: I was invited to give a\ntalk\non \"In-situ 3D Content Creation in Mobile AR\" at the Affiliated Forum on Human, Technology and Future of IWHEC 2021.\n2020-12\n: Our paper\n\"3D Curve Creation on and around Physical Objects with Mobile AR\"\nwas accepted by IEEE TVCG, and was invited to be presented in IEEE VR 2021.\n2020-10\n: I was invited to give a talk on ARAnimator at SCM|ACIM Colloquium, CityU.\n2020-09\n: I was awarded \"Research Tuition Scholarship\" of CityU.\n2020-03\n: Our paper\nARAnimator\nwas accepted by SIGGRAPH 2020 and I will present it on SIGGRAPH 2020 online in August.\n2019-12\n: I will visit the Institute of HCI and Media Integration, Tsinghua University as a visiting PhD student.\n2018-12\n: The books\n\"Press Time to Sit Flight: Exploring the Secrets of Nature Science Tour\"\n（坐着时间去飞行）and\n\"Introduction to New Media Science Popularization\"\n（新媒体科普概论）that I participated in planning and produced were published. \"Press Time to Sit Flight: Exploring the Secrets of Nature Science Tour\"（坐着时间去飞行）is an interactive digital book, which was recommended as \"National Excellent Publication Recommended to the Elderly\" in 2019.\n2018-10\n: I worked as a student helper in PG 2018.\n2017-12\n: I attended SIGGRAPH Asia 2017 in Bangkok.\nSelected Publications\nShow All\nAll Publications\nBook Sections\nYanxiang Zhang,\nHui Ye\n, et al.\nPress Time to Sit Flight: Exploring the Secrets of Nature Science Tour\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China Press. 2018.\nKey Publication Planning Project during the 13th Five-Year Plan\n2022 National Outstanding Popular Science Works\n2019 National Excellent Publication Recommended to the Elderly\nYanxiang Zhang,\nHui Ye\n, et al.\nIntroduction to New Media for Science Popularization\nChina Science and Technology Press. 2017.\nChapter 14: Interactive Science Popularization Based on Natural Interaction.\nTeaching\nInstructor\nGAME4026 Creative Production in Extended Reality\nSpring 2026, HKBU\nGAME4006 3D Game World Programming\nSpring 2026, HKBU\nGAME4007 AI for Game Design\nFall 2025, HKBU\nTeaching Assistant\nSM1103A Introduction to Media Computing\nFall 2018, Fall 2019, CityUHK\nSM2716 Physical Computing & Tangible Media\nSpring 2018, CityUHK\nInvited Instructor\nMaya and 3D Animation Creation\nFall 2016, USTC\nScience and Technology Week\n2013-16, USTC\nTalks\n10/2025\nAR/Generative AI-powered Content and Interaction Creation\nInvited Guest Lecturer, HKUST\nInvited Guest Lecturer, HKUST(GZ)\n09/2025\nArt-Tech: Technology-assisted Artistic Creation\nInvited Speaker, Federation of Hong Kong Jiangsu Youth\n09/2025\nAR/Generative AI-powered Content and Interaction Creation for Social Interactive Media\nInvited Guest Lecturer, HKUST\n04/2025\n3D Interaction Authoring and Prototyping in AR & Interdisciplinary Research on HCI, CG, and Communication\nInvited Speaker and Experience Sharer, Striving for Excellence PhD Workshop, Chinese Society of Graphic Science\n10/2024\n3D Content and Interaction Prototyping with Mobile AR\nInvited Speaker, Technical Colloquium: Academic Rising Stars Forum, Chinagraph 2024\n05/2024\nProInterAR: A Visual Programming Platform for Creating Immersive AR Interactions\nConference Paper Presenter, Hot-Desk Demo, CHI 2024\n05/2023\nProObjAR: Prototyping Spatially-aware Interactions of Smart Objects with AR-HMD\nConference Paper Presenter, CHI 2023\n08/2022\nFrom Communication to Computer Graphics\nInvited Presenter, Student Colloquium, CAD&CG 2022+2023\n05/2022\nProGesAR: Mobile AR Prototyping for Proxemic and Ge...[truncated]"
  },
