    "homepage_text": "Youzhi Zhang\nYouzhi Zhang\nHome\nPublications\nHome\nYouzhi Zhang\nAssociate Professor\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence and Robotics (CAIR)\nHong Kong Institute of Science & Innovation, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nWe are looking for highly motivated interns, RA, and postdocs   to join our team. If you want to work with us, feel free to email me.\nScholar Profile:\nGoogle Scholar Profile\n&\nDBLP\nE-mail: youzhi dot zhang dot lgc@gmail dot com\nAddress: Room 301-303, 305-309, 317-320, 3/F, 17W, Science Park West Avenue, Hong Kong Science Park, Pak Shek Kok, New Territories, Hong Kong\nBrief Biography\nDr. Zhang is an associate professor of CAIR, HKISI-CAS and was an assistant professor during August 2022 - April 2025. Before joining CAIR, he was a postdoctoral researcher at the Northwestern University, USA, working with Professor V.S. Subrahmanian. From August 2020 to August 2021, he was a postdoctoral researcher at the Dartmouth College, USA, working with Professor V.S. Subrahmanian. He received the Ph.D degree in Computer Science from the Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, where he was advised by Professor Bo An. Prior to that, he received the Bachelor and Master degrees from the Sun Yat-sen University, China.\nHis research interests include Agentic AI, multi-agent systems, computational game theory, multi-agent reinforcement learning, LLM for game theory,  AI governance, AI for science, AI for drug discovery, and decision making in complex environments including security and healthcare.\nTop News\n[January 2026] Two papers were accepted by ICLR 2026 and AISTATS 2026, respectively.\n[December 2025] One paper was accepted by AAMAS 2026.\n[November 2025] Two papers were accepted by AAAI 2026 with one oral presentation.\n[October 2025] Two papers were accepted by IEEE TASE and  CAAI TIT, respectively.\n[September 2025] Two papers were accepted by NeurIPS 2025, and three papers were accepted by ACSAC 2025, Frontiers of Computer Science, and Autonomous Robots, respectively.\n[May 2025] One paper was accepted by ICML 2025 Spotlight (the top 2.6% of 12,107 submissions).\n[January 2025] One paper was accepted by WWW 2025 (TheWebConf25).\n[December 2024] Attend  DAI 2024 (session chair) and present our work on adversarial team games.\n[December 2024] Give a talk about game theory and its applications at  DAI 2024 MARL worshop\n[December 2024] Visit Sun Yat-sen University, SUTD, SMU.\n[October 2024] Attend RLChina 2024.\n[July 2024] Attend ICML 2024.\n[May 2024] Two papers was accepted by ICML 2024.\n[April 2024] One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics.\n[January 2024] One paper was accepted by WWW 2024 (TheWebConf24) (Oral presentation).\n[December 2023] One paper was accepted by AAMAS 2024.\n[November&December 2023] Visit  Nanyang Technological University and attend DAI 2023 (session chair).\n[September 2023] One paper was accepted by NeurIPS 2023 and one paper was accepted by  IEEE Transactions on Computational Social Systems.\n[August 2023] Distinguished  Program Committee Member at IJCAI 2023 (the top 3% of reviewers).\n[July 2023] One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (a top journal on security).\n[July 2023] Visit Nanjing University,   Southeast University, and HUAWEI NOAH'S ARK LAB.\n[July 2023] Attend IJCAI YES 2023.\n[June 2023] Visit Southern University of Science and Technology and Sun Yat-sen University.\n[May 2023] Attend AAMAS 2023.\n[January 2023] One paper was accepted by AAMAS 2023.\n[November 2022] Invited talk at the Southeast University.\n[November 2022] Invited talk at the Huawei–CAIR AI and Robotics Workshop.\n[November 2022] Two papers were accepted by AAAI 2023.\n[September 2022] The Best Paper Award at the 20th IEEE International Conference on Dependable, Autonomic & Secure Computing (DASC 2022).\n[July 2022] Outstanding Reviewer at ICML 2022 (the top 10% of reviewers).\n[April 2022] One paper was accepted by IJCAI 2022 as Long Oral Presentation (3.75% rate).\nAwards & Honors\nDistinguished  Program Committee Member Award, IJCAI, 2023.\nThe  Best Paper Award, IEEE DASC, 2022.\nOutstanding Reviewer Award, ICML, 2022.\nThe Ph.D Best Thesis Award, NTU SCSE, 2021.\nFinalist (25/1000+), KDD'20 Reinforcement Learning Competition Track, 2020.\nStudent Travel Award, AAAI, 2019 & 2020.\nResearch Scholarship, NTU, 2016-2020.\nNational Scholarship for Graduate Students, Ministry of Education of China, 2014 & 2015.\nOutstanding Graduates Award,   Sun Yat-sen University, 2013.\nOutstanding Thesis Award,   Sun Yat-sen University, 2013.\nResearch Appointments\nAssociate  Professor\n(May 2025 - Present)\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence and Robotics (CAIR), Hong Kong Institute of Science & Innovation, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nAssistant Professor\n(August 2022 - April 2025)\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence and Robotics (CAIR), Hong Kong Institute of Science & Innovation, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nPostdoctoral Researcher\n(September 2021 - August 2022)\nDepartment of Computer Science, Northwestern University, USA\nPostdoctoral Researcher\n(August 2020 - August 2021)\nDepartment of Computer Science, Dartmouth College, USA\nResearch Assistant\n(March 2020 - July 2020)\nAgent Mediated Intelligence Research Group, School of Computer Science and Engineering, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore\nInvited Talks\nGame theory and LLM security\n(July 2025)\nHKSIA 2025 Minisymposia of Trustworthy ML: Theory and Applications\nGame theory and LLM security\n(June 2025)\nGuangzhou University\nGame-theoretic AI: From urban network security games to adversarial team games\n(January 2025)\nHUAWEI HK\nGame-theoretic AI: From urban network security games to adversarial team games\n(December 2024)\nDAI 2024 MARL Workshop, Singapore\nDAG-based column generation for adversarial team games\n(December 2024)\nDAI 2024, Singapore\nGame-theoretic AI: From urban network security games to adversarial team games\n(December 2024)\nSun Yat-sen University, China\nComputing optimal Nash equilibria in multiplayer games\n(December 2023)\nNanyang Technological University and DAI 2023\nSolving network pursuit games: Challenge and the state-of-the-art\n(July 2023)\nHUAWEI NOAH'S ARK LAB, Hong Kong SAR, China\nSolving network pursuit games: Challenge and the state-of-the-art\n(July 2023)\nNanjing University, Nanjing, China\nSolving network pursuit games: Challenge and the state-of-the-art\n(July 2023)\nSoutheast University, Nanjing, China\nSolving network pursuit games: Challenge and the state-of-the-art\n(June 2023)\nSun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, China\nSolving network pursuit games: Challenge and the state-of-the-art\n(June 2023)\nSouthern University of Science and Technology, Shenzhen, China\nCorrelation-based algorithm for team-maxmin equilibrium in multiplayer extensive-form games\n(November 2022)\nSoutheast University of Science and Technology, Online\nCorrelation-based algorithm for team-maxmin equilibrium in multiplayer extensive-form games\n(November 2022)\nHuawei--CAIR AI and Robotics Workshop, Online\nConverging to team-maxmin equilibria in zero-sum multiplayer games\n(December 2020)\nDartmouth College, Online\nComputing team-maxmin equilibria in zero-sum multiplayer games\n(November 2020)\nUniversity of California, Berkeley, Online\nConverging to team-maxmin equilibria in zero-sum multiplayer games\n(October 2020)\nDAI, Online\nProfessional Services\nProgram  Co-Chair\nThe 2025 IEEE International Conference on Intelligence and Security Informatics (IEEE ISI 2025)\nConference Program Committee Member\n(Reviewer)\nICML (2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026); NeurIPS (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025); AAAI (2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026); IJCAI (2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026); ICLR (2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026); AAMAS (2025, 2026); KDD (2026); ACL (2026)\nJournal Reviewer\nScience; Science Advances; IEEE Intelligent Systems;  Autonomous Agents and Multi-Agent Systems; INFORMS Journal on Computing\nMinisymposia Organizer\nTrustworthy ML: Theory and Applications at the Third Hong Kong Society for Industrial and Applied\nMathematics (HKSIAM) Biennial Conference, 2025\nEducation\nDoctor of Philosophy\nin Computer Science. Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (July 2016 - July 2020)\nThe Ph.D Best Thesis Award, NTU SCSE, 2021.\nSupervised by\nProfessor Bo An\n.\nMaster  of Philosophy\nin Logic. Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, China (August 2013 - June 2016)\nBachelor  of Philosophy\nin Logic. Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, China (Sep 2009 - June 2013)\nOutstanding Graduate of Sun Yat-sen University and Outstanding Thesis of Sun Yat-sen University.\nSupervising\nShangkun Zheng\n,  Ph.D student\nShuxin Zhuang\n,   Ph.D student\nRong Feng\n, Ph.D student\nAlumni\nRunSheng Yu\n, Visiting PhD student/intern from HKUST, now ByteDance\nJiazhi Zhang\n, Visiting Master student/intern from HKUST, now ByteDance"
  },
