  "serper::Tyler Chen": {
    "homepage": "https://wides.usc.edu/",
    "emails": [
      "details@wiley.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "WiDeS - USC\nWireless Devices and\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSystems Group\nThe WiDeS group performs ground-breaking research in the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tarea of wireless propagation, system design, communication theory, and cross-layer design.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWiDeS is dedicated to research that is both scientifically challenging and practically\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\trelevant.\nLearn more\nPioneers of the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFuture\nWiDeS members are doing pioneering work in communication\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttheory, system design, and propagation research.\nFrom the invention\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tof hybrid beamformers to the development of the femtocaching concept that provides\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\torder-of- magnitude gains in efficiency of video distribution, to groundbreaking channel\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmeasurements, we are the forefront of innovation, providing insights and patents to our\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsponsors and advancing the state of the art.\nLearn more\nCollaboration\nA hallmark of WiDeS is the very collaborative atmosphere.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWe work (and celebrate!) together, and also have extensive national and international\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcollaborations, from China to Finland to Virginia.\nAlumni of the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tgroup are now professors at prestigious universities, or have careers in startups as\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\twell as established players such as Amazon, Google, or Intel.\nLearn more\nAwards\nWe keep a high profile, publishing in the top journals,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tand at the flagship international conferences.\nMany WiDeS students\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thave received best-paper awards. All of this translates into great career opportunities\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfor our alumni.\nTeaching\nOf course teaching is one of our\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcore missions.\nFrom providing a textbook on wireless communications that is used\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tall over the world, to giving tutorials at major conferences, to lecture tours on\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcutting-edge topics, WiDeS head\nAndy Molisch\nis dedicated to all\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tforms of education.\nLearn more\nMeet Our Founder\nAndy Molisch founded WiDeS when he joined USC as professor in\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t2009, after 15 years in industry (AT&T (Bell) Labs, Mitsubishi Electric Research Labs) and\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tacademia; in 2017 he was appointed as the Golomb-Viterbi Chair.\nâUSC\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tis a stellar place for electrical engineering, and I am lucky to have great colleagues\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tas well as wonderful studentsâ he said. âThe success of WiDeS is based on the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontributions of all of themâ.\nLearn more\nPrevious\nNext\nNews\nIn the new semester, two new PhD students and a PostDoctoral researcher join the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWiDeS group. Yijing Zhang, a recent MS graduate from Columbia University, and\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFerdous Pervej, an expert in Federated Learning who this summer received his PhD\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfrom North Carolina State University, will be working on privacy-preserving\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcaching of video. Chin-Wei Huang, an MS graduate from National Taiwan\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tUniversity, will be working on robust networks that perform joint computation,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcommunication, and caching of information. Welcome to the group.\nWiDeS welcomes two new PhD students and a Postdoc\nLinkedIn, a popular professional networking application, is trying to grab the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmost sensitive data of users. The company has started to â seemingly arbitrarily\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t- block users and then demand copies of driverâs licenses to make the accounts\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taccessible again. Since driversâ license is the most sensitive government-issued\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdocument in the US, and LinkedIn is the culprit of two of the largest data\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tbreaches in the history of the internet, sending them this information puts\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tusers at extremely high risk for identity theft â leaving them with the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tunpalatable option of either giving up the network they have built up over the\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tyears, or risking falling victim to identity theft.\nBeware of LinkedIn\nWiDeS PostDocs Lei Chu and Ju-Hyung Lee acted as mentors in the Viterbi Summer\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tInstitute (VSI), which gives incoming freshmen from underrepresented minorities\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttheir first research experiences. Eryn Osei and Zolia Sarmiento (advised by Dr.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLee), and Naomi Cruz (advised by Dr. Chu, shown in photo) learned about\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfundamental research methodology and did some first machine learning projects.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNaomi Cruz will continue her work with Dr. Chu as CURVE student in the upcoming\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsemester.\nWiDeS giving first research experience to incoming URM freshmen\nThe third, expanded and completely revised edition of the popular textbook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Wireless Communications\" was just published by IEEE Press - Wiley. Subtitled\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"From Fundamentals to Beyond 5G\", the text leads from the basics of wireless\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tpropagation, digital modulation, to cellular system design, to cutting-edge\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttopics such as massive MIMO, NOMA, and the 5G standards. More details at\nwiley.com/go/molisch/wireless3e\nand\nhere\nThird Edition of Molisch's \"Wireless Communications\" published\nPrevious\nNext\nSee Previous News\nGallery\nPrevious\nNext\nPrevious\nNext\nFor Students\nCourses\nTextbooks\nDirected Research\nProspective PhD students, PostDocs, and Visitors\nResearch for undergraduate and MS students - apply here\nFor Sponsors\nBenefits\nForms of Collaboration\nCurrent Sponsors\nResearch\nPropagation Channels\nPropagation channels\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tare at the core of any wireless system: they determine not only the ultimate performance\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tlimits, but also the relative merits of different systems, and even give guidelines of\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thow systems should be designed. The first axiom of wireless systems is :\nto design\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ta wireless system, you must understand the channel in which it will\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\toperate.\nBuilding Channel Sounders\nParameter Extraction Methods\nChannel Modelling\nMm-wave and THz channels\nV2V and UAV channels\nMassive MIMO and Cloud RAN\nCommunication System Design\nAn exciting challenge in wireless system design is the need to merge insights from\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmany different disciplines. From communication theory to networking, optimization\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttheory, to physics, system design requires both broad and deep thinking.\nWiDeS has established itself as a pioneer in a number of select topics, namely MIMO\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsystems (particularly reduced-complexity MIMO transceivers, wireless video distribution,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tultrawideband communication and localization, and novel modulation and multiplexing\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmethods (particularly OAM and OTFS). In all of these fields we follow our philosophy of\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfinding innovative approaches that are inspired by practical applications, but grounded\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tin solid theory.\nMachine Learning for Communications and Localization\nMobile Edge Computing and Joint Communication, Computing, and Caching\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t(3C)\nWireless Video Distribution\nNovel Modulation and Multiplexing Methods\nMIMO Systems\nUltrawideband Communication and Localization\nPublications\nUp-to-date listing of our publications can be seen from our Google scholar pages, in\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tparticular\nHERE\n.\nOpen Source Dataset and Code\nFind Source Codes for\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tpublications\nOpen-Source Pathloss Map Prediction Dataset\nCode for generating files with realistic popularity distribution\nOpen-Source Cell-Free Massive MIMO Channel Data 2020\nProjects\nProjects being worked\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tupon, or built.\nDroTerNet\nFLVideo\nRINGS\nIRTSCS\nMLWPC"
  },
