    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/chao-jia-6157ba14",
    "homepage_text": "Chao Jia's homepage\nChao Jia\nI graduated in May 2014 with a Ph.D. degree, and\n       I'm working for Qualcomm Research in San Diego, CA USA.\nI earned my Ph.D. in\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nat\nThe University of Texas at Austin\n.\n   At UT Austin, I was a member of\nCenter for Perceptual Systems\nand\nWireless Networking and communications Group\n.\n      My supervisor is\nProf. Brian L. Evans\n.\n   I received my B.S. degree in Electrical Engineering Department at Tsinghua University, China,\n      in July 2009, and then enrolled at UT Austin in fall 2009 for graduate ECE studies.\nResearch Overview\nGenerally I'm interested in computer vision and machine learning. My graduate research mainly focuses on the area of computational photography, including video acquisition, motion deblurring and superresolution on mobile phone cameras. Besides, I'm also interested in sparse coding for object recognition and image restoration.\nPublications at UT Austin\nOnline Camera-Gyroscope Auto-Calibration for Cellphones\nC. Jia and B. L. Evans,\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n, vol. 23, no. 12, pp. 5070-5081, Dec. 2014.\n[\npdf\n]\n\"Real-Time 3D Rotation Smoothing for Video Stabilization\"\nC. Jia, Z. Sinno and B. L. Evans,\nProc. Asilomar Conf. on Signals, Systems, and Computers\n, Nov. 2-5, 2014, pp. 673-677, Pacific Grove, CA USA.\n[\npdf\n]\n\"Constrained 3D Rotation Smoothing via Global Manifold Regression for Video Stabilization\"\nC. Jia and B. L. Evans,\nIEEE Transactions on Signal Processing\n, vol. 62, no. 13, pp. 3293-3304, Jul. 1, 2014.\n[\npdf\n]\n\"Online Calibration and Synchronization of Cellphone Camera and Gyroscope\"\nC. Jia and B. L. Evans,\nIEEE Global Conference on Signal and Information Processing (GlobalSIP)\n, Dec. 3-5, 2013, pp. 731-734, Austin, TX USA.\n[\npdf\n]\n\"3D Rotational Video Stabilization using Manifold Optimization\"\nC. Jia and B. L. Evans,\nIEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing (ICASSP)\n, May 26-31, 2013, Vancouver, Canada.\n[\npdf\n] (Google Travel Grant Winner)\n\"Probabilistic 3D Motion Estimation for Rolling Shutter Video Rectification from Visual and Inertial Measurements\"\nC. Jia and B. L. Evans,\nIEEE International Workshop on Multimedia Signal Processing (MMSP)\n, May 26-31, 2013, Vancouver, Canada.\n[\npdf\n] (Top 10% Best Paper Award)\n\"Mobile Multipath Cooperative Network for Real-time Streaming\"\nV. Raveendran, P. Bhamidipati, X. Luo, X. Huang and C. Jia,\nSignal Processing: Image Communication\n, vol. 27, Feb. 2012.\n\"Patch-based Image Deconvolution via Joint Modeling of Sparse Priors\"\nC. Jia and B. L. Evans,\nIEEE International Conference on Image Processing (ICIP)\n, Sep. 11-14, 2011, Brussels, Belgium.\n[\npdf\n]\nGraduate Courses\nVisual recognition\nDigital Video\nMachine learning\nComputer graphics\nSparsity, structure and algorithms\nVision systems\nNumerical linear algebra\nStochastic optimization\nModel-based detection and estimation\nIntroduction to system theory\nprobability and stochastic processes\nInformation theory\nAnalysis and design of communication networks\nDigital communications"
  },
