    "homepage_text": "Zhen Li's Homepage\nZhen Li (李震)\nResearcher in HCI\n©\nCopyright ©\nAll rights reserved | This template is made with\nby\nColorlib\nHi!\nI'm Zhen\nI am a senior researcher at Huawei Canada.\nAbout\nAbout Me\nHi I'm Zhen Li.\nI am a senior researcher at Huawei Canada (Toronto Research Centre).\nI received my Ph.D. at the University of Toronto, supervised by\nProf. Daniel Wigdor\n.\nMy research interests lie in Augmented Reality, Virtual Reality, and Cross-device Interaction.\nDownload CV\nPublications\nPublications\nArmstrong: An Empirical Examination of Pointing at Non-Dominant Arm-Anchored UIs in Virtual Reality\nZhen Li\n, Joannes Chan, Joshua Walton, Hrvoje Benko, Daniel Wigdor, and Michael Glueck. In\nProceedings of the CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\n(CHI '21).\nPDF\n|\nVideo\n|\nVideo\nEyelid Gestures on Mobile Devices for People with Motor Impairments\nMingming Fan*,\nZhen Li*\n, and Franklin Mingzhe Li*. In\nThe 22nd International ACM SIGACCESS Conference on Computers and Accessibility\n(ASSETS '20).\n(Best Artifact Award)\nPDF\n|\nCode\n|\nAPK\n|\nVideo\n|\nVideo\nHoloDoc: Enabling Mixed Reality Workspaces that Harness Physical and Digital Content\nZhen Li\n, Michelle Annett, Ken Hinckley, Karan Singh and Daniel Wigdor. In\nProceedings of the CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\n(CHI '19).\nPDF\n|\nVideo\n|\nVideo\nSMAC: A Simplified Model of Attention and Capture in Multi-Device Desk-Centric Environments\nZhen Li\n, Michelle Annett, Ken Hinckley and Daniel Wigdor. In\nProceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction\n(EICS '19), Vol. 3, EICS, Article 02 (June 2019).\nPDF\n|\nVideo\n|\nVideo\nTOAST: Ten-Finger Eyes-Free Typing on Touchable Surfaces\nWeinan Shi, Chun Yu, Xin Yi,\nZhen Li\n, and Yuanchun Shi. In\nProceedings of the ACM on Interactive, Mobile, Wearable, and Ubiquitous Technologies\n(UBICOMP '18), Vol. 2, No. 1, Article 33 (March 2018).\nPDF\n|\nVideo\n|\nVideo\nEducation\nEducation\n2017 - 2022\nPh.D. in Computer Science, University of Toronto\n2015 - 2017\nM.S. in Computer Science, University of Toronto\n2011 - 2015\nB.Eng. in Computer Science, Tsinghua University\nExperience\nWork Experience\nSenior Researcher\nJune 2022 - now\nHuawei Canada (Toronto Research Centre).\nResearch Intern\nApr. - Sep. 2019\nArmstrong: An Empirical Examination of Pointing at Non-Dominant Arm-Anchored UIs in Virtual Reality\nSupervised by\nDr. Michael Glueck\nat Chatham Labs\nPublished at CHI 2021:\nLink\nResearch Intern\nJuly - Sep. 2014\nKeyboard-Surface Interaction: Using the Keyboard's Surface as a Pointing Device\nSupervised by\nProf. Anind Dey\n, HCI Institute, Carnegie Mellon University\nDesigned the first stage of the user study and contributed to the gesture recognition\nGet in Touch\nContact\nzhen.li1@huawei.com\n19 Allstate Pkwy, Markham, Ontario, Canada L3R 5A4"
  },
  "serper::Pinyan Lu": {
