  "serper::Chenhao Wang": {
    "homepage": "https://chenhwang4.github.io/homepage/",
    "emails": [
      "chenhaowang@uic.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Chenhao Wang's homepage (UIC)\nChenhao Wang's Homepage\nAssistant Professor\nDivision of Science and Technology\nBeijing Normal University-Hong Kong Baptist University United International College (UIC)\nZhuhai, Guangdong, China\nOffice:\nT3-602-R14\nEmail:\nchenhaowang@uic.edu.cn\nBio\nI am current an Assistant Professor in Department of Computer Science and Technology at UIC, and also an Associate Distinguished Research Fellow in the Institute of AI and Future Networks, Beijing Normal University, Zhuhai.\nBefore joining UIC and BNU in December 2021, I was a Postdoctoral Fellow working with\nMakoto Yokoo\n(the first AAAI Fellow in Asia) in Graduate School of Information Science and Electrical Engineering at Kyushu University, \n\t\tand with\nHau Chan\nin Department of Computer Science & Engineering at University of Nebraska-Lincoln. \n\t\tI received my PhD in Operations Research from Academy of Mathematics and Systems Science, Chinese Academy of Sciences, under the supervision of\nXiaodong Hu\nand\nXujin Chen\n, \n\t\tand a joint PhD in Computer Science from Department of Computer Science at City University of Hong Kong, under the supervision of\nMinming Li\n.\t\t\n\t\tI completed my B.S. in Applied Maths at Hua Loo-Keng Class, Beihang University.\nOpenings\nWe regularly have several positions for PhD/MPhi students in Computer Science each year, as well as for Research Assistant (Visiting Scholar).\nIf you are interested in my research and want to join our group, please don't hesitate to send me an email with your CV.\nResearch Interests\nI am broadly interested in algorithms, AI and computational economics, including problems related to\nAlgorithmic Game Theory and Mechanism Design\nComputational Social Choice\nMulti-Agent Systems\nApproximation and Online Algorithms\nSelected Publications (\nFull List\n)\nFacility Location Games with Ordinal Preferences\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nHau Chan, Zifan Gong, Minming Li and Yingchao Zhao\n, Theoretical Computer Science, 2023.\nImproved Analysis of Greedy Algorithm on k-Submodular Knapsack.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nZhongzheng Tang\n, ECAI 2023.\nMechanism Design for Improving Accessibility to Public Facilities.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nHau Chan\n, AAMAS 2023.\nMonotone k-Submodular Secretary Problems: Cardinality and Knapsack Constraints.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nZhongzheng Tang and Hau Chan\n, Theoretical Computer Science, 2022.\nBudget Feasible Mechanisms for Facility Location Games with Strategic Facilities.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nMinming Li and Mengqi Zhang\n, Autonomous Agents and Multi-Agent Systems, 2022.\nA Note on the Online Interval Scheduling Secretary Problem.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nBo Li and Ruilong Zhang\n, Operations Research Letters, 2022.\nApproximate Group Fairness for Clustering. \n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nBo Li, Lijun Li, Ankang Sun and Yingfan Wang\n, ICML 2021.\nFacility's Perspective to Fair Facility Location Problems.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nHau Chan, Minming Li and Xiaoying Wu\n, AAAI 2021.\nMechanism Design for Facility Location Problem: A Survey. \n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nHau Chan, Aris Filos-Ratsikas, Bo Li and Minming Li\n, IJCAI 2021.\nGame-theoretic Analysis of Effort Allocation of Contributors to Public Projects.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nHau Chan, Jared Soundy and Clay Stevens\n, AAAI 2021.\nFairness and Efficiency in Facility Location Problems with Continuous Demands.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nMengqi Zhang\n, AAMAS 2021.\nMulti-Robot Task Allocation -- Complexity and Approximation.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nHaris Aziz, Hau Chan, Agnes Cseh, Bo Li and Fahimeh Ramezani\n, AAMAS 2021.\nAlgorithms for the Metric Ring Star Problem with Fixed Edge-Cost Ratio.\n\t\t\t\t\t  Joint work with\nXujin Chen, Xiaodong Hu, Xiaohua Jia, Zhongzheng Tang and Ying Zhang\n, Journal of Combinatorial Optimization, 2021.\nServices\nPC Member: AAAI'21/22/23, IJCAI'21/22/23, AAMAS'21/22/23\nJournal Reviewer: \n\t\t\t\tMath Reviewer of American Mathematical Society, Mathematics of Operations Research, European Journal of Operational Research, Science China Mathematics,  Theoretical Computer Science\nTeaching\nCOMP7340 Special Topics in Machine Learning II (Rpg), Spring 2022\nMATH2003 Discrete Structures (Y1 1002/1007), Spring 2022, 2023\nGTSC2093 IT for Success in Everyday Life and Work, Fall 2022, 2023\nMATH1163 Advanced Calculus, Spring 2023, Fall 2023"
  },
