    "homepage_text": "Chia-Hao Lee\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nChia-Hao Lee\nHome\nSee the atomic world\nI’m Chia-Hao Lee, a Schmidt AI for Science postdoc at Cornell University!\nMy research explores the fusion of AI with\nthe state-of-the-art aberration-corrected scanning transmission electron microscopy (AC-S/TEM) and 4D-STEM techniques\nto achieve sub-angstrom resolution characterization of quantum and energy materials.\nMy CV\n(updated\nJune\n07\n, 202\n4\n)\nchia-hao.lee@cornell.edu\nPtychographic reconstruction of twisted bilayer WSe2\nPtychographic reconstruction of graphene-encapsulated twisted bilayer WSe2\nMoire pattern of twisted few-layer graphene\nDiffraction pattern of MoTe2 IDB superlattice\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Simeng Han": {
    "homepage": "https://sophiahan6.github.io/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/academicpages",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Sophia Simeng Han\nSophia Han\nIn pursuit of Lux et Veritas\nFollow\nEmail\nTwitter\nGoogle Scholar\nI work on making reasoning systems precise, verifiable, and usable in law and policy as a postdoc at Stanford Law School and Stanford NLP.\nI finished my PhD in Computer Science at Yale where I studied AI for logical reasoning and legal reasoning with Tom McCoy, Emily Hau and Sarah Insley. I interned at Google Brain, Google Deepmind, Meta Superintelligence Labs and Amazon Web Services during my Ph.D., working on advancing LLM capabilities in frontier LMs. Before my PhD, I did my undergraduate studies at NTU, Singapore where I wanted to become a geek and built many interesting softwares. Even before that, I underwent intensive Math and Physics Olympiad training in my high school in China.\nOutside of research and work, I am a jack-of-all-trades in art. I am an amateur opera singer, photographer, piano player, and Guzheng player."
  },
  "serper::Jiashuo Liu": {
    "homepage": "https://ljsthu.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "liujiashuo77@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/LJSthu",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jiashuo Liu's Website\nJiashuo Liu（刘家硕）\nByteDance Seed Team\n(prev)\nMember of TopSeed Talent Program\n(prev)\nEmail\n:\nliujiashuo77@gmail.com\nScholar\nTwitter\nGithub\nCV\nI work on LLM Eval & Synthetic Data.\nI was a Research Scientist at ByteDance Seed, as a member of\nTopSeed\nProgram, working with\nWenhao Huang\n. I received my Ph.D. from the Department of Computer Science and Technology at Tsinghua University, advised by Professors\nPeng Cui\nand\nBo Li\n. Previously, I was a visiting student researcher at Stanford University, working with Professor\nJose Blanchet\n; and at the Cambridge Centre for AI in Medicine, working with Professor\nMihaela van der Schaar.\nI obtained my Bachelor's degree from Tsinghua University.\nResearch\nI focus on building next-generation LLM evaluation systems and large-scale, data-centric AI. I believe LLM evaluation should be\nreliable\n,\nefficient\n, and\nanchored in realistic real-world tasks\n, and it must rest on a deep understanding of data. I contribute to the Seed Evaluation System at ByteDance Seed (part of my insights are demonstrated in\nSeed1.8 Model Card\n).\nSpecific topics include:\nReliable LLM Eval\n: We design new perturbation algorithms and future prediction tasks with completely no data contamination to reliably assess the true capabilities of Agentic LLMs. Together with Prof.\nMengdi Wang\n, our\nFutureX project\n,described by Elon Musk as the \"Best Measure of Intelligence\"(\nmedia\n), has received over 100 million views on X(Twitter). Following this line, we release\nCryptoBench\nfor expert-level tasks in cryptocurrency domains. Also, we design\nLLM Swiss Round\nto give a holistic ranking of leading LLMs.\nEfficient LLM Eval\n: We design algorithms to efficiently and accurately evaluate LLM's performance.\nRealistic LLM Eval\n: We use realistic, professional and valuable tasks to benchmark LLM's true value in helping with daily works. Together with Prof.\nHongseok Namkoong\n, our\nFinSearchComp\nhas received over 20 million views on X(Twitter), and is recently adopted in MiniMax-M2's report and Kimi-K2-Thinking's report.\nLLM Calibration\n: We design\nBehaviorally Calibrated-RL\nto calibrate LLM's confidence estimation, enabling LLM's to say \"I don't know\".\nCurrent Academic Collaborators\n:\nJose Blanchet\n(Stanford MS&E),\nEmmanuel Candès\n(Stanford Statistics),\nHongseok Namkoong\n(Columbia DRO),\nMihaela van der Schaar\n(Cambridge CCAIM), and\nMengdi Wang\n(Princeton ECE).\nCurrent Interns\n:\nZerui Cheng\n(Princeton University, reliable evaluation),\nJiayun Wu\n(CMU, LLM calibration)\nEducation/Experience\n2020-2025: Ph.D. in Computer Science, Tsinghua University\n2016-2020: B.Eng in Computer Science, Tsinghua University\n2024/6-2024/11: Visiting Student Researcher at the University of Cambridge\n2023/10-2024/3: Visiting Student Researcher at Stanford University\nTemplate adapted from\nDanqi Chen\n's."
  },
