    "homepage_text": "Yutong's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYutong's Homepage\nYutong Wu\nOffice:\nKline Tower 935, Yale University\nEmail:\nyutong dot wu dot yw894 at yale dot edu\nI am a third year graduate student in the\nDepartment of Mathematics\nat\nYale University\n. My advisor is Prof.\nWilhelm Schlag\n. Before coming to Yale, I received my bachelor's degree in\nMathematics\nfrom\nPeking University\n.\nMy research interests lie in partial differential equations, with particular focuses on multisoliton solutions and blow-up dynamics in dispersive equations.\nHere is my\nCV\n.\nUpcoming events\n04/18\n—04/\n19\nRecent Developments in Dynamics of Nonlinear Dispersive Equations\n, AMS Central Sectional Meeting Special Session, North Dakota University, Fargo, ND\nPapers\nMultisoliton solutions and blow up for the L^2-critical Hartree equation\n, with Jaime Gómez and Tobias Schmid,\narXiv:2501.18398,\nsubmitted. [\npdf\n]\nExistence of multisoliton solutions of the gravitational Hartree equation in three dimensions\n,\nTrans. Am. Math. Soc.\n, electronically published on January 23, 2026,\nDOI:\nhttps://doi.org/10.1090/tran/9654\n(to appear in print)\n[\npdf\n]\nTalks\nPDE Seminar, Georgia Institution of Technology, Atlanta, GA, 2026.03\nMath Physics Seminar, Georgia Southern University, Statesboro, GA, 2026.03\nWorkshop in PDE and Applied Math in the Northeast Region\n, University of Connecticut, Storrs, CT,  2026.03\nRecent Advances in Harmonic Analysis and Partial Differential Equations\n(poster), Baylor University,\nWaco, TX\n,\n2025.05\nThe AMS New England Graduate Conference, Brown University, Providence, RI, 2025.04\nSpectral Analysis of Schrodinger Operators\n(poster), ICERM, Providence, RI, 2024.08\nInternational Congress of Basic Science (ICBS) (poster),\nBIMSA,\nBeijing\n,\n2024.07\nBrown-Yale PDE Seminar, Brown University, Providence, RI, 2024.05\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
