    "homepage_text": "Group of Chengkuo Lee | Members\nNUS Lab of Sensors, MEMS and NEMS\nfor Internet of Things (IoT) Applications\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nAwards\nConferences\nMembers\nNews & Announcements\nLinks\nMembers\nResearch Fellows\nLI Dongxiao\nReceived his B.Sc. degree in College of Artificial Intelligence from Chongqing Technology and Business University, Chongqing, China, and Ph.D. degree in Instrument Science and Technology from Chongqing University, China, in 2022. He is now a Research Fellow at the Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering, NUS. His research interests are focused on mid-IR metamaterials and nanophotonics for sensing applications.\nArticles Published:\nDongxiao Li, Hong Zhou, Ziwei Chen, Zhihao Ren, Cheng Xu, Xianming He, Tao Liu, Xin Chen, He Huang,\nChengkuo Lee\nand Xiaojing Mu, Ultrasensitive Molecular Fingerprint Retrieval Using Strongly Detuned Overcoupled Plasmonic Nanoantennas,\nAdvanced Materials\n, 2301787, 2023.\nHong Zhou,\nDongxiao Li\n, Zhihao Ren, Xiaojing Mu, and Chengkuo Lee, Loss-induced phase transition in mid-infrared plasmonic metamaterials for ultrasensitive vibrational spectroscopy, InfoMat, e12349, 2022. (shared first authorship)\nDongxiao Li\n, Hong Zhou, Xindan Hui, Xianming He, He Huang, Jiajia Zhang, Xiaojing Mu, Chengkuo Lee, and Ya Yang, Multifunctional Chemical Sensing Platform Based on Dual-Resonant Infrared Plasmonic Perfect Absorber for On-Chip Detection of Poly(ethyl cyanoacrylate), Adv. Sci., 2101879, 2021.\nREN Zhihao\nReceived his B.Sc. degree from the School of Physics at the University of Electronic Science and Technology of China (UESTC), Chengdu, China, in 2017 After that he received his M.Sc. degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) from National University of Singapore (NUS). He is currently a Research Engineer in the Department of ECE, NUS. His research interests are focused on mid-IR chemical sensors on metamaterials and nanophotonics for biomedical applications.\nArticles Published:\nHong Zhou,\nZhihao Ren\n, Cheng Xu, Liangge Xu, and Chengkuo Lee, MOF/Polymer-integrated Multi-Hotspot Mid-Infrared Nanoantennas for Sensitive Detection of CO2 Gas,\nNano-Micro Letters\n,vol. 14, 207, 2022\nZhihao Ren\n, Zixuan Zhang, Jingxuan Wei, Bowei Dong, and Chengkuo Lee, Wavelength-multiplexed hook nanoantennas\r\n                                for machine learning enabled mid-infrared spectroscopy,\nNat. Commun.\n, vol. 13, 3859, 2022.\nZhihao Ren\n, Bowei Dong, Qifeng Qiao, Xinmiao Liu, Jinyuan Liu, Guangya Zhou and Chengkuo Lee, Subwavelength On-chip Light Focusing with Bigradient All-dielectric Metamaterials for Dense Photonic Integration,\nInfoMat\n, vol.4, no.2, e12264, 2022.\nJikai Xu,\nZhihao Ren\n, Bowei Dong, Xinmiao Liu, Chenxi Wang, Yanhong Tian, and Chengkuo Lee, Nanometer-Scale Heterogeneous Interfacial Sapphire Wafer-Bonding for Enabling Plasmonic-Enhanced Nanofluidic Mid-Infrared Spectroscopy,\nACS Nano\n, vol. 14, no.9, pp.12159-12172, 2020. (shared first authorship)\nZhihao Ren\n, Yuhua Chang, Yiming Ma, Kailing Shih, Bowei Dong and Chengkuo Lee, Leveraging of MEMS Technologies for Optical Metamaterials Applications,\nAdv. Optical Mater.\n, Vol. 8, 1900653, 2020.\nZHANG Zixuan\nReceived his B.Eng. degree from the School of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering at the University of Electronic Science and Technology of China (UESTC), Chengdu, China, in 2018. After that he received his M.Sc degree from Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at National University of Singapore in 2019. Currently, he is a Research Assistant in the Dept. of ECE, NUS. His research interests are focused on energy harvesters, self-powered sensors and triboelectric nanogenerator.\nArticles Published:\nZixuan Zhang\n, Luwei Wang, and Chengkuo Lee, Recent Advances in Artificial Intelligence Sensors,\nAdvanced Sensor Research\n, to be published, 2023.\nZixuan Zhang\n, Feng Wen, Zhongda Sun, Xinge Guo, Tianyiyi He, and Chengkuo Lee<, Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Sensing Technologies in the 5G/ Internet of Things Era : From Virtual Reality / Augmented Reality to the Digital Twin,\nAdv. Intell. Syst.\n, vol.4, no.7, 2100228, 2022\nZixuan Zhang\n, Qiongfeng Shi, Tianyiyi He, Xinge Guo, Bowei Dong, Jason Lee, and Chengkuo Lee, Artificial Intelligence of Toilet (AI-Toilet) for an Integrated Health Monitoring System (IHMS) using Smart Triboelectric Pressure Sensors and Image Sensor,\nNano Energy\n, vol. 90, Part A, 106517, 2021\nZixuan Zhang\n, Tianyiyi He, Minglu Zhu, Zhongda Sun, Qiongfeng Shi, Jianxiong Zhu, Bowei Dong, Mehmet Rasit Yuce, and Chengkuo Lee, Deep Learning Enabled Triboelectric Smart Socks for IoT Based Gait Analysis and VR Applications,\nnpj Flexible Electronics\n, Accepted for publication, 2020.\nJingkai Zhou,\nZixuan Zhang\n, Bowei Dong, Zhihao Ren, Weixin Liu, and Chengkuo Lee, Mid-infrared Spectroscopic Analysis of Aqueous Mixtures Using Artificial-Intelligence-Enhanced Metamaterial Waveguide Sensing Platform,\nACS Nano\n, vol. 17, no.1, 711-724, 2023.(shared first authorship)\nZhihao Ren, Zixuan Zhang, Jingxuan Wei, Bowei Dong, and Chengkuo Lee, Wavelength-multiplexed hook nanoantennas\r\n                                for machine learning enabled mid-infrared spectroscopy,\nNat. Commun.\n, vol. 13, 3859, 2022. (shared first authorship)\nFeng Wen,\nZixuan Zhang\n, Tianyiyi He, and  Chengkuo Lee, AI-enabled sign language recognition and VR-space bidirectional communication using triboelectric smart glove,\nNat. Commun.\n, vol.12, 5378, 2021. (shared first authorship)\nQiongfeng Shi,\nZixuan Zhang\n, Tao Chen, and Chengkuo Lee,\nMinimalist and Multi-Functional Human Machine Interface (HMI) Using A Flexible Wearable Triboelectric Patch\n,\nNano Energy,\nvol. 62, p.355-366, 2019. (shared first authorship)\nLIU Weixin\nReceived his B.Eng degree in Mechatronics Engineering from the School of Mechanical Engineering at Zhejiang University, Hangzhou, China, in 2019. He is currently a Research Assistant in the Dept. of ECE, NUS. His research interests focus mainly on MEMS piezoelectric resonant sensors and actuators.\nArticles Published:\nWeixin Liu\n, Yiming Ma, Xinmiao Liu, Jingkai Zhou, Cheng Xu, Bowei Dong, and Chengkuo Lee, Larger-Than-Unity External Optical Field Confinement Enabled by Metamaterial-Assisted Comb Waveguide for Ultrasensitive Long-Wave Infrared Gas Spectroscopy,\nNano Letters\n, vol. 22, no. 15, 6112-6120, 2022.\nWeixin Liu\n, Yiming Ma, Yuhua Chang, Bowei Dong, Jingxuan Wei, Zhihao Ren, and Chengkuo Lee, Suspended silicon waveguide platform with subwavelength grating metamaterial cladding for long wave infrared sensing applications,\nNanophotonics.\n, vol. 10, no. 7, 1861-1870, 2021.\nXU Yunlong\nReceived his M.Sc. degree at Jiangnan University, Wuxi, China, in 2019. After that he received his PhD degree at Donghua University, Shanghai, China. He is an associate investigator starting in Feb. 2025. His research interests are focused on advanced wearable sensors.\nArticles Published:\nYunlong Xu\n, Zhongda Sun, Zhiqing Bai, Hua Shen, Run Wen, Fumei Wang, Guangbiao Xu and Chengkuo Lee, Bionic E-skin with Precise Multi-Directional Droplet Sliding Sensing for Enhanced Robotic Perception,\nNat. Commun.\n, vol. 15, 6022, 2024.\nHONG Jianlong\nReceived his B. Sc. degree and Ph. D. degree from the School of Electronic Science and Engineering at the Southeast University (SEU), Nanjing, China in 2025. He is now a Research Fellow at the Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering, NUS. His research interests are focused on wearable AI sensors and e-skin.\nWAN Zhen\nReceived his B.Eng. degree from the School of Mechano-Electronic Engineering at Xidian University, Xi'an, China, in 2019. After that, he received his Ph.D. degree from the School of Instrumentation and Optoelectronic Engineering at Beihang University (BUAA), Chinai, in 2025. Then, he joined NTU a Research Fellow, in 2025. He is currently a Research Fellow in the Dept. of ECE, NUS. His research interests are focused on in-sensor computing and MEMS resonant sensors.\nPh.D. Candidates/Students\nWANG Luwei\nPh.D. Candidate / Self-finance / Aug., 2022\nReceived her B.Eng. degree in Electronic Science and Technology at Shenzhen University, China, in 2021. After that she received her M.Sc degree from the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE), National University of Singapore (NUS), in 2022. She is currently a Research Engineer in the Department of ECE, NUS. Her research interests are focused on neuromorphic computing and smart sensor systems.\nXIAO Zian\nPh.D. Candidate / Self-finance / Aug., 2022\nReceived his B.Eng. degree from the School of Electronic and Information at Soochow University, Suzhou, China, in 2020. Then he worked at HiSilicon, Huawei as an ASIC verification and test engineer. He is currently a Research Engineer in the Department of ECE, NUS. His research interests are focused on specific integrated photonics circuits for artificial intelligence.\nZHUGE Yangyang\nPh.D. Candidate / Self-finance / Aug., 2023\nReceived his B.Eng. degree in Communication Engineering from Soochow University, China, in 2022, and M.Sc. degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) from National University of Singapore (NUS), in 2023. He is currently a Research Engineer in the Dept. of ECE, NUS. His research interests are focused on MIR photonics and photonic AI chips for computation applications.\nWANG Yinpeng\nPh.D. Candidate / Self-finance / Aug., 2023\nReceived the B.S. degree in Electronic and Information Engineering and the M.S. degree in Electronic Science and Technology both at Beihang University, Beijing, China in 2020 and 2023, respectively. He is currently a PhD student at the Department of ECE, NUS. His research interests focus mainly on MEMS metamaterials and deep learning techniques.\nXU Jinlong\nPh.D. Student / Self-finance / Aug., 2023\nReceived his B.Eng. degree in Communication Engineering at Jilin University, China, in 2022. After that he received his M.Sc degree from the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE), National University of Singapore...[truncated]"
  },
