    "homepage_text": "Ming-Liang Zhang's Home Page\nMing-Liang Zhang (张明亮)\nResearch Scientist/Staff Engineer\nFuture Living Lab, Taobao and Tmall Group, Alibaba\nAbout me\nI work as a Research Scientist/Staff Engineer at Alibaba now in Beijing, collaborating with Dr. Jun Song. I received my Ph.D. degree from the Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences under the supervision of Professor Cheng-Lin Liu. My recent research interests include Multimodal Large Language Model, Multimodal Mathmatical Reasoning, Scene Parsing etc.\nNews\n[05/2024] One co-author paper accepted by ACL-24\n[05/2024] One co-first-author paper accepted by ACL-24\n[06/2023] Glad and honored to join Baidu as a research intern\n[04/2023] One first-author paper accepted by IJCAI-23\n[11/2022] One first-author paper accepted  to the 2nd MATH-AI Workshop at NeurIPS 2022\n[09/2022] One first-author paper accepted by Journal of Pattern Recognition\n[07/2022] One co-author paper accepted by ICPR-22\n[04/2022] One first-author paper accepted by IJCAI-22\n[12/2021] Pleased to join SenseTime as a research intern\nEducation\nInstitute of Automation of Chinese Academy of Sciences (CASIA)\nSep. 2018 - Jan. 2024\nPhD in Pattern Recognition and Intelligent Systems\nChina, Beijing\nHefei University of Technology (HFUT)\nSep. 2014 - Jul. 2018\nB.E. in Information and Computing Science\nChina, Hefei\nSelected Publications\nGeoEval: Benchmark for Evaluating LLMs and Multi-Modal Models on Geometry Problem-Solving\nJiaxin Zhang, Zhong-Zhi Li, Ming-Liang Zhang, Fei Yin, Cheng-Lin Liu, Yashar Moshfeghi\nAccepted by the Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL-24). [\nPaper\n]\nLANS: A Layout-Aware Neural Solver for Plane Geometry Problem\nZhong-Zhi Li, Ming-Liang Zhang*, Fei Yin and Cheng-Lin Liu\nAccepted by the Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL-24). [\nPaper\n]\nA Multi-Modal Neural Geometric Solver with Textual Clauses Parsed from Diagram\nMing-Liang Zhang, Fei Yin and Cheng-Lin Liu\nAccepted by the 32nd International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI-23). [\nPaper\n][\nCode\n][\nDataset\n]\nLearning to Understand Plane Geometry Diagram\nMing-Liang Zhang, Fei Yin, Yi-Han Hao and Cheng-Lin Liu\nAccepted by the 2nd MATH-AI Workshop at NeurIPS 2022. [\nPaper\n][\nVideo\n]\nTowards prior gap and representation gap for long-tailed recognition\nMing-Liang Zhang, Xu-Yao Zhang, Chuang Wang, Cheng-Lin Liu\nAccepted by the Journal of Pattern Recognition. [\nPaper\n]\nPGDP5K: A Diagram Parsing Dataset for Plane Geometry Problems\nYihan Hao, Ming-Liang Zhang, Fei Yin and Lin-Lin Huang\nAccepted by the 26th International Conference on Pattern Recognition (ICPR-22). [\nPaper\n]\nPlane Geometry Diagram Parsing\nMing-Liang Zhang, Fei Yin, Yi-Han Hao and Cheng-Lin Liu\nAccepted by the 31nd International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI-22). [\nPaper\n][\nCode\n][\nDataset\n][\nVideo\n]\nSelected Competition\nCVPR 2020 workshop: AliProducts Challenge: Large-scale Product Recognition\nMing-Liang Zhang, Baole Wei and Yirong Yang\nTeam Name\n: UCASTAR\nRanking\n: 5 / 688 [\nReport\n][\nCode\n]\nCCF 2019 Big Data & Computing Intelligence Contest: ID Card Elements Extraction based on OCR\nMing-Liang Zhang, Baole Wei, Chen Du and Jingzhong Jiang\nTeam Name\n: 民间 baseline\nRanking\n: 5 / 1727 [\nReport\n]\n2017 America Mathematical Contest In Modeling (MCM)\nYujie Sun, Mingliang Zhang and Teng Sun\nFaculty Advisor\n: Xianfa Jiao\nRanking\n: Meritorious Winner (for top 5% teams)\nExperience\nInternship |\nBaidu Search Strategy Lab\nAdvisor\n:\nLingyong Yan\nJun. 2023 - Sep. 2023, Beijing, China\nTeaching Assistant |\nUCAS, School of Artificial Intelligence\nAdvisor\n: Prof.\nCheng-Lin Liu\nPattern recognition 22-23 Autumn, 081100M01001H\nSep. 2022 - Jan. 2023, Beijing, China\nInternship |\nSenseTime AI Lab\nAdvisor\n:\nYichao Wu\nDec. 2021 - Feb. 2022, Beijing, China\nVisiting Student |\nCASIA\nAdvisor\n: Prof.\nChunheng Wang\nThe State Key Laboratory of Management and Control for Complex Systems\nFeb. 2018 - Jun. 2018, Beijing, China\nAcademic Service\nReviewer,\nIEEE Trans. Image Processing\nReviewer, PRCV\n2022\n/\n2023\nReviewer,\nInternational Journal on Document \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAnalysis and Recognition (IJDAR)\nSelected Honors\nRuwei Dai Scholarship, 2023\nOutstanding Undergraduate, Anhui, 2018\nNational Scholarship (for top 1% students), 2016\nNational Scholarship (for top 1% students), 2015\n© Ming-Liang Zhang | Last updated: Dec. 2023"
