    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nWentao Wang (王文韬), Ph.D.\nAssistant Research Scientist\nDept. of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nUniversity of Michigan, Ann Arbor\n2160 G. G. Brown Building,\n2350 Hayward St, Ann Arbor, MI 48109\nEmail:\nwangwent@umich.edu\nTel:(+1)734-647-5572\nDr. Wentao Wang is currently a research faculty in the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, MI, United States. He received his Ph.D. degree in 2016 from Harbin Institute of Technology, supervised by\nProf. Hui Li\nand\nProf. Jerome P. Lynch\n. His CV is attached.\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nAssistant Research Scientist\nJun\n.\n2021\n–\npresent\nDepartment of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nUniversity of Michigan, Ann Arbor\nResearch Investigator\nJan\n. 20\n2\n0 –\nMay\n.\n2021\nDepartment of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nUniversity of Michigan, Ann Arbor\n(Postdoctoral) Research Fellow\nJan\n.\n2017\n–\nDec\n.\n2019\nDepartment of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nUniversity of Michigan, Ann Arbor\nRESEARCH\nStructural health monitoring (SHM), Non-destructive testing/evaluation (NDE/T), Acoustic emission (AE) technique, Ultrasonic testing, Lamb wave, SH wave, earthquake and etc.\nDamage detection and risk assessment in drinking water system including transient modelling and assessment of pipe structural capacity;\nCompressive sensing (CS), Digital signal processing, Wavelet transform, Support vector machine (SVM), Relevance vector machine (RVM), Deep mining, Big data and etc.\nd\n36\ntype wafer phased array, PZT wafer, Acoustic emission sensor, Ultrasonic probe and etc.\nSmart city, Wireless sensing, Edge computing, Neuron network.\nWearable sensor, Biocompatible prosthesis sensor development.\nMeta-materials, Meta-structures, Acoustic Meta-material.\nEDUCATION\nPh.D.\nin Civil Engineering                                                                         Sep. 2012 – Dec. 2016\nHARBIN INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY(HIT), Harbin, CHINA\nTotal GPA:90.0/100 (3.87/4)     Rank:1/23\nM.S.\nin Disaster Prevention and Mitigation Engineering                       Sep. 2010 – Jul. 2012\nHARBIN INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY(HIT), Harbin, CHINA\nTotal GPA:83.5/100 (3.69/4)     Rank:6/198\nB.S.\nin Engineering Mechanics                                                                   Sep. 2006 – Jul. 2010\nHARBIN INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY(HIT), Harbin, CHINA\nTotal GPA:88.1/100 (3.72/4)     Rank:1/44\nHONORS & AWARDS\n2007\nNational Endeavor Fellowship of China (National level)\nExcellent student of Harbin Institute of Technology\n2008\nThomas T. C. Hsu Scholarship of Honors School\nFirst prize of people scholarship of Honors School\nExcellent student of Harbin Institute of Technology\n2009\nNational Scholarship of China (National level)\nFirst prize of people scholarship of Honors School\nSecond prize of National College Students Innovation Experiment Program\n2010\nThomas T. C. Hsu Scholarship of Honors School\nExcellent student of Harbin Institute of Technology\n‘Best student dissertation’ of Harbin Institute of Technology\n2011\nFirst prize of postgraduate student scholarship of Harbin Institute of Technology\nExcellent student of Harbin Institute of Technology\n2012\n1st Place of Structure control and SHM competition in APSS\n(Asia-Pacific Summer School)\nExcellent graduates of Harbin Institute of Technology\n2013\nGuanghua Scholarship of Graduate student\nExcellent student of Harbin Institute of Technology\n2014\nOutstanding student leaders of Harbin Institute of Technology\n2015\nNational Scholarship of China of Graduate student (National level)\nExcellent student of Heilongjiang Province (Provincial level)\n2016\nExcellent graduates of Harbin Institute of Technology\n2022-2023 University of Michigan, College of Engineering Outstanding Research Scientist Award (\nNomination\n)\nACTIVITIES\n2011 The 6\nth\nInternational Workshop on Advanced Smart Materials and Smart Structures Technology (ANCRiSST-2011), Dalian, China\n2012 Asia-Pacific Summer School of Smart Structures Technology (APSS-2012), Bangalore, India\n2013 Proceeding of the SPIE, San Diego, California, US\n2015-2016 Visiting student in University of Michigan supported by China Scholarship Counsil (CSC).\n2017.03 Proceeding of SPIE, NDE and Health Monitoring, Portland, OR, United States\n2017.09 IWSHM-2017, Stanford, California, United States\n2017.10 “Fitbit-style prosthetics? Navy developing 'smart' artificial limbs” (\nLink\n)\n2017.11 Invited Seminar : “Guided Wave Based Sensing Approaches for Structural Health Monitoring (SHM)”\n2018.03 Proceeding of the SPIE, Smart Structures+ Nondestructive Evaluation, Denver, CO, United States\n2019.09 The 12th International Workshop on Structural Health Monitoring, Stanford, CA\n2018.07-2020.05 Serves as the Guest Editor of Sensors, an International Journal\n2021.01-now Serves as the Guest Editor of Sensors, with a Special Issue \"Smart Sensors and Machine Learning Technique for Damage Detection and Visualization\"\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
