    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jiwoong-lee-571b9b70",
    "homepage_text": "Jiwoong Lee\n      -  University of Copenhagen Research Portal\nUniversity of Copenhagen Research Portal Home\nHelp & FAQ\nLink opens in a new tab\nDansk\nEnglish\nSearch content at University of Copenhagen Research Portal\nJiwoong Lee\nAssociate Professor - Promotion Programme\n,\nDepartment of Chemistry\n,\nDepartment of Chemistry\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0001-6177-4569\nPhone\n+4535333312, +4593565534\nEmail\njiwoong.lee\nchem.ku\ndk\nWebsite\nhttps://researchprofiles.ku.dk/da/persons/jiwoong-lee\nUniversitetsparken 5\n2100\nKøbenhavn Ø\nPersonal profile\nShort presentation\nPI, The Novo Nordisk CO\n2\nResearch Center (2022-)\nAssociate professor (full professor promotion program), Department of Chemistry, University of Copenhagen (2021-)\nAssistant professor (tenure-track), Department of Chemistry, University of Copenhagen (2016-2021)\nPostdoctoral Researcher with Prof. Jeffrey R. Long, University of California, Berkeley (2015-2016)\nPostdoctoral Researcher with Prof. Rafal Klajn, Weizmann Institute of Science, Israel (2014)\nPh.D. (Dr. rer. nat, summa cum laude) with Prof. Benjamin List, Max-Planck-Institut für Kohlenforschung, Germany (2013)\nM. Sc. and B. Sc. in Chemistry with Prof. Choong Eui Song, Sungkyunkwan University, Korea (2009)\nResearch Interests\n-\nHomogeneous and Heterogeneous catalysis\nSpecific themes in my research career include asymmetric catalysis, organic synthesis, and heterogeneous catalysis using chiral organocatalysts, organometallic complexes, nanoscale materials such as nanoparticles and metal-organic frameworks to develop methodologies of CO2 capture and functionalization, desalination, water purification and fluorination.\nExternal positions\nCSO,\nGlyon ApS\n1 Aug 2024\n→ …\nCSO,\nCowatech ApS\n1 Jan 2019\n→\n1 Feb 2023\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n52\nJournal article\n4\nLetter\n4\nReview\n2\nBook chapter\n1\nMore\n1\nEditorial\nCarbon Dioxide-Mediated Chemical Processes in Aqueous Solutions\nKustiana, B. A., Ayyar, A. S. R.,\nSowers, A. J.\n,\nAdelodun, A. A.\n,\nPoderyte, M.\n&\nLee, J. W.\n,\n2026\n, (Accepted/In press)\nIn:\nChemistry - A European Journal.\ne03287.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nJournal article\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nNonporous hydrophobic organic crystals for carbon dioxide capture via chain-melting phase transition\nPetrović, A.\n,\nLima, R. J. D. S.\n, Hadaf, G. B., Lanza, A., Aalestrup, K., Olesen, K. L. L., Juhl, D. W., Nielsen, N. C.,\nAdelodun, A. A.\n,\nBordallo, H. N.\n, Daasbjerg, K. &\nLee, J.-W.\n,\n3 Feb 2026\n, (Accepted/In press)\nIn:\nNature Communications.\n30 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nJournal article\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\n1\nDownloads\n(Pure)\nA Prebiotic Route to Lactate from Acetaldehyde, Cyanide and Carbon Dioxide\nSharma, S., Yang, Y. &\nLee, J. W.\n,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nChemistry - A European Journal.\n31\n,\n11\n,\n6 p.\n, e202403763.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nJournal article\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\n1\nCitation\n(Scopus)\n9\nDownloads\n(Pure)\nComprehensive Analysis of Crystalline Hydrophobic Alkylated Poly(ethyleneimine)s\nAyyar, A. S.,\nLima, R. J. S.\n,\nAdelodun, A. A.\n, Nagorsen, B. L.,\nKirkensgaard, J. J. K.\n, Rudić, S.,\nBordallo, H. N.\n&\nLee, J.\n,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nChemistry: A European Journal.\n31\n,\n34\n,\n9 p.\n, e202500764 .\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nJournal article\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\n1\nCitation\n(Scopus)\n7\nDownloads\n(Pure)\nOpportunities for the renewable energy transition via reactive carbon capture\nKearns, E., Siegel, R. E., D'Alessandro, D. M.,\nLee, J.-W.\n& Berben, L. A.,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nChemical Society Reviews.\n54\n,\n9\n,\np. 4096-4103\n8 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nReview\n›\npeer-review\n3\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nPhysical aging of defect-free asymmetric functionalized PIM hollow fiber membranes\nJean-Baptiste, P., Ayyar, A.S.-R., Mattewal, S., Dean, P. A., Joo, T.,\nLee, J.-W.\n& Smith, Z. P.,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nJournal of Membrane Science.\n722\n,\n12 p.\n, 123875.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nJournal article\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\n3\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nRepurposing polyethylene terephthalate plastic waste to capture carbon dioxide\nPoderyte, M.\n, Lima, R.,\nGolbaekdal, P. I.\n, Juhl, D. W., Olesen, K. L., Nielsen, N. C., Lanza, A. &\nLee, J.-W.\n,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nScience Advances.\n11\n,\n36\n,\n9 p.\n, eadv5906.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nJournal article\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\n3\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nRevisiting the reactivity of carbon dioxide: from physical and chemical properties to reactive carbon capture\nLauridsen, J. M. V.\n&\nLee, J.-W.\n,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nChemical Society Reviews.\n54\n,\n15\n,\np. 7058-7066\n9 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nReview\n›\npeer-review\n4\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 63 research outputs"
