    "homepage_text": "Kang Li's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nKang Li's Homepage\nKang Li (李康)\nW1\nProfessor for Mathematics\nContact\nDepartment of Mathematics\nFriedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU)\nCauerstraße 11, 91058 Erlangen, Germany\nEmail:\nkang.li@fau.de\nORCID:\n0000-0003-0756-0396\nMy ResearchGate\nMy MathSciNet\nMy Google Scholar\nAbout Me\nMy name is\nKang Li\nand I am a Danish mathematician.\nI\nn January 2016 I\nreceived my Ph.D. in Mathematics from the University of Copenhagen under the supervision of\nUffe Haagerup\nand\nRyszard Nest\n. My previous employments are\nUniversity of Copenhagen,\nUniversity of Münster,\nPolish Academy of Sciences in Warsaw\nand\nKU Leuven.\nCurrently, I am a\nJunior Professor\nfor Mathematics in\nRepresentation Theory and\nOperator Algebras at\nDepartment of Mathematics\nof\nFriedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg\nin Germany. I am affiliated to the\nLie Groups\nleading by\nProf. Karl-Hermann Neeb\n. As of April 1, 2026, I will start my new position as Senior Lecturer in Mathematics at Lund University (kang.li@math.lth.se).\nMy main research area is Operator Algebras and their interactions with\nDynamical Systems,\nG\neometric\nG\nroup\nT\nheory\nand Representation Theory with the following topics:\nProperty A, coarse embedding and higher index theory in coarse geometry;\nApproximation properties for simple Lie groups and groupoid dynamical systems;\nThe Baum-Connes conjecture for algebraic groups;\nRigidity, structure and K-theor\ny of\nl\np\nuniform Roe algebras;\nIdeal structure and dimension theories for étale groupoid C*-algebras;\nRegularity and homology for\nétale\ngroupoids and groupoid models for classifiable C*-algebras;\nMeasured (asymptotic) expanders.\nBeides Mathematics, I spend my leisure time mostly on traveling, playing badminton and keyboard, watching movies, enjoying excellent beers and food,\nlearning languages\nsuch as\nChinese (\nN\native), Danish (\nF\nluent), English (Proficient), French (\nB\nasic), German (Conversant B2), Swedish (basic).\nResearch\n3\n5\n. (with\nLiang Guo and Qin Wang\n)\nK-theory of ghostly ideals for\nl\np\n-coarsely embeddable spaces\n,\narXiv:2511.22438\n, (202\n5\n),\nSubmitted\n34. (with Kevin Aguyar Brix, Chris Bruce and Eduardo Scarparo)\nMaximal ideals of reduced group C*-algebras and Thompson's groups\n,\narXiv:2403.13645\n, (2024),\nto appear in Transactions of the American Mathematical Society\n33.\n(with Jiawen Zhang)\nTracial states on groupoid C*-algebras and essential freeness\n,\narXiv:2401.15546\n, (2024), to appear in Journal of Noncommutative Geometry\n32. (with Xin Ma)\nNonfree almost finite actions for locally finite-by-virtually Z groups\n,\narXiv:2311.00649\n,\nJ. Lond. Math. Soc. (2) 110 (2024), no. 1, Paper No. e12959\n31. (with Christian Bönicke)\nNuclear dimension of subhomogeneous twisted groupoid C*-algebras and dynamic asymptotic dimension\n,\narXiv:2309.17178\n,\nInt. Math. Res. Not. IMRN (2024), no. 16, 11597–11610\n30. (with Hung-Chang Liao and Wilhelm Winter)\nThe diagonal dimension of sub-C*-algebras\n,\narXiv:2303.16762\n, (2023), Submitted\n29. (with Eduardo Scarparo)\nC*-irreducibility of commensurated subgroups\n,\narXiv:2210.00827\n,\nPacific J. Math. 322 (2023), no. 2, 369–380\n28. (with Xuanlong Fu and Huaxin Lin)\nTracial approximate divisibility and stable rank one\n,\narXiv:2108.08970\n,\nJ. Lond. Math. Soc. (2) 106 (2022), no. 4, 3008–3042\n27. (with Jorge Castillejos and Gabor Szabo)\nOn tracial Z-stability of simple non-unital C*-algebras\n,\narXiv:2108.08742\n, (2021),\nto appear in Canadian Journal of Mathematics\n26. (with Ján Špakula and Jiawen Zhang)\nMeasured expanders\n,\narXiv:2104.06052\n,\nJ. Topol. Anal. 16 (2024), no. 6, 917–944\n25. (with Ján Špakula and Jiawen Zhang)\nMeasured asymptotic expanders and rigidity for Roe algebras\n,\narXiv:2010.10749\n, Int. Math. Res. Not. IMRN (2023), no. 17, 15102–15154\n24. (with Federico Vigolo and Jiawen Zhang)\nA Markovian and Roe-algebraic approach to asymptotic expansion in measure\n,\narXiv:2008.12572\n, Banach Journal of Mathematical Analysis, 17, no. 74, 2023\n23. (with Massoud Amini, Damian Sawicki and Ali Shakibazadeh)\nDynamic asymptotic dimension for actions of virtually cyclic groups\n,\narXiv:2007.00960\n, Proceedings of the Edinburgh Mathematical Society 64 (2), 364–372\n(2021)\n22. (with Piotr Nowak and Sanaz Pooya)\nHigher Kazhdan projections,\nl\n2\n-Betti numbers and Baum-Connes conjectures\n,\narXiv:2006.09317\n, J. Noncommut. Geom. 18 (2024), no. 1, 313–336\n21. (with Federico Vigolo and Jiawen Zhang)\nAsymptotic expansion in measure and strong ergodicity\n,\narXiv:2005.05697\n, J. Topol. Anal. 15 (2023), no. 2, 361–399\n20. (with Bartosz K. Kwaśniewski and Adam Skalski)\nThe Haagerup property for twisted groupoid dynamical systems\n,\narXiv:2004.06317\n, Journal of Functional Analysis 283 (2022) 109484\n19. (with Pere Ara, Christian Bönicke and Joan Bosa)\nStrict comparison for C*-algebras arising from almost finite groupoids\n,\narXiv:2002.12221\n, Banach J. Math. Anal. 14, 1692–1710 (2020)\n18. (with Pere Ara, Christian Bönicke and Joan Bosa)\nThe type semigroup, comparison, and almost finiteness for ample groupoids\n,\narXiv:2001.00376\n, Ergodic Theory Dynam. Systems 43 (2023), no. 2, 361–400\n17. (with Ana Khukhro, Federico Vigolo and Jiawen Zhang)\nOn the structure of asymptotic expanders\n,\narXiv:1910.13320\n, Advances in Mathematics 393 (2021) 108073\n16. (with Piotr Nowak, Ján Špakula and Jiawen Zhang)\nQuasi-local algebras and asymptotic expanders\n,\narXiv:1908.07814\n, Groups Geom. Dyn. 15 (2021), 655–682\n15. (with Bruno M. Braga and Yeong Chyuan Chung)\nCoarse Baum-Connes conjecture and rigidity for Roe algebras\n,\narXiv:1907.10237\n, J. Funct. Anal. 279 (2020), no. 9, 108728\n14. (with Yeong Chyuan Chung)\nStructure and K-theory of\nl\np\nuniform Roe algebras\n,\narXiv:1904.07050\n, J. Noncommut. Geom. 15 (2021), 581–614\n13. (with Zhijie Wang and Jiawen Zhang)\nA quasi-local characterisation of\nL\np\n-Roe algebras\n,\narXiv:1808.08593\n, J. Math. Anal. Appl. 474 (2019), no. 2, 1213-1237\n12. (with Yeong Chyuan Chung)\nRigidity of\nl\np\nRoe-type algebras\n,\narXiv:1802.08921\n, Bull. London Math. Soc. (6) 50 (2018), 1056–1070\n11. (with Christian Bönicke)\nIdeal structure and pure infiniteness of ample groupoid C*-algebras\n,\narXiv:1707.03740\n, Ergodic Theory Dynam. Systems 40 (2020), no. 1, 34–63\n10. (with Rufus Willett)\nLow-dimensional properties of uniform Roe algebras\n,\narXiv:1705.01290\n, J. London Math. Soc. (2) 97 (2018), 98–124\n9. (with Hung-Chang Liao)\nClassification of uniform Roe algebras of locally finite groups\n,\narXiv:1705.03716\n, J. Operator Theory 80 (2018), no. 1, 25–46\n8. (with Siegfried Echterhoff and Ryszard Nest)\nThe orbit method for the Baum-Connes conjecture for algebraic groups over local function fields\n,\narXiv:1704.08548\n, J. Lie Theory 28 (2018), no. 2, 323-341\n7. (with Pere Ara, Fernando Lledó and Jianchao Wu)\nAmenability and uniform Roe algebras\n,\narXiv:1706.04875\n, J. Math. Anal. Appl. 459 (2018), no. 2, 686–716\n6. (with Pere Ara, Fernando Lledó and Jianchao Wu)\nAmenability of coarse spaces and K-algebras\n,\narXiv:1607.00328\n, Bull. Math. Sci. 8 (2018), no. 2, 257-306\n5. (with Jacek Brodzki and Chris Cave)\nExactness of locally compact groups\n,\narXiv:1603.01829\n, Adv. Math. 312 (2017), 209-233\n4. (with Søren Knudby)\nA Schur multiplier characterization of coarse embeddability\n,\narXiv:1505.01364\n, Bull. Belg. Math. Soc. Simon Stevin 22 (2015), no. 3, 403-409\n3. (with Søren Knudby)\nApproximation properties of simple Lie groups made discrete\n,\narXiv:1408.5238v2\n, J. Lie Theory 25 (2015), no. 4, 985-1001\n2. (with Steven Deprez)\nPermanence properties of property A and coarse embeddability for locally compact groups\n,\narXiv:1403.7111\n, (2014)\n1. (with Steven Deprez)\nProperty A and uniform embedding for locally compact groups\n,\narXiv:1309.7290\n, J. Noncommut. Geom. 9 (2015), no. 3, 797-819\nUpcoming Talks in 2026\nTBD\n,\nScandinavian Operator Algebra Workshop\nat Lund University, Sweden, June 8\n-\n9, 2026\nTBD\n, Workshop \"\nGroups and Operator Algebras\n\" at SwissMAP research station at Les Diablerets, Switzerland, June 14 - 19, 2026\nTheses\nProperty A and coarse embedding for locally compact groups\n(Ph.D. Thesis, Advisors:\nRyszard Nest\nand\nUffe Haagerup\n)\nIntroduction to Deformation/Rigidity Theory for II\n1\nFactors\n(Master Thesis, Advisors:\nSteven Deprez\nand\nUffe Haagerup\n)\nThe Baum-Connes Conjecture with Coefficients\n(Graduate Course Project, Advisor:\nRyszard Nest\n)\nExact C*-Algebras\n(Bachelor Thesis, Advisor:\nMikael Rørdam\n)\nTeaching\n2008, Block 1: Introduction to Mathematics.\n2008, Block 2: Linear Algebra.\n2012, Block 4: Introduction to Non-commutative Geometry.\n2012, Block 1: Introduction to Mathematics.\n2012, Block 2: Linear Algebra.\n2013, Block 1: Introduction to Mathematics.\n2013, Block 2: Linear Algebra.\n2014, Block 1: Introduction to Mathematics.\n2014, Block 2: Linear Algebra.\n2015, Block 2: Linear Algebra.\n2021, Spring: Operator Algebras.\n2021, Winter: Introduction to Operator Algebras.\n2022, Summer: Introduction to Abstract Harmonic Analysis.\n202\n2\n, Winter:\nCurves and surfaces.\n2022, Winter:\nR\neading\nS\neminar \"Unitary representation theory for groups and C*-algebras\".\n2023,\nSummer\n: Topologie\n.\n2023, Winter: Bachelor Seminar \"Topics in Topology\n\".\n2024,\nSummer:\nInterdisciplinary module \"Topologie und Anwendungen\".\n2024, Winter:\nInterdisciplinary Bachelor Seminar \"Topolog\ny\n\".\n2025, Summer:\nIntroduction to Operator Algebras.\n2025, Summer: Bachelor Seminar \"\nAmenable Groups\n\".\n2025,\nWinter:\nFunctional Analysis II\n.\n2026, Spring:\nIntroduction to Operator Algebras.\nBA Supervision\nBachelor Thesis Advisor for Lennard Kossmann “\nMackey Machine and Unitary Duals\n” at FAU, 28 August 2023.\nBachelor Thesis Advisor for Luciano Melodia “\nAlgebraic and Topological Persistence\n” at FAU, 08 October 2024.\nBachelor Thesis Advisor for Jonas Schindhelm “\nThe Künneth Formula for Cohomology Rings\n” at FAU, 20 November 2024.\nBachelor Thesis Advisor for Peter Langer “\nThe Banach-Tarski Paradox and\namenable groups\n” at FAU,\n03 February 2025.\nBachelor Th...[truncated]"
