    "homepage_text": "Home | Yiyang Zhao\nYiyang Zhao(èµµä¸é³)\nResearch Scientist,\nMeta\nEmail: zyyaoiang@gmail.com\n🎓  About Me\nMy name is Yiyang Zhao (èµµä¸é³ in chinese), I am a Research Scientist at\nMeta\n. I completed my Ph.D in\nWorcester Polytechnic Institute (WPI)\n, advised by Prof.\nTian Guo\n. My Ph.D dissertation is available\nhere\n.\n                I was born in Tsingtao (China). Before joining to WPI, I earned my bachelor degree in Electronic and Information Engineering from\nXidian University\n(Xi'an, China),\n                and my master degree in Computer Engineering from\nNortheastern University\n(Boston, U.S.A.).\nI am a big fan of computer game and enjoy designing and programming them. Additionally, I am a good amateur pianist, and I love playing basketball and traveling.\n                I like technology, I like artificial intelligence, I like cute puppy and I love my life.\nHere\nis my CV.\n💫 Interests\nDesigning deep learning (DL) models is typically reserved for experts. My primary research interest is to bridge the gap between everyday life and the field of artificial intelligence (AI), making AI and DL accessible to everybody through the use of\nNeural Architecture Search (NAS)\n.\n       I am also interested in application in machine learning and large language models.\n📖 Selected Publications\nYiyang Zhao\n, Yunzhuo Liu, Bo Jiang, Tian Guo\nCE-NAS: An End-to-End Carbon-Efficient Neural Architecture Search Framework\n38th Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS 2024\n)\nPaper\nÂ·\nCode\nÂ·\nPoster\nÂ·\nSlides\nYiyang Zhao\n, Linnan Wang, Tian Guo\nMulti-Objective Neural Architecture Search by Learning Search Space Partitions\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (\nJMLR 2024\n)\nPaper\nÂ·\nCode\nYiyang Zhao\n, Linnan Wang, Kevin Yang, Tianjun Zhang, Tian Guo, Yuandong Tian\nMulti-Objective Optimization by Learning Space Partitions\n10th International Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR 2022\n)\nPaper\nÂ·\nCode\nÂ·\nPoster\nÂ·\nç¥ä¹ä¸æ \nYiyang Zhao*\n, Linnan Wang*, Yuandong Tian, Rodrigo Fonseca, Tian Guo\nFew-shot Neural Architecture Search\n38th International Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML 2021\n)\nLong Oral\nPaper\nÂ·\nCode\nÂ·\nFAIR Blog\nÂ·\nPoster\nÂ·\næºå¨ä¹å¿\nLinnan Wang*,\nYiyang Zhao*(equally contributed)\n, Yuu Jinnai, Yuandong Tian, and Rodrigo Fonseca\nNeural Architecture Search using Deep Neural Networks and Monte Carlo Tree Search\n34th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI 2020\n)\nPaper\nÂ·\nCode\nÂ·\nPoster\nMore Publications >>>\n🎞 Work Experiences\nHTML Example\nResearch Scientist\nMeta\n2024.7 - present\nMenlo Park, California, United States\nDeep Learning Algorithm Engineering Intern\nNVIDIA\n2022.5 - 2022.8\nSanta Clara, California, United States\nResearch Intern\nTiktok\n2021.5 - 2021.8\nNew York, New York, United States\nÂ© Yiyang Zhao Last Updated: August 16, 2024."
