    "homepage_text": "Xuebin Zheng--Shanghai Institute of Ceramics, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nContact Us\nChinese\nCAS\nContact Us\nChinese\nCAS\nToggle navigation\nHome\nAbout Us\nHistory\nDirectors\nOrganization Structure\nContact Us\nNews\nResearch\nState Key Laboratory of High Performance Ceramics\nState Key Laboratory of Functional Crystals and Devices\nThe Frontier Department\nStructural Ceramics and Composite Materials\nInformation Functional Materials and Devices\nInorganic Coating Materials\nArtificial Crystal\nTransparent Ceramics\nEnergy Materials\nBiomaterials and Tissue Engineering\nAncient Ceramics and Industrial Ceramics\nPilot Test for New Materials\nPeople\nAcademicians\nFaculty and Staff\nInternational Cooperation\nInternational Conferences\nPresidentâs International Fellowship Initiative\nEducation\nEnrollment Guide\nAcademic Activities\nNews and Activities\nContact Us\nJournals\nLinks\nXuebin Zheng\nPh.D\nAcademic title:\nProfessor\nPhone:\n021-52414104, 69163711\nE-mail:\nxbzheng@mail.sic.ac.cn\nAddress:\n1295 Dingxi Road, Shanghai, P.R.China\nPostal Code:\n200050\nWebsite:\n-\nResume:\nProf. Xuebin Zheng was born in Zhejiang Province of China in 1971. He received his Bachelor degree of Chemistry in 1992 from Fudan University and obtained Ph.D. degree of Material Science in 2000 from Shanghai Institute of Ceramics, Chinese Academy of Science (SICCAS). He was appointed as assistant professor (2000) and associate professor (2002) in SICCAS. Now he is a professor and the director of Research Group of Plasma Sprayed Coatings. His current major research interests are biomedical coatings and protective coatings. Bioactivity, biocompatibility, osseointegration as well as antibacterial effect of the coating materials are carried out in his group. More than 200 scientific papers have been published in the scientific journals including\nBiomaterials, Acta Biomaterialia, Journal of Biomedical Materials Research, Surface & Coatings Technology,\netc. by his research group. Besides basic research, he cooperates with the companies of orthopedic implants for the development of better human medical products. His group successfully applies vacuum plasma spray (VPS) technology to manufacture porous Ti coating and bioactive HA coating on orthopedic implants. More than 300,000 bone substitutes (artificial hip joints, spinal implants, etc.) with VPS Ti coating or/and HA coating have been manufactured and applied clinically in these years.\nCopyright © SHANGHAI INSTITUTE OF CERAMICS CHINESE ACADEMY OF SCIENCES\næ²ªICPå¤05005480å·-1\næ²ªå¬ç½å®å¤ 31010502006565å·"
  },
  "serper::Junyuan Hong": {
