    "homepage_text": "Haoyu Ma, UCI\nHaoyu Ma\nResearch Scientist @GenAI, Meta\nEmail\n: haoyum3 [at] uci [dot] edu\nAbout Me\nI am a Research Scientist at GenAI, Meta. Previously, I obtained my PhD degree from\nDonald Bren School of Information and Computer Sciences\n,  UC Irvine in 2024, supervised by\nProf. Xiaohui Xie\n. I obtained my B.Eng degree from\nSoutheast University (SEU)\n, Nanjing, China in 2019.\nMy research interests are deep learning and computer vision.\nNews\n02/2025: Two papers are accepted by CVPR 2025.\n10/2024: We launched\nMovie Gen\n. Please see our\ntechnical report\nfor more details!\n07/2024: We launched\nImagine Yourself\n. Try it in IG, Messenger, and\nmeta.ai\n03/2024: I joined GenAI, Meta as a research scientist\n03/2024: I earned my PhD degree from University California, Irvine\n02/2024: Two papers are accepted by CVPR 2024.\n11/2023: One paper is accepted by CPAL 2024.\n10/2023: Three papers are accepted by WACV 2024.\n11/2022: One paper is accepted by AAAI 2023.\n07/2022: Two papers are accepted by ECCV 2022.\n05/2022: One paper is accepted by ICML 2022.\n03/2022: One paper is accepted by ICLR-PAIR2Struct 2022.\n03/2022: One paper is accepted by CVPR 2022.\n10/2021: One paper is accepted by BMVC 2021.\n05/2021: One paper is accepted by KDD 2021.\n01/2021: One paper is accepted by ICLR 2021 (Spotlight).\n08/2020: One paper is accepted by BMVC 2020 (Oral).\n11/2019: Two papers are accepted by WACV 2020.\nSelected Publications [\nFull List\n]\nMoCha: Towards Movie-Grade Talking Character Synthesis\nC. Wei, B. Sun,\nH. Ma\n, J. Hou, F. Xu, Z. He, X. Dai, L. Zhang, K. Li, T. Hou, A. Sinha, P. Vajda, W. Chen\nPreprint, 2025.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nMovie Weaver: Tuning-Free Multi-Concept Video Personalization with Anchored Prompts\nF. Liang,\nH. Ma\n, Z. He, T. Hou, J. Hou, K. Li, X. Dai, F. Xu, S. Azadi, A. Sinha, P. Zhang, P. Vajda, D. Marculescu\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference (\nCVPR\n), 2025.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nHOIGPT: Learning Long-Sequence Hand-Object Interaction with Language Models\nM. Huang, FJ. Chu, B. Tekin, K. Liang,\nH. Ma\n, W. Wang, X. Chen, P. Gleize, H. Xue, S. Lyu, K. Kitani, M. Feiszli, H. Tang\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference (\nCVPR\n), 2025.\n[\nPaper\n]\nMovie Gen: A Cast of Media Foundation Models\nCore Contributor\nPreprint, 2024.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nImagine yourself: Tuning-Free Personalized Image Generation\nZ. He , B. Sun , F. Xu,\nH. Ma\n, A. Ramchandani, V. Cheung, S. Shah, A. Kalia, N. Zhang, P. Zhang, R. Sumbaly, P. Vajda, A. Sinha\nPreprint, 2024.\n[\nPaper\n]\nMaskINT: Video Editing via Interpolative Non-autoregressive Masked Transformers\nH. Ma\n, S. Mahdizadehaghdam, B. Wu, Z. Fan, Y. Gu, Z. Zhao, L. Shapira and X. Xie\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference (\nCVPR\n), 2024.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nHRBP: Hardware-friendly Regrouping towards Block-based Pruning for Sparse CNN Training\nH. Ma\n, C. Zhang, L. Xiang, X. Ma, G. Yuan, W. Zhang, S. Liu, T. Chen, D. Tao, Y. Wang, Z. Wang, and X. Xie\nConference on Parsimony and Learning (\nCPAL\n), 2024.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n] [\nSlides\n]\nCVTHead: One-shot Controllable Head Avatar with Vertex-feature Transformer\nH. Ma\n, T. Zhang, S. Sun, X. Yan, K. Han, and X. Xie\nIEEE Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (\nWACV\n), 2024.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nSlides\n]\nLight Field Diffusion for Single-View Novel View Synthesis\nY. Xiong,\nH. Ma\n, S. Sun, K. Han, H. Tang, and X. Xie\nArxiv Preprint, 2023.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nPeeling the Onion: Hierarchical Reduction of Data Redundancy for Efficient Vision Transformer Training\nZ. Kong*,\nH. Ma*\n, G. Yuan*, M. Sun, Y. Xie, P. Dong, X. Meng, X. Shen, H. Tang, M. Qin, T. Chen, X. Ma, X. Xie, Z. Wang, and Y. Wang\nThirty-Seventh AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n), 2023.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n]\nPPT: token-Pruned Pose Transformer for monocular and multi-view human pose estimation\nH. Ma\n, Z. Wang, Y. Chen, D. Kong, L. Chen, X. Liu, X. Yan, H. Tang, and X. Xie\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (\nECCV\n), 2022.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n]\nTraining Your Sparse Neural Network Better with Any Mask\nA. Jaiswal,\nH. Ma\n, T. Chen, Y. Ding, and Z. Wang\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2022.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n]\nEI-CLIP: Entity-aware Interventional Contrastive Learning for E-commerce Cross-modal Retrieval\nH. Ma\n, H. Zhao, Z. Lin, A. Kale, Z. Wang, T. Yu, J. Gu, S. Choudhary, and X. Xie\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference (\nCVPR\n), 2022.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nPoster\n]\nSparse Logits Suffice to Fail Knowledge Distillation\nH. Ma\n, Y. Huang. H. Tang, C. You, D. Kong, and X. Xie\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)  Workshop on PAIR^2Struct, 2022\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n]\nTransFusion: Cross-view Fusion with Transformer for 3D Human Pose Estimation\nH. Ma\n, L. chen, D. Kong, Z. Wang, X. Liu, H. Tang, X. Yan, Y. Xie, S. Lin, and X. Xie\nBritish Machine Vision Virtual Conference (\nBMVC\n), 2021.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPresentation\n] [\nSlides\n]\nPD-Net: Quantitative Motor Function Evaluation for Parkinson's Disease via Automated Hand Gesture Analysis\nY. Chen,\nH. Ma\n, J. Wang, J. Wu, X. Wu, and X. Xie\nProceedings of the 27th ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (\nKDD\n), 2021.\n[\nPaper\n]\nUndistillable: Making A Nasty Teacher That CANNOT Teach Students\nH. Ma\n, T. Chen, T. Hu, C. You, X. Xie, and Z. Wang\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2021.\n(Spotlight)\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPresentation\n] [\nSlides\n] [\nPoster\n]\nSIA-GCN: A Spatial Information Aware Graph Neural Network with 2D Convolutions for Hand Pose Estimation\nD. Kong,\nH. Ma\nand X. Xie\nBritish Machine Vision Virtual Conference (\nBMVC\n), 2020.\n(Oral)\n[\nPaper\n]\nNonparametric Structure Regularization Machine for 2D Hand Pose Estimation\nY. Chen*,\nH. Ma*\n, D. Kong, X. Yan, J. Wu, W. Fan, and X. Xie\nIEEE Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (\nWACV\n), 2020.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPresentation\n] [\nSlides\n] [\nPoster\n]\nLSTM Multi-modal UNet for Brain Tumor Segmentation\nF. Xu,\nH. Ma\n, J. Sun, R. Wu, X. Liu, and Y. Kong\nIEEE Conference on Image, Vision and Computing(\nICIVC\n), 2019.\n[\nPaper\n] [\nSlides\n] [\nCode\n]\nAcademic Service\nConference Reviewer\nCVPR2025, ICCV2025\nCVPR2024, ICML2024, ECCV2024, ICLR2024, CPAL2024, WACV2024\nCVPR2023, ICML2023, ICCV2023, NeurIPS2023\nCVPR2022, ICML2022, ECCV2022, NeurIPS2022, WACV2022, BMVC2022\nBMVC2021\nTA/Readers:\nCOMPSCI 271/171, Introduction to Artificial Intelligence (2020-2024)\nCOMPSCI 274C, Neural Networks and Deep Learning (2021,2023)\nCOMPSCI 178, Machine Learning & Data Mining (2020)\nContests\nKaggle\nPeking University/Baidu - Autonomous Driving\n,\nRank\n: 52/866(Top 6%), Bronze medal\nAwards\nWACV 2024 Doctor Consortium\nDean's Awards from Donald Bren School of Information and Computer Sciences, 2019\nMerit Student, 2016/2017\nNational Scholarship, 2016\nPublished with\nGitHub Pages"
  },
  "serper::Ying Ding": {
    "homepage": "https://yingding.ischool.utexas.edu/",
    "emails": [
      "paper@arxiv.org",
      "ying.ding@austin.utexas.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ying-ding-6a63bb/",
    "homepage_text": "Ying Ding's Homepage\nYing Ding's Homepage\nHome\nTeaching\nResearch\nPublication\nService\nNew Highlights\nWe co-organzie\nGenerative AI for Healthcare Workshop\nat NeurIPS2025 on Dec 6-7, 2025.\nWe co-organzied\nGenerative AI for Healthcare Workshop\nat NeurIPS2024 on Dec 14, 2024.\nWe co-organzied\nUT System AI Health Symposium\nat UT Southwestern in May 2024.\nWe have organized\nThe Web Conference 2023\nin Austin in May 2023.\nWe have organized\nInternational Workshop on Digital Twins for Smart Health\nat The Web Conference 2023\nWe have organized\n3rd International Workshop on Scientific Knowledge Representation, Discovery, and Assessment (Sci-K 2023)\nat The Web Conference 2023\nCheck our new publications at\nWACV2022\n, ICDM2021,\nAMIA2021\n,\nISBI2021\nWe are PC members and Senior PCs for CVPR, ICML, WWW, ICDM, WSDM, SDM, KDD, ICHI, JCDL\nOur\nCOVID paper\nabout research novelty and parachuting collaboration during the COVID-19 pandemic\nhas been featured on\nNature\nand\nThe Atlantic\n.\nTACC is currently hosting our\nCOVID portal\nand\nPubMed portal\nWe summarize our\nCOVID-19 researches\nin 2020, which include:\nCOVID-19 knowledge graph\n,\nmisinformation in China\n, machine learning for COVID-19 patient risk prediction,\ninnovation and collaboration in COVID-19 researches\n, COVID-19 research article portal. We would like to thank all our collaborators. Please check the\nvideo\nhere. I joined the COVID-19 panel at\nIEEE Services 2020.\nWe received the\nAmazon Machine Learning Research Award\n2020. We are going to build Human-centered AI Medical Imaging Diagnosis approaches using knowledge graph, NLP, and computer vision. We are working on topics related to knowledge graph for medical images, merging scene graph with text graph, visual grounding for medical images, and visual question&answer for medical imaging, auto annotation of medical images. If you are interested in joining us, please feel free to contact me. Please check our latest\npaper\nabout using radiomics and deep learning to automaticlly generate bounding boxes for chest x-rays\n.\nWe are building the high quality\nPubMed Knowledge Graph\nby extracting biological entities using BioBERT and disambiguating millions of authors. It is published at\nScientific Data\n. Knowledge Graph can be downloaded at\nhttp://er.tacc.utexas.edu/datasets/ped\n.\nOur\nCOVID-19 Seminar\n: Fighting against COVID-19: Clinical Research, Drug Discovery, and Literature Mining is well received. Here is the\nlink\nfor the 3 hour long video.\nNew Papers in Progress\nPlease check our\nnew paper\nwhether pandemic can reshape science and drive more innovations, and will scienists become more creative during the pandemic\nplease check out our\nattribute2vec\npaper at arxiv.org. It is the deep learning algorithm which can consider the attributes of your knowledge graph\nOur\nedge2vec\ncan address the heterogenity by considering the edge semantics of your knowledge graph\nPlease check our paper about the evolution of\nCOVID-19 misinformation in China\nby analzying 3 million weibo data\nCo-editing Journals/Book Series/books\nCo-editor\nSemantic Web Synthesis\n(Springer Nature)\nAssociate Editor: ACM Transactions on Computing for Healthcare\nSemantic Breakthrough in Drug Discovery\nPast Events\nDigital Twins for Health Consortium\nInternational Workshop on Knowledge Graph: Open Knowledge Network (OKN)\nat ACM KDD 2022\nGraph Deep Learning Track at The Knowledge Graph Conference\n, May 2-5, 2022, New York.\nExplainable AI to Enable Better Health\nat WWW2022\nKnowledge Graph Workshop\nat ACM KDD 2021\nAI Health Data Challenge\nPersonal Health Knowledge Graph Workshop\nat KGC2021\nKnowledge-Infused Learning Workshop\nat KGC2021\nAI in Health Workshop\nat WWW2021\nWomen in Data Science in Austin 2021\nKnowledge Graph Workshop\nat KDD 2020\nWomen in Data Scicence in Austin 2020\nKnowledge Graph Workshop\nat WWW 2019\nChatbot Workshop\nat ICWSM 2018\nData-Driven Discovery Workshop\nat KDD 2017\nYing Ding, Ph.D.\nAI Health Lab\nBill & Lewis Suit Professor\nSchool of Information\nUniversity of Texas at Austin\nDepartment of Population Health\nDell Medical School\nUniversity of Texas at Austin\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nLinkedIN\nContact Information\nMailing Address:\nSchool of Information, ST STE 5202\nUniversity of Texas at Austin\n1616 Guadalupe St, Austin, TX 78701-1204\nEmail: ying.ding@austin.utexas.edu\nOffice: UTA 5.432\nTel: 512 471 3877\nResearch Interests\nAI in Health\nData-Driven Science of Science\nKnowledge Graph and Mining\nAI in Healthcare and Drug Discovery\nMedical Imaging Diagnosis: Computer Vision, Knowledge Graph, NLP\nSemantic Web\nData-Driven Knowledge Discovery\nScholarly Communication\nTeam Collaboration\nBusiness\nCo-Founder of\nData2Discovery\nEducation\nPh.D, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore"
  },
  "serper::Insup Lee": {
    "homepage": "https://www.cis.upenn.edu/~lee/home/index.shtml",
    "emails": [
      "lee@cis.upenn.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Insup Lee\nDepartment of Computer & Information Science\nSchool of Engineering and Applied Science\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\nInsup Lee is the\nCecilia Fitler Moore\nProfessor in\r\nthe\nDepartment of Computer and\r\nInformation Science\nand the Director of\nPRECISE Center\nin the School of Engineering and Applied Science.  He also holds a secondary appointment in the Department of Electrical and Systems Engineering and the Perelman School of Medicineâs Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology, and Informatics.\r\n\r\nHis research interests include cyber-physical systems (CPS), real-time and embedded systems, safe autonomy, runtime assurance and veriï¬cation, internet of medical things, and connected health. The theme of his research activities has been to assure and improve the safety, security, and timeliness of life-critical embedded systems\r\n\r\nHe received IEEE TC-RTS Outstanding Technical Achievement and Leadership Award in 2008, an appreciation award from Ministry of Science, and ACM SIGBED Inaugural Distinguished Leadership Award in 2022. He is an IEEE fellow, an ACM fellow, and an AAAS fellow.\nA founding co-Editor-in-Chief of\nACM Transactions on Computing for Healthcare (HEALTH)\nGoogle Scholar\nDBLP\nPlease contact Professor\nInsup Lee\nif you are interested in joining his group as a PhD student or Postdoctoral fellow.\n[\nAbout Me\n]\nMay 2022:\nThe Best Paper Award for the 13th ACM/IEEE International Conference on Cyber-Physical Systems (ICCPS 2022) went to the paper entitled Interpretable Detection of Distribution Shifts in Learning Enabled Cyber-Physical Systems by Yahan Yang, Ramneet Kaur, Souradeep Dutta, and Insup Lee.\nRead more\n.\nAugust 2020:\nInsup Lee and his team partner with Hillrom and Penn Nursing to optimize the use of medical devices in clinical settings to improve patient outcomes.\nRead more\nMarch 2020:\nThe inaugural issue of ACM Transactions on Computing for Healthcare (HEALTH) with Insup Lee as Co-Editor-in-Chief has been published and is now available in the\nACM Digital Library\n!\nNovember 2019:\nPRECISE members Insup Lee and Oleg Sokolsky, along with Sampath Kannan, Moonzoo Kim, and Mahesh Viswanathan, win the Test-of-Time Award for their 2001 paper \"\nJava-MaC: a run-time assurance tool for Java programs\n\" at the 2019 Conference on Runtime Verification.\n[\nAll News\n]\nVerisig 2.0: Verification of Neural Network Controllers Using Taylor Model Preconditioning\n. Radoslav Ivanov, Taylor Carpenter, James Weimer, Rajeev Alur, George Pappas, Insup Lee. Proceedings of\nthe 33rd International Conference on Computer-Aided Verification (CAV)\n, Los Angeles, CA, July 2021.\nDetecting OODs as datapoints with High Uncertainty\n. Ramneet Kaur, Susmit Jha, Anirban Roy, Sangdon Park, Oleg Sokolsky, Insup Lee. Proceedings of\nWorkshop on Uncertainty and Robustness in Deep Learning (UDL)\n, Virtually, July 2021.\nModelGuard: Runtime Validation of Lipschitz-continuous Models\n. Taylor Carpenter, Radoslav Ivanov, Insup Lee, James Weimer. Proceedings of\nthe 7th IFAC Conference on Analysis and Design of Hybrid Systems (ADHS)\n, Brussels, Belgium, July 2021.\nRaproto: An Open Source Platform for Rapid Prototyping of Wearable Medical Devices\n. Amanda Watson, Hyonyoung Choi, Insup Lee, and James Weimer. Proceedings of\nthe 12th ACM/IEEE International Conference on Cyber-Physical Systems (ICCPS)\n, Nashville, TN, May 2021.\n[\nAll Publications\n]\nCopyright © 2011-2019 University of Pennsylvania. All Rights Reserved. Site designed by\nAcademic Web Pages\n."
  },
