    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/junghyun-nick-lee-89799a197/",
    "homepage_text": "Junghyun Lee\nSearch\nJunghyun Lee\nPhD Student\nKAIST AI\nWelcome!\nI am a final-year PhD student at the\nKim Jaechul Graduate School of AI\n, KAIST, where I am very fortunate to be advised by\nSe-Young Yun\n(\nOSI Lab\n) and\nChulhee “Charlie” Yun\n(OptiML Lab).\nI had the pleasure of spending the summer of 2025 as a Research Scientist Intern at Adobe Research, San Jose, working with\nBranislav “Brano” Kveton\n,\nAnup Rao\n,\nSubhojyoti Mukherjee\n,\nRyan A. Rossi\n,\nSunav Choudhary\n, and\nAlexa Siu\n.\nMy research focuses primarily on\ninteractive machine learning\n(bandits, RL, active learning), “theoretical aspects” of LLMs (alignment, reasoning), optimization theory, and statistical analyses of large networks with an emphasis on\ncommunity detection\n.\nMore broadly, my interests encompass all aspects of\nmathematical and theoretical AI\n, as well as related problems in mathematics and statistics.\nI enjoy organizing seminars and workshops to foster Korea’s theoretical AI community; see ‘Organizer’.\nOutside of research, I am an avid violinist and have performed as a first violinist with various amateur orchestras, including the KAIST Orchestra (KAO), PASSIONATE Orchestra, MDOP Orchestra, KAO-S, PROJECT Starlight, and PROJECT IDEA.\nFeel free to reach out if you’d like to collaborate on any of my research topics or just to connect!\n(\nThird-person bio here\n.)\n(Last updated: 2026.02.12.)\nInterests\nBandits, Online Learning\nStatistical RL\nTopics related to LLMs\nStatistics, Learning Theory\nCommunity Detection, Networks\nDL/Optim Theory\nAlgorithmic Fairness\nDistributed Algorithms\nEducation\nPhD in Artificial Intelligence (GSAI), 2023-\nKorea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology\nMSc in Artificial Intelligence (GSAI), 2021-2023\nKorea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology\nBSc in Mathematical Sciences and Computer Science (double major, cum laude), 2017-2021\nKorea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology\nFeatured Publications\nGL-LowPopArt: A Nearly Instance-Wise Minimax-Optimal Estimator for Generalized Low-Rank Trace Regression\nWe present GL-LowPopArt, a novel Catoni-style estimator for generalized low-rank trace regression. Building on LowPopArt (Jang et al., …\nJunghyun Lee\n,\nKyoungseok Jang\n,\nKwang-Sung Jun\n,\nMilan Vojnović\n,\nSe-Young Yun\nPDF\nCite\nNear-Optimal Clustering in Mixture of Markov Chains\nWe study the problem of clustering T trajectories of length H, each generated by one of K unknown ergodic Markov chains over a finite …\nJunghyun Lee\n,\nYassir Jedra\n,\nAlexandre Proutière\n,\nSe-Young Yun\nPDF\nCite\nRegularized Online RLHF with Generalized Bilinear Preferences\nWe consider the problem of contextual online RLHF with general preferences, where the goal is to identify the Nash Equilibrium. We …\nJunghyun Lee\n,\nMinju Hong\n,\nKwang-Sung Jun\n,\nChulhee Yun\n,\nSe-Young Yun\nPDF\nCite\nA Jointly Efficient and Optimal Algorithm for Heteroskedastic Generalized Linear Bandits with Adversarial Corruptions\nWe consider the problem of heteroskedastic generalized linear bandits (GLBs) with adversarial corruptions, which subsumes various …\nSanghwa Kim\n,\nJunghyun Lee\n,\nSe-Young Yun\nPDF\nCite\nLearning to Reason in LLMs by Expectation Maximization\nLarge language models (LLMs) solve reasoning problems by first generating a rationale and then answering. We formalize reasoning as a …\nJunghyun Lee\n,\nBranislav Kveton\n,\nAnup Rao\n,\nSubhojyoti Mukherjee\n,\nRyan A. Rossi\n,\nSunav Choudhary\n,\nAlexa Siu\nPDF\nCite\nSee all publications\nCollaborators\nAlexa Siu\nAlexandre Proutière\nAnup Rao\nBohan Wang\nBranislav Kveton\nChang D. Yoo\nChulhee Yun\nGwangsu Kim\nHanseul Cho\nHuishuai Zhang\nJinwoo Shin\nKunwoo Na\nKwang-Sung Jun\nKyoungseok Jang\nLaura Schmid\nMilan Vojnović\nMinju Hong\nPrin Phunyaphibarn\nRyan A. Rossi\nSanghwa Kim\nSe-Young Yun\nSeong Jin Cho\nShin Yoo\nSubhojyoti Mukherjee\nSunav Choudhary\nSungbin Lim\nWoosung Koh\nYassir Jedra\nKeywords\nActive Learning\nBandits\nClustering\nDeep Learning Theory\nDiffusion Model\nFairness\nInformation Theory\nLearning in Games\nLLMs\nMarkov Chain\nMARL\nNetworks\nOnline Learning\nOptimization\nProbabilistic Machine Learning\nProbability Theory\nReasoning\nRL\nRLHF\nSBSE\nStatistics\nContact\njh_lee00(AT)kaist.ac.kr\n85 Hoegi-ro, Dondaemun-gu, Seoul, 02455\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
  "serper::Yoonhyung Lee": {
    "homepage": "https://leeyoonhyung.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "cpi1234@snu.ac.kr"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/leeyoonhyung",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yoonhyunglee/?locale=en_US",
    "homepage_text": "Yoonhyung Lee | Postdoctoral Researcher at Seoul National University\nYoonhyung Lee\n이윤형\nPh.D. Candidate at Seoul National University\nlocation_on\nSeoul, Korea\nemail\ncpi1234@snu.ac.kr\nGoogle Scholar\nSemantic Scholar\nGithub\nLinkedIn\ninsert_drive_file\nCV\nI am currently pursuing my Ph.D. at the Machine Intelligence Lab, Seoul National University, under the guidance of Professor Kyomin Jung. My research has primarily focused on Text-to-Speech (TTS), particularly aligning text and speech modalities and separating linguistic information from other prosodic elements such as pitch and energy. My current research are centered on disentangling various speech components to enhance the performance and controllability of deep learning models across a range of speech processing tasks. In particular, I am interested in uncovering linguistic information in speech for Textless-NLP applications such as speech translation, an area I believe holds potential to bring people from all over the world closer together.\nEducation\naccount_balance\nSeoul National University (SNU)\n,\n          Seoul, Korea\n2022.08\nPh.D. Candidate in\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nAdvisor:\nProf. Kyomin Jung\nschool\nSeoul National University (SNU)\n,\n          Seoul, Korea\n2019.02\nB.S. in\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nSelected Publications\nVarianceFlow: High-quality and Controllable Text-to-Speech\n                  Using Variance Information via Normalizing Flow,\nYoonhyung Lee\n, Jinhyeok Yang, Kyomin Jung\nICASSP 2022\nBidirectional Variational Inference for Non-Autoregressive\n                  Text-to-Speech. International Conference on Learning\n                  Representation,\nYoonhyung Lee\n, Seunghyun Yoon, Kyomin Jung\nICLR 2021 [\nCode\n]\nMultimodal Speech Emotion Recognition Using Cross Attention\n                  with Aligned Audio and Text,\nYoonhyung Lee\n, Seunghyun Yoon, Kyomin Jung\nInterSpeech 2020\nFast and Accurate Deep Bidirectional Language Representations\n                  for Unsupervised Learning,\nJoongbo Shin,\nYoonhyung Lee\n, Seunghyun Yoon, Kyomin Jung\nACL 2020 [\nCode\n]\nEffective Sentence Scoring Method Using BERT for Speech\n                  Recognition,\nJoongbo Shin,\nYoonhyung Lee\n, Kyomin Jung\nACML 2019\nMILAB at SemEval-2019 Task 3: Multi-View Turn-by-Turn Model\n                  for Context-Aware Sentiment Analysis,\nYoonhyung Lee\n, Yanghoon Kim, Kyomin Jung\nSemEval@NAACL-HLT 2019\nScholarships & Awards\nYoulchon AI STAR Scholarship\n2022.07\nSamsung Electronics Research Scholarship Student\n2018.07-2018.12"
  },
