  "serper::Jing Wu": {
    "homepage": "https://jingwu2121.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "\"jing.wu@eng.ox.ac.uk\""
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/jingwu2121",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jing-wu-068b7b1b4",
    "homepage_text": "Home | Jing Wu\nJing Wu 🍄\nHello! :D 👋\nWelcome to my homepage.\nI am a 3rd year DPhil/PhD student at\nActive Vision Group\n,\nUniversity of Oxford\n, jointly supervised by Professor\nVictor Prisacariu\nand Dr.\nIro Laina\n. I am currently interning at\nMicrosoft Research Redmond\nand I am mentored by Dr.\nVibhav Vineet\nand\nYanan Jian\n.\nI obtained my M.Sc. degree with\nDistinction\nfrom\nImperial College London\n. Prior to that, I received my B.Eng. from the\nUniversity of Electronic Science and Technology of China (UESTC)\n. I was awarded the Outstanding Graduate Award of Sichuan Province.\n📢📢 Check Our New Paper: OS-Marathon\nhere\nand Reflect3r\nhere\n😆\n💡 Research Interests\nI am broadly interested in\nAgentic AI\n,\nMultimodal LLMs/VLMs\nand\n3D vision\n. \n            My research focuses on how to make digital assistants/robots/agents perceive the world, interact with the world, and generate the world.\nAgentic AI, Computer Use Agents, Multimodal LLMs/VLMs\n3D Agents\n3D Reconstruction, 3D Generative Models, 3D Editing\n📰 News\n[11/2025]: Our Reflect3r paper is accepted by 3DV 2026! 🥳\n[09/2025]: Starting my internship at Microsoft Research Redmond!\n[07/2024]: Two papers accepted by ECCV 2024!\n[10/2023]: Starting my PhD at Oxford\n🎓 Recent research\nSee all research\nOS-Marathon: Benchmarking Computer-Use Agents on Long-Horizon Repetitive Tasks\nJing Wu\n, Daphne Barretto, Yiye Chen, Nicholas Gydé, Yanan Jian, Yuhang He, Vibhav Vineet\nPaper\nWeb\nIn\nArXiv2026\nReflect3r: Single-View 3D Stereo Reconstruction Aided by Mirror Reflections\nJing Wu\n, Zirui Wang, Iro Laina, Victor Adrian Prisacariu\nPaper\nCode\nWeb\nData\nIn\n3DV2026\nLatest posts\nSee all posts\nTennis Drills and Practice Notes\nA note for my tennis journey.\nZero to hero | How to build a personal website with Astro and deploy on Github (Windows)\nBuild Astro personal website, blog and deploy them on Github.\n📞 Let's Connect\nIf you want to get in touch with me about something or just to say\n                hi, reach out on social media or send me an email. Subscribe to the academic blogs with RSS!\n😉 Art Works\nBesides research, I have great passion for visual arts and music. Here are some of my works.\nOS-Marathon Banner\nMade with Blender\nOriginal\nLuv\nMade with Blender\nInspired by\nthis link\nSwimming Pool\nMade with Blender\nInspired by\nthis link\nTraffic Light\nMade with Procreate\nOriginal\n🎧 Music\nMore music\nHere are some of my old original music and guitar arrangements.\n冬日黄昏\nA Chinese style arrangement\nYour browser does not support the audio element.\nMy Original Music\n理想？ 现实？\nSummertime vibes\nYour browser does not support the audio element.\nMy Original Music\nPress\nEsc\nor click anywhere to close"
  },
  "serper::Yu-Kun Lai": {
    "homepage": "https://yukunlai.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "yukun.lai@cs.cardiff.ac.uk",
