    "homepage_text": "Andrew Shen\nAndrew Shen\nFollow\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nX (formerly Twitter)\nHi, my name is Andrew! I’m a PhD student in\nBiomedical Data Science\nat\nStanford University\nwhere I am advised by\nJames Zou\n. I’m fortunate to be supported by the\nNSF Graduate Research Fellowship\n. I am broadly interested in problems at the intersection of AI and Science/Medicine, but I’m currently working on improving autonomous scientific discovery. Before I started my PhD, I worked with some amazing advisors including\nMarinka Zitnik\n,\nJoshua Glaser\n,\nHeather Moss\n,\nMelissa Gymrek\n, and\nKavita Sarin\n.\nIf you are interested in my work or would like to connect, please reach out!"
  },
  "serper::Siqi Miao": {
    "homepage": "https://siqi.plus/",
    "emails": [
      "siqi.miao@gatech.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/siqim",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Siqi Miao (苗思奇) - Homepage\nSiqi Miao (苗思奇)\nPhD Student at Gatech\nAtlanta, GA\nGoogle Scholar\nEmail\nGithub\nTwitter\nZhihu\nStrava\nI am a fifth-year PhD student in the Machine Learning program at\nGeorgia Tech\n’s School of Electrical and Computer Engineering, supervised by\nProf. Pan Li\n. Before coming to Georgia Tech, I was a PhD student in the Department of Computer Science at\nPurdue University\n. Prior to that, I worked at\nTencent\nBig Data Lab after receiving my master’s degree from the\nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\n. My Chinese given name is 思奇(siqi), pronounced as 思/si/ 奇/tʃiː/. My Chinese surname is 苗(miao), pronounced as 苗/mɪaʊ/. You can also call me Aki.\nMy current research focuses on:\nAI for science\n, particularly on geometric deep learning applications in high-energy physics.\nAgentic AI\n, where I study how large language models can act as autonomous reasoning and simulation agents, and how they can interact with network-structured data.\n🔥 News\nNews in 2025\n2025.10\n: Our paper on\nHEPTv2\nis accepted to NeurIPS 2025 Machine Learning and the Physical Sciences Workshop!\n2025.10\n: Our paper on\nGraph-KV\nis accepted to NeurIPS 2025!\n2025.06\n: Our paper on Weak-to-Strong GraphRAG is released on\narXiv\n.\n2025.04\n: Our paper on the universal graph structural encoder is released on\narXiv\n.\n2025.03\n: Our paper on explainable geometric deep learning is accepted to\nNature Machine Intelligence\n!\n2025.02\n: Our paper on\nSubgraphRAG\nis accepted to ICLR 2025!\nNews in 2024\n2024.11\n: Our paper on KG-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation is released on\narXiv\n.\n2024.09\n: Our paper\nGeSS\non benchmarking OOD performance in geometric deep learning is accepted to NeurIPS 2024 D&B Track.\n2024.07\n: Our paper on explainable geometric deep learning is released on\narXiv\n.\n2024.06\n: Our paper on graph state space model (GSSC) is released on\narXiv\n.\n2024.05\n: Our paper\nHEPT\nis accepted to ICML 2024 and selected for oral presentation! See you in Vienna!\n2024.03\n: Gave a talk at\nA3D3\ninstitute HEP group on\nHEPT\n.\n2024.02\n: Our paper on efficient point transformer (HEPT) is released on\narXiv\n.\nNews in 2023\n2023.10\n: Our paper on benchmarking OOD performance in geometric deep learning is released on\narXiv\n.\n2023.07\n: One paper accepted to CTD’23.\n2023.03\n: Received ICLR’23 Travel Award! Thanks ICLR and see you in Kigali in the coming May!\n2023.01\n: Our paper\nLRI\nis accepted to ICLR 2023 and NeurIPS 2022 AI4Science!\nNews in 2022\n2022.11\n: Gave a talk at\nIML Machine Learning Working Group\non\nLRI\nwith slides\nhere\n.\n2022.11\n: I will be moving to Georgia Tech in December as a PhD student in Machine Learning (ECE) with Prof. Pan Li.\n2022.11\n: Our latest paper on model interpretability (\nLRI\n) will show up at NeurIPS 2022\nAI for Science\nWorkshop!\n2022.10\n: Gave two lectures at\nCS593-CLG\n(\ncode\n) and\nPhys570-AI\n(\ncode\n).\n2022.07\n: Gave two talks at\nFastML\nand\nAITime\non our ICML 2022 paper\nGSAT\n(\nslides\n).\n2022.07\n: Awarded free registration and graduate travel grant for ICML! Thanks!\n2022.05\n: One paper accepted to ICML 2022!\n📝 Publications\nPreprint 2025\nCan LLM Agents Assist Dynamic Network Simulation? A Case Study on Email Networks and Phishing Synthesis\nSiqi Miao\n, Ziyang Chen, Yuhong Luo, Hans Hao-Hsun Hsu, Mufei Li, Kaiqing Zhang, Pan Li.\nPreprint 2025\nNature Machine Intelligence\nTowards unveiling sensitive and decisive patterns in explainable AI with a case study in geometric deep learning\nJiajun Zhu*,\nSiqi Miao*\n, Rex Ying, Pan Li.\nNature Machine Intelligence\n(*Equal contribution)\nICLR 2025\nSimple is Effective: The Roles of Graphs and LLMs in KG-Based Retrieval-Augmented Generation\nMufei Li*,\nSiqi Miao*\n, Pan Li.\nICLR 2025\n(*Equal contribution)\nPreprint 2024\nWhat Can We Learn from State Space Models for Machine Learning on Graphs?\nYinan Huang*,\nSiqi Miao*\n, Pan Li.\nPreprint 2024\n(*Equal contribution, listed in alphabetical order)\nICML 2024\nLSH-Based Efficient Point Transformer with Applications in High-Energy Physics\nSiqi Miao\n, Zhiyuan Lu, Mia Liu, Javier Duarte, Pan Li.\nICML 2024\n(Oral, Top 1.5%)\nICLR 2023\nInterpretable Geometric Deep Learning via Learnable Randomness Injection\nSiqi Miao\n, Yunan Luo, Mia Liu, Pan Li.\nICLR 2023\nICML 2022\nInterpretable and Generalizable Graph Learning via Stochastic Attention Mechanism\nSiqi Miao\n, Mia Liu, Pan Li.\nICML 2022\n(Spotlight)\nBlogs (\nEnglish\n-\n中文\n)\n|\nSlides\n|\nPoster\nLocality-Sensitive Hashing-Based Efficient Point Transformer for Charged Particle Reconstruction\n, Shitij Govil, Jack P Rodgers, Yuan-Tang Chou*,\nSiqi Miao*\n, Amit Saha, Advaith Anand, Kilian Lieret, Gage DeZoort, Mia Liu, Javier Duarte, Pan Li, Shih-Chieh Hsu. (*Corresponding authors)\nGraph-KV: Breaking Sequence via Injecting Structural Biases into Large Language Models\n, Haoyu Wang, Peihao Wang, Mufei Li, Shikun Liu,\nSiqi Miao\n, Zhangyang Wang, Pan Li.\nWeak-to-Strong GraphRAG: Aligning Weak Retrievers with Large Language Models for Graph-based Retrieval Augmented Generation\n, Deyu Zou*, Yongqiang Chen*, Mufei Li,\nSiqi Miao\n, Chenxi Liu, Bo Han, James Cheng, Pan Li. (*Equal contribution)\nTowards A Universal Graph Structural Encoder\n, Jialin Chen, Haolan Zuo, Haoyu Wang,\nSiqi Miao\n, Pan Li, Rex Ying.\nGeSS: Benchmarking Geometric Deep Learning under Scientific Applications with Distribution Shifts\n, Deyu Zou*, Shikun Liu*,\nSiqi Miao\n, Victor Fung, Shiyu Chang, Pan Li. (*Equal contribution)\nHigh Pileup Particle Tracking with Object Condensation\n, Kilian Lieret, Gage DeZoort, Devdoot Chatterjee, Jian Park,\nSiqi Miao\n, Pan Li.\n🎖 Honors and Awards\n2024.07\nOpenAI Research Grant (7500 USD API Credits)\n2024.02\nA3D3 Institute HDR NextGen Leaders Fellowship Nominee\n2023.03\nICLR’23 Travel Award\n2022.07\nICML’22 Travel Award\n2022.07\nPurdue Graduate Travel Grant\n2020.03\nTencent Innovation Award\n2020.01\nTencent Outstanding Employee (Top 10%)\n💬 Invited Talks\n2024.03\n, A3D3 Institute HEP Group\n2022.11\n, Inter-Experimental LHC Machine Learning Working Group, CERN\n2022.10\n, Department of Physics, Purdue University\n2022.08\n, AI Time\n2022.07\n, Fast Machine Learning Lab\n💻 Experience\n2023.01 - Present\n, Georgia Tech, Research Assistant, Atlanta, USA\n2021.08 - 2022.12\n, Purdue University, Research Assistant, West Lafayette, USA\n2019.07 - 2020.05\n, Tencent, Machine Learning Engineer, Guangzhou, China\n2018.05 - 2018.08\n, Tencent, Machine Learning Intern, Guangzhou, China\n📖 Academic Services\nConference Reviewer: ICML, ICLR, NeurIPS, AAAI, AISTATS, LOG, WWW\nJournal Reviewer: TMLR, IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing\n🎮 Misc\nI started cycling in 2025! By June 2025, my FTP reached ~240W. My strava profile is\nhere\n, and\nthis\nis my road bike!\nI have 5.5k+ followers on\nZhihu\n, a Quora-like platform in China.\nThe Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild\nand\nThe Witcher 3: Wild Hunt\nare the best games ever.\nGenshin Impact\nis also awesome!\nI’m a big fan of\nLego Technic\n. I once combined them with RC cars to build a few cool Lego cars that could drift and climb!\nI built my own PC and home automation system. I also liked to play with Jetson TX2 and Raspberry Pi."
  },
  "serper::Winnie Xu": {
    "homepage": "https://www.blackhc.net/",
    "emails": [
