    "homepage_text": "Homepage - Tiexin\nTiexin Qin\nPostdoc\nI am currently a postdoc in the Department of Electrical Engineering at City University of Hong Kong, advised by Prof.\nHong Yan\n.  I got my Ph.D. degree from City University of Hong Kong, supervised by Prof.\nHaoliang Li\n,  and MSc degree from Nanjing University, supervised by Prof.\nYinghuan Shi\n.  I also had a wonderful experience as a visiting scholar at the University of Oxford, working with Prof.\nTerry Lyons\n.\nMy research interests encompass machine learning for complex systems, neural differential equations, and transfer learning, with a particular focus on their grounded mathematical principles and practical applications.\ntiexinqin(at)gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nCV\nAction required\nProblem:\nThe current root path of this site is \"\n\",\n            which does not match the\nbaseurl\n(\"\n\") configured in\n_config.yml\n.\nSolution:\nPlease set the\nbaseurl\nin\n_config.yml\nto \"\n\".\nNews\n2026\nOne paper is accepted to TKDE 2026.\nFeb 16\n2025\nOur\nGN-CDEs\nfor dynamic graph is accepted to TPAMI 2025.\nSep 28\nOne paper is accepted to NeurIPS 2025.\nSep 19\nPass my\nPhD thesis\ndefense.\nJul 16\nInvited talk at\nRough Path Interest Group\n.\nJul 09\nOne paper is accepted to ICCV 2025.\nJun 26\nOne paper is accepted to TPAMI 2025.\nJun 17\nOne paper is accepted to CVPR 2025.\nMar 10\nTwo papers are accepted to ICLR 2025.\nJan 23\n2024\nOne work about molecular dynamics has been released.\nRead more\nOct 02\nI received\nResearch Tuition Scholarship\n.\nSep 05\nOne paper is accepted to TMI 2024.\nJun 22\n🎉 One paper to appear in ICML 2024.\nMay 30\nStart visiting\nProf. Terry Lyons\n's group at Oxford.\nJan 27\n2023\nTwo papers are accepted to TPAMI 2023.\nSep 05\n2022\nInvited talk at AI Time, See\nbilibili\nAug 17\nPublications\n(view all\n)\nLearning dynamic graph embeddings with neural controlled differential equations\nTiexin Qin\n,\nBenjamin Walker,\nTerry Lyons,\nHong Yan,\nHaoliang Li\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\n2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nLearning dynamic graph embeddings with neural controlled differential equations\nTiexin Qin\n,\nBenjamin Walker,\nTerry Lyons,\nHong Yan,\nHaoliang Li\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\n2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nDeep Signature: Characterization of Large-Scale Molecular Dynamics\nTiexin Qin\n,\nMengxu Zhu,\nChunyang Li,\nTerry Lyons,\nHong Yan,\nHaoliang Li\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nDeep Signature: Characterization of Large-Scale Molecular Dynamics\nTiexin Qin\n,\nMengxu Zhu,\nChunyang Li,\nTerry Lyons,\nHong Yan,\nHaoliang Li\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nGeneralizing to Evolving Domains with Latent Structure-Aware Sequential Autoencoder\nTiexin Qin\n,\nShiqi Wang,\nHaoliang Li\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n2022\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nGeneralizing to Evolving Domains with Latent Structure-Aware Sequential Autoencoder\nTiexin Qin\n,\nShiqi Wang,\nHaoliang Li\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n2022\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nAll publications\nEducation\nCity University of Hong Kong\nDepartment of Electrical Engineering\nPh.D. Student\nSep. 2021 - Oct. 2025\nNanjing University\nM.S. in Computer Science\nOutstanding Postgraduate\nSep. 2018 - Jul. 2021\nChina University of Mining and Technology\nB.S. in Computer Science\nOutstanding Undergraduate\nSep. 2014 - Jul. 2018\nHonors & Awards\nResearch Tuition Scholarship\n2024\nChina National Scholarship\n2016\nService\nConference reviewer:\nICML, ICLR, NeurIPS, AISTATS, AAAI, KDD, CVPR, ICCV, WACV\nJournal reviewer:\nTPAMI, TCSVT, TIT"
  },
  "serper::Quanqi Hu": {
    "homepage": "https://quanqihu.github.io/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/quanqi-hu-80b840145/",
    "homepage_text": "Quanqi Hu's Homepage\nQuanqi Hu / 胡筌淇\ngoogle scholar\nLinkedIn\nI am a research scientist at Meta. I obtained my PhD in computer science from Texas A&M University. I was fortunate to be advised by\nDr. Tianbao Yang\n. Before Texas A&M, I spent three years in the Applied Mathematical and Computational Sciences program at University of Iowa and recieved my master's degree in mathematics. I recieved my bachelor's degree in mathematics from the Pennsylvania State University.\nExperience\nResearch Scientist, Meta, June 2025 - Now\nAI/ML PhD Intern, GE Healthcare, May - Aug. 2024\n- Utilized a latent diffusion model to generate synthetic 3D cardiac CT volumes along with their corresponding segmentation masks.\n- Enhanced segmentation performance on 3D cardiac CT volumes by incorporating the generated synthetic volumes and masks into the training process.\n- Further improved segmentation accuracy through the application of a self-supervised learning pretraining procedure.\nResearch Scientist Intern, KLA, May - Aug. 2023\n- Improved the defect detection performance on scanning electron microscope (SEM) images using self-supervised pretrained Vision Transformer (ViT).\n- Applied Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) to further improve the training efficiency.\nPublications\nSingle-loop Stochastic Algorithms for Difference of Max-Structured Weakly Convex Functions\n[Preprints]\nQuanqi Hu\n, Qi Qi, Zhaosong Lu, Tianbao Yang.\nTo appear in Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2024.\nNon-Smooth Weakly-Convex Finite-sum Coupled Compositional Optimization\n[Preprints]\nQuanqi Hu\n, Dixian Zhu, Tianbao Yang.\nIn Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2023.\nBlockwise Stochastic Variance-Reduced Methods with Parallel Speedup for Multi-Block Bilevel Optimization\n[Preprints]\nQuanqi Hu\n, Zi-Hao Qiu, Zhishuai Guo, Lijun Zhang, Tianbao Yang.\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2023.\nNot All Semantics are Created Equal: Contrastive Self-supervised Learning with Automatic Temperature Individualization\n[Preprints]\nZi-Hao Qiu,\nQuanqi Hu\n, Zhuoning Yuan, Denny Zhou, Lijun Zhang, Tianbao Yang.\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2023.\nMulti-block Min-max Bilevel Optimization with Applications in Multi-task Deep AUC Maximization\n[Preprints]\nQuanqi Hu\n, Yongjian Zhong, Tianbao Yang.\nIn Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2022.\nLarge-scale Stochastic Optimization of NDCG Surrogates for Deep Learning with Provable Convergence\n[Preprints]\nZi-Hao Qiu*,\nQuanqi Hu\n*, Yongjian Zhong, Lijun Zhang, Tianbao Yang.\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2022.\nA Stochastic Momentum Method for Min-max Bilevel Optimization\n[PDF]\nQuanqi Hu\n, Bokun Wang, Tianbao Yang.\nIn NeurIPS Workshop on Optimization for Machine Learning (OPT), 2021.\n* Denotes Equal Contribution.\nPreprints\nProvable Optimization for Adversarial Fair Self-supervised Contrastive Learning\n[Preprints]\nQi Qi,\nQuanqi Hu\n, Qihang Lin, Tianbao Yang.\nRandomized Stochastic Variance-Reduced Methods for Multi-Task Stochastic Bilevel Optimization\n[Preprints]\nZhishuai Guo,\nQuanqi Hu\n, Lijun Zhang, Tianbao Yang.\nTeaching Assistant\nMATH:1560 Engineer Math II: Multivariable Calculus, University of Iowa, Fall 2021\nMATH:1260 The Mathematics of Pokemon Go, University of Iowa, Spring 2021\nMATH:2560 Engineer Math IV: Differential Equations, University of Iowa, Fall 2020\nMATH:1440 Mathematics for the Biological Sciencess, University of Iowa, Fall 2020\nMATH:1460 Calculus for the Biological Sciences, University of Iowa, Spring 2020\nMATH:1380 Calculus and Matrix Algebra for Business, University of Iowa, Spring 2020\nMATH:3800 Elementary Numerical Analysis, University of Iowa, Fall 2019\nMATH:3600 Intro to Ordinary Differential Equations, University of Iowa, Fall 2019\nSelected Awards\nTravel Award, Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2022\nTravel Award, International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2022\nSteven and Sherry McCrystal Award, Penn State, April 2018\nWomen in Math Scholarship, Penn State, April 2018\nServices\nConference Reviewer of ICML, NeurIPS."
  },
  "serper::Yongjian Zhong": {
