    "homepage_text": "Zhiren Wang's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZhiren Wang  王之任\nzhirenw(AT)jhu.edu\nI am a mathematician. My research interests include homogeneous dynamical systems, classification of group actions, number theory, and machine learning.\nTeaching\nIntroduction to Topology, AS.110.413 (Spring 2025)\nResume\nProfessor,\nJohns Hopkins\nUniv., 202\n5\nPr\nofessor, Penn State Univ., 20\n23-2024\nAssociate professor, Penn State Univ., 2019-2023\nAssistant professor, Penn State Univ., 2014-2019\nGibbs assistant professor, Yale Univ., 2011-2014\nPh.D. Princeton Univ. (Advisor: Prof. Elon Lindenstrauss), 2006-2011\nM.Sc. Univ. Paris-Sud, 2005-2006\nM.Sc. Ecole Polytechnique, 2004-2006\nB.Sc. Fudan Univ., 2001-2004\nResearch\n• with A. Algom and F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nPolynomial Fourier decay and a cocycle version of Dolgopyat's method for self conformal measures\nsubmitted\n[pdf]\n• with E. Lindenstrauss, A. Mohammadi and L. Yang,\nAn effective version of the Oppenheim conjecture with a polynomial error rate\nresearch announcement\n[pdf]\n• with E. Lindenstrauss and A. Mohammadi,\nEffective equidistribution for some one parameter unipotent flows\nAnnals of Math. (2025)\n[pdf]\nannouncement appeared in\nComptes Rendus Math. (2023)\n[announcement]\n• with Y. Wang,\nCW complex hypothesis for image data\nIC\nML\n(Int. Conf.\nMachine Learning\n) (2024)\n[pdf]\n• with Z. Li and Y. Wang,\nFast equilibrium of SGD in generic situations\nICLR (Int. Conf. Learning Representations) (2024)\n[pdf]\n• with A. Algom,\nArbitrarily slow decay in the logarithmically averaged Sarnak conjecture\nJ. Math. Anal. & Appl\n. (202\n4\n)\n[pdf]\n• with F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nNon-rig\nidity of partially hyperbolic abelian\nC\n1\n-actions on tori\nErgodic Th. & Dyn. Sys. (2024)\n[pdf]\n• with A. Algom,\nArbitrarily slow deca\ny in the Möbius disjointness conjecture\nErgodic Th. & Dyn. Sys.\n(2023)\n[pdf]\n• with W. Huang, J. Wang and Q. Zhou,\nQuan\ntitative almost reducibility and Möbius disjointness for analytic quasiperiodic Schrödinger cocycles\nPeking Journal of Mathematics (2023)\n[pdf]\n• with E. Lindenstrauss and A. Mohammadi,\nQuantitative equidistribution and the local statistics of the spectrum of a flat torus\nJournal d'Analyse Mathématique (2023)\n[pdf]\n• with A. Brown and F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nSmo\noth ergodic theory of\nZ\nd\n-actions, Part 3: Product structure of entropy\nJournal of Modern Dynamics (2023)\n[pdf]\n• with A. Brown and F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nInva\nriant measures and measurable projective factors for actions of higher-rank lattices on manifolds\nAnnals of Math. (2022)\n[pdf]\n• with Y. Wang,\nThree-stage evolution and fast\nequilibrium for SGD with non-degenerate critical points\nICML (Int. Conf. Machine Learning) (2022)\n[pdf]\n• with A. Brown and F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nThe\nnormal subgroup theorem through measure rigidity\n(expository book chapter)\nDynamics, Geometry, Number Theory: The Impact of Margulis on Modern Mathematics (2022)\n[pdf]\n• with A. Algom and F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nLogarithmic\nFourier decay for self-conformal measures\nJournal of London Math. Soc. (2022)\n[pdf]\n• with A. Algom and F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nPointwis\ne normality and Fourier decay for self-conformal measures\nAdvances Math. (2021)\n[pdf]\n• with X. He,\nMöbius\ndisjointness along short intervals for nilsequences\nTrans. Amer. Math. Soc. (2021)\n[pdf]\n• with F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nOn\nε\n-\nescaping trajectories in homogeneous spaces\nDisc. Cont. Dyn. Sys. 25 Years Special Vol. (2021)\n[pdf]\n• with W. Huang and X. Ye,\nMea\nsure complexity and Möbius disjointness\nAdvances Math. (2019)\n[pdf]\n• with M. Litman,\nMöbius d\nisjointness for skew products on the Heisenberg nilmanifold\nProc. Amer. Math. Soc. (2019)\n[pdf]\n• with W. Huang and G. Zhang,\nMöbius di\nsjointness for topological models of ergodic systems with discrete spectrum\nJournal of Modern Dynamics (2019)\n[pdf]\n• Multi-invariant measures and subsets on nilmanifolds\nJ. Analyse Math. (2018)\n[pdf]\n• with A. Brown and F. Rodriguez Hertz,\nGlobal sm\nooth and topological rigidity of hyperbolic lattice actions\nAnnals of Math. (2017)\n[pdf]\n• Möbius disjointness for analytic skew products\nInventiones Math. (2017)\n[pdf]\n• with F. Rodriguez Hertz\n, G\nlobal rigidity of higher rank Anosov algebraic actions\nInventiones Math. (2014)\n[pdf]\n• with U. Shapira\n, Re\nmarks on Euclidean minima\nJ. Number Theory (2012)\n[pdf]\n• with E. Lindenstrauss\n, Topologi\ncal self-joinings of Cartan actions by toral automorphisms\nDuke Math. J. (2012)\n[pdf]\n• Rigidity of commutative non-hyperbolic actions by toral automorphisms\nErgodic Th. & Dyn. Sys. (2012)\n[pdf]\n•\nQuantitative density und\ner higher rank abelian algebraic toral actions\nInt. Math. Res. Notices (2011)\n[pdf]\nRecognition\nBrin Prize\nin dynamical systems\n,\n2022\nV\non Neummann Fellowship, Institute for Advanced Study, 2022-2023\nNSF CAREER Grant, 2018-2023\nGold Prize for Ph.D. Thesis, International Congress of Chinese Mathematicians, 2012\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Jialu Wang": {
    "homepage": "https://jialuwang123321.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "jialu.wang@keble.ox.ac.uk"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/jialuwang123321",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/wang-jialu-267302280/",
    "homepage_text": "Jialu Wang | University of Oxford\nJialu Wang\nD.Phil. Student\nUniversity of Oxford\njialu.wang@keble.ox.ac.uk\nAbout Me\nI am a D.Phil. candidate in Computer Science at the\nUniversity of Oxford\n, co-supervised by Profs.\nNiki Trigoni\nand\nAndrew Markham\n.\nI plan on submitting my thesis in the coming months and will soon be entering the job market. Feel free to contact me for any research opportunities!\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests primarily focus on advancing robotics and autonomous systems, particularly in achieving human-level perception and comprehensive environmental understanding for mobile robotic platforms. I aim to develop cutting-edge AI techniques and methodologies to enable robust and efficient spatial perception solutions, enhancing the reliability, intelligence, and security of intelligent machines in real-world scenarios. Additionally, my research includes efficient camera localization using state space models for edge-cloud collaborative IoT and terminal devices, further enhancing AI applications in these areas.\nTechniques\n: Visual Localization, Adversarial Training, Data Augmentation, Domain Adaptation, 3D Reconstruction, and Neural Rendering\nApplications\n: Autonomous Driving, Robotics, Virtual Reality, edge-cloud collaborative IoT and terminal devices\nPublications\nRADA\nRADA: Robust Adversarial Data Augmentation for Camera Localization in Challenging Conditions\nJialu Wang , Muhamad Risqi U. Saputra , Chris Xiaoxuan Lu , Niki Trigoni and Andrew Markham\n(IROS 2023)\nPaper\nVideo\nCode\nWSCLoc\nWSCLoc: Weakly-Supervised Sparse-View Camera Relocalization via Radiance Field\nJialu wang, Kaichen Zhou, Andrew Markham and Niki Trigoni\n(IROS 2024, Oral Presentation)\nPaper\nProject Website\nMambaLoc\nMambaLoc: Efficient Camera Localization with State Space Model for Edge-Cloud Collaborative IoT and Terminal Devices\nJialu wang, Kaichen Zhou, Andrew Markham and Niki Trigoni\n(Submitted to  RA-L)\nPaper\nVideo\nREDLoc\nREDLoc: Towards Robust, Efficient, and Deployable Visual Localization\nJialu Wang, Bing Wang, Niki Trigoni\n(Submitted to  CVPR 2025)\nServices\nConference Reviewers\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters (\nRA-L\n) 2024\nIEEE International\nConference\non Robotics & Automation (ICRA) 2024\nPowered by Jekyll and\nMinimal Light\ntheme."
  },
