  "serper::Ling Li": {
    "homepage": "https://lingliatvt.wixsite.com/ling-li",
    "emails": [
      "lingli@seas.harvard.edu",
      "lzli@sea.upenn.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Ling Li's page\ntop of page\nThis website was built on Wix. Create yours today.\nGet Started\nLaboratory of Biological and\nBio-inspired Materials\nMaterials Science and Engineering\n@ University of Pennsylvania\nUntitled-1\nAsset 11\nAsset 13\nUntitled-1\n1/8\nWelcome!\n​\nThe Laboratory of Biological and Bio-inspired Materials led by Dr. Ling Li is based at the Department of Mechanical Engineering at Virginia Tech. Our group seeks to discover the fundamental structure-property relationships in multifunctional biological materials, elucidate the formation principles for biological and bio-inspired materials, develop novel in-situ mechanical measurement and\nanalysis technologies, and finally develop bio-inspired structural and multifunctional materials. Feel free to browse our group website for more details.\nIf you have any questions about me or my research, feel free to email me at\nlzli@sea.upenn.edu\n.\nOur group is moving to the Department of Materials Science and Engineering at University of\nPennsylvania\nin January 2024\n. The new group website will be updated soon. For information regarding graduate and postdoc openings, please email Dr. Li at lzli/at/seas/dot/upenn/dot/edu.\nMore news\n..\nbottom of page"
  },
  "serper::Ke Xu": {
    "homepage": "https://lukexuke.github.io/",
    "emails": [
