    "homepage_text": "Yinshuang Xu 许吟霜\nYinshuang Xu 许吟霜\nI'm a fifth year Ph.D. student at the Department of\nComputer and Information Science\n,\nUniversity of\n                    Pennsylvania\n, and my advisor is Prof.\nKostas Daniilidis\n.\nBefore that, I got my bachelor's degree in Engineering Mechanics at\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nand my master's degree in Robotics at University of Pennsylvania.\nMy research interest lies in equivariance, geometric deep learning and their applications in computer vision, robotics and machine learning.\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\nResearch\nEqNIO: Subequivariant Neural Inertial Odometry\nRoyina Karegoudra Jayanth*\n,\nYinshuang Xu*\n,\nZiyun Wang\n,\nEvangelos Chatzipantazis\n,\nDaniel Gehrig\n,\nKostas Daniilidis\nICLR\n, 2025\npaper\n/\nbibtex\n\\(SE(3)\\) Equivariant Ray Embeddings for Implicit Multi-View Depth Estimation\nYinshuang Xu\n,\nDian Chen\n,\nKatherine Liu\n,\nSergey Zakharov\n,\nRares Andrei Ambrus\n,\nKostas Daniilidis\n,\nVitor Campagnolo Guizilini\nNeurIPS\n, 2024\npaper\n/\nbibtex\n\\(SE(3)\\) Equivariant Convolution and Transformer in Ray Space\nYinshuang Xu\n,\nJiahui Lei\n,\nKostas Daniilidis\nNeurIPS\n(Spotlight), 2023\npaper\n/\ncode\n/\nbibtex\nUnified Fourier-based Kernel and Nonlinearity Design for Equivariant Networks\n                    on Homogeneous Spaces\nYinshuang Xu*\n,\nJiahui Lei*\n,\nEdgar Dobriban\n,\nKostas Daniilidis\nICML\n(Spotlight), 2022\narXiv\n/\nbibtex\nEquivariant Multi-View Networks\nCarlos Esteves*\n,\nYinshuang Xu*\n,\nChristine Allen-Blanchette\n,\nKostas Daniilidis\nICCV\n(Oral), 2019\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\nposter\n/\nbibtex\nNested Scale-Editing for Conditional Image Synthesis\nLingzhi Zhang*\n, Jiancong Wang*,\nYinshuang Xu\n, Jie Min, Tarmily Wen,\nJames C. Gee\n,\nJianbo Shi\nCVPR\n, 2020\narXiv\n/\nbibtex\nTeaching\nCIS580\n: Machine Perception\n. Teaching assistant,\nSpring2020\n,\nSpring2021\nESE546\n: Principles of Deep Learning\n. Teaching assistant, Fall2021\nService\nICML reviewer\n(International Conference on Machine Learning)\nECCV reviewer\n(European Conference on Computer Vison)\nNeurIPS reviewer\n(Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems)\nCVPR reviewer\n(Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition)\nICLR reviewer\n(International Conference on Learning Representations)\nCo-organizer:\nCVPR2024 Workshop on\nEquivariant Vision: From Theory to Practice\nCo-organizer:\nRSS2024 Workshop on\nEquivariant Robotics: The Role of Symmetry Across Perception, Estimation, and\n                    Control\nCo-organizer:\nCVPR2025 Workshop on\nEquivariant Vision: From Theory to Practice\nDeveloped from this webpage"
