    "homepage_text": "Dongjie Yu - HKU\nDongjie Yu\nAbout\nCV\nResearch\nPublications\nProjects\nDongjie Yu\n余冬杰\nDongjie Yu\nPhD student\nPan's Lab\nDepartment of Computer Science\nThe University of Hong Kong\nMail box 132, Floor 3, Chow Yei Ching Bulding, The University of Hong Kong, Pokfulam Road, Central and Western District, Hong Kong 999077\nEmail: djyu [at] connect [dot] hku [dot] hk\nORCID\n·\nGoogle Scholar\n·\nGithub\nBrief Introduction\nI am a PhD student in Computer Science at the Department of Computer Science, The University of Hong Kong, fortunately advised by\nProf. Jia Pan\n. Now I am working on robot learning approaches, especially imitation learning, for manipulation tasks.\nBefore that, I received the M.S. and B.S. degree in Mechanical Engineering at the School of Vehicle and Mobility from Tsinghua University, Beijing, China, in 2023 and 2020, respectively.\nAt THU, I was supervised by\nProf. Shengbo Li\nwho leads\niDLab\n, working on reinforcement learning applied in autonomous driving. I also collabrated with\nProf. Jianyu Chen\n, who leads the Intelligent System and Robotics Lab at Institute of Interdisciplinary Information Sciences, Tsinghua University. During my time as a Master student, I was interested in reinforcement learning (RL) combined with optimal control, especially safe RL (where agents should not violate certain state constraints during and/or after the learning process), and their applications to autonomous driving and robotics.\nNews\n08/2024: Check our WAFR 2024 paper\nBiKC: Keypose-Conditioned Consistency Policy for Bimanual Robotic Manipulatio\n, introducing a hierarchical policy for bimanual robotic manipulation. Congrats to all co-authors!\n09/2023: Check our paper\nSafe Model-Based Reinforcement Learning with an Uncertainty-Aware Reachability Certificate\naccepted by IEEE Transactions on Automation Science and Engineering. Congrats to all co-authors!\n05/2022: Our paper\nReachability Constrained Reinforcement Learning\nwas accepted for short presentation at ICML 2022. Thank all co-authors!\nPage generated 2025-09-07 20:53:29 CST, by\njemdoc+MathJax\n."
  },
