  "serper::Shipu Zhao": {
    "homepage": "https://www.shiyuzhao.net/",
    "emails": [
      "zhaoshiyu@westlake.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/MathFoundationRL",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Shiyu Zhao's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nShiyu Zhao's Homepage\nHome\nShiyu Zhao\nDirector of the\nWINDY Lab\n,\nAssociate Head of Department\nDepartment of Artificial Intelligence\n,\nSchool of Engineering\n,\nWestlake University\n,\nHangzhou, China\nEmail: zhaoshiyu[AT]westlake.edu.cn\nWelcome to my homepage!\nMore information about my research group (WINDY Lab) can be found at\nhttps://shiyuzhao.westlake.edu.cn\nBio:\nShiyu Zhao is currently an Associate Professor and Associate Head of the Department of Artificial Intelligence in the School of Engineering at Westlake University. He is the founder and director of the Intelligent Unmanned Systems Laboratory (WINDY Lab). His research focuses on aerial manipulation robotics (single-robot systems) and general swarm intelligence (multi-robot systems), with a particular emphasis on decision-making, perception, and system development. Currently, he serves as the Executive Editor-in-Chief of Unmanned Systems and an Associate Editor for the International Journal of Robotics Research (IJRR). Previously, he served as an associate editor for IEEE-RAL and IJRNC, Program Committee Chair and UK Regional Chair for IEEE ICCA, a member of the IEEE Control Systems Society Conference Editorial Board Committee, and an associate editor for several premier international conferences, including IEEE ICRA, IROS, CDC, and ACC. He has been consistently listed in the Stanford-Elsevier World’s Top 2% Scientists rankings, both in the career-long and single-year categories. He independently created a textbook and an open course titled “Mathematical Foundations of Reinforcement Learning.” The textbook has sold over 15,000 copies to date with its GitHub repository receiving over 14,000 stars. The open course has received over 2.5 million views across platforms.\nShiyu Zhao received his BE and ME degrees from Beijing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics in 2006 and 2009, respectively. He got his PhD in Electrical and Computer Engineering from the National University of Singapore in 2014. He was a postdoctoral researcher at the Technion – Israel Institute of Technology and the University of California, Riverside from 2014 to 2016. In 2016, he became a Lecturer in Aerospace Systems in the Department of Automatic Control at the University of Sheffield, UK. He joined Westlake University in 2019. He is an IET Fellow and IEEE Senior Member.\nHighlight:\n(Mar 2026) IET Fellow:\nI was recently selected as an IET Fellow\n(Feb 2026) Five ICRA papers:\nWe have five papers accepted for publication by IEEE ICRA 2026. Please see the publication page.\n(Jan 2026) Nature Electronics:\nOn January 30th, Nature Electronics published its first issue of 2026 online, designating\nrobotics as its \"Technology of the Year 2026.\"\nThis issue includes\nfour Comment articles\n, each corresponding to one of the four development directions in robotics. I am honored to be invited to contribute the comment titled \"Collective General Collective Intelligence of Multi-Robot Systems.\"​ In this article, drawing on over a decade of research experience in multi-robot systems, I argue that advancing from specialized to general tasks is a key direction for multi-robot systems as they move toward open-world applications.\nNature Electronics website\n(Jan 2026) npj Robotics and TRO papers:\nOur recent work on multi-robot systems and target motion estimation has been accepted for publication by\nnpj Robotics\nand\nIEEE Transactions on Robotics\n. You are welcome to check.\n(Sep 2025)\nNature\n:\nIt's exciting that we have a research article published by Nature. The research article is about aerial manipulation.\nhttps://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09575-x\n(Jun 2025) IROS and other paper\ns\n:\nWe have four papers accepted by IROS 2025 and one paper accepted by IEEE-RAL lately. You are welcome to check our publication page.\n(May 2025)\nIEEE Senior Member:\nI was promoted to an\nIEEE Senior Member\nlately.\n(May 2025) IROS2025 workshop:\nWe are organizing a workshop at ​​IROS 2025​​, which will be held in the beautiful city of ​​Hangzhou​​ (where I’m based!). The workshop is titled ​​\"\nMulti-Robot Systems Empowered by Large Language Models\n\"​​ and has already been accepted, receiving highly positive feedback from the reviewers. Feel free to check out the\nworkshop’s homepage\nfor more details!\n(Apr 2025) <\n强化学习的数学原理\n>\nThe Chinese version of my textbook \"Mathematical Foundations of Reinforcement Learning\" has been published in China by Tsinghua University Press in April 2025.\n(Mar 2025) Six research papers:\nSix research articles have been uploaded to arxiv.\nYou are welcome to check on the Publication page\n(Feb 2025) ICRA and Automatica papers:\nRecently we have two papers accepted by ICRA2025 and one by Automatica. These papers are about cooperative aerial target motion estimation and aerial manipulation. You are welcome to check on the Publication page.\n(Sep 2024)\nWorld's Top 2% Scientists:\nI\nwas selected as one of the World's Top 2% Scientists by Stanford University. I simultaneously entered both the \"Career-long impact\" and \"Single-year impact\" ranks. My rank is top 0.2%=250/113,906 in the subfield\n.\n(Jul 2024)\nEnglish open course\n: My\nEnglish open course on reinforcement learning is online now! You are welcome to check our\nYouTube channel\nor\nGitHub homepage\n. The Chinese version of the open course has received 1,000,000 views over the Internet has received very good feedback from the readers.\n(May 2024) IEEE-TRO paper:\nOur latest work \"Keypoint-Guided Efficient Pose Estimation and Domain Adaptation for Micro Aerial Vehicles\" has been accepted for publication by\nIEEE Transactions on Robotics\n. More details can be found on my publication page.\n(Mar 2024) Our GitHub:\nMost of the code of our research work can be found in our GitHub page! Welcome to check https://github.com/WestlakeIntelligentRobotics\n(Feb 2024) IEEE-TASE paper:\nOur research work \"\nDomain a\ndaptive detection of MAVs: A benchmark and noise suppression network\"\nhas been accepted for publication by IEEE\nTransactions on Automation Science and Engineering.\nThe paper will be online soon.\n(Jan 2024) Multiple papers:\nWe got three research articles accepted for publication lately by\nIEEE Transactions on Automation Science and Engineering\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems\n, and\nNew Journal of Physics\n, respectively.\n(Jan 2024) My RL course:\na student from the UC Davis emailed me and would like to share the notes he made when he studied my RL textbook. You are welcome to visit:\nlink\n(Jan 2024) IJRR paper:\nOur recent work about vision-based target motion estimation has been officially accepted by the\nInternational Journal of Robotics Research\n.\n(Nov 2023) Our first LLM work:\nOur first research work about large language models is online.\narXiv link\nPaper website\n(Sep 2023) Source code available:\nThe source code of our Nature Communications work on robotic swarms is uploaded online:\nGitHub\n(Sep 2023) AE for IEEE-RAL:\nI recently became an Associate Editor for IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters. This journal has a very efficient and high-standard reviewing process. High-quality robotics-related submissions are welcome.\n(Sep 2023) 1000+ stars:\nMy textbook\n\"Mathematical foundation of reinforcement learning\" has received more than\n1000\nstars\nin\nGitHub\n.\n(Aug 2023)\nTextbook major update:\nThe second version of the draft of my textbook \"Mathematical foundation of reinforcement learning\" is online now!!  Compared to the first version, which was online one year ago, the second version has been improved in various ways. It is almost the same as the printed version. See the\nGitHub page\nfor details.\n(Jun 2023)\nNature Communications:\nOur recent research work entitled \"\nMean-shift exploration in shape assembly of robot swarms\n\" has been published by Nature Communications:\nhttps://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-023-39251-5\n(June, 2023)\n(Dec 2022) Lecture videos:\nMy new lecture videos and slides on the course \"\nMathematical Foundations of Reinforcement Learning\n\" are online now. For the videos (in Chinese), please check:\nhttps://space.bilibili.com/2044042934\n(Aug 2022) Textbook:\nMy new textbook (draft) entitled \"Mathematical Foundations of Reinforcement Learning\" is online now.\nThe GitHub homepage of this book is here.\nThis book aims to provide a mathematical but friendly introduction to the fundamental concepts, basic problems, and classical algorithms in reinforcement learning.\nMedia channels:\nOur\nYouTube\nand\nBilibili\nvideo channels are open! Welcome to check our videos out.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
