    "homepage_text": "Gang Li, PhD | Department of Pathology\nSkip to main content\nDepartment of Pathology\nGang Li, PhD\nAssistant Professor of Medicine, Division of Cardiology/The Aging Institute\nOffice Location:\nBridgeside Point I\nRoom 561\n100 Technology Drive\nPittsburgh, PA 15219\nContact Information:\nOffice Telephone: 412-383-3429\nEmail: lig@pitt.edu\nResearch Interests\nThe main research interest in Dr. Li’s lab is to understand the molecular mechanisms underlying the contribution of disease-associated functional SNPs to the pathogenesis of, and the susceptibility to age-related diseases. To do so, Dr. Li’s lab has recently developed multiple cutting edge techniques to rapidly identify disease-associated functional SNPs based on GWAS analysis and characterize these functional SNPs by identifying the SNP-bound regulatory proteins that modulate risk gene expression. Currently, Dr. Li’s lab is focusing on studying the role of cellular senescence and ferroptosis (iron-induced cell death) in the pathogenesis of two age-related diseases: atherosclerosis and Alzheimer’s disease. The lab’s goal is to use human genetics as a guide to identify new drug targets and, ultimately, to apply these findings to develop precision medicines for age-related diseases.\nSelected Publications:\nTing Wu, Yuwei Wu, Danli Jiang, Wei Sun, Meijuan Zou, Sathish Babu Vasamsetti\n,\nPartha Dutta,\nSteven A. Leers\n,\nWu Di, and\nGang Li\n(\n2023\n)\nSATB2, coordinated with CUX1, regulates IL-1β-induced senescence-like phenotype in endothelial cells by fine-tuning the atherosclerosis-associated p16INK4a expression\n. Aging Cell, 00, e13765. 2023.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1111/acel.13765\nTing Wu and\nGang Li (2022)\nAn Improved EMSA-based Method to Prioritize Candidate cis-REs for Further Functional Validation. Bio-protocol 12(8): e4397. DOI: 10.21769/Bioprotoc.4397.\nXiaoyu Zhang, Meijaun Zou, Yuwei Wu, Danli Jiang, Ting Wu, Yihan Zhao, Di Wu, Jing Cui and\nGang Li\n(\n2022\n) Regulation of the Late Onset Alzheimer’s Disease Associated HLA-DQA1/DRB1 Expression. American Journal of Alzheimer’s Disease & Other Dementias. January 2022. doi:\n10.1177/15333175221085066\nTing Wu, Danli Jiang, Meijuan Zou, Wei Sun, Di Wu, Jing Cui, Ian Huntress, Xinxia Peng, and\nGang Li\n(\n2022\n) Coupling high-throughput mapping with proteomics analysis delineates cis-regulatory elements at high resolution. Nucleic Acids Research Volume 50, Issue 1, 11 January 2022, Page e5,\nhttps://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkab890\nDanli Jiang, Wei Sun, Ting Wu, Meijuan Zou, Sathish Babu Vasamsetti, Xiaoyu Zhang, Yihan Zhao, Julie A. Phillippi, Sina Tavakoli, Partha Dutta, Jonathan Florentin, Stephen Y. Chan, Di Wu, Jing Cui, Ian Huntress, Xinxia Peng, Toren Finkel, and\nGang Li\n(\n2022\n) Post-GWAS functional analysis of the CDKN2A/B locus identifies CUX1 as a regulator of p16INK4a expression and cellular senescence. Nature Aging. 2022;2(2):140-54. doi: 10.1038/s43587-022-00177-0.\nMeijuan Zou, Danli Jiang,\nTing Wu\n,\nXiaoyu Zhang\n,\nYihan Zhao\n, Di Wu, Wei Sun, Jing Cui, Larry Moreland, and\nGang\nLi\n(\n2021\n)\nPost-GWAS functional studies reveal an RA-associated CD40-induced NF-kB signal transduction and transcriptional regulation network targeted by class II HDAC inhibitors.\nHum Mol Genet\n.\n2021 May 28;\n30\n(9)\n:823-835\n. doi: 10.1093/hmg/ddab032. PubMed PMID: 33517445\n; PubMed Central PMCID: PMC8161515\n.\nMeijuan Zou,\nXiaoyu Zhang\n, Danli Jiang,\nYihan Zhao\n,\nTing Wu\n, Qia Gong, Hau Su, Di Wu, Larry Moreland, and\nGang\nLi\n(\n2020\n)\nTranscriptional Regulation of\nCD40\nExpression by 4 Ribosomal Proteins via a Functional SNP on a Disease-Associated\nCD40\nLocus.\nGenes (Basel)\n.\n2020 Dec 21;\n11\n(12)\n. doi: 10.3390/genes11121526. PubMed PMID\n: 33371207\n; PubMed Central PMCID: PMC7767238\n.\nYihan Zhao, Di Wu, Danli Jiang, Xiaoyu Zhang, Ting Wu, Jing Cui, Min Qian, Jean Zhao, Steffi Oesterreich,\nWei Sun,\nToren Finkel,\nand\nGang Li\n(\n2020\n) A sequential methodology for the rapid identification and characterization of breast cancer-associated functional SNPs. Nat. Commun. 11, 3340 (2020) https:doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-17159-8\nGang Li\n(co-corresponding author)\n, Yu Yang, Di Wu, Jing Cui, Hung N. Nguyen, Pierre Cunin, Anaïs Levescot, Ming Bai, Yukinori Okada, Michael B. Brenner, Soumya Raychaudhuri, Eric A. Hendrickson, Richard Maas, and Peter A. Nigrovic\n(\n2018\n) High throughput identification of Disease-associated non-coding functional SNPs via type IIS enzyme restriction. Nature Genet. 2018 Jul. 16; PubMed PMID: 30013183.\nGang Li (co-corresponding author)\n, Pierre Cunin, Yu Yang, Di Wu, Dorothee Diogo, Yukinori Okada, Robert Plenge and Peter Nigrovic (\n2016\n) The rheumatoid arthritics risk variant CCR6DNP regulates CCR6 via PARP-1.\nPLoS Genetics\n. Published September 14, 2016 http://dx.doi.org/10.1371/journal. Pgen. 1006292."
