    "homepage_text": "Yifei Gong - Center for Language Science\nSkip to content\nCenter for\nLanguage Science\nNews\nEvents\nMake a Gift\nMenu\nHome\nAbout\nPeople\nPeople Overview\nCLS Directors\nFaculty\nStaff\nPostdoctoral Fellows\nGraduate Students\nVisiting Scholars\nAffiliates\nAlumni\nResearch\nPublic Engagement\nPublic Engagement Overview\nPeople\nBilingualism Matters\nNewsletters\nLanguage Science Activities\nLinguistic Discrimination Research Repository\nFAQ's About Bilingualism Matters\nLinks and Other Resources\nFunding Opportunities\nCenter for\nLanguage Science\nNext in the Speaker Series\nCenter for Language Science Speaker Series: John Lipski\n9:00 a.m.–10:30 a.m.\nFoster Auditorium, 102 Paterno Library\nApr\n3\nYifei Gong\nHome\nPeople\nYifei Gong\nGraduate Student of Cognitive Psychology\nyfg5209@psu.edu\nWebsites:\nM.A. in Linguistics, Lanzhou University, China, 2023\nBiography:\nYifei Gong is a graduate student in Cognitive Psychology and Language Science of the\nBilingualism and Linguistic Diversity Lab\n. Her research interests center on the cognitive and neural mechanisms underlying bilingualism. Before joining Penn State, she pursued a master’s in Linguistics at Lanzhou University, China, where she examined the relationship between domain-general cognitive control and language control in Tibetan multilingual speakers from Gannan Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture. Through her graduate research at Penn State, she aims to explore the bilingual brain using both neurophysiological techniques and behavioral methods.\nResearch Interests\nBilingualism, language processing, executive control, inhibitory control.\nCenter for\nLanguage Science\n110 Moore Building\nContact Us\nAffiliations\nProgram in Linguistics\nCenter for Language Acquisition\nCollege of the Liberal Arts\nMake a Gift\nInstagram\nFacebook"
  },
