    "homepage_text": "S. Zhang\nPlease note: this is a legacy homepage which is no longer updated (including contact details). I have moved to the\nUniversity of Minnesota\nsince Aug 2019.\nShiwen Zhang\nDepartment of Mathematics\nMichigan State University\n619 Red Cedar Road\nEast Lansing, MI, 48824\nOffice\n: Wells Hall C320\nEmail\n: zhangshiwen@math.msu.edu\nI am a Visiting Assistant Professor  in the\nDepartment of Mathematics\nat the\nMichigan State University\n. I earned my Ph.D. in Mathematics at UC, Irvine in June 2016 under my dissertation advisor:\nSvetlana Jitomirskaya\n.  Here is my curriculum vitae:\nCV\nCurrent Teaching:\nMath 309.\nClass Webpage\n.\nCurrent Undergrad Research Project: Landscape theory for tight-binding Hamiltonians.\nProject Webpage.\nResearch Interests:\nMathematical Physics, Harmonic Analysis, Dynamical Systems,   Geometric Measure Theory,  Partial Differential Equations\nEducation & Employment:\n2016-present: Visiting Assistant Professor,  Department of Mathematics at  the Michigan State University.\n2013-2016: Ph.D. Mathematics, University of California, Irvine — Irvine, CA\n2009-2013: graduate student  in Mathematics, Nanjing University, China. (Transfer to UC Irvine in Sept. 2013)\n2005-2009: B.S. Mathematics, Nanjing University, China.\nPreprints/Publications:\nJ. Schenker, Z. Tilocco and S. Zhang,\nDiffusion in the mean for a periodic Schrödinger equation perturbed by a fluctuating potential\n. Preprint. arXiv:1901.06598.\nS. Jitomirskaya,W. Liu and S. Zhang,\nArithmetic spectral    transitions: a competition between hyperbolicity and the arithmetics of small denominators\n.   (\nLecture Notes.) To appear in IAS/Park City Mathematics Series: Harmonic Analysis, 2018.\nF. Yang, S. Zhang,\nSingular continuous spectrum and generic full spectral/packing dimension for unbounded quasiperiodic Schrödinger operators\n.\nSubmitted\n. arXiv:1804.10732\nR. Han, F. Yang and S. Zhang,\nSpectral dimension for β-almost periodic singular Jacobi operators and the extended Harper's model\n.\nTo appear in Journal d'Analyse Mathématique\n.\nS. Zhang,\nThe exact power law for Buffon's needle landing near some random Cantor sets\n. To appear in  Rev. Mat. Iberoam. (Revista Matemática Iberoamericana).\nR. Han, S. Zhang,\nLarge deviation estimates and Hölder regularity of the Lyapunov exponents for quasi-periodic Schrödinger cocycles\n.  To appear in Int. Math. Res. Not.\nS. Zhang,\nMixed spectral types for one frequency discrete quasi-periodic Schrödinger operator\n.  Proc. Amer. Math. Soc.\n144\n(2016), 2603-2609.\nS. Jitomirskaya, S. Zhang,\nQuantitative continuity of singular continuous spectral     measures and arithmetic criteria for quasiperiodic    Schrödinger operators\n.\nSubmitted\n. arXiv:1510.07086.\nJ. You, S. Zhang and Q. Zhou,\nPoint Spectrum of the Quasi-Periodic Long\r\n    Range Operators\n. J. Spectr. Theory\n4\n(2014),  769-781.\nJ. You and S. Zhang,\nHölder continuity of the Lyapunov exponent for\r\n    analytic quasiperiodic Schrödinger cocycle with\r\n    weak Liouville frequency\n. Ergodic Theory Dynam. Systems\n34\n(2014), 1395-1408.\nS. Zhang, Z. Zhao,\nDiffusion Bound and Reducibility for Discrete Schrödinger Equations with Tangent Potential\n. Front. Math. China\n7\n(2012), 1213-1235\nRecent Conferences &\nSeminars\n:\nOrganizer\n:\n(together with Ilya Kachkovskiy and Matthew Cha),\nAMS Fall Central Sectional Meeting 2018, Special Session \"Ergodic and topological quantum systems\"\n,  Ann Arbor, October 20-21, 2018.\nSeminar Talks\n:\nAnalysis Seminar Talk, Yale University, CT, Spetember 28, 2018\nDynamical Systems Seminar Talk, Tsinghua University, China, May 23, 2018\nErgodic Theory and Spectral Theory Seminar Talk, UCR, May 18, 2018\nDynamical Systems Seminar Talk, MSU, March 1, 2018.\nDynamical Systems Seminar Talk, Nanjing University, Nanjing, China.   July 27, 2017.\nAnalysis and PDE Seminar Talk, MSU.   Oct 31, 2016.\nDynamical Systems and Fractal Geometry Seminar Talk, Mathematics Morningside center, CAS, Beijing, China. May 22, 2015\nDynamical Systems Seminar Talk, Nanjing University,\nNanjing, China.   July 20, 2014.\nGeometry-Analysis Seminar Talk, Rice University, Houston, Texas.   April 23, 2014.\nConferences & Workshops:\nJoint Mathematics Meetings AMS Special Session on Localization and Delocalization for Disordered Quantum Systems, Baltimore Convention Center, January 18-19, 2019.\nSpectral Theory of Quasi-Periodic and Random Operators, CRM, Montreal, November 12-16, 2018.\nRecent Advances in Functional Analysis-dedicated to the memory of Joe Diestel and Victor Lomonosov, poster session, Kent State University, October 11-14, 2018.\nYoung Researchers Symposium at ICMP, McGill University, Montreal 07/21/2018\n28th Annual PCMI Summer Session: Research Program in  Harmonic Analysis, Park City, Utah, July 1 – July 21, 2018.\nSpecial Session  on ``Spectral Theory'' at the AMS sectional meeting, Portland, OR, April 14-15, 2018\n8th Ohio River Analysis Meeting, University of Kentucky, Lexington, March 24-25, 2018\nSpecial Session on Spectral Theory, Disorder and Quantum Physics at the JMM, San Diego, CA, Jan 10-13, 2018\nRecent Developments in Harmonic Analysis, MSRI, Berkeley, CA 05/15-05/19/2017\n7th Ohio River Analysis Meeting, University of Cincinnati 03/25/2017\nIntroductory Workshop: Harmonic Analysis, MSRI, Berkeley, CA 01/23-01/27/2017\nAMS Special Session\nat the Joint Mathematics Meeting, Seattle, WA, Jan 6-9, 2016\nAMS Fall Western Sectional Meeting, Fullerton, CA, Oct 24-25, 2015\nWorkshop: Spectral Properties of Quasicrystals via Analysis, Dynamics, and Geometric Measure Theory, BIRS, Oaxaca, Mexico,  Sept 27-Oct 2, 2015\nAlmost Periodic and Other Ergodic Problems, University of Cambridge, UK, Mar 20-May 20, 2015\n33nd Annual Western States Mathematical Physics Meeting, Caltech, Pasadena, CA, Feb 16-17, 2015\nSpecial Session at the USA-Uzbekistan Conference on Analysis and Mathematical Physics, CSUF, Fullerton ,CA, May 20-24, 2014\nTeaching/General audience Talks:\nMath. Department Colloquium, Oberlin College, Oberlin, OH. 09/20/2018\nDepartment Seminar, Loyola Marymount University, Los Angeles, CA.  Nov 5, 2015\nColloquium at CSULB, Long Beach, CA. Mar 13, 2015\nGeometry and Topology Seminar, CSUF, Fullerton, CA.  Feb 20, 2015\nAwards/Honors:\nKovalevsky Outstanding PhD Thesis Award, UC Irvine  2016\nEuler Award for Outstanding Promise as a Graduate Student, UC Irvine 2014\nSamsung Scholarship, Nanjing University, China 2007\nNational Encouragement Scholarship, Nanjing University, China 2006\nTeaching at MSU:\nUndergrad Rsearch Program\nat MSU (part of the Discovering America Program    of math department at MSU) on\nLandscape theory\n,  Fall 2018, Spring 2019.\nProject website\n(under construction).\nTeaching Assistant for lectures by Svetlana Jitomirskaya at the PCMI Graduate Summer School on Harmonic Analysis, Park City, July 2018:\nArithmetic spectral transitions: a competition between hyperbolicity and the arithmetics of small denominators\n, July 8–14, 2018\nInstructor\n:\nSpring 2019, Math 309.\nClass Webpage\n.\nFall 2018, Math 132.\nClass Webpage\n.\nSpring 2018, Math 132.\nClass Webpage\n.\nFall 2017, Math 133.\nClass Webpage\n.\nSpring 2017, Math 132.\nClass Webpage\n.\nFall 2016, Math 133.\nClass Webpage\n.\nPast Teaching at UCI:\nWinter 2015,\nUC Irvine\n:\nTA\nMath 3D, Elementary Differential Equation.\nFall 2015,\nUC Irvine\n:\nInstructor\nfor Math 2B, Calculus II.\nCourse Webpage\nSummer 2015,\nUC Irvine\n:\nTA\nMath 176/Econ135: Math of Finance (Summer Session II, 2015)\nFall 2014,\nUC Irvine\n:\nTA\nMath 2B: Calculus II"
  },
