    "homepage_text": "Sheng Guo's Research  Group - PI\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nSheng Guo's Research  Group\nPI\nDr. Sheng Guo (郭晟)\nIndustrial and Materials Science\nChalmers University of Technology\nGothenburg, SE-41296, Sweden\n# Current Position\n2020.9- Professor\nIndustrial and Materials Science, Chalmers University of Technology, Sweden\nResearch area: Alloy design, and structural and functional properties of high entropy alloys\n# Previous Positions\n2017.5- 2020.8 Associate Professor\nIndustrial and Materials Science, Chalmers University of Technology, Sweden\n2016.6- 2017.4 Associate Professor\nMaterials and Manufacturing Technology, Chalmers University of Technology, Sweden\n2013.4- 2016.5 Assistant Professor\nMaterials and Manufacturing Technology, Chalmers University of Technology, Sweden\n2011.5-2013.3 Research Fellow\nMechanical and Biomedical Engineering Department, City University Hong Kong, Hong Kong\n2009.5-2011.5 Postdoctoral Fellow\nMechanical Engineering Department, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University, Hong Kong\n2009.11-2010.2 Visiting Researcher\nWPI-AIMR, Tohoku University, Japan\n# Education\n2016.3 Docent in High Entropy Materials (educational title)\nChalmers University of Technology, Gothenburg, Sweden\n2005.10-2009.3 D. Phil in Materials Science\nUniversity of Oxford, Oxford, United Kingdom\n2002.9-2005.6 M. Eng in Materials Science and Engineering\nCentral South University, Changsha, China\n1998.9-2002.6 B. Eng in Powder Metallurgy\nCentral South University, Changsha, China\n# Invited Lectures\n2024.4 Keynote speaker at IIAP-HEA (Industry Insights and Academia Perspectives on High Entropy Alloys) 2024, Jodhpur, India\n2023.7 Invited lecture at Powder Metallurgy Research Institute, Central South University, China\n2023.5 Invited speaker at Directionally Solidified Eutectics Conference – VII, Istanbul, Turkey\n2023.5 Invited speaker at ISE Research Seminar Series, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University\n2022.11 Invited speaker at ASM Finland High Entropy Alloys webinar, Finland\n2022.11 Invited external speaker at ECMetAC (European Integrated Center for the Development of Metallic Alloys & Compounds) 2022, High-Entropy Alloys: From Basic Studies to Industrial Applications, Split, Croatia.\n2022.5 Invited speaker at DGM (German Materials Society) Symposium \"High Entropy Alloys: Potential for industrial applications\", Dresden, Germany\n2022.3 Invited speaker at DGM (German Materials Society) workshop on Functional High Entropy Alloys, Bochum, Germany\n2021.10 Invited speaker at Jacob Wallenberg Foundation Seminar, Slottsviken SKF, Gothenburg, Sweden\n2021.10 Invited lecture for Materials Science PhD students at Northwestern Polytechnical University (online), Xi’an, China\n2021.9 Invited lecture at Tandem Webinar series, Area of Advance Materials Science, Chalmers University of Technology, Gothenburg, Sweden\n2021.8 Invited lecturer at the International Summer School on Structural and Functional Materials (online), Changsha, China\n2021.5 Invited speaker at Thermec’2021 Virtual Conference, organized by TU Graz, Austria\n2021.3 Invited external speaker at ECMetAC (European Integrated Center for the Development of Metallic Alloys & Compounds) on-line workshop, High-Entropy Alloys: From Basic Studies to Industrial Applications\n2020.1 Invited lecture at Department of Manufacturing and Materials Engineering, University of Campinas (UNICAMP), Brazil\n2019.9 Invited lecturer at the 5\nth\nSummer School of Condensed Matter on Energy, Szczecin, Poland\n2019.7 Invited speaker at ISMANAM (International Symposium of Metastable, Amorphous and Nanostructured Materials)-2019, Chennai, India\n2018.12 Invited speaker at the 2\nnd\nInternational Conference on High-Entropy Materials, Jeju Island, South Korea (session chair)\n2108.10 Invited lecture at Institute of Plasma Physics, Czech Academy of Science, Czech Republic\n2018.5 Invited speaker for voestalpine Synergy Platform 2018, Vienna, Austria\n2018.4 Invited lecture at the Jožef Stefan Institute, Ljubljana, Slovenia\n2018.3 Invited lecture at College of Engineering, Koc University, Istanbul, Turkey\n2017.9 Invited speaker for EUROMAT 2017, Thessaloniki, Greece (session chair)\n2017.8 Invited lecture at Material Science and Characterization section, Wind Energy Department, Denmark University of Technology, Roskilde, Denmark\n2017.7 Invited speaker for FiMPART (Frontiers in Materials Processing Applications, Research and Technology) 2017, Bordeaux, France\n2016.11 Invited speaker for International Conference on High-Entropy Materials, Hsinchu, Taiwan (session chair)\n2015.8 Invited lecture at European Space Research and Technology Centre (ESTEC) at Noordwijk, Netherlands\n2014.3 Invited lecture at Sandvik Coromant, Stockholm, Sweden\n2013.11 Invited lecture at Materials Microstructure division, Applied Physics Department, Chalmers University of Technology, Gothenburg, Sweden\n# Training on Pedagogy, Leadership and Entrepreneurship\n2013-2015 Diploma of Higher Education, completing 18 higher education credit points on courses dedicated to theory and practice of teaching, learning and supervision, Chalmers University of Technology\n2014-2015 Leadership Program for Chalmers Areas of Advance Assistant Professors, a program to support trainees to become critical independent researchers at the highest international level\n2013-2014 Mentor4Research Program (now Mentors2Research), supported by IVA (The Royal Swedish Academy of Engineering) and aiming for a catalyst for commercializing academic research results\n# Commission of Trust\n2024- Member of International Scientific Committee, Center of Excellence NOMATEN, National Centre for Nuclear Research, Poland\n2024- Review panelist for research applications in mechanics, structural and materials engineering submitted to the Research Council of Finland, Finland\n2023 External evaluator, for docent qualification assessment at Karlstad University\n2023- External reviewer, for research proposals applying to M-ERA.NET, European Union\n2023-2024 Board member, Swedish Neutron Scattering Society\n2023- Editorial board, European Journal of Materials, Taylor & Francis\n2023 External reviewer, for Research Assessment Exercise (RAE) at Department of Industrial and System Engineering, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University, Hong Kong, China\n2023- Editorial board, journal Metals, MDPI\n2023- Editorial board, journal Materials Research Express, IOP Publishing\n2023 International advisory Committee member, the 3rd World Congress on High Entropy Alloys (HEA 2023), Pittsburg, USA\n2023 Organizer for symposium High Entropy Alloys at Euromat 2023, Frankfurt, Germany\n2022 External reviewer, for faculty appointment/postdoc researchers recruitment assessment at University West\n2022 External reviewer, for faculty appointment assessment at Zhejiang University, China\n2022- External reviewer, for research proposals applying to the German Research Foundation (DFG), Germany\n2022- Editorial advisory board, journal High Entropy Alloys & Materials, Springer\n2021- Associate Editor, Structural Materials section within Frontiers in Materials and Frontiers in Built Environment, Frontiers\n2021- External reviewer, for research proposals applying to The Czech Science Foundation (GACR), Czech Republic\n2021 External reviewer, for research proposals applying to the Research Council of Norway (RCN)\n2021 External reviewer, for faculty appointment assessment at University of Ljubljana, Slovenia\n2021 Organizer for symposium High Entropy Alloys at Euromat 2021, Virtual Conference\n2021 Organizer for symposium Mechanochemical Coupling in Chemical Treatment and Materials Degradation—Modeling and Experimentation at MRS 2021 Virtual Spring Meeting\n2021 Remote external reviewers for the ADMIRE Postdoctoral Fellowship Programme, a Marie Skłodowska-Curie COFUND Action, hosted by the Science Foundation Ireland Centre for Advanced Materials and BioEngineering Research\n2021- Editorial board, journal Advanced Powder Materials, Elsevier\n2020- External reviewer, for research proposals applying to the Austrian Science Fund (FWF), Austria\n2020 External reviewer, for faculty appointment assessment at The Hong Kong Polytechnic University, Hong Kong, China\n2020 External reviewer, for faculty appointment assessment at American University of Sharjah, UAE\n2020 External reviewer, for faculty appointment assessment at Dalarna University\n2020- External reviewer, for research proposals applying to the Israeli Ministry of Science and Technology, Israel\n2020- External reviewer, for research proposals applying to the French National Research Agency (ANR), France\n2020 Editorial board, journal Tungsten, Springer\n2020 External reviewer, for research proposals applying to Research Council KU Leuven, Belgium\n2020- Opponent or committee members for PhD (Fernando Henrique da Costa/University of Campinas, Brazil; Saber Haratian/DTU, Denmark; Rahul John/Deakin University, Australia; Reliance Jain/Indian Institute of Technology Indore, India; Roopam Jain/ Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur, India; Angelo Fernandes Andreoli/TU Dresden, Germany; Xuan Yang/Aalto University, Finland; Madan Patnamsetty/Tampere University, Finland) dissertation defenses outside Sweden\n2020- External reviewer, for research proposals applying to Department of Energy (DOE/ASCR), United States\n2019 Guest editor for a special issue on high-entropy alloys for the journal Frontier in Materials (Frontiers)\n2019 Project Peer Reviewer (Lead Reviewer), for the Science Fund of the Republic of Serbia (SF), Serbia\n2019 Remote referee, for ERC Consolidator Grant, European Research Council\n2019 Organizer for symposium High Entropy Alloys at Euromat 2019, Stockholm, Sweden\n2019 Editorial board, journal Materials & Design, Elsevier\n2018- External reviewer, for research proposals applying to The Croatian Science Foundation (HRZZ), Croatia\n2018 Member of Scientific Program Committee for the 2\nnd\nInternational Conference on High-Entropy Materials, Jeju Island, South Korea\n2017-\nExternal ...[truncated]"
