    "homepage_text": "Bailin Wang\nBailin\nWang\nResearcher at Meta, working on multimodal and long-context modeling.\nPreviously: Apple, MIT, Microsoft and University of Edinburgh.\n(Recurrent) Research Interests:\nlong context modeling with memory,\ntest-time training at scale.\nI’m currently based in NYC. Feel free to reach out : )\nnews\nJan 20, 2026\nWe released a new sparse attention model for long context, see\npreprint\n.\nJul 17, 2025\nRAttention code is released\nhere\nin Axlearn.\nJun 20, 2025\nYour sliding window size of local attention can be reduced to 512, see\npreprint\n.\nJan 22, 2025\nWe have open-sourced Jax/Pallas implementatins of Mamba/Mamba2 via\nAxlearn\nselected publications\narXiv\nSPLA: Block Sparse Plus Linear Attention for Long Context Modeling\nBailin Wang\n, Dan Friedman, Tao Lei, and Chong Wang\nPreprint\n, 2026\narXiv\narXiv\nRAttention: Towards the Minimal Sliding Window Size in Local-Global Attention Models\nBailin Wang\n, Chang Lan, Chong Wang, and Ruoming Pang\nPreprint\n, 2025\narXiv\nCode\nICML\nGated linear attention transformers with hardware-efficient training\nSonglin Yang*,\nBailin Wang*\n, Yikang Shen, Rameswar Panda, and Yoon Kim\nICML\n, 2024\narXiv\nCode\nICML\nIn-Context Language Learning: Architectures and Algorithms\nEkin Akyürek,\nBailin Wang\n, Yoon Kim, and Jacob Andreas\nICML\n, 2024\narXiv\nCode\nNeurIPS\nParallelizing Linear Transformers with the Delta Rule over Sequence Length\nSonglin Yang,\nBailin Wang\n, Yu Zhang, Yikang Shen, and Yoon Kim\nNeurIPS\n, 2024\narXiv\nCode\nNeurIPS\nStructured Reordering for Modeling Latent Alignments in Sequence Transduction\nBailin Wang\n, Mirella Lapata, and Ivan Titov\nNeurIPS\n, 2021\narXiv\nCode\nlatest posts\nJun 14, 2024\nThe End of Training Log"
  },
  "serper::Y. Tan": {
    "homepage": "https://research-information.bris.ac.uk/en/persons/y-tan/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Y Tan\n      -  University of Bristol\nUniversity of Bristol Home\nHelp & Terms of Use\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at University of Bristol\nView Scopus Profile\nDr Y Tan\nPhD(Bristol)\nResearch Fellow\n,\nBristol Medical School (PHS)\nBristol Population Health Science Institute\nMRC Integrative Epidemiology Unit\nEmail\nVanessa.Tan\nbristol.ac\nuk\nBS1 5DS\nPersonal profile\nResearch interests\nI am a Post-doctoral Research Associate in Applied Genetic Epidemiology in the Cancer Research UK  (CRUK) programme based in the School of Social and Community Medicine. I am currently working on the design and undertaking of Recall by Genotype (RbG) studies under the supervision of Dr Nicholas Timpson. The RbG studies involve the recruitment of a subset of participants or their biosamples from an existing cohort for more detailed phenotypic analysis. The aim of my research is to understand biological mechanisms underlying cancer risk and progression by undertaking the RbG studies.\nI did a cross-disciplinary Ph.D. in Cell Biology and Clinical Epidemiology. My Ph.D. research involved using a unique combination of cell biology and epidemiological approaches to better understand the regulation of fascin-1 in cancer and the translational potential of fascin-1, as well as its regulators, as potential cancer biomarkers.\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Y Tan is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n12\nSimilar Profiles\nMendelian Randomization Analysis\nMedicine and Dentistry\n100%\nMendelian Randomization\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n79%\nCancer Risk\nMedicine and Dentistry\n60%\nProstate Cancer\nPharmacology, Toxicology and Pharmaceutical Science\n47%\nMetabolite\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n44%\nBody Mass Index\nMedicine and Dentistry\n37%\nGenome-Wide Association Study\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n36%\nMalignant Neoplasm\nPharmacology, Toxicology and Pharmaceutical Science\n36%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n16\nArticle (Academic Journal)\n2\nReview article (Academic Journal)\n1\nConference Abstract\n1\nComment/debate (Academic Journal)\nAdiposity, metabolites and endometrial cancer risk: Inference from combinations of Mendelian randomization and Observational analyses\nTan, Y.\n,\nLee, M.\n, Pournaras, D., Wang, S., Gunter, M., Dossus, L.,\nWade, K. H.\n,\nCorbin, L. J.\n&\nTimpson, N. J.\n,\n21 Oct 2025\n,\nIn:\nBMC Cancer.\n25\n,\n1\n,\n15 p.\n, 1619.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle (Academic Journal)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nMendelian Randomization Analysis\n100%\nCancer Risk\n100%\nUterine Cancer\n100%\nMetabolite\n100%\nBody Mass Index\n42%\nA Genome-Wide Association Study Using the Bacillus Calmette-Guerin Scar to Elucidate the Genetic Basis of Scarring in a European Population\nCollins, I.,\nCanadas Garre, M.\n,\nPeña, O.\n,\nTan, Y.\n,\nMartin, P. B.\n,\nTimpson, N. J.\n& al , E.,\n1 Oct 2025\n,\np. 21-22\n.\n2 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to conference\n›\nConference Abstract\nThe Effect of Circulating Proteins and Their Role in Mediating Adiposity's Effect on Endometrial Cancer Risk: Mendelian Randomization and Colocalization Analyses\nWang, S. E.,\nTan, V. Y.\n,\nYarmolinsky, J.\n, Zheng, Y., O'Mara, T. A.,\nTimpson, N. J.\n, Gunter, M. J., Dossus, L. &\nLee, M. A.\n,\n1 Sept 2025\n,\nIn:\nCancer Epidemiology Biomarkers and Prevention.\n34\n,\n9\n,\np. 1534-1543\n10 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle (Academic Journal)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nPTEN (Gene)\n100%\nLCN2\n100%\nView all 20 research outputs\nProjects\n1\nActive\nRole of directly measured metabolic profile as an intermediate between adiposity and endometrial cancer: triangulation of evidence from independent sources\nTimpson, N. J.\n(Principal Investigator) &\nTan, Y.\n(Co-Principal Investigator)\n1/05/23\n→\n1/05/26\nProject\n:\nResearch\nDatasets\nAdditional file 2 of Identifying molecular mediators of the relationship between body mass index and endometrial cancer risk: a Mendelian randomization analysis\nHazelwood, E.\n(Creator),\nSanderson, E.\n(Creator),\nTan, V. Y.\n(Creator), Ruth, K. S. (Creator), Frayling, T. M. (Creator), Dimou, N. (Creator), Gunter, M. J. (Creator), Dossus, L. (Creator), Newton, C. (Creator),\nRyan, N.\n(Creator), Pournaras, D. J. (Creator), O’Mara, T. A. (Creator),\nDavey Smith, G.\n(Creator),\nMartin, R. M.\n(Creator) &\nYarmolinsky, J.\n(Creator), figshare,\n19 Apr 2022\nDOI\n:\n10.6084/m9.figshare.19613752\n,\nhttps://springernature.figshare.com/articles/dataset/Additional_file_2_of_Identifying_molecular_mediators_of_the_relationship_between_body_mass_index_and_endometrial_cancer_risk_a_Mendelian_randomization_analysis/19613752\nDataset\nGenome-wide Association Study of Cancer Risk in UK Biobank\nBurrows, K.\n(Creator),\nHaycock, P.\n(Creator), Bull, C. (Contributor),\nDudding, T.\n(Contributor),\nGormley, M.\n(Contributor),\nRobinson, T.\n(Contributor),\nTan, V.\n(Contributor) &\nYarmolinsky, J.\n(Contributor), University of Bristol,\n23 Nov 2021\nDOI\n:\n10.5523/bris.aed0u12w0ede20olb0m77p4b9\n,\nhttp://data.bris.ac.uk/data/dataset/aed0u12w0ede20olb0m77p4b9\nDataset\nMetabolite summary statistics for Mendelian randomization analyses\nLangenberg, C. (Creator), Stewart, I. (Creator), Butterworth, A. (Creator), Surendran, P. (Creator),\nTan, V.\n(Creator),\nCorbin, L.\n(Creator) &\nTimpson, N.\n(Creator), University of Bristol,\n9 Sept 2021\nDOI\n:\n10.5523/bris.33bq35s9lbos026r1xukxijoqu\n,\nhttp://data.bris.ac.uk/data/dataset/33bq35s9lbos026r1xukxijoqu\nand one more link\n,\nhttps://data.bris.ac.uk/data/dataset/33bq35s9lbos026r1xukxijoqu\n(show fewer)\nDataset"
