    "linkedin": "http://www.linkedin.com/in/yuxinnan",
    "homepage_text": "Felix X. Yu\nFelix X. Yu\nI am a Principal Scientist, Director at Google DeepMind, New York.\nI work on improving Gemini's fundamental capabilities of memorizing and retrieving information, \n        and applying the capabilities in Ads, memory/personalization, long-context and more.\nBefore DeepMind, I worked on deep retrieval, efficient LLMs and their intersections. \n       The deep retrieval algorithms and models developed by my team and me are \n       widely used at Google (Search, Ads, YouTube, Play and the new GenAI experience).\nBefore Google, I received my Ph.D. from \n        the Department of Electrical Engineering at Columbia University in 2015, \n        and my B.S. from the Department of Electronic Engineering at Tsinghua University in 2010.\n[Email]\n[Google Scholar]\n[LinkedIn]\n>\nDisclaimer: Responses are generated by an AI (gemini-2.0-flash) based on public information and are for entertainment purposes only. There is no guarantee of accuracy. Please do not share any personal or sensitive information. For real answers, please send me an email.\nLast updated: Aug, 2025"
  },
  "serper::Duo Wang": {
    "homepage": "https://dw-david.com/",
    "emails": [
      "blog@wordpress.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "David-Duo Wang – Ph.D. in Information Science\nHome\nSearch\nDuo Wang’s Homepage\nI am a researcher and entrepreneur committed to utilizing Extended Reality (XR) and Generative AI technologies to deliver products that bring value to end users. As an HCI researcher, my recent research has centered around combining Mixed Reality (MR) and AI Agents powered by Large Language Models (LLM). As an entrepreneur, I actively integrate XR and AI technologies to develop immersive games and applications that provide innovative user experiences. My multidisciplinary approach allows me to contribute to the advancement of technology while addressing practical user needs and delivering tangible solutions.\n2021-2023\nI was the director of the Application Software Product department at BLOO. My responsibilities included strategic planning, design, and development of applications for the Standalone Virtual Reality Headset, team management, technical evaluation, project management, and overseeing the development of key products such as the BLOO OS, BLOO mobile app, and BLOO official website.\n2021-2021\nFollowing the completion of my Ph.D., I embarked on a professional journey as a Human-Computer Interaction Expert in\nvivo\n. In this role, I led a team dedicated to creating groundbreaking augmented reality interactive applications leveraging vivo Origin OS. My responsibilities included overseeing augmented reality UX design, demo production, and prototype development.\n2017-2020\nDuring my Ph.D., I managed the Virtual Human Behavior Lab, conducting research on user interaction in virtual reality. I also worked as a research assistant at the Big Data Management Research Center, where I focused on data mining, business analytics, and social network analysis using machine learning techniques. Additionally, I taught the course\n3D Game Engine Techniques\nas an affiliated lecturer at the School of Virtual Reality,\nJilin Animation Institute\n.\n2016-2017\nI previously worked as a Virtual Reality Application Development Engineer at\nFaraday Future\n(China). In this role, I led a dedicated VR team responsible for designing and developing VR applications for electric vehicles, including the\nFF91\n. These VR applications were utilized for maintenance, sales, and business promotions.\nStart my second Ph.D. journey!\n@University of Illinois Urbana Champaign – 2024\nLet’s go! Apple Vision Pro!\n@Illinois – 2024\nMeet Forbes – an AI-driven conversational virtual companion in Mixed Reality.\n@MOONBOOW Studio – 2023\nThis is how we fought and built the next-generation XR product as a startup company.\n@BLOO – Shanghai 2022\nWorking as an HCI Expert in vivo is a significant step toward the consumer electronics industry.\n@vivo – Shenzhen 2021\nA key moment of my Ph.D. in Information Science.\nMy team has done an extraordinary job to make this project happen!\n@Virtual Human Behavior Research Lab – Jilin University 2020\nGroup SWE\nPresentation in\nDecision Making\nStanford summer session is a great place to meet young people with big dreams.\n@Stanford University – 2019\nDeveloping VR Experience for FF91\n@Faraday Future – Beijing 2017\nUnity 3D Engine New York VR Group Meeting\n@Manhattan, NY – 2016\nTesting\n3D Printing\nVR Developing\nVR Content Creating\n3D Printing and VR Developing\n@The Hive Lab, NYIT – 2016\nShowcasing our stunning VR experience in New York City’s Virtual Reality Lab DEMO Splash\n@Hearst Tower, NYC – 2016\nDemonstrating our VR project at the Symposium of University Research and Creative Expression (SOURCE)\n@Lincoln Square – New York 2016\nMy first job ever as a VR content designer and developer\n@FloorplanGRP – New York City 2016\nMy short documentary “Live For The Moment” won a Silver Award\n@The Houston International Film Festival – 2016\nClose Search (ESC)\nSearch\nSubmit\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nDavid-Duo Wang\nSign me up\nAlready have a WordPress.com account?\nLog in now.\nDavid-Duo Wang\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nSign up\nLog in\nCopy shortlink\nReport this content\nView post in Reader\nManage subscriptions\nCollapse this bar\nLoading Comments...\nWrite a Comment...\nEmail (Required)\nName (Required)\nWebsite"
  },
