    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Guo Research Group – Animal and Dairy Science\nSearch for:\nPress\ntab\nto complete the suggestion.\nMenu\nHome\nNews\nPeople\nPublications\nResearch\nTeaching\nContact\nSkip to content\nGuo Research Group\nAnimal and Dairy Science\nGuo Research Group Logo Image\nGuo Research Group\nAnimal and Dairy Science\nYour UW\nUW-Madison\nMy UW\nCampus Map\nHome\nWelcome to Guo Research Group\nWei Guo, Ph.D.\nAssociate Professor\n, Department of Animal and Dairy Sciences, Cardiovascular Research Center, University of Wisconsin-Madison.\nFaculty trainer\n,\nUW Graduate Program in Cellular and Molecular Biology\nFaculty trainer\n,\nUW Graduate Program in Molecular and Environmental Toxicology\nFaculty trainer\n,\nUW Graduate Program in Cellular and Molecular Pathology\nThe Guo Lab is dedicated to advancing our understanding of posttranscriptional regulation and RNA metabolism in muscle structure and function. Our research focuses particularly on the RBM20–titin pathway and its critical roles in striated muscle biology, encompassing cardiomyopathies, heart failure, and skeletal muscle hypertrophy and regeneration. We employ both in vitro and in vivo models to dissect molecular mechanisms and disease pathways. The long-term goal of the Guo Lab is to develop innovative RNA-based therapeutic strategies aimed at improving human health and enhancing animal production efficiency.\n1933 Observatory Dr\nMadison, WI 53706\nLogin\nRequest Help\nHelp Docs"
  },
