    "homepage_text": "Surui Xie, University of Houston\nI am migrating my website to\nhttps://xie.cive.uh.edu/\n. Some information on this website may not be up to date.\nStudent and Postdoc Opportunities: RA positions and a postdoc are available at the National Center for Airborne Laser Mapping (\nNCALM\n). \n\tProspective students interested in pursuing graduate degrees in the\nGeosensing Systems Engineering and Sciences Program\nwith me are encouraged to fill in this\nOnline Form\n.\n\tI will contact you if further information is needed. \n\tFor possible postdoctoral opportunities, please send your CV and research statement to\nsxie9@central.uh.edu\n.\nSurui Xie\n/suːrɪ/     /ʃiè/\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nUniversity of Houston\nUH NCALM, 5000 Gulf Freeway, Bldg. 4, Rm 216\nHouston, TX 77204-5059\nEmail:\nsxie9@central.uh.edu"
  },
  "serper::Q. Liao": {
    "homepage": "http://qveraliao.com/",
    "emails": [
      "veraliao@umich.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/qvliao",
    "homepage_text": "Q. Vera Liao\nQ. Vera Liao\nToggle navigation\nHome\nAbout\nPublications\nOutreach\nMentoring\nHCI, Human-AI Interaction, Responsible Computing and Experience\nCurricula Vitae\nGoogle Scholar\nResearch Statement\nAbout\nI am an Associate Professor at\nUniversity of Michigan CSE\n. I am often interested in examining and mitigating risks of emerging technologies. My most recent work focuses on transparency of AI technologies (e.g. explainability, evaluation, uncertainty communication) and its intersection with important aspects of human experiences with AI such as trust, reliance and control. Prior to joining U-M in 2025, I worked at\nMicrosoft Research\n, where I was part of the\nFATE (Fairness, Accountability, Transparency, and Ethics of AI)\ngroup, and\nIBM T.J. Watson Research Center\n, where my research contributed to IBM products such as\nAI Explainability 360\n,\nUncertainty Quantification 360\n, and Watson Assistant. I studied at the\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\nand\nTsinghua University\n.\nHere are a few topics I often speak about:\nhuman-centered AI explainability\nand\ntransparency\n(watch a version\nhere\n, and\na video in Chinese（中文）\n. I also had the pleasure to speak at\nthe Gradient Podcast\n),\nUX and responsible AI\n, appropriate\ntrust\nand\nreliance\non AI\n, and\nconversational interfaces\n. For more details see\nOutreach\n. I enjoy teaching tutorials, and taught\nHuman-Centered Evaluation of Language Technologies\nat EMNLP 2024,\nHCI and AI\nat CHI 2023,\nAlgorithmic Fairness at the Intersection\nat NeurIPS 2022,\nHuman-centered Evaluations of Explanations\nat NAACL 2022, and\nIntro to Explainable AI\n(course\nslides\n) at CHI 2021.\nWhat I am up to\nNews\nNow serving as a Paper Co-Chair for CHI 2026\n.\nTaught Human-Centered Evaluation of Language Technologies at EMNLP 2024. Slides are on\ntutorial website\n.\nNow serving as a Subcommittee Chair for the new \"AI and Design\" SC for\nDIS 2025\n.\nNow serving as a Subcommittee Chair (Understanding People-Quantitative) for\nCHI 2025\n.\nUpcoming Travel/Talks\nOct 2025: COLM 2025, speaking at the\nORIGen Workshop\n, and organizing the\nWorkshop on the Application of LLM Explainability to Reasoning and Planning\nElsewhere Online\nContact me\nveraliao [at] umich [dot] edu\nSelected Publications\n2025\nCanvil: Designerly Adaptation for LLM-Powered User Experiences (\nworking paper version\n)\nK. J. Kevin Feng, Q. Vera Liao, Ziang Xiao, Jennifer Wortman Vaughan, Amy X. Zhang, David W. McDonald\nTo apper in\nCHI 2025: ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\nFostering Appropriate Reliance on Large Language Models: The Role of Explanations, Sources, and Inconsistencies\nSunnie S. Y. Kim, Jennifer Wortman Vaughan, Q. Vera Liao, Tania Lombrozo, Olga Russakovsky\nTo apper in\nCHI 2025: ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\n* Best Paper Award, Honorable Mention\nAs Confidence Aligns: Understanding the Effect of AI Confidence on Human Self-confidence in Human-AI Decision Making\nJingshu Li, Yitian Yang, Q. Vera Liao, Junti Zhang, Yi-Chieh Lee\nTo apper in\nCHI 2025: ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\n* Best Paper Award, Honorable Mention\n\"It was 80% me, 20% AI\": Seeking Authenticity in Co-Writing with Large-Language Models\nAngel Hsing-Chi Hwang, Vera Liao, Su Lin Blodgett,Alexandra Olteanu, Adam Trischler\nTo apper in\nCSCW 2025: ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing\nWhy is AI not a Panacea for Data Workers? An Interview Study on Human-AI Collaboration in Data Storytelling\nHaotian Li, Yun Wang, Q Vera Liao, Huamin Qu\nIEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics\nGenerative AI and Creative Work: Narratives, Values, and Impacts\nBaptiste Caramiaux, Kate Crawford, Q. Vera Liao, Gonzalo Ramos, Jenny Williams\nWorking paper\n2024\nUX Matters: The Critical Role of UX in Responsible AI (Cover Story)\nQ. Vera Liao, Mihaela Vorvoreanu, Hari Subramonyam, Lauren Wilcox\nACM Interactions\nGenerative Echo Chamber? Effect of LLM-Powered Search Systems on Diverse Information Seeking\nNikhil Sharma, Q Vera Liao, Ziang Xiao\nCHI 2024: ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\n* Best Paper Award\nThe Who in XAI: How AI Background Shapes Perceptions of AI Explanations\nUpol Ehsan, Samir Passi, Q Vera Liao, Larry Chan, I-Hsiang Lee, Michael Muller, Mark O Riedl\nCHI 2024: ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\nGeneration Probabilities Are Not Enough: Exploring the Effectiveness of Uncertainty Highlighting in AI-Powered Code Completions (\nworking paper version\n)\nHelena Vasconcelos, Gagan Bansal, Adam Fourney, Q. Vera Liao, and Jennifer Wortman Vaughan\nTo apper in\nTOCHI: ACM Transactions on Computer-Human Interaction\nSeamful XAI: Operationalizing Seamful Design in Explainable AI (\nworking paper version\n)\nUpol Ehsan, Q Vera Liao, Samir Passi, Mark Riedl, Hal Daume III\nTo apper in\nCSCW 2024: ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing\nI'm Not Sure, But...\": Examining the Impact of Large Language Models' Uncertainty Expression on User Reliance and Trust\nSunnie S. Y. Kim, Q. Vera Liao, Mihaela Vorvoreanu, Stephanie Ballard, and Jennifer Wortman Vaughan\nTo appear in\nFAccT 2024: ACM Conference on Fairness, Accountability, and Transparency\nECBD: Evidence-Centered Benchmark Design for NLP\nYu Lu Liu, Su Lin Blodgett, Jackie Chi Kit Cheung, Q. Vera Liao, Alexandra Olteanu, Ziang Xiao\nACL 2024: Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics\n2023\nEvaluating Evaluation Metrics: A Framework for Analyzing NLG Evaluation Metrics using Measurement Theory\nZiang Xiao, Susu Zhang, Vivian Lai, Q. Vera Liao\nEMNLP 2023: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing\nAI Transparency in the Age of LLMs: A Human-Centered Research Roadmap\n(\nblog post\n)\nQ Vera Liao & Jennifer Wortman Vaughan\nHarvard Data Science Review\nRethinking Model Evaluation as Narrowing the Socio-Technical Gap\nQ Vera Liao & Ziang Xiao\nAI&HCI Workshop @ ICML 2023\n* Best Paper Award, Honorable Mention\nDesignerly Understanding: Information Needs for Model Transparency to Support Design Ideation for AI-Powered User Experience\nQ. Vera Liao, Hariharan Subramonyam, Jennifer Wang, Jennifer Wortman Vaughan\nCHI 2023: ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\nfAIlureNotes: Supporting Designers in Understanding the Limits of AI Models for Computer Vision Tasks\nSteven Moore, Q. Vera Liao, Hariharan Subramonyam\nCHI 2023: ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\nTowards a Science of Human-AI Decision Making: An Overview of Design Space in Empirical Human-Subject Studiesa\n(a longer\nworking paper version\n)\nVivian Lai, Chacha Chen, Q. Vera Liao, Alison Smith-Renner, Chenhao Tan\nFAccT 2023:  ACM Conference on Fairness, Accountability, and Transparency\nUnderstanding the Role of Human Intuition on Reliance in Human-AI Decision-Making with Explanations\nValerie Chen, Q. Vera Liao, Jennifer Wortman Vaughan, Gagan Bansal\nCSCW 2023: ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing\nSelective Explanation: Leveraging Human Input to Align Explainable AI\nVivian Lai, Yiming Zhang, Chacha Chen, Q. Vera Liao, Chenhao Tan\nCSCW 2023: ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing\nSensing Wellbeing in the Workplace, Why and For Whom? Envisioning Impacts with Organizational Stakeholders\n)\nAnna Kawakami, Shreya Chowdhary, Shamsi T. Iqbal, Q. Vera Liao, Alexandra Olteanu, Jina Suh, Koustuv Saha\nCSCW 2023: ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing\nPowering an AI Chatbot with Expert Sourcing to Support Credible Information Access\nZiang Xiao, Q. Vera Liao, Michelle Zhou, Tyrone ndre Grandison, Yunyao Li\nIUI 2023: ACM International Conference on Intelligent User Interface\nUnderstanding Uncertainty: How Lay Decision-makers Perceive and Interpret Uncertainty in Human-AI Decision Making\nSnehal Prabhudesai, Sumit Asthana, Leyao Yang, Xun Huan Q. Vera Liao, Nikola Banovic\nIUI 2023: ACM International Conference on Intelligent User Interface\nSupporting Qualitative Analysis with Large Language Models: Combining Codebook with GPT-3 for Deductive Coding\nZiang Xiao, Xingdi Yuan, Q. Vera Liao, Rania Abdelghani, Pierre-Yves Oudeyer\nIUI 2023 (Poster): ACM International Conference on Intelligent User Interface\nGeneration Probabilities Are Not Enough: Exploring the Effectiveness of Uncertainty Highlighting in AI-Powered Code Completions\nHelena Vasconcelos, Gagan Bansal, Adam Fourney, Q Vera Liao, Jennifer Wortman Vaughan\nWorking paper\n2022\nDesigning for Responsible Trust in AI Systems: A Communication Perspective\nQ. Vera Liao & S. Shyam Sundar\nFAccT 2022:  ACM Conference on Fairness, Accountability, and Transparency\nConnecting Algorithmic Research and Usage Contexts: A Perspective of Contextualized Evaluation for Explainable AI\nQ. Vera Liao, Yunfeng Zhang, Ronny Luss, Finale Doshi-Velez, Amit Dhurandhar\nHCOMP 2022:  AAAI Conference on Human Computation and Crowdsourcing\n* Best Paper Award, Honorable Mention\nHuman-AI Collaboration via Conditional Delegation: A Case Study of Content Moderation\nVivian Lai, Samuel Carton, Rajat Bhatnagar, Q. Vera Liao, Yunfeng Zhang, Chenhao Tan\nCHI 2022: ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems\nInvestigating Explainability of Generative Models for Code through Scenario-Based Design\nJiao Sun, Q. Vera Liao, Michael Muller, Mayank Agarwal, Stephanie Houde, Kartik Talamadupula,  Justin D. Weisz\nIUI 2022: ACM International Conference on Intelligent User Interface\nHuman-AI Collaboration for UX Evaluation: Effects of Explanations and Synchronization\nMingming Fan, Xianyou Yang, Tsz Tung Yu, Q. Vera Liao, Jian Zhao\nCSCW 2022: ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing\n2021\nHuman-Centered Explainable AI (XAI): From Algorithms to User Experiences\nQ. Vera Liao, Kush R. Varshney\nBook chapter draft\nExpanding Explainability: Towards Social Transparency in AI systems\nUpol Ehsan, Q. Vera Liao, Michael Muller, Mark Riedl, Justin D. Weisz\nCHI 2021: ACM Confe...[truncated]"
