    "homepage_text": "Staff - Seungmin Jin – HSE University\nВ старых версиях браузеров сайт может отображаться некорректно. Для оптимальной работы с сайтом рекомендуем воспользоваться современным браузером.\nA\nA\nA\nABC\nABC\nABC\nА\nА\nА\nА\nА\nRegular version of the site\nCampus in\nMoscow\nNizhny Novgorod\nSaint Petersburg\nPerm\nРУС\nEN\nFor visually-impaired\nFor visually-impaired\nUser profile (HSE staff only)\nSearch\nSearch\nAdvanced search\nMenu\nHSE University\nHSE University\nAbout HSE\nFaculty and Staff\nSeungmin Jin\nРУС\nEN\nUser profile (HSE staff only)\nSearch\nAdvanced search\nHome\nTeaching\nResearch and Publications\nEmployment history\nIn HSE news\nLanguage Proficiency\nEnglish\nKorean\nContacts\nPhone:\n27362\nAddress: 26 Shabolovka Ulitsa, Building 1, room 1218\nTimetable\nORCID\n:\n0000-0002-8242-6157\nResearcherID\n:\nAAB-1073-2021\nScopus AuthorID\n:\n57219371488\nGoogle Scholar\nSupervisor\nS. Kuznetsov\nPrintable version\nwith publications\nwith news\nPrint\nHave you spotted a\ntypo\n?\nHighlight it, click Ctrl+Enter and send us a message. Thank you for your help!\nTo be used only for spelling or punctuation mistakes.\nSeungmin Jin\nAssociate Professor:\nHSE Graduate School of Business\n/\nDepartment of Business Informatics\nSenior Research Fellow:\nFaculty of Computer Science\n/\nInternational Laboratory for Intelligent Systems and Structural Analysis\nSeungmin Jin has been at HSE University since 2024.\nHome\nTeaching\nResearch and Publications\nEmployment history\nIn HSE news\nEducation and Degrees\n2024\nCandidate of Sciences\n*\n(PhD)\nHSE University\n2023\nDoctoral programme\nHSE University\n2018\nMaster's\nHSE University\n*\nCandidate of Sciences\nAccording to the International Standard Classification of Education (ISCED) 2011, Candidate of Sciences belongs to ISCED level 8 - \"doctoral or equivalent\", together with PhD, DPhil, D.Lit, D.Sc, LL.D, Doctorate or similar. Candidate of Sciences allows its holders to reach the level of the Associate Professor.\nProfessional Interests\nexplainable AI\ndeep learning\nBig Data analysis\nvisual analysis\nCourses (2025/2026)\nAI in business: technologies and solutions\n(Mago-Lego;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\n; 1, 2 module)\nEng\nAI in business: technologies and solutions\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 2 year, 1, 2 module)\nEng\nNeural Networks and Deep Learning\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 2 year, 1, 2 module)\nEng\nNeural Networks and Deep Learning\n(Mago-Lego;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\n; 1, 2 module)\nEng\nNeural Networks and Deep Learning\n(Mago-Lego;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\n; 3, 4 module)\nEng\nNeural Networks and Deep Learning\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 1 year, 3, 4 module)\nEng\nRecommender Systems\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 2 year, 1, 2 module)\nEng\nRecommender Systems\n(Mago-Lego;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\n; 1, 2 module)\nEng\nResearch Seminar \"Big Data: Principles and Paradigms\"\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 1 year, 2, 3 module)\nEng\nResearch Seminar \"Latest Trends in Data Governance, Big Data Analytics & Data Architecture\"\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 2 year, 2, 3 module)\nEng\nPast Courses\nCourses (2024/2025)\nAI in business: technologies and solutions\n(Mago-Lego; 1, 2 module)\nEng\nAI in business: technologies and solutions\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 2 year, 1, 2 module)\nEng\nNeural Networks and Deep Learning\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 2 year, 1, 2 module)\nEng\nNeural Networks and Deep Learning\n(Mago-Lego; 1, 2 module)\nEng\nRecommender Systems\n(Mago-Lego; 1, 2 module)\nEng\nRecommender Systems\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 2 year, 1, 2 module)\nEng\nResearch Seminar \"Big Data: Principles and Paradigms\"\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 1 year, 2, 3 module)\nEng\nResearch Seminar \"Latest Trends in Data Governance, Big Data Analytics & Data Architecture\"\n(Master’s programme;\nHSE Graduate School of Business\nfield of study Business Informatics; 2 year, 2, 3 module)\nEng\nCourses (2023/2024)\nMentor's Seminar\n(Master’s programme;\nFaculty of Computer Science\nfield of study Applied Mathematics and Informatics; 1 year, 1-4 module)\nEng\nTimetable for today\nFull timetable\nDissertation for a Candidate of Sciences degree\n2024\nS. Jin\nСистема визуальной аналитики для объяснения и улучшения моделей прогнозирования дорожного движения на основе механизма внимания\nGrants\nWinner of the Sino-Russian Mathematical Challenge Fund 2025 (\nResearch Project Competition of the Sino-Russian Mathematical Problems Fund\n).\nEmployment history\n2024 – Present:\nHSE University (National Research University Higher School of Economics)\n2016 – 2024:\nResearcher, UNIST (Ulsan National Institute of Science and Technology), South Korea\n2015 – 2016:\nResearcher, Daumsoft (Social Mining & Big Data Company), South Korea\n2\nJul\n2025\n‘The Cost of Making Mistakes Is Small, While the Experience Is Invaluable’\nFor the second year in a row, the Moscow Chamber of Commerce and Industry has held the Start a Business with Moscow international business school for students of Moscow Universities. Last year, Wang Yue, an HSE University student from China, became the winner of the project. On June 16, 2025, the finalists defended their projects and business ideas in front of business representatives and potential investors. This year, six students from HSE University made it to the finals. Ekaterina Leibel, second-year student of the master’s programme ‘Science of Learning and Assessment,’ whose project took third place, and Md Yeashin Arafat, first-year student of the master’s programme ‘Business Analytics and Big Data Systems,’ talk about their studies, project presentations, and future plans.\nHSE University\n→\nAbout HSE\n→\nFaculty and Staff\n→\nSeungmin Jin\nAbout\nAbout\nKey Figures & Facts\nSustainability at HSE University\nFaculties & Departments\nInternational Partnerships\nFaculty & Staff\nHSE Buildings\nHSE University for Persons with Disabilities\nPublic Enquiries\nStudies\nAdmissions\nProgramme Catalogue\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nExchange Programmes\nSummer University\nSummer Schools\nSemester in Moscow\nBusiness Internship\nResearch\nInternational Laboratories\nResearch Centres\nResearch Projects\nMonitoring Studies\nConferences & Seminars\nAcademic Jobs\nYasin (April) International Academic Conference on Economic and Social Development\nMedia & Resources\nPublications by staff\nHSE Journals\nPublishing House\niq.hse.ru: commentary by HSE experts\nLibrary\nEconomic & Social Data Archive\nVideo\nHSE Repository of Socio-Economic Information\nEditor\n©  HSE University 1993–2026\nContacts\nCopyright\nPrivacy Policy\nSite Map\nHSE Sans and HSE Slab fonts developed by the HSE Art and Design School"
