    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/hyeshinchu",
    "homepage_text": "Hyeshin Chu\nHyeshin Chu 🦄\nHi, I am an HCI Researcher and AI Product Manager in\nSNOW Corporation.\nMy research focuses on exploring how we can utilize generative AI technologies to enhance user experience and improve interaction between them. I believe in the intersectionality of quantitative and qualitative subjects, that neither approach alone can lead one to the absolute truth.\nPreviously, I received my M.S. in AI at\nUNIST\nand B.B.A. in College of Business Administration at\nEwha Womans University.\nhyeshinchu\nRecent projects\nVirtual Try-on\nAI Avatar Profile\nSynthetic Data Pipeline for AI Architectures\nUser Satisfaction on 3D Avatar Facial Expression\nAn Empirical Study on How People Perceive AI-generated Music\nCIKM '22\nA Visual Analytics System for Improving Attention-based Traffic Forecasting Models\nTVCG '23\nLearning to Remember Patterns - Pattern Matching Memory Networks for Traffic Forecasting\nICLR '21\nWait, Let’s Think about Your Purchase Again - A Study on Interventions for Supporting Self-Controlled Online Purchases\nWWW '21\nAn Empirical Experiment on Deep Learning Models for Predicting Traffic Data\nICDE '21\n> View All\nNews\nLaunching AI avatar profile generation service\nSep 20, 2023\nSo excited to share our new service in Korea, Japan, and Thailand. You can generate your own avatar profile using AI🎨\nFirst in-person conference attendance @ CIKM 2022\nOct 17, 2022\nExcited to attend my first in-person conference (CIKM '22) in Atlanta, Georgia. I'll present my paper on AI-generated music🎶\nSelected as a recipient of SIGIR Travel Award\nSep 18, 2022\nGrateful to be selected as one of the authors receiving the SIGIR Travel Award\nCIKM paper accepted\nAug 16, 2022\nExcited to share my 1st first-author paper on\nAI-generated music\nhas been accepted to\nCIKM 2022\n> View All"
  },
  "serper::Alex J. Chan": {
    "homepage": "https://alexjchan.com/",
    "emails": [
      "me@alexjchan.com"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/XanderJC",
    "linkedin": "https://linkedin.com/in/alexjchan",
    "homepage_text": "Alex J. Chan\nDirector of Software Engineering\nand\nAutonomous Agents ML Research Lead\nat\nSalesforce\nPreviously, Founding Member of Technical Staff at\nConvergence\n, before we were\nacquired by Salesforce\n. Before that, Research Scientist at\nSpotify\n, and PhD at the University of Cambridge in collaboration with\nMicrosoft Research\n.\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nEmail\nCV\nI am interested in developing safe and effective machine learning systems that can successfully complete complex tasks in the real world. My work has often explored (inverse) reinforcement learning, imitation learning and simulation in order to learn from intrinsic rewards and humans, applied most recently to large language/multimodal models for autonomous computer-using agents.\nRecent News\nMay 2025\nWe're being acquired by Salesforce! I'll be joining as a Director of Software Engineering to continue our work building the future of computer-using agents.\nAnnouncement\nDec 2024\nOur first agent Proxy has achieved state-of-the-art results (82%) on the WebVoyager benchmark!\nPost\nSep 2024\nJoined Convergence Labs Ltd. as a Member of Technical Staff! We're a seed-stage startup building a future of abundance by automating workflows with AI.\nConvergence\nSep 2024\nNew work accepted to NeurIPS 2024: \"Discovering Preference Optimization Algorithms with and for Large Language Models\"!\nPaper\nMay 2024\n\"Dense Reward for Free in Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback\" accepted to ICML!\nPaper\nMar 2024\nI'm back at Spotify as a full-time Research Scientist working on RLHF for internal LLMs and products including AI Playlist.\nShow all 17 items"
  },
