  "serper::Peng Gao": {
    "homepage": "https://people.cs.vt.edu/penggao/",
    "emails": [
      "penggao@vt.edu",
      "penggao.jobs@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Peng Gao\nPeng Gao\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science\nVirginia Tech\nOffice: Gilbert Place 4104\nE-mail: penggao [at] vt [dot] edu\nFollow @penggaotweets\nBio\n|\nPublications\n|\nLab\n|\nTeaching\n|\nServices\nI am an assistant professor of Computer Science at Virginia Tech. Previously, I was a postdoctoral researcher in Computer Science at UC Berkeley (with Dawn Song). I received my Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering from Princeton University (with Prateek Mittal, Sanjeev R. Kulkarni). I received my B.E. in Electrical and Computer Engineering from Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\nResearch Interests\nSystems Security, Network Security, (Agentic) AI for Cybersecurity, AI Safety and Security, AI for Science\nEducation & Experience\nPh.D. in Electrical Engineering (M.A. en route), Princeton University, 2013-2019\nB.E. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, 2009-2013\nExchange Student, Electrical and Electronics Engineering, The University of Hong Kong, Spring 2012\nPostdoctoral Scholar, EECS Department, UC Berkeley, 06/2019-04/2021\nVisiting Student Researcher, EECS Department, UC Berkeley, 01/2019-06/2019\nResearch Intern, Microsoft Research Asia, 06/2018-09/2018\nResearch Intern, Facebook (Meta), 06/2017-09/2017\nResearch Intern, NEC Laboratories America, 10/2016-12/2016\nResearch intern, NEC Laboratories America, 11/2015-01/2016\nResearch intern, Microsoft Research Redmond, 06/2015-09/2015\nSelected Awards\nAmazon Research Award (ARA), 2026\nGoogle Academic Research Award (GARA), 2025\nNational Science Foundation (NSF) CAREER Award, 2025\nIEEE Senior Member, 2025\nAmazon-VT Initiative Faculty Research Award, 2022\nMeta Research Award Finalist, 2021\nCisco Research Award, 2021\nCommonwealth Cyber Initiative (CCI) Faculty Fellow, 2021\nGoogle Cloud Research Credits Award, 2021\nAmazon Research Award (ARA), 2021\nMicrosoft Security AI Research Award, 2020\nCSAW Best Applied Security Paper Award Finalist, 2018\nPrinceton University Fellowship in Natural Sciences and Engineering, 2013\nShanghai Excellent Graduate, 2013\nLi & Fung Scholarship, 2012\nChina National Scholarship, 2010, 2011\nSJTU Academic Excellence Scholarship, 2010, 2012\nProspective students:\nI am seeking highly motivated Ph.D. students and postdoctoral researchers to join my lab. If you’re interested, please email your CV and transcript to penggao.jobs [at] gmail [dot] com. In your message, please include a brief statement explaining your understanding of our research topics and relevant publications. While I may not be able to respond to every message due to the volume of inquiries, I genuinely appreciate your interest.\nSponsor"
  },
