    "homepage_text": "Di Yang\nSearch\nDi Yang\nPhD candidate\nPenn State University\nI’m on the job market!\nMy research interests include impact evaluation, health inequality, health economics, and global health. My studies focused on socioeconomic determinants of health, particularly in low-and-middle income countries. My methodology focus is causal inference, particularly Difference-in-Differences and fixed effects model, while I am gaining knowledge on machine learning. I am looking for postdoctoral or faculty position, and research position in international organizations.\nDownload my\nCV\n.\nInterests\nPolicy and Impact Evaluation\nHealth Inequality\nSocial Determinants of Health\nHealth Economics\nMachine Learning\nEducation\nPhD in Health Policy and Administration, 2023\nPenn State University\nBachelor of Management, 2018\nZhejiang Univeristy\nPublications\nDi Yang\n,\nYubraj Archarya\n,\nXiaoting Liu\n(2022).\nSocial Health Insurance Consolidation and Urban-Rural Inequality in Utilization and Financial Risk Protection in China\n.\n  Social Science & Medicine.\nPDF\nDOI\nYubraj Archarya\n,\nDi Yang\n(2022).\nThe Effect of Disability on Educational, Labor Market, and Marital Outcomes in a Low-Income Context\n.\n  SSM - Population Health.\nPDF\nDOI\nYubraj Archarya\n,\nDi Yang\n(2021).\nEconomic and Social Drivers of Antibiotic Dispensing Practices among Community Pharmacies in Nepal\n.\n  Tropical Medicine & International Health.\nPDF\nDOI\nYubraj Archarya\n,\nDi Yang\n,\nAndrew D Jones\n(2021).\nLivestock ownership and anaemia in Sub-Saharan African households\n.\n  Public Health Nutrition.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
