    "homepage_text": "Wenjie Qiu\nWenjie Qiu\nApplied Scientist\nAmazon\necho-inception[at]live.com\nAbout Me\nHi, I'm\nWenjie Qiu\n(邱文杰). I recently completed my Ph.D. in Computer Science at Rutgers University and now work as an\nApplied Scientist at Amazon\n. Before that, I earned an M.S. in Computer Science from Washington University in St. Louis and a B.E. in Electronic Information Engineering from Central China Normal University. My industry experience includes internships at Amazon, LinkedIn, and Samsung Research America. My research spans\nReinforcement Learning\n,\nAI Agent\n,\nPreference Learning\n, and\nLarge Language Models\n.\nI’m always open to new research ideas and collaborations. If my work aligns with your interests, I’d love to connect.\nNews\n[2026.03]\nJoin\nAmazon\nas an Applied Scientist at New York City.\n[2026.02]\nInvited as a reviewer for ICLR 2026 Workshop VerifAI-2.\n[2026.01]\nOne paper is accepted to\nICLR'26\n.\n[2026.01]\nInvited as a reviewer for ICLR 2026 Workshop ES-Reasoning.\n[2026.01]\nGraduated from Ph.D. in Computer Science at\nRutgers University\n.\n[2026.01]\nInvited as a reviewer for ICML 2026.\n[2025.11]\nSuccessfully defended Ph.D. dissertation.\n[2025.09]\nTwo papers are accepted to\nNeurIPS'25\n.\n[2025.09]\nJoin\nAmazon\nas an Applied Scientist Intern.\n[2025.09]\nInvited as a reviewer for ICLR 2026.\n[2025.08]\nInvited as a reviewer for AISTATS 2026.\n[2025.05]\nJoin\nLinkedIn\nas a PhD AI/ML Intern.\n[2025.02]\nInvited as a reviewer for NeuS 2025.\n[2025.02]\nInvited as a reviewer for NeurIPS 2025.\n[2025.01]\nInvited as a reviewer for ICLR 2025 Workshop VerifyAI.\n[2024.11]\nInvited as a reviewer for AISTATS 2025.\n[2024.09]\nInvited as a reviewer for TNNLS.\n[2024.08]\nInvited as a reviewer for TIST.\n[2024.06]\nInvited as a reviewer for NeurIPS 2024.\n[2024.04]\nOne paper is accepted at\nPLDI'24\n.\n[2023.12]\nPresent our work on program synthesis on RL agent at\nNeurIPS'23\nin New Orleans.\n[2023.09]\nOne paper is accepted to\nNeurIPS'23\n.\nEarlier news\n[2023.03]\nSuccessfully passed Ph.D. qualifying exam.\n[2022.05]\nJoin\nSamsung Research America\nas a Research Intern.\n[2022.05]\nPresent our work on programmatic reinforcement learning at\nICLR'22\n.\n[2022.04]\nInvited talk on programmtic reinforcement learning at RLChina.\n[2022.01]\nOne paper is accepted to\nICLR'22\nas a\nSpotlight\npresentation.\n[2020.09]\nJoin Rutgers Automated Reasoning Lab as a Research Assistant.\n[2020.09]\nStart Ph.D. in Computer Science at\nRutgers University\n.\n[2020.05]\nComplete M.S. in Computer Science at\nWashington University in St. Louis\n.\n[2019.06]\nStart a research internship at S3 Lab at\nStevens Institute of Technology\n.\n[2019.01]\nJoin Computer Security & Privacy Lab as a Research Assistant.\n[2018.08]\nStart M.S. in Computer Science at\nWashington University in St. Louis\n.\nResearch Interests\nReinforcement Learning\nLarge Language Models\nProgram Synthesis\nEmbodied AI\nAgentic Systems\nEducation\nRutgers University\n, Ph.D. in Computer Science\nAdvisor: Prof. He Zhu\nResearch Interests: Reinforcement Learning, Large Language Models, Program Synthesis, Preference Learning, Embodied AI\nDissertation:\nFrom Reasoning to Acting: A Program Synthesis Approach to Reinforcement Learning\nPDF\nBibTeX\nLoading BibTeX...\nWashington University in St. Louis\n, M.S. in Computer Science\nAdvisor: Prof. Ning Zhang\nResearch Interests: System Security, Software Security\nThesis:\nA Performance Analysis of Hardware-assisted Security Technologies\nPDF\nBibTeX\nLoading BibTeX...\nCentral China Normal University\n, B.E. in Electronic Information Engineering\nPublications\n(* indicates equal contribution)\nICLR'26\nPreference-based Policy Optimization from Sparse-reward Offline Dataset\nWenjie Qiu\n, Guofeng Cui, Shicheng Liu, Yuanlin Duan, He Zhu\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2026.\nPDF\nBibTeX\nLoading BibTeX...\nNeurIPS'25\nExplainable Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback to Improve Alignment\nShicheng Liu, Siyuan Xu,\nWenjie Qiu\n, Hangfan Zhang, Minghui Zhu\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2025.\nPDF\nBibTeX\nLoading BibTeX...\nNeurIPS'25\nLearning from Demonstrations via Capability-Aware Goal Sampling\nYuanlin Duan, Yuning Wang,\nWenjie Qiu\n, He Zhu\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2025.\nPDF\nCode\nBibTeX\nLoading BibTeX...\nPLDI'24\nReward-Guided Synthesis of Intelligent Agents with Control Structures\nGuofeng Cui*, Yuning Wang*,\nWenjie Qiu*\n, He Zhu\nProgramming Language Design and Implementation (PLDI), 2024.\nPDF\nCode\nBibTeX\nLoading BibTeX...\nNeurIPS'23\nInstructing Goal-Conditioned Reinforcement Learning Agents with Temporal Logic Objectives\nWenjie Qiu*\n, Wensen Mao*, He Zhu\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2023.\nPDF\nCode\nBibTeX\nLoading BibTeX...\nICLR'22\nProgrammatic Reinforcement Learning without Oracles\nWenjie Qiu\n, He Zhu\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2022.\n[Spotlight]\nPDF\nCode\nBibTeX\nLoading BibTeX...\nRecent Submissions (Under Review)\nFinLCR: Scaling Financial Long-Context Reasoning via Curriculum Reinforcement Learning (ACL)\nCompositional Policy Optimization with Language Models (AAAI)\nHonors & Awards\nSpotlight Presentation, ICLR 2022 (Top 3%)\nBoya Scholarship, Central China Normal University (Top 3%)\nAcademic Service\nConference Reviewer: NeurIPS 2024–2025, ICLR 2025–2026, ICML 2026, AISTATS 2025–2026, NeuS 2025\nJournal Reviewer: TIST, TNNLS\nVisitor Map"
