    "homepage_text": "Han Wu's Homepage\nHan Wu's Homepage\nAbout me\nHan Wu\nTry to be an NLPer.\nLinks\nBio\nI am a researcher in Huawei Noah’s Ark Lab in Hong Kong. I finished my Ph.D degree at Department of Computer Science, City University of Hong Kong, supervised by\nProf. Linqi Song\n. Prior to that, I obtained my bachelor degree from Xi’an Jiaotong University. My research interests are lied on LLM reasoning (especially LLM4OR) and model merging.\nNews\nWe have some intern openings based in HK, focusing on the research of LLMs. Drop me your CV if interesed.\nMay. 2025. We have two papers (1 main + 1 Findings) accepted by ACL, focusing on LLM reasoning and model merging.\nMay. 2025. We have one survey paper accepted by IJCAI, focusing on LLM for Operations Research. (\nFirst survey of LLM4OR\n)\n🔥 Mar. 2025. We present the work of effecient long-to-short reasoning with model merging.\n[paper]\n[code]\nFeb. 2025. We have one paper focusing on model ensembling accepted as\nICLR Spotlight (Top 5%)\n.\nJul. 2024. We have two paper accepted in COLM, 2024.\nJun. 2024. We have one paper accepted in JSTSP, 2024.\nOct. 2023. The last paper produced in my PhD time was accepted in TASLP.\nOct. 2023. Two papers are accepted in EMNLP main conference, 2023.\nJul. 2023. Pass the oral defense!\nMay. 2023. We have one paper accepted in ACL findings, 2023.\nJan. 2023. We have on paper accepted in ICLR 2023.\nPublications\n(* - equal contribution; † - corresponding author.)\nA Survey of Optimization Modeling Meets LLMs: Progress and Future Directions.\n[paper]\nZiyang Xiao, Jingrong Xie, Lilin Xu, Shisi Guan, Jingyan Zhu, Xiongwei Han, Xiaojin Fu, WingYin Yu,\nHan Wu\n, Wei Shi, Qingcan Kang, Jiahui Duan, Tao Zhong, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng, Yuan Wang, Gang Chen, Dongxiang Zhang.\nIJCAI Survey, 2025\nUnlocking Efficient Long-to-Short LLM Reasoning with Model Merging.\n[paper]\n[code]\nHan Wu*\n, Yuxuan Yao*, Shuqi Liu*, Zehua Liu*, Xiaojin Fu, Xiongwei Han, Xing Li, Hui-Ling Zhen, Tao Zhong, Mingxuan Yuan.\nPreprint, 2025\nBPP-Search: Enhancing Tree of Thought Reasoning for Mathematical Modeling Problem Solving.\n[paper]\nTeng Wang, Wing-Yin Yu, Zhenqi He, Zehua Liu, Hailei Gong,\nHan Wu\n, Xiongwei Han, Wei Shi, Ruifeng She, Fangzhou Zhu, Tao Zhong.\nACL, 2025\nSens-Merging: Sensitivity-Guided Parameter Balancing for Merging Large Language Models.\n[paper]\nShuqi Liu,\nHan Wu†\n, Bowei He, Xiongwei Han, Mingxuan Yuan, Linqi Song.\nACL Findings, 2025\n1bit-Merging: Dynamic Quantized Merging for Large Language Models.\n[paper]\nShuqi Liu,\nHan Wu†\n, Bowei He, Zehua Liu, Xiongwei Han, Mingxuan Yuan, Linqi Song.\nPreprint, 2025\nLoRE-Merging: Exploring Low-Rank Estimation For Large Language Model Merging.\n[paper]\nZehua Liu,\nHan Wu\n, Yuxuan Yao, Ruifeng She, Xiongwei Han, Tao Zhong, Mingxuan Yuan.\nPreprint, 2025\nOPTISHEAR: Towards Efficient and Adaptive Pruning of Large Language Models via Evolutionary Optimization.\n[paper]\nShuqi Liu, Bowei He,\nHan Wu†\n, Linqi Song.\nPreprint, 2025\nDetermine-Then-Ensemble: Necessity of Top-k Union for Large Language Model Ensembling.\n[paper]\n[code]\nYuxuan Yao,\nHan Wu†\n, Mingyang Liu, Sichun Luo, Xiongwei Han, Jie Liu, Zhijiang Guo and Linqi Song.\nICLR Spotlight, 2025\nCoCA: Regaining Safety-awareness of Multimodal Large Language Models with Constitutional Calibration.\n[paper]\n[code]\nJiahui Gao, Renjie Pi, Tianyang Han,\nHan Wu\n, Lanqing Hong, Lingpeng Kong, Xin Jiang and Zhenguo Li.\nThe First Conference on Language Modeling, 2024.\n(COLM, 2024)\nLearning From Correctness Without Prompting Makes LLM Efficient Reasoner.\n[paper]\n[code]\nYuxuan Yao*,\nHan Wu*\n, Zhijiang Guo, Biyan Zhou, Jiahui Gao, Sichun Luo, Hanxu Hou, Xiaojin Fu and Linqi Song.\nThe First Conference on Language Modeling, 2024.\n(COLM, 2024)\nTowards Improving Interpretability of Language Model Generation Through a Structured Knowledge Discovery Approach.\n[paper]\n[code]\nShuqi Liu,\nHan Wu\n, Guanzhi Deng, Jianshu Chen, Xiaoyang Wang and Linqi Song.\nIEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing, 2024.\n(JSTSP, 2024)\nBuilding Structure-Aware Conversational Semantic Role Labeling Model via Relational Graph Network.\n[paper]\n[code]\nHan Wu\n, Kun Xu and Linqi Song.\nIEEE Transactions on Audio, Speech and Language Processing, 2023.\n(TASLP, 2023)\nReconstruct Before Summarize: An Efficient Two-Step Framework for Condensing and Summarizing Meeting Transcripts.\n[paper]\n[code]\nHaochen Tan,\nHan Wu\n, Wei Shao, Xinyun Zhang, Mingjie Zhan, Zhaohui Hou, Ding Liang and Linqi Song.\nIn Proceedings of Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing, 2023.\n(EMNLP, 2023)\nFine-grained Conversational Decoding via Isotropic and Proximal Search.\n[paper]\n[code]\nYuxuan Yao,\nHan Wu\n, Qiling Xu, and Linqi Song.\nIn Proceedings of Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing, 2023.\n(EMNLP, 2023)\nVCSUM: A Versatile Chinese Meeting Summarization Dataset.\n[paper]\n[code]\nHan Wu\n, Mingjie Zhan, Haochen Tan, Zhaohui Hou, Ding Liang, Linqi Song.\nIn Findings of the Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics, 2023.\n(ACL Findings, 2023)\nLearning Locality and Isotropy in Dialogue Modeling.\n[paper]\n[code]\nHan Wu\n, Haochen Tan, Mingjie Zhan, Gangming Zhao, Shaoqing Lu, Ding Liang and Linqi Song.\nIn the Eleventh International Conference on Learning Representations, 2023.\n(ICLR 2023)\nZero-Shot Cross-Lingual Conversational Semantic Role Labeling.\n[paper]\n[code]\nHan Wu\n, Haochen Tan, Kun Xu, Shuqi Liu, Lianwei Wu and Linqi Song.\nIn Findings of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics - Human Language Technologies (NAACL-HLT), 2022.\n(NAACL Findings, 2022)\nA Sentence is Worth 128 Pseudo Tokens: A Semantic-Aware Contrastive Learning Framework for Sentence Embeddings.\n[paper]\nHaochen Tan, Wei Shao,\nHan Wu\n, Ke Yang and Linqi Song.\nIn Findings of the Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics, 2021.\n(ACL Findings, 2022)\nCSAGN: Conversational Structure Aware Graph Network for Conversational Semantic Role Labeling.\n[paper]\n[code]\nHan Wu\n, Kun Xu and Linqi Song.\nIn Proceedings of the Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing, 2021.\n(EMNLP 2021)\nDomain-Adaptive Pretraining Methods for Dialogue Understanding.\n[paper]\n[code]\nHan Wu\n, Kun Xu, Linfeng Song, Lifeng Jin, Haisong Zhang and Linqi Song.\nIn Proceedings of the Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics, 2021.\n(ACL 2021)\nConversational Semantic Role Labeling.\n[paper]\n[dataset]\nKun Xu,\nHan Wu\n, Linfeng Song, Haisong Zhang, Linqi Song and Dong Yu.\nIEEE Transactions on Audio, Speech and Language Processing, 2021.\n(TASLP)\nK-CSRL: Knowledge Enhanced Conversational Semantic Role Labeling.\n[paper]\nBoyu He,\nHan Wu\n, Congduan Li, Linqi Song and Weigang Chen.\nIn Proceedings of 13th International Conference on Machine Learning and Computing, 2021.\n(ICMLC 2021)\nSemantic Role Labeling Guided Multi-turn Dialogue Rewriter.\n[paper]\nKun Xu, Haochen Tan, Linfeng Song,\nHan Wu\n, Haisong Zhang, Linqi Song and Dong Yu.\nIn Proceedings of the Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing, 2020.\n(EMNLP 2020)\nEducation\nPh.D. student, Department of Computer Science, City University of Hong Kong. Sep. 2019 - Aug. 2023.\nB.Eng., School of Software Engineering, Xi’an Jiaotong University. Sep. 2014 - Jun. 2018.\nResearch Experience\nSensetime Research Institute.,\nResearch Intern\nwith Mingjie Zhan and\nDing Liang\n.\nWorking on large-scale dialogue pre-training and dialogue summarization.\nMar. 2022 - Feb. 2023, Beijing.\nTencent AI Lab,\nResearch Intern\nwith\nDr. Kun Xu\n.\nWorking on dialogue system and semantic parsing.\nDec. 2019 - Oct. 2021, Shenzhen.\nDept. of Computer Science, CityU,\nResearch Assistant\nwith\nDr. Linqi Song\n.\nWorking on privacy-preserving recommender system.\nMay. 2019 - Aug. 2019, Hong Kong.\nLab of Social Intelligence and Complex Data Processing, XJTU,\nResearch Assistant\nwith\nProf. Yuan Rao\n.\nWorking on event detection and storyline generation.\nSep. 2018 - Apr. 2019, Xi’an.\nProfessional Service\nConference Reviewer: AAAI’(21-24), ACL’(22-24), NAACL’22, EMNLP’(21-24), IJCAI’23, NeurIPS’23-24, ICLR’24, ARR\nJournal Reviewer: TASLP, TNNLS\nAward\nOutstanding Academic Performance Award(25%), CityU, 2021, 2022.\nResearch Tuition Scholarship (20%), CityU, 2021.\nCityU PhD Studentship, 2019-2023.\nFirst-class scholarship, XJTU, 2016, 2017.\nAbout me"
  },
