    "homepage_text": "Cheng Tan | Cheng Tan’s homepage\nCheng Tan\nI am an assistant professor of\nKhoury College of Computer Sciences\nat\nNortheastern University\n.\n  I’m part of\nSystems Research Group\nat Northeastern University.\nI’m broadly interested in computer systems.\n  I build systems that enable\n  users to verify their outsourced services.\n  In particular, my recent research includes:\nbuliding Faithful LLM Systems\n,\nverifying ML systems,\nverifying consistency models of concurrent systems,\nverifying the execution of applications on untrusted servers.\nIf you are interested in building systems, we should talk [c.tan (at) northeastern.edu].\nPublications\nLLM Jailbreak Oracle\nShuyi Lin, Anshuman Suri, Alina Oprea, and\nCheng Tan\nMLSys 2026\n, Bellevue, WA, May 2026.\n[pdf (to appear),\n  code (to appear),\narxiv\n]\nVirtual Machine NUMA Placement at Scale: Learning the Norm, Shielding the Tail\nYibo Zhao, Tianyuan Wu, Hui Xue, Qi Chen, Zhenhua Han, Zikai Xu, Yuntai Chang, Rui Gao,\nSteve Deng, Ray Jui-Hao Chiang, Mingxia Li, Yuqing Yang,\nCheng Tan\n,\nFan Yang, Peng Cheng, Yongqiang Xiong, Lili Qiu, and Lidong Zhou\nMLSys 2026\n, Bellevue, WA, May 2026.\n[pdf (to appear), code (to appear), arxiv (to appear)]\nTrainVerify: Equivalence-Based Verification for Distributed LLM Training\nYunchi Lu, Youshan Miao,\nCheng Tan\n, Peng Huang, Yi Zhu, Xian Zhang, and Fan Yang\nSOSP 2025\n, Seoul, Republic of Korea, October 2025.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n,\narxiv\n]\nPipeLLM: Fast and Confidential Large Language Model Services with Speculative Pipelined Encryption\nYifan Tan,\nCheng Tan\n, Zeyu Mi, and Haibo Chen\nASPLOS 2025\n, Rotterdam, The Netherlands, March 2025.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n,\narxiv\n]\nNN4SysBench: Characterizing Neural Network Verification for Computer Systems\nShuyi Lin, Haoyu He, Tianhao Wei, Kaidi Xu, Huan Zhang, Gagandeep Singh, Changliu Liu, and\nCheng Tan\nNeurIPS 2024, Datasets and Benchmarks Track\n, Vancouver, Canada, December 2024.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n,\nwebsite\n]\nDropout Attacks\nAndrew Yuan, Alina Oprea, and\nCheng Tan\nS&P 2024\n, San Francisco, CA, May 2024.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n,\narxiv\n]\nEncrypted Databases Made Secure Yet Maintainable\nMingyu Li, Xuyang Zhao, Le Chen,\nCheng Tan\n, Huorong Li, Sheng Wang, Zeyu Mi, Yubin Xia, Feifei Li, and Haibo Chen\nOSDI 2023\n, Boston, MA, July 2023.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n]\nBuilding Verified Neural Networks for Computer Systems with Ouroboros\nTianhao Wei, Zhihao Jia, Changliu Liu, and\nCheng Tan\nMLSys 2023\n, Miami, FL, June 2023.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n]\nViper: A Fast Snapshot Isolation Checker\nJian Zhang, Ye Ji, Shuai Mu, and\nCheng Tan\nEuroSys 2023\n, Rome, Italy, May 2023.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n]\nNNSmith: Generating Diverse and Valid Test Cases for Deep Learning Compilers\nJiawei Liu, Jinkun Lin, Fabian Ruffy,\nCheng Tan\n, Jinyang Li, Aurojit Panda, and Lingming Zhang\nASPLOS 2023\n, Vancouver, Canada, March 2023.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n,\narxiv\n]\nDistinguished Artifact Award\nBringing Decentralized Search to Decentralized Services\nMingyu Li, Jinhao Zhu, Tianxu Zhang,\nCheng Tan\n, Yubin Xia, Sebastian Angel, and Haibo Chen\nOSDI 2021\n, July 2021.\n[\npdf\n,\ncode\n]\nCobra: Making Transactional Key-Value Stores Verifiably Serializable\nCheng Tan\n, Changgeng Zhao, Shuai Mu, and Michael Walfish\nOSDI 2020\n, November 2020.\n[\npdf\n,\nslides\n,\ntalk\n,\ncode\n]\nAuditing Outsourced Services\nCheng Tan\nPh.D. Dissertation, August 2020.\n[\npdf\n]\nJanet Fabri Prize in Courant Institute\nNetBouncer: Active Device and Link Failure Localization in Data Center Networks\nCheng Tan\n, Ze Jin, Chuanxiong Guo, Tianrong Zhang, Haitao Wu, Karl Deng, Dongming Bi, and Dong Xiang\nNSDI 2019\n, Boston, MA, February 2019.\n[\npdf\n,\nslides\n,\ntalk\n]\nThe Efficient Server Audit Problem, Deduplicated Re-execution, and the Web\nCheng Tan\n, Lingfan Yu, Joshua B. Leners, and Michael Walfish\nSOSP 2017\n, Shanghai, China, October 2017.\n[\npdf\n,\nslides\n,\ntalk\n,\nextended report\n,\ncode\n]\nBest paper award\nTinMan: Eliminating Confidential Mobile Data Exposure with Security-oriented Offloading\nYubin Xia, Yutao Liu,\nCheng Tan\n, and Mingyang Ma, Haibing Guan, Binyu Zang, and Haibo Chen.\nEuroSys 2015\n, Bordeaux, France, April 2015.\n(\nsee all papers\n)\nRecent workshop papers\nCan LLMs Replace Time-Tested System Policies? Perhaps\nYibo Zhao and\nCheng Tan\nApSys’25\n, Seoul, Korea, October 2025.\nSpecification Generation for Neural Networks in Networking Systems\nIsha Chaudhary, Shuyi Lin,\nCheng Tan\n, and Gagandeep Singh\nML4Wireless@ICML’25\n, Vancouver, Canada, July 2025.\nTeaching\nSpring 2026:\nOperating Systems Implementation (CS6640)\nOperating Systems Implementation (CS6640):\n25sp\n,\n23fa\nComputer Systems, Undergrad (CS3650):\n24sp\nComputer Systems (CS5600):\n23sp\n,\n22sp\n,\n21fa\nComputer Systems Seminar (CS7670):\nNN4Sys (22fa)\n,\nLLMSys (25fa)\nStudents\nJian Zhang\n(PhD)\nBrent Zhao (PhD, co-advised with Pete Manolios)\nShuyi Lin (PhD)\nZikai Wang\n(PhD)\n(see\nAlumni\n)\nProgram committee\nEuroSys 2026\n,\nMLSys 2026\nOSDI 2025\n,\nEuroSys 2025\n,\nATC 2025\n,\nMLSys 2025\nMLSys 2024\n,\nAAAI SRRAI 2024\nATC 2023\n,\nICDCS 2023\n,\nSoCC 2022\n,\nVEE 2022\n,\nCoNEXT 2021\nHonors and Awards\nMSR Asia StarTrack Scholar\n, 2024\nASPLOS Distinguished Artifact Award\n, 2023\nNSF CAREER Award\n, 2023\nNYU Janet Fabri Prize\n, 2021\nSOSP Best Paper Award\n, 2017\nAbout me\nBefore joining Northeastern, I worked \nas a research scientist\nat\nByteDance AI Lab\nfor a year.\nBefore that, I got my Ph.D. from\nCourant Institute\nNYU\nadvised by\nMichael Walfish\n,\nand my M.S. and B.E.\nfrom\nFudan University\nand\nNanjing University\n, respectively.\nI was a student at\nNYU Systems Group\n.\nBefore that, I was at\nIPADS\nadvised by\nBinyu Zang\nand\nHaibo Chen\n,\nwhere I did research on mobile systems and system virtualization."
  },
