  "serper::Jie Yu": {
    "homepage": "https://research.nottingham.edu.cn/en/persons/jie-yu/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jie YU\n      -  University of Nottingham Ningbo China\nUniversity of Nottingham Ningbo China Home\nSearch content at University of Nottingham Ningbo China\nView Scopus Profile\nDr Jie YU\nProfessor in Information Systems, Associate Dean for Global Engagement and Partnerships\nDepartment of Entrepreneurship, Marketing and Management Systems\nResearch Base on Ningbo Dual Circulation and New Economic Development\nEmail\nJie.YU\nnottingham.edu\ncn\nh-index\n1108\nScopus Citations\n13\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2007\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nResearch Interests\nHis research interests include Social Media, E-Commerce, and Business Analytics and has published on top international journals including Journal of Management Information Systems, Journal of the Associations for Information Systems, and International Journal of Production Economics. He also work closely with industries such as Alibaba/Taobao, Duckbill Logistic Technology and local manufacturing companies.\nTeaching\nIntroduction to Business Programming\nIntroduction to Data Science\nLeading Bigdata Business Project\nURL\nhttps://www.nottingham.edu.cn/en/Business/People/Profile.aspx?id=1e3b3cd5-3736-4271-8a2d-2af66e33884c&language=en-GB\nPersonal profile\nDr Jie Yu joined University of Nottingham Business School China in September 2010 . He has a BSc in Computer Science from Fudan University, and a PhD in Information Systems from the National University of Singapore. Prior to joining Nottingham University, he worked in the National University of Singapore as a teaching assistant in Information Systems (2007 – 2009). His research interests include knowledge management, healthcare information systems, and virtual communities. His research work has been presented in a number of international conferences (PACIS, AMCIS, EurOMA, SIGCHI) and research seminars. Some of his research work has appeared on top international journals (Journal of Management Information Systems, International Journal of Production Economics, IEEE transactions on Professional Communication).\nEducation/Academic qualification\nPhD,\nNational University of Singapore\n15 Aug 2003\n→\n30 Jun 2010\nAward Date: 30 Jun 2010\nBachelor,\nFudan University\n10 Sept 1999\n→\n30 Jun 2003\nAward Date: 30 Jun 2003\nDisciplines\nInformation and Document Management\nManagement Science and Engineering\nPerson Types\nStaff\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 9\nIndustry, Innovation, and Infrastructure\nSDG 11\nSustainable Cities and Communities\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Jie YU is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n4\nSimilar Profiles\nVirtual Community\nKeyphrases\n100%\nChina\nKeyphrases\n93%\nProblem Solving\nKeyphrases\n64%\nElectronic Commerce\nKeyphrases\n50%\nInformation System\nComputer Science\n45%\nDecision-Making\nComputer Science\n45%\nE-retailer\nKeyphrases\n41%\nInformation Technology\nKeyphrases\n40%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nProjects\n1\nFinished\nDesign, Implementation and Evaluation of an Intelligent Dispatching Platform Based on IoT Logistics Technologies\nYU, J.\n(PI)\n1/11/19\n→\n31/10/22\nProject\n:\nGovernment Funded Projects\n›\nVertical-Municipal/Departmental Government (市厅局级) Funded Projects\nFile\nPlatform-based\n100%\nMaster Students\n100%\nDesign Implementation\n100%\nSoftware Copyright\n100%\nIntelligent Dispatching\n100%\nResearch output\n21\nArticle\n12\nConference contribution\n8\nPaper\n2\nEditorial\n1\nMore\n1\nBook Chapter\nChallenges in developing information and communication technology (ICT) use for rural e-governance: An ecology perspective\nShou, M., Jia, F.,\nYu, J.\n& Wu, Y.,\nJan 2025\n,\nIn:\nInformation Systems Journal.\n35\n,\n1\n,\np. 247-278\n32 p.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publication\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nRural E-Governance\n100%\nInformation and Communication Technologies\n100%\nFixed Effects\n100%\nInstrumental Variable Analysis\n100%\nInformation and Communication Technology\n100%\n12\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nDisentangling e-commerce gamification affordances on recommendation acceptances from a perceived value perspective\nJia, F. &\nYu, J.\n,\n19 May 2025\n,\nIn:\nInformation Technology and People.\n38\n,\n4\n,\np. 1843-1870\n28 p.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publication\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nGamification\n100%\nRecommendation Acceptance\n100%\nSelf-Expression\n25%\nUtilitarian Dimension\n16%\nQuantitative Design\n16%\n13\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nExploring metaverse: affordances and risks for potential users\nBao, X.,\nYu, J.\n& Shou, M.,\nNov 2025\n,\nIn:\nInformation Technology and People.\n38\n,\n7\n,\np. 2710-2733\n24 p.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publication\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nInteroperability\n100%\nDecision-Making\n100%\nSocial Presence\n100%\nSurvey Response\n100%\nQualitative Data\n100%\n8\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nPredicting marine tourism intention through information processing: an ability-motivation-opportunity framework\nZhuge, Y., Jiao, Y., Tong, H. &\nYu, J. J.\n,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nFrontiers in Marine Science.\n12\n, 1629706.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publication\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nInformation Processing\n100%\nTourism\n100%\nMarine Tourism\n100%\nInformation Literacy\n100%\nTourism Information Quality\n50%\nBlockchain innovations: Technological applications and management challenges\nLim, E. T. K.,\nYu, J. J.\n, Cai, S. & Tuunainen, V.,\nApr 2024\n,\nIn:\nInformation and Management.\n61\n,\n3\n, 103756.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publication\n›\nEditorial\n3\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 44 research outputs"
