    "homepage_text": "Ruifei He's Personal website\nRuifei He (何睿飞)\nPh.D. Candidate in HKU\nMajor: Computer Vision\nAdvisor:\nProf. Xiaojuan Qi\nAbout\nPublication\nTA\nCoursework\nNews!\nAbout\nCV\nI'm currently a fourth-year Ph.D. student at the University of Hong Kong, advised by\nProf. Xiaojuan Qi\n. Before that, I obtained my B.Eng. degree (Ranked\n3/153\n, GPA\n3.95/4.0\nor\n91.25/100\n) in Automation at Zhejiang University (2021) supervised by\nProf. Yong Liu\n, and I was also at\nChu Kochen Honors College's\nmixed class.\nMy research interest lies in the wild areas of artificial intelligence and computer vision, with a focus on\ndata-centric/efficient learning (e.g. synthetic/generative data, mixing multi-modal data, and semi-supervised learning)\nfor computer vision tasks. During my Ph.D. study, I have been fortunate to intern at ByteDance AI Lab, advised by\nSong Bai\n.\nI'm currently seeking full-time opportunities starting in Summer 2025, please feel free to reach out if you have any openings!\nLearn More\nSelected Publication\nIs synthetic data from generative models ready for image recognition?\nRuifei He\n, Shuyang Sun, Xin Yu, Chuhui Xue, Wenqing Zhang, Philip Torr, Song Bai, Xiaojuan Qi.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2023.\nSpotlight\n[\npaper\n]\n                            [\ncode\n]\nKnowledge Distillation as\n                            Efficient Pre-training: Faster Convergence, Higher Data-efficiency, and Better Transferability.\nRuifei He\n, Shuyang Sun, Jihan Yang, Song Bai, Xiaojuan Qi.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2022.\n[\npaper\n]\n                            [\ncode\n]\nRe-distributing Biased Pseudo Labels in Self-training for Semi-supervised Semantic Segmentation.\nRuifei He\n, Jihan Yang, Xiaojuan Qi.\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2021.\nOral (3.4% acceptance rate)\n[\npaper\n]\n                            [\ncode\n]\nMulti-Modal Controllable Video-to-Audio Generation: A Data Perspective.\nRuifei He\n, Chuhui Xue, Wenqing Zhang, Yingchen Yu, Zhengzhe Liu, Song Bai, Xiaojuan Qi.\nUnder review, 2025.\nMC-MoE: Mixture Compressor for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs Gains More.\nWei Huang, Yue Liao, Jianhui Liu,\nRuifei He\n, Haoru Tan, Shiming Zhang, Hongsheng Li, Si Liu, Xiaojuan Qi.\nICLR, 2025.\n[\npaper\n]\nDebiasing Text-to-Image Diffusion Models.\nRuifei He\n, Chuhui Xue, Haoru Tan, Wenqing Zhang, Yingchen Yu, Song Bai, Xiaojuan Qi.\nProceedings of the 1st ACM Multimedia Workshop on Multi-modal Misinformation Governance in the Era of Foundation Models\n(\nACM MM Workshop\n), 2024.\n[\npaper\n]\nVertical Layering of Quantized\n                            Neural Networks for Heterogeneous Inference.\nHai Wu,\nRuifei He\n, Haoru Tan, Xiaojuan Qi, Kaibin Huang.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n), 2023.\n[\npaper\n]\nLUMix:\n                            Improving Mixup by Better Modelling Label Uncertainty.\nShuyang Sun, Jie-Neng Chen,\nRuifei He\n, Alan Yuille, Philip Torr, Song Bai.\nIEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (\nICASSP\n), 2022.\n[\npaper\n]\n                            [\ncode\n]\nLearning by Analogy: Reliable Supervision from Transformations for Unsupervised Optical Flow Estimation.\nLiang Liu, Jiangning Zhang,\nRuifei He\n, Yong Liu, Yabiao Wang, Ying Tai, Donghao Luo, Chengjie Wang, Jilin Li, Feiyue Huang.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2020.\n[\npaper\n]\n                            [\ncode\n]\nResearch on artificial intelligence algorithm of edge computing.\nCo-work with Zizhang Li and Jintao Lu\n[\nreport\n]\n                            [\nslides\n]\nTeaching Assistant\nELEC6604 Neural networks, fuzzy systems and genetic algorithms, 2024~2025\nELEC8108 Deep learning and applications, 2022~2024\nENGG1310 Electricity and electronics, 2021~2022\nUndergraduate Course Projects\nThese projects mainly represent my undergraduate work.\nVROOM: Interactive rendering virtual environment with binocular vision.\nCourse Project, CS 21120970 Mixed Reality, 2019 Winter. Instructor:\nProf. Hujun Bao\n[\ndemo\n]\n                            [\ncode\n]\nEigenface: face recognition and rebuild using Eigenvalue decomposition.\nCourse Project, CS 21191070 Computer Vision, 2019 Winter. Instructor:\nProf. Mingli Song\n[\ncode\n]\nResearch on where to build charging stations and the quantity of charging piles.\nCo-work with Jintao Lu and Yuheng Zha\nCourse Project, EE 68190140 Mathematical Modeling & Simulating, 2019 Spring. Instructor:\nProf. Jian Chen\n[\nreport\n]\n                            [\nslides\n]\nRobot Navigation: Augmented A* with feedback control.\nCo-work with Anqiao Li\nCourse Project, EE 86120080 Robotics, 2019 Fall. Instructor:\nProf. Rong Xiong\n[\ndemo\n]\n                            [\ncode\n]\nNews!\nPh.D. Journey\nStarting from Sept. 2021, I have been awarded the Hong Kong PhD Fellowship (\nHKPFS\n) and the HKU Presidential PhD Scholarship (\nHKU-PS\n) and pursuing my Ph.D. in\nCVMI Lab\n, The University of Hong Kong, advised by\nProf. Xiaojuan Qi\n.\nSlides from recent talk\n\"Application Of Optical Flow\"\nLanguage test\nMy TOEFL scores (test date--8th December, 2019): 109 (R30 L29 S24 W26)"
  },
