    "homepage_text": "Tao Song | Economist\nTao Song\nAssociate Professor of Economics\nLabor and Immigration\nAbout\nI am a labor economist with a focus on immigration and discrimination. I am interested in understanding how social changes and ethnic neighborhoods affect the outcomes of immigrants.\nIf you do not find me teaching or nerding out on STATA codes, you will find me cooking with my husband James, hiking with our dog Hugo, traveling or planning our next trip, or playing video games.\nDownload my CV\nResearch\nPublications\nâNative-Immigrant Wage Gaps and the Growing Importance of Social Skillsâ\n(Accepted at Journal of Human Capital)\nâEthnic Enclaves: Causes and Consequences for Immigrantsâ, 2024,  in\nRefugees and Migrants - Current Conditions and Future Trends (Samson M.T. (eds))\n.\nwith\nMate Istvan Szurop\nâEthnic Segregation, Education, and Immigrants Labor Market Outcomesâ, 2023,\nIZA Journal of Labor Economics\n, 12(1).\nwith\nTian Lou\nâUnemployment Insurance and Business Ownershipâ, 2023,\nInternational Journal of Applied Economics, Finance and Accounting\n, 16(2), 118â126.\nwith\nLhakpa Sherpa\nâInterethnic Marriagesâ, 2022, in\nHandbook of Labor, Human Resources and Population Economics\n(Zimmermann, K.F. eds).\nwith\nDelia Furtado\nâAnywhere They Go, We Go: Immigration Inflowâ Impact on Co-ethnic Nativesâ, 2020,\nSouthern Economic Journal\n, 2020(87), 191-215.\nwith\nHuanan Xu\nâIntermarriage and Socioeconomic Integration: Trends in Earnings Premiums among U.S. Immigrants Who Marry Nativesâ, 2015,\nANNALS of the American Academy of Political and Social Science\n, 662(1), 207-22.\nwith\nDelia Furtado\nâThe Supply and Demand Factors Behind the Relative Earnings Increases in Urban China at the Turn of the 21st Century\", 2013,\nComparative Economic Studies\n, 55(1), 121- 143.\nwith\nJoseph Marchand\nâAlbertan Labour in the Previous Energy Boom, in Institute for Public Economicsâ, 2013,\nAn Examination of Alberta Labour Markets\n, University of Alberta, 10-24.\nwith\nJoseph Marchand\nInvited Columns\nâHow Technological Change and Globalization are Driving Higher Wages of Immigrants Married to Nativesâ, 2016,\nLSE USAPP\n,\nwith\nDelia Furtado\nOpen\nWorking Papers\n\"Young Immigrantsâ Post-Secondary Education Attainment: The Role of Enclaves\"\nwith\nMÃ¡tÃ© Istvan Szurop\nWork in Progress\nâObergefell v. Hodgesâs Effect on the Career Choices of Intermarried Same-Sex Couples in the U.S.â\nâYou Are Where You Live. An Investigation on Efficient Refugee and Immigrant Placement Strategiesâ\nTeaching\nEconomics Tutorials YouTube Channel\nUniversity of the South\nAssociate Professor\n2017 - Present\nECON101 Introduction to Microeconomics\nECON102 Introduction to Macroeconomics\nECON133 Principles of Econometrics\nECON233 Applied Econometrics\nECON304 Labor Economics\nECON308 Urban Economics\nECON339 Economics of Immigration\nECON410 Research Seminar\nUniversity of Connecticut\nInstructor of Record and Teaching Assistant\r\n                                                    2012 - 2017\nECON1202 Principles of Macroeconomics\nECON2202 Intermediate Macroeconomics\nECON3441 Labor Economics\nUniversity of Alberta\nTeaching Assistant\r\n                                                    2010 - 2011\nECON281 Intermediate Microeconomic Theory\nECON323 International Economics\nLinks\nDownload my CV\nEmail Me\nEconomics Tutorials YouTube Channel\nElements\nText\nThis is\nbold\nand this is\nstrong\n. This is\nitalic\nand this is\nemphasized\n.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThis is\nsuperscript\ntext and this is\nsubscript\ntext.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tThis is\nunderlined\nand this is code:\nfor (;;) { ... }\n. Finally,\nthis is a link\n.\nHeading Level 2\nHeading Level 3\nHeading Level 4\nHeading Level 5\nHeading Level 6\nBlockquote\nFringilla nisl. Donec accumsan interdum nisi, quis tincidunt felis sagittis eget tempus euismod. Vestibulum ante ipsum primis in faucibus vestibulum. Blandit adipiscing eu felis iaculis volutpat ac adipiscing accumsan faucibus. Vestibulum ante ipsum primis in faucibus lorem ipsum dolor sit amet nullam adipiscing eu felis.\nPreformatted\ni = 0;\r\n\r\nwhile (!deck.isInOrder()) {\r\n    print 'Iteration ' + i;\r\n    deck.shuffle();\r\n    i++;\r\n}\r\n\r\nprint 'It took ' + i + ' iterations to sort the deck.';\nLists\nUnordered\nDolor pulvinar etiam.\nSagittis adipiscing.\nFelis enim feugiat.\nAlternate\nDolor pulvinar etiam.\nSagittis adipiscing.\nFelis enim feugiat.\nOrdered\nDolor pulvinar etiam.\nEtiam vel felis viverra.\nFelis enim feugiat.\nDolor pulvinar etiam.\nEtiam vel felis lorem.\nFelis enim et feugiat.\nIcons\nTwitter\nFacebook\nInstagram\nGithub\nActions\nDefault\nDefault\nDefault\nDefault\nTable\nDefault\nName\nDescription\nPrice\nItem One\nAnte turpis integer aliquet porttitor.\n29.99\nItem Two\nVis ac commodo adipiscing arcu aliquet.\n19.99\nItem Three\nMorbi faucibus arcu accumsan lorem.\n29.99\nItem Four\nVitae integer tempus condimentum.\n19.99\nItem Five\nAnte turpis integer aliquet porttitor.\n29.99\n100.00\nAlternate\nName\nDescription\nPrice\nItem One\nAnte turpis integer aliquet porttitor.\n29.99\nItem Two\nVis ac commodo adipiscing arcu aliquet.\n19.99\nItem Three\nMorbi faucibus arcu accumsan lorem.\n29.99\nItem Four\nVitae integer tempus condimentum.\n19.99\nItem Five\nAnte turpis integer aliquet porttitor.\n29.99\n100.00\nButtons\nPrimary\nDefault\nDefault\nSmall\nIcon\nIcon\nDisabled\nDisabled\nForm\nName\nEmail\nCategory\n-\nManufacturing\nShipping\nAdministration\nHuman Resources\nLow\nHigh\nEmail me a copy\nNot a robot\nMessage"
