    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jing-huang-935b0216/",
    "homepage_text": "Jing Huang's homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJing Huang's homepage\nJing Huang, PhD\nSenior tech leader in AI applications\nAmazon\nI lead the development of\nLLM-based conversational AI technologies\nfor search, recommendation, and advertising, driving\ninnovative product delivery\nand\nstrategic management\n. Under my leadership, teams are advancing state-of-the-art\nconversational AI\nby enhancing human-machine interactions with deeper context understanding, commonsense reasoning, and personalization, while pioneering\nmulti-modal generative AI solutions\nusing large language models. I oversee\nproduct design and delivery\n, impacting millions of users globally. In my prior role as\nSenior Director\nat\nJD AI Research and Platforms (JD.com)\n, I spearheaded critical AI initiatives on speech, NLP and knowledge graphs. With over 20 years of extensive R&D experience, I have led\ngroundbreaking projects\nspanning\nmulti-modal content generation, natural language processing\n, including\nfoundation models/LLMs\n,\nconversational AI\n,\nknowledge graph and recommendation systems\n,\nspeech recognition\n, and\nadvanced deep learning architectures (GNNs and DNNs)\n, showcasing my\ntechnological leadership\nand\nproduct-focused management expertise\n.\nI serve in the IEEE SPS Speech and Language Processing Technical Committee. I am also an AE for IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech and Language Processing, from 2021-2024.\nMy publications via Google Scholar\nMy professional experiences via LinkedIn\nI am an alumni of\nCornell University Computer Science PhD program\nTsinghua University Undergraduate in Applied Mathematics\nFor professional connections please contact me via\nLinkedIn\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
