  "serper::Chujie Lu": {
    "homepage": "https://learningforlife.tudelft.nl/instructors/chujie-lu/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Chujie Lu | TU Delft Learning for Life\nSkip to search\nJavaScript seems to be disabled in your browser.\nFor the best experience on our site, be sure to turn on Javascript in your browser.\nSkip to Content\nClose panel\nLearning for Life for Business\nSearch\nsearch\nSearch\nLogin\nWishlist\nLearning for Life for Business\nChujie Lu\nPostdoc Researcher\nShare webpage\nBio\nChujie Lu is a postdoc researcher with the Faculty of Architecture and the Built Environment at TU Delft, the Netherlands. He concentrates on implementing advanced artificial intelligence and data science within practical applications in the building industry to achieve sustainable development goals. Currently, he is actively participating in the Brains4Buildings project sponsored by the Dutch grant program for Mission-Driven Research, Development and Innovation.\nChujie has a multidisciplinary background with a Ph.D. in Computer Science and a B.Eng. in Building Environment and Energy Engineering. His doctoral research focused on intelligent computing techniques for energy efficiency in occupant-centric buildings. During his Ph.D. study, he was a visiting scholar at Carleton University, Canada, and Umeå University, Sweden. Chujie is the (co)author of more than 10 publications. He also serves as a reviewer for several prominent academic journals (e.g., Energy and Buildings, Building Simulation, Journal of Building Engineering, Engineering Applications of Computational Fluid Mechanics, etc.) and a scientific committee member for international academic conferences.\nFaculty\nArchitecture and the Built Environment\nDegrees\nPhD, Computer Science, Guangdong University of Technology\nB.Eng, Building Environment and Energy Engineering, Guangdong University of Technology\nCourses and programs by this instructor\nEfficient HVAC Systems\n4 - 6 Hours per week\nFree\nBuildings as Sustainable Energy Systems\nStart date                    Nov 20, 2026\nFree"
  },
  "serper::C. Tan": {
    "homepage": "https://scholars.cityu.edu.hk/en/persons/chaoltan/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Chaoliang TAN\n      -  CityUHK Scholars\nCityUHK Scholars Home\nResearcher Login\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at CityUHK Scholars\nProf. Chaoliang TAN, 譚超良\nAssociate Professor\n,\nDepartment of Electrical Engineering\nAssociate Professor\n,\nDepartment of Biomedical Engineering\nPhone\n+852 34427784\nEmail\nchaoltan\ncityu.edu\nhk\nYEUNG-G6423\nAccepting PhD Students\nh-index\n35337\nScopus Citations\n88\nScopus h-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2010\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nAuthor IDs\nORCID iD:\n0000-0003-1695-5285\nScopus Author ID:\n36092205700\nResearcherID:\nT-3036-2017\nGoogle Scholar Profile:\no9_klS4AAAAJ\nImpact\nMetrics for Academic and Research Impact\nBiography\nDr. Chaoliang Tan\nis an\nAssociate Professor\n(Tenured) in the Department of Electrical Engineering (EE) with a joint appointment in the Department of Biomedical Engineering of City University of Hong Kong (CityU), HKSAR, China. He received his PhD degree in Materials Science from Nanyang Technological University (Singapore) with\nProf. Hua Zhang\nin 2016. After working as a Postdoc Research Fellow in the same place for about one year, then he worked as a Postdoc Research Fellow in Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Sciences at University of California, Berkeley with\nProf. Ali Javey\nfor two years. He started his independent career as an\nAssistant Professor\nat CityU EE in 2020. He was an\nAssistant Professor\nat the Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering of The University of Hong Kong from 2023 to 2024 before he moved back to CityU EE. His current research interests are highly interdisciplinary including 2D materials, electronics, optoelectronics, neuromorphic devices, biomaterials and nanomedicine. He has authored or co-authored over\n210\nSCI papers (\n39\nESI Highly Cited Papers\n) on journals like\nNature\n(1)\n,\nNat. Nanotechnol.\n(1)\n,\nNat. Mater.\n(1)\n,\nNat. Chem.\n(1)\n,\nNat. Catal.\n(1)\n,\nNat. Rev. Mater.\n(1)\n,\nNat. Rev. Chem.\n(1)\n,\nNat. Commun.\n(3)\n,\nChem. Rev.\n(3)\n,\nChem. Soc. Rev.\n(6)\n,\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\n(12)\n,\nAngew. Chem. Int. Ed.\n(12)\n,\nAdv. Mater.\n(33)\n,\nCell Biomater.\n(1)\n, etc. The total citation of his published papers is over\n39,000\nwith a H-index of\n93\n. Among them, more than\n110\nare first-authored or corresponding-authored papers, including\nNat. Nanotechnol.\n,\nNat. Rev. Mater.\n,\nChem. Rev.\n,\nChem. Soc. Rev.\n,\nNat. Commun.\n,\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\n,\nAngew. Chem. Int. Ed.\n,\nAdv. Mater.\n,\nCell Biomater.\n,\nAdv. Funct. Mater.\n,\nACS Nano\n,\nNano-Micro Lett.,\nSmall\nand\nAppl. Phys. Lett.\nHe received the “\nBeijing Natural Science and Technology Award-Second Class Award\n”\nin 2025.\nHe has been elected as a\nFellow of International Association of Advanced Materials (FIAAM)\nin 2024. He has been listed as the “\nHighly Cited Researcher\n” (Clarivate Analytics) in the last 8 years (since 2018) as well as “\nTop 2% Scientists in the world\n” by Stanford University in last 6 years (since 2020). He also received the\nNSFC Excellent Young Scientist Fund (HK & Macau)\nin 2021. He serves as an\nAssociate Editor\nof\nSmartMat\n(IF=12.8) (Since 2025) and\nSmart Materials and Devices\n(Since 2024). He sites on the Editorial Board of\nScience Bulletin\n(since 2023),\nActa Physico-Chimica Sinica\n(since 2022),\nNanomaterials\n(since 2023) and\nEnergies\n(since 2021).\nRelated Links\nContact Knowledge Transfer Office for Technology Licensing\nPersonal Homepage\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 3\nGood Health and Well-being\nSDG 6\nClean Water and Sanitation\nSDG 7\nAffordable and Clean Energy\nSDG 9\nIndustry, Innovation, and Infrastructure\nSDG 13\nClimate Action\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Chaoliang TAN is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nNanosheet\nMaterial Science\n100%\nNanostructured Material\nMaterial Science\n40%\nTransition Metal Dichalcogenide\nMaterial Science\n31%\nNanostructure\nMaterial Science\n30%\nMetal-Organic Framework\nMaterial Science\n26%\nNanoparticle\nMaterial Science\n19%\nLayered Double Hydroxides\nMaterial Science\n19%\nGraphene\nMaterial Science\n18%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration based on locations. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a place from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a place to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a place from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n209\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n3\nErratum\n2\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n1\nRGC 12 - Chapter in an edited book (Author)\n2\nMore\n1\nEditorial Preface\n1\nRGC 51 - Patents (CityUHK)\nA LDH-Based Supramolecular Photosensitizer-Functionalized Bioactive Glass Scaffold for Integrated Postoperative Osteosarcoma Recurrence Prevention and Bone Regeneration\nWang, T. (Co-first Author), Bian, Y. (Co-first Author), Hu, T. (Co-first Author), Li, M., Tan, Y., Yang, Y., Jian, X., Weng, X.,\nTan, C.\n& Liang, R.,\n9 Feb 2026\n, (Online published)\nIn:\nAdvanced Science.\ne24296.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nOsteosarcoma\n100%\nPhotosensitizer\n100%\nRecurrent Disease\n100%\nBioactive Glass\n100%\nOxygen Derivative\n100%\nCorrection: Metallic phase enabling MoS\n2\nnanosheets as an efficient sonosensitizer for photothermal‑enhanced sonodynamic antibacterial therapy\nChen, H. (Co-first Author), He, X. (Co-first Author), Zhou, Z. (Co-first Author), Wu, Z., Li, H., Peng, X., Zhou, Y.,\nTan, C.\n& Shen, J.,\n2026\n,\nIn:\nJournal of Nanobiotechnology.\n24\n,\n4 p.\n, 48.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nErratum\nNanosheet\n100%\nNanobiotechnology\n100%\nMolybdenum Disulfide\n100%\nLayered Double Hydroxide-Based Sonosensitizer Triggers “Paraptosis+” Multidimensional Cell Death Network for Augmented Sonodynamic Immunotherapy\nYang, Y. (Co-first Author), Hu, T. (Co-first Author), Zhu, Y., Zhong, Z., Yang, Y., Wang, T., Li, H.,\nTan, C.\n& Liang, R.,\n3 Mar 2026\n,\nIn:\nAdvanced Materials.\n38\n,\n13\n, e22763.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nImmunotherapy\n100%\nCell Death\n100%\nParaptosis\n100%\nLactate Dehydrogenase\n100%\nOxygen Derivative\n100%\nScalable fabrication of mid-wavelength and long-wavelength infrared photodetectors based on narrow bandgap semiconductors: challenges and opportunities\nMoon, J. H., Nam, S., Kim, S.,\nZha, J.\n,\nTan, C.\n& Kim, H.,\nFeb 2026\n,\nIn:\nInternational Journal of Extreme Manufacturing.\n8\n,\n1\n,\n43 p.\n, 012012.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nEnergy Gaps (Solid State)\n100%\nPhotometer\n100%\nPhotosensor\n100%\nDetectors\n28%\nQuantum Dot\n14%\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitation\n(Scopus)\n2\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nA Library of Polyphenol-Amino Acid Condensates for High-Throughput Continuous Flow Production of Nanomedicines with Ultra-High Drug Loading\nYi, Z. (Co-first Author), Ma, X. (Co-first Author), Tong, Q., Ma, L., Tan, Y., Liu, D.,\nTan, C.\n, Chen, J. & Li, X.,\n16 Apr 2025\n,\nIn:\nAdvanced Materials.\n37\n,\n15\n, 2417534.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nAmino Acid\n100%\nNanomedicine\n100%\nPolyphenol\n100%\nPaclitaxel\n50%\nNanoparticle\n25%\n21\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n20\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nView all 217 research outputs\nProjects\n4\nFinished\n8\nActive\nGRF:\nProgrammable Optoelectronic Memory Device Made from Selenium Nanoflake-Based 2D Heterostructures for In-Sensor Compressing\nTAN, C.\n(Principal Investigator / Project Coordinator) & WANG, Z. (Co-Investigator)\n1/01/26\n→ …\nProject\n:\nResearch\nNeuromorphic Computing\n100%\nTransistor\n93%\nLithium Ion\n75%\nNanosheet\n75%\nNanostructured Material\n75%\nSZNSFC-GP-SRI:\n水滑石基压电纳米材料用于肿瘤催化治疗\nTAN, C.\n(Principal Investigator / Project Coordinator), HU, T. (Co-Investigator) & YU, C. (Co-Investigator)\n21/10/25\n→ …\nProject\n:\nResearch\nYCRG-ExtU-Lead:\nOrganic/two-dimensional Materials Heterostructure Based Memristor Array for Flexible Retinomorphic System\nHAN, S. (Main Project Coordinator [External]) &\nTAN, C.\n(Principal Investigator / Project Coordinator)\n1/05/25\n→ …\nProject\n:\nResearch\nHeterojunction\n100%\nNeuromorphic Computing\n80%\nOptoelectronic Sensor\n80%\nNanostructured Material\n80%\nComputer Vision\n80%\nYCRG-ExtU-Lead:\nPerovskite Opto-ionics for In-sensor Computing\nZHOU, Y. (Main Project Coordinator [External]) &\nTAN, C.\n(Principal Investigator / Project Coordinator)\n30/06/24\n→ …\nProject\n:\nResearch\nNeuromorphic Computing\n100%\nTransistor\n93%\nHeterojunction\n93%\nOptoelectronic Sensor\n75%\nNanosheet\n75%\nGRF:\nGrowth of High-Quality Tellurium Thin Films via Substrate Engineering for High-Performance p-Type Field-Effect Transistors and Circuits\nTAN, C.\n(Principal Investigator / Project Coordinator)\n1/01/23\n→ …\nProject\n:\nResearch\nElectronic Circuit\n100%\nThin Films\n100%\nField Effect Transistor\n100%\nTwo-Dimensional Material\n66%\nHeterojunction\n62%\nView all 12 projects\nPrizes\nStanford's Top 2% most highly cited scientists 2025\nTAN, C.\n(Recipient),\nSept 2025\nPrize\n:\nRGC 64B - Prizes and awards\nScientific Field\n100%\nHighly Cited Paper\n100%\nHighly Cited Researcher in Materials Science, 2025\nTAN, C.\n(Recipient),\nNov 2025\nPrize\n:\nRGC 64B - Prizes and awards\nMaterials Engineering\n100%\nQualitative Method\n100%\nElectrospray Ionization\n100%\nHighly Cited Researcher in Materials Science, 2024\nTAN, C.\n(Recipient),\nNov 2024\nPrize\n:\nRGC 64B - Prizes and awards\nMaterials Engineering\n100%\nQualitative Method\n100%\nElectrospray Ionization\n100%\nHighly Cited Researcher in Chemistry, 2024\nTAN, C.\n(Recipient),\nNov 2024\nPrize\n:\nRGC 64B - Prizes a...[truncated]"
