    "homepage_text": "Y Lab | Purdue | Yang Yang\ntop of page\nHeading 1\nLab\nAdvancing precision medicine to cure brain disorders\nAt Y lab, we remember we are peacetime warriors\ncombating devastating human diseases by pushing the endless frontiers in science\n.\nResearch Mission\nOur lab aims to advance pharmacogenomics and precision medicine to treat genetic brain disorders (\nYang, Neuron 2025\n).\nOne main focus of the lab is disorders related to\nSCN2A\ngenetic variants, recently discovered as a leading monogenic cause of autism and epilepsy.\nSCN2A\ngene encodes the voltage-gated sodium channel Nav1.2, mediating neuronal action potential firing in the central nervous system. We use rodent models and human induced Pluripotent Stem Cells (hiPSCs) derived neurons, microglia, and brain organoid models for disease modeling and unveiling disease mechanisms. We also develop next-generation therapeutics, including CRISPR Prime Editing, to tackle the disorders with the ultimate goal of effectively treating patients in a precision medicine manner.\nVincent Van Gogh had epilepsy and possibly fell on the autism spectrum.\nTraining Mission\nOur lab aims to train future leaders in science and society with critical and hypothesis-driven thinking, teamwork and leadership spirit, and the desire and ability to get things done to make a dent in the universe.\nAcknowledgement\nWe thank patient families, the\nFamilieSCN2A\nFoundation, philanthropic donors, and NIH for supporting our work.\nWe will fight until a magical future arrives\n.\nYang lab short video:\n\"we will fight for you\"\n​\nYang Lab Core values\nYang Lab Core values\nYang Lab Core values\nYang Lab Core values\nImpact\nImpact\nImpact\nImpact\nrigor\nrigor\nrigor\nrigor\npassion\npassion\npassion\npassion\nUrgency\nUrgency\nUrgency\nUrgency\nWe\nstrive to conduct impactful research that will push the field forward and change lives towards a better future.\nWe\nwant our work to stand the test of time, and the knowledge and products we created to be trusted, used and built up on.\nWe\nopen our eyes every day feeling excited to come to work to solve mystery, make the impossible possible and touch lives.\nWe\nknow patients are suffering now, and families are desperately waiting for cures. There is no time to waste.\ninnovative\ninnovative\ninnovative\ninnovative\ninclusive\ninclusive\ninclusive\ninclusive\ncollaborative\ncollaborative\ncollaborative\ncollaborative\nproactive\nproactive\nproactive\nproactive\nWe\nfearlessly advance cutting-edge technologies to perform transformative research that generate strong impact.\nWe\nvalue each member' opinion and appreciate the diverse perspectives brought in by each person's unique background.\nWe\neach has expertise and strengths, but we alone won't be enough. We build strong partnership to achieve great outcomes.\nWe\nare driven to get things done and refuse to wait. We embrace underdog mentality, pushing boundaries to turn bold ideas into reality.\nWe always look for hungry postdocs, graduate students, and technicians who dream big and work hard. Please contact Dr. Yang Yang (\nyangyang@purdue.edu\n) for opportunities.\n​\n​\nThe human brain is a vast internal ocean where every neural current must find its perfect equilibrium. Our lab's translational effort: Aequovix Bio (aequo: of tides and balance; vix: of life and restoration) resolves this biological equation through precision genetic interventions, transforming neurological turbulence into enduring vitality (details forthcoming).\n​\n​\nbottom of page"
  },
