    "homepage_text": "Zhengyang Zhou\n      -  UNT Health\nUNT Health Home\nSearch content at UNT Health\nView Scopus Profile\nZhengyang Zhou, PhD\nCollege of Public Health\nAssociate Professor\n,\nPopulation and Community Health\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-8039-418X\nEmail\nZhengyang.Zhou\nunthsc\nedu\nh-index\n663\nCitations\n15\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2017\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nResearch Interests\nAging, Alzheimer's disease, Biostatistics, Clinical trials, Health behaviors, Machine learning, Statistical genetics, Substance use\nURL\nDr Zhengyang Zhou's webpage\nArea of Expertise\nMy research agenda can be broadly classified into two major dimensions: statistical methodology and discovery-oriented collaboration. In methodological research, I focus on (a) developing novel statistical methods to address real-world research challenges and (b) evaluating existing methods to inform practical recommendations for applied researchers. In discovery-oriented collaborative research, I aid discoveries with sophisticated data analytics in large interdisciplinary research groups. Thus far, I have contributed to three scientific areas: aging and Alzheimer’s disease, health behaviors and substance use, and statistical genetics / genetic epidemiology.\nEducation/Academic qualification\nBS in Mathematics ,\nBeijing Institute of Technology\nMS in Statistics,\nSouthern Methodist University\nPhD in Biostatistics,\nSouthern Methodist University\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Zhengyang Zhou is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n7\nSimilar Profiles\nOlder Adults\nKeyphrases\n100%\nAlcohol Use\nKeyphrases\n66%\nAlzheimer's Disease\nKeyphrases\n64%\nNon-Hispanic White\nKeyphrases\n55%\nIntervention Effect\nKeyphrases\n52%\nMexican Americans\nKeyphrases\n47%\nAlcohol\nKeyphrases\n41%\nCount Outcomes\nKeyphrases\n37%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nProjects\n8\nActive\n11\nFinished\nExploring Daily-Level Associat\nZhou, Z.\n(PI)\nNIAAA: Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism\n1/09/25\n→\n31/08/27\nProject\n:\nResearch\nInvestigating the association\nCurry, K.\n(PI),\nWiechmann, A.\n(CoI),\nZhou, Z.\n(CoI) &\nFranks, S.\n(CoI)\nThe University of Texas System\n1/09/24\n→\n31/08/26\nProject\n:\nResearch\nInvestigating the association\nCurry, K.\n(PI),\nFranks, S.\n(CoI),\nWiechmann, A.\n(CoI) &\nZhou, Z.\n(CoI)\nThe University of Texas System\n1/09/24\n→\n31/08/26\nProject\n:\nResearch\nINACTIVE\nCurry, K.\n(PI),\nWiechmann, A.\n(CoI) &\nZhou, Z.\n(CoI)\nThe University of Texas System\n1/09/24\n→\n31/08/26\nProject\n:\nResearch\nInnovative Computational Tools\nZhou, Z.\n(PI) &\nMun, E.-Y.\n(CoI)\nUniversity of Washington\n21/06/24\n→\n30/04/26\nProject\n:\nResearch\nView all 19 sponsored projects\nResearch output\n56\nArticle\n4\nReview article\n2\nLetter\nDo Brief Alcohol Interventions Reduce Driving After Drinking Among College Students? A Two-step Meta-analysis of Individual Participant Data\nMun, E. Y.\n, Li, X., Lineberry, S., Tan, Z., Huh, D.,\nWalters, S. T.\n,\nZhou, Z.\n& Larimer, M. E.,\n1 Jan 2022\n,\nIn:\nAlcohol and Alcoholism.\n57\n,\n1\n,\np. 125-135\n11 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nReview article\n›\npeer-review\nDriving after Drinking\n100%\nMeta-analysis\n100%\nCollege Students\n100%\nIndividual Participant Data\n100%\nBrief Alcohol Intervention\n100%\nSample size calculation for cluster randomized trials with zero-inflated count outcomes\nZhou, Z.\n, Li, D. & Zhang, S.,\n30 May 2022\n,\nIn:\nStatistics in Medicine.\n41\n,\n12\n,\np. 2191-2204\n14 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nCluster Randomized Trial\n100%\nSample Size Calculation\n100%\nCount Outcomes\n100%\nZero-inflated Counts\n100%\nRandomized Trial\n100%\nA comparison of Bayesian to maximum likelihood estimation for latent growth models in the presence of a binary outcome\nKim, S. Y., Huh, D.,\nZhou, Z.\n&\nMun, E. Y.\n,\n1 Sep 2020\n,\nIn:\nInternational Journal of Behavioral Development.\n44\n,\n5\n,\np. 447-457\n11 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nBayesian Estimation\n100%\nBayesian\n100%\nMaximum Likelihood\n100%\nMaximum Likelihood Estimation\n100%\nBinary Outcome\n100%\nA novel syndrome with short stature, mandibular hypoplasia, and osteoporosis may be associated with a PRRT3 variant\nGarg, A., El-Shanti, H., Xing, C.,\nZhou, Z.\n, Abujbara, M., Al-Rashed, K., El-Khateeb, M., Ajlouni, K. & Agarwal, A. K.,\n1 Aug 2020\n,\nIn:\nJournal of the Endocrine Society.\n4\n,\n8\n, bvaa088.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOsteoporosis\n100%\nProline-rich\n100%\nTransmembrane Protein\n100%\nShort Stature\n100%\nNovel Syndrome\n100%\nInstability of TCF4 triplet repeat expansion with parent– child transmission in Fuchs’ endothelial corneal dystrophy\nSaade, J. S., Xing, C., Gong, X.,\nZhou, Z.\n& Mootha, V. V.,\nAug 2018\n,\nIn:\nInvestigative Ophthalmology and Visual Science.\n59\n,\n10\n,\np. 4065-4070\n6 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nParent-child Relationship\n100%\nTriplet Repeat Expansion\n100%\nFuchs Endothelial Corneal Dystrophy\n100%\nTranscription Factor 4 (TCF4)\n100%\nAllele\n100%\nView all 62 Research outputs"
