    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Bo Wang\nSearch\nBo Wang\nScientist of AI for Health and Genomics\nUniversity of Toronto\nBiography\nBo Wang is an assistant professor at Dept. of Medical Biophysics at University of Toronto. He leads the AI team for Peter Munk Cardiac Centre (PMCC) at University Health Network (UHN). He is also a CIFAR AI Chair at Vector Institute, Toronto.\nBo obtained his PhD from the Department of Computer Science at Stanford University, and has extensive industrial research experience at many leading companies such as Illumina and Genentech. His PhD work covers statistical methods for solving problems in computational biology with an emphasis on integrative cancer analysis and single-cell analysis.\nBo Wang’s long-term research goals aim to develop integrative and interpretable machine learning algorithms that can help clinicians with predictive models and decision support to tailor patients’ care to their unique clinical and genomic traits.\nInterests\nMachine Learning\nComputational Biology\nComputer Vision\nEducation\nPhD in Computer Science, 2017\nStanford University\nMaster in Computer Science, 2012\nUniversity of Toronto\nBSc in Electronic Engineering, 2010\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nSelected Publications\nVicus: Exploiting local structures to improve network-based analysis of biological data.\nVicus is a new type of Laplacian matrix for biological networks with specific focus on local structures.\nBo Wang, Lin Huang, Yuke Zhu, Anshul Kundaje, Serafim Batzoglou, Anna Goldenberg\nIn\nPlos Combio\n,\n    \n    2017\nPDF\nCode\nVisualization and analysis of single-cell RNA-seq data by kernel-based similarity learning\nSIMLR is an AI-based tool that can visualize and analyze single-cell RNA-seq data.\nBo Wang, Junjie Zhu, Emma Pierson, Daniele Ramazzotti, Serafim Batzoglou\nIn\nNature Methods\n,\n    \n    2017\nPDF\nCode\nSimilarity network fusion for aggregating data types on a genomic scale\nSNF is an integrative algorithm that can combine multiple omics data for cancer subtyping.\nBo Wang, Aziz M. Mezlini, Feyyaz Demir, Marc Fiume, Zhuowen Tu, Michael Brudno, Benjamin Haibe-Kains, Anna Goldenberg\nIn\nNature Methods\n,\n    \n    2014\nPDF\nCode\nRecent Publications\nNetwork Enhancement: a general method to denoise weighted biological networks.\nNetwork Enhancement (NE) is an automatic algorithm that denoises biological networks. This work has been recently published in Nature …\nBo Wang, Armin Pourshafeie, Marinka Zitnik, Junjie Zhu, Carlos D. Bustamante, Serafim Batzoglou, Jure Leskovec\nPDF\nCode\nSingle-Shot Object Detection with Enriched Semantics.\nAn improved single-stage object detection system that utilizes enriched semantics by applying segmentation modules in detection.This …\nZhishuai Zhang, Siyuan Qiao, Cihang Xie, Wei Shen, Bo Wang, Alan L Yuille\nPDF\nCode\nContact\nName\nEmail\nMessage\nSend\n661 University Ave., Suite 710, Toronto, ON M5G 1M1, Canada\nemail for appointment\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
  "serper::Yueyu Hu": {
    "homepage": "https://huzi96.github.io/",
