    "homepage_text": "Woojin Lee\n      -  Nazarbayev University\nNazarbayev University Home\nEnglish\nрусский\nSearch content at Nazarbayev University\nView Scopus Profile\nWoojin Lee\nProfessor, Ph.D. in Environmental Engineering, Head / National Laboratory Astana\nProfessor\n,\nSchool of Engineering and Digital Sciences\nSchool of Engineering and Digital Sciences\n,\nDepartment of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-7082-5687\nPhone\n+7-7172-70-6540\nEmail\nwoojin.lee\nnu.edu\nkz\nAccepting PhD Students\nPhD projects\n1. Smart environmental catalysis\n2. Development of Integrated Wastewater Treatment System with Energy Generation\n3. CO2 and Green House Gas Sequestration\n4. Fate of environmental emerging contaminants\nh-index\n6433\nCitations\n44\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n1995                 …\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nEducation/Academic qualification\nEnvironmental Engineering, Ph.D.,\nTexas A&M University\nSept 1 1995\n→\nAug 21 2001\nAward Date: Aug 21 2001\nEnvironmental Chemistry, Postdoctoral Fellow,\nIndiana University Bloomington\nJan 1 2002\n→\nAug 31 2003\nEnvironmental Engineering, Research Associate,\nTexas A&M University\nSept 1 2001\n→\nDec 31 2001\nExternal positions\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Woojin Lee is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nreduction\nINIS\n100%\nremoval\nINIS\n94%\niron\nINIS\n67%\ncatalysts\nINIS\n62%\nsurfaces\nINIS\n58%\nkazakhstan\nINIS\n54%\nnanostructures\nINIS\n49%\ncarbon dioxide\nINIS\n48%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nProjects\n5\nActive\n6\nFinished\nStudy of the potential technological application of natural nemalite-serpentinite and technogenic serpentinite rocks for carbon capture, absorption and storage\nLee, W.\n(PI)\n10/2/24\n→\n12/20/26\nProject\n:\nGovernment\nTechnogenic Materials\n100%\nSerpentinite\n100%\nCarbon Capture\n100%\nCarbon Absorption\n100%\nTechnological Applications\n100%\nRisk assessment of micropollutants in Astana urban water system\nLee, W.\n(PI)\n1/1/24\n→\n12/31/26\nProject\n:\nGovernment\nMicropollutants\n100%\nRisk Assessment\n100%\nUrban Water System\n100%\nAstana\n100%\nrisk assessment\n100%\nEnvironmental Assessment of Kazakhstan’s urban water and wastewater treatment plants\nLee, W.\n(PI)\n1/1/24\n→\n12/31/26\nProject\n:\nFDCRGP\nWastewater Treatment Plant\n100%\nWater Treatment Plant\n100%\nEnvironmental Assessment\n100%\nKazakhstan\n100%\nUrban Water\n100%\nApplication of carbon capture utilization and sequestration (CCUS) and hydrogen production technologies to the different industrial sectors of Kazakhstan for its carbon neutralization\nLee, W.\n(PI),\nMadani, N.\n(Co-PI), Baimatova, N. (Co-PI) & Zholdayakova, S. (Co-PI)\n1/1/24\n→\n12/31/26\nProject\n:\nCRP\nCarbon Capture Utilization\n100%\nHydrogen Production Technology\n100%\nCarbon Capture Sequestration\n100%\nCarbon Neutralization\n100%\nIndustrial Sector\n100%\nCopper Porphyry Mine Tailings: Workflow for Valorization and Environmental Remediation\nMadani, N.\n(PI),\nAtakhanova, Z.\n(Co-PI),\nLee, W.\n(Co-PI), Bekbotayeva, A. (Co-PI), Barmenshinova, M. (Co-PI) & Frenzel , M. (Co-PI)\n1/1/23\n→\n12/31/26\nProject\n:\nCRP\nFile\nmine tailings\n100%\nstorage facilities\n100%\nremedial action\n100%\ncopper\n100%\nTailings Storage Facility\n100%\nView all 11 projects\nResearch output\n235\nAbstract\n175\nArticle\n6\nConference contribution\n6\nChapter (peer-reviewed)\n12\nMore\n4\nComment/debate\n3\nConference article\n2\nReview article\n1\nBook\n1\nEditorial\n1\nPatent\nBio-inspired ZIF-derived Co/N-doped carbon for efficient one-step CO\n2\nmineralization under ambient conditions\nAbid, H. M. W., Nurmyrza, M.,\nLee, W.\n&\nBalanay, M. P.\n,\nMar 15 2026\n,\nIn:\nChemical Engineering Journal.\n532\n, 174618.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nCo@N-doped Carbon\n100%\nZIF-derived Carbon\n100%\nCalcium Carbonate\n50%\nCO2 Capture Technologies\n33%\nCO2 Utilization Technologies\n33%\nRevealing the hidden burden: A life cycle assessment (LCA) of water treatment sludge disposal\nAlibekov, A., Almagambetov, E. &\nLee, W.\n,\nJan 1 2026\n,\nIn:\nWater Research X.\n30\n, 100461.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nwater treatment\n100%\nlife cycle assessment\n100%\nsludges\n100%\nWater Treatment Sludge\n100%\nLagooning\n80%\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitation\n(SciVal)\nUnbottling the risk: Microplastic release and health hazards from bottled drinks\nAlibekov, A., Shakhmaral, I., Meirambayeva, M., Batyrbayeva, A. &\nLee, W.\n,\nJan 15 2026\n,\nIn:\nScience of the Total Environment.\n1012\n, 181195.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nMicroplastic Release\n100%\nBottled Beverages\n100%\nrisks\n100%\nhealth hazards\n100%\nmicroplastics\n100%\nCarbon Neutrality of Central Asia: Technological Prospects and Challenges\nLee, W.\n,\nNov 14 2025\n,\nIn:\nACS ES and T Engineering.\n5\n,\n11\n,\np. 2698-2700\n3 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nComment/debate\n›\npeer-review\nCarbon neutrality of Central Asia: Technological prospects and challenges\nLee, W.\n,\n2025\n, (Accepted/In press)\nIn:\nACS ES and T Engineering.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nView all 434 research outputs\nPrizes\nAsian University Alliance (AUA) Professor\nLee, W.\n(Recipient),\n2019\nPrize\n:\nHon