    "homepage_text": "Xiaoyan Yang | Graduate & Postdoctoral Studies\nGraduate & Postdoctoral Studies\nToggle navigation\nXiaoyan Yang\n2020 MSc Tourism and Hospitality\nWords of advice for someone considering graduate school.\nDo not hesitate to ask questions in all aspects of overseas study. Your peers, professors, graduate coordinators, and everyone you meet here would love to help.\nProfile\nProgram​\nMSc. Tourism and Hospitality\nWhy I chose Guelph\nU of G is one of the best universities which offers master degrees in Tourism and Hospitality.\nAbout my advisor\nMy advisor was very instructive and patient in coaching\nMy favorite thing about the campus\nThe library, the gym, and the quiet campus during summer.\nHow will my work Improve Life?\nMy research interest was in hospitality employee well-being and the way to face their work-life conflicts. One of the objectives of my study was to improve hospitality employees' quality of life.\nProspective Students\nProspective Students Overview\nWhy Choose Guelph\nGraduate Programs\nApplying to Guelph\nInformation Sessions\nProfessional Course-based Masters Programs\nScholarships & Funding\nTuition, Fees and Cost of Living\nInternational Applicants\nGraduate Student Perspectives\nSpotlight on Faculty\nFAQ – Frequently Asked Questions\nAcademic Programs\nCotutelle"
