    "homepage_text": "Shengju Qian\nShengju Qian\nI received my PhD at\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong\n, supervised by\nProf. Jiaya Jia\n.\nMy research interests lie primarily in generative modeling and transformers.\nI have spent wonderful times at Google Brain, Amazon AI, and SenseTime Research.\nEmail\n/\nLinkedIn\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\nPublication\nGoogle Scholar\nExperience\nJune. 2022 - Dec. 2022\n,\nGoogle Brain\nMentor: Han Zhang, Huiwen Chang.\nJune. 2020 - June. 2022\n,\nAmazon AI\nMentor: Yi Zhu, Mu Li.\nDec. 2018 - Apr.2019\n,\nTencent Youtu, X-Lab\nMentor: Xiaoyong Shen.\nMar. 2018 - Dec.2018\n,\nSenseTime Research\nMentor: Wayne Wu, Chen Qian.\nServices\nConference Reviewer: CVPR, ECCV, AAAI, ICML, NeurIPS, ICLR\nJournal Reviewer:Transactions on Image Processing(TIP), Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence(TPAMI)\nMisc\nAn amateur in trail running, cycling, and triathlon.\nHoh Xil, 2016"
