  "serper::Ting Zhang": {
    "homepage": "http://www.ting-zhang.com/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Ting Zhang - Ting Zhang\nTing Zhang\nHome\nResearch + Data\nTeaching\nMedia\nCV\nDevelopMENTOR Lab\nTing Zhang is an Assistant Professor of Business Administration and Hellman Faculty Fellow in the Organizational Behavior Unit at Harvard Business School,\nwhere she teaches the Leadership and Organizational Behavior course (LEAD) in the Required Curriculum.\nHer research focuses on the challenges of developing talent and\nexamines how organizations can foster more effective coaching,\nmentoring, and sponsorship\n.\nHer research has been published in journals such as the\nAcademy of Management Journal\n,\nManagement Science\n,\nOrganizational Behavior and Human Decision Processes\n,\nPsychological Science\n,\nJournal of Experimental Psychology: General\n, and\nResearch in Organizational Behavior\nand covered in media outlets including\nThe Atlantic\n,\nNew York Times,\nand\nThe Washington Post\n.​\nPrior to joining HBS, she was a Postdoctoral Research Scholar in the Management Division at Columbia Business School, where she taught Managerial Negotiations. She received her A.B. in Economics and Ph.D. in Organizational Behavior from Harvard University.\nProudly powered by\nWeebly"
  },
  "serper::Kan Guo": {
    "homepage": "https://han-guo.info/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/github.com",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Han Guo\nHan Guo\nI am a PhD student at\nMIT CSAIL\n, advised by\nProf. Yoon Kim\nand\nProf. Eric P. Xing\n.\n                Prior to this, I spent several wonderful years at CMU's\nLanguage Technologies Institute\nand the\nUNC-NLP\nresearch group with\nProf. Mohit Bansal\n.\n                These days, I focus primarily on algorithms and systems for scalable and efficient ML/NLP.\n                I am a recipient of\n2022 Microsoft Research PhD Fellowship\n.\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nCV\n/\nGitHub\nNews\n2025-06\nStarted internship with\nTri Dao\nat\nTogether AI\n.\n2025-02\nTalked about flexible LLM quantization at Meta (Efficiency lecture series).\n2024-12\nTest-Time Training received 2nd place in ARC Prize (Paper Award).\n2024 Summer\nTalked about low-bit and non-uniform LLM quantization at Salesforce, Amazon (InfOpt Quantization Talk), Fireworks AI, Bloomberg LLM Reading Group, Neural Magic, and Together AI.\n2023-05\nSelected as one of the\nMachine Learning and Systems Rising Stars\n.\n2022-10\nHonored to receive the 2022 Microsoft Research Ph.D. Fellowship.\n2021-06\nStarted internship with\nYoon Kim\nat\nMIT-IBM Watson AI Lab\n.\n2020-06\nStarted internship with\nCaiming Xiong\nand\nNazneen Rajani\nat\nSalesforce Research\n.\n2019-12\nAwarded Finalist for the 2020\nCRA Outstanding Undergraduate Researcher Award\n.\n2019-08\nHad a wonderful summer working with\nBoyang Li\nat\nBaidu Research\n.\n2018-12\nAwarded Honorable Mention for the 2019\nCRA Outstanding Undergraduate Researcher Award\n.\n2018-06\nOur paper \"Dynamic Multi-Level Multi-Task Learning for Sentence Simplification\" is selected as\nArea Chair Favorites\nat COLING 2018.\n2018-05\nThanks NSF / ACL Walker Fund for travel award.\n2017-11\nThanks UNC Office of Undergraduate Research for travel award.\nResearch\nThis guy makes a nice webpage."
  },
  "serper::Suzhong Wei": {
    "homepage": "http://wzhongwise.weebly.com/research.html",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Research - Welcome to Wei Zhong's Homepage\nWelcome to Wei Zhong's Homepage\nHome\nResearch\nCourses\nLinks\nPhotos\nResearch Interests\n> High Dimensional Data Analysis and Feature Selection\n> Statistical Learning and Data Mining\n>\nEndogeneity Problems in\nEconometrics\n> Nonparametric and Semiparametric Models\n> Applications of Statistics in Business Analytics, Information Science etc.\nResearch Papers\n[16] \"Forward Additive Regression for Ultrahigh Dimensional Nonparametric Models.\" (with Sunpeng Duan, Liping Zhu).\nStatistica Sinica\n, Accepted 2018.\n[15] \"Variable Selection for Structural Equation Using Adaptive LASSO.\" (with Qingliang Fan),\nJournal of Systems Science and Complexity.\nAccepted 2017\n[14] \"Test for High Dimensional Regression Coefficients Using Refitted Cross-validation Variance Estimation.\" (with Hengjian Cui, Wenwen Guo).\nThe Annals of Statistics.\nAccepted, 2017.\n[13] \"Variable Selection and Direction Estimation for Single-Index Models via DC-TGDR Method.\" (with Shuangge Ma, Xi Liu).\nStatistics and Its Interface.\n11, 169-181, 2018.\n[12] \"Projection correlation between two random vectors.\" (with Liping Zhu, Kai Xu and Runze Li).\nBiometrika.\n104, 829-843, 2017.\n[11] \"Nonparametric Additive Instrumental Variable Estimator: A Group Shrinkage Estimation Perspective.\" (with Qingliang Fan).\nJournal of Business & Economic Statistics\n, Accepted, 2016.\n[10] \"Regularized Quantile Regression and Robust Feature Screening for Single Index Models\". (with Liping Zhu, Runze Li and Hengjian Cui).\nStatistica Sinica\n, 26, 69-95, 2016.\n[9] \"Estimation and Inference on Central Mean Subspace for Multivariate Response Data.\" (with Liping Zhu).\nComputational Statistics & Data Analysis\n, 92, 68--83, 2015.\n[8] \"A Selective Overview of Feature Screening for Ultrahigh-Dimensional Data.\" (with Runze Li and Jingyuan Liu).\nScience China Mathematics\n, 58, 2033--2054, 2015.\n[7] \"Model Selection for High-Dimensional Problems.\" (with Jing-zhi Huang and Zhan Shi). Chapter 77,\nHandbook of Financial Econometrics and Statistics\n, Springer-Verlag, New York, 2015. ISBN 978-1-4614-7749-5.\n[6] \"Model-Free Feature Screening for Ultrahigh Dimensional Discriminant Analysis\". (with Hengjian Cui and Runze Li).\nJournal of the American Statistical Association\n,\n58, 2033-2054, 2015.\n[5] \"An Iterative Approach to Distance Correlation Based Sure Independence Screening.\" (with Liping Zhu).\nJournal of Statistical Computation and Simulation,\n85, 2331-2345, 2015.\n[4] \"Robust Sure Independence Screening for Ultrahigh Dimensional Non-normal Data\".\nActa Mathematica Sinica, English Series\n, 30(11), 1885-1896, 2014.\n[3] \"A Fast Algorithm for Detecting Gene-Gene Interactions in Genome-Wide Association Studies\". (with Jiahan Li, Runze Li and Rongling Wu).\nAnnals of Applied Statistics\n, 8(4), 2292-2318, 2014.\n[2] \"Feature Screening via Distance Correlation Learning\".  (with Runze Li and  Liping Zhu).\nJournal of the American Statistical Association\n, Vol. 107, No. 499, 1129-1139, 2012.\n[1] \"Assessing Mediation Using Marginal Structural Models in the Presence of Confounding and Moderation\". (with Danna Coffman).\nPsychological Methods\n, Vol. 17, No. 4, 642–664, 2012.\nPowered by\nCreate your own unique website with customizable templates.\nGet Started"
