esearch and Faculty\nAdmission Info\nAdmission Info\nApplication Procedures for Admissions\nFinancial Supports\nPast Paper Test for Five-Year Doctor Course\nCareer After Graduation\nInter-University Researcher\nSpecial Inter-University Researcher\nFor Current Students\nLecture Schedule & Annual Events\nSyllabus\nRequirements for doctor degree\nApplication Procedures for Students\nStudent Handbook\nStudent Consultation\nMental Health\nLife@Okazaki\nLife@Okazaki\nImmigration and Access\nLegal Procedures\nProcedures at IMS\nAccommodation\nLodges\nApartment Houses\nDaily Life\nLifelines\nMedical care and Emergency\nBanking and Insurance\nTransportation\nShopping and Restaurants\nFamily and Children\namily's Visit\nNursery school and education\nPregnancy and Delivery\nAbout Okazaki City\nAbout Okazaki City\nVoice from Alumni\nImpressions of IMS\nContact Us\nContact Us\nAccess\nResearchers List\nPublication\nContact\nJapanese\nResearch\nResearchers detail\nIMS Researchers\nResearchers List\nResearch Group List\nHOME\n-\nResearch\n-\nResearchers detail\n-\nWang Yuelin\nResearch\n- IMS Researchers\nResearch Group List\nResearch Facilities\nResearchers List\nOrganization List\n- Seminar & Events\nUpcoming Seminars\nPast List\n- Activity\nActivities List\nResearcher interview\nProjects\n6251\nWang Yuelin\nRes. Assist. Prof.\nTEL: 0564-55-7274\nE-Mail : yuelin_at_ims.ac.jp (Please replace the \"_at_\" with @ )\nLocation: Myodaiji\nAffiliation laboratory >\nDepartment\nDepartment of Theoretical and Computational Molecular Science, Computational Molecular Science\nBiography\n2016   B.S. at Hebei Normal University Department of Chemistry\n2019   M.S. at Northeast Normal University Department of Chemistry\n2023   Ph.D. at Osaka University Department of Precision Engineering\n2022. April- 2023. November   Japan Society for the Promotion of Science (JSPS) Research Fellow (DC2) at Osaka University\n2023. December-2024. March   JSPS Postdoctoral Research Fellow (PD) at Osaka University\n2024. April-2024. May   Postdoctoral Researcher at Institute for Molecular Science\n2024. June-   Research Assistant Professor at Institute for Molecular Science\nAwards\n2022 The Japan Society of Vacuum and Surface Science Best Female Student Award\nMain research themes\nTheoretical study on electronic structure and catalytic performance of catalysts\nHeterogeneous catalysts, Carbon-based catalysts, Energy conversion system, First-principles multiscale simulations\nAwards & Honors\nInternational collaboration\nLinks"
