    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Cheng Ji, PhD - Keck School of Medicine of USC\nSkip to Content\nOpen Site Navigation\nWHAT ARE YOU LOOKING FOR?\nWHAT ARE YOU LOOKING FOR?\nSubmit\nKey Searches\nMD Program\nResidencies and Clinical Fellowships\nPhysician Assistant Program\nMaster of Public Health\nKeck School Research\nFaculty\nNewsroom\nUSC.edu\nAre You a Patient?\nCheng Ji, PhD\nProfessor of Research Medicine\nWebsites\nCheng Ji, GI/Liver, USC\nCheng Ji, USC\nIs this your profile?\nClick to edit\nPhone\n+1 323 442 2224\nEmail\n[email protected]\nCTSI Profile\nOverview\nDr. Ji joined the faculty of Keck School of Medicine of USC in September 2000. Prior to the faculty, he earned his M.S. in Chemistry from Shanghai Jiao Tong Univ. and completed his PhD in Biochemistry and postdoctoral fellowships in Pathology/Medicine at Univ. of California and Keck School of Medicine of USC, respectively. Dr. Ji’s research interests include cellular organelle (e.g., ER, Golgi, mitochondria, or lysosomes) stress and liver disease, alcohol-induced hyperhomocysteinemia, and hepatotoxicity of anti-viral drugs and substance use disorders. He was among the first discovered in vivo the association of ER stress response with development of liver disease. Dr. Ji has published original research papers in leading journals such as Gastroenterology, Journal of Hepatology, Hepatology, PNAS, Cell, Nature Nanotech. and Advanced Materials.\nPublications\nEffects of Ritonavir, Lopinavir, and Alcohol on ABC Transporters and Secretion of Bile Acid and Bilirubin in Senescent Hepatocytes. Int J Mol Sci. 2026 Jan 25; 27(3).. View in\nPubMed\nAlcohol, Anti-HIV Drugs, and/or Hippuric Acid Deteriorate Cellular Stresses in Senescent Hepatocytes and Aging Murine Liver. J Addict Prev. 2025 Aug; 13(1).. View in\nPubMed\nTargeting of Tumoral NAC1 Mitigates Myeloid-Derived Suppressor Cell-Mediated Immunosuppression and Potentiates Anti-PD-1 Therapy in Ovarian Cancer. Cancer Immunol Res. 2025 Feb 03; 13(2):286-302.. View in\nPubMed\nCabozantinib selectively induces proteasomal degradation of p53 somatic mutant Y220C and impedes tumor growth. J Biol Chem. 2025 02; 301(2):108167.. View in\nPubMed\nEBUS-guided Iodine-125 seed implantation in lymph node as a novel therapy for MCAO: A case report. Medicine (Baltimore). 2025 Jan 17; 104(3):e41198.. View in\nPubMed\nEffects of Combination of Ethanol With Ritonavir, Lopinavir or Darunavir on Expression and Localization of the ER-Associated Set Protein and Infection of HIV-1 Pseudovirus in Primary Human Cells. J Acquir Immune Defic Syndr. 2024 06 01; 96(2):e6-e10.. View in\nPubMed\nChinese expert consensus on cone-beam CT-guided diagnosis, localization and treatment for pulmonary nodules. Thorac Cancer. 2024 03; 15(7):582-597.. View in\nPubMed\nMolecular Factors and Pathways of Hepatotoxicity Associated with HIV/SARS-CoV-2 Protease Inhibitors. Int J Mol Sci. 2023 Apr 27; 24(9).. View in\nPubMed\nLiver Injury Impaired 25-Hydroxylation of Vitamin D Suppresses Intestinal Paneth Cell defensins, leading to Gut Dysbiosis and Liver Fibrogenesis. Am J Physiol Gastrointest Liver Physiol. 2020 Oct 21.. View in\nPubMed\nRitonavir and Lopinavir Suppress RCE1 and CAAX Rab Proteins Sensitizing the Liver to Organelle Stress and Injury. Hepatol Commun. 2020 Jun; 4(6):932-944.. View in\nPubMed\nProtective Effects of Facilitated Removal of Blood Alcohol and Acetaldehyde Against Liver Injury in Animal Models Fed Alcohol and Anti-HIV Drugs. Alcohol Clin Exp Res. 2019 06; 43(6):1091-1102.. View in\nPubMed\nProtective Effects of Emodin on Lung Injuries in Rat Models of Liver Fibrosis. Open Life Sci. 2019 Jan; 14:611-618.. View in\nPubMed\nHuman Mesenchymal Stem Cell Derived Exosomes Alleviate Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus by Reversing Peripheral Insulin Resistance and Relieving β-Cell Destruction. ACS Nano. 2018 08 28; 12(8):7613-7628.. View in\nPubMed\nA Hepatocyte-Mimicking Antidote for Alcohol Intoxication. Adv Mater. 2018 May; 30(22):e1707443.. View in\nPubMed\nDisrupted ER-to-Golgi trafficking underlies anti-HIV drugs and alcohol-induced cellular stress and hepatic injury. Hepatology Commun. 2017; 1(2):122-139.\nDissecting the role of disturbed ER-Golgi trafficking in antivirals and alcohol abuse-induced pathogenesis of liver disorders. Journal of Drug Abuse. 2017; 3(3):14 .\nMolecules, Systems and Signaling in Liver Injury. Cell Death in Biology and Diseases. Nature Springer. Role of Endoplasmic Reticulum Stress in Hepatic Injury. 2017; 221-250.\nExpression of 78 kD glucose-regulated protein is increased in cirrhotic cardiomyopathy induced by intestinal endotoxin. Int J Clin Exp Pathol. 2017; 10(2):1549-1557.\nEffect of artesunate supplementation on bacterial translocation and dysbiosis of gut microbiota in rats with liver cirrhosis. World J Gastroenterol. 2016 Mar 14; 22(10):2949-59.. View in\nPubMed\nEnhanced expression of glucose-regulated protein 78 correlates with malondialdehyde levels during the formation of liver cirrhosis in rats. Exp Ther Med. 2015 Dec; 10(6):2119-2125.. View in\nPubMed\nAdvances and New Concepts in Alcohol-Induced Organelle Stress, Unfolded Protein Responses and Organ Damage. Biomolecules. 2015 Jun 03; 5(2):1099-121.. View in\nPubMed\nPrevention of hepatitis C virus infection and spread in human liver chimeric mice by an anti-CD81 monoclonal antibody. Hepatology. 2015 Apr; 61(4):1136-44.. View in\nPubMed\nIncreased expression of 78 kD glucose-regulated protein promotes cardiomyocyte apoptosis in a rat model of liver cirrhosis. Int J Clin Exp Pathol. 2015; 8(8):9256-63.. View in\nPubMed\nEffects of combined alcohol and anti-HIV drugs on cellular stress responses in primary hepatocytes and hepatic stellate and kupffer cells. Alcohol Clin Exp Res. 2015 Jan; 39(1):11-20.. View in\nPubMed\nGlucose-regulated protein 78 may play a crucial role in promoting the pulmonary microvascular remodeling in a rat model of hepatopulmonary syndrome. Gene. 2014 Jul 15; 545(1):156-62.. View in\nPubMed\nExpression of the 78 kD glucose-regulated protein is induced by endoplasmic reticulum stress in the development of hepatopulmonary syndrome. Gene. 2014 Mar 01; 537(1):115-9.. View in\nPubMed\nNew Insights into the Pathogenesis of Alcohol-Induced ER Stress and Liver Diseases. Int J Hepatol. 2014; 2014:513787.. View in\nPubMed\nCD133 positive cells isolated from A549 cell line exhibited high liver metastatic potential. Neoplasma. 2014; 61(2):153-60.. View in\nPubMed\nRestoration of intrahepatic regulatory T cells through MMP-9/13-dependent activation of TGF-β is critical for immune homeostasis following acute liver injury. J Mol Cell Biol. 2013 Dec; 5(6):369-79.. View in\nPubMed\nEvaluation of protein extraction protocols for 2DE in marine ecotoxicoproteomics. Proteomics. 2013 Nov; 13(21):3205-10.. View in\nPubMed\nEffects of Bacillus subtilis ANSB060 on growth performance, meat quality and aflatoxin residues in broilers fed moldy peanut meal naturally contaminated with aflatoxins. Food Chem Toxicol. 2013 Sep; 59:748-53.. View in\nPubMed\nBiomimetic enzyme nanocomplexes and their use as antidotes and preventive measures for alcohol intoxication. Nat Nanotechnol. 2013 Mar; 8(3):187-92.. View in\nPubMed\nAssociation of cyclin D and estrogen receptor α36 with hepatocellular adenomas of female mice under chronic endoplasmic reticulum stress. J Gastroenterol Hepatol. 2013 Mar; 28(3):576-83.. View in\nPubMed\nAltered methylation and expression of ER-associated degradation factors in long-term alcohol and constitutive ER stress-induced murine hepatic tumors. Front Genet. 2013; 4:224.. View in\nPubMed\nDetection of transgenic and endogenous plant DNA fragments and proteins in the digesta, blood, tissues, and eggs of laying hens fed with phytase transgenic corn. PLoS One. 2013; 8(4):e61138.. View in\nPubMed\nInvestigation of chronic alcohol consumption in rodents via ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry based metabolite profiling. J Chromatogr A. 2012 Oct 12; 1259:128-37.. View in\nPubMed\nThe effects of dietary fatty acid composition in the post-sucking period on metabolic alterations in adulthood: can ω3 polyunsaturated fatty acids prevent adverse programming outcomes? J Endocrinol. 2012 Oct; 215(1):119-27.. View in\nPubMed\nHuman immunodeficiency virus protease inhibitors modulate Ca2+ homeostasis and potentiate alcoholic stress and injury in mice and primary mouse and human hepatocytes. Hepatology. 2012 Aug; 56(2):594-604.. View in\nPubMed\nInterstrain differences in liver injury and one-carbon metabolism in alcohol-fed mice. Hepatology. 2012 Jul; 56(1):130-9.. View in\nPubMed\nDevelopment of a multiplex UPLC-MRM MS method for quantification of human membrane transport proteins OATP1B1, OATP1B3 and OATP2B1 in in vitro systems and tissues. Anal Chim Acta. 2012 Mar 02; 717:67-76.. View in\nPubMed\nExperimental SSM-CVB3 infection in macaques. Exp Mol Pathol. 2012 Feb; 92(1):131-9.. View in\nPubMed\nMechanisms of alcohol-induced endoplasmic reticulum stress and organ injuries. Biochem Res Int. 2012; 2012:216450.. View in\nPubMed\nFacilitated Removal of Blood Alcohol From Alcohol-Fed Animals by Nanocapsules of Alcohol Metabolizing Enzymes. Gastroenterology 142 (5): S-544. 2012.\nSynergistic steatohepatitis by moderate obesity and alcohol in mice despite increased adiponectin and p-AMPK. J Hepatol. 2011 Sep; 55(3):673-682.. View in\nPubMed\nLiver-specific loss of glucose-regulated protein 78 perturbs the unfolded protein response and exacerbates a spectrum of liver diseases in mice. Hepatology. 2011 Jul; 54(1):229-39.. View in\nPubMed\nRole of cAMP-responsive element-binding protein (CREB)-regulated transcription coactivator 3 (CRTC3) in the initiation of mitochondrial biogenesis and stress response in liver cells. J Biol Chem. 2011 Jun 24; 286(25):22047-54.. View in\nPubMed\nThe contribution of endoplasmic reticulum stress to liver diseases. Hepatology. 2011 May; 53(5):1752-63.. View in\nPubMed\nClinical evaluation of targeted arterial infusion of verapamil in the interventional chemotherapy of primary hepatocellular carcinoma. Cell Biochem Biophys. 2011 Mar; 59(2):1...[truncated]"
