    "homepage_text": "Chengjiang Long - Personal Website\nChengjiang Long\né¾ææ±\nPh.D., Research Engineer & Tech Leader\nByteDance Inc.\n1199 Coleman Ave\nSan Jose, CA 95110\nEmail: chengjiang.long AT gmail.com\nShort Biography\nDr. Chengjiang Long is currently a Research Engineer/Tech Leader in\nByteDance Inc.\nat the San Jose office. Prior joining ByteDance, he worked as a Scientist/Tech Leader in\nMeta Reality Labs\nat the Burlingame office from Dec 2021 to Apr 2025, a Principal Scientist/Tech Leader in\nJD Tech\nR&D Center at Silicon Valley (a part of\nJD.COM\n) from June 2020 to Dec 2021, and worked as a Computer Vision Researcher/Senior R&D Engineer at Kitware from February 2016 to April 2020. He also worked as an Adjunct Professor at\nUniversity at Albany, SUNY\nfrom August 2018 to May 2019, and was an Adjunct Professor at\nRensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI)\nfrom Jan 2018 to May 2018. He received the M.S. degree in Computer Science from Wuhan University in 2011 and a B.S degree in Computer Science and Technology from\nWuhan University\nin 2009 under the supervision of Prof.\nJianhui Zhao\n. He got his Ph.D. degree in Computer Science from\nStevens Institute of Technology\nin 2015 under the supervision of Prof.\nGang Hua\n.\nDuring his Ph.D. study, he worked at\nNEC Labs America\nand\nGE Global Research\nas a research intern in 2013 and 2015, respectively. To date, he has published over 90 papers including top journals such as ACM Transactions on Graphics (TOG), IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI), International Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV), IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics (TVCG), IEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP) and IEEE Transactions on multimedia (T-MM), top international conferences such as ACM SIGGRAPH Conference and Exhibition in Asia (SIGGRAPH Asia), IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI) and ACM International Conference on Multimedia (ACM MM), and owns 1 patent. He serves as Area Chair for top-tier conferences like CVPR and Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), and as Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for the top-tier AAAI conference. He is also the reviewer for more than 20 top international journals and conferences. His research interests involve various areas of Computer Vision, Computer Graphics, Multimedia, Machine Learning, and Artificial Intelligence. He is a member of IEEE and AAAI.\nIf you are interested in collaboration with him, please feel free to send him an email at chengjiang.long AT gmail.com.\nNews\n[03/24/2026] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nNeurIPS 2026\n!\n[03/18/2026] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nBMVC 2026\n!\n[02/21/2026] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nICPR 2026\n!\n[02/20/2026] Two papers were accepted to\nCVPR 2026\n!\n[01/26/2026] One paper was accepted to\nICLR 2026\n!\n[01/11/2026] One paper was accepted to\nTIP\n!\n[11/19/2025] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nICML 2026\n!\n[08/15/2025] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nCVPR 2026\n!\n[07/30/2025] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nAAAI 2026\n!\n[07/12/2025] I will serve as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nAAAI 2026\n.\n[06/25/2025] Four papers were accepted to\nICCV 2025\n!\n[06/09/2025] I will start to work as a Research Engineer & Tech Leader in\nByteDance\nat the San Jose office.\n[02/17/2025] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nNeurIPS 2025\n.\n[12/14/2024] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nICML 2025\n.\n[11/29/2024] I will serve as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nIJCAI 2025\n.\n[09/25/2024] One paper was accepted to\nNeurIPS 2024\n!\n[09/13/2024] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nCVPR 2025\n.\n[07/15/2024] One paper was accepted to\nACM MM 2024\n!\n[07/01/2024] Three papers were accepted to\nECCV 2024\n!\n[06/26/2024] One paper was accepted to\nTVCG\n!\n[06/14/2024] I will serve as a Session Chair for\nCVPR 2024\n.\n[06/10/2024] I will serve as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nAAAI 2025\n.\n[05/06/2024] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nNeurIPS 2024\n.\n[12/08/2023] One paper was accepted to\nAAAI 2024\n!\n[12/06/2023] One paper was accepted to\nT-MM\n!\n[07/01/2023] I will serve as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nAAAI 2024\n.\n[06/19/2023] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nCVPR 2024\n.\n[04/14/2023] One paper was accepted to\nT-PAMI\n!\n[02/27/2023] Three papers were accepted to\nCVPR 2023\n!\n[02/03/2023] One paper was accepted to\nRA-L\n!\nMore News..."
