    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yicong Li, National University of Singapore\nYicong Li\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nPhD Candidate\nNExT++ Research Center\nNUS School of Computing\nNUS Integrative Sciences and Engineering Programme\nEmail: lyc071719 at gmail.com\n•\nGoogle Scholar Page\n•\nGitHub Page\nBiography\nI am a PhD Candiate at\nNExT++\n, where I am supervised by\nProf.Chua Tat-Seng\nand mentored by\nWang Xiang\n. With my friends and collaborators, we strive to develop models on\nVideo and 3d scene understanding\nwith better\ninterpretability, generalization, and robustness\n. Our research is motivated by, and contributes to, Multi-modal learning.\nCollaborators\nAlways welcomed!Shot me an Email if you are interested.\nNews\n[New!]\n2024/02 One 1st author paper accepted by CVPR'24!\nLASO: Language-guided Affordance Segmentation on 3D Object\n.\n[New!]\n2023/07 One 1st author paper accepted by ACM MM'23!\nRedundancy-aware Transformer for Video Question Answering\n.\n[New!]\n2023/07 One 1st author paper accepted by ICCV'23!\nDiscovering Spatio-Temporal Rationales for Video Question Answering\n.\n[New!]\n2023/06 One 1st author paper accepted by TPAMI'23!\nTransformer-Empowered Invariant Grounding for\n                            Video Question Answering\n.\n2022/07 One 1st author paper accepted by ACM MM'22!\nEquivariant and Invariant Grounding for Video Question Answering.\n.\n2022/10 One paper accepted by EMNLP'22! Big congrats to Yaoyao ZHong and Other Collaborators!\nVideo Question Answering: Datasets, Algorithms and Challenges\n.\n2022/03 one 1st author paper accepted by CVPR'22!\nInvariant Grounding for Video Question Answering\n.\n[Oral Presentation & Best Paper Finalist]\n2021/12 One paper accepted by AAAI'22! Big congrats to Junbin and Other Collaborators!\nVideo as Conditional Graph Hierarchy for Multi-Granular Question Answering\n.\n2021/7 One  1st author paper accepted by ACM MM'21!\nInterventional Video Relation Detection\n.\nHighlights\nInvariant Grounding for Video Question Answering\ngot into the\nBest Paper Finalist CVPR'22\n. 33/8161.\nHonors and Awards\nBest Paper Award Finalist, CVPR 2022\nDean’s Graduate Research Excellence Award, National University of Singapore 2023\nResearch Achievement Award, National University of Singapore 2022\nBackground\nPhD in Computer Science, NExT++, National University of Singapore.\nSupervisor:\nProf Tat-Seng Chua\n; Mentor:\nProf Wang Xiang\nMaster in Robotics, Columbia University\nBachelor in Mechanical and Automation, HuaZhong University of Sience and Technology\nWebpage template borrows from\nProf Xiangnan He\nand\nProf Xia Hu"
  },
