    "homepage_text": "﻿\nXin Zhao\nXin Zhao\nTenured Associate Professor\nXin Zhao received his Ph.D. in Computer Science from Peking University in 2014. His research interests include data mining, natural language processing and information retrieval in general. The main goal is to study how to organize, analyze and mine user generated data for improving the service of real-world applications.\nEnter Personal Website\nEducation\n• PhD: School of Electronics Engineering and Computer Science, Peking University, September 2008——June 2014\n• Bachelor: School of Computer Science, Harbin Institute of Technology, September 2004 to July 2008\nWork Experience\n• School of Information, Renmin University of China，September 2017 to present, associate professor\n• Iflytek Beijing, visiting scholar, August 2018 to present\nRESEARCH INTERESTS\n• Topic modeling (mining topics from social text data)\n• Recommender systems (knowledge-aware recommendation, cross-site recommendation)\n• Social media data mining (tagging, event detection, burst detection, link prediction, user profiling)\nPUBLICATIONS\n2021\nA Novel Macro-Micro Fusion Network for User Representation Learning on Mobile Apps\nShuqing Bian, Xin Zhao, Kun Zhou, Xu Chen, Jing Cai, Yancheng He, Xingji Luo and Ji-Rong Wen\nWWW\nDual Sparse Attention Network for Session-Based Recommendation\nJiahao Yuan, Mingyou Sun, Zihan Song, Xiaoling Wang, Wayne Xin Zhao\nAAAI\nRocketQA: An Optimized Training Approach to Dense Passage Retrieval for Open-Domain Question Answering\nYingqi Qu, Yuchen Ding, Jing Liu, Kai Liu, Ruiyang Ren, Wayne Xin Zhao, Daxiang Dong, Hua Wu and Haifeng Wang\nNAACL\nPersonalized Route Recommendation with Neural Network Enhanced A∗ Search Algorithm\nJingyuan Wang, Ning Wu, and Wayne Xin Zhao\nIEEE TKDE\nKnowledge-based Review Generation by Coherence Enhanced Text Planning\nJunyi Li, Wayne Xin Zhao, Zhicheng Wei, Nicholas Jing Yuan and Ji-Rong Wen\nSIGIR\nLighter and Better: Low-Rank Decomposed Self-Attention Networks for Next-Item Recommendation\nXinyan Fan, Zheng Liu, Jianxun Lian, Wayne Xin Zhao, Xing Xie, and Ji-Rong Wen\nSIGIR (Short paper)\nPretrained Language Model for Text Generation: A Survey\nJunyi Li∗, Tianyi Tang∗, Wayne Xin Zhao and Ji-Rong Wen\nIJCAI (Survey Track)\nA Survey on Complex Knowledge Base Question Answering: Methods, Challenges and Solutions\nYunshi Lan∗ , Gaole He∗ , Jinhao Jiang, Jing Jiang, Xin Zhao and Ji-Rong Wen\nIJCAI (Survey Track)\nKnowledge-Guided Disentangled Representation Learning for Recommender Systems\nShanlei Mu, Yaliang Li, Wayne Xin Zhao, Siqing Li and Ji-Rong Wen\nTOIS\nFew-shot Knowledge Graph-to-Text Generation with Pretrained Language Models\nJunyi Li, Tianyi Tang, Wayne Xin Zhao, Ji-Rong Wen\nACL (Findings)\nLeveraging Passage-Centric Similarity Relation for Improving Dense Passage Retrieval\nRuiyang Ren*, Shangwen Lv*, Yingqi Qu, Jing Liu, Wayne Xin Zhao, Qiaoqiao She, Hua Wu, Haifeng Wang, Ji-Rong Wen\nACL (Findings)\nEnabling Lightweight Fine-tuning for Pre-trained Language Model Compression based on Matrix Product Operators\nPeiyu Liu*, Ze-Feng Gao*, Wayne Xin Zhao, Zhi-Yuan Xie, Zhong-Yi Lu and Ji-Rong Wen\nACL\nData Poisoning Attack against Recommender System Using Incomplete and Perturbed Data\nHengtong Zhang*, Changxin Tian*, Yaliang Li, Lu Su, Jing Gao, Nan Yang, Wayne Xin Zhao\nKDD\nRAPT: Pre-training of Time-Aware Transformer for Learning Robust Healthcare Representation\nHouxing Ren, Jingyuan Wang, Wayne Xin Zhao, Ning Wu\nKDD (Applied Data Science Track)\nLearning Reliable User Representations from Volatile and Sparse Data to Accurately Predict Customer Lifetime Value\nMingzhe Xing, Shuqing Bian, Wayne Xin Zhao, Zhen Xiao, Xinji Luo, Cunxiang Yin, Jing Cai, Yancheng He\nKDD (Applied Data Science Track)\nDebiasing Learning based Cross-domain Recommendation\nSiqing Li, Liuyi Yao, Shanlei Mu, Wayne Xin Zhao, Yaliang Li, Tonglei Guo, Bolin Ding and Ji-Rong Wen\nKDD (Applied Data Science Track)\nInterpretable Aspect-aware Capsule Network for Peer Review based Citation Count Prediction\nSiqing Li, Yaliang Li, Wayne Xin Zhao, Bolin Ding and Ji-Rong Wen\nTOIS\nCRSLab: An Open-Source Toolkit for Building Conversational Recommender System\nKun Zhou, Xiaolei Wang, Yuanhang Zhou, Chenzhan Shang, Yuan Cheng, Wayne Xin Zhao, Yaliang Li, Ji-Rong Wen\nACL (Demo)\nTextBox: A Unified, Modularized, and Extensible Framework for Text Generation\nJunyi Li, Tianyi Tang, Gaole He, Jinhao Jiang, Xiaoxuan Hu, Puzhao Xie, Zhipeng Chen, Zhuohao Yu, Wayne Xin Zhao, Ji-Rong Wen\nACL (Demo)\nGenerating Long and Coherent Text with Multi-Level Generative Adversarial Networks\nTianyi Tang, Junyi Li, Wayne Xin Zhao, Ji-Rong Wen\nAPWeb-WAIM\n2020\nMining Implicit Entity Preference from User-Item Interaction Data for Knowledge Graph Completion via Adversarial Learning\nGaole He, Junyi Li, Wayne Xin Zhao, Peiju Liu, Ji-Rong Wen\nWWW\nImproving Multi-Turn Response Selection Models with Complementary Last-Utterance Selection by Instance Weighting\nKun Zhou, Wayne Xin Zhao, Yutao Zhu, Ji-Rong Wen, Jingsong Yu\nPAKDD\nKERL: A Knowledge-Guided Reinforcement Learning Model for Sequential Recommendation\nPengfei Wang, Yu Fan, Long Xia, Wayne Xin Zhao, Shaozhang Niu, Jimmy Huang\nSIGIR\nSequential Recommendation with Self-Attentive Multi-Adversarial Network\nRuiyang Ren, Zhaoyang Liu, Yaliang Li, Wayne Xin Zhao, Hui Wang, Bolin Ding, Ji-Rong Wen\nSIGIR\nImproving Conversational Recommender Systems via Knowledge Graph based Semantic Fusion\nKun Zhou, Wayne Xin Zhao, Shuqing Bian, Yuanhang Zhou, Ji-Rong Wen, Jingsong Yu\nKDD\nLearning Effective Road Network Representation with Hierarchical Graph Neural Networks\nNing Wu, Wayne Xin Zhao, Jingyuan Wang, Dayan Pan\nKDD\nLeveraging Historical Interaction Data for Improving Conversational Recommender System\nKun Zhou, Xin Zhao, Hui Wang, Sirui Wang, Fuzheng Zhang, Zhongyuan Wang and Ji-Rong Wen\nCIKM (Short paper)\nRevisiting Alternative Experimental Settings for Evaluating