  "serper::Xiaoyan Sun": {
    "homepage": "https://med.miami.edu/faculty/xiaoyan-sun-mdphd",
    "emails": [
      "lcme@aamc.org",
      "wei@miami.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xiaoyan Sun MDPhD  Miller School of Medicine\nSkip to Main Content\nMenu\nSeeking Patient Care?\nCareers\nFaculty\nAlumni\nGiving\nHome\nFaculty Directory\nXiaoyan Sun MDPhD\nXiaoyan Sun, M.D.,Ph.D.\nDepartment:\nNeurology\nDivision:\nCognitive Neurology\nSeeking Patient Care?\nClinical Profile\nRoles\nAssociate Professor of Clinical Neurology\nEducation Director, Mcknight Brain Institute\nClinical Director,  Brain Endowment Bank,\nBiography\n+\n–\nDr. Sun is a board-certified neurologist with fellowship training in cognitive neurology. She started her medical career as a neurologist in China, where she earned her M.D. and obtained a Ph.D. in neuroscience in Japan. Dr. Sun finished her Neurology residency at the Medical University of South Carolina in the United States and completed a cognitive/behavioral neurology fellowship in the VA Boston Healthcare System.\nDr. Sun is a fully trained physician-scientist. Currently, she sees patients with cognitive problems at Memory Disorder Clinic of University of Miami. Dr. Sun’s research activities have focused on Alzheimer’s disease and related disorders. She is actively involved with medical students, neurology residents, psychiatry residents and cognitive fellows education at the medical school. Dr. Sun serves as a Clinical Director at Brain Endowment Bank. Dr. Sun is in charge of making final clinical diagnosis of donor brains.\nEducation & Training\n+\n–\nEducation\n1984: Xi'an jiaotong University\nMD\nPost Graduate Training\n2014: Veterans Administration Medical Center\nFellowship, Behavioral Neeurology\n2012: Medical University of South Carolina (MUSC)\nResidency, Neurology\n2009: Medical University of South Carolina (MUSC)\nInternship, Neurology\nTeaching Interests\n+\n–\nShe is actively involved with medical students, neurology residents, psychiatry residents and cognitive fellows education at the medical school. She is Education Director for the McKnight Brain Institute.\nResearch Interests\n+\n–\nDr. Sun’s research activities have focused on Alzheimer’s disease and related disorders.\nPublications\n+\n–\nDisclaimer:\nThe information presented in this section has been consolidated using AI and machine learning technologies. While every effort has been made to ensure accuracy, errors may occur. If you identify any inaccuracies, please use\nthis link\nto inform our data team. Your feedback is greatly appreciated and helps us improve the quality of our content."
  },
