    "homepage_text": "Wei Lin's Homepage\nWei Lin\nelonlin24@gmail.com\ngithub.com/Elin24\ngoogle scholar\nEducation\nPh.D. in Computer Science and Techonology\nCity University of Hong Kong\n2021 - now\nMA.Sc in Computer Science and Techonology\nNorthwestern Polytechnical University\n2018 - 2021\nB.S. in Information Security\nNorthwestern Polytechnical University\n2014 - 2018\nCareer Profile\nI am a CV researcher based in  Hong Kong SAR, China, pursuing the Ph.D. from\nVideo, Image, and Sound Analysis Lab (VISAL)\n,\nDepartment of Computer Science\n,\nCity University of Hong Kong\n, \n\t\t\t\t\t\tadvised by\nAntoni B. Chan\n. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tMy Ph.D. research topics encompass crowd analysis, class-agnostic counting, and optimal transport. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tMy research interests lie in the fields of computer vision, deep learning, and machine learning. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tI am also interested in AI for Science and am looking forward to potential cooperation.\nI received Ma.Sc in\nNorthwestern Polytechnical University\nin 2021,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tstudying in the\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence, OPtics and ElectroNics (iOPEN)\n,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tadvised by\nQi Wang\nand\nXuelong Li\n,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tcollaborating with\nJunyu Gao\n.\nPublications\nW. Lin\n, Y. Zhou, J. Zhang, R. Shao, Z. Zhao, J. Gao, A.B. Chan, and X. Li\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"PUO-Bench: A Panel Understanding and Operation Benchmark with A Privacy-Preserving Framework,\"\nProc. NeurIPS\n, 2025.\n[Paper]\n[Benchmark]\nW. Lin\n, C. Zhao, and A.B. Chan\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Point-to-Region Loss for Semi-Supervised Point-Based Crowd Counting,\"\nProc. CVPR\n, 2025.\n[Code]\nW. Lin\n, J. Wan, and A.B. Chan\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Proximal Mapping Loss: Understanding Loss Functions in Crowd Counting & Localization,\"\nProc. ICLR\n, 2025.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nJ. Wan, Q. Wu,\nW. Lin\n, and A.B. Chan\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Robust Zero-Shot Crowd Counting and Localization with Adaptive Resolution SAM,\"\nProc. ECCV\n, 2024.\n[Paper]\nF. Chen,\nW. Lin\n, Z. Liu, A.B. Chan\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"A Secure Image Watermarking Framework with Statistical Guarantees via Adversarial Attacks on Secret Key Networks ,\"\nProc. ECCV\n, 2024.\n[Paper]\nW. Lin\n, and A.B. Chan,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"A Fixed-Point Approach to Unified Prompt-Based Counting,\"\nProc. AAAI\n, 2024.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nW. Lin\n, and A.B. Chan,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Optimal Transport Minimization: Crowd Localization on Density Maps for Semi-Supervised Counting,\"\nProc. CVPR\n2023. (highlight)\n[Code]\nW. Lin\n, K. Yang, X. Ma, J. Gao, L. Liu, S. Liu, J. Hou, S. Yi, and A.B. Chan,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Scale-Prior Deformable Convolution for Exemplar-Guided Class-Agnostic Counting,\"\nProc. BMVC\n2022.\n[Project Page]\n[Code]\nQ. Zhang,\nW. Lin\n, and A.B. Chan, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Cross-View Cross-Scene Multi-View Crowd Counting,\"\nProc. CVPR\n, 2021.\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\nW. Lin\n, J. Gao, Q. Wang, and X. Li, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Learning to Detect Anomaly Events in Crowd Scenes from Synthetic Data,\"\nNeurocomputing\n, 2021.\n[Dataset Link (code: n445)]\nQ. Wang, J. Gao,\nW. Lin\n, and X. Li, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Pixel-wise Crowd Understanding via Synthetic Data,\"\nIJCV\n, 2021.\nQ. Wang,\nW. Lin\n, J. Gao, and X. Li, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Density-Aware Curriculum Learning for Crowd Counting,\"\nT-CYB\n, 2020.\n[Paper]\n[Benchmark]\nQ. Wang, J. Gao,\nW. Lin\n, and X. Li, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"NWPU-Crowd: A Large-Scale Benchmark for Crowd Counting,\"\nT-PAMI\n, 2020.\n[Paper]\n[Benchmark]\nW. Lin\n, J. Gao, Q. Wang, and X. Li, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Pixel-Level Self-Paced Learning for Super-Resolution,\"\nProc. ICASSP\n, 2020.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nJ. Gao,\nW. Lin\n, B. Zhao, D. Wang, C. Gao, and J. Wen, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"C^3 Framework: An Open-source PyTorch Code for Crowd Counting,\"\narXiv\n, 2019.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nQ. Wang, J. Gao,\nW. Lin\n, and Y. Yuan, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Learning from Synthetic Data for Crowd Counting in the Wild,\"\nProc. CVPR,\n2019.\n[Project Page]\n[Paper]\n[Code-SFCN\n/\nGCC-CL]\nOthers\nAwards\nThe ACM-ICPC Asia Regional Contest Qingdao Site 2016, Silver Medal\nThe ACM-ICPC Asia Regional Contest Beijing Site 2017, Bronze Medal\nRegular Reviewer\nCVPR (22-23), ICLR (23)\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\nIEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing\nNeurocomputing\nSkills &\n\t\t\t\t\tProficiency\nPython\nHTML/CSS/JS\nC/C++\nJulia"
