    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Wen's Research Group – Explore the Nano World\nWen's Research Group\nExplore the Nano World\nHome\nWelcome to Wen’s Research Group\nWen Zhang is leading the Sustainable Environmental Nanotechnology and Nanointerfaces Laboratory at NJIT. My research at NJIT embraces (1) hybrid atomic force microscope (AFM) for nanoscale characterization of nanomaterials or reactions, such as in situ chemical and electrochemical mapping; (2) Colloidal behavior and interfacial processes for engineered nanomaterials, plastic particulates and nanobubbles in water; (3) Reactive membrane filtration systems enabled by photocatalytic, electrochemical and electromagnetic catalysis for water/wastewater treatment and membrane distillation (MD). My research areas or application areas span from agricultural applications to energy systems such as lithium-ion battery. More details are available at my website: www.wenresearch.com.\n​​My research goals address the climate change challenges in environmental pollution abatement, improved resilience and agricultural systems. For instance, my research incorporates green chemical processes via electrified treatment technologies, nutrient recovery from wastewater, desalination from hyper brines, lithium ion battery repurposing and recovery, microalgae removal, bioaerosol treatment and viral removal, methane emission mitigation and agricultural irrigation using novel nanobubble and hydrogel technologies.\nLatest News\n2026 Annual AWWA Conference – New Jersey Section\nMarch 19, 2026\nFrom Treatment to Recovery: Transforming Desalination Brines into Valuable Chemicals\nJanuary 30, 2026\nCEE Annual Holiday Gathering 2025: Celebrating Community and Togetherness\nDecember 12, 2025\nContact Information\nWen Zhang, Ph.D., P.E., BCEE\nPrincipal Investigator\nProfessor\nPhone:\n(973) 596-5520\nFax:\n(973) 596-5790\nEmail:\nwen.zhang@njit.edu\nOffice Location:\nColton Hall 211\nFaculty Profile\n:\nhttps://people.njit.edu/profile/wzhang81\nJoin Us\nFind us on the map"
  },
