    "homepage_text": "Huanhuan Yang\nHuanhuan Yang\nI am an associate professor at Central China Normal University.\nBefore my current position, I was an associate professor at Shantou University from Aug 2017 to July 2023.\nEarlier, I was a postdoctoral researcher at Florida State University, working with Max Gunzburger on applied Mathematics.\nParticular areas\n: PDE constrained optimization, parallel computing, ocean modeling.\nI obtained my PhD degree in the Department of Mathematics at Emory University, supervised by Alessandro Veneziani on computational Mathematics.\nParticular areas\n: computational electrocardiology, inverse problems, reduced order modeling.\nMore information about my research interests can be found on the\nResearch\ntab.\nAddress:\nNO.152 Luoyu Road,\nWuhan,Hubei,P.R.China 430079\nE-mail:\nhuan2yang@ccnu.edu.cn\nLast update: Dec. 2024"
  },
