    "homepage_text": "Suyuan Liu - Homepage\nSuyuan Liu\nPRMI Lab\nPh.D student at National University of Defense and Technology.\nChang Sha, China\nEmail\nResearchGate\nDBLP\nGithub\nI am currently pursuing the Ph.D. degree with the College of Computer Science and Technology, National University of Defense Technology, under the supervisor of Prof.\nXinwang Liu\n. I received my bachelor degree and master degree at NUDT in 2020 and 2022. My current research interests include machine learning and data mining, especially in multi-view learning, clustering, and graph learning. Any questions are welcome to contact me by suyuanliu@nudt.edu.cn.\nNews\n2025.11:\nOne paper have been accepted by IEEE TIP.\n2025.11:\nThree paper have been accepted by AAAI 2026.\n2025.09:\nThree paper have been accepted by NeurIPS 2025.\n2025.05:\nOne paper have been accepted by ICCV 2025.\n2025.05:\nFour papers have been accepted by ICML 2025.\n2025.02:\nTwo papers have been accepted by CVPR 2025.\n2025.02:\nOne paper has been accepted by ICDE Poster Track.\n2025.01:\nOne paper has been accepted by ICLR 2025.\n2024.12:\nOne paper has been accepted by AAAI 2025.\n2024.09:\nThree papers have been accepted by NeurIPS 2024.\n2024.07:\nOne paper has been accepted by IEEE TIP.\n2024.07:\nThree papers has been accepted by ACM MM 2024.\n2024.04:\nOne paper has been accepted by CVPR 2024.\n2024.01:\nOne paper has been accepted by IEEE TKDE.\n2023.12:\nOne paper has been accepted by AAAI 2024.\n2023.11:\nOne paper has been accepted by IEEE TNNLS.\n2023.07:\nThree papers have been accepted by ACM MM 2023.\n2022.11:\nOne paper has been accepted by IEEE TNNLS.\n2022.09:\nOne paper has been accepted by NeurIPS 2022.\n2021.12:\nOne paper has been accepted by AAAI 2022.\nSelected Publications\nJournals\nSuyuan Liu\n, Qing Liao, Siwei Wang, Xinwang Liu, and En Zhu. Robust and Consistent Anchor Graph Learning for Multi-view Clustering.\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (\nTKDE\n)\n. (CCF Rank A, JCR Q1) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nSuyuan Liu\n, Xinwang Liu, Siwei Wang, Xin Niu, and En Zhu. Fast Incomplete Multi-View Clustering With View-Independent Anchors.\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (\nTNNLS\n)\n. (CCF Rank B, JCR Q1) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\n刘溯源\n, 王思为, 唐厂, 周思航, 王思齐, 刘新旺. 基于加权锚点的多视图聚类算法.\n自动化学报\n. (CCF Rank A) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nShengju Yu,\nSuyuan Liu\n, Siwei Wang, Chang Tang, Zhigang Luo, and Xinwang Liu. Sparse Low-rank Multi-view Subspace Clustering with Consensus Anchors and Unified Bipartite Graph.\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (\nTNNLS\n)\n. (CCF Rank B, JCR Q1) [\nPaper\n]\nSiwei Wang, Xinwang Liu,\nSuyuan Liu\n, Wenxuan Tu, and En Zhu. Scalable and Structural Multi-view Graph Clustering with Adaptive Anchor Fusion.\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (\nTIP\n)\n. (CCF Rank A, JCR Q1) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nConferences\nSuyuan Liu\n,Hao Yu, Hao Tan, Ke Liang, Siwei Wang, Shengju Yu, En Zhu, Xinwang Liu. Efficient Federated Incomplete Multi-View Clustering.\nThe Forty-second International Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n)\n, 2025. (CCF Rank A) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nSuyuan Liu\n, Siwei Wang, Ke Liang, Junpu Zhang, Zhibin Dong, Tianrui Liu, En Zhu, Xinwang Liu, and Kunlun He. Alleviate Anchor-Shift: Explore Blind Spots with Cross-View Reconstruction for Incomplete Multi-View Clustering.\nProceedings of the Thirty-eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing System (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2024. (CCF Rank A) [\nPaper\n]\nSuyuan Liu\n, Ke Liang, Zhibin Dong, Siwei Wang, Xihong Yang, Sihang Zhou, En Zhu, Xinwang Liu. Learn from View Correlation: An Anchor Enhancement Strategy for Multi-view Clustering.\nProceedings of the Thirty-Sixth IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n)\n, 2024,  pages: 26151-26161. (CCF Rank A)  [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nSuyuan Liu\n, Junpu Zhang, Yi Wen, Xihong Yang, Siwei Wang, Yi Zhang, En Zhu, Chang Tang, Long Zhao, and Xinwang Liu. Sample-level Cross-view Similarity Learning for Incomplete Multi-view Clustering.\nProceedings of the Thirty-Eighth AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n)\n, 2024, pages: 14017-14025. (CCF Rank A) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nSuyuan Liu*\n, Siwei Wang*, Pei Zhang, Kai Xu, Xinwang Liu, Changwang Zhang, and Feng Gao. Efficient One-pass Multi-view Subspace Clustering with Consensus Anchors.\nProceedings of the Thirty-Sixth AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n)\n, 2022, pages: 7576-7584.\n(CCF Rank A)\n[\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nDayu Hu*,\nSuyuan Liu*\n, Jun Wang, Junpu Zhang, Siwei Wang, Xingchen Hu, Xinzhong Zhu, Chang Tang, and Xinwang Liu. Reliable Attribute-missing Multi-view Clustering with Instance-level and Feature-level Cooperative Imputation.\nProceedings of the 32st ACM International Conference on Multimedia (\nACM MM\n)\n, 2024. (CCF Rank A) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nYi Wen*,\nSuyuan Liu*\n, Xinhang Wan, Siwei Wang, Ke Liang, Xinwang Liu, Xihong Yang, and Pei Zhang. Efficient Multi-View Graph Clustering with Local and Global Structure Preservation.\nProceedings of the 31st ACM International Conference on Multimedia (\nACM MM\n)\n, 2023, pages: 3021-3030. (CCF Rank A) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nSiwei Wang, Xinwang Liu,\nSuyuan Liu\n, Jiaqi Jin, Wenxuan Tu, Xinzhong Zhu, and En Zhu. Align then Fusion: Generalized Large-Scale Multi-View Clustering with Anchor Matching Correspondences.\nProceedings of the Thirty-Sixth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing System (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2022, pages: 5882-5895. (CCF Rank A) [\nPaper\n], [\nCode\n]\nEducations\n[Jan 2023 - Now] Doctor, National University of Defense Technology, Changsha, China\n[Sep 2020 - Dec 2022] Master, National University of Defense Technology, Changsha, China\n[Sep 2016 - Jul 2020] Bachelor, National University of Defense Technology, Changsha, China\nService\nReviewer for ICLR 2025, ICML 2025, NeurIPS 2024-2025, AAAI 2023-2025, IJCAI 2025, AISTATS 2025\nReviewer for CVPR 2024-2025, ICCV 2025, ACM MM 2023-2025, SIGKDD 2024-2025, WSDM 2025\nReviewer for IEEE TKDE, IEEE TIP, IEEE TNNLS, IEEE TCVST, PR, EAAI, Neurocomputing"
