  "serper::Yansong Zhao": {
    "homepage": "https://www.hvl.no/person/?user=Yansong.Zhao",
    "emails": [
      "yansong.zhao@hvl.no"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yansong Zhao - Høgskulen på Vestlandet\nHopp til innhald\nÅpne søk\nLukk søk\nÅpne meny\nLukk meny\nEnglish\nSøk i nettstedet\nSøk\nProfessor\nYansong Zhao\nInstitutt for sikkerheit, kjemi- og bioingeniørfag\nTel:\n+47\n55 58 77 70\nEpost:\nSend epost\nBergen\nKRONSTAD D333\nLast ned kontaktkort\nSjå forskarprofil i NVA\nArbeids- og kompetanseområde\nDr. Yansong Zhao is a full professor in chemical engineering and an elected member of Norwegian Academy of Technological Sciences (NTVA). His research interests are ionic liquids, battery technology, renewable energy, biotechnology, new medicine design, CO\n2\ncapture, polymer and catalysis science. He is Group Leader of\nIonic Liquids and Advanced Technology\nResearch\nGroup\nat Western Norway University of Applied Sciences. He has >120 publications. The peer-reviewed journal articles have been published in Ind. Eng. Chem. Res., Energy & Fuels, Fuels, AIChE J., Int. J. Greenhouse Gas Control, RSC Advances, Greenhouse Gases: Science and Technology, J. Chem. Eng. Data, Fluid Phase Equilib., J. Therm. Anal. Calorim., Chem. Eng. Technol., Journal of Molecular Liquids, Micro & Nano Letters, Current Organic Chemistry, Science China Chemistry, J. Dispersion Science and Technology, Computers and Applied Chemistry. These journal articles have been cited for >1900 times according to Google Scholar; h index is 25.\nPlease feel free to contact me (yansong.zhao@hvl.no) if you are interested to work or study at my research group. We have opportunities for bachelor and master lelvel projects. In addiiton, we have possibilities for PhD and postdoctoral research fellow projects.\nOn going PhD projects at Yansong's research group\n:\nPhD project 1: PhD project in battery technology\nPhD project 2: PhD project in geothermal energy storage\nLink of homepage of research group\n(Ionic Liquids and Advanced Technology Reserch Group) is as follows: https://www.hvl.no/en/research/group/ionic-liquid-and-advanced-technology/\nThe list of selected publications is as follows:\nPersonal webpage 1: https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Yansong_Zhao/reputation\nPersonal webpage 2: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=sLwZKTQAAAAJ&hl=en\nPersonal webpage 3: https://wo.cristin.no/as/WebObjects/cristin.woa/wa/fres?sort=ar&pnr=417178&la=no&action=sok\nIn addition, he is Editorial Board Member of\nLiquids\nJournal.\nMoreover, he is a reviewer for project submitted to U. S. Department of Energy. He is also a reviewer for the journals of Ind. Eng. Chem. Res., Energy & Fuels, Fuels, Langmuir, Electrochimica Acta, Advanced Functional Materials, Separation Science and Technology, Mini-review in organic chemistry, Letters in Organic Chemistry, Open Physics, Journal of Chemical Engineering&Data, Journal of Petroleum Science and Engineering, Brazilian Journal of Chemical Engineering and etc. In average, Yansong reviews ca. 30 peer-review articles every year.\nYansong Zhao's teaching work is relevant to chemical engineering. He is the teacher for the courses of: \" Unit operation of Chemical engineering: Heat transfer (KJE203)\", \"Energy Storage (KJE204)\", \"Battery Technology (KJE205)\", and \" Electrochemistry for Batteries, Electrolyzers and Fuel Cell Systems (MAS534)\".\nWork/Education Experiences\n26.01.2024-Present: Full professor in Chemical Engineering (permanent position) at Department of Safety, Chemistry and Biomedical Laboratory Sciences, Western Norway University of Applied Sciences, Bergen, Norway\n05.2019-Present: Leader of Ionic liquids and Advanced Technology Research Group, Faculty of Engineering and Science, Western Norway University of Applied Sciences, Bergen, Norway\n21.09.2017-25.01.2024: Associate professor in Chemical Engineering (permanent position) at Department of Safety, Chemistry and Biomedical Laboratory Sciences, Western Norway University of Applied Sciences, Bergen, Norway\n14.08.2014-20.09.2017: Post doctor research fellow (Full time) at Department of Physics and Technology, UiT The Arctic University of Norway, Tromsø, Norway\nFeb.2017-Aug.2017: Visiting scientist at Helmholtz Institute Ulm, Germany\n14.12.2013-13.08.2014 Researcher at Department of Chemical Engineering, NTNU, Trondheim, Norway\n07.07.2011-13.12.2013 PhD Candidate at Department of Chemical Engineering, NTNU, Trondheim, Norway (He received his PhD degree in Chemical Engineering in December 2013)\nAug. 2008-Jun. 2011 Master student at University of Chinese Academy of Sciences and Institute of Process Engineering, Chinese Academy of Sciences and received his master degree in Chemical Engineering\nOct. 2007-Aug. 2008 Graduation Project for Bachelor Degree at Group of Ionic Liquids Clean Process and Energy-saving, Institute of Process Engineering, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, P. R. China\nSep. 2004-Jun. 2008 Bachelor student at College of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering, Henan University and received his bachelor degree in Chemical Engineering and Technology\nUnderviser i\nVarmetransport og varmeoverføring (KJE203)\nEnergilagring (KJE204)\nBatteriteknologi (KJE205)\nElektrokjemi for batteri, elektrolyzer og brenselceller (MAS534)\nForskar på\nIonic liquids\nBattery technology\nRenewable energy\nBiotechnology\nLife science\nSolar cells\nSupercapacitors\nNanotechnology\nCO2 capture\nOil & gas\nCatalysis science\nNew medicine design\nForskargrupper\nHVL Battery Laboratory\nGroup of Ionic Liquids and Advanced Technology\nUnderviser i\nKJE203\n, Varmetransport og varmeoverføring, Høst 2025\nKJE204\n, Energilagring, Høst 2025\nKJE205\n, Batteriteknologi, Vår 2026\nMAS534\n, Electrochemistry for Batteries, Electrolyzers and Fuel Cell Systems, Vår 2026\nForskargrupper\nForskningsgrupper\nIoniske væsker og avansert teknologi\nPublikasjonar\nOxidative dissolution of metals in metal-based ionic liquids: iron, copper, silver and aluminum\nYuchao Li, Yanxia Zheng, Huishuang Zhao, Qingshan Zhu, Yansong Zhao (2025)\nJournal of Ionic Liquids 2025\nAdsorption of Asphaltenes at Model Oil/Brine Interface: Influence of Solvent Polarity\nWei Wang, Fajun Sheng, Guifang Ou, Yansong Zhao, Guangyu Sun (2024)\nACS Omega 2024 ;Volum 9. s. 19879-19891\nThe exploration of relationship between the evolution of Cu to Cu<inf>2</inf>O/CuO and photocatalytic efficiency toward water oxidation reaction\nTingxiang Chen, Liugen Zhang, Jiang Li, Changyan Guo, Shanshan Qiao, Yansong Zhao (2024)\nInternational Journal of Hydrogen Energy 2024 ;Volum 67. s. 644-650\nHighly efficient supported bimetallic Au-Pd catalysts for oxidative esterification of methacrolein to methyl methacrylate\nYubo Yang, Yanxia Zheng, Lu Cai, Yuchao Li, Rui Xu, Cuncun Zuo (2024)\nCanadian Journal of Chemical Engineering 2024 ;Volum 102. s. 2468-2480\nDesigan and functional regulaiton of ionic liquid for energy technology and health scicence application\nYansong Zhao (2024)\nVis alle\nLaster...\nHei! 👋 Har du spørsmål om studier eller studentliv? Våre studenter er tilgjengelige på chat akkurat nå. Klikk her for å starte en samtale!\nChat"
