    "homepage_text": "Director - VISION & LEARNING LAB\nVISION & LEARNING LAB\nHome\nAbout\nMembers\nDirector\nStudents\nAssistants\nPublications\nConference\nJournal\nCourses\nDLCV\nMaintenance\nOthers\n​Laboratory Director\n​​Prof. Yu-Chiang Frank Wang\n王鈺強\n教授\n​Research Interests: Computer Vision, Machine Learning, Pattern Recognition, Image Processing\nContact: ycwang AT ntu.edu.tw\nY\nu-Chiang Frank Wang\nreceived his B.S. degree in Electrical Engineering from National Taiwan University in 2001. He received his M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Electrical and Computer Engineering from Carnegie Mellon University in 2004 and 2009, respectively. In 2009, Dr. Wang joined the Research Center for Information Technology Innovation (CITI) of Academia Sinica, leading the Multimedia and Machine Learning Lab. Dr. Wang joined the Department of Electrical Engineering at National Taiwan University as an Associate Professor in 2017, and was promoted to Professor in 2019. Since 2022, Dr. Wang joins NVIDIA, where he serves as the Research Director in Deep Learning & Computer Vision and leads\nNVIDIA Research Taiwan\n. With continuing research focuses on computer vision and machine learning, Dr. Wang's recent research topics include deep learning for vision & language, transfer learning, and 3D vision. Dr. Wang serves as organizing committee members and area chairs of multiple international conferences such as CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, and ACCV. Several of his papers are nominated for the best paper awards, including IEEE ICIP, ICME, AVSS and MVA. Dr. Wang is twice selected as the Outstanding Young Researcher by the Ministry of Science and Technology of Taiwan (2013-2015 and 2017-2019), as well as the Technological Research Innovation Award from the College of EECS at NTU. In 2022, Dr. Wang receives the Y. Z. Hsu Scientific Paper Award in Artificial Intelligence from the Far Eastern Y. Z. Hsu Science & Technology Memorial Foundation. In 2023, Dr. Wang is recognized as the Outstanding Young Scholar by the Foundation for the Advancement of Outstanding Scholarship.\nWork Experiences\nResearch Director, Deep Learning & Computer Vision  AI研究總監\n2022 - present\nNVIDIA, Taiwan\nProfessor  教授\n2019 - present\nDept. Electrical Engineering & Graduate Inst. Communication Engineering, National Taiwan University 國立台灣大學電機工程學系暨電信工程學研究所\nPrincipal AI Consultant 首席AI顧問\n2021- 2022\nInventec Corporation 英業達 AI研發中心\nAI Advisory Consultant  AI諮詢顧問\n2019 - 2022\nASUS Intelligent Cloud Services, ASUSTek Computer Inc. 華碩AI研發中心\nDirector  中心主任\n2019 - 2022\nComputing Center, Dept. Electrical Engineering, National Taiwan University 國立台灣大學電機工程學系計算中心\nSection Director for Technology Promotion & Public Relation  技術推廣暨對外關係組組長\n2018 - present\nMOST Joint Research Center for AI Technology & All Vista Healthcare 科技部台灣大學人工智慧研究中心\nAI Program Review Committee AI計畫審查委員\n2019 - present\nIndustrial Development Bureau, Ministry of Economic Affairs 經濟部工業局\nProject Consultant  專案顧問\n2019 - 2021\nInstitute for Information Industry 財團法人資訊工業策進會\nAssociate Professor  副教授\n2017 - 2019\nDept. Electrical Engineering & Graduate Inst. Communication Engineering, National Taiwan University 國立台灣大學電機工程學系暨電信工程學研究所\nResearch Consultant  研究顧問\n2017\nViscovery 創意引晴\nDeputy Director  中心副主任\n2015 - 2017\nResearch Center for IT Innovation, Academia Sinica 中央研究院資訊科技創新研究中心\nAssistant/Associate Research Fellow  助/副研究員\n2009 - 2017\nResearch Center for IT Innovation, Academia Sinica 中央研究院資訊科技創新研究中心\nIndustrial Partners\n(alphabetical order)\nAICS, Bitmark, Chunghwa Telecom, Deep01, Digital Drift, E.SUN Commercial Bank,\nGoogle, ITRI, Inventec, KaiKuTek, Moxa, Novatek, Qualcomm, Taiwan AI Labs,\nTheia, Tron Future Tech, TSMC, Umbo Computer Vision, Viscovery​\n​\n學新館 514 室 (MK 514) @ NTU\nContact Us\nTel: 02-33663241\n​Admin. Assistant:\nFang-Ru Shih\n(frs106 AT ntu.edu.tw)\nWeb Admin. :\nKai-Chen Yang\n(d14942011 AT ntu.edu.tw)\nWeb Photo Credit:\nYuan-Fang Lin\n(\nb02901003 AT ntu.edu.tw\n)\n​\nHome\nAbout\nMembers\nDirector\nStudents\nAssistants\nPublications\nConference\nJournal\nCourses\nDLCV\nMaintenance\nOthers"
