    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/LavinWong",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Wenbin Zhang | Florida International University\n<\nWenbin Zhang\nAssistant Professor\nKnight Foundation School of Computing and Information Sciences\nFlorida International University\n11200 SW\n                                8th Street, INV 449\nMiami, Florida, USA 33199\n+1\n                                305-348-4249\n11200 SW\n                                8th Street,\nINV 449\nMiami, Florida, USA 33199\n+1\n                                305-348-4249\n11200 SW\n                                    8th Street, INV 449\nMiami, Florida, USA 33199\n+1\n                                    305-348-4249\n11200\n                                    SW 8th Street, INV 449\nMiami, Florida, USA 33199\n+1\n                                    305-348-4249\nHello, my name is Wenbin Zhang (pronounced:\n                    Wuhn-bin Jahng).\n                    I am a\nHakka\nborn\n                    Assistant Professor at\nFlorida International University\n,\n                    and an Associate Member at the\nTe Ipu o te Mahara\n                        Artificial Intelligence Institute\n. The main focus of my research is on designing machine\n                    learning algorithms that not only provide theoretical performance guarantees but also behave in ways\n                    aligned with human values and societal goals.\n                    I am particularly interested in combining the aspect of gaining machine learning knowledge with an\n                    orientation towards making machine learning usable\n                    and useful for high-stakes decision-making, such as healthcare, digital forensics, finance, climate,\n                    policy, and law.\n                    To this end, I have been exploring complex real-world data (e.g., EHR, MODIS, supply chain data),\n                    under multifarious contexts (e.g., censorship, imbalance, distribution shift),\n                    subject to different metrics (e.g., fairness, regime centroids, c-index),\n                    through joyful collaboration and team work with computational scientists and domain experts.\n                    Supporting and recognizing my work, I was invited to deliver a New Faculty Highlights talk at\n                    AAAI’24, received the NSF CRII Award, was named to the Stanford/Elsevier Top 2% Scientists List, and\n                    earned distinctions including the Leibniz Fellowship, Distinguished Area Chair Award at ECML\n                    PKDD'25, Outstanding Senior Program Committee Member Award at ECAI'25, and Distinguished Senior\n                    Program Committee Award for IJCAI'23, along with best paper awards/candidates at ECML PKDD’25,\n                    FAccT’23, ICDM’23, DAMI, and ICDM’21.\n                    Incidentally,\n                    my\nErdős\nnumber is 3\n                    (Me -> Alan Evans -> David Avis -> Erdős) as a result of the enjoyed interdisciplinary\n                    collaboration. In line with this collaborative spirit, I also contribute to the research community\n                    by serving on conference organizing committees and journal editorial boards across computer science\n                    and interdisciplinary venues—including roles such as Sponsorship Chair for AAAI'26, Travel Award\n                    Chair for AIES'25, Associate Editor for ACM Computing Surveys, and Action Editor for Data Mining and\n                    Knowledge Discovery.\nI southwarded all the way to Miami from the Upper Peninsula where I held the same role at\nMichigan\n                        Technological University\n. Prior to that,\n                    I was a Postdoctoral Researcher at\nCarnegie Mellon\n                        University\nafter receiving a Ph.D. degree from the\nUniversity of\n                        Maryland, Baltimore County\n.\n                    I also spent time at multiple global research centers and institutions, including\nL3S\n                        Research Center\n,\nUniversity\n                        of Milano-Bicocca\n,\nKing\n                        Abdullah University of Science and Technology\n,\nTélécom Paris\n,\nGeorge\n                        Mason University\nand\nNational\n                        Institutes of Health\n.\n                    I had four Stendhal syndrome years in\nBeijing\nand\nTianjin\nbefore starting my study abroad\n                    in\nNewfoundland\n, where it snowed in June (not anymore\n                    due to global warming).\nAside from my obvious interest in research, I enjoy watching and playing all kinds of sports\n                    especially\n                    soccer. I had the experience of my life at\nKaliningrad Stadium\ncheering the 2018 World Cup. I ran my very first Marathon at\nVirginia\n                        Beach\ncredit to\nNovember Project\n.\n                    Finally, I believe Manchester is red as I thought David Beckham was cool when I was young. Him\n                    growing\n                    up, me supporting United till date.\nLast but not least, I appreciate you taking the time to surf the internet this far to check up on\n                    and to\n                    read a bit of my story.\n                    Presuming I am not that boring, I encourage you to say hello before you leave for our interesting\n                    conversations to come.\nNews Highlights\nCurrent\nIf you’re interested in reviewing for leading\n                                                        AI/ML and interdisciplinary conferences and journals (e.g.,\n                                                        healthcare), I’m always seeking reviewers year-round — please\nreach\n                                                                out.\n• If you’re interested in\n                                                        reviewing for leading AI/ML and interdisciplinary conferences\n                                                        and journals (e.g., healthcare), I’m always seeking reviewers\n                                                        year-round — please\nreach\n                                                                out.\nFeb 2026\nI serve as Associate Program Co-Chair for\n                                                        ICPADS 2026 and look forward to your\nsubmission.\n• I serve as Associate Program\n                                                        Co-Chair for ICPADS 2026 and look forward to your\nsubmission.\nNov 2025\nHumbled to receive the Distinguished Area\n                                                        Chair Award at ECML PKDD 2025.\n• Humbled to receive the\n                                                        Distinguished Area Chair Award at ECML PKDD 2025.\nOct 2025\nHumbled to receive the\nOutstanding\n                                                                Senior Program Committee Member\nAward at ECAI\n                                                        2025.\n• Humbled to receive the\nOutstanding\n                                                                Senior Program Committee Member\nAward at ECAI\n                                                        2025.\nSep 2025\nNamed to the Stanford/Elsevier Top 2%\n                                                        Scientists List.\n• Named to the\n                                                        Stanford/Elsevier Top 2% Scientists List.\nHonored to be appointed to a four-year term\n                                                        on the ECML PKDD\nSteering\n                                                                Committee.\n• Honored to be appointed to a\n                                                        four-year term on the ECML PKDD\nSteering\n                                                                Committee.\nAug 2025\nI am an action editor for\nMachine\n                                                                Learning\nand am awaiting your submissions.\n• I am an action editor for\nMachine\n                                                                Learning\nand am awaiting your submissions.\nPanelist at the Responsible AI Day at KDD\n                                                        2025, discussing the intersection of AI, ethics, and society.\n• Panelist at the Responsible\n                                                        AI Day at KDD 2025, discussing the intersection of AI, ethics,\n                                                        and society.\nAppointed to the ACCESS Researcher Advisory\n                                                        Committee to provide guidance on advancing the national\n                                                        cyberinfrastructure ecosystem and researcher support.\n• Appointed to the ACCESS\n                                                        Researcher Advisory Committee to provide guidance on advancing\n                                                        the national cyberinfrastructure ecosystem and researcher\n                                                        support.\nJul 2025\nZichong and Zhipeng won the Best Student\n                                                        Paper Award at ECML PKDD 2025.\n• Zichong and Zhipeng won the\n                                                        Best Student Paper Award at ECML PKDD 2025.\nArea Chair/Senior Program Committee at IJCAI,\n                                                        AISTATS, ICDM, ECML PKDD, ECAI, AAMAS, ICPR, CHI, AAAI, and\n                                                        TheWebConf.\n• Area Chair/Senior Program\n                                                        Committee at IJCAI, AISTATS, ICDM, ECML PKDD, ECAI, AAMAS, ICPR,\n                                                        CHI, AAAI, and TheWebConf.\nMay 2025\nWe launch the competition on fairness in AI\n                                                        face detection and look forward to your\nparticipation\nin advancing\n                                                        responsible AI research.\n• We launch the competition on\n      ...[truncated]"
