  "serper::Chenyu You": {
    "homepage": "https://chenyuyou.me/",
    "emails": [
      "chenyu.you@stonybrook.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/charlesyou999648",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/chenyu-you-b07475a4/",
    "homepage_text": "Chenyu You\nChenyu You\nHome\nBio\nResearch\nGroup\nTopics\nPapers\nProspective\nStudents\nTeaching\nCourses\nService\nRecent\nChenyu You\nChenyu You\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Applied Mathematics & Statistics\nDepartment of Computer Science\nStony Brook University\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nLinkedIn\nIntroduction\nChenyu You is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Applied Mathematics & Statistics and Department of Computer Science at Stony Brook University. \nHe is also the core faculty member of the\nCVLab\n,\nAI institute\n,\nand affiliated with the\nInstitute for Advanced Computational Science\n.\nPreviously, he received his Ph.D. in 2024 from Yale University under the advisement of\nJames S. Duncan\n, \nhis M.S. in 2019 from Stanford University under the advisement of\nDaniel Rubin\n, \nand his B.S. in 2017 from Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute under the advisement of\nGe Wang\n, all in electrical engineering.\nHe has also spent wonderful time at\nFacebook AI Research (FAIR)\n, \nas well as\nGoogle Research\n.\nResearch\nMy group studies focuses on fundamental and applied problems in\ncomputer vision\nand\nmachine learning\n, with a focus on\nAI for health\n.\nWe build intelligent systems that learn from complex data, reason about and interact with the real world, and drive meaningful impact on healthcare.\nBesides learning algorithms, we ask: how AI should represent knowledge across imaging, text, and multi-omics data; what principles ensure robustness, trustworthy, and clinical reliability; and how algorithmic advances can translate into real-world healthcare domains. \nOur research aims to answer these questions by advancing machine learning methods in close collaboration with biomedical and clinical science.\nFoundation:\nHow do we build world foundation models that generalize across diverse clinical tasks?\nRepresentative projects\n:\nMedSAM\n/\nMONA\n/\nARCO\n/\nKGAE\n/\nUniHGKR\nReliability:\nHow can we build complex AI systems that clinicians can trust and rely on?\nRepresentative projects\n:\nSpuriousMemorization\n/\nCFR\n/\nCASTformer\nAccess:\nHow can we turn advances in AI into efficient, deployable tools that improve healthcare and advance scientific discovery?\nRepresentative projects\n:\nCSR\n/\nCSRv2\n/\nOTSurv\n/\nMORSE\nHere is some information for prospective students and visitors.\nNews\n[2026.03]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair NeurIPS 2026.\n[2026.03]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive Lambda Research Grant Award!\n[2026.03]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Nature Communications.\n[2026.02]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE TAI.\n[2026.02]\nPAPER\nFour paper accepted at CVPR 2026.\n[2026.02]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MIDL 2026.\n[2026.02]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive the Excellence in Teaching Award for Fall 2025.\n[2026.01]\nPAPER\nTwo papers on\nultra-sparse embeddings\nand\nsparse feature attention\naccepted at ICLR 2026.\n[2026.01]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive CPAL Rising Stars Award 2026. Many thanks for the acknowledgment!\n[2026.01]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair MICCAI 2026.\n[2026.01]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive Tinker Research Grant Award from Thinking Machines Lab!\n[2025.12]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging Distinguished Associate Editor Certificate of Excellence!\n[2025.12]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair MIDL 2026.\n[2025.11]\nEDITOR\nThrilled to serve as Associate Editor for Medical Image Analysis!\n[2025.11]\nPAPER\nOur work\nCoMA\n, a multi-agent complex human motion generation framework, is accepted at AAAI 2026. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.11]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive AAAI New Faculty Highlights 2026. Many thanks for the acknowledgment!\n[2025.11]\nEDITOR\nThrilled to serve as Associate Editor for Transactions on Machine Learning Research.\n[2025.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE TMI (Impact Factor 9.8).\n[2025.10]\nSERVICE\nThrilled to serve on the\nSUNY AI Symposium Planning Committee\n!\n[2025.09]\nPAPER\nOur work\nMartian World Model\naccepted at NeurIPS 2025. [\nNews\n]\n[2025.09]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at RSNA 2025\n(Oral)\n.\n[2025.09]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair CVPR 2026.\n[2025.08]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at EMNLP 2025.\n[2025.07]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive the Excellence in Teaching Award for Spring 2025.\n[2025.07]\nAWARD\nCongratulations to my Ph.D. student, Qin Ren, on winning the MICCAI 2025 NIH Registration Grant!\n[2025.06]\nPAPER\nOur work\nOuroboros\non cycle-consistent rendering via diffusion models is accepted at ICCV 2025. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.06]\nPAPER\nOur work\nOTSurv\n, leveraging Optimal Transport for survival analysis, is accepted at MICCAI 2025. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.06]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nUncovering Memorization Effect in the Presence of Spurious Correlations\n” has been formally accepted by Nature Communications. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.05]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ACL 2025.\n[2025.05]\nPAPER\nOur work\ncontrastive sparse representations (CSR)\naccepted at ICML 2025\n(Oral, Top ~1%)\n. [\nCode\n|\nHugging Face Blog\n]\n[2025.04]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair NeurIPS 2025.\n[2025.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at AIME 2025.\n[2025.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at EMBC 2025\n(Oral, Top Paper Award)\n.\n[2025.03]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ACM TKDD.\n[2025.03]\nPAPER\nOur work\nUniHGKR\n, a universal retrieval-augmented generation framework, is accept at NAACL 2025\n(Oral)\n. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.02]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair EMNLP 2025.\n[2025.02]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair COLM 2025.\n[2025.02]\nTALK\nInvited as panel speaker at the AAAI Bridge: AI for Medicine and Healthcare.\n[2025.02]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve on scientific committee for the 11th Workshop on Medical Computer Vision at CVPR 2025.\n[2025.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Nature Reviews Bioengineering.\n[2025.01]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair MICCAI 2025!\n[2025.01]\nEDITOR\nThrilled to serve as Guest Associate Editor for IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging!\n[2024.12]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MedIA (Impact Factor 10.9).\n[2024.12]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE TMI (Impact Factor 8.9).\n[2024.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Computerized Medical Imaging and Graphics.\n[2024.10]\nAWARD\nThrilled to be recognized as IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (TMI) Platinum Distinguished Reviewer (Highest award).\n[2024.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MedIA (Impact Factor 10.9).\n[2024.09]\nAWARD\nWorld’s Top 2% Scientists by Stanford University.\n[2024.09]\nPAPER\nOur paper\nMONA\nhas been formally accepted by\nIEEE-TPAMI\n(Impact Factor 20.8). [\nCode\n]\n[2024.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at BMVC 2024\n(Oral)\n.\n[2024.06]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nMedical image registration via neural fields\n” accepted by Medical Image Analysis (MedIA) (Impact Factor 10.9). Congrats to Shanlin, and all collaborators!\n[2024.06]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI 2024.\n[2024.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at UAI 2024.\n[2024.04]\nAWARD\nPrivileged to be elected into\nSigma Xi\n!\n[2024.03]\nSERVICE\nThrilled to serve as Area Chair MICCAI 2024!\n[2024.02]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nCalibrating Multi-modal Representations: A Pursuit of Group Robustness without Annotations\n” has been accepted at CVPR 2024.\n      [\nCode\n]\n[2024.02]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at CVPR 2024.\n[2024.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ICLR 2024.\n[2024.01]\nAWARD\nThrilled to be recognized as WACV 2024 Outstanding Reviewer.\n[2024.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Imaging Neuroscience.\n[2023.12]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE SaTML 2023.\n[2023.11]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nSegment Anything in Medical Images\n” has been formally accepted by Nature Communications.\n      [\nCode\n]\n[2023.10]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at WACV 2024.\n[2023.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE BIBM 2023.\n[2023.10]\nAWARD\nThrilled to be recognized as IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (TMI) Platinum Distinguished Reviewer.\n[2023.09]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nRethinking Semi-Supervised Medical Image Segmentation: A Variance-Reduction Perspective\n” has been accepted at NeurIPS 2023!\n      [\nCode\n]\n[2023.09]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at NeurIPS 2023!\n[2023.09]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at npj Digital Medicine (Impact Factor 15.357).\n[2023.09]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Physics in Medicine and Biology.\n[2023.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-MLCN 2023.\n[2023.06]\nPAPER\nFour papers accepted at IEEE NSS-MIC-RTSD 2023 (1 Oral).\n[2023.06]\nPAPER\nSix papers accepted at MICCAI 2023.\n[2023.05]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Investigative Radiology (Impact Factor: 10.065).\n[2023.05]\nPAPER\nThree papers\nearly accepted\nat MICCAI 2023!\n[2023.05]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at ACL 2023.\n[2023.02]\nPAPER\nOur paper\nACTION\nhas been accepted at IPMI 2023.\n      [\nCode\n]\n[2023.02]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IPMI 2023.\n[2023.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Medical Physics.\n[2022.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at WACV 2023.\n[2022.09]\nPAPER\nOur paper\nCASTformer\nhas been accepted at NeurIPS 2022!\n[2022.09]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at NeurIPS 2022!\n[2022.08]\nTALK\nGave a talk at\nMeta AI Research (FAIR)\nEastcoast Vision Group about Contrastive Learning.\n[2022.08]\nAWARD\nVery honored to be recognized as IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (TMI) Platinum Distinguished Reviewer.\n[2022.08]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at WACV 2023.\n[2022.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-STACOM 2022.\n[2022.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-DeCaF 2022.\n[2022.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-DGM4MICCAI 2022.\n[2022.06]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at MICCAI 2022.\n[2022.05]\nPAPER\nOne paper\nearly accepted\nat MICCAI 2022!\n[2022.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at NAACL 2022.\n[2022.03]\nPAPER\nOur paper\nSimCVD\nhas been formally accepted by\nIEEE-TMI\n(Impact Factor: 10.048).\n[2022.03]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ICLR-PAIR2Struct 2022.\n[2022.03]\nSTATUS\nI will be interning at\nFacebook AI Research (FAIR)\n, New York, starting from June 2022.\n[2022.02]\nAWARD\nVery proud to be recognized as a\nDistinguished Referee\nfor Medical Physics.\n[2021.12]\nAWARD\nAwarded 2021 - 2022 Yale Fellowship.\n[2021.12]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at AAAI 2022.\n[2021.11]\nPAPER\nOne paper has been formally accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (IEEE-TPAMI)\n(Impact Factor 17.861).\n[2021.10]\nPA...[truncated]"
