    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/leonlee666",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Liang Li | Academic Homepage\nLiang Li (李梁)\nPh.D. in Computer Science\nResearcher, Cloud Computing Research Institute,\n                    China Telecom\nResearch Interests\n: Vector Database ·\n                    Cloud-Native Database · In-Memory\n                    Database Systems\nView\n                        Publications\nContact Me\nDBLP\nAbout Me\nI am currently a Researcher at the Cloud Computing Research Institute of\n                        China Telecom, focusing\n                        on vector database research. My work centers on developing high-performance, scalable vector\n                        database systems for AI and machine learning applications.\nBefore joining China Telecom, I worked at ByteDance in 2024 on the\n                        development of VeDB, a\n                        cloud-native database system. From 2020 to 2023, I was at Huawei Cloud working on GaussDB, a\n                        distributed relational database system. These experiences have given me extensive expertise in\n                        database internals, distributed systems, and cloud-native architectures.\nI received my Ph.D. and B.S. degrees in Computer Science from Northeastern\n                        University, China. I\n                        am passionate about building robust and efficient database systems that power modern\n                        data-intensive applications.\nEducation\n2014 - 2020\nPh.D. in Computer Science\nNortheastern University, China\n2010 - 2014\nB.S. in Computer Science\nNortheastern University, China\nWork Experience\n2024 - Present\nResearcher\nCloud Computing Research Institute, China Telecom\n2023 - 2024\nDatabase Engineer\nByteDance (VeDB)\n2020 - 2023\nDatabase Engineer\nHuawei Cloud (GaussDB)\nResearch Interests\n🗄️\nVector Database\nHigh-dimensional vector indexing, approximate nearest neighbor\n                        search, vector query optimization,\n                        and vector database system architecture for AI applications.\n☁️\nCloud-Native Database\nDatabase disaggregation, storage-compute separation, distributed\n                        transaction processing, and\n                        cloud-native database architecture design.\n⚡\nIn-Memory Database\nMain-memory database systems, in-memory indexing structures,\n                        transaction processing optimization,\n                        and real-time data analytics.\n🔧\nHardware-Software Codesign\nFPGA and GPU acceleration for databases, hardware-aware query\n                        processing, and co-design of\n                        database systems with modern hardware architectures.\nProjects\n🗄️\nVector Database System\nDeveloping a high-performance vector database system at China\n                            Telecom, supporting\n                            billion-scale vector indexing and real-time similarity search for AI applications.\nVector Search\nANN Index\nDistributed\n☁️\nVeDB - Cloud-Native Database\nContributed to VeDB development at ByteDance, a cloud-native\n                            database with storage-compute\n                            separation architecture for high scalability and availability.\nCloud-Native\nDisaggregation\nOLTP\n📊\nGaussDB - Distributed RDBMS\nWorked on Huawei Cloud GaussDB, a distributed relational\n                            database with focus on query\n                            optimization, transaction processing, and distributed storage engine.\nDistributed DB\nQuery Optimizer\nHuawei Cloud\nContact\n📧\nEmail\nliangneu@yeah.net\n📍\nAddress\nCloud Computing Research Institute\nChina Telecom,\n                                Beijing, China\n🔗\nAcademic Links\nGoogle\n                                    Scholar\n|\nDBLP\n|\nResearchGate\n|\nORCID\nSend\n                            Message"
  },
