  "serper::Ling Sun": {
    "homepage": "https://www.lingsun.org/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nDr Ling (Lilli) Sun\nResearch Fellow, Centre for Gravitational Astrophysics, The Australian National University\nARC DECRA Fellow\nI am a research fellow at the\nCentre for Gravitational Astrophysics (CGA)\nat\nthe Australian National University\n. I am a member of the\nLaser Interferometer Gravitational-wave Observatory (\nLIGO\n)\nScientific Collaboration, an ARC DECRA\nF\nellow, and one of the Chief Investigators of the ARC Centre of Excellence for Gravitational Wave Discovery (\nOzGrav\n)\n.\nMy primary research interests\nare gravitational-wave data analysis and\nstudying fundamental physics from gravitational-wave observations,\nincluding:\nblack hole\nsuperradiance, ultralight bosons, particle dark matter\nblack hole\nspectroscopy\nbinary neutron star\npost-merger physics\ncontinuous waves from neutron stars\ncalibration of the gravitational-wave detector\ns\nscience of the next-generation detectors\nIn particular, I am interested in bringing together advanced computing and signal processing techniques, gravitational-wave data and theory, as well as the understanding of the instruments for gravitational-wave observation.\nNews:\nDec\n29, 2025\nUltralight boson constraints from gravitational wave observations of spinning binary black holes (Aswathi, East, Siemonsen, Sun, Jones) is\npublished\nin\nPhys. Rev. D 112, 123048\n(2025),\narXiv:2507.20979\nOct 28, 2025\nGW241011 and GW241110: Exploring Binary Formation and Fundamental Physics with Asymmetric, High-spin Black Hole Coalescences\n(LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA Collaboration) is published in\nAstrophys. J. Lett. 993, L21\n(2025)\nOct\n15\n, 2025\nImpact of Detector Calibration Accuracy on Black Hole Spectroscopy (Sinha, Sun, Ma) is published in\nPRD 112, 084038\n,\narXiv:2506.15979\n(2025)\nOct\n8\n, 2025\nToward Low-Latency, High-Fidelity Calibration of the LIGO Detectors with Enhanced Monitoring Tools (Wade, Betzwieser, Bhattacharjee, Dartez, Goetz, Kissel, Sun, Viets, Carney, Makelele, Wade) is\npublished\nin\nClass. Quantum Grav. 42 215016\n(2025)\n,\narXiv:2508.08423\nOct 1, 2025\nGW250114 reveals black hole horizon signatures (Lu, Ma, Piccinni, Chen, Sun) is posted on\narXiv:2510.01001\n(2025)\nSep\n17\n, 2025\nStatistical identification of ringdown modes with rational filters (Lu, Ma, Piccinni, Sun, Finch) is published in\nPhys. Rev. D 112, 064047\n(2025),\narXiv:2505.18560\nSep 10, 2025\nGW250114: Testing Hawking’s Area Law and the Kerr Nature of Black Holes (LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA Collaboration) is published in\nPhys. Rev. Lett. 135, 111403\n(2025); Black Hole Spectroscopy and Tests of General Relativity with GW250114\n(LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA Collaboration) is posted on\narXiv:2509.08099\n(2025)\nSep 9, 2025\nGW230814: investigation of a loud gravitational-wave signal observed with a single detector (LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA Collaboration) is posted on\narXiv:2509.07348\n(2025)\nSep 9, 2025\nDirected searches for gravitational waves from ultralight vector boson clouds around merger remnant and galactic black holes during the first part of the fourth LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA observing run (LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA Collaboration) is posted on\narXiv:2509.07352\n(2025)\nApr\n24\n, 202\n5\nInvited talk at \"\nFrom Quarks to Neutron Stars: Insights from kHz Gravitational Wave\n\" workshop\n:\nGravitational Wave Discoveries — Now and the Near Future\n, Tokyo, Japan\nApr\n7\n, 2025\nSearch for continuous gravitational waves from neutron stars in five globular clusters with a phase-tracking hidden Markov model in the third LIGO observing run (Dunn, Melatos, Clearwater, Suvorova, Sun, Moran, Evans) is\npublished\nin\nPhys. Rev. D 111, 083012\n(2025)\n,\narXiv:2503.15773\nApr 1, 2025\nMedia release \"\nRandom conversation leads to innovative dark matter detector design\n\"\nMar\n24\n, 2025\nDifferential torsion sensor for direct detection of ultralight vector dark matter (Sun, Slagmolen, Qin) is\npublished\nin\nPhys. Rev. D 111, 063064\n(2025)\n,\narXiv:2402.08935\nMar\n12\n, 2025\nImpact of calibration uncertainties on Hubble constant measurements from gravitational-wave sources (Huang, Chen, Haster, Sun, Vitale, Kissel) is\npublished in\nPhys. Rev. D\n111, 063034 (2025)\n,\narXiv:2204.03614\nMar\n11, 2025\nMapping inspiral-merger-ringdown waveforms of binary black holes from black hole perturbation waveforms by machine learning (Zhong, Han, Sun) is published in\nPhys. Rev. D\n111, 064033 (2025)\n,\narXiv:2503.04534\nMar\n1\n0\n, 2025\nMethodology for constraining ultralight vector bosons with gravitational wave searches targeting merger remnant black holes (Jones, Siemonsen, Sun, East, Miller, Wette, Piccinni) is\npublished\nin\nPhys. Rev. D\n111, 063028 (2025)\n,\narXiv:2412.00320\nFeb 26, 2025\nDetermination of the birth-mass function of neutron stars from observations (You et al.) is published in\nNature Astronomy (2025)\n,\narXiv:2412.05524\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::X. Yang": {
    "homepage": "https://www.med.upenn.edu/apps/faculty/index.php/g20001883/p20138",
