  "serper::Haoling Tang": {
    "homepage": "https://www.tangphotonicslab.com/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Tang Reconfigurable Photonics Lab\ntop of page\nTang Lab\nReconfigurable Photonics Lab\nOur lab is actively hiring and\nwill officially launch in MIT MechE in the summer of 2026.\nOur homepage at MIT MechE\nOur homepage at UC Berkeley EECS\nJoin us? Check\nOpportunities\n.\nMEGA-PC: Hyper-reconfigurable sensor\nMicro-Electro-Mechanical Systems (MEMS)\nNonlinear Spectroscopy\nMEGA-PC: Hyper-reconfigurable sensor\n1/5\nOur Research Focus\nThe Tang lab conducts interdisciplinary research at the intersection of\nnanophotonics\n,\noptical\ninstrumentation\n, and\ndevice engineering\n, with a focus on\nmetamaterials\n,\nquantum materials\n, and\nMEMS-enabled platforms\n. We develop innovative approaches to in situ tuning of mechanical, electrical, and optical properties of metamaterials and thin films, enabling hyper-reconfigurable light sources, strong light–matter interactions, and meta-optic sensors and modulators. Our work combines\nnonlinear and quantum optics\n,\nintegrated photonics\n, and\nnanofabrication\nto advance next-generation photonic technologies.\nNEWS\n01/20/2026\nInvited talk on\nSPIE Photonics West\nfor our new unpublished result in nonlinear optics.\n01/14/2026\nOur new paper \"\nForbidden second harmonics in centrosymmetric bilayer crystals\n\" is on arXiv!\n08/29/2025\nThe\nMIT webpage\nis online now!\n05/05/2025\nWe are hosting a\nSpecial Symposia\n- Twistopics for Light-Matter Interactions in CLEO 2025 Long Beach. Check and join us! ​\n04/03/2025\nOur Nature Photonics Paper, '\nAn adaptive moiré sensor for spectro-polarimetric hyperimaging,\n' is now online and has been featured in a\nHarvard News Story\n!​​​​​​\n02/14/2025\nOur paper '\nA Van der Waals Moiré Bilayer Photonic Crystal Cavity\n' is on ArXiv now.\n01/31/2025\nOur paper '\nControl of chirality and directionality of nonlinear metasurface light source via moiré engineering\n' is online at Physical Review Letters. Congrats Huanyu!\n11/04/2024\nDr. Haoning Tang received the\nRising Stars of Light Award\nfrom Springer Nature, Light Sci. Appl., and iCANX Association. Congratulations!\n11/04/2024\nOur Nature paper, '\nOn-chip multi-degree-of-freedom control of two-dimensional materials\n' is now online and has been featured in the\nHarvard Gazette\n.\n07/12/2024\nOur paper, '\nFree-Space Beam Steering with Twisted Bilayer Photonic Crystal Slabs\n,' which was co-authored with Shanhui Fan's group at Stanford, is now online in ACS Photonics.\n16/02/2024\nOur paper '\nThree-Dimensional Reconfigurable Optical Singularities in Bilayer Photonic Crystals\n' is available now on Physical Review Letters. Congrats Xueqi!\nbottom of page"
  },
