    "homepage_text": "Rares-Darius Buhai\nRares-Darius Buhai\nI am a postdoc in the School of Computer and Communication Sciences at EPFL, hosted by\nProf. Ola Svensson\n.\n          I am interested in theoretical aspects of computer science and machine learning.\nEmail\nrares-darius.buhai@epfl.ch\nCV\nScholar\nDBLP\nBio\n2025-present: postdoc, EPFL, hosted by\nProf. Ola Svensson\n2020-2025: PhD, ETH Zurich, advised by\nProf. David Steurer\n2015-2020: BSc & MEng, MIT, advised by\nProf. Guy Bresler\nPublications\n2025\nFinding Colorings in One-Sided Expanders\nRB\n, Yiding Hua, David Steurer, Andor Vári-Kakas\nFOCS 2025\nThe Quasi-Polynomial Low-Degree Conjecture is False\nRB\n, Jun-Ting Hsieh, Aayush Jain, Pravesh K. Kothari\nFOCS 2025\nLasso and Partially-Rotated Designs\nRB\nPreprint\n2024\nDimension Reduction via Sum-of-Squares and Improved Clustering Algorithms for Non-Spherical Mixtures\nPrashanti Anderson, Mitali Bafna,\nRB\n, Pravesh K. Kothari, David Steurer\nPreprint\nRobust Mixture Learning when Outliers Overwhelm Small Groups\nDaniil Dmitriev,\nRB\n, Stefan Tiegel, Alexander Wolters, Gleb Novikov, Amartya Sanyal, David Steurer, Fanny Yang\nNeurIPS 2024\nSemirandom Planted Clique and the Restricted Isometry Property\nJarosław Błasiok,\nRB\n, Pravesh K. Kothari, David Steurer\nFOCS 2024\nComputational-Statistical Gaps for Improper Learning in Sparse Linear Regression\nRB\n, Jingqiu Ding, Stefan Tiegel\nCOLT 2024\n2023\nBeyond Parallel Pancakes: Quasi-Polynomial Time Guarantees for Non-Spherical Gaussian Mixtures\nRB\n, David Steurer\nCOLT 2023\nAlgorithms approaching the threshold for semi-random planted clique\nRB\n, Pravesh K. Kothari, David Steurer\nSTOC 2023\n2020\nLearning Restricted Boltzmann Machines with Sparse Latent Variables\nGuy Bresler,\nRB\nNeurIPS 2020\nEmpirical Study of the Benefits of Overparameterization in Learning Latent Variable Models\nRB\n, Yoni Halpern, Yoon Kim, Andrej Risteski, David Sontag\nICML 2020"
