    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/skchao74",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/shih-kang-chao",
    "homepage_text": "About me - Shih-Kang Chao\nShih-Kang Chao\nMachine Learning Scientist\nFollow\nResearchGate\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nPublons\nMath Stackexchange\nAbout me\nI am a Sr. Applied Scientist at Amazon. Previously, I was a machine learning scientist at a precision health startup\nHealth[at]Scale\nin San Jose. Before that, I was an assistant professor in the\nDepartment of Statistics\nat the\nUniversity of Missouri\n.\nThe major part of this website showcases the works I have done in my previous career as a researcher in statistics. Even though my research activity goes dormant, I remain active in writing blog posts.\nDisclaimer: all opinions presented in this website are my own and not the views of my employer.\nNews\nA new manuscript “Balancing Approach for Causal Inference at Scale” has been uploaded to\nArXiv\n. This is a joint effort with the applied data science team at Snap.\nMy paper “Distributed Bootstrap for Simultaneous Inference Under High Dimensionality” coauthored with Dr. Yang Yu (Meta) and Dr. Guang Cheng (UCLA) has been accepted for publication by the\nJournal of Machine Learning Research\n.\nMy abstract “Automatic lung segmentation for hyperpolarized gas MRI using transferred generative adversarial network and three-view aggregation” submitted to the\nJoint Meeting of ISMRM 2022\nhas been accepted! The presentation will be in-person. I look forward to the meeting in London!"
  },
