    "homepage_text": "Ricardo Olmedo\nRicardo Dominguez-Olmedo\nI am a PhD Student at the Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems, working with\nMoritz Hardt\nand\nBernhard Schoelkopf\n.\nMy research focuses broadly on language models.\nGoogle Scholar\nTwitter\nEmail\nSelected works:\nTraning on the Test Task Confounds Evaluation and Emergence\n,\nICLR 2025 (Oral)\n.\nLawma: The Power of Specialization for Legal Annotation\n,\nICLR 2025 + CS&Law'25\n.\nQuestioning the Survey Responses of Large Language Models\n,\nNeurIPS 2024 (Oral)\n.\nBlog posts:\nmini-coder: small models for research on SWE agents\nHow to Fix the LMArena? Release All Data\nIf you're interested in working with me as a master's student or intern, feel free to reach out via email."
