    "homepage_text": "CV - Carlos Villacampa-Calvo, PhD\nCarlos Villacampa-Calvo\nPhD\nFollow\nUniversidad Autónoma de Madrid\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nCV\nEducation\nB.S. in GitHub, GitHub University, 2012\nM.S. in Jekyll, GitHub University, 2014\nPh.D in Version Control Theory, GitHub University, 2018 (expected)\nWork experience\nSummer 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Tagging issues\nSupervisor: Professor Git\nFall 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Merging pull requests\nSupervisor: Professor Hub\nSkills\nSkill 1\nSkill 2\nSub-skill 2.1\nSub-skill 2.2\nSub-skill 2.3\nSkill 3\nPublications\nScalable multi-class Gaussian process classification using expectation propagation\nVillacampa-Calvo, C., & Hernández-Lobato, D.(2017). \"Scalable multi-class Gaussian process classification using expectation propagation.\"\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning\n. 70(3550-3559).\nMulti-class Gaussian Process Classification with Noisy Inputs\nVillacampa-Calvo, C., & Zaldívar, B., & Garrido-Merchán, E. C., & Hernández-Lobato, D.(2020). \"Multi-class Gaussian Process Classification with Noisy Inputs.\"\nJournal of Machine Learning Research\n. 22(1-52).\nAlpha divergence minimization in multi-class Gaussian process classification\nVillacampa-Calvo, C., & Hernández-Lobato, D.(2020). \"Alpha divergence minimization in multi-class Gaussian process classification.\"\nNeurocomputing\n. 378(210-227).\nDeep Gaussian Processes Using Expectation Propagation and Monte Carlo Methods\nHernández-Muñoz, G., & Villacampa-Calvo, C., & Hernández-Lobato, D.(2020). \"Deep Gaussian Processes Using Expectation Propagation and Monte Carlo Methods.\"\nEuropean Conference on Machine Learning and Knowledge Discovery in Databases\n. (479-494).\nInput Dependent Sparse Gaussian Processes\nJafrasteh, B., & Villacampa-Calvo, C., & Hernández-Lobato, D.(2020). \"Input Dependent Sparse Gaussian Processes.\"\narXiv preprint\n.\nTalks\n