    "homepage_text": "Jung-hun Kim\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJung-hun Kim\nJung-hun Kim\n(김정훈)\n[\nCV\n]\nPostdoctoral Researcher at CREST, ENSAE, IP Paris\n–\nFairPlay team\njunghunkim7786@gmail.com | junghun.kim@ensae.fr\n[\nLinked\nI\nn\n]\n, [\nGoogle Scholar\n]\nResearch Overview\nI work on\nonline learning and decision-making under uncertainty and non-stationarity\n, with applications to\noptimal stopping, matching, queueing systems, dynamic pricing, and recommendation\n.\nMy research combines theoretical guarantees with practically motivated models to study dynamic decision-making in complex systems.\nAcademic Positions\nPostdoctoral\nResearcher\n, CREST, ENSAE, IP Paris –\nFairPlay team,\nFrance\nJune\n202\n5\n-\nPresent\nSupervisor\n:\nVianney Perchet\nResearch focus\n: Optimal stopping and prophet inequalities\nPostdoctoral Researcher\n, IDIS, Seoul National University, South Korea\nSep 2023 - May 2025\nSupervisor\n:\nMin-hwan Oh\nResearch focus:\nOnline learning for matching and dynamic pricing\nPh.D.\nin Industrial and Systems Engineering, KAIST,  South Korea\nSep 2018 - Aug 2023\nAdvisor:\nSe-Young Yun\nResearch focus: Online learning\nin\nnon-stationary environments\nResearch intern\n,\nDepartme\nnt of Statistics,\nLondon School of Economics, UK\nMar 2021 - Jul 2021\nSupervisor\n:\nMilan Vojnovi\nć\nResearch focus:\nOnline learning\nfor\nscheduling in dy\nnamic systems\nPublications\n[\nICLR 2026,\nto appear\n]\nLearning in Prophet Inequalities with Noisy Observations\nJung-hun Kim\n,\nVianney Perchet\n[\nNeurIPS\n2025]\nOrac\nle-Efficient Combinatorial Semi-Bandits\nJung-hun Kim\n, Milan Vojnovi\nć,\nMin-hwan Oh\n[TMLR 2025]\nAdversarial Bandits Against Arbitrary Strategies\nJung-hun Kim\n, Se-Young Yun\n[ICML 2025]\nTracking Most Significant Shifts in Infinite-Armed Bandits\nJoe Suk,\nJung-hun Kim\n[ICLR 2025]\nDynamic Assortment Selection and Pricing with Censored Preference Feedback\nJung-hun Kim\n, Min-hwan Oh\n[NeurIPS 2024]\nQueueing Matching Bandits with Preference Feedback\nJung-hun Kim\n, Min-hwan Oh\n[NeurIPS 2024]\nAn Adaptive Approach for Infinitely Many-armed Bandits under Generalized Rotting Constraints\nJung-hun Kim\n, Milan Vojnovi\nć\n, Se-Young Yun\n[AISTATS 2023]\nContextual Linear Bandits under Noisy Features: Towards Bayesian Oracles\nJung-hun Kim\n, Se-Young Yun, Minchan Jeong, Junhyun Nam, Jinwoo Shin, Richard Combes\n[IC\nML 2022]\nRotting Infinitely Many-armed Bandits\nJung-hun Kim\n, Milan Vojnovi\nć\n, Se-Young Yun\n[\nIEEE BigData 2018\n]\nResearch Hypothesis Generation using Link Prediction in a Bipartite Graph\nJung-hun Kim\n,\nAviv Segev\nWorking Papers\nMatching Optimization with\nPreference Feedback (\nlin\nk\n)\nJung-hun Kim\n, Min-hwan Oh\nScheduling with Bilinear Rewards\n(\nlink\n)\nJung-hun Kim\n,\nMilan Vojnovi\nć\nAcademic Activities\nReviewer: NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, AISTATS, JMLR, CDC, AAAI\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
